\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Radicalized\u8217\'20\'19 anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  movement poses increased threat, US warned\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 649 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 July 2021\par 11:15 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Comments from Anu Kumar of reproductive rights group Ipas come as militant anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups gain legislative influence\par \par \uc2 The president and chief executive of an international reproductive rights non-profit has warned that the American anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement has significantly radicalized and is working to spread its ideology around the world.\par \par \uc2 The comments came as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/06/anti-abortion-activists-operation-save-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pro-gun anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  theocratic militant groups }}}\uc2  who seek to prosecute women who have abortions under murder statutes have gained increasing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/06/anti-abortion-activists-operation-save-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legislative influence }}}\uc2  in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the 90s we saw groups like Operation Rescue and Operation Save America, and they were quite violent,\u8221\'20\'1D said Anu Kumar of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ipas.org/about-us/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ipas}}}\uc2 , an international non-governmental organization that works to expand access to contraception and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis recent uptick is really an even more radicalized version of what we saw back then, and in some ways it\u8217\'20\'19s not your mother\u8217\'20\'19s anti-choice groups.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Operation Save America denies condoning violence, though leaders of affiliated groups such as Defy Tyrants, led by Matt Trewhella, were signatories to a statement which described murdering \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers as \u8220\'20\'1Cjustifiable homicide\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Since Donald Trump left office, and as the US suffered among the worst Covid outbreaks in the world, Republican legislatures have worked to make 2021 the most hostile year for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the procedure was legalized nationally in 1973.\par \par \uc2 States enacted 90 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions in 2021, breaking the previous record of 89 in 2011. These restrictions stand in contrast to the \u8220\'20\'1Cunmistakable trend toward the liberalization of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws\u8221\'20\'1D globally, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cfr.org/article/abortion-law-global-comparisons"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Council on Foreign Relations}}}\uc2 . Since 2000, more than 28 nations have liberalized their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws. Only one, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2006/oct/27/topstories3.mainsection"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nicaragua}}}\uc2 , restricted legal grounds for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At the same time, the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has never been so perilously close to being removed since 1973, when the supreme court decided the landmark case Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Late this year the supreme court is expected to hear a case out of Mississippi called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/18/us-supreme-court-abortion-test-case-mississippi-precedent"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization}}}\uc2 , which will consider whether a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is constitutional. Because Roe allows pregnant people to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to the point of viability, roughly understood to be 24 weeks, scholars speculate the court could substantially redefine people\u8217\'20\'19s right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe reason they\u8217\'20\'19re different, and it\u8217\'20\'19s important, is they are not interested in incremental change. They\u8217\'20\'19re not interested in using regulations. They\u8217\'20\'19re not even that interested in Roe,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kumar.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat they\u8217\'20\'19re militant about is defying the courts, defying the constitution and defying the rule of law,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd they use scripture to justify their violence. Yes they are definitely anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they are misogynist, they are anti-immigrant as well.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut fundamentally they are about democracy \u8211\'20\'13 they are anti-democratic zealots, this is not just about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mainstream anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups have placed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/09/us-voting-restrictions-conservative-groups-lobbying-against-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 multimillion-dollar bets}}}\uc2  on restricting voting rights, while militant groups have openly advocated for theocracy, while also experiencing newfound success in conservative legislatures. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/apr/27/us-tiny-towns-anti-abortion-ordinances"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In Oklahoma, Texas and Arizona}}}\uc2 , state lawmakers have all introduced legislation to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a crime punishable under murder statutes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhite supremacy is the thread that ties everything together,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kumar. \u8220\'20\'1CFrom the insurrection we saw on 6 January to the racial uprisings to the uptick in anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation [in the US],\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Kumar added that, while the most militant groups have small direct memberships, their ideology has proved sufficiently appealing to attract legislators and new followers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the bright shining light that needs to be put on this issue, that all people should be concerned about these groups,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kumar. \u8220\'20\'1CBecause their agenda is really big and far-reaching.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 9 July 2021. Nicaragua has restricted its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws since 2000, not expanded them as stated in an earlier version.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210708eh78000p4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
