\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden says \u8216\'20\'18I will not send another generation of Americans to war in Afghanistan\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Julia Carrie Wong, Lois Beckett and Joan E Greve \par \uc2 9,788 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 July 2021\par 00:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Biden speaks on US troop withdrawal after 20 years at warPresident to receive update on military withdrawal process\u8216\'20\'18Radicalized\u8217\'20\'19 anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement posed increased threat\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Evening summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s all from me today. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a rundown of the day\u8217\'20\'19s biggest stories:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  defended his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/08/joe-biden-afghanistan-military-pullout-ahead-of-schedule"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision to withdraw all US troops from Afghanistan}}}\uc2 , arguing that continuing the operation would only result in further casualties. \u8220\'20\'1CI will not send another generation of Americans to war in Afghanistan with no reasonable expectation of achieving a different outcome,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said this afternoon. The president\u8217\'20\'19s speech came two days after the Pentagon announced the troop withdrawal was already more than 90% complete.\par \par \uc2 * Biden and his chief spokesperson acknowledged there will not be a \u8220\'20\'1Cmission accomplished\u8221\'20\'1D moment in Afghanistan, although the president insisted the US had already met its objectives in the military operation. \u8220\'20\'1CNo, there\u8217\'20\'19s no mission accomplished,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden told reporters after his speech. \u8220\'20\'1CThe mission was accomplished in that we got \uc2 Osama bin Laden\uc2 , and terrorism is not emanating from that part of the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The Texas special legislative session began, as Republicans attempt to once again enact voting restrictions in the state. Republican legislators failed to pass their original bill during the regular session because Democrats staged a walkout at the 11th hour. The Republican governor of Texas, Greg Abbott, has now called the chamber back into session to try to get a slightly altered bill passed.\par \par \uc2 * Meanwhile, the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  announced a $25m investment in efforts to strengthen voting rights. Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  announced the initiative this afternoon at \uc2 Howard University\uc2 , her alma mater. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the fight of our lifetime,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said of the campaign. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the fight of our nation\u8217\'20\'19s lifetime.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Later in the day, Harris and Biden met with a group of civil rights leaders, who expressed their \u8220\'20\'1Cexasperation\u8221\'20\'1D that the administration has not done more to push back against the Republican attack on voting rights.\par \par \uc2 * The director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention said the Delta variant of coronavirus is \u8220\'20\'1Csurging\u8221\'20\'1D in areas with low rates of vaccination. The CDC director, \uc2 Dr Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , noted that the Delta variant accounts for as much as 80% of new coronavirus cases in certain parts of the Midwest and upper mountain states. \u8220\'20\'1CAlthough we expected the Delta variant to become the dominant strain in the United States, this rapid rise is troubling,\u8221\'20\'1D Walensky said at a press briefing today.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Civil rights leaders urged \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to take much more aggressive action against Republican voter suppression efforts in a meeting Thursday, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/harris-voting/2021/07/08/6f26d150-e007-11eb-b507-697762d090dd_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post}}}\uc2  reports.\par \par \uc2 The meeting at the White House stretched more than twice as long as expected, as leaders including \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2  of the National Action Network, Marc Morial of the \uc2 National Urban League\uc2 , and \uc2 Sherrilyn Ifill\uc2  of the \uc2 NAACP Legal Defense and Educational Fund\uc2 , expressed their \u8220\'20\'1Cexasperation\u8221\'20\'1D to the president, according to the report.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe must have the president use his voice, use his influence, use his power \u8212\'20\'14 and use what he clearly understands about this moment,\u8221\'20\'1D Ifill told the Post. \u8220\'20\'1CThe president understands us to be in a moment of peril in terms of our democracy. And that means that we have to put all the options on the table, figure out what can work, keep talking, keep pressing and move forward.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Other attendees included \uc2 Derrick Johnson\uc2  of the \uc2 NAACP\uc2 , Wade Henderson of the Leadership Conference on Civil and Human Rights and Damon Hewitt of the Lawyers\u8217\'20\'19 Committee for Civil Rights Under Law, Dr. Johnnetta Betsch Cole of the \uc2 National Council of Negro Women\uc2 , and \uc2 Melanie Campbell\uc2  of the National Coalition on Black Civic Participation.\par \par \uc2 The civil rights leaders released a joint statement about the meeting:\par \par \uc2 The civil rights leaders expressed their very serious concern over the dangerous anti-voter efforts by some who are intent on taking the nation backwards through voting barriers for Black, Brown, Indigenous, and new Americans. They made clear that these severely harmful efforts are a historic and existential crisis of democracy that requires urgent attention. The leaders expressed their thanks to the president and vice president for their support so far and asked them to do even more in pushing Congress to pass the For the People Act and the \uc2 John Lewis\uc2  Voting Rights Advancement Act in order to make real the promise of our democracy for all.\par \par \uc2 The civil rights leaders also discussed the urgent need to provide meaningful changes to hold police accountable for misconduct and ensure the safety of all community members, including Black and Brown people who disproportionately face violence and abuse at the hands of police. The leaders urged the president and vice president to do everything possible to ensure legislation like the George Floyd Justice In Policing Act is passed into law.\par \par \uc2 Earlier today \uc2 Kamala Harris{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jul/08/joe-biden-us-troop-withdrawal-afghanistan-covid-coronavirus-politics-latest?page=with:block-60e735788f08fa158fe1daae#block-60e735788f08fa158fe1daae"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  that the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  was investing $25m in an expanded effort to protect voting rights.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.19am BST\par \par \uc2 The president and chief executive of an international reproductive rights non-profit has warned that the American anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement has significantly radicalized and is working to spread its ideology around the world.\par \par \uc2 The comments came as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/06/anti-abortion-activists-operation-save-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pro-gun anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  theocratic militant groups }}}\uc2  who seek to prosecute women who have abortions under murder statutes have gained increasing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/06/anti-abortion-activists-operation-save-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legislative influence }}}\uc2  in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the 90s we saw groups like Operation Rescue and Operation Save America, and they were quite violent,\u8221\'20\'1D said Anu Kumar of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ipas.org/about-us/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ipas}}}\uc2 , an international non-governmental organization that works to expand access to contraception and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis recent uptick is really an even more radicalized version of what we saw back then, and in some ways it\u8217\'20\'19s not your mother\u8217\'20\'19s anti-choice groups.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Operation Save America denies condoning violence, though leaders of affiliated groups such as Defy Tyrants, led by Matt Trewhella, were signatories to a statement which described murdering \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers as \u8220\'20\'1Cjustifiable homicide\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  left office, and as the US suffered among the worst Covid outbreaks in the world, Republican legislatures have worked to make 2021 the most hostile year for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the procedure was legalized nationally in 1973.\par \par \uc2 States enacted 90 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions in 2021, breaking the previous record of 89 in 2011. These restrictions stand in contrast to the \u8220\'20\'1Cunmistakable trend toward the liberalization of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws\u8221\'20\'1D globally, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cfr.org/article/abortion-law-global-comparisons"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Council on Foreign Relations}}}\uc2 . Since 2000, more than 28 nations have liberalized their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws. Only one, Nicaragua, expanded legal grounds for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Read the full report here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jul/08/anti-abortion-movement-radicalized"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Radicalized\u8217\'20\'19 anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  movement poses increased threat, US warned}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Two men believed to be Haitian Americans were among the six who have been arrested in connection with the assassination of Haiti\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Jovenel Mo\u239\'00\'EFse\uc2 , according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 Seven other suspects were killed in the raid, Haitian police said.\par \par \uc2 Mathias Pierre, Haiti\u8217\'20\'19s minister of elections, named one of the Haitian Americans as James Solages to the AP, but did not provide further details or the name of the second American suspect.\par \par \uc2 From the report:\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US State Department\uc2  said it was aware of reports that Haitian Americans were in custody but could not confirm or comment.\par \par \uc2 Solages described himself as a \u8220\'20\'1Ccertified diplomatic agent,\u8221\'20\'1D an advocate for children and budding politician on a website for a charity he established in 2019 in south Florida to assist residents.\par \par \uc2 On his bio page for the charity, Solages said he previously worked as a bodyguard at the Canadian Embassy in Haiti. The Canadian Embassy didn\u8217\'20\'19t immediately comment; calls to the foundation and Solages\u8217\'20\'19 associates at the charity either did not go through or weren\u8217\'20\'19t answered.\par \par \uc2 The assassination of Mo\u239\'00\'EFse on Wednesday has left a political vaccuum in Haiti. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a summary of the situation, from my Guardian colleagues:\par \par \uc2 On Thursday Haitians woke up to a country without a head of state, with a parliament long suspended, two rival interim prime ministers \u8211\'20\'13 one of whom was due to be sworn in during the coming days \u8211\'20\'13 and a constitutional legal vacuum after the death from coronavirus of the head of its supreme court.\par \par \uc2 That has generated confusion about who is the legitimate leader of the country of 11 million people \u8211\'20\'13 [ interim prime minister Claude] Joseph, who has assumed power for now, or Ariel Henry, who was appointed as PM by Mo\u239\'00\'EFse just before his death and was due to be sworn in this week. \u8220\'20\'1CAll the cards are up in the air,\u8221\'20\'1D Fatton said of the apparent struggle between Henry and Joseph.\par \par \uc2 Ryan Berg, an analyst with the \uc2 Center for Strategic and International Studies\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CI can picture a scenario under which there are issues regarding to whom the armed forces and national police are loyal, in the case there are rival claims to being placeholder president of the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here is their full report:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jul/08/haiti-president-assassination-arrests-gunmen-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Haiti security forces arrest six alleged gunmen after president\u8217\'20\'19s assassination}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hello everyone. This is Julia Carrie Wong, picking up the live blog for the rest of the afternoon from Oakland, California, where we\u8217\'20\'19re in the midst of a devastating drought and about to be hit with another brutal heat wave.\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, California governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  asked businesses and people to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/08/california-drought-water-use-restriction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cut water use by 15%}}}\uc2  in a sign of growing concern over dwindling water reserves.\par \par \uc2 From our report:\par \par \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s request is not an order, but it demonstrates the growing challenges of a drought that will only worsen throughout the summer and fall and is tied to recent heatwaves. Reservoirs across the state, which are depended on for agriculture, drinking water and fish habitat, have dwindled to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/30/california-drought-water-shortage-photo-essay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dangerously low levels}}}\uc2  and some counties have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/12/dire-situation-silicon-valley-cracks-down-on-water-use-as-california-drought-worsens"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already enacted}}}\uc2  mandatory water restrictions.\par \par \uc2 California\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor is asking for voluntary water conservation, which would include actions such as taking shorter showers, running dishwashers only when they are full and reducing the frequency of watering lawns.\par \par \uc2 Nearly 95% of the state is experiencing severe drought, according to the US drought monitor. While California has long cycled through wet and dry periods, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/07/california-drought-oregon-west-climate-change"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 climate crisis}}}\uc2  has made the dry periods drier, hotter and longer. Already some communities are facing water shortages, and the state is bracing for what is likely to be a severe fire season.\par \par \uc2 enltr-- {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CAgovernor?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CAGovernor}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GavinNewsom?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GavinNewsom}}}\uc2  says {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mOy55KDXS2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/mOy55KDXS2}}}\uc2  site available to residents to learn latest on how to reduce their water consumption. Says 50 of 58 CA counties now facing drought emergency, but notes Californians are now schooled in many of the basics of conservation. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VntVcef1Kv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VntVcef1Kv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Carla Marinucci (@cmarinucci) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cmarinucci/status/1413214485830008837?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  plans to seek authorization for a third vaccine dose\par \par \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  is about to seek US authorization for a third dose of its Covid-19 vaccine, saying Thursday that another shot within 12 months could dramatically boost immunity and maybe help ward off the latest worrisome coronavirus variation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/europe-coronavirus-pandemic-science-health-34c3f2536747a7c08980d7359a8de70c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Research from multiple countries shows the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  shot and other widely used Covid-19 vaccines offer strong protection against the highly contagious delta variant, which is spreading rapidly around the world and now accounts for most new US infections.\par \par \uc2 Two doses of most vaccines are critical to develop high levels of virus-fighting antibodies against all versions of the coronavirus, not just the delta variant \u8211\'20\'13 and most of the world still is desperate to get those initial protective doses as the pandemic continues to rage.\par \par \uc2 But antibodies naturally wane over time, so studies also are under way to tell if and when boosters might be needed.\par \par \uc2 enltrPfizer says it plans to seek U.S. regulators\u8217\'20\'19 approval for a third COVID-19 vaccine dose. The company says its research suggests antibody levels jump markedly after a third dose, but it's not yet clear if and when boosters might truly be needed. ? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nD631SWYlx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/nD631SWYlx}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Associated Press (@AP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP/status/1413249916353253376?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Dr Mikael Dolsten\uc2  told the Associated Press that early data from the company\u8217\'20\'19s booster study suggests people\u8217\'20\'19s antibody levels jump five- to 10-fold after a third dose, compared to their second dose months earlier.\par \par \uc2 In August, \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  plans to ask the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  for emergency authorization of a third dose, he said.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 FDA\uc2  authorization would be just a first step \u8211\'20\'13 it wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t automatically mean Americans get offered boosters, cautioned Dr William Schaffner, a vaccine expert at \uc2 Vanderbilt University\uc2  medical center. Public health authorities would have to decide if they\u8217\'20\'19re really needed, especially since millions of people have no protection.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe vaccines were designed to keep us out of the hospital\u8221\'20\'1D and continue to do so despite the more contagious delta variant, he said. Giving another dose would be \u8220\'20\'1Ca huge effort while we are at the moment striving to get people the first dose.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Currently only about 48% of the US population is fully vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump spotted playing golf with \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s son, a gubernatorial hopeful\par \par \uc2 Andrew Giuliani\uc2 , son of former New York mayor-cum-Trump attorney {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/rudygiuliani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rudy Giuliani}}}\uc2 , received exactly no votes in a poll of state Republican leaders about the party\u8217\'20\'19s next choice for governor of New York state, my colleague Martin Pengelly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/29/andrew-giuliani-poll-new-york-republican-leaders-governor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported a week ago}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But now, the junior Giuliani has been spotted playing golf with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , raising questions about whether Trump might endorse him over a more mainstream Republican pick, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 Maggie Haberman reports.\par \par \uc2 enltrFresh off his lawsuit/fundraising effort, Trump was seen playing golf with NY gubernatorial candidate \uc2 Andrew Giuliani\uc2  at Bedminster today, as his campaign in the primary against \uc2 Rep. Lee Zeldin\uc2  continues. Trump had indicated previously he was leaning toward Zeldin.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Maggie Haberman (@maggieNYT) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maggieNYT/status/1413241669663797255?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Toyota\uc2  will no longer donate to politicians who voted against certifying 2020 election\par \par \uc2 This is Lois Beckett, picking up our live US politics coverage for the next hour.\par \par \uc2 Japanese automaker Toyota has put out a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pressroom.toyota.com/toyota-statement-on-pac-contributions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 press release}}}\uc2  saying \u8220\'20\'1C we have decided to stop contributing to those members of Congress who contested the certification of certain states in the 2020 election\u8221\'20\'1D, and citing stakeholders who were \u8220\'20\'1Ctroubled\u8221\'20\'1D by Toyota\u8217\'20\'19s donations to some of those politicians earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 NBC News reports that Toyota\u8217\'20\'19s statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/elections/toyota-will-stop-donating-republicans-who-objected-election-certification-n1273407"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 followed an announcement by the Lincoln Project}}}\uc2 , an anti-Trump Republican PAC, that it would begin to run advertisements targeting companies that continued to donate to members of Congress who formally contested the legitimacy of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory, even after a mob of Trump supporters stormed the Capitol building and forced lawmakers to flee during the official certification of the 2020 election results.\par \par \uc2 enltrToyota says it will stop donating to Republicans who objected to election certification {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Ya4j5p5xqf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Ya4j5p5xqf}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Geoff Bennett (@GeoffRBennett) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GeoffRBennett/status/1413240542708867081?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrICYMI: \u8220\'20\'1CThe Lincoln Project, a group focused on antagonizing President \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  during his re-election bid, is targeting corporations linked to Republicans who disputed the 2020 presidential vote and played down the attack on the U.S. Capitol...\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ShqL7hmKza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ShqL7hmKza}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Lincoln Project (@ProjectLincoln) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ProjectLincoln/status/1413200034292772866?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleagues will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  defended his decision to withdraw all US troops from Afghanistan, arguing that continuing the operation would only result in further casualties. \u8220\'20\'1CI will not send another generation of Americans to war in Afghanistan with no reasonable expectation of achieving a different outcome,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said this afternoon. The president\u8217\'20\'19s speech came two days after the Pentagon announced the troop withdrawal was already more than 90% complete.\par \par \uc2 * Biden and his chief spokesperson acknowledged there will not be a \u8220\'20\'1Cmission accomplished\u8221\'20\'1D moment in Afghanistan, although the president insisted the US had already met its objectives in the military operation. \u8220\'20\'1CNo, there\u8217\'20\'19s no mission accomplished,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden told reporters after his speech. \u8220\'20\'1CThe mission was accomplished in that we got \uc2 Osama bin Laden\uc2 , and terrorism is not emanating from that part of the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The Texas special legislative session began, as Republicans attempt to once again enact voting restrictions in the state. Republican legislators failed to pass their original bill during the regular session because Democrats staged a walkout at the 11th hour. The Republican governor of Texas, Greg Abbott, has now called the chamber back into session to try to get a slightly altered bill passed.\par \par \uc2 * Meanwhile, the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  announced a $25m investment in efforts to strengthen voting rights. Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  announced the initiative this afternoon at \uc2 Howard University\uc2 , her alma mater. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the fight of our lifetime,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said of the campaign. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the fight of our nation\u8217\'20\'19s lifetime.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention said the Delta variant of coronavirus is \u8220\'20\'1Csurging\u8221\'20\'1D in areas with low rates of vaccination. The CDC director, \uc2 Dr Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , noted that the Delta variant accounts for as much as 80% of new coronavirus cases in certain parts of the Midwest and upper mountain states. \u8220\'20\'1CAlthough we expected the Delta variant to become the dominant strain in the United States, this rapid rise is troubling,\u8221\'20\'1D Walensky said at a press briefing today.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 US assurances that Julian Assange would not be held under the strictest maximum-security conditions if extradited from the UK have been rejected by his fiancee, who described them as a formula to keep him in prison for the rest of his life.\par \par \uc2 Details of the proposals made to British authorities emerged after permission was granted this week to appeal against January\u8217\'20\'19s ruling that the Wikileaks co-founder cannot be extradited on mental health grounds.\par \par \uc2 They include assurances that Assange, if convicted in relation to charges of alleged espionage and hacking, would be allowed to serve any jail time in his native Australia.\par \par \uc2 The package contains a particular assurance that Assange would not be subject to \u8220\'20\'1Cspecial administrative measures\u8221\'20\'1D (SAMs) in US custody or imprisoned at the \u8220\'20\'1Csupermax\u8221\'20\'1D prison in Florence, Colorado, procedures reserved for high-security prisoners. The assurances were subject to change if he were to \u8220\'20\'1Cdo something\u8221\'20\'1D subsequently that met the US test for the imposition of the high-security measures.\par \par \uc2 Stella Moris, Assange\u8217\'20\'19s fiancee, described reports about US undertakings as \u8220\'20\'1Cgrossly misleading\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that 80,000 prisoners in US prisons were held in solitary confinement on any given day and only a handful were held in the conditions specifically mentioned in the proposals.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 US government\uc2  also says it may change its mind if the head of the CIA advises it to do so once Julian Assange is held in US custody,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2021/jul/08/julian-assange-fiancee-rejects-us-proposals-over-possible-extradition"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Assange fiancee rejects US proposals over possible extradition}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Two dozen groups, including the \uc2 US Chamber of Commerce\uc2  and the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2 , are launching the Coalition for Bipartisan Infrastructure Investment to urge Congress to pass a bill mirroring the bipartisan infrastructure framework.\par \par \uc2 enltrToday we joined leading business & labor organizations to launch the Coalition for Bipartisan Infrastructure Investment, urging Congress to turn the bipartisan infrastructure framework into legislation that can be signed into law. Read full statement: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cyt9SLMlDm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/cyt9SLMlDm}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jYVJqI6y3o"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jYVJqI6y3o}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 U.S. Chamber (@USChamber) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/USChamber/status/1413206316638744577?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur organizations commend the bipartisan group of 22 senators and the Biden administration on finding common ground and reaching agreement on a historic $1.2 trillion infrastructure framework,\u8221\'20\'1D the coalition said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow is the time to turn these promises into projects. We urge Congress to turn this framework into legislation that will be signed into law, and our organizations are committed to helping see this cross the finish line.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The group also warned lawmakers not to \u8220\'20\'1Clet partisan differences get in the way of action -- pass significant, meaningful infrastructure legislation now\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has endorsed the framework, and Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer has indicated he wants the upper chamber to pass a bill by the end of the month. However, much work remains to turn the framework into an actual bill.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are now meeting with leaders of civil rights groups at the White House to discuss voting rights and policing reform.\par \par \uc2 The president said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  earlier today, \u8220\'20\'1CThis afternoon, the Vice President and I will be meeting with Black leaders of legacy civil rights organizations. We have urgent work before us \u8212\'20\'14 and we are committed to doing everything we can to protect the sacred right to vote and pass the George Floyd Justice in Policing Act.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrThis afternoon, the Vice President and I will be meeting with Black leaders of legacy civil rights organizations. We have urgent work before us \u8212\'20\'14 and we are committed to doing everything we can to protect the sacred right to vote and pass the George Floyd Justice in Policing Act.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1413185671565619200?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Voting rights bills and the George Floyd Justice in Policing Act have both stalled in the Senate, and it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear how congressional Democrats will be able to advance the proposals.\par \par \uc2 Bipartisan negotiations over the policing bill have been ongoing for months, but the talks appear to be on the brink of collapse, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/police-reform-negotiations-congress-are-teetering-collapse-cops-may-be-n1272555"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to NBC News}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Among those participating in today\u8217\'20\'19s meeting are Reverend \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2 , NAACP president \uc2 Derrick Johnson\uc2  and \uc2 Sherrilyn Ifill\uc2  of the NAACP Legal Defense Fund.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Maya Yang reports for \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  continuing to charge the Secret Service thousands of dollars a month to use his properties:\par \par \uc2 Trump charged the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/secret-service"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Secret Service}}}\uc2  nearly $10,200 for its use of guest rooms at his New Jersey golf club in May, newly released records indicate.\par \par \uc2 The May charges at the Trump National golf club in Bedminster, New Jersey totaled $10,199.52 for an 18-day stay \u8211\'20\'13 about $566 per night at the resort.\par \par \uc2 The Secret Service also released documents including a \u8220\'20\'1Chotel request\u8221\'20\'1D form that covered the period from 28 May to 1 July, as well as bills indicating $3,400 worth of resort charges for January, February and early May. The agency has not disclosed the reason behind those charges, which were placed before Trump\u8217\'20\'19s arrival.\par \par \uc2 Charging rent from his government-provided security detail is not novel, as Trump has frequently charged the Secret Service for rooms used by its agents, even during his presidency, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/trump-secret-service-charges/2021/07/07/7f88043a-df2e-11eb-b507-697762d090dd_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Currently, there are no laws that prevent Trump and his company from demanding the Secret Service pay rent at his properties, and rates are at the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s discretion. The Secret Service is required by law to pay whatever is required to rent rooms near its clients.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/08/trump-golf-club-secret-service-may-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump golf club charged Secret Service $10,000 for rooms in May, records show}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Michael Avenatti\uc2  sentenced to two and a half years in prison over \uc2 Nike\uc2  scheme\par \par \uc2 Michael Avenatti\uc2 , the former lawyer to Stormy Daniels who repeatedly clashed with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  during his presidency, has been sentenced to two and a half years in prison for trying to extort \uc2 Nike\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Reuters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/michael-avenatti-gets-2-12-years-prison-nike-extortion-scheme-2021-07-08/?utm_source=twitter&utm_medium=Social"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 U.S. District Judge Paul Gardephe in Manhattan said Avenatti, 50, \u8216\'20\'18had become drunk on the power of his platform\u8217\'20\'19 in betraying his client, a youth basketball coach, in order to obtain riches for himself.\par \par \uc2 The sentencing caps a precipitous downfall for a once-obscure lawyer who in 2018 became a cable news fixture, disparaging then-President Trump and even flirting with a White House run himself.\par \par \uc2 Avenatti was convicted for threatening to expose \uc2 Nike\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s alleged corrupt payments to families of college basketball prospects unless it forked over up to $25 million for him and another lawyer to conduct an internal probe.\par \par \uc2 Avenatti openly cried in the courtroom as he delivered a statement before the sentencing. He told the judge that he had \u8220\'20\'1Clost\u8221\'20\'1D his way during his quick rise to fame.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve learned that all the fame, notoriety and money in the world is meaningless,\u8221\'20\'1D Avenatti said, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/avenatti-sentence-nike-trump/2021/07/08/149d95e8-df58-11eb-9f54-7eee10b5fcd2_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 per the Washington Post}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CTV and \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , your Honor, mean nothing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  rejected comparisons between the end of the Vietnam War and the conclusion of the war in Afghanistan, insisting the two events are nothing alike.\par \par \uc2 However, some American veterans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/american-vets-see-echoes-of-vietnam-in-afghanistan-withdrawal-plan-11619446397]"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have said}}}\uc2  they feel the US military is leaving a job undone in Afghanistan, just as it did in Vietnam. Some also fear that Kabul will soon fall to the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 , as Saigon fell after US troops departed Vietnam.\par \par \uc2 Answering another reporter\u8217\'20\'19s question, Biden echoed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jul/08/joe-biden-us-troop-withdrawal-afghanistan-covid-coronavirus-politics-latest?page=with:block-60e72d678f08fa158fe1da45#block-60e72d678f08fa158fe1da45"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comments from his press secretary}}}\uc2  that the troop withdrawal does not mark a \u8220\'20\'1Cmission accomplished\u8221\'20\'1D moment for the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo, there\u8217\'20\'19s no mission accomplished,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe mission was accomplished in that we got \uc2 Osama bin Laden\uc2 , and terrorism is not emanating from that part of the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After taking several questions from reporters, Biden left the podium in the East Room, ending the event.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 As the US completes its withdrawal of troops from Afghanistan, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was asked whether he believes the last 20 years of fighting have been worthwhile.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know my record,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CI opposed permanently having American forces in Afghanistan.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrCNN's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KaitlanCollins}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CWere the last 20 years worth it?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 President Biden: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WEb2vTQ4ke"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/WEb2vTQ4ke}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1413205094829641733?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The president noted that \u8220\'20\'1Cno nation has ever unified Afghanistan,\u8221\'20\'1D but he argued the US had achieved its primary objectives in going to Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe went for two reasons. One, to bring \uc2 Osama bin Laden\uc2  to the gates of hell, as I said at the time. The second reason was to eliminate Al Qaida\u8217\'20\'19s capacity to deal with more attacks on the United States from that territory. We accomplished both of those objectives. Period.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden said the US military\u8217\'20\'19s accomplishments in Afghanistan made the troop withdrawal \u8220\'20\'1Cthe right decision and, quite frankly, overdue\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 After concluding his prepared remarks on Afghanistan, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took several questions from reporters about the US troop withdrawal.\par \par \uc2 Asked if he believed a \uc2 Taliban\uc2  takeover of Afghanistan was now inevitable, Biden said he did not.\par \par \uc2 enltrReporter: "Is a \uc2 Taliban\uc2  takeover of Afghanistan now inevitable?"\par \par \uc2 Pres. Biden: "No, it is not."\par \par \uc2 Watch the full answer: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/t1712nYGG9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/t1712nYGG9}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3SWmsQ1zoN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3SWmsQ1zoN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News (@ABC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABC/status/1413202372860469254?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The president argued the Afghan troops are well prepared and well equipped to resist \uc2 Taliban\uc2  advances.\par \par \uc2 Biden was also asked whether he trusted the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIs that a serious question?\u8221\'20\'1D Biden replied. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a silly question. Do I trust the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 ? No. But I trust the capacity of the Afghan military.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  offered assurances that the Afghan interpreters and others who assisted US troops will be provided protection by America.\par \par \uc2 The president said his administration is already working to arrange flights for those who provided aid to the US, and they have been offered special visas as well.\par \par \uc2 Biden told the Afghan interpreters, \u8220\'20\'1CThere is a home for you in the United States if you so choose, and we will stand with you just as you stood with us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 'I will not send another generation of Americans to war in Afghanistan,' Biden says\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  warned that remaining in Afghanistan would mean additional US casualties to continue a war started two decades ago.\par \par \uc2 The president noted that 2,448 Americans have been killed in the war in Afghanistan, and another 20,722 have been wounded.\par \par \uc2 Biden expressed appreciation for all the US troops who had given the ultimate sacrifice in Afghanistan and the many others who returned home with serious injuries, both physical and mental.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will not send another generation of Americans to war in Afghanistan with no reasonable expectation of achieving a different outcome,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden: "After 20 years, a trillion dollars spent training and equipping hundreds of thousands of Afghan national security and defense forces, 2,448 Americans killed, 20,722 more wounded...I will not send another generation of Americans to war in Afghanistan" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/e7c0k3YQfQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/e7c0k3YQfQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1413201957146316800?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  defended his decision to end the US military operation in Afghanistan, saying America\u8217\'20\'19s objectives in the mission had already been met.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe did not go to Afghanistan to nation-build,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd it\u8217\'20\'19s the right and the responsibility of the Afghan people alone to decide their future and how they want to run their country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president emphasized that the US would \u8220\'20\'1Ccontinue to provide civilian and humanitarian assistance\u8221\'20\'1D in Afghanistan, including defending the rights of the country\u8217\'20\'19s women and girls.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s remarks come as the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  makes advances in Afghanistan, which some senior Afghan officials have blamed on the abrupt departure of US troops.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden says Afghanistan withdrawal will end by August 31: 'Speed is safety'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now delivering his remarks on the US troop withdrawal from Afghanistan, after receiving a briefing on the operation from his national security team.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur military mission in Afghanistan will conclude on August 31,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The president had previously said the withdrawal would wrap up by September 11, but the Pentagon announced this week that more than 90% of the operation was already completed.\par \par \uc2 Biden said senior defense officials had told him that moving swiftly was the most effective method to protect US troops, and the president noted that no service members have been lost in the withdrawal process so far.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn this context, speed is safety,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Sam Levine reports:\par \par \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s top election official {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SecretaryHobbs/status/1412909800099176448/photo/2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  is asking}}}\uc2  the state\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general to investigate whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  and Kelly Ward, the chair of the Arizona GOP, committed a criminal offense by attempting to interfere in the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 The request from Arizona secretary of state \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 , a Democrat, comes after the Arizona Republic obtained telephone and text messages from Giulani and Ward in which the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azcentral.com/story/news/politics/elections/2021/07/02/records-show-trump-allies-kelli-ward-rudy-giuliani-pressured-county-officials-over-election-results/7813304002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two pressured officials}}}\uc2  in Maricopa county to try and get favorable results for Trump.\par \par \uc2 enltrLocal reporting recently uncovered intense efforts to interfere with the tabulation of ballots and canvass of the 2020 election in Maricopa County. In Arizona, interfering with election officials is a felony. Today, I asked {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GeneralBrnovich?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GeneralBrnovich}}}\uc2  to investigate. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qSFytrrll7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qSFytrrll7}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Secretary \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  (@SecretaryHobbs) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SecretaryHobbs/status/1412909800099176448?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 7, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 As votes were still being counted, Ward sent a Maricopa county supervisor a text message saying \u8220\'20\'1Cwe need you to stop the counting.\u8221\'20\'1D In December, Giuliani left a voicemail for another supervisor saying \u8220\'20\'1CI have a few things I\u8217\'20\'19d like to talk over with you. Maybe we can get this thing fixed up. You know, I really think it\u8217\'20\'19s a shame that Republicans sort of are both in this kind of situation. And I think there may be a nice way to resolve this for everybody.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump also tried to reach at least one Maricopa county supervisor from the White House.\par \par \uc2 In her letter, to attorney general \uc2 Mark Brnovich\uc2 , a Republican running for \uc2 US senate\uc2 , Hobbs requests a probe into whether those actions amounted to election interference.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CArizona law protects election officials from those who would seek to interfere with their sacred duties to ascertain and certify the will of the voters,\u8221\'20\'1D Hobbs, who is running for governor, wrote to Brnovich.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris announces $25 million DNC investment in voting rights campaign\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Sam Levine reports:\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  (Dnc) on Thursday launched a $25m expansion of the party\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to protect voting rights, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  announced Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The investment will expand the Dnc\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CI will vote\u8221\'20\'1D initiative and will focus on three areas: voter registration, voter education, and voter protection, including litigation to challenge voting restrictions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the fight of our lifetime,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said at \uc2 Howard University\uc2 , her alma mater, as she announced the initiative. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the fight of our nation\u8217\'20\'19s lifetime.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: We\u8217\'20\'19re proud to announce we\u8217\'20\'19re expanding our I Will Vote initiative. This $25 million investment will educate, register, turn out voters to the polls\u8212\'20\'14and more. We are fighting tooth and nail to protect the right to vote and stop Republican lawmakers\u8217\'20\'19 assault on our democracy.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Democrats (@TheDemocrats) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheDemocrats/status/1413185418091130880?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2 , the DNC chair, said in a statement, \u8220\'20\'1C Republicans know that their policies are unpopular\u8212\'20\'14and that the only way for them to hold on to power is to attack the constitutional right to vote, held by the people they swore to serve. That\u8217\'20\'19s why the Republican Party has made unprecedented efforts to keep people from voting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The announcement comes as Democrats have been unable to pass federal legislation to expand voting rights in Congress. Republicans have launched an aggressive effort, pushing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brennancenter.org/our-work/research-reports/voting-laws-roundup-may-2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hundreds of bills}}}\uc2  to make it harder to vote.\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, activists have publicly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/28/biden-democrats-voting-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expressed frustration}}}\uc2  that the White House and congressional Democrats aren\u8217\'20\'19t doing enough to match the Republican intensity around voting rights.\par \par \uc2 enltrLet me get this out right now. Just saying \u8220\'20\'1CI will vote\u8221\'20\'1D was not enough following slavery & Reconstruction; nor is it an adequate response to current historic systemic attacks on voting rights. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @VP}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenSchumer}}}\uc2  & {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DNC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @DNC}}}\uc2  have yet to demonstrate the \u8220\'20\'1Cfierce urgency of now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Cliff Albright (@cliff_notes) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cliff_notes/status/1412948298579726339?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , was also asked again about whether Jill Biden will attend the Tokyo Olympics.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said the White House is \u8220\'20\'1Cstill assessing the feasibility of the first lady attending\u8221\'20\'1D the games, which are scheduled to start on July 23.\par \par \uc2 Psaki\u8217\'20\'19s comment comes hours after organizers in Tokyo announced no spectators would be allowed at the games because of concerns about the potential spread of coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 The daily White House press briefing has now ended, and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will soon deliver remarks on the US troop withdrawal from Afghanistan. Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  was asked about this year\u8217\'20\'19s scheduled elections in Haiti, after the country\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Jovenel Mo\u239\'00\'EFse\uc2 , was assassinated yesterday.\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary said the Biden administration supports the elections moving forward this year, even as people on the ground in Haiti say elections are not possible because of the fearful environment there.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe stand by to provide assistance, to provide help in whatever way possible,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jul/08/haiti-reels-murder-president-police-hunt-assassins-jovenel-moise"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Haiti reels from murder of president as police hunt assassins}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Multiple reporters pressed \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  on whether \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  believes the war in Afghanistan was a mistake and that US troops should have left sooner.\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary repeatedly deflected the questions, instead saying that the president believes the US has met its objectives in Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs president of the United States, he\u8217\'20\'19s not here to give grades,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki told reporters.\par \par \uc2 The press secretary said Biden will explain his rationale for withdrawing US troops and ongoing assistance to the Afghan government in his remarks this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  justified \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s decision to withdraw all US troops from Afghanistan, saying the administration does not believe it is worth continuing the military operation there.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe is not going to ask another generation of kids to go and serve in Afghanistan in a war he does not think can be won militarily,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House press secretary said.\par \par \uc2 The president is scheduled to deliver remarks on the US withdrawal in about 30 minutes, amid accusations that American troops\u8217\'20\'19 departure has left Afghanistan vulnerable to \uc2 Taliban\uc2  advances.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 There will not be a \u8216\'20\'18mission accomplished\u8217\'20\'19 moment in Afghanistan, White House says\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said the US will be running flights out of Afghanistan to evacuate Afghan interpreters who helped American forces in recent years.\par \par \uc2 The interpreters are expected to be granted special immigration visas, due to concerns about how they may be punished by the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  as it makes advances in Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 enltrAhead of President Biden's address on Afghanistan troops withdrawal, Psaki says there won't be a "Mission Accomplished moment" for the war: "It's a 20-year war that has not been won militarily...We're not having a moment of celebration" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Bkl9Fdc4Nw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Bkl9Fdc4Nw}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mWQqpGGCty"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/mWQqpGGCty}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1413180900083478531?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Asked about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s remarks on the Afghanistan troop withdrawal this afternoon, Psaki said, \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not going to have a \u8216\'20\'18mission accomplished\u8217\'20\'19 moment in this regard. It\u8217\'20\'19s a 20-year war that has not been won militarily.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That remark seemed to be a reference to \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s infamous {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bostonglobe.com/news/nation/2018/04/14/bush-was-haunted-his-own-mission-accomplished/E73SdIkXxBfUGsbyXv7ISI/story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMission Accomplished\u8221\'20\'1D speech}}}\uc2  in 2003, in which he announced \u8220\'20\'1Cmajor combat operations in Iraq have ended\u8221\'20\'1D. That false pronouncement has been widely mocked in the 18 years since it was delivered.\par \par \uc2 The press secretary emphasized that this is not a \u8220\'20\'1Cmoment of celebration\u8221\'20\'1D but rather an opportunity to thank the US troops who have served in Afghanistan over the past 20 years.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , is now holding her daily briefing with reporters, and she provided an update on US efforts to ship coronavirus vaccine doses abroad.\par \par \uc2 Psaki announced that the US is sending 500,000 doses of the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  vaccine to Uruguay and 1.4 million doses of the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine to Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 That news comes about an hour before \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is scheduled to deliver remarks on the US troop withdrawal from Afghanistan, which is already more than 90% complete, according to the Pentagon.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said the president\u8217\'20\'19s remarks would focus on \u8220\'20\'1Cthe security challenges he inherited in Afghanistan\u8221\'20\'1D. She added, \u8220\'20\'1CThe status quo was not sustainable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Texas special session begins as Republicans push for voting restrictions\par \par \uc2 The partisan battle over voting rights and democracy in the US continues apace.\par \par \uc2 Texas is rapidly hurtling towards a showdown on voting rights as Republicans in the state are moving aggressively ahead with efforts to pass new voting restrictions in the state.\par \par \uc2 Today marks the start of a special session for the Texas legislature. Governor Greg Abbott, a Republican, has designated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gov.texas.gov/news/post/governor-abbott-announces-special-session-agenda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Celection integrity\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  as one of the items for the legislature to address.\par \par \uc2 The push comes after Texas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/02/texas-democrats-republican-voting-rights-assault-example"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats thwarted}}}\uc2  an earlier attempt to pass sweeping new restrictions.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/tlodocs/871/billtext/html/HB00003I.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new bill}}}\uc2  filed in the state House of Representatives revives many of the provisions in the earlier bill - it would impose new identification requirements on mail-in ballots, prohibit local election officials from sending out unsolicited mail-in ballots, empower poll watchers to have expanded access at the polls, create new regulations for 3rd party collection of absentee ballots, and prohibit 24 hour drive-thru voting.\par \par \uc2 Many of the regulations appear aimed at Harris County, the state\u8217\'20\'19s most populous, where election officials moved to expand voting access amid the pandemic last year.\par \par \uc2 Texas is already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://elections.mit.edu/#/data/map?view=state-profile&state=TX&year=2018"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of the hardest places to vote}}}\uc2  in the US and was among the states with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1h_2pR1pq8s_I5buZ5agXS9q1vLziECztN2uWeR6Czo0/edit#gid=2030096602"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lowest voter turnout}}}\uc2  in 2020. It also severely restricts mail-in voting to people who are age 65 or older, people with disabilities, and other few select groups.\par \par \uc2 The bill does not contain two significant provisions that were in the legislation that failed earlier this year. Those measures would have curtailed early voting on Sundays, a time traditionally utilized by Black voters, and allowed judges to more easily overturn elections.\par \par \uc2 Read all the special coverage: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/series/the-fight-to-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Fight to Vote}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Soon, Biden will offer his most extensive comments to date about the US withdrawal from Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 A British Royal Air Force Puma Helicopter flies over Kabul, the capital city of Afghanistan, during a routine transit between compounds within the city. As Operation TORAL, the UKs contribution to NATO Resolute Support, draws to a close, a small number of UK military personnel will temporarily remain to support the transition to a new phase. Photograph: UK Ministry of Defence/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 The US pullout is 90% complete, and is not only raising concerns about a civil war there but also drawing Republican criticism.\par \par \uc2 Reuters further reports:\par \par \uc2 A senior administration official said Biden will provide an update on US plans to move thousands of Afghan interpreters out of the country by the end of August....The Pentagon says the withdrawal of US forces is 90% complete.\par \par \uc2 Washington agreed to withdraw in a deal negotiated last year under Biden\u8217\'20\'19s Republican predecessor, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Biden overruled military leaders who wanted to keep a larger presence to assist Afghan security forces and prevent Afghanistan from becoming a staging ground for extremist groups.\par \par \uc2 Instead, the United States plans to leave 650 troops in Afghanistan to provide security for the US Embassy.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s order in April to pull out US forces by September 11 this year, after 20 years of conflict has coincided with major gains by the Islamist militant \uc2 Taliban\uc2  movement against overwhelmed Afghan forces after peace talks sputtered.\par \par \uc2 The commander of US troops in Afghanistan, General Austin Miller, warned last week that the country may be headed toward a civil war.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. intelligence community believes the Afghan military is weak and that the Kabul government\u8217\'20\'19s prospects for survival in the short term are not good, \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  sources familiar with official assessments said.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s administration is also grappling with its plan for expedited visas for Afghan people most at risk of being attacked by the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 , including translators who worked with foreign forces. Rights groups are pushing to add up to 2,000 vulnerable women to the list, and Biden is expected to mention women\u8217\'20\'19s rights in his remarks...Some Republicans are criticizing Biden for the pullout, although Trump had also sought to end American involvement in the war.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is under huge pressure to bring Afghan interpreters but also many other vulnerable people to the United States as soon as possible, post-US withdrawal, such as police officers trained by the US and women in leadership.\par \par \uc2 The US president is due to make public remarks around 1.45pm ET on the process of US troop withdrawal as the government seeks to end participation in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jul/04/afghanistan-americas-longest-war-ends-amid-accusations-of-betrayal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 America\u8217\'20\'19s longest war}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 enltrToday Biden will address his plan to evacuate thousands of Afghan interpreters amid the troop withdrawal & say he plans to start relocating them in August, according to a senior administration official.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaitlan Collins (@kaitlancollins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins/status/1413160116678021122?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 US troops did an alarming {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jul/02/us-troops-leave-afghanistans-bagram-air-base-after-nearly-20-years"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nighttime flit}}}\uc2  last week from Bagram, the sprawling airbase north of Kabul that was the symbolic and operational heart of the American military operation in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/afghanistan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Afghanistan}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Retired Major General James \u8220\'20\'1CSpider\u8221\'20\'1D Marks just told CNN he sees no outcome for Afghanistan in the near future other than civil war, with the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  surging to take control of vital chunks of the country but leaving enough of a vacuum that it creates \u8220\'20\'1Ca breeding ground for terrorism\u8221\'20\'1D, creating an awful sense of deja vu.\par \par \uc2 As my colleague Emma Graham-Harrison {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jul/07/taliban-attack-city-as-us-ramps-up-afghanistan-withdrawal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports from Kabul}}}\uc2 , the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/taliban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taliban}}}\uc2  fought their way into the centre of a key Afghan city yesterday and accepted the surrender of senior security officials, as militants and Afghan government representatives met in Iran for negotiations.\par \par \uc2 And from the UK side of things, as my colleague \uc2 Dan Sabbagh{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jul/02/us-troops-leave-afghanistans-bagram-air-base-after-nearly-20-years"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports today}}}\uc2  from London, prime minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  has announced the end of Britain\u8217\'20\'19s military mission in Afghanistan, too, following a hasty and secretive exit of the last remaining troops 20 years after the post September 11, 2001, invasion that started the west\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cwar on terror\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Johnson confirmed to Members of Parliament that the intervention, which claimed the lives of 457 British soldiers, would end even as the insurgent \uc2 Taliban\uc2  were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jul/07/taliban-attack-city-as-us-ramps-up-afghanistan-withdrawal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rapidly gaining territory}}}\uc2  in rural areas, as UK, US and other forces withdrew.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, a \uc2 Twitter\uc2  intervention which is ruffling journalists\u8217\'20\'19 feathers, from former military top brass HR McMaster, who was heavily involved in the conflicts in Afghanistan and Iraq and served as national security adviser to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrUS media is finally reporting on the transformation of Afghanistan after their disinterest and defeatism helped set conditions for capitulation and a humanitarian catastrophe. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0YV7P0VjgG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/0YV7P0VjgG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 H.R. McMaster (@LTGHRMcMaster) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LTGHRMcMaster/status/1413135773814071300?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Delta variant is 'surging' in low-vaccination areas, CDC director says\par \par \uc2 Jeff Zients, the coordinator of the White House pandemic response team, acknowledged that new cases of coronavirus will likely increase as the Delta variant spreads.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at the response team\u8217\'20\'19s press briefing this morning, Zients emphasized that the country would see \u8220\'20\'1Cfewer hospitalizations and deaths\u8221\'20\'1D from the new cases because of the coronavirus vaccines.\par \par \uc2 Zients reminded Americans that getting vaccinated is the most effective way to \u8220\'20\'1Cprotect themselves, their loved ones and their communities\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrDr. \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2 , citing research on the COVID vaccine: \u8220\'20\'1CPlease, get vaccinated. It will protect you against the surging of the Delta variant.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4GgotCZ7iX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4GgotCZ7iX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1413158399303462915?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Dr Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , the director of the Centers for Disease Control, noted that the Delta variant has now become {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jul/08/joe-biden-us-troop-withdrawal-afghanistan-covid-coronavirus-politics-latest?page=with:block-60e701a28f08d0b6a57c3fc5#block-60e701a28f08d0b6a57c3fc5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the dominant variant}}}\uc2  of the virus in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAlthough we expected the Delta variant to become the dominant strain in the United States, this rapid rise is troubling,\u8221\'20\'1D Walensky said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know that the Delta variant has increased transmissibility, and it is currently surging in pockets of the country with low vaccination rates.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2 , the president\u8217\'20\'19s chief medical adviser, presented data indicating the coronavirus vaccines provide effective protection against the Delta variant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPlease get vaccinated,\u8221\'20\'1D Fauci said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt will protect you against the surging of the Delta variant.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 A group of prominent communications specialists has urged Democrats to go on the offensive against Republican and right-wing disinformation, by creating a year-round campaign to sell Democratic Party achievements and combat lies told to the American public.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medium.com/@PersuasionUSA/c50f5115a05c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a public letter}}}\uc2  to the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  and Democratic funders, the communications experts warned that the right-wing is successfully pushing regular \u8220\'20\'1Cpurposeful and highly effective disinformation attacks across digital media\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 By contrast, the experts said, Democrats and the left is suffering from a \u8220\'20\'1Clack of competitive counter-measures of sufficient scale\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 and risk allowing the right-wing to dominate the narrative and cement conspiracy theories among Americans which will hamper Democrats come election time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CStop waiting until the last minute to persuade Americans about the issues that decide elections. Build campaign infrastructure that is always-on, rather than stood up and taken down between election cycles,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Persuasion USA Coalition, which is made up of former creative director at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://moveon.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MoveOn.org}}}\uc2  Laura Dawn, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://frontpagelive.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Front Page Live}}}\uc2  CEO Stacy Whittle, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MeidasTouch?ref_src=twsrc%5Egoogle%7Ctwcamp%5Eserp%7Ctwgr%5Eauthor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Meidas Touch}}}\uc2  founder Ben Meiselas, among others.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe lack of consistent, long-term messaging and media campaigns between election cycles continues to be one of the most critical gaps in communications capabilities - a gap that contributed to the razor thin outcome in 2020, a gap that is giving bad actors in the disinformation opposition a competitive edge as 2022 approaches, and a gap that may be one of the primary reasons why the great United States slides towards autocracy in 2024.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The group said Democrats need to build long-term marketing strategies that \u8220\'20\'1Clook beyond the next election and plan ahead decade by decade towards the country we hope to have 30 years from now\u8221\'20\'1D, to tackle a \u8220\'20\'1Cone-sided advantage that favors purveyors of untruths\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s not abandon millions of the hearts and minds of this nation to weaponized disinformation,\u8221\'20\'1D Persuasion USA Coalition wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CThe time has come for funders, decision-makers, and even corporations to spend more money and resources on programs that bridge echo chambers and bring all of us, black, white or brown, closer together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Surfside condo building collapse death toll rises to 60\par \par \uc2 The death toll in the Surfside condo building collapse has risen to 60, after search crews recovered additional bodies at the site.\par \par \uc2 Of the 60 confirmed victims, 35 have been identified, Miami-Dade county mayor \uc2 Daniella Levine Cava\uc2  said at a press conference this morning.\par \par \uc2 Two hundred people have been accounted for, and 80 people remain potentially unaccounted for, \uc2 Levine Cava\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe number of confirmed deaths in the Surfside condo collapse is now 60, Miami-Dade mayor says.\par \par \uc2 200 people are accounted for and 80 are potentially unaccounted for. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/poaebn6ODX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/poaebn6ODX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1413142179015319560?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The update comes one day after rescue efforts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/08/miami-condo-collapse-surfside-rescue-efforts-end"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 came to an official close}}}\uc2 . Local officials had determined they would not find any additional survivors in the rubble.\par \par \uc2 The rescue teams held a somber moment of silence at the site of the building collapse yesterday as their efforts shifted to a recovery mission, honoring the victims of the disaster.\par \par \uc2 enltrIn tribute to lives lost, our rescue teams held a moment of silence & prayer near the Surfside building collapse. With heavy hearts, we begin search & recovery efforts, and will continue to give our all as our commitment still remains to reunite families with their loved ones. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FJ7GKWXhXn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/FJ7GKWXhXn}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Miami-Dade Fire Rescue (@MiamiDadeFire) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MiamiDadeFire/status/1412932111930175497?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tokyo Olympics to be held without spectators\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/justinmccurry"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justin McCurry}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/seaningle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sean Ingle}}}\uc2  report:\par \par \uc2 Olympic organisers have decided to ban spectators from the Tokyo Games after Japan\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister declared a state of emergency in the host city.\par \par \uc2 The news was confirmed by the Olympic minister, \uc2 Tamayo Marukawa\uc2 , following talks between the government, organisers and Olympic and paralympic representatives - although he left open the possibility that some venues outside Tokyo could still have fans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVenues in Tokyo will not include spectators,\u8221\'20\'1D said Marukawa. \u8220\'20\'1CFor those areas where the state of emergency is not implemented... we will discuss.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The widely expected move is the latest blow to the troubled Olympics, delayed by a year because of the pandemic and plagued by a series of setbacks, including massive budget overruns.\par \par \uc2 But Japan\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, Y oshihide Suga, said it was essential to prevent Tokyo from becoming the source of another wave of infections, especially with the highly infectious Delta Covid-19 variant spreading.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2021/jul/08/tokyo-to-be-put-under-state-of-emergency-for-duration-of-2020-olympic-games"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Spectators banned from Olympics as Tokyo Covid emergency declared}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 A CNN reporter spotted defense secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  arriving at the White House for the Situation Room meeting on the Afghanistan withdrawal.\par \par \uc2 enltrDefense Secretary Austin arrives ahead of today\u8217\'20\'19s Situation Room meeting on Afghanistan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0DQB0cEvfP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/0DQB0cEvfP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kevin Liptak (@Kevinliptakcnn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Kevinliptakcnn/status/1413138541073235972?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 8, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will receive an update on the troop withdrawal from their national security team, and the president will then deliver remarks on the operation this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Amid concerns about the Delta variant of coronavirus spreading rapidly among unvaccinated Americans, public health experts warn the variant is already more dominant than data suggests.\par \par \uc2 Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/07/08/delta-coronavirus-variant-widespread-498787"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The more-transmissible Delta coronavirus variant is believed to be significantly more widespread than the current federal projections, according to two senior Biden administration health officials with knowledge of the situation.\par \par \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  data released late Tuesday shows the Delta strain accounted for more than 51 percent of new Covid-19 cases from June 20 to July 3. But the reality on the ground is likely much higher because states and private labs are taking weeks to report testing results to the CDC, the officials said.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It is everywhere now,\u8217\'20\'19 one of the officials said, adding that recent data shows the Pfizer Covid vaccine works well against the Delta variant. \u8216\'20\'18The risk really is in the unvaccinated community. We\u8217\'20\'19re starting to see more and more people get sick and need medical attention.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, \uc2 Dr Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , said last week that there are about 1,000 US counties where less than 30% of the community is vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese communities, primarily in the Southeast and Midwest, are our most vulnerable,\u8221\'20\'1D Walensky said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs the Delta variant continues to spread across the country, we expect to see increased transmissions in these communities, unless we can vaccinate more people now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fears of new US Covid surge as Delta spreads\par \par \uc2 More than nine out of 10 Americans who died from Covid-19 in the US in June were unvaccinated, according to \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a statistic that health officials say is especially concerning given the prevalence of vaccine hesitancy in some regions and the rise of the Delta variant.\par \par \uc2 Maryland reported this week that 100% of those who died from coronavirus there in June had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/local/covid-maryland-unvaccinated-cases-deaths/2021/07/06/400bf08a-de86-11eb-ae31-6b7c5c34f0d6_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not been vaccinated}}}\uc2 , while more than 93% of those with new cases or who were hospitalized were similarly unprotected.\par \par \uc2 Cases are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coronavirus.jhu.edu/data/new-cases-50-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rising}}}\uc2  in nearly half the states as low vaccination rates are being met with the more transmissible and severe Delta or B.1.617.2, variant, identified in India in December 2020.\par \par \uc2 Vaccinations administered in the US have shown to be effective against the Delta variant, though it poses serious risks to those who remain unvaccinated.\par \par \uc2 The variant is already the dominant strain of Covid-19 in the country, accounting for more than 50% of all new US cases and up to 80% of cases in some regions, according to \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://covid.cdc.gov/covid-data-tracker/#variant-proportions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data}}}\uc2  released Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/08/fears-of-new-us-covid-surge-as-delta-spreads-and-many-remain-unvaccinated"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fears of new US Covid surge as Delta spreads and many remain unvaccinated}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  did not provide reporters a preview of his remarks on Afghanistan yesterday, as he toured McHenry County College in Crystal Lake, Illinois, to promote his infrastructure proposals.\par \par \uc2 When reporters repeatedly pressed Biden last week on the US military\u8217\'20\'19s unexpected departure from Bagram air base north of Kabul, the president became agitated, trying to bring attention back to the strong June jobs report.\par \par \uc2 enltrNOW - Biden on Afghanistan: "I want to talk about happy things, man!" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PuZyebqAFv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/PuZyebqAFv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Disclose.tv ?? (@disclosetv) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/disclosetv/status/1410981518701477899?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want to talk about happy things, man,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said last Friday, just before US Independence Day.\par \par \uc2 He added moments later, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m concerned that you guys are asking me questions that I\u8217\'20\'19ll answer next week. But this is a holiday weekend. I\u8217\'20\'19m going to celebrate it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  has announced the end of Britain\u8217\'20\'19s military mission in Afghanistan following a hasty and secretive exit of the last remaining troops 20 years after the post 9/11 invasion that started the \u8220\'20\'1Cwar on terror\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The prime minister confirmed to MPs that the intervention, which claimed the lives of 457 British soldiers, would end even as the insurgent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jul/07/taliban-attack-city-as-us-ramps-up-afghanistan-withdrawal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taliban have been rapidly gaining territory}}}\uc2  in rural areas as UK and other forces withdraw.\par \par \uc2 Speaking in the Commons, Johnson confirmed that \u8220\'20\'1Call British troops assigned to Nato\u8217\'20\'19s mission in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/afghanistan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Afghanistan}}}\uc2  are now returning home\u8221\'20\'1D. While he would not disclose the exact timetable of the departure for security reasons, the prime minister added: \u8220\'20\'1CI can tell the house that most of our personnel have already left.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a separate defence briefing, the head of the armed forces, Sir \uc2 Nick Carter\uc2 , acknowledged that recent news from Afghanistan had been \u8220\'20\'1Cpretty grim\u8221\'20\'1D but said the Afghan military had been regrouping to defend urban areas.\par \par \uc2 While it was \u8220\'20\'1Cfair to say the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  now hold nearly 50% of the rural districts in Afghanistan\u8221\'20\'1D and that the Afghan army would also \u8220\'20\'1Cno longer have access to [western] air power\u8221\'20\'1D from within the country, he said he hoped there would eventually be peace talks between the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  and the Afghan government.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2021/jul/08/boris-johnson-announces-end-uk-military-mission-afghanistan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Boris Johnson announces end to UK military mission in Afghanistan}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to speak on Afghanistan amid criticism of US troop withdrawal\par \par \uc2 Greetings from Washington, live blog readers.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will deliver remarks on Afghanistan today, as the US military moves quickly to withdraw all troops from the country.\par \par \uc2 The president and the vice-president will first meet with their national security team this morning to receive an update on the withdrawal process, and Biden will then deliver his speech in the afternoon.\par \par \uc2 According to the White House, the president\u8217\'20\'19s remarks will touch on the troop withdrawal as well as \u8220\'20\'1Congoing security and humanitarian assistance to the Afghan National Defense and Security Forces (ANDSF) and the Afghan people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Afghan National Army keep watch after the US forces left Bagram airfield in the north of Kabul, Afghanistan. Photograph: Anadolu Agency/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech comes amid criticism of the troop withdrawal from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jul/06/afghan-anger-over-uss-sudden-silent-bagram-departure"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some senior Afghan officials}}}\uc2 , who argue the operation has been rushed to fit a political timeline, leaving the country vulnerable to \uc2 Taliban\uc2  advances.\par \par \uc2 The Pentagon said Tuesday that the withdrawal process is already more than 90% complete, about two months ahead of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s September 11 deadline to remove all US troops from Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 Reporters will likely press Biden on that criticism after he delivers his prepared remarks this afternoon, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210708eh78001xk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
