\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Progressive groups urge US media to \u8216\'20\'18prioritize accuracy\u8217\'20\'19 in culture war topics\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 659 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 July 2021\par 18:19 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Coalition of immigration, gun reform, LGBTQ+ and reproductive rights groups band together to create \u8216\'20\'18guiding principles\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 A coalition of progressive advocacy organizations are urging journalists to challenge charged rhetoric in a document they\u8217\'20\'19re describing as \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tellthewholestorynow.com/guiding-principles/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 guiding principles}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D to cover so-called culture war issues without amplifying misinformation.\par \par \uc2 Groups who specialize in immigration, gun reform, LGBTQ+ and reproductive rights banded together in the effort, saying it was frequently difficult to counter the volume of misleading statements on a one-on-one basis.\par \par \uc2 The coalition came out of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prochoiceamerica.org/2020/06/15/naral-pro-choice-america-releases-media-analysis-evaluating-abortion-news-coverage/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report released}}}\uc2  by the organization previously known as the National \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Reproductive Rights Action League, now known as Naral Pro-Choice America, which found just 11% of news reports about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cfeatured a real woman\u8217\'20\'19s story\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith the supreme court gearing up to hear a direct challenge to Roe, we must ensure that the media has the tools necessary to accurately cover this case, and the issue of reproductive freedom more broadly,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kristin Ford, Naral Pro-Choice America\u8217\'20\'19s acting vice-president of communications and research, about the landmark 1973 case Roe v Wade.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2020/may/22/aka-jane-roe-documentary-norma-mccorvey"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  provided women in the US the right to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This year, the court took up a case called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/18/us-supreme-court-abortion-test-case-mississippi-precedent"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization}}}\uc2  that could fundamentally challenge that precedent.\par \par \uc2 Presently, women have the legal right to opt for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until the fetus can live outside the womb, generally understood to be 24 weeks gestation. About six in 10 Americans believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2021/06/17/key-facts-about-the-abortion-debate-in-america/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pew Research Center}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate, obstetricians and gynecologists have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/jun/05/abortion-doctors-fetal-heartbeat-bills-language-misleading"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 long lamented}}}\uc2  the misuse of medical terms, especially as Republicans have passed increasingly extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans termed \u8220\'20\'1Cheartbeat bills\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Such bans would make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegal before most women know they are pregnant, around six weeks gestation. None have gone into effect because they are unconstitutional per legal precedent set by Roe.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/apr/25/the-anti-abortion-crusader-hopes-her-heartbeat-law-will-test-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 homophobic lobbyist}}}\uc2  coined the term \u8220\'20\'1Cheartbeat bill\u8221\'20\'1D to focus attention on the moment when fetal cardiac activity is detected, but before an embryo develops a functioning heart. In 2019, the Guardian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/jun/07/abortion-the-guardian-style-guide"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 changed its style guide}}}\uc2  to reflect that \u8220\'20\'1Cheartbeat bill\u8221\'20\'1D was a misleading term for state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 Groups said similar situations have played out across immigration, gun violence prevention and LGBTQ+ rights. Naral Pro-Choice America partnered with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://giffords.org/lawcenter/gun-laws/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Giffords Law Center to Prevent Gun Violence}}}\uc2 , the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thetaskforce.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 National LGBTQ Task Force}}}\uc2  and the immigration advocacy group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://unitedwedream.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 United We Dream}}}\uc2  in the effort.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn a world where there is so much misinformation, and so many new voices who can proactively get misinformation out there, we thought it was important to highlight the way misinformation is getting out there,\u8221\'20\'1D said Brian Wesolowski, communications director for the Giffords Law Center, a gun violence prevention advocacy group.\par \par \uc2 In other cases, news coverage has actively endangered migrants, some of whom flee persecution, or has allowed politicians to purposefully misgender trans people to advance anti-transgender legislation.\par \par \uc2 In gun violence prevention, Wesolowski said the media often failed to note large majorities of Americans support proposals such as universal background checks. In another example, large majorities of both gun owners and non-gun owners oppose allowing people to carry a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/24/texas-unlicensed-handgun-carry-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 concealed weapon without a permit or training}}}\uc2 , according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2017/06/22/key-takeaways-on-americans-views-of-guns-and-gun-ownership/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pew}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe gun rights movement has gotten far more extremist,\u8221\'20\'1D said Wesolowski. \u8220\'20\'1CThe voices we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing in so much news really [are] just not a reflection of the majority of Americans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ford said the groups\u8217\'20\'19 partnership shows the urgency of challenging misinformation cuts across policy areas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not alone in this fight,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ford. \u8220\'20\'1CBy partnering with leading LGBTQ, immigration and gun violence prevention groups, we are presenting a unified front to say that it is long past time to prioritize accuracy and inclusion in media coverage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210707eh77001e4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
