\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 New York City mayoral race: Eric Adams wins Democratic primary \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh in Oakland and Joan E Greve in Washington \par \uc2 8,662 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 July 2021\par 23:59 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Former police captain leads by nearly 8,500 votesPresident wanted 70% of adults at least partially vaccinated by 4 July1,000 US counties where less than 30% of people are vaccinatedThe anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists gaining ground on the right\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.59am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  outlined his administration\u8217\'20\'19s renewed efforts to reach unvaccinated Americans. The president said in a speech this afternoon that the White House would expand door-to-door outreach efforts and partner with local pharmacies and doctors\u8217\'20\'19 offices to convince hesitant Americans to get their shot. \u8220\'20\'1CThe bottom line is: the virus is on the run, and America is coming back, and we\u8217\'20\'19re coming back together,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut our fight against this virus is not over.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * More than 90% of the US withdrawal from Afghanistan is now complete, the Pentagon said in a statement today. Afghan officials have complained that the withdrawal is being carried out too quickly to accommodate a politically motivated schedule, leaving the country vulnerable to \uc2 Taliban\uc2  attacks.\par \par \uc2 * The Pentagon announced it is dropping its $10bn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2019/oct/26/microsoft-wins-pentagons-10bn-cloud-computing-contract"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cloud-computing contract}}}\uc2  with \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 . The \u8220\'20\'1CJedi\u8221\'20\'1D cloud contract had caused controversy during \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidency. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  filed a lawsuit over \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  winning the contract, alleging that Trump had interfered in the process because of his animosity toward \uc2 Amazon\uc2  founder \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2 , who also owns the Washington Post.\par \par \uc2 * Today marks six months since the Capitol insurrection. The anniversary comes as some of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jul/06/joe-biden-covid-coronavirus-vaccines-us-politics-live?page=with:block-60e462d58f08d660ba38ba9f#block-60e462d58f08d660ba38ba9f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 working to deny}}}\uc2  the reality of that violent day, which resulted in five deaths.\par \par \uc2 * The death toll in the Surfside condo building collapse rose to 32, after four more bodies were recovered. Local officials said 113 people remain potentially unaccounted for, as search and rescue teams brace for heavy rains from Tropical Storm Elsa that could affect the disaster site.\par \par \uc2 * In the Democratic primaries for the New York mayoral race, former police captain Eric Adams has a lead of 1% over Kathryn Garcia, according to the latest count of ballots. The Associated Press has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/ny-state-wire-government-and-politics-9c564828a29831747f9c2e6f52daf55e?utm_campaign=SocialFlow&utm_source=Twitter&utm_medium=AP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared}}}\uc2  Adams the winner of the race. The unusual election began amid the pandemic and marked a major test of the system of ranked-choice voting. The race was marred by a vote tallying debacle, which led to an erroneous tally on 29 June before being corrected.\par \par \uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 Joan E Greve and Maanvi Singh\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.46am BST\par \par \uc2 The election results have not been finalized, though Adams appears to be the likely winner.\par \par \uc2 The unusual election began amid the pandemic and marked a major test of the system of ranked-choice voting. The race was marred by a vote tallying debacle, which led to an erroneous tally on 29 June before being corrected.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.41am BST\par \par \uc2 AP: Eric Adams wins New York Democratic mayoral primary\par \par \uc2 In the Democratic primaries for the New York mayoral race, former police captain Eric Adams has a lead of 1% over Kathryn Garcia, according to the latest count of ballots. The Associated Press has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/ny-state-wire-government-and-politics-9c564828a29831747f9c2e6f52daf55e?utm_campaign=SocialFlow&utm_source=Twitter&utm_medium=AP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared}}}\uc2  Adams the winner of the race.\par \par \uc2 Adams leads Garcia by nearly 8,500 votes in the first mayoral race decided by ranked-choice voting. Adams also beat out \uc2 Maya Wiley\uc2 , the legal adviser who had the support of progressives including representative Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe preliminary RCV round by round elimination report 2 is now live! Please visit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/y3JRuS6TiB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/y3JRuS6TiB}}}\uc2  We thank you for your patience.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NYC Board of Elections (@BOENYC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BOENYC/status/1412541738321907712?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 6, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.47am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.32am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The spirit of our ancestry\u8217\'20\'19: how California\u8217\'20\'19s Black Wall Streets are changing their cities\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/abene-clayton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Like hundreds of other shopping districts, Sacramento\u8217\'20\'19s Florin Square had to shut its doors during the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 The space in California\u8217\'20\'19s state capital is part cultural center and incubator and has been home to Black entrepreneurs since 2003. At the mercy of Covid-19 closures, evolving guidelines and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/26/minority-owned-firms-pandemic-covid-toll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 elusive}}}\uc2  government aid, many similar operations failed to recover, with an estimated 200,000 more small businesses shuttering in 2020 than in the average year.\par \par \uc2 But, amazingly, out of more than 60 mostly Black-owned businesses in Florin Square, only one had to close for good. The hub\u8217\'20\'19s owner, Tom Donaldson, says this feat is due to its unique approach to entrepreneurship, which has earned Florin Square the title of Sacramento\u8217\'20\'19s Black Wall Street.\par \par \uc2 Donaldson and his marketing manager, Aaron Boyce, say their goal was always to balance \u8220\'20\'1Ctough love\u8221\'20\'1D and high expectations with a grace and guidance rarely afforded to Black business owners.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe systems in this country create roadblocks to success but not only did our tenants survive the pandemic, they also found a way to thrive and prosper,\u8221\'20\'1D said Donaldson.\par \par \uc2 One of the first things Donaldson did was waive his penalties for late rent payments and look for grants to help struggling businesses. Boyce also helped people increase their online presences.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe get entrepreneurs coming to us with all kinds of stories about why things in their business aren\u8217\'20\'19t working out, but if they\u8217\'20\'19re not able to serve the community we have to give them some tough love,\u8221\'20\'1D Boyce said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut it\u8217\'20\'19s all a part of the incubation process.\u8217\'20\'19\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Florin Square is just one of dozens of such districts in the US \u8211\'20\'13 from Denver, Colorado, to Baton Rouge, Louisiana \u8211\'20\'13 established to support Black entrepreneurs and develop commercial and cultural corridors for Black businesses.\par \par \uc2 Last summer\u8217\'20\'19s reckoning with racism and inequality has put many of the central issues Black Wall Streets seek to address at the center of the national conversation. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/06/09/economy/black-owned-banks/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Black-owned banks}}}\uc2  have seen huge investment and can now \u8220\'20\'1Cleverage that into $1.5bn to serve minority communities\u8221\'20\'1D, Robert E James II, chair of the National Bankers Association, told CNN Business recently. Elsewhere, as the #BuyBlack hashtag circulated on social media, US states added directories of Black businesses to their tourism websites and banks promised to address decades of economic racism.\par \par \uc2 All of this comes in the 100th anniversary year of the massacre in Tulsa, Oklahoma\u8217\'20\'19s Greenwood community, home to the best-known Black Wall Street. Greenwood, and the dozens of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/in-depth/opinion/2021/05/30/discrimination-urban-renewal-killed-black-wall-streets-outside-tulsa/5031417001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 other}}}\uc2  Black Wall Streets that were born during the early 20th century, have long served as aspirational examples of cooperative economics among Black people, who have been shut out of US financial institutions for generations.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/06/black-wall-street-california-sacramento-san-francisco"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The spirit of our ancestry\u8217\'20\'19: how California\u8217\'20\'19s Black Wall Streets are changing their cities}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.04am BST\par \par \uc2 On the six-month anniversary of the 6 January attack on the capitol, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said the breach was \u8220\'20\'1Ca sad reminder that there is nothing guaranteed about our democracy\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden said:\par \par \uc2 Not even during the Civil War did insurrectionists breach our Capitol, the citadel of our democracy. But six months ago today, insurrectionists did. They launched a violent and deadly assault on the people\u8217\'20\'19s house, on the people\u8217\'20\'19s representatives, and on the \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  sworn to protect them, as our duly elected Congress carried out the sacred ritual of our republic and certified the Electoral College vote.\par \par \uc2 This was not dissent. It was disorder. It posed an existential crisis and a test of whether our democracy could survive\u8212\'20\'14a sad reminder that there is nothing guaranteed about our democracy.\par \par \uc2 The capitol police today released {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uscp.gov/media-center/press-releases/after-attack-future-us-capitol-police"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a list}}}\uc2  of reforms and policy changes in an effort to be better prepared in the future, and to support officers who responded to the attack, including ramping up training and expanding officers\u8217\'20\'19 access to trauma counseling and spiritual support services.\par \par \uc2 But as my colleague David Smith {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/06/republicans-effort-to-deny-the-capitol-attack-is-working-and-its-dangerous"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  this morning, Republicans have spent the past six months denying and downplaying the attack:\par \par \uc2 Six months on from the mayhem on 6 January, when a mob of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  supporters stormed the heart of American democracy to disrupt the confirmation of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election victory, Republicans and rightwing media have variously attempted to downplay the attack or blame it on leftwing infiltrators and the \uc2 FBI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Interviews with diehard Trump fans suggest that the riot denialism is working. Many refuse to condemn the insurrectionists who beat police officers, smashed windows and called for then Vice-President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  to be hanged. The swirl of conspiracy theories, combined with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s deluded claims of a stole election, raise fears of a replay that could be even more violent.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRightwing media and some Republicans, including Republicans in the Senate and the House, are trying to make it seem as though what was a siege on the Capitol was not actually a siege on the Capitol,\u8221\'20\'1D said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fordham.edu/info/24277/ma_in_elections_and_campaign_management_faculty/6866/monika_l_mcdermott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Monika McDermott,}}}\uc2  a political science professor at Fordham University in New York.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Senate minority leader, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , told constituents that the $1.9tn American Rescue Plan, which he opposed and which Democrats passed almost entirely along party lines, means, \u8220\'20\'1Cyou\u8217\'20\'19re going to get a lot more money\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Democrats have seized on the moment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNot a single member of my party voted for it,\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell said of the relief package that passed in March. \u8220\'20\'1CSo, you\u8217\'20\'19re going to get a lot more money. I didn\u8217\'20\'19t vote for it. But you\u8217\'20\'19re going to get a lot more money. Cities and counties in Kentucky will get close to $700 or $800m. If you add up the total amount that will come into our state, $4bn. That\u8217\'20\'19s twice what we sent in last year.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, Andrew Bates, shared a clip of McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s comments, made today at an event in Kentucky.\par \par \uc2 enltrWhat he said. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LeaderMcConnell?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @LeaderMcConnell}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CI didn\u8217\'20\'19t vote for [the ARP], but you\u8217\'20\'19re going to get a lot more money. Cities and counties in Kentucky will get close to $700 or $800 million. If you add up the total amount that will come into our state, $4 billion.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/A0MZcMOBMA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/A0MZcMOBMA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Bates (@AndrewJBates46) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewJBates46/status/1412488863654756355?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 6, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 McConnell has vowed to oppose Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 efforts to pass legislation via budget reconciliation - and has successfully blocked efforts to pass a broader infrastructure plan and voting rights reform \u8211\'20\'13 and said he plans to oppose any additional covid relief efforts.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.01am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Delta variant rapidly gaining ground in US west as vaccination rates stagnate\par \par \uc2 Public health authorities across the US west are sounding the alarm that the Delta variant, a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jul/03/joe-biden-coronavirus-covid-delta-variant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hyper-transmissible}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D form of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/coronavirus-outbreak"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Covid-19}}}\uc2  responsible for about 25% of new US infections, is rapidly gaining significant ground.\par \par \uc2 These concerns come amid stagnating vaccination rates in some communities, spurring still more concerns about heightened transmission.\par \par \uc2 In California, the Delta variant is on the rise, accounting for 35.6% of specimens sequenced that are categorized as \u8220\'20\'1Cvariants of concern\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cvariants of interest\u8221\'20\'1D as of 21 June, up from 5.6% in May, according to the state\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdph.ca.gov/Programs/CID/DCDC/Pages/COVID-19/COVID-Variants.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 public health department}}}\uc2 . Covid-19 cases have surged in excess of 20% in California since the state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/15/california-reopening-covid-19-restrictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lifted the majority of coronavirus restrictions}}}\uc2  on 15 June, with the Delta variant spurring the greatest proportion of new cases, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sfchronicle.com/health/article/Delta-variant-in-Bay-Area-This-is-not-a-good-16289983.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 San Francisco Chronicle}}}\uc2 ,\par \par \uc2 Authorities in Los Angeles county said that the Delta variant was responsible for almost half of genetically sequenced variants, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/07/01/us/what-to-know-about-the-delta-variant-in-california.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 . The county\u8217\'20\'19s public health guidance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.ph.lacounty.gov/phcommon/public/media/mediapubhpdetail.cfm?prid=3206"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  on 28 June that it \u8220\'20\'1Cstrongly recommends\u8221\'20\'1D masking indoors \u8211\'20\'13 regardless of vaccination status \u8211\'20\'13 due to increased circulation of the Delta variant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have enough risk and enough unvaccinated people for Delta to pose a threat to our recovery, and masking up now could help prevent a resurgence in transmission,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Barbara Ferrer\uc2 , the county\u8217\'20\'19s public health director, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2021-07-06/california-delta-variant-spread-impact-masks-vaccines"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quoted}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Los Angeles Times\uc2  as saying.\par \par \uc2 Grant Colfax, the San Francisco public health department director, said of the Delta variant: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s like Covid on steroids.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s about 30% of cases locally right now,\u8221\'20\'1D the San Francisco Chronicle quoted Colfax as saying. \u8220\'20\'1CWithin just a few months, we expect it to be over 90% of our cases.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Officials have repeatedly said that the surge in the Delta variant is all the more reason to get vaccinated. Almost 70% of Californians age 12 and older are partially or fully vaccinated, but some {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/02/covid-cases-northern-california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rural counties}}}\uc2  lag behind.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jul/06/delta-variant-infections-us-west-vaccines"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Delta variant rapidly gaining ground in US west as vaccination rates stagnate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Bureau of Land Management\uc2  pick grilled over 30-year old protest\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/mike-jordan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike Jordan}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s pick to lead the \uc2 Bureau of Land Management\uc2  is in danger of failing to be confirmed, over her involvement in an ecological protest more than 30 years ago which Republican senators say marks her as an environmental extremist.\par \par \uc2 Tracy Stone-Manning is currently a senior adviser at the \uc2 National Wildlife Federation\uc2 . She acknowledges that in early 1989 she borrowed a typewriter to copy an anonymous letter given to her by environmental activists who claimed to have driven hundreds of metal spikes into trees in the Clearwater national forest, in Idaho.\par \par \uc2 Her purpose in typing and mailing a copy of the letter to the authorities, Stone-Manning testified when the matter came to court, was to warn the \uc2 US Forest Service\uc2  that anyone attempting to cut down trees in the forest would be in danger of harm.\par \par \uc2 Stone-Manning testified against the activists who claimed to have spiked the trees, after law enforcement raided student housing. Her testimony resulted in federal convictions for two people.\par \par \uc2 Stone-Manning has risen to political prominence in Montana. Before joining the \uc2 National Wildlife Federation\uc2 , she was chief of staff for the former Montana governor Steve Bullock and also worked for Democratic senator Jon Tester.\par \par \uc2 A Republican senator from Wyoming, \uc2 John Barrasso\uc2 , has emerged as a leading opponent to Stone-Manning\u8217\'20\'19s nomination for the \uc2 Bureau of Land Management\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.energy.senate.gov/2021/6/barrasso-tracy-stone-manning-lied-to-the-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling for Biden to withdraw it}}}\uc2  and alleging she lied to the Senate about her involvement in the tree-spiking incident.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTracy Stone-Manning collaborated with eco-terrorists who had booby trapped trees with metal spikes,\u8221\'20\'1D a Barrasso statement read. \u8220\'20\'1CShe mailed the threatening letter for them and she was part of the cover-up. She did not cooperate with investigators until she was caught.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bill Cassidy\uc2  of Louisiana, another Republican, said Stone-Manning\u8217\'20\'19s political affiliations were of concern.\par \par \uc2 At her confirmation hearing, Stone-Manning encountered heavy questioning by Republicans regarding a role on the board of directors of Montana Conservation Voters, a nonprofit which claims to be nonpartisan but which endorsed Bullock\u8217\'20\'19s unsuccessful Senate run against the Republican Steve Daines last year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCan you speak from your heart?\u8221\'20\'1D Cassidy asked. \u8220\'20\'1CBecause it seems like your heart is that you really don\u8217\'20\'19t particularly care for Republicans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Tester praised Stone-Manning, calling her \u8220\'20\'1Ca good person that has a good heart\u8221\'20\'1D and who understands the value of public lands.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would not be here today, introducing her, if I thought she was the person that you described,\u8221\'20\'1D Tester told Barrasso.\par \par \uc2 Jeff Fairchild, who served time in prison for his role in the tree-spiking incident, has defended Stone-Manning. In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/climate-environment/2021/07/04/student-tracy-stone-manning-sent-letter-behalf-eco-saboteurs-its-now-complicating-her-chance-lead-bureau-land-management/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview with the Washington Post}}}\uc2 , he called her \u8220\'20\'1Ca bridge builder\u8221\'20\'1D and a moderating voice against activities that could distract from resolving environmental disagreements.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/06/tracy-stone-manning-bureau-of-land-management-nomination-protest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s Bureau of Land Management pick grilled over 30-year old protest}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Report: Republic National Committee systems breached by Russian hackers\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s computer systems were breached by Russian hackers, Bloomberg reports, based on two anonymous sources.\par \par \uc2 From {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2021-07-06/russian-state-hackers-breached-republican-national-committee?sref=ylv224K8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  William Turton and Jennifer Jacobs:\par \par \uc2 The government hackers were part of a group known as APT 29 or Cozy Bear, according to the people. That group has been tied to \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s foreign intelligence service\uc2  and has previously been accused of breaching the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  in 2016 and of carrying out a supply-chain cyberattack involving \uc2 SolarWinds Corp\uc2 ., which infiltrated nine \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  agencies and was disclosed in December.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not known what data the hackers viewed or stole, if anything. An RNC spokesman on Tuesday denied its systems were breached and referred to a statement citing IT provider \uc2 Synnex Corp\uc2 . released on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Microsoft\uc2  informed us that one of our vendors, \uc2 Synnex\uc2 , systems may have been exposed,\u8221\'20\'1D Mike Reed, a spokesman for the RNC, said in the earlier statement. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no indication the \uc2 RNC\uc2  was hacked or any \uc2 RNC\uc2  information was stolen. We are investigating the matter and have informed DHS and the \uc2 FBI\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Maanvi Singh, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  outlined his administration\u8217\'20\'19s renewed efforts to reach unvaccinated Americans. The president said in a speech this afternoon that the White House would expand door-to-door outreach efforts and partner with local pharmacies and doctors\u8217\'20\'19 offices to convince hesitant Americans to get their shot. \u8220\'20\'1CThe bottom line is: the virus is on the run, and America is coming back, and we\u8217\'20\'19re coming back together,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut our fight against this virus is not over.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * More than 90% of the US withdrawal from Afghanistan is now complete, the Pentagon said in a statement today. Afghan officials have complained that the withdrawal is being carried out too quickly to accommodate a politically motivated schedule, leaving the country vulnerable to \uc2 Taliban\uc2  attacks.\par \par \uc2 * The Pentagon announced it is dropping its $10bn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2019/oct/26/microsoft-wins-pentagons-10bn-cloud-computing-contract"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cloud-computing contract}}}\uc2  with \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 . The \u8220\'20\'1CJedi\u8221\'20\'1D cloud contract had caused controversy during \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidency. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  filed a lawsuit over \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  winning the contract, alleging that Trump had interfered in the process because of his animosity toward \uc2 Amazon\uc2  founder \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2 , who also owns the Washington Post.\par \par \uc2 * Today marks six months since the Capitol insurrection. The anniversary comes as some of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jul/06/joe-biden-covid-coronavirus-vaccines-us-politics-live?page=with:block-60e462d58f08d660ba38ba9f#block-60e462d58f08d660ba38ba9f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 working to deny}}}\uc2  the reality of that violent day, which resulted in five deaths.\par \par \uc2 * The death toll in the Surfside condo building collapse rose to 32, after four more bodies were recovered. Local officials said 113 people remain potentially unaccounted for, as search and rescue teams brace for heavy rains from Tropical Storm Elsa that could affect the disaster site.\par \par \uc2 Maanvi will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 News from Ohio, via the Associated Press:\par \par \uc2 The Ohio supreme court has announced it will not consider an appeal over the firing of a white police officer who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/cities/2019/nov/22/tamir-rice-killed-police-theaster-gates-black-artist-gazebo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shot and killed 12-year-old Tamir Rice}}}\uc2  outside a Cleveland recreation center in 2014.\par \par \uc2 The appeal was filed in April by the Cleveland Police Patrolment\u8217\'20\'19s Association on behalf of former officer Timothy Loehmann. Cleveland fired Loehmann in 2017 not for killing Tamir, who was Black, but for providing false information on his job application. An arbitrator and a county judge upheld his firing.\par \par \uc2 A state appellate court earlier this year dismissed \uc2 Loehmann\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  appeal, citing the union\u8217\'20\'19s failure to serve notice on outside attorneys hired by the city.\par \par \uc2 Loehmann, a rookie, shot Tamir within seconds of a cruiser skidding to a stop near {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/cities/2019/nov/22/tamir-rice-killed-police-theaster-gates-black-artist-gazebo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a gazebo where the child had been sitting}}}\uc2 . Officers responded to a call from a man who said someone was waving a gun around. The man also told a dispatcher the gun could be a fake and the person might be a juvenile.\par \par \uc2 A state grand jury declined to indict Loehmann in Tamir\u8217\'20\'19s shooting and, in December, federal authorities announced they would not bring federal criminal charges.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C I am glad that Loehmann will never have a badge and gun in Cleveland again,\u8221\'20\'1D Tamir\u8217\'20\'19s mother, Samaria Rice, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 More on Tamir Rice and other similar cases, here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/aug/24/police-killings-families-ramarley-graham-terence-crutcher-tamir-rice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 'Our dad is dead': the families left behind after police shootings}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 In case you missed it earlier today: the Problem Solvers Caucus, a bipartisan group in Congress, came out in favor of the bipartisan infrastructure framework.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn light of the bipartisan, bicameral genesis of the framework, we encourage an expeditious, stand-alone vote in the House and thank our bipartisan Senate partners and the Biden Administration for working so closely with us to demonstrate that cooperation is still possible in Washington,\u8221\'20\'1D the caucus said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The caucus\u8217\'20\'19 support means that Democrats can likely afford to lose the votes of some progressives, who have voiced reservations about the framework, and still pass the plan. Those progressives have argued the framework does not adequately address the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has already indicated his support for the framework, and he is traveling to Illinois tomorrow to promote the proposal, as lawmakers scramble to translate the framework into an actual bill.\par \par \uc2 Congressional leaders have signaled they want to pass the bill by the end of the month, but much work remains to be done to meet that goal.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are also working to quickly craft a reconciliation package, which would enact elements of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s American Jobs Plan and American Families Plan that did not make it into the bipartisan proposal.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 More than 90% of US withdrawal from Afghanistan is complete, Pentagon says\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Emma Graham-Harrison in Kabul and Peter Beaumont report:\par \par \uc2 US forces plunged their main operating base in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/afghanistan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Afghanistan}}}\uc2  into darkness and abandoned it to looters when they slipped away in the middle of the night after two decades at the site without notifying their Afghan allies.\par \par \uc2 The furtive departure from Bagram airbase, which is vital to the security of Kabul and holds about 5,000 mostly \uc2 Taliban\uc2  prisoners, infuriated the Afghans. Many saw it as emblematic of a withdrawal they say is being carried out entirely to fit an American political schedule, with no heed for the collapsing security situation on the ground.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople are saying: \u8216\'20\'18The Americans didn\u8217\'20\'19t ask Afghans about coming here, and they didn\u8217\'20\'19t consult Afghans about leaving\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D said one senior official.\par \par \uc2 Much of northern Afghanistan, once an anti-\uc2 Taliban\uc2  stronghold, has fallen to the group in the last two weeks, and the militants have made substantial advances across the rest of the country. Afghanistan has just over 400 districts, and the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  now hold nearly half, and are fighting for many more.\par \par \uc2 With Bagram and its two runways no longer in American hands, the main US mission in Afghanistan is in effect over already. The Pentagon said in a statement on Tuesday that the withdrawal was more than 90% completed.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jul/06/afghan-anger-over-uss-sudden-silent-bagram-departure"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Afghan anger over US\u8217\'20\'19s sudden, silent Bagram departure}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 As part of the Biden administration \u8217\'20\'19s new efforts to reach unvaccinated Americans, the White House is partnering with 42,000 local pharmacies, as well as family doctors and pediatricians, to convince people to get their shot.\par \par \uc2 The administration has also encouraged employers to give their workers paid time off to get vaccinated, and it is expanding mobile clinic efforts to make the vaccines more accessible than ever.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at the White House moments ago, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said, \u8220\'20\'1CThink about where you were last year, where you are today. What you were able to do last year at this time and do today. It\u8217\'20\'19s a year of hard-fought progress. We can\u8217\'20\'19t get complacent now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took one question from reporters after finishing his prepared remarks on his administration\u8217\'20\'19s renewed outreach efforts to get more Americans vaccinated against coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 Asked about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/jul/06/kaseya-ransomware-hackers-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the latest ransomware attack}}}\uc2  that affected hundreds of businesses around the world, Biden said he was briefed on the incident this morning and was told it caused \u8220\'20\'1Cminimal damage to US businesses\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Biden added that his administration is still gathering information on the incident, noting he would have more to say on the matter \u8220\'20\'1Cin the next several days\u8221\'20\'1D. With that, Biden walked away from the podium.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  emphasized that getting vaccinated is the \u8220\'20\'1Cbest thing you can do to protect yourself and your family,\u8221\'20\'1D as the delta variant of coronavirus spreads across the US.\par \par \uc2 The president celebrated the progress his administration has made in getting people vaccinated, but he warned that millions of eligible Americans have not yet gotten their shot.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s finish the job \u8212\'20\'14 finish it together,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said as he wrapped up his prepared remarks.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  lamented that younger Americans seem particularly reluctant to get vaccinated, putting them more at risk of contracting the delta variant of coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 The president noted that the delta variant is now responsible for almost half of new coronavirus cases in many parts of the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSeems to me, it should cause everyone to think twice,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said of the delta variant.\par \par \uc2 Encouraging all eligible Americans to get vaccinated as soon as possible, the president said, \u8220\'20\'1CDo it now, for yourself and for the people you care about.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden outlines new steps to reach unvaccinated Americans: 'Our fight against this virus is not over'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now delivering remarks on his administration\u8217\'20\'19s plans to launch targeted outreach efforts in communities with lower rates of vaccination against coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 Celebrating his administration\u8217\'20\'19s vaccination efforts so far, Biden said at the White House, \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re closer than ever to declaring our independence from this deadly virus.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president noted that more than 160 million Americans will be vaccinated by the end of this week, just a few days after the July 4 deadline that Biden set for that milestone.\par \par \uc2 New coronavirus cases and deaths are also down 90% since January, allowing Americans to start \u8220\'20\'1Cliving their lives as they did before,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe bottom line is: the virus is on the run, and America is coming back, and we\u8217\'20\'19re coming back together,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut our fight against this virus is not over.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The White House said earlier today that it would expand door-to-door outreach efforts in communities with lower vaccination efforts. The administration is also working to deliver more vaccine doses to primary care doctors and pediatricians, so Americans can get their shot from their own physicians.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will soon deliver remarks on his administration\u8217\'20\'19s ongoing efforts to vaccinate more Americans against coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has already said it will launch more targeted outreach efforts in communities with lower vaccination rates, amid concerns about the spread of the delta variant of the virus.\par \par \uc2 The president also just received a briefing from members of his coronavirus response team, including chief medical adviser \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2  and CDC director \uc2 Rochelle Walensky\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Hillbilly Elegy author turned Republican Ohio Senate candidate JD Vance has apologised for a former political position: critic of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLike a lot of people, I criticised Trump back in 2016,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance told Fox News. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I ask folks not to judge me based on what I said in 2016, because I\u8217\'20\'19ve been very open that I did say those critical things and I regret them, and I regret being wrong about the guy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vance\u8217\'20\'19s need to address the subject came out of good digging by CNN, which unearthed deleted tweets. However, Vance\u8217\'20\'19s dislike of Trump and intent to vote for the independent conservative Evan McMullin was widely known in 2016.\par \par \uc2 As Hillbilly Elegy surged up the charts, for example, Vance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mattklewis.com/matt-lewis-and-the-news/jd-vance/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke to}}}\uc2  the journalist Matt Lewis.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe reason, ultimately, that I am not\u8221\'20\'1D a Trump voter, he said, \u8220\'20\'1Cis because I think that [Trump] is the most-raw expression of a massive finger pointed at other people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Of course, back then Trump did not have a stranglehold on the Republican party of the kind which meant anyone running for office as a Republican anywhere had to kiss the ring to stand any chance of winning a nomination.\par \par \uc2 Full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/06/hillbilly-elegy-jd-vance-trump-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hillbilly Elegy author JD Vance sorry for since-deleted anti-Trump tweets}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pentagon drops controversial 'Jedi' cloud contract\par \par \uc2 The Pentagon has announced it has dropped {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2019/oct/26/microsoft-wins-pentagons-10bn-cloud-computing-contract"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a $10bn cloud-computing contract}}}\uc2  with \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  that caused a huge political kerfuffle when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was in the White House, over the question of whether Trump intervened to steer the contract away from \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , the owner of the Washington Post.\par \par \uc2 The Department of Defense said on Tuesday the contract for the Joint Enterprise Defense Infrastructure \u8211\'20\'13 or Jedi, Star Wars fans \u8211\'20\'13 no longer met its needs.\par \par \uc2 Microsoft{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2019/oct/26/microsoft-wins-pentagons-10bn-cloud-computing-contract"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won}}}\uc2  the contract in 2019 \u8211\'20\'13 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/jul/09/amazon-microsoft-war-cloud-pentagon-contract-battle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amazon sued to block it}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a statement not light on defenseworld {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2017/jan/25/george-orwell-donald-trump-kellyanne-conway-1984"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newspeak}}}\uc2 , John Sherman, acting DoD chief information officer, said: \u8220\'20\'1CJedi was developed at a time when the department\u8217\'20\'19s needs were different and both the CSPs technology and our cloud conversancy was less mature. In light of new initiatives like JADC2 and AI and Data Acceleration (ADA), the evolution of the cloud ecosystem within DoD, and changes in user requirements to leverage multiple cloud environments to execute mission, our landscape has advanced and a new way-ahead is warranted to achieve dominance in both traditional and non-traditional warfighting domains.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CThe department intends to seek proposals from a limited number of sources, namely the \uc2 Microsoft Corporation\uc2  (\uc2 Microsoft\uc2 ) and \uc2 Amazon Web Services\uc2  (AWS), as available market research indicates that these two vendors are the only Cloud Service Providers (CSPs) capable of meeting the Department\u8217\'20\'19s requirements.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s an in-depth read on \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s move into the defense industry:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/jan/31/amazon-defense-cloud-computing-pentagon-jeff-bezos"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 From books to bullets: inside Amazon's push to 'defend' America}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said the administration does not currently plan to set any new goals in terms of administering coronavirus vaccines.\par \par \uc2 The US failed to reach \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s goal of having 70% of American adults at least partially vaccinated by July 4. About 67% of US adults have received at least one vaccine dose as of today.\par \par \uc2 The administration is now launching more targeted outreach efforts in communities with lower vaccination rates, and the president will deliver a speech outlining those plans in a speech this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 The White House press briefing has now concluded.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Asked about the crafting of the reconciliation package, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said this week will include \u8220\'20\'1Ca lot of behind-the-scenes bill-writing\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Clong nights and lots of coffee\u8221\'20\'1D for Democratic staffers on Capitol Hill.\par \par \uc2 Democratic congressional leaders hope to include many elements of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s American Jobs Plan and American Families Plan in the package.\par \par \uc2 A number of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s proposals were not included in the bipartisan infrastructure framework, and the reconciliation package is a second chance to enact those policies.\par \par \uc2 Because the bill will be passed via reconciliation, Democrats will not need to attract any Republican support in order to get the legislation to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s desk.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will convene an interagency meeting tomorrow to address the administration\u8217\'20\'19s ongoing efforts to respond to ransomware attacks.\par \par \uc2 The meeting follows a series of high-profile ransomware attacks on major companies, which have been blamed on groups based in Russia.\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary also said that \u8220\'20\'1Ca high level of our national security team\u8221\'20\'1D has been in touch with senior Russian officials to engage in discussions about preventing such attacks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the Russian government cannot or will not take action against criminal actors residing in Russia, we will take action or reserve the right to take action on our own,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 enltrPsaki says "high level" of U.S. national security has been in touch with top Russian officials about $70 million ransomware attack by a Russia-linked hacking group\par \par \uc2 She says if Russia doesn't take action against cyber criminals residing there, "we will" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6096ZKXN39"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/6096ZKXN39}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GLhelp2Wyg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GLhelp2Wyg}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1412463413490503680?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 6, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  confirmed an earlier {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/saudi-prince-khalid-bin-salman-brother-of-crown-prince-to-visit-washington-11625260545"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wall Street Journal report}}}\uc2  that national security adviser Jake Sullivan will meet with Saudi Arabia\u8217\'20\'19s deputy defense minister in Washington this week.\par \par \uc2 The Saudi deputy defense minister, \uc2 Prince Khalid bin Salman\uc2 , is the son of Saudi Arabia\u8217\'20\'19s King Salman and a younger brother of Saudi Crown Prince \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has implicated the crown prince in the 2018 killing of dissident journalist Jamal Khashoggi, and Psaki indicated that issue could possibly come up during the Saudi official\u8217\'20\'19s meeting with Sullivan.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  gave some details on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s trip tomorrow to Crystal Lake, Illinois, saying he will promote the bipartisan infrastructure framework.\par \par \uc2 The press secretary said Biden will also explain the need to enact his American Families Plan, which congressional Democrats hope to pass via reconciliation, meaning they will not have to get any Republican support to approve the proposal.\par \par \uc2 Biden has made several trips in recent weeks to promote his infrastructure plans, most recently traveling to La Crosse, Wisconsin, last week.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , is now holding her daily briefing, and she opened her remarks with a preview of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s speech this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said the president will outline the administration\u8217\'20\'19s reinvigorated efforts to get more Americans vaccinated against coronavirus, which she said is critically important because \u8220\'20\'1Cfully vaccinated people are protected against the Delta variant\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The press secretary explained that the administration is launching door-to-door outreach efforts in communities with lower vaccination rates and working to get more doses to primary care doctors and pediatricians in those communities.\par \par \uc2 Psaki also announced that the US is shipping 1.5 million doses of the Moderna coronavirus vaccine to Guatemala and 2 million doses of the Moderna vaccine to Vietnam, confirming an earlier report.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will deliver an update this afternoon on his administration\u8217\'20\'19s ongoing efforts to vaccinate more Americans against coronavirus. The update comes after the country missed Biden\u8217\'20\'19s goal of having 70% of Americans adults at least partially vaccinated by July 4. A senior administration official said the president will outline the White House\u8217\'20\'19s plans to launch targeted outreach efforts in communities with lower vaccination rates.\par \par \uc2 * Today marks six months since the Capitol insurrection. The anniversary comes as some of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s supporters are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jul/06/joe-biden-covid-coronavirus-vaccines-us-politics-live?page=with:block-60e462d58f08d660ba38ba9f#block-60e462d58f08d660ba38ba9f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 working to deny}}}\uc2  the reality of that violent day, which resulted in five deaths.\par \par \uc2 * The death toll in the Surfside condo building collapse rose to 32, after four more bodies were recovered. Local officials said 113 people remain potentially unaccounted for, as search and rescue teams brace for heavy rains from Tropical Storm Elsa that could affect the disaster site.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US continues to distribute more coronavirus vaccines to other nations, with 2 million doses being shipped to Vietnam today.\par \par \uc2 AFP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.msn.com/en-us/news/world/us-sends-vietnam-2-mn-covid-vaccine-doses/ar-AALPrQS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The Moderna vaccine shipment -- part of a first 80 million doses that President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has pledged to allocate worldwide -- should arrive in Vietnam this weekend, a White House official, who spoke on condition of anonymity, told AFP.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18This is just the beginning of doses being shipped to southeast Asia,\u8217\'20\'19 the official said.\par \par \uc2 A million doses went to Malaysia on Monday and last week the White House announced delivery \u8216\'20\'18soon\u8217\'20\'19 of four million doses to Indonesia.\par \par \uc2 Biden had initially pledged to ship 80 million vaccine doses abroad by the end of June, but the White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fortune.com/2021/06/21/biden-falls-short-covid-19-vaccine-sharing-goal-white-house/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fell short}}}\uc2  of that goal.\par \par \uc2 Jeff Zients, the coordinator of the White House pandemic response team, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/07/01/politics/us-covid-vaccines-global/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said on Friday}}}\uc2  that the White House was working to deliver tens of millions of additional doses over the next couple of months.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 The journalist Nikole Hannah-Jones said on Tuesday she will join \uc2 Howard University\uc2 , a prominent historically black college in Washington, as its Knight chair in race and journalism, turning down a similar position at \uc2 University of North Carolina-Chapel Hill\uc2  even though it reversed a controversial decision to deny her tenure.\par \par \uc2 Howard has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/education/2021/07/06/howard-nikole-hannah-jones-tanehisi-coates/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also}}}\uc2  appointed the award-winning writer Ta-Nehisi Coates as writer-in-residence.\par \par \uc2 Hannah-Jones is a journalist for the New York Times best known for creating the Pulitzer-winning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2019/08/14/magazine/1619-america-slavery.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1619 Project}}}\uc2 , which focuses on the place of slavery in American history.\par \par \uc2 She has been at the center of a tense fight in academia since the UNC board of trustees denied her tenure, despite her having the support of faculty and students.\par \par \uc2 Hannah-Jones was offered a five-year contract at the UNC Hussman School of Journalism and Media that did not initially include tenure.\par \par \uc2 In her first interview about the controversy, Hannah-Jones told \uc2 CBS\uc2  on Tuesday every Knight chair before her at UNC \u8220\'20\'1Creceived that position with tenure\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is my alma mater,\u8221\'20\'1D she said of UNC. \u8220\'20\'1CI love the university \u8230\'20\'26 it was embarrassing to be the first person to be denied tenure. It was embarrassing, and I didn\u8217\'20\'19t want this to become a public scandal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/06/nikole-hannah-jones-howard-university-rejecting-unc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nikole Hannah-Jones joins Howard University after rejecting UNC role}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Surfside death toll rises to 32 after four more victims recovered\par \par \uc2 The death toll in the Surfside condo building collapse has risen to 32, after rescue crews discovered four more bodies in the rubble.\par \par \uc2 Miami-Dade County mayor \uc2 Daniella Levine Cava\uc2  announced the news at a press conference this morning, noting that 113 people remain potentially unaccounted for.\par \par \uc2 enltrLATEST from Surfside building collapse:\par \par \uc2 - Four more victims recovered\par \par \uc2 - Death toll rises to 32; 26 identified\par \par \uc2 - 191 people accounted for\par \par \uc2 - 113 potentially unaccounted for\par \par \uc2 Read more: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3X2kcOrSwu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/3X2kcOrSwu}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ugldhxKs0X"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ugldhxKs0X}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News (@ABC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABC/status/1412416743352459276?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 6, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Of those 113 people, detectives have only been able to confirm that 70 of them were definitely in the building when it collapsed, so that number may change as investigation efforts continue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe continue to urge all of the families who are missing loved ones to please reach out and connect with us so that our detectives can file missing persons reports with the police, and we want to confirm every single account,\u8221\'20\'1D Levine Cava said.\par \par \uc2 The press conference came as local officials braced for potentially heavy rains from Tropical Storm Elsa, which could complicate the search and rescue efforts.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/06/tropical-storm-elsa-latest-florida-hurricane-watch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tropical Storm Elsa lashes Florida Keys as conditions worsen}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protesters lined blocks along a four-lane thoroughfare called Indian School Road in Phoenix, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2 , enduring the suck of whooshing cars and blistering late June desert heat to advocate for their cause \u8211\'20\'13 effectively, theocracy in America.\par \par \uc2 Rising temperatures promised a sweaty, nauseous apex of 104F for the protest in front of Camelback Family Planning and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic. Their ranks were defined by gruesome and bloody signs, some taller than the protesters who held them, a microphone and an amplifier.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a slaughterhouse!\u8221\'20\'1D a man\u8217\'20\'19s voice growled. Some protesters leaned into car windows going into the clinic parking lot. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is unnatural for a mother to do this to a child!\u8221\'20\'1D one cried.\par \par \uc2 This is the national conference for Operation Save America (OSA), one in a network of extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups gaining increasing sway with rightwing lawmakers. In some sense, they\u8217\'20\'19re not news \u8211\'20\'13 their homophobic, transphobic, Islamophobic, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/AbortionFront/videos/4140170639358267"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 misogynist}}}\uc2  leadership has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/inside-anti-abortion-underground-187894"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 harassed \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  providers}}}\uc2  for decades.\par \par \uc2 But, like the world around them, they\u8217\'20\'19ve evolved.\par \par \uc2 Once at the fringes, but moving into legislative efforts are protesters like these, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cabolitionists\u8221\'20\'1D who advocate for women and doctors to be prosecuted under murder statutes. Their name is an appropriation of a term used by anti-slavery organizers before the American civil war.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/06/anti-abortion-activists-operation-save-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It shakes you to your core\u8217\'20\'19: the anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  extremists gaining ground on the right}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 In his remarks this afternoon, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will also note that nearly 160 million Americans are expected to be fully vaccinated against coronavirus by the end of the week.\par \par \uc2 As of today, 157.3 million Americans are fully vaccinated, representing 47.4% of the total population, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://covid.cdc.gov/covid-data-tracker/#vaccinations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Biden had previously set a goal of having 160 million Americans fully vaccinated by US independence day on July 4, but the country fell short of that objective.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to outline renewed vaccination outreach efforts amid concerns about delta variant\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will use his speech this afternoon to outline five major areas where his administration is doubling down on community outreach efforts to get more Americans vaccinated, a senior administration official said.\par \par \uc2 The White House official said, \u8220\'20\'1CAfter the President is briefed by his COVID-19 response team, he will speak to the American people about the strong progress that the country has made in recovery because of its robust vaccination campaign, as well as the importance of every eligible American getting vaccinated, especially as the Delta variant continues to grow among unvaccinated people across the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The official noted that Biden will describe how his administration is continuing to work with state and local leaders \u8220\'20\'1Cto get more Americans vaccinated by making vaccines available in more health care settings, and respond to hotspots\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Specifically, the White House is working to distribute more vaccine doses to primary care doctors and pediatricians, so local leaders in the medical community can directly explain the benefits of the vaccines to their patients.\par \par \uc2 The administration is also expanding targeted community outreach efforts, mobile vaccine clinics and vaccination sites at workplaces to make it as easy as possible for Americans to get their shot.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic congressman Andy Kim, who famously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/asian-america/behind-viral-photo-rep-andy-kim-cleaning-midnight-after-riots-n1253519"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cleaned the halls of Congress}}}\uc2  after the January 6 insurrection, is donating the suit he wore that day to the \uc2 Smithsonian Institution\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a \uc2 Twitter\uc2  thread, Kim described how he wore the suit on January 6 to celebrate Democrats flipping the Senate, after their two victories in the Georgia runoff races.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI bought it to be a suit of celebration, and I thought what better way to give the suit meaning than to wear it when I confirm the electoral college and then later to the inauguration,\u8221\'20\'1D Kim said.\par \par \uc2 enltr6 months ago today I wore this blue suit as I cleaned the Capitol after the insurrection, now I just donated it to the Smithsonian. Jan6 must never be forgotten. While some try to erase history, I will fight to tell the story so it never happens again. Here is one story\u8230\'20\'26(THREAD) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GKePd1ZMrr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GKePd1ZMrr}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andy Kim (@AndyKimNJ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndyKimNJ/status/1412399056090021889?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 6, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Kim noted that he only wore the suit one more time after January 6 -- when he voted to impeach \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for incitement of insurrection on January 13. After that, he could barely bring himself to even look at the suit.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the following days, I started to receive thousands of cards from across the country,\u8221\'20\'1D Kim said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey talked about the blue suit. The suit meant something different to them than it did to me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kim said he hoped the suit would be one piece of an exhibit that tells the truth of January 6, as many Trump supporters try to deny the reality of that violent day.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI told the Smithsonian yes to donating the blue suit because the telling of the story of [January 6] isn\u8217\'20\'19t optional, it is necessary,\u8221\'20\'1D Kim said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot heal as a nation unless we have truth. Let truth be truth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrIn the following days, I started to receive thousands of cards from across the country. Many from kids. Strangers who wanted to tell me how they felt when they saw the photo of me. They talked about the blue suit. The suit meant something different to them than it did to me.7/17 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5BCe6VJaH7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5BCe6VJaH7}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andy Kim (@AndyKimNJ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndyKimNJ/status/1412399075895414785?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 6, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Six months after January 6, Republican efforts to deny the Capitol attack are working\par \par \uc2 It has been described as America\u8217\'20\'19s darkest day since the terrorist attacks of September 11, 2001. But whereas 9/11 is solemnly memorialised in stone, a concerted effort is under way to airbrush {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/06/trump-mob-capitol-clash-police-washington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the US Capitol insurrection}}}\uc2  from history.\par \par \uc2 Six months on from the mayhem on 6 January, when a mob of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  supporters stormed the heart of American democracy to disrupt the confirmation of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election victory, Republicans and rightwing media have variously attempted to downplay the attack or blame it on leftwing infiltrators and the \uc2 FBI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Interviews with diehard Trump fans suggest that the riot denialism is working. Many refuse to condemn the insurrectionists who beat police officers, smashed windows and called for then Vice-President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  to be hanged. The swirl of conspiracy theories, combined with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s deluded claims of a stole election, raise fears of a replay that could be even more violent.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRightwing media and some Republicans, including Republicans in the Senate and the House, are trying to make it seem as though what was a siege on the Capitol was not actually a siege on the Capitol,\u8221\'20\'1D said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fordham.edu/info/24277/ma_in_elections_and_campaign_management_faculty/6866/monika_l_mcdermott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Monika McDermott,}}}\uc2  a political science professor at Fordham University in New York.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe all saw it. We saw them breaking down doors. We saw our members of Congress running for cover and trying to get away. We saw \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  being shuttled out of the chamber. All of these frightening things that we saw happen are now being denied or being or being laid at the feet of Antifa or the \uc2 FBI\uc2  or some other source, which just seems at this point ludicrous.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/06/republicans-effort-to-deny-the-capitol-attack-is-working-and-its-dangerous"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 effort to deny the Capitol attack is working \u8211\'20\'13 and it\u8217\'20\'19s dangerous}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jeff Zients, the coordinator of the White House pandemic response team, acknowledged that lower vaccination rates among younger Americans contributed to the US missing its July 4 vaccination goal.\par \par \uc2 enltrOn the White House missing its July Fourth vaccination goal, COVID-19 response coordinator Jeff Zients tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MarthaRaddatz?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @MarthaRaddatz}}}\uc2  young adults "have felt less vulnerable to the disease," adding they were made eligible for the vaccine later as well. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/j3J01CTcMy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/j3J01CTcMy}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3sOnuibc6Y"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3sOnuibc6Y}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 This Week (@ThisWeekABC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ThisWeekABC/status/1412069718958161922?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 5, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Speaking to ABC News on Sunday, Zients said the country still had \u8220\'20\'1Ca lot to celebrate\u8221\'20\'1D for its independence day, noting that 67% of American adults have received at least one vaccine dose.\par \par \uc2 He went on to say, \u8220\'20\'1CYounger people, particularly those in their 20\u8217\'20\'19s, have felt less vulnerable to the disease and therefore less eager to get shots.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Zients noted the dangers for unvaccinated Americans as the delta variant spreads, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to continue to vaccinate everyone, particularly young people, because what we know is, if you are vaccinated, you\u8217\'20\'19re protected. And if you\u8217\'20\'19re not vaccinated, you\u8217\'20\'19re not protected. And that\u8217\'20\'19s particularly important for everyone, including young people, in light of the delta variant.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But according to a recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/vaccine-hesitant-americans-reject-delta-variant-risk-posing/story?id=78609691"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ABC News/Washington Post poll}}}\uc2 , 74% of unvaccinated Americans say they will not get a shot.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 In his address over the weekend to mark US independence day, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  urged all Americans to get vaccinated as quickly as possible, arguing it is the \u8220\'20\'1Cpatriotic\u8221\'20\'1D thing to do.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe all know powerful variants have emerged, like the Delta variant, but the best defense against these variants is to get vaccinated,\u8221\'20\'1D the president told an audience at the White House, where invited frontline workers gathered to celebrate the holiday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy fellow Americans, it\u8217\'20\'19s the most patriotic thing you can do. So, please, if you haven\u8217\'20\'19t gotten vaccinated, do it. Do it now for yourself, for your loved ones, for your community, and for your country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech came as vaccination rates lag in many Republican-led states that he did not win in November, intensifying concerns that political polarization is affecting the country\u8217\'20\'19s pandemic response.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Edward Helmore reports:\par \par \uc2 Several Republican governors with lagging vaccine rates in their states have urged residents to accept the shots as the Biden administration comes under pressure to reopen US borders to overseas visitors.\par \par \uc2 The Arkansas governor, Asa Hutchinson, West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Jim Justice and \uc2 Spencer Cox\uc2  of Utah warned against vaccine hesitancy, which some disease experts, including the White House chief medical adviser, \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2 , said could create {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jul/02/trump-organization-charges-politics-joe-biden-washington-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Ctwo types of America\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are in a race,\u8221\'20\'1D Hutchinson said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://transcripts.cnn.com/TRANSCRIPTS/2107/04/sotu.01.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  on CNN\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union on Sunday.}}}\uc2  About {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coronavirus.jhu.edu/vaccines/us-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 32% of people in Arkansas}}}\uc2  are fully vaccinated, compared with 47.9% nationwide, according to \uc2 Johns Hopkins University\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIf we stopped right here, and we didn\u8217\'20\'19t get a greater per cent of our population vaccinated, then we\u8217\'20\'19re going to have trouble in the next school year and over the winter.\u8221\'20\'1D The solution, he said, \u8220\'20\'1Cis the vaccinations\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/vaccine-rollout-slows-younger-population-remains-unvaccinated/story?id=78654008"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justice told ABC\u8217\'20\'19s This Week}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CRed states probably have a lot of people that are very, very conservative in their thinking and they think, \u8216\'20\'18Well, I don\u8217\'20\'19t have to do that.\u8217\'20\'19 But they\u8217\'20\'19re not thinking right.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/05/us-coronavirus-vaccinations-republican-governors-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican governors urge vaccine-hesitant residents to get Covid shots}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to speak on Covid response after US misses July 4 vaccination goal\par \par \uc2 Greetings from Washington, live blog readers.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will speak this afternoon on his administration\u8217\'20\'19s ongoing efforts to get Americans vaccinated against coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 The speech comes two days after the country failed to meet Biden\u8217\'20\'19s goal of having 70% of American adults at least partially vaccinated by July 4, the US independence day.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://covid.cdc.gov/covid-data-tracker/#vaccinations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 , 67.1% of American adults have now received at least one vaccine dose, and 58.2% of adults are fully vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 enltrWATCH: Dr. Fauci says Covid-19 vaccination rate disparities could create 'two types of America' {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/MTP?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #MTP}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jFHF2L9OBC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jFHF2L9OBC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Meet the Press (@MeetThePress) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MeetThePress/status/1411012054195056654?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 2, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 However, there are large regional disparities in vaccination rates. The CDC director, \uc2 Dr Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , noted last week that there are about 1,000 US counties where less than 30% of the community is vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 As the more highly contagious delta variant of coronavirus continues to spread, those communities could be at much higher risk of outbreaks, as \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2  warned in an interview on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFortunately, we have a substantial proportion of the population vaccinated. So it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be regional,\u8221\'20\'1D Fauci told NBC News. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to see, and I\u8217\'20\'19ve said, almost two types of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 2021-07-06T13:19:44Z 2021-07-07T00:31:19Z {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/79f21c7b4d90ab02b403639f0b42d51e96e3f517/0_448_6720_4032/500.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/79f21c7b4d90ab02b403639f0b42d51e96e3f517/0_448_6720_4032/500.jpg}}}\uc2  Eric Adams triumphed over a large field in New York\u8217\'20\'19s first major race to use ranked choice voting.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210706eh76001s3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
