\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It shakes you to your core\u8217\'20\'19: the anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  extremists gaining ground on the right\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza in Phoenix, Arizona \par \uc2 1,954 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 July 2021\par 13:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Operation Save America opposes Covid vaccination, women in power and same-sex marriage \u8211\'20\'13 and allies are making inroads among legislators\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protesters lined blocks along a four-lane thoroughfare called Indian School Road in Phoenix, Arizona, enduring the suck of whooshing cars and blistering late June desert heat to advocate for their cause \u8211\'20\'13 effectively, theocracy in America.\par \par \uc2 Rising temperatures promised a sweaty, nauseous apex of 104F for the protest in front of Camelback Family Planning and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic. Their ranks were defined by gruesome and bloody signs, some taller than the protesters who held them, a microphone and an amplifier.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a slaughterhouse!\u8221\'20\'1D a man\u8217\'20\'19s voice growled. Some protesters leaned into car windows going into the clinic parking lot. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is unnatural for a mother to do this to a child!\u8221\'20\'1D one cried.\par \par \uc2 This is the national conference for Operation Save America (OSA), one in a network of extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups gaining increasing sway with rightwing lawmakers. In some sense, they\u8217\'20\'19re not news \u8211\'20\'13 their homophobic, transphobic, Islamophobic, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/AbortionFront/videos/4140170639358267"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 misogynist}}}\uc2  leadership has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/inside-anti-abortion-underground-187894"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 harassed \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  providers}}}\uc2  for decades.\par \par \uc2 But, like the world around them, they\u8217\'20\'19ve evolved.\par \par \uc2 New millennial leadership built a social media infrastructure on \uc2 YouTube\uc2 , \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and Gab. Their protests have moved from streets to city council chambers and state capitols. A book published by one of their leaders has become an underground hit. And the government response to Covid-19 has provided a new form of \u8220\'20\'1Ctyranny\u8221\'20\'1D against which to lobby.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll murderers forfeit their right to live,\u8221\'20\'1D said a protester. He gives his name only as \u8220\'20\'1Cpreacher man\u8221\'20\'1D, but he is easy to identify. He is Ante Pavkovic, a Charlotte, North Carolina-based protester whose antics have led to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://charmeckda.com/news/051618_1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrests}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose is \u8220\'20\'1CMarxist cliche sloganeering\u8221\'20\'1D, Pavkovic said. In 2018, Pavkovic was convicted of resisting arrest while breaking Charlotte\u8217\'20\'19s noise ordinance outside an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic. Although the noise ordinance charge was dropped, an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://casetext.com/case/state-v-pavkovic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appellate court}}}\uc2  affirmed an order that barred him from protesting within 1,500 feet of a clinic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis group is very close to each other,\u8221\'20\'1D said Shawn Cox, a 19-year-old protester with glasses and a DSLR camera with a colorful strap. Her family goes to an OSA event \u8220\'20\'1Cat least once a year\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1973 in the landmark case {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2020/may/22/aka-jane-roe-documentary-norma-mccorvey"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , and the majority of Americans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2021/06/17/key-facts-about-the-abortion-debate-in-america/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 still support}}}\uc2  the ruling in remarkably stable public opinion polls. But in the decades since, as evangelical {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/apr/05/americans-religion-rightwing-politics-decline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Christians and Catholics}}}\uc2  gained increasing power in the Republican party, lawmakers have worked to obstruct that right.\par \par \uc2 Those efforts have accelerated in the last decade, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/may/30/revealed-womens-fertility-app-is-funded-by-anti-abortion-campaigners"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  fundraising}}}\uc2  fueled an entire {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jun/04/states-divert-federal-welfare-funding-anti-abortion-clinics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cottage industry}}}\uc2  of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/may/22/iowa-anti-abortion-heartbeat-bill-passed-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawyers}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/apr/25/the-anti-abortion-crusader-hopes-her-heartbeat-law-will-test-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lobbyists}}}\uc2  and single-issue alternative news sources devoted to advancing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2019/aug/22/a-new-poll-shows-what-really-interests-pro-lifers-controlling-women"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 secular arguments}}}\uc2  to obstruct \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Once at the fringes, but moving into legislative efforts are protesters like these, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cabolitionists\u8221\'20\'1D who advocate for women and doctors to be prosecuted under murder statutes. Their name is an appropriation of a term used by anti-slavery organizers before the American civil war.\par \par \uc2 Their views are extreme. Anyone who has an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cshould be prosecuted for murder\u8221\'20\'1D, Cox said. And she adds about the case that is the foundation of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in America: \u8220\'20\'1CRoe v Wade is not law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Their guiding texts, such as the Doctrine of Lesser Magistrates, by the leader of the affiliated group Defy Tyrants, Matt Trewhella, argues \u8220\'20\'1CChristians\u8221\'20\'1D should defy laws with which zealots disagree. Trewhella was among a notorious group of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates who, in the 1990s, signed a letter declaring the murder of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.splcenter.org/fighting-hate/intelligence-report/2015/signers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 justifiable homicide}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. The letter was also joined by a man convicted of firebombing a Cincinnati, Ohio, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic and planning an attack on another in Florida, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dispatch.com/news/20200511/facebook-fact-check-convicted-1980s-abortion-clinic-bomber-attended-ohio-statehouse-protests-of-stay-at-home-order"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 John Brockhoeft}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here in Arizona, OSA has just crowned a new leader, Jason Storms. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat the abolitionists have done is bring clarity to the [anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] movement,\u8221\'20\'1D said Storms. Storms and OSA\u8217\'20\'19s followers want {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://religiondispatches.org/convergence-of-far-right-anti-democratic-factions-in-the-northwest-could-provide-a-model-for-the-rest-of-the-nation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 their Christian ideology to be the basis of American law}}}\uc2 . Otherwise, Storms argued, \u8220\'20\'1Cwe are heading for cultural suicide\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A tall man with a pinched gait, thick black glasses and an Operation Save America shirt walked up to Storms: \u8220\'20\'1CGod bless you as you transition to leadership.\u8221\'20\'1D He shook Storms\u8217\'20\'19s hand, turned to the wind and wetly uttered, \u8220\'20\'1CWhere\u8217\'20\'19s the mill?\u8221\'20\'1D referring to the clinic. His red shirt read \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is murder\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Across the gauntlet of cars from the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protests, Storms mocked a counter-protester. \u8220\'20\'1CTough guy,\u8221\'20\'1D said Storms, as he mimicked her stance and derided her silence.\par \par \uc2 This woman, however, is part of a counter-protest organized by \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Access Front (AAF), a female-led comedy group who have become the unlikely antagonists of these extremists.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22\u8226\'20\'22\u8226\'20\'22\par \par \uc2 On another day and in another part of town, clinic escorts, legal observers, nurses and volunteers gather under the high ceilings of the Duce, a warehouse turned bar where a rainbow of color seems to ricochet around the room. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Access Front has gathered this crowd for a moment of joy, hosting a happy hour.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt shakes you to your core,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lizz Winstead, the founder of AAF, about Operation Save America\u8217\'20\'19s protests, and perhaps its ideology writ large. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s hard to explain to people until you see it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 OSA\u8217\'20\'19s leaders and adherents oppose not only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but homosexuality and same-sex marriage, in vitro fertilization, Islam, Covid-19 vaccines and masks. At times, they appear to be opposed to the modern world, railing against public school, women in positions of power, sex before marriage and birth control.\par \par \uc2 Opposing them is the AAF, which started as a traveling standup comedy show in 2015 led by Winstead, a former writer at Comedy Central\u8217\'20\'19s The Daily Show. Initially, it was called the Lady Parts Justice League. But it quickly became a mutual aid, counter-protest and intelligence gathering organization. It describes itself as a \u8220\'20\'1Cmedia hub\u8221\'20\'1D that uses \u8220\'20\'1Chumor to bust stigma\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protesters had made it impossible for clinics to get even basic maintenance done on their buildings. Protesters would call and harass contractors who showed up to work. AAF organized local supporters to plant bushes, paint or provide basic supplies like heating pads to clinics.\par \par \uc2 Following events organized by OSA, AAF believed someone needed to show people that the majority of Americans support the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They started protests meant to disrupt and frustrate street preachers. In Arizona, one AAF organizer repeatedly interrupted a street preacher, following him with a camera and ridiculing his shorts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWitch!\u8221\'20\'1D he snorted at the AAF organizer, prompting the entire AAF group to break into a chant: \u8220\'20\'1CWitch! Witch! You\u8217\'20\'19re a witch!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Most notably, they have also developed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aafront.org/operation-save-america-an-overview-of-their-bll-sht/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 detailed knowledge}}}\uc2  of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protesters themselves, tracking their whereabouts with a camera once devoted to making television.\par \par \uc2 The AAF managing director, Kat Green, said she began \u8220\'20\'1Crecreationally\u8221\'20\'1D tracking extremists, sharing intel with local escorts and clinic security teams. AAF identified and collected evidence of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aafront.org/anti-abortion-extremists-at-capitol/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at least 15 anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  leaders}}}\uc2  among those at the Capitol insurrection, including Storms and the Arizona-based pastor Jeff Durbin, who runs the \u8220\'20\'1Cabolitionist\u8221\'20\'1D social media presence.\par \par \uc2 In a three-minute video posted to \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , Storms shows himself astride scaffolding surrounding the Capitol, woooo!- ing and calling the insurrection \u8220\'20\'1CRevolution 2.0\u8221\'20\'1D. Another person in the crowd calls out \u8220\'20\'1Chang \u8217\'20\'19em high!\u8221\'20\'1D in reference to members of Congress.\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, at the protest, Storms said: \u8220\'20\'1CJanuary 6th was a non-issue,\u8221\'20\'1D and added: \u8220\'20\'1CThere was no insurrection.\u8221\'20\'1D He called the insurrection \u8220\'20\'1C1 million unarmed people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 AAF also began to understand the connections between groups like Operation Save America and other militant religious groups. Operation Save America leaders appeared on the podcast of the former Washington state representative Matt Shea, and Shea appeared at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.spokesman.com/stories/2018/aug/11/anti-abortion-protestors-picket-planned-parenthood/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protests in support}}}\uc2  of \u8220\'20\'1Cabolitionists\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Shea opted not to run for re-election after it was revealed he had \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/dec/20/matt-shea-domestic-terrorism-washington-state-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 participated in an act of domestic of terrorism}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D and distributed a document that outlined \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and same-sex marriage as justification for a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/nov/03/matt-shea-washington-republican-biblical-basis-for-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biblical basis for war}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe reason they\u8217\'20\'19re different \u8211\'20\'13 and it\u8217\'20\'19s important \u8211\'20\'13 is they are not interested in incremental change. They\u8217\'20\'19re not interested in using regulations. They\u8217\'20\'19re not even that interested in Roe,\u8221\'20\'1D said Anu Kumar, president and CEO of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ipas.org/about-us/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ipas}}}\uc2 , an international non-profit that works to expand \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat they\u8217\'20\'19re militant about is defying the courts, defying the constitution, and defying the rule of law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They are pro-gun, and though they did not appear to be carrying weapons at the Arizona protest, they advertise their armaments and argue Christians should be trained in \u8220\'20\'1Ctrench warfare\u8221\'20\'1D. They want to save \u8220\'20\'1Cour constitutional republic\u8221\'20\'1D by making American law \u8220\'20\'1CMirror the Law and Justice of God\u8221\'20\'1D. They support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat\u8217\'20\'19s hard for Americans to understand is the actions by these extremists seem very hyperlocal,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kumar. \u8220\'20\'1CThese are connected movements and the rightwing extremism is actually transnational.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At the same time, they have seen increasing success introducing legislation to prosecute \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as murder, as they did in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/apr/27/us-tiny-towns-anti-abortion-ordinances"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oklahoma, Texas and most recently Arizona}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 These state efforts to narrow legal access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  threaten to make {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cfr.org/article/abortion-law-global-comparisons"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 America an outlier}}}\uc2 . The past 50 years have been defined by \u8220\'20\'1Can unmistakable trend toward the liberalization of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws\u8221\'20\'1D, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cfr.org/article/abortion-law-global-comparisons"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Council on Foreign Relations}}}\uc2  wrote. Twenty-eight countries have liberalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access since 2000, and only one has legally restricted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 Nicaragua.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYes, they are definitely anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they are misogynist, they are anti-immigrant as well. But fundamentally, they are about democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kumar. \u8220\'20\'1CThey are anti-democratic zealots,\u8221\'20\'1D she added, and in that sense, \u8220\'20\'1Cthis is not about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22\u8226\'20\'22\u8226\'20\'22\par \par \uc2 At a later OSA-sponsored worship service, a man named Ken greeted outsiders at the edge of the Desert Hills Bible church and ambled slowly to the entrance as he described the joy he felt that reporters would \u8220\'20\'1Chear the word of God\u8221\'20\'1D. Certainly, he emphasized, he would not want anyone to be cast into hell.\par \par \uc2 Inside, a crowd probably vulnerable to Covid-19 filled the hall\u8217\'20\'19s stuffy still air with song and inestimable respiratory droplets. Trewhella, one of the leaders of the affiliated group Defy Tyrants, has repeatedly urged congregants to \u8220\'20\'1Cnever\u8221\'20\'1D get vaccinated, claiming the life-saving drugs are government \u8220\'20\'1Ctyranny\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Durbin, who also leads the local Apologia church, said he chose not to attend the evening because he and his daughter contracted \u8220\'20\'1Cthe rona\u8221\'20\'1D at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/jun/29/southern-baptist-convention-america-culture-wars"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Southern Baptist Convention}}}\uc2  about a week prior.\par \par \uc2 The outgoing leader of OSA and a longtime menace to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics, Rusty Thomas, stepped to the dais to rally the flock. He called \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Cpagan nightmare\u8221\'20\'1D that \u8220\'20\'1Cassaulted the nation\u8221\'20\'1D. He illustrated his points with a story of how he hit his children.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll that anger, all that frustration, and I pummeled my own children,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. Then he begged for their forgiveness. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I said, let me get on my knees in front of my kids and said, \u8216\'20\'18Would you please forgive your father?\u8217\'20\'19 And I tell you that won them over more than any of my teachings.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 OSA was a family, leaders said, a \u8220\'20\'1Crock\u8221\'20\'1D in its members\u8217\'20\'19 lives, the way a church \u8220\'20\'1Cshould work\u8221\'20\'1D. And they believe their efforts, no matter how extreme, are altering the fabric of American society.\par \par \uc2 On this point, experts agree.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMost Americans do not actually support these radical extreme points of view and yet we have elected officials who do,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kumar. \u8220\'20\'1COur politics have become extreme, and these groups are responsible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210706eh76000rw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
