\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Unique problem\u8217\'20\'19: Catholic bishops split over Biden\u8217\'20\'19s support for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Harriet Sherwood religion correspondent \par \uc2 1,137 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 June 2021\par 07:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 US bishops to debate whether the president should be denied communion over his pro-choice stance\par \par \uc2 At some point this weekend, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will take his place in a line of people approaching the altar of a Catholic church to receive communion.\par \par \uc2 The US president, a devout Catholic whose speeches regularly include biblical references and who carries a rosary that belonged to his late son, attends Mass every weekend \u8211\'20\'13 in Washington, his home town of Wilmington in Delaware, or wherever he happens to be traveling. If the traditional Sunday morning Eucharist service is not possible because of his schedule, he will receive the sacrament on Saturday evening as permitted by the Roman Catholic church.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s really an encounter with God,\u8221\'20\'1D Father Kevin Gillespie of Holy Trinity in Washington, the church Biden usually attends in the capital, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/politics/archive/2021/02/joe-biden-catholic-communion-abortion/618067/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Atlantic}}}\uc2  earlier this year. For Biden, this \u8220\'20\'1Csacred and intimate moment\u8221\'20\'1D is a \u8220\'20\'1Cgift that enhances his faith\u8221\'20\'1D, and \u8220\'20\'1Cwe most certainly encourage him to improve his intimacy with God through the Eucharist\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But not everybody in the Catholic church in America is quite so keen on Biden receiving communion. Next week, a national online meeting of US bishops will discuss whether the president and other high-profile political figures should be denied the sacraments because of his stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow can he say he\u8217\'20\'19s a devout Catholic and he\u8217\'20\'19s doing these things that are contrary to the church\u8217\'20\'19s teaching?\u8221\'20\'1D archbishop Joseph Naumann, chair of the US Conference of Catholic Bishops\u8217\'20\'19 (USCCB) committee on pro-life activities, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/health-coronavirus-government-and-politics-religion-22e0d1ba299fe8693013036e3cc85c81"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked last month}}}\uc2 . Biden\u8217\'20\'19s position was a \u8220\'20\'1Cgrave moral evil\u8221\'20\'1D which presents a \u8220\'20\'1Cunique problem\u8221\'20\'1D for the church, Naumann said.\par \par \uc2 Cardinal Raymond Burke, a leading conservative and critic of \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 , has gone further, saying that politicians who \u8220\'20\'1Cpublicly and obstinately\u8221\'20\'1D support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are \u8220\'20\'1Capostates\u8221\'20\'1D who should not only be barred from receiving communion but deserve excommunication.\par \par \uc2 At their meeting, the bishops will consider a document aimed at clarifying the church\u8217\'20\'19s position on the Eucharist, and decide whether to commission further work on the circumstances in which the sacraments may be denied. The proposal needs the support of at least two-thirds of the 280 bishops in the USCCB \u8211\'20\'13 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pillarcatholic.com/p/bishops-press-gomez-to-halt-communion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 60 have already requested a suspension}}}\uc2  of all discussion, citing divisions within the conference.\par \par \uc2 Among opponents of the move is Robert McElroy, the bishop of San Diego, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americamagazine.org/faith/2021/05/05/joe-biden-communion-eucharistic-exclusion-abortion-us-bishops-240596"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote in America Magazine}}}\uc2 , the Jesuit journal, that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Eucharist is being weaponised and deployed as a tool in political warfare. This must not happen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americamagazine.org/faith/2021/05/10/vatican-communion-bishops-biden-catholic-politicians-abortion-240627"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter from a senior Vatican official}}}\uc2  last month urged US bishops not to rush any debate and decision, and there has been speculation that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.eurasiareview.com/04062021-pope-francis-and-president-biden-may-meet-on-june-15/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first meeting between President Biden and Pope Francis}}}\uc2  could take place at the Vatican the day before the USCCB\u8217\'20\'19s virtual session opens. That would be seen as a strong signal from Rome.\par \par \uc2 Whatever the outcome of the USCCB\u8217\'20\'19s deliberations, the decision on whether an individual parishioner should be denied communion lies with the local bishop. Wilton Gregory of Washington and Francis Malooly of Wilmington, Delaware, have both made it clear that Biden is welcome to receive communion at churches in their dioceses.\par \par \uc2 Father Gillespie\u8217\'20\'19s public defence of Biden attending Mass has drawn angry phone calls, letters and emails. He told \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  it seemed best to refrain from speaking further on the matter, but said the president \u8220\'20\'1Chas and will be welcomed to receive the Holy Eucharist\u8221\'20\'1D at his church.\par \par \uc2 Biden, the second Catholic to occupy the White House after John F Kennedy, has said his faith shapes \u8220\'20\'1Call that I do\u8221\'20\'1D and will \u8220\'20\'1Cserve as my anchor\u8221\'20\'1D through his term in office. In his book, Promises to Keep: On Life and Politics, he wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CMy idea of self, of family, of community, of the wider world comes straight from my religion.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Biden has said he personally believes life begins at conception but recognises others do not share his view. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I\u8217\'20\'19m not prepared to do is impose a precise view that is borne out of my faith on other people,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in 2015.\par \par \uc2 In recent months, the Biden administration has lifted restrictions on federal funding for research involving human foetal tissue, rescinded a Trump policy barring organisations that refer women for abortions from receiving federal grants, and allowed women to remotely obtain a prescription for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill during the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 The Catholic church says that Catholics in public life should uphold principles consistent with its doctrine. But in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2021/03/30/u-s-catholics-divided-by-party-on-whether-biden-should-be-denied-communion-over-his-abortion-stance/ft_2021-03-30_bidencommunion_03/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a survey carried out by the Pew Research Center in March}}}\uc2 , more than two-thirds of US Catholics said Biden\u8217\'20\'19s views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should not disqualify him from receiving communion.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/elections/interactive/2020/exit-polls/presidential-election-exit-polls/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exit polls}}}\uc2  taken during last November\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election, just over half of US Catholics (51%) voted for Biden, compared with 45% who voted Democrat in 2016; and 47% voted for Trump, compared with 52% in the previous election.\par \par \uc2 Andrew Chesnut, professor of religious studies at \uc2 Virginia Commonwealth University\uc2 , said the USCCB\u8217\'20\'19s proposal \u8220\'20\'1Cserves to further polarise an already sharply divided episcopy, some of whom have been outspoken opponents of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2020/feb/14/pope-francis-liberal-supporters-let-down"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pope Francis\u8217\'20\'19s relatively progressive papacy}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe proposal to exclude Biden and all election officials who support legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from communion is an effort on the part of conservative bishops to shore up their base of regular Mass-goers who are the life blood of the church. But exclusionary ecclesial policies will only lead to greater defection from the pews, especially among Millennials and Generation Z.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Michael Budde, professor of Catholic studies and political science at \uc2 DePaul University in Chicago\uc2 , said barring Biden from communion \u8220\'20\'1Cwill be rightly seen as a move of desperation, an attempt to coerce what has not been won by persuasion or dialogue\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no consensus among the Catholic faithful on this measure; significantly, there is no real support for it at the level of the worldwide Catholic communion as voiced by \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 . That there are finally some important US cardinals and bishops who are tired of this can\u8217\'20\'19t-win strategy may be an indication that someday a better vision might finally emerge.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A scathing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncronline.org/news/opinion/editorial-why-we-support-bishops-plan-deny-communion-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 editorial in the National Catholic Reporter}}}\uc2  earlier this month said the \u8220\'20\'1Ctragic reality\u8221\'20\'1D of proceeding with the proposal was that \u8220\'20\'1Cit will seal the deal on the branding of Catholicism in the United States as a culture war project.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis culture war \u8230\'20\'26 is not the church of mercy and encounter that \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  is trying to offer the world. Nor does it resemble what the carpenter\u8217\'20\'19s son from Galilee preached and died for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Associated Press contributed to this article\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210612eh6c000gv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
