\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s dehumanizing\u8217\'20\'19: Texas valedictorian goes off script to attack  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh \par \uc2 481 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 June 2021\par 08:37 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Paxton Smith criticizes near-total ban that makes no exception for rape or incest\par \par \uc2 The valedictorian at a Texas high school went off script while delivering her graduation speech, criticising the state\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/19/texas-abortion-ban-law-greg-abbott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extreme \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2  in an address that has since been widely shared on social media.\par \par \uc2 School administrators had signed off on Paxton Smith\u8217\'20\'19s pre-written speech on how TV and media have shaped her worldview. But, when it came time to address the graduating class of Lake Highlands high school, she pivoted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn light of recent events, it feels wrong to talk about anything but what is currently affecting me and millions of other women in this state,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, her voice shaking as she began.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CStarting in September, there will be a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy, regardless of whether the pregnancy was the result of rape or incest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In May, the state\u8217\'20\'19s governor, Greg Abbott, signed into law a near-total ban on abortions, prohibiting the procedure at six weeks, when most people do not even know that they are pregnant. The extreme ban also allows private citizens to sue any \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider or anyone who \u8220\'20\'1Caids and abets\u8221\'20\'1D an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that violates the restriction \u8211\'20\'13 opening the floodgates to harassment and frivolous lawsuits.\par \par \uc2 The law makes no exception for rape or incest, and advocates say it will, in effect, make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/19/texas-abortion-ban-law-greg-abbott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 impossible}}}\uc2  for women to access in the state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have dreams, hopes and ambitions,\u8221\'20\'1D Smith said. \u8220\'20\'1CEvery girl here does. We have spent our whole lives working towards our futures, and without our consent or input, our control over our futures has been stripped away from us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am terrified that if my contraceptives fail me, that if I\u8217\'20\'19m raped, then my hopes and efforts and dreams for myself will no longer be relevant,\u8221\'20\'1D she added. \u8220\'20\'1CI hope you can feel how gut-wrenching it is, how dehumanizing it is, to have the autonomy over your own body taken from you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The speech has been viewed hundreds of thousands of times on TikTok and drew the attention of prominent political figures. \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , the 2016 presidential candidate and longtime activist for women\u8217\'20\'19s rights, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HillaryClinton/status/1400127800288419840"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThis took guts. Thank you for not staying silent, Paxton.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The former Democratic Texas congressman \uc2 Beto O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BetoORourke/status/1400151466531344388"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thanked}}}\uc2  Smith \u8220\'20\'1Cfor having the courage of your convictions and inspiring Texas with your refusal to accept injustice as the price of participation in civic life\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Smith {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dmagazine.com/frontburner/2021/06/lake-highlands-high-valedictorian-pulls-switcheroo-on-commencement-speech/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  D Magazine that the viral fame had felt \u8220\'20\'1Cweird for me personally\u8221\'20\'1D, though she was pleased that the issues she raised were getting attention. She also urged people to vote, \u8220\'20\'1Cand to stay involved in local elections because those have more power than I think the media gives them credit for\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210603eh6300001\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
