\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 UK-based doctor under investigation over  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  \u8216\'20\'18reversal\u8217\'20\'19 medication\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 963 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 June 2021\par 16:59 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Dr Eileen Reilly allegedly offered to prescribe \u8216\'20\'18unproven and experimental\u8217\'20\'19 treatment promoted by US anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists\par \par \uc2 A UK-based doctor is under investigation for offering to prescribe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Creversal\u8221\'20\'1D medication, an \u8220\'20\'1Cunproven and experimental\u8221\'20\'1D treatment promoted by US-based anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists.\par \par \uc2 The doctor allegedly offered to prescribe pessaries to an undercover investigator with the media outlet {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opendemocracy.net/en/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 openDemocracy}}}\uc2 . The undercover investigator was connected to the doctor after calling a US-based Christian hotline run by Heartbeat International, a large anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUK doctors should not be working with anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists to advise and prescribe a treatment that is unproven and dangerous,\u8221\'20\'1D said MP \uc2 Nadia Whittome\uc2 . She said she was \u8220\'20\'1Cglad\u8221\'20\'1D the GMC was investigating.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  reversal\u8221\'20\'1D is an \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.acog.org/advocacy/facts-are-important/medication-abortion-reversal-is-not-supported-by-science"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unproven and unethical}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D treatment promoted to women who opt for medication abortions to terminate a pregnancy. Medication abortions are available to people who wish to terminate a pregnancy that is less than 10 weeks along. Crucially, the medication can be taken at home, which has caused its popularity to increase amid the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 However, since 2014, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/jul/25/revealed-doctor-reverse-abortion-trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California-based doctor}}}\uc2  has promoted a \u8220\'20\'1Ctreatment\u8221\'20\'1D to \u8220\'20\'1Creverse\u8221\'20\'1D a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  through large doses of progesterone, though {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/jul/25/revealed-doctor-reverse-abortion-trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US-based doctors associations and OB-GYNs}}}\uc2  have repeatedly said there is no evidence to show it is safe or effective.\par \par \uc2 An editorial in the New England Journal of Medicine called the treatment \u8220\'20\'1Cunproven and experimental\u8221\'20\'1D, and said it should only be offered, \u8220\'20\'1Cin the context of clinical research supervised by an institutional review board (IRB)\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The only high-quality, randomized controlled trial to be conducted on the treatment was halted in 2019 when three women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31809439/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suffered severe hemorrhaging}}}\uc2  and had to be hospitalized.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWomen who have medical abortions bleed, but this was not typical medical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bleeding,\u8221\'20\'1D Dr Mitchell Creinin, a professor of obstetrics-gynecology at the University of California, Davis Health who led and ultimately halted the study, told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.self.com/story/myth-of-reverse-abortions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Self magazine in 2020}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt wasn\u8217\'20\'19t safe for me to expose women to this treatment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, regulators have allowed the treatment to flourish in the US, and state legislators have promoted its growth by mandating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers counsel women their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be \u8220\'20\'1Creversed\u8221\'20\'1D if they change their mind.\par \par \uc2 UK doctors should not be working with anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists to advise and prescribe a treatment that is unproven and dangerous\par \par \uc2 MP \uc2 Nadia Whittome\par \par \uc2 One North Dakota law was the subject of a 2019 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ama-assn.org/press-center/press-releases/ama-lawsuit-protect-patient-physician-relationship-north-dakota"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit by the American Medical Association}}}\uc2 , the largest professional organization of doctors in the country, who said it required doctors to, \u8220\'20\'1Cmislead and misinform their patients with messages that contradict reality and science\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis trend is troubling because of the lack of medical evidence demonstrating the safety and efficacy of the treatment,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Dr Daniel Grossman\uc2 , a professor of obstetrics, gynecology and reproductive sciences at the Bixby Center for Reproductive Health at the \uc2 University of California, San Francisco\uc2 , wrote in the same Nejm editorial. \u8220\'20\'1CLaws promoting it essentially encourage women to participate in an unmonitored research experiment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Additionally, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/jul/25/revealed-doctor-reverse-abortion-trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guardian investigation}}}\uc2  into the doctor who invented the regime, \uc2 Dr George Delgado\uc2 , revealed he continued to use an affiliation with the \uc2 University of California, San Diego\uc2  years after his connection with the school had ended, and a year after the university had asked him to stop.\par \par \uc2 Delgado is the \u8220\'20\'1Cmedical director\u8221\'20\'1D of a \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D Catholic-oriented clinic in San Diego. He has also made \u8220\'20\'1Chundreds of presentations\u8221\'20\'1D to anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  fundraisers, a biography on the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lozierinstitute.org/team-member/george-delgado/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Charlotte Lozier Institute website}}}\uc2  said. His paper on the treatment was widely criticized and briefly retracted.\par \par \uc2 Despite repeated condemnations of professional organizations and a lack of viable research, openDemocracy investigations have found doctors in at least a dozen countries promoting the \u8220\'20\'1Ctreatment\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 An operator on the Heartbeat International hotline told an investigator the group \u8220\'20\'1Chelps[s] hundreds of women everyday in the UK\u8221\'20\'1D. The operator added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are like the international \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill reversal line,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The General Medical Council\uc2 , the regulatory body for doctors in the UK, is now investigating the doctor the openDemocracy reporter was connected to \u8211\'20\'13 Dr Eileen Reilly. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gmc-uk.org/doctors/3498051?__cf_chl_captcha_tk__=c3e668e371b06ad055c43ab4336b13f9643d40ed-1622042875-0-Aemqwyj_qUXC6tjIIb2wyAhPR6aYnhmbJvhsklwjwmVhcNoTIRBiLvuLdCDM2MwGaUCwKPN46mrebjrHF3yes8J3K2YPaw03RU18Xohaii3RQfu0IzaxMYD29U78TV6KmwaqjA721RIf4ZljMgaj1XA8jLvf9wNgZidlNiTzE9A0NaJYBnIHrenAQRoUabg1fgUvIMpA8bKYFC1s4VH9jQR7GUA-VtLlXea0h-DXfwoLMM5MUe9o2pHKwY7Yf44YS-8U-epN7WaFASkEhJx0Yl-j2tWDTjGhUaP8kkgSyUmfb6bGbx2XGQPOeTeDG2bEgj-GGAMfF0W1FJDNFji7RPtHSEylkXUytlx5_XJ7WfOtT8pvP2S590ackJJCCDh9PO098Czjo9qFRKsOdh4mKZwCaRI4O_MwOi01n1lNQu1deV3VUZGHn2Owitnfvld_xWVxQwm5d10LL6TFm7EWgMfcuIH-TbYY-0IIrPo392ljPGmfPG1NXgDna_c6N27ZVKLS7WPLHl2AGy17k1nTNbAXKYMLDrj3JnYUIbpLSisHl5GzEd6YX7NXBVaZwkpyT6tDGb-PfQemAc5u9GwZOqWDJvmtuyTcx9G92gkNxWfp1C6i7XSlSKYWEmwO7gjDLxleQHl-lp5dl0Gc7_r3y5aoy59zqLJuYQjTd-YI5sZHME4ybe3mpN4SOLt5Qt-ALQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 public listing of regulatory actions shows}}}\uc2  Reilly is now subject to supervisory conditions while the GMC considers her case.\par \par \uc2 Regarding health concerns, openDemocracy said its investigator was told by Reilly, \u8220\'20\'1CAt the end of the day, you live in the UK, you\u8217\'20\'19ve got a hospital there and if you were worried about the bleeding, you\u8217\'20\'19d go get help.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The regulatory tribunal may take no action, impose conditions on a doctor\u8217\'20\'19s ability to practice, or suspend the doctor while the tribunal investigates, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gmc-uk.org/concerns/information-for-doctors-under-investigation/our-sanctions/interim-sanctions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 GMC website states}}}\uc2 . A referral to the tribunal alone does not mean the GMC has reached a decision about fitness to practice.\par \par \uc2 Investigators with openDemocracy said they called Reilly for comment ahead of publishing their report, but \u8220\'20\'1Cshe hung up\u8221\'20\'1D. Reilly appears to have made comments about medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as recently as February, when she appeared on a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/MarchForLifeUK/videos/dr-eileen-reilly-raises-concerns-about-diy-abortions/165802285079002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video}}}\uc2  hosted by the UK-based anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group March for Life UK.\par \par \uc2 Melissa Upreti, the vice-chair of the United Nations working group on discrimination against women and girls said, \u8220\'20\'1CThe situation warrants not one but multiple investigations by government bodies, as well as professional associations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWomen who have been misled and subjected to medically dangerous procedures to supposedly reverse their abortions must be provided with appropriate medical assistance, options for legal recourse and reparations for the emotional and physical suffering caused to them,\u8221\'20\'1D Upreti said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere can be no doubt that women are the victims here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 1 June 2021 to clarify that openDemocracy is a media outlet, rather than an advocacy group as an earlier version said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210527eh5r0012y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
