\par\par \uc2 Law\par \b \uc2 Supreme court justice \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2 : Democrats must \u8216\'20\'18get Republicans talking\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Pengelly and agencies \par \uc2 724 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 June 2021\par 14:45 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights case looms before 6-3 conservative panel 82-year-old liberal touts belief in upholding precedent\u8216\'20\'18Un-American and wrong\u8217\'20\'19: Biden blasts Texas voting bill\par \par \uc2 The supreme court justice \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2  has told young Americans Democrats facing Republican intransigence, obstruction and outright attacks on democracy should \u8220\'20\'1Cget \u8216\'20\'18em talking\u8221\'20\'1D, in search of compromise and progress.\par \par \uc2 Breyer was speaking to middle- and high-school students on Friday, in an event organised by the \uc2 National Constitution Center\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The same day, Republicans in the Senate deployed the filibuster, by which the minority can thwart the will of the majority, to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/29/mitch-mcconnell-us-capitol-attack-commission-senate-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 block the establishment}}}\uc2  of a 9/11-style commission to investigate the attack on the US Capitol by supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on 6 January.\par \par \uc2 Thomas Kean\uc2 , who led the 9/11 panel, told \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  the Republican move was \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/29/9-11-commission-chief-republican-6-january-rejection-thomas-kean"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 democracy\u8217\'20\'19s loss}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 From the White House, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  faces Republican reluctance to engage on his plans for investment in infrastructure and the pandemic-battered economy. Amid concerted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/29/wrong-un-american-biden-republicans-texas-sb7-voting-rights-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attacks on voting rights in Republican states}}}\uc2 , federal bills to protect such rights seem unlikely to pass the Senate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou need that Republican\u8217\'20\'19s support?\u8221\'20\'1D Breyer told the listening students. \u8220\'20\'1CTalk to them \u8230\'20\'26 You say, \u8216\'20\'18What do you think? My friend, what do you think?\u8217\'20\'19 Get \u8217\'20\'19em talking. Once they start talking eventually they\u8217\'20\'19ll say something you agree with.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats do not agree with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lie that his election defeat by Biden was the result of electoral fraud, which fuelled the deadly attack on the Capitol. Nor do they agree with Republican {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/25/anti-abortion-movement-bullish-us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempts to overturn Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , the 1973 supreme court ruling which safeguards a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The court has a 6-3 conservative majority, after Republicans ripped up precedent to block \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s final appointment then installed three justices under Trump, in the last case reversing their own position on appointments in the last year of a presidency.\par \par \uc2 Breyer was speaking less than two weeks after the court agreed to hear {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/25/anti-abortion-movement-bullish-us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a major challenge}}}\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 The case, which the justices will hear in their next term, beginning in October, involves an attempt by Mississippi to revive a law that bans the procedure after 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 In 2019 the conservative \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , who has backed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/article/us-usa-court-thomas/justice-thomas-urges-u-s-supreme-court-to-feel-free-to-reverse-precedents-idUSKCN1TI2KJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged the court}}}\uc2  to feel less bound to upholding precedent. Asked about the value of adhering to past rulings, Breyer said the court should overturn precedent only in the \u8220\'20\'1Crare case where it\u8217\'20\'19s really necessary\u8221\'20\'1D and said law is about stability.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe law might not be perfect but if you\u8217\'20\'19re changing it all the time people won\u8217\'20\'19t know what to do, and the more you change it the more people will ask to have it changed, and the more the court hears that, the more they\u8217\'20\'19ll change it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Many on the left seek change on the court, in the form of Breyer\u8217\'20\'19s retirement. After {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/sep/18/ruth-bader-ginsburg-supreme-court-justice-dies-aged-87"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the death}}}\uc2  of the progressive champion \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2  at 87 last September, Breyer, at 82, is the oldest judge on the panel. Ginsburg was replaced by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/amy-coney-barrett"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett}}}\uc2 , a strict Catholic widely seen as likely to favour overturning precedent on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 , another conservative justice, was installed by Republicans after \uc2 Anthony Kennedy\uc2  retired, a move {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/feb/04/trump-family-anthony-kennedy-brett-kavanaugh-dark-towers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supported by}}}\uc2  the Trump White House. Kennedy was conservative but a swing vote on key rulings regarding individual rights. Kavanaugh, once an aide to President \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 , is more reliably rightwing.\par \par \uc2 Breyer told the students, aged between 11 and 18, that as part of his daily routine he watches reruns of M*A*S*H, a hit sitcom that ran from 1972 to 1983. He also rides a stationary bike and meditates.\par \par \uc2 Questioned about deepening polarisation some fear may tear the US apart, Breyer said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cbasically optimistic\u8221\'20\'1D. For all of its flaws, he said, American democracy is \u8220\'20\'1Cbetter than the alternatives\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He also urged his listeners to put \u8220\'20\'1Cunfortunate things\u8221\'20\'1D in historical context.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s happened before,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not the first time that people have become discouraged with the democratic process. This is not the first time that we\u8217\'20\'19ve had real racism in this country. It used to be slavery before that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210601eh610020f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
