\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Senate Republicans block commission to investigate deadly Capitol attack \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Sam Levin in Los Angeles (now) and Joan E Greve in Washington (earlier) \par \uc2 8,745 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 May 2021\par 00:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Republicans block creation of 9/11-style January 6 commissionDemocrats fail to win 60 votes needed to break a Senate filibuster\u8216\'20\'18Shame on the Republican party,\u8217\'20\'19 says majority leader Schumer\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.06am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s all for today, thanks for following along and have a nice three-day weekend. Here are some key links from the day:\par \par \uc2 * Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/28/joe-biden-budget-proposal-infrastructure-education-climate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 set out a $6tn budget proposal}}}\uc2  that, if passed, would fund a sweeping overhaul of US infrastructure and pour money into education and climate action, while driving government spending to its highest sustained levels since the second world war.\par \par \uc2 * Senate Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/28/senate-republicans-6-january-capitol-attack-commission"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked the creation of a special commission}}}\uc2  to study the deadly 6 January attack on the Capitol, dashing hopes for a bipartisan panel amid a Republican push to put the violent insurrection by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters behind them.\par \par \uc2 * Sewage sludge that wastewater treatment districts across America package and sell as home fertilizer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/may/28/home-fertilizer-toxic-pfas-forever-chemicals-sewage-sludge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contain alarming levels of toxic PFAS}}}\uc2 , also known as \u8220\'20\'1Cforever chemicals\u8221\'20\'1D, a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sierraclub.org/sludge-garden-toxic-pfas-home-fertilizers-made-sewage-sludge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  has revealed.\par \par \uc2 * San Jose residents {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/28/san-jose-shooting-vigil-victims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mourned after the deadliest shooting in the region\u8217\'20\'19s history}}}\uc2 , saying, \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t sweep this under the rug.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * A Guardian analysis revealed that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/28/us-capitol-attack-suspects-jail-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at least 70% of people charged in the Capitol riot}}}\uc2  have been released as they wait for trial.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  became the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/may/28/enate-republicans-capitol-attack-commission-joe-biden-covid-live-updates?page=with:block-60b108f18f088d8c3178c17c#block-60b108f18f088d8c3178c17c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first woman to deliver the Naval Academy commencement}}}\uc2  address earlier today.\par \par \uc2 * For {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/28/joe-biden-abortion-hyde-amendment-budget"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the first time in nearly 30 years}}}\uc2 , a US president has released a budget that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/aliceollstein/status/1398331135361441799?s=21"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 doesn\u8217\'20\'19t ban}}}\uc2  federal funding for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * A judge said on Friday that he will appoint a \u8220\'20\'1Cspecial master\u8221\'20\'1D to protect attorney-client privilege during a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/28/rudy-giuliani-judge-special-master-electronic-devices"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 review of materials seized from Rudy Giuliani}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/may/28/enate-republicans-capitol-attack-commission-joe-biden-covid-live-updates?page=with:block-60b14eec8f086d71cc15de83#block-60b14eec8f086d71cc15de83"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released a statement}}}\uc2  condemning the recent rise in anti-Semitic attacks across the country.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.28am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.45am BST\par \par \uc2 A gunman who killed nine of his co-workers at a rail yard in San Jose, California, had stockpiled weapons and ammunition at his home, including 12 guns and 22,000 rounds of ammunition, authorities said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Investigators found the cache of weapons at the home of Samuel James Cassidy, the Santa Clara county sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s office said in a news release. They also turned up multiple cans of gasoline and suspected molotov cocktails. Authorities have said that Cassidy set his house on fire using a timer or slow-burn device to coincide with his attack.\par \par \uc2 The guns he used to open fire on his co-workers appear to be legal, officials said. They have not said how he obtained them.\par \par \uc2 The nine victims in the worst mass shooting in the region have been identified as: Paul Delacruz Megia, 42; Taptejdeep Singh, 36; Adrian Balleza, 29; Jose Dejesus Hernandez III, 35; Timothy Michael Romo, 49; Michael Joseph Rudometkin, 40; Abdolvahab Alaghmandan, 63, Lars Kepler Lane, 63; and Alex Ward Fritch, 49.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/28/san-jose-shooting-gunman-home-weapons-ammunition"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 San Jose gunman stockpiled weapons and 22,000 rounds of ammunition}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.32am BST\par \par \uc2 The US Post Office announced today that it is increasing the price of a first-class postage stamp \u8211\'20\'13 from 55 cents to 58 cents \u8211\'20\'13 in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/us-post-office-plans-raise-stamp-price-58-cents-2021-05-28/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 effort to offset declining revenues}}}\uc2 , Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Mail volume has decreased 28% in the last ten years, USPS said in a statement. The rates for international letters and postcards will also increase later this summer.\par \par \uc2 The postmaster general, \uc2 Louis DeJoy\uc2 , is working to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2021/05/28/usps-rate-hike-stamps/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 erase $160bn in projected liabilities}}}\uc2  over the next decade. More details on the changes here:\par \par \uc2 enltrPostal Service raises rates, sending the price of a first-class stamp to 58 cents {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xe6iMydwRm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/xe6iMydwRm}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Washington Post (@washingtonpost) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/washingtonpost/status/1398363377890648075?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s proposed 2022 budget removes a ban on federal funding for most abortions that has been included in government spending bills for decades, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/biden-budget-drops-hyde-amendment-allow-public-funding-abortion-2021-05-28/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The budget, released today, omits any mention of the Hyde amendment, which was first passed in 1976, and has been included in spending bills since.\par \par \uc2 That change, however, is not likely to get through the Senate:\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Biden's budget drops the Hyde amendment, the decades-old ban on federal funding for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that he pledged to get rid of on the campaign trail. But the change is unlikely to survive the 50-50 Senate. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XcGW6MXLeQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/XcGW6MXLeQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alice Miranda Ollstein (@AliceOllstein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AliceOllstein/status/1398331135361441799?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The longstanding amendment restricts \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  coverage for recipients of Medicare, Medicaid, federal employees, service members and Washington DC residents. It could still be added to a later spending bill. Advocates celebrated:\par \par \uc2 enltrExciting to see the admin\u8217\'20\'19s historic step! For too long, the Hyde amendment has put the gov't in control of personal health care decisions for people with low incomes. Your ZIP code, income, or health insurance should never determine the care you can access, incl. \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CCCUAft8Wd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/CCCUAft8Wd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Planned Parenthood (@PPFA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PPFA/status/1398335436469248002?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The move comes at a time when the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement in the US is emboldened and looking forward to a supreme court case directly challenging the laws underpinning the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US. More here from \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s health reporter, Jessica Glenza:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/25/anti-abortion-movement-bullish-us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  movement bullish as legal campaign reaches US supreme court}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is working to \u8220\'20\'1Cdramatically reshape\u8221\'20\'1D the way asylum seekers are processed, in an effort to prevent a growing backlog of immigration court cases, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.buzzfeednews.com/article/hamedaleaziz/biden-new-asylum-process-plan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BuzzFeed News reported}}}\uc2 , citing government documents.\par \par \uc2 enltrSCOOP: The Biden administration is planning to dramatically reshape how asylum-seekers are processed in order to prevent an increase to the backlog of immigration court cases, according to government docs \uc2 BuzzFeed\uc2  News obtained. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/X9AOKEepWD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/X9AOKEepWD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hamed Aleaziz (@Haleaziz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Haleaziz/status/1398354662982520834?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The changes could cut the waiting period by years for some applicants, according to reporter Hamed Aleaziz. The new policy, which is not finalized yet, would give asylum officers the power to decide cases instead of immigration judges in certain instances.\par \par \uc2 enltrDepending on how it is implemented, the plan could represent President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s most consequential immigration policy to date and fundamentally change the dynamics at the southern border by preventing asylum cases from taking years to complete in court.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hamed Aleaziz (@Haleaziz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Haleaziz/status/1398354931170430978?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration overhauled the asylum process in significant ways, creating more obstacles for migrants seeking protection in the US. From the draft Biden policy cited in the report:\par \par \uc2 If there is any area of agreement on immigration, it is that the system for dealing with asylum claims at the border is \u8216\'20\'18overwhelmed\u8217\'20\'19 and in desperate need of repair. A system that takes years to get to a result is not a working system. It is unfair to those who need protection, and it encourages abuse by those undeserving of protection and the smugglers who exploit dysfunction for profit. The aim of this rule is to begin urgently replacing a broken system with a more efficient one, adjudicating asylum claims expeditiously without [compromising] fairness.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 CDC\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/28/health/summer-camps-masks-covid-19.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released new guidelines}}}\uc2  for children\u8217\'20\'19s summer camps, saying unvaccinated kids generally {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/coronavirus/2019-ncov/community/schools-childcare/summer-camps.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 do not have to wear masks outside}}}\uc2 , except for activities that involve sustained close contact:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCamp programs should encourage people who are not fully vaccinated and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/coronavirus/2019-ncov/need-extra-precautions/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 those who might need extra precautions}}}\uc2  to wear a mask consistently and correctly,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 CDC\uc2  said, explaining:\par \par \uc2 * Indoors. Mask use indoors is strongly encouraged for people who are not fully vaccinated including children. No child under the age of 2 should wear a mask.\par \par \uc2 * Outdoors. In general, people do not need to wear masks when outdoors. However, particularly in areas of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://covid.cdc.gov/covid-data-tracker/#county-view"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 substantial to high transmission}}}\uc2 , people who are not fully vaccinated are encouraged to wear a mask in crowded outdoor settings or during activities that involve sustained close contact with other people who are not fully vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 More info here:\par \par \uc2 enltrCDC eases summer camp guidance, saying kids will not always need masks {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DioWG6HLN3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/DioWG6HLN3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Washington Post (@washingtonpost) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/washingtonpost/status/1398339264627331081?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 A federal judge is appointing a \u8220\'20\'1Cspecial master\u8221\'20\'1D to protect attorney-client privilege during a review of materials seized fro m \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  and another attorney who has represented \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/28/rudy-giuliani-judge-special-master-electronic-devices"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AP reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The judge rejected efforts by Giuliani and lawyer Victoria Toensing to force prosecutors to divulge more about why they seized electronic devices on 28 April. Prosecutors made the unusual request for the appointment of a lawyer or \u8220\'20\'1Cspecial master\u8221\'20\'1D to protect attorney-client privilege the day after the raids, citing the need to make it clear that materials were reviewed appropriately.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors are examining Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s interactions with Ukrainian figures and whether he violated a law governing lobbying on behalf of foreign countries or entities.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors later revealed that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  had successfully downloaded 11 devices belonging to Giuliani and returned them to him.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/28/rudy-giuliani-judge-special-master-electronic-devices"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Judge to appoint a \u8216\'20\'18special master\u8217\'20\'19 in Rudy Giuliani case}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 My colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/abene-clayton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton}}}\uc2  spent time in San Jose yesterday where families were mourning the sudden losses of their loved ones in the Bay Area\u8217\'20\'19s worst mass shooting.\par \par \uc2 The shooting unfolded on Wednesday when a 57-year-old employee of the Valley Transportation Authority (VTA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/27/san-jose-shooting-gunman-talked-about-killing-people"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 walked}}}\uc2  into a facility and opened fire, killing nine of his co-workers.\par \par \uc2 enltrIn Downtown San Jose, hundreds of people, including dozens of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VTA?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @VTA}}}\uc2  employees have gathered for a vigil in honor of their colleagues who were slain yesterday. Manny are here wearing t-shirts with the names and faces of their deceased co-workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uL9Uk7CLRb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/uL9Uk7CLRb}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 N\u233\'00\'E9n\u233\'00\'E9 (@abene_writes) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/abene_writes/status/1398080604424478722?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 John Costa, the president of the union that the slain rail workers belonged to, offered words to remember the victims: Paul Delacruz Megia, 42; Taptejdeep Singh, 36; Adrian Balleza, 29; Jose Dejesus Hernandez III, 35; Timothy Michael Romo, 49; Michael Joseph Rudometkin, 40; Abdolvahab Alaghmandan, 63, Lars Kepler Lane, 63; and Alex Ward Fritch, 49.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want to send a message that we have to honor our brothers today and not forget what happened here,\u8221\'20\'1D Costa said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/28/san-jose-shooting-vigil-victims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 San Jose mourns after deadliest shooting in region\u8217\'20\'19s history: \u8216\'20\'18We can\u8217\'20\'19t sweep this under the rug\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Family of Capitol officer who died after attack: 'all talk and no action'\par \par \uc2 Hi all - Sam Levin in Los Angeles here, continuing our live coverage for the rest of the day.\par \par \uc2 The mother of Brian Sicknick, the Capitol police officer who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/15/brian-sicknick-death-arrests-capitol-attack-bear-spray"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 died}}}\uc2  after the 6 January insurrection, has spoken out about Senate Republicans blocking the creation of a special commission to study the attack.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t understand it. They are elected for us, the people, and they don\u8217\'20\'19t care about that,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/05/28/politics/sicknick-interview-disappointed-gop-senators/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gladys Sicknick told CNN}}}\uc2  after meeting with GOP senators on Thursday. \u8220\'20\'1CThey care about money, I guess, their pocketbooks. So they\u8217\'20\'19ll be in front of the cameras when they feel like it. They just don\u8217\'20\'19t care, and it\u8217\'20\'19s not right.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Her son was sprayed with a chemical during the insurrection, collapsed and later suffered a stroke.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think you know it\u8217\'20\'19s all talk and no action. Clearly, they\u8217\'20\'19re not backing the blue,\u8221\'20\'1D Sandra Garza, the late officer\u8217\'20\'19s girlfriend, told CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Jake Tapper. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just unbelievable to me that they could do nothing about this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrAn honor to have on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheLeadCNN?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @TheLeadCNN}}}\uc2  today Sandra Garza, the partner of the late Capitol Police Officer Brian Sicknick, and Gladys Sicknick, his mother. They\u8217\'20\'19re in DC to lobby for the bipartisan Jan 6 Commission that the Senate GOP just blocked. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cBEWTyhgj8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/cBEWTyhgj8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Tapper (@jaketapper) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jaketapper/status/1398366758998888455?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/28/senate-republicans-6-january-capitol-attack-commission"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed the effort to set up a 9/11-style inquiry}}}\uc2  into the attack on the Capitol by a pro-Trump mob despite broad popular support for such an investigation and pleas from the family of a Capitol police officer who collapsed and died after the siege and other officers who battled the rioters.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/28/senate-republicans-6-january-capitol-attack-commission"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate Republicans block creation of US Capitol attack commission}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Sam Levin, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * Senate Republicans blocked the bill to form a bipartisan commission to study the Capitol insurrection. The final vote on whether to start debate on the commission bill was 54-35, with six {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  joining 48 Democrats in supporting the motion to advance the proposal. Democrats needed 60 votes to take up the bill because Republicans invoked the first official Senate filibuster of Joe Biden \u8217\'20\'19s presidency to defeat the legislation.\par \par \uc2 * Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer condemned Republicans for preventing the commission bill from moving forward. \u8220\'20\'1CShame on the Republican party for trying to sweep the horrors of that day under the rug because they\u8217\'20\'19re afraid of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said in a floor speech shortly after the vote concluded.\par \par \uc2 * Biden released his $6tn budget proposal, calling for massive investments in infrastructure, education and climate action. A president\u8217\'20\'19s budget proposal is largely considered a political document that outlines the White House\u8217\'20\'19s legislative priorities. However, if Biden\u8217\'20\'19s budget were adopted, it would increase \uc2 US government\uc2  spending to the highest levels since the second world war.\par \par \uc2 * Biden spoke to US troops to thank them for their service ahead of the Memorial Day holiday. Speaking at the military base in Hampton, Virginia, the president expressed appreciation for the sacrifices made by service members and their families. \u8220\'20\'1CSimply stated, you are the backbone of the country,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  became the first woman to deliver a commencement address at the \uc2 US Naval Academy in Annapolis, Maryland\uc2 . The vice-president told the Naval Academy graduates, \u8220\'20\'1CThe American people are depending on you: the best, the bravest, the most brilliant.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sam will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 The question now is not so much whether the Republican party can be saved any time in the foreseeable future. It is what {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  and the Democrats should do when faced with a party determined to subvert democracy through any means necessary, including violence.\par \par \uc2 On Friday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  in the Senate torpedoed an effort to create a bipartisan commission to investigate the deadly insurrection by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s supporters at the US Capitol on 6 January, deploying the procedural move known as the filibuster to stop it even being debated.\par \par \uc2 Fearful perhaps of what such a commission might uncover about their own role as co-conspirators, most brushed aside personal pleas by Gladys Sicknick, the mother of a police officer who was that day sprayed with a chemical, collapsed and later had a stroke and died.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA country that cannot even agree to investigate an assault on its Capitol is in big trouble, indeed,\u8221\'20\'1D observed Susan Glasser in the New Yorker magazine.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/28/republicans-capitol-attack-commission-vote-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 blocking of the Capitol commission shows how deep the rot is}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden condemns rise in 'despicable' anti-Semitic attacks\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has released a statement condemning the recent rise in anti-Semitic attacks across the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese attacks are despicable, unconscionable, un-American, and they must stop,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said. \u8220\'20\'1CI will not allow our fellow Americans to be intimidated or attacked because of who they are or the faith they practice.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot allow the toxic combination of hatred, dangerous lies, and conspiracy theories to put our fellow Americans at risk.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden noted that attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  has pledged to deploy all tools available to the justice department to combat hate crimes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe must all stand together to silence these terrible and terrifying echoes of the worst chapters in world history, and pledge to give hate no safe harbor,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet us all take up that work and create a nation that stands for, and stands up for, the dignity and safety of all of our people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.adl.org/blog/antisemitic-incidents-reported-to-adl-increase-sharply-during-israel-hamas-conflict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Anti-Defamation League}}}\uc2 , reports of anti-Semitic hate incidents increased by 75% during the two weeks of military conflict between Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  in Gaza. Over those two weeks, 222 hate incidents were reported, compared to 127 for the two-week period before that.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMany of these incidents appear to have been perpetrated by individuals scapegoating American Jews for the actions of the Israeli government,\u8221\'20\'1D the ADL said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, congressional Republicans criticized \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s $6 trillion as a wasteful spending spree that would do little to improve Americans\u8217\'20\'19 lives.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden\u8217\'20\'19s proposal would drown American families in debt, deficits, and inflation,\u8221\'20\'1D Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden\u8217\'20\'19s proposal would drown American families in debt, deficits, and inflation.\par \par \uc2 My full statement: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5mulxq0UwO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/5mulxq0UwO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Leader McConnell (@LeaderMcConnell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LeaderMcConnell/status/1398338246199984131?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 McConnell noted that Senate Republicans laid out a counteroffer to the president\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure plan yesterday, calling for investing an additional $257 billion above baseline infrastructure spending over the next eight years. (Biden has called for spending $1.7 trillion above the baseline level on infrastructure.)\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Washington Democrats can move beyond the socialist daydreams and the go-it-alone partisanship, we could get a lot of important work done for our country,\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  praised \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s newly announced budget as \u8220\'20\'1Can unequivocal declaration of the value that Democrats place on America\u8217\'20\'19s workers and middle class families\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrA federal budget should be a statement of our national values. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  Biden\u8217\'20\'19s budget is an unequivocal declaration of the value that Democrats place on America\u8217\'20\'19s workers and middle class families, who are the foundation of our nation\u8217\'20\'19s strength and the key to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BuildBackBetter?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BuildBackBetter}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (@SpeakerPelosi) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerPelosi/status/1398359532657643521?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Biden budget makes historic investments in the American workforce and economy. It does so by seizing a once-in-a-generation opportunity to create millions of good-paying Americans jobs, supercharge America\u8217\'20\'19s global competitiveness and power growth for generations to come,\u8221\'20\'1D the Democratic speaker said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCongressional Democrats look forward to working with the Biden-Harris Administration to enact this visionary budget, which will pave the path to opportunity and prosperity for our nation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The release of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s budget comes as the White House continues to negotiate with Senate Republicans over an infrastructure bill, with the hope that the final proposal can attract bipartisan support in Congress.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris becomes first woman to deliver Naval Academy commencement address\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  delivered the commencement address this morning at the \uc2 US Naval Academy in Annapolis, Maryland\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The speech made the vice-president the first woman to address the academy\u8217\'20\'19s graduating class since its founding in 1845.\par \par \uc2 enltrVP Kamala Harris delivers 2021 \uc2 U.S. Naval Academy\uc2  commencement address.\par \par \uc2 Harris just became the first woman to give the graduation speech at the Naval Academy. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nbIFvZ7OYz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/nbIFvZ7OYz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1398290967896244231?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Harris expressed confidence that the Naval Academy graduates are prepared to meet any challenge they may face in a rapidly changing world.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe American people are depending on you: the best, the bravest, the most brilliant,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president said. \u8220\'20\'1CClass of 2021, you are prepared for all of this. You are prepared for any threat. And you are prepared for this new era.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden proposes $6tn budget to boost infrastructure, education and climate\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/dominic-rushe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dominic Rushe}}}\uc2  has the latest on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s $6tn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/28/joe-biden-budget-proposal-infrastructure-education-climate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 budget proposal}}}\uc2  Friday:\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s budget would fund a dramatic overhaul of US infrastructure, and dedicate extensive funds to education and climate action\u8212\'20\'14which would put government spending at its \u8220\'20\'1Chighest sustained levels since the second world war,\u8221\'20\'1D Rushe explains.\par \par \uc2 Importantly, Rushe points out, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s first budget is \u8220\'20\'1Clargely a political document.\u8221\'20\'1D While this proposal makes clear Biden\u8217\'20\'19s hopes for revitalizing the US in the wake of the coronavirus pandemic, Republicans are already chaffing against its scale.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, no Republicans voted in favor of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/10/joe-biden-covid-relief-bill-passed-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $1.9tn Covid stimulus bill}}}\uc2 . Biden has also been forced to limit his infrastructure bill to $1.7tn, down from his originally proposed $2.2tn initiative. So, the chances of getting GOP support for such a budget are slim.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s two-part initiative to revitalize the US economy is rooted in ramping up its flagging infrastructure and broadening its social safety net. These initiatives would cause the US to have yearly deficits of more than $1.3tn over the next 10 years, with debt increasing to 117% of the value of economic output before 2031.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s plan would be funded, in part, by increasing taxes on corporations and the extremely wealthy. He supports increasing corporate taxes to 28%, up from 21%. All Republicans oppose this tax increase plan, as do some Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/28/joe-biden-budget-proposal-infrastructure-education-climate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden proposes $6tn budget to boost infrastructure, education and climate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.49pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/may/27/joe-biden-republicans-covid-coronavirus-us-politics-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Manchin}}}\uc2  has slammed GOP senators who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/may/28/enate-republicans-capitol-attack-commission-joe-biden-covid-live-updates?page=with:block-60b117128f088d8c3178c299#block-60b117128f088d8c3178c299"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked }}}\uc2  the creation of a bipartisan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/may/28/enate-republicans-capitol-attack-commission-joe-biden-covid-live-updates?page=with:block-60b10c8c8f088d8c3178c1d4#block-60b10c8c8f088d8c3178c1d4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 commission }}}\uc2  to study the deadly Capitol insurrection on 6 January.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CChoosing to put politics and political elections above the health of our Democracy is unconscionable, and the betrayal of the oath we each take is something they will have to live with,\u8221\'20\'1D Manchin, a Democrat senator from West Virginia, has said.\par \par \uc2 enltrChoosing to put politics and political elections above the health of our Democracy is unconscionable. And the betrayal of the oath we each take is something they will have to live with. My statement on the January 6th Commission vote: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tlPme9LMIo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/tlPme9LMIo}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator Joe Manchin (@Sen_JoeManchin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Sen_JoeManchin/status/1398335147003502592?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was our chance to have a bipartisan commission that would allow for an impartial investigation into the events of that horrific day, so that we are better able to prevent another attack on our nation,\u8221\'20\'1D Manchin also says.\par \par \uc2 Manchin tells viewers that Democratic leadership in the house and Senate accepted Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 proposed changes \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause a commission of this nature must be bipartisan to be successful.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He recognizes the \u8220\'20\'1Csix brave Republicans\u8221\'20\'1D who favored establishing the commission, while pointing out that four more were needed to advance this legislation.\par \par \uc2 Manchin, in his address, has also issued a broad apology about the commission\u8217\'20\'19s failure to progress.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou deserve better, and I am sorry that my Republican colleagues and friends, let political fear prevent them from doing what they know in their hearts to be right.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s remarks to troops at Joint Base Langley-Eustis have now concluded. Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * Senate Republicans blocked consideration of the bill to form a bipartisan commission to study the Capitol insurrection. The final vote on whether to start debate on the commission bill was 54-35, with six {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  joining 48 Democrats in supporting the motion to advance the proposal. Democrats needed 60 votes to take up the bill because Republicans invoked the first official Senate filibuster of the Biden era to defeat the legislation.\par \par \uc2 * Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer condemned Republicans for preventing the commission bill from moving forward. \u8220\'20\'1CShame on the Republican party for trying to sweep the horrors of that day under the rug because they\u8217\'20\'19re afraid of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said in a floor speech shortly after the vote concluded.\par \par \uc2 * Biden spoke to US troops to thank them for their service ahead of the Memorial Day holiday. Speaking at the military base in Hampton, Virginia, the president expressed appreciation for the sacrifices made by service members and their families. \u8220\'20\'1CSimply stated, you are the backbone of the country,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden speaks to troops before Memorial Day: 'You are the backbone of the country'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  delivered remarks to US troops at Joint Base Langley-Eustis in Hampton, Virginia, ahead of Memorial Day weekend.\par \par \uc2 The president began his speech with an emotional retelling of how his son, Beau, decided to join the military. \uc2 Beau Biden\uc2  died of brain cancer in 2015.\par \par \uc2 Biden said the sacrifices that his son made to join the military reminded him of the sacrifices that service members and their families make every day.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSimply stated, you are the backbone of the country,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 enltr"Simply stated you are the backbone of this country, you are the backbone of the country," Pres. Biden says to military service members and their families. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dw4Kx8GzNd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/dw4Kx8GzNd}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MhgDWLWPS9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/MhgDWLWPS9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 This Week (@ThisWeekABC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ThisWeekABC/status/1398341889234030596?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden spoke at Joint Base Langley-Eustis before \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  delivered his own remarks to US troops ahead of the Memorial Day holiday.\par \par \uc2 The first lady, who has made supporting military families a primary focus of her work, expressed appreciation for the sacrifices of service members and their loved ones.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur military is a community bound together by love,\u8221\'20\'1D the first lady said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s time that our nation matches that devotion.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 The stage is set at Joint Base Langley-Eustis in Hampton, Virginia, where \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will soon speak to US troops to thank them for their service ahead of Memorial Day weekend.\par \par \uc2 enltrToday\u8217\'20\'19s site. Thank you, advance team! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SZou1kWrKK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SZou1kWrKK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Meghan Hays (@MegHays46) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MegHays46/status/1398335501212475394?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden celebrates progress in US fight against coronavirus in Virginia\par \par \uc2 As the Senate voted on the January 6 commission bill, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  delivered remarks on the country\u8217\'20\'19s fight against coronavirus in Alexandria, Virginia.\par \par \uc2 Appearing alongside Virginia Governor Ralph Northam, the president celebrated the significant progress that the state has made to limit the spread of coronavirus since he took office in January.\par \par \uc2 Virginia has received more than $247 million in federal funding for community vaccination sites, and more than 1,000 pharmacies across the state have participated in the federal vaccination program.\par \par \uc2 enltrPres. Biden: "If we succeed, we can celebrate our independence from the virus together on the Fourth of July, as we celebrate our independence as a nation. And the future is only going to get brighter." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/u6H8vujYyc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/u6H8vujYyc}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/82bvHFj7t0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/82bvHFj7t0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 This Week (@ThisWeekABC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ThisWeekABC/status/1398312614791364618?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 As more Virginians have gotten vaccinated, case numbers have consistently fallen in the state, with deaths and hospitalizations having decreased substantially since January.\par \par \uc2 Although this progress is encouraging, Biden emphasized the importance of getting even more Virginians vaccinated in order to get the virus under control by July 4.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we succeed, we can celebrate our independence from the virus together on the Fourth of July, as we celebrate our independence as a nation,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the future is only going to get brighter.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president and the first lady will also soon deliver remarks in Hampton, Virginia, to kick off the start of Memorial Day weekend, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Sam Levine reports on the upcoming Senate vote on Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 election reform bill:\par \par \uc2 The senate will vote in about a month on sweeping legislation that would dramatically expand access to the ballot box , Chuck Schumer, the senate majority leader, said Friday.\par \par \uc2 The announcement came immediately after senate Republicans blocked the creation of a bipartisan commission to probe the 6 January attack on the US capitol. Republicans used the filibuster, a procedural tactic that prevents legislation from moving ahead in the senate unless it has 60 votes.\par \par \uc2 enltrIn a Dear Colleague letter, Senate Majority Leader Chuck Schumer announces a pretty ambitious schedule with a vote on S1 during the last week of June. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/o67dexFMg9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/o67dexFMg9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Daniel Strauss (@DanielStrauss4) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DanielStrauss4/status/1398320339055222788?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The comments from Schumer are significant because there is some {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/27/democrats-voting-rights-us-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  handwringing}}}\uc2  over how exactly Democrats plan to get over the filibuster when it comes to passing the sweeping voting rights bill.\par \par \uc2 Those conversations have become more urgent in recent weeks as Republicans have moved aggressively in state legislatures across the country to impose new restrictions. Schumer said the senate would vote on the bill during the last week of the senate\u8217\'20\'19s June work period.\par \par \uc2 A key senator in the vote will be Joe Manchin, a West Virginia Democrat, who continues to back the filibuster, even as it harms his own party. Manchin has also said he wants bipartisan buy-in for the bill. After the Friday filibuster blocking the 6 January commission, Manchin tweaked Republicans for not supporting the panel.\par \par \uc2 enltr"To see fear take over is truly disheartening," Joe Manchin told reporters after the vote, calling Republicans cowards in an oblique way\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Arthur Delaney (@ArthurDelaneyHP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ArthurDelaneyHP/status/1398318726341144581?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pelosi: 'Republican Senators surrendered to the January 6th mob assault'\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  sharply criticized Senate Republicans for blocking consideration of the January 6 commission bill.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  asked Senate Republicans to do him a \u8216\'20\'18personal favor\u8217\'20\'19 and vote against the January 6th Commission,\u8221\'20\'1D the Democratic speaker said in a new statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn doing so, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  asked them to be complicit in his undermining of the truth of January 6th. In bowing to McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s personal favor request, Republican Senators surrendered to the January 6th mob assault.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pelosi argued the vote on the commission bill brought \u8220\'20\'1Cshame\u8221\'20\'1D to the Senate and would make the country less safe. She indicated that House committees, which are under Democratic leadership, would continue to investigate the attack.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHonoring our responsibility to the Congress in which we serve and the Country which we love, Democrats will proceed to find the truth,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  commended the six Republican senators who voted in favor of taking up the January 6 commission bill.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThank you to Senators Cassidy, Collins, Murkowski, Portman, Sasse, and Romney for voting for truth and defense of our constitution,\u8221\'20\'1D the Republican congresswoman said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CHistory will remember those who put country ahead of politics.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrThank you to Senators Cassidy, Collins, Murkowski, Portman, Sasse, and Romney for voting for truth and defense of our constitution. History will remember those who put country ahead of politics.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  (@Liz_Cheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Liz_Cheney/status/1398318341123629060?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Cheney was ousted as House Republican conference chair earlier this month over her criticism of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s lies about the presidential election, which sparked the Capitol attack.\par \par \uc2 Last week, Cheney voted with 34 other House Republicans and every House Democrat in support of the commission bill.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Progressives are already pointing to the Republican blockade of the January 6 commission bill as evidence for why Senate Democrats should eliminate the filibuster.\par \par \uc2 Senator Elizabeth Warren said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CIf Senate Republicans can block an independent commission investigating a deadly armed attack on the Capitol because it might hurt their poll numbers with insurrectionists, then something is badly wrong with the Senate. We must get rid of the filibuster to protect our democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrIf Senate Republicans can block an independent commission investigating a deadly armed attack on the Capitol because it might hurt their poll numbers with insurrectionists, then something is badly wrong with the Senate. We must get rid of the filibuster to protect our democracy. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/foIyeTOFar"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/foIyeTOFar}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Elizabeth Warren (@SenWarren) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWarren/status/1398313195664781320?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 At least two Senate Democrats -- Joe Manchin and \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  -- have indicated they are still against eliminating the filibuster.\par \par \uc2 Although Manchin expressed severe disappointment about today\u8217\'20\'19s vote, he previously indicated he would not be willing to end the filibuster to make the commission happen.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Republican Senator \uc2 Pat Toomey\uc2  told HuffPost that he was not in Washington for the commission bill vote today because of a family obligation.\par \par \uc2 However, the spokesperson said, Toomey would have voted in favor of starting debate on the bill.\par \par \uc2 enltrSen. Toomey's spokesperson tells me he missed the vote because of a family commitment but would have supported advancing Jan 6 commission bill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4N5EHw7IIO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4N5EHw7IIO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Igor Bobic (@igorbobic) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/igorbobic/status/1398315350412910592?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The Pennsylvania senator also voted to convict \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for incitement of insurrection shortly after the Capitol attack, and he had expressed openness to the commission proposal.\par \par \uc2 Toomey\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Caye\u8221\'20\'1D vote would have made seven Republicans in support of advancing the bill, but that is still short of 10 Republican votes necessary to overcome the filibuster.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 'Shame on the Republican Party,' Schumer says after January 6 commission bill fails\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer condemned his Republican colleagues for blocking consideration of the bill to form a bipartisan commission to study the Capitol insurrection.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShame on the Republican Party for trying to sweep the horrors of that day under the rug because they\u8217\'20\'19re afraid of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said in a floor speech moments ago.\par \par \uc2 enltrSen. Schumer after a failed vote on a Jan. 6 commission: "The Republican minority just prevented the American people from getting the full truth."\par \par \uc2 "Shame on the Republican Party for trying to sweep the horrors of that day under the rug because they're afraid of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/t63QMG5aNX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/t63QMG5aNX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MSNBC (@MSNBC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MSNBC/status/1398316454609575936?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 This marked Senate Republicans \u8217\'20\'19 first official use of the filibuster to defeat a bill, and Schumer said he hoped this was not the beginning of a trend of Republicans blocking \u8220\'20\'1Creasonable, common-sense legislation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Because Republicans invoked the filibuster, Democrats needed 60 votes to take up the commission bill, and they only got 54 by the time the vote was gaveled out.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 The six Senate Republicans who voted with Democrats in favor of taking up the January 6 commission bill were \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2 , \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2 , \uc2 Bill Cassidy\uc2 , Lisa Murkowski, \uc2 Ben Sasse\uc2  and Rob Portman.\par \par \uc2 Two Republican senators who voted earlier this year to convict \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for incitement of insurrection, \uc2 Pat Toomey\uc2  and \uc2 Richard Burr\uc2 , were not present for the vote.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate Republicans block January 6 commission bill\par \par \uc2 Republicans have successfully blocked the Senate from taking up the bill to form a bipartisan commission to study the Capitol insurrection.\par \par \uc2 The final vote was 54-35, with six Republicans joining 48 Democrats in supporting the motion to advance the bill. Eleven senators did not participate in the vote.\par \par \uc2 enltrNot invoked, 54-35: Motion to invoke cloture on the motion to proceed to Cal. #60, H.R.3233, January 6th Commission. (60 vote affirmative threshold)\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senate Cloakroom (@SenateCloakroom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenateCloakroom/status/1398311722948120581?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Democrats needed 10 of their Republican colleagues to join them in order to break the filibuster and take up the commission bill, but they fell short of that.\par \par \uc2 The January 6 commission is dead -- for now, at least.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator Joe Manchin told reporters that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cvery disappointed\u8221\'20\'1D about the likely defeat of the January 6 commission bill.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPolitics has trumped - literally and figuratively - the good of the country,\u8221\'20\'1D the Democratic senator said, according to a Wall Street Journal reporter.\par \par \uc2 enltrA distressed Manchin, as the commission appears headed for defeat in the Senate:\par \par \uc2 "I'm very disappointed, very frustrated that politics has trumped - literally and figuratively - the good of the country." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/APn2FluQW1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/APn2FluQW1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lindsay Wise (@lindsaywise) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lindsaywise/status/1398309078103961602?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Republicans will likely be able to defeat the commission bill because of the 60-vote threshold needed to overcome a Senate filibuster.\par \par \uc2 But Manchin has continued to defend the filibuster, saying he is unwilling to eliminate it, even if it means the commission will not happen.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rob Portman of Ohio has become the sixth Republican senator to vote in favor of taking up the January 6 commission bill.\par \par \uc2 Portman voted to acquit \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in his impeachment trial earlier this year, but the senator acknowledged the former president had \u8220\'20\'1Cencouraged the mob\u8221\'20\'1D to attack the Capitol on January 6.\par \par \uc2 Democrats need four more Republicans to join them in order to overcome a filibuster of the commission bill.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Two more Republican senators, Lisa Murkowski of Alaska and \uc2 Ben Sasse\uc2  of Nebraska, have voted in favor of taking up the January 6 commission bill.\par \par \uc2 That makes five Republicans total who have voted with Democrats so far, but it remains unlikely that five more Republicans will join them.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Because of the Republican filibuster, 60 votes are needed just to start the Senate debate over the January 6 commission bill.\par \par \uc2 Only three Republicans -- \uc2 Bill Cassidy\uc2  of Louisiana, \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  of Maine and \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  of Massachusetts -- have voted in favor of advancing the bill so far.\par \par \uc2 It seems very unlikely that seven more Republicans will join Democrats in voting to take up the bill, so the proposal will almost certainly be defeated.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Before the vote began, Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer pleaded with his colleagues to support the January 6 commission bill.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis commission is desperately needed,\u8221\'20\'1D the Democratic leader said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf our Republican friends vote against this, I would ask them: what are you afraid of? The truth?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr"This commission is desperately needed," Senate Majority Leader Schumer said ahead of a vote on the proposed Jan. 6th commission.\par \par \uc2 "If our Republican friends vote against this, I would ask them: what are you afraid of? The truth?" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/bDMfLL8f10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/bDMfLL8f10}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NbI8VM0vs9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/NbI8VM0vs9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News (@ABC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABC/status/1398301093252173825?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Schumer argued \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s lies about widespread fraud in the presidential election had \u8220\'20\'1Ceroded\u8221\'20\'1D American democracy and the commission was necessary to rebut those lies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not a Democratic or Republican obligation. This is an American obligation,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate now voting on January 6 commission bill\par \par \uc2 The Senate is now holding a procedural vote on the bill to create a bipartisan commission to study the Capitol insurrection.\par \par \uc2 enltrNOW VOTING: Motion to invoke cloture on the motion to proceed to Cal. #60, H.R.3233, January 6th Commission. (60 vote affirmative threshold)\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senate Cloakroom (@SenateCloakroom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenateCloakroom/status/1398298992681930762?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The bill is not likely to advance, as only a handful of Republicans have indicated they will support the proposal and Democrats need 60 votes to break a filibuster.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate to hold procedural vote on January 6 commission bill in the next hour\par \par \uc2 The Senate has reached an agreement to delay final consideration of the Endless Frontier Act until after the Memorial Day holiday.\par \par \uc2 The upper chamber will now shift focus to a procedural vote on the bill to form a bipartisan commission to study the Capitol insurrection, as well as votes on two of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nominees.\par \par \uc2 enltrVote Update: The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Senate?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Senate}}}\uc2  will shortly proceed to up to 3 votes on:\par \par \uc2 1. Cloture on the motion to proceed to H.R.3233, January 6th Commission.\par \par \uc2 2. Confirmation of Anton Hajjar to be a Governor of the USPS for a term expiring December 8, 2023.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senate Press Gallery (@SenatePress) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenatePress/status/1398297404898742273?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer said moments ago that the commission bill vote will occur sometime in the next hour.\par \par \uc2 Republicans are expected to defeat the bill, as Democrats will need 60 votes to overcome a filibuster of the proposal.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Senate vote on the January 6 commission bill may actually happen sooner rather than later, with a potential deal between Democrats and Republicans in the works.\par \par \uc2 According to multiple reports, Republicans are discussing the possibility of delaying final passage of the Endless Frontier Act until after Memorial Day weekend.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: Senate leaders are seeking unanimous consent to punt final passage of USICA/EFA to June 8, allowing votes on 1/6 Commission and two Biden noms today and letting senators start their break. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/S362eEZInd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/S362eEZInd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mike DeBonis (@mikedebonis) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mikedebonis/status/1398289324366614539?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 If Democrats agree to that, then the Senate will vote on the commission bill and two of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s nominations before leaving for the holiday weekend.\par \par \uc2 However, it\u8217\'20\'19s still unclear if Democrats will be on board, as they wanted to wrap up the Endless Frontier Act before going into recess. Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Russian \uc2 SolarWinds\uc2  hackers launch email attack on government agencies\par \par \uc2 Guardian staff and agencies report:\par \par \uc2 The state-backed Russian cyber spies behind the \uc2 SolarWinds\uc2  hacking campaign launched a targeted phishing assault on US and foreign government agencies and thinktanks this week using an email marketing account of the \uc2 US Agency for International Development\uc2  (\uc2 USAid\uc2 ), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/microsoft"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Microsoft}}}\uc2  has said.\par \par \uc2 The effort targeted about 3,000 email accounts at more than 150 different organisations, at least a quarter of them involved in international development, humanitarian and human rights work, the Microsoft vice-president Tom Burt {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bit.ly/2SzLGmO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote in a blog post late on Thursday}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It did not say what portion of the attempts may have led to successful intrusions. The cybersecurity firm Volexity, which also tracked the campaign but has less visibility into email systems than \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 , said in a post that relatively low detection rates of the phishing emails suggested the attacker was \u8220\'20\'1Clikely having some success in breaching targets\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  identified the group carrying out the attacks as Nobelium, originating from Russia and the same actor behind the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2020/dec/15/orion-hack-solar-winds-explained-us-treasury-commerce-department"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attacks on SolarWinds customers in 2020}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Burt said the campaign appeared to be a continuation of efforts by the Russian hackers to \u8220\'20\'1Ctarget government agencies involved in foreign policy as part of intelligence-gathering efforts\u8221\'20\'1D. He said the targets spanned at least 24 countries.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/may/28/russian-solarwinds-hackers-launch-assault-government-agencies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russian SolarWinds hackers launch email attack on government agencies}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Another issue as the Senate prepares to vote on the January 6 commission bill: about 10 senators have already left town for Memorial Day weekend, according to Fox News reporter Chad Pergram.\par \par \uc2 enltr1) There are about ten senators who have cut town for the Memorial Day break, even though the Senate was in session until 2:51 am et today and likely will be in most of the day today.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chad Pergram (@ChadPergram) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChadPergram/status/1398281948116758531?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Even though the Senate may not be at full attendance today, the number of senators required to break the expected Republican filibuster of the commission bill will not change.\par \par \uc2 So even if only 90 senators are present to vote on the bill later today, 60 votes will still be required to advance the legislation past the filibuster.\par \par \uc2 Republicans are expected to defeat the bill because Democrats need 10 of their colleagues from across the aisle to vote with them to break a filibuster, and that seems extremely unlikely to happen.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  said he hopes the vote on the January 6 commission bill will happen today, but he did not definitively say whether he thought that would happen.\par \par \uc2 According to CNN, reporters asked McConnell as he entered the Senate how long today\u8217\'20\'19s session will take. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ll have to ask the folks who feel compelled to speak,\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell replied.\par \par \uc2 enltrAs he entered the Senate, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  said when asked how long today\u8217\'20\'19s session will take: \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ll have to ask the folks who feel compelled to speak.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked if he thinks votes on the China bill and Jan. 6 bill will be done today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hope so but we will see how it goes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1398277670518001672?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Asked if the votes on the Endless Frontier Act and the January 6 commission bill will wrap up today, the Republican leader said, \u8220\'20\'1CI hope so, but we will see how it goes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Senate had expected to give final approval to the Endless Frontier Act yesterday, but some late-night disagreements pushed that to today. Senator \uc2 Jon Ossoff\uc2  did not gavel out the Senate until almost 3 am this morning, and the chamber returned from recess about six hours later.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden will join \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  when he travels to Europe next month, the White House has just announced.\par \par \uc2 The White House said the first lady will accompany her husband as he attends the \uc2 G-7\uc2  summit in Cornwall from June 11 to 13.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis will be the first overseas travel by President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and First Lady Jill Biden,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis trip will highlight the President\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to restoring our alliances, showing that democracies can deliver, and working in close cooperation with our allies and multilateral partners.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 CNN reported earlier this week that Biden will meet with Queen Elisabeth II during his trip to the UK, but the White House has not yet confirmed that plan.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is making some history this morning: the vice-president will become the first woman to deliver the commencement address at the \uc2 US Naval Academy in Annapolis, Maryland\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/28/us/politics/kamala-harris-commencement-speech-naval-academy.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The vice president\u8217\'20\'19s speech is expected to focus on some of the Biden administration \u8217\'20\'19s most urgent challenges, like the coronavirus pandemic, climate change and a host of increasingly sophisticated cybersecurity threats.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The global pandemic has launched us into a new era. It has forever impacted our world,\u8217\'20\'19 Ms. Harris is expected to say, according to prepared remarks shared with The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 . \u8216\'20\'18If we weren\u8217\'20\'19t clear before, we know now: Our world is interconnected. Our world is interdependent. Our world is fragile.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The vice president\u8217\'20\'19s speech at the Naval Academy, in Annapolis, Md., will be her first to focus on the military, and it comes as the Biden administration is accelerating its withdrawal of troops from Afghanistan, well ahead of the deadline President Biden set in April: Sept. 11.\par \par \uc2 According to a press pool report, Harris stopped at the gravesite of \uc2 John McCain\uc2  before her speech to pay her respects to the late senator and lay some flowers on his headstone.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Arizona \u8216\'20\'18refurbishes\u8217\'20\'19 its gas chamber to prepare for executions, documents reveal\par \par \uc2 The state of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2  is preparing to kill death row inmates using hydrogen cyanide, the same lethal gas that was deployed at Auschwitz.\par \par \uc2 Documents obtained by \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  reveal that Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s department of corrections has spent more than $2,000 in procuring the ingredients to make cyanide gas. The department bought a solid brick of potassium cyanide in December for $1,530.\par \par \uc2 It also purchased sodium hydroxide pellets and sulfuric acid which are intended to be used to generate the deadly gas. The gas chamber itself, built in 1949 and disused for 22 years, has been dusted off and, according to the department, \u8220\'20\'1Crefurbished\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Over the past few months the Republican-controlled state has moved aggressively to restart its deeply flawed execution system. The death penalty has been in abeyance in Arizona for seven years following the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2014/aug/02/arizona-inmate-injected-15-times-execution-drugs-joseph-wood"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gruesomely botched lethal injection}}}\uc2  of Joseph Wood in 2014.\par \par \uc2 Last month, \uc2 the Guardian{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/apr/09/revealed-republican-led-states-secretly-spending-huge-sums-on-execution-drugs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revealed}}}\uc2  that Arizona spent a jaw-dropping $1.5m on a batch of pentobarbital in October, a sedative which it now hopes to use as its main lethal injection method.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/28/arizona-gas-chamber-executions-documents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona \u8216\'20\'18refurbishes\u8217\'20\'19 its gas chamber to prepare for executions, documents reveal}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Senate is now back in session to wrap up votes on the Endless Frontier Act before holding a vote on the January 6 commission bill.\par \par \uc2 The upper chamber stood in recess for a little over six hours. Democratic Senator \uc2 Jon Ossoff\uc2  of Georgia gaveled out the Senate at 2:52 am this morning, per a C-SPAN producer.\par \par \uc2 enltr2:52am: GA Senator Jon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ossoff?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ossoff}}}\uc2  gaveled out the Senate earlier this morning. A sleepy Senate returns at 9am for more work on the science and tech research China bill with votes expected later today including on the January 6th Commission bill, ahead for their Memorial Day break. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xyWdXicHAS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xyWdXicHAS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Craig Caplan (@CraigCaplan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CraigCaplan/status/1398259388956266496?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer said in a floor speech moments ago that he expects the chamber to pass the Endless Frontier Act later today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have every intention of sticking it out until the job is done, and that\u8217\'20\'19s what we\u8217\'20\'19re going to do,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 At least 70% of people charged in the Capitol riot have been released as they wait for trial, according to a Guardian analysis.\par \par \uc2 That high pretrial release rate stands in stark contrast with the usual detention rates in the federal system, where only {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uscourts.gov/sites/default/files/data_tables/jb_h14_0930.2019.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  25% of defendants nationwide}}}\uc2  are typically released before their trial.\par \par \uc2 Eric Munchel, known as \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/10/us-capitol-mob-rioters-arrests-violence-brutality"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Zip Tie Guy}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, who was allegedly photographed wearing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/10/us-capitol-mob-rioters-arrests-violence-brutality"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tactical gear and carrying wrist restraints}}}\uc2  in the Senate chamber, was released in late March, along with his mother, after an appeals court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/03/26/capitol-riot-defendants-win-appeals-court-478157"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 questioned whether he posed any danger}}}\uc2  outside the specific context of 6 January.\par \par \uc2 Richard Barnett, the Arkansas man photographed with his foot on \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s desk, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/local/legal-issues/pelosi-desk-rioter-released/2021/04/27/9fb5f3f8-a797-11eb-8d25-7b30e74923ea_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released in late April}}}\uc2 , nearly two months after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/05/us-capitol-riot-man-pelosi-feet-desk-richard-barnett"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 screaming during a court hearing}}}\uc2  that \u8220\'20\'1Cit\u8217\'20\'19s not fair\u8221\'20\'1D that he was still in custody when \u8220\'20\'1Ceverybody else who did things much worse are already home\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Multiple alleged members of the Proud Boys and the Oath Keepers, two groups facing the most serious conspiracy charges related to their alleged plans for violence, have been released before trial, though some prominent leaders in these groups remain in custody.\par \par \uc2 The disparity in pretrial detention rates highlights what legal experts said was a broader development in the 6 January cases: the likelihood that a substantial swathe of the alleged rioters may not serve any prison time at all, even if they are convicted or plead guilty.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/28/us-capitol-attack-suspects-jail-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Revealed: majority of people charged in Capitol attack aren\u8217\'20\'19t in jail}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate Republicans expected to defeat January 6 commission bill\par \par \uc2 Greetings from Washington, live blog readers.\par \par \uc2 The Senate is expected to vote later today on whether to advance the bill to form a bipartisan commission to study the Capitol insurrection \u8211\'20\'13 for real this time.\par \par \uc2 The Senate was originally planning to hold a procedural vote on the commission bill yesterday, but some late-night disagreements over the Endless Frontier Act pushed the vote to today.\par \par \uc2 Now the vote is expected to take place later this morning or possibly early this afternoon, according to CNN.\par \par \uc2 enltrSenate update: Key vote on Jan. 6 bill will spill into later Friday AM and potentially afternoon as some GOP senators delay final votes on China bill to raise concerns over the process. (Jan. 6 bill is next up). GOP sens now speaking on floor overnight\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1398141780873338881?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Senate Republican leaders seem confident that they have the votes to defeat the bill, which they worry could jeopardize their hopes of taking back Congress in next year\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Senator Lisa Murkowski, one of the few Republicans who is expected to support the commission bill, sharply criticized that logic yesterday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo be making a decision for the short-term political gain at the expense of understanding and acknowledging what was in front of us on January 6, I think we need to look at that critically. Is that really what this is about, one election cycle after another?\u8221\'20\'1D Murkowski {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/january-6-commission-murkowski-mcconnell_n_60b046e4e4b0c5658f91cff4?35i"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told reporters}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more details on the vote as it unfolds, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210528eh5s001ut\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
