\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 House votes to establish commission to investigate Capitol attack \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now) and Joan E Greve (earlier) \par \uc2 8,079 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 May 2021\par 00:44 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Republicans were urged to support the proposal and 35 voted in favorBiden speaks to Netanyahu about Gaza conflictMcConnell announces opposition to Capitol attack commission billSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  told \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  he expects a \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant de-escalation today on the path to a ceasefire,\u8221\'20\'1D according to a White House readout of the latest call between the US president and the Israeli prime minister. The call comes as Israeli forces and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  continue to exchange attacks in Gaza, and Netanyahu said today that Israel is \u8220\'20\'1Cdetermined to continue this operation until its aim is met\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * The House voted 252-175 to establish a commission investigating the 6 January attack on the US Capitol. Among those who voted in favor of establishing the commission were 35 Republicans. But the legislation will face big hurdles in Senate, as minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  opposes the bill. McConnell called the commission \u8220\'20\'1Cslanted\u8221\'20\'1D, though Republicans and Democrats would be equally represented on it.\par \par \uc2 * House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  sharply criticized Republicans for opposing the January 6 commission bill. The Democratic speaker said at a press conference this afternoon, \u8220\'20\'1CIt sounds like they are afraid of the truth, and that\u8217\'20\'19s most unfortunate, but hopefully they\u8217\'20\'19ll get used to the idea that the American people want us to find the truth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * House Democrats defeated an effort by minority leader Kevin McCarthy to end the mask mandate in the chamber. Several Republican lawmakers have been refusing to wear masks. Pelosi has maintained that the mask mandate should remain in place, as it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear that all the lawmakers and their staff have been vaccinated. Some Republicans have publicly rejected the vaccine or refused to disclose whether or not they had gotten it.\par \par \uc2 * Survivors of the 1921 Tulsa race massacre testified before a House committee, as lawmakers consider whether to compensate the massacre survivors and their descendants. One survivor, 107-year-old Viola Fletcher, told the committee, \u8220\'20\'1CI am here seeking justice. I am here asking my country to acknowledge what happened in Tulsa in 1921.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The Texas governor signed a bill banning abortions after six weeks of pregnancy, despite widespread criticism from the medical and legal communities. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups have indicated they will legally challenge the law.\par \par \uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 Joan E Greve and Maanvi Singh\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.07am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.42am BST\par \par \uc2 A group of anonymous Capitol Police officers expressed \u8220\'20\'1Cprofound disappointment\u8221\'20\'1D in House minority leader Kevin McCarthy and Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  over their opposition to creating the commission.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is inconceivable that some of the Members we protect, would downplay the events of January 6th. Member safety was dependent upon the heroic actions of the USCP,\u8221\'20\'1D they said in a letter.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEWS: MEMBERS of the \uc2 U.S. Capitol Police\uc2  have issued a statement to members of Congress expressing "profound disappointment" with McConnell and McCarthy's positions on the Jan. 6 commission, citing the "trauma" that officers endured that day. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CRweVhIAnD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/CRweVhIAnD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Olivia Beavers (@Olivia_Beavers) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Olivia_Beavers/status/1395125137943498756?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The USCP issued a statement distancing themselves, clarifying that it was not an official statement from the Capitol Police. Democratic representative \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2  said he was given the anonymous letter by two officers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith each passing week, a new revelation about Jan 6th reveals itself....It is unconscionable to even think anyone could suggest, we need to move forward and get over it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.16am BST\par \par \uc2 Before the vote to establish a commission on the Capitol attack, the House defeated an effort by minority leader Kevin McCarthy to end the mask mandate in the chamber.\par \par \uc2 Several Republican lawmakers have been refusing to wear masks. \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  has maintained that the mask mandate should remain in place, as it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear that all the lawmakers and their staff have been vaccinated. Several Republicans have publicly rejected the vaccine or refused to disclose whether or not they had gotten it.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy nevertheless argued against the mandate by saying it \u8220\'20\'1Csends the erroneous message that the efficacy of the vaccines cannot be trusted\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.32am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 House votes to establish a commission to investigate the Capitol attack\par \par \uc2 The House voted 252-175 to establish a commission investigating the 6 January attack on the US Capitol. Among those who voted in favor of establishing the commission were 35 Republicans.\par \par \uc2 John Katko\uc2 , the Republican ranking member of the House homeland security committee helped write the bill to establish the commission, had urged his fellow Republicans to support the proposal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI strongly believe this is a fair and necessary legislation,\u8221\'20\'1D Katko said. \u8220\'20\'1CI encourage all members, Republicans and Democrats alike, to put down their swords for once, just for once and support this bill.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But the legislation will face big hurdles in Senate, as minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  opposes the bill. McConnell called the commission \u8220\'20\'1Cslanted\u8221\'20\'1D despite concessions that Republicans and Democrats would be equally represented on it.\par \par \uc2 House leader \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  slammed Republicans who opposed the bill. \u8220\'20\'1CIt sounds like they are afraid of the truth, and that\u8217\'20\'19s most unfortunate, but hopefully they\u8217\'20\'19ll get used to the idea that the American people want us to find the truth,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans flout mask requirement in US House chamber\par \par \uc2 Republicans in Congress are rebelling against the mask requirement on the House chamber, which remains in place due to Covid-19 safety concerns from Democrats, who hold the majority.\par \par \uc2 During votes on Tuesday, several Republican lawmakers refused to wear masks as they stood in the chamber and encouraged other members to join them.\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers who refuse to wear a face covering are subject to a fine of $500 for the first offense and subsequent offenses can result in a $2,500 fine. In practice, however, the House sergeant-at-arms gives a warning for the first offense.\par \par \uc2 The seven lawmakers who received warnings include Representatives \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  of Colorado, \uc2 Thomas Massie\uc2  of Kentucky, \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  of Georgia, Chip Roy of Texas, Bob Good of Virginia, \uc2 Louie Gohmert\uc2  of Texas and Mary Miller of Illinois, according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 Greene, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/18/democrats-holly-mccormack-republican-extremist-marjorie-taylor-greene"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Republican extremist}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepThomasMassie/status/1394825639597838336"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted a photo of herself with three other Republicans}}}\uc2  on the House floor without masks. The Georgia lawmaker tweeted: \u8220\'20\'1CEnd the oppression!\u8221\'20\'1D along with: \u8220\'20\'1C#FreeYourFace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Massie also tweeted a card casting a \u8220\'20\'1CNo\u8221\'20\'1D vote, along with a caption {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepThomasMassie/status/1394764104804585475"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimating that 10 Republicans were going maskless on the floor}}}\uc2  on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The Republican stunt comes after the House speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , said on Thursday that she would continue requiring masks to be worn on the floor of the chamber. \uc2 The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (\uc2 CDC\uc2 ) said earlier that day that fully vaccinated people can stop wearing masks in almost all settings, including indoors.\par \par \uc2 When asked why she kept the mask rule for the chamber, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2021-05-13/pelosi-says-mask-to-stay-on-house-floor-despite-cdc-guidance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pelosi told Bloomberg}}}\uc2  that it\u8217\'20\'19s not known how many lawmakers and their staff are vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 Democratic lawmakers in both chambers of Congress have a 100% vaccination rate against Covid-19, according to answers from a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/05/14/politics/democrats-vaccination-rates-house-mask-rules/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN survey of Capitol Hill}}}\uc2  published on Friday. However, for Republicans, the numbers are less clear.\par \par \uc2 In total, it is estimated that at least 44% of House members are vaccinated and at least 92% of senators are.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House national security advisor Jake Sullivan said he met with Israel\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Meir Ben-Shabbat\uc2  and Egypt, as the Biden administration urges de-escalation.\par \par \uc2 enltrI spoke with Israeli National Security Advisor \uc2 Meir Ben-Shabbat\uc2  and the Government of Egypt again today about the ongoing crisis. The United States is engaged in intensive diplomacy and our efforts will continue.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sullivan (@JakeSullivan46) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSullivan46/status/1395105626448093194?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Egypt has been pushing for a brokered end to the conflict, which has killed 227 people in Gaza, including 64 children. The Egyptian effort is gaining momentum, as my colleagues {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-chulov"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Chulov}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/julianborger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Julian Borger}}}\uc2  report:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/19/israel-gaza-conflict-frances-adds-to-ceasefire-pressure-on-us-as-violence-rages"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel-Gaza conflict: France adds to ceasefire pressure on US as violence rages}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 For nearly a century she was denied a voice by a culture of silence. Finally, at the age of 107, Viola Fletcher got a national stage on Wednesday to bear witness to America\u8217\'20\'19s deep history of racial violence.\par \par \uc2 Fletcher is the oldest living survivor of a massacre that took place in Tulsa, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/oklahoma"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oklahoma}}}\uc2 , on 31 May and 1 June 1921 when a white mob attacked the city\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CBlack Wall Street\u8221\'20\'1D, killing an estimated 300 African Americans while robbing and burning more than 1,200 businesses, homes and churches.\par \par \uc2 She was just seven years old at the time.\par \par \uc2 For decades the atrocity was actively covered up and wished away. But Fletcher and her 100-year-old brother are seeking reparations and, ahead of the massacre\u8217\'20\'19s centenary, appeared before a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/house-of-representatives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House of Representatives}}}\uc2  judiciary subcommittee considering legal remedies.\par \par \uc2 Congressman \uc2 Steve Cohen\uc2 , chairman of the panel, acknowledged coronavirus restrictions and said: \u8220\'20\'1CThose in the room, I\u8217\'20\'19d like to ask you to keep your face mask on at all times unless you\u8217\'20\'19re speaking \u8211\'20\'13 or unless you\u8217\'20\'19re over a hundred years old.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fletcher, born before the first world war, said she was visiting Washington for the first time in her life. She had left home at 6am on Tuesday and got to her hotel after midnight. Wearing an aquamarine jacket, floral blouse, glasses and headphones, she read steadily from a prepared statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am here seeking justice,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.house.gov/meetings/JU/JU10/20210519/112648/HHRG-117-JU10-Wstate-FletcherV-20210519.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fletcher said.}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CI am here asking my country to acknowledge what happened in Tulsa in 1921.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Viola Fletcher, the oldest living survivor of the Tulsa Race Massacre appeared before a House Committee on the Judiciary. Photograph: REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 She recalled how the Greenwood neighborhood of Tulsa had once been a thriving and affluent African American community where she could have lived her own American dream. But this bright future was suddenly taken away. \u8220\'20\'1CThe night of the massacre, I was awakened by my family. My parents and five siblings were there. I was told we had to leave and that was it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will never forget the violence of the white mob when we left our home. I still see Black men being shot, Black bodies lying in the street. I still smell smoke and see fire. I still see Black businesses being burned. I still hear airplanes flying overhead. I hear the screams. I have lived through the massacre every day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The hearing was told that there has never been any direct compensation from the city or state for massacre survivors or their descendants, and that racial disparities, compounded by gentrification and urban planning, persist in Tulsa today \u8211\'20\'13 a microcosm of America.\par \par \uc2 Fletcher continued: \u8220\'20\'1COur country may forget this history but I cannot. I will not and other survivors do not and our descendants do not. When my family was forced to leave Tulsa, I lost my chance of an education. I never finished school past the fourth grade. I have never made much money.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy country, state and city took a lot from me. Despite this, I spent time supporting the war effort in the shipyards of California. But most of my life, I was a domestic worker serving white families. I never made much money. To this day, I can barely afford my everyday needs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/19/viola-fletcher-tulsa-race-massacre-congress-oldest-survivor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I am seeking justice\u8217\'20\'19: Tulsa massacre survivor, 107, testifies to US Congress}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Maanvi Singh, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  told \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  he expects a \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant de-escalation today on the path to a ceasefire,\u8221\'20\'1D according to a White House readout of the latest call between the US president and the Israeli prime minister. The call comes as Israeli forces and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  continue to exchange attacks in Gaza, and Netanyahu said today that Israel is \u8220\'20\'1Cdetermined to continue this operation until its aim is met\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * The House is now debating the bill to form a bipartisan commission to study the January 6 insurrection. The Democratic-controlled House is expected to pass the bill, but the legislation will face hurdles in the evenly divided Senate. Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  announced today that he opposes the bill.\par \par \uc2 * House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  sharply criticized Republicans for opposing the January 6 commission bill. The Democratic speaker said at a press conference this afternoon, \u8220\'20\'1CIt sounds like they are afraid of the truth, and that\u8217\'20\'19s most unfortunate, but hopefully they\u8217\'20\'19ll get used to the idea that the American people want us to find the truth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Survivors of the 1921 Tulsa race massacre testified before a House committee, as lawmakers consider whether to compensate the massacre survivors and their descendants. One survivor, 107-year-old Viola Fletcher, told the committee, \u8220\'20\'1CI am here seeking justice. I am here asking my country to acknowledge what happened in Tulsa in 1921.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The Texas governor signed a bill banning abortions after six weeks of pregnancy, despite widespread criticism from the medical and legal communities. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups have indicated they will legally challenge the law.\par \par \uc2 Maanvi will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Although most House Republicans are expected to oppose the January 6 commission bill, the GOP members who are participating in the floor debate have largely spoken in favor of the legislation, a New York Times reporter noted.\par \par \uc2 enltrHouse Republicans are going to vote against the Jan. 6 commission but not seeing a lot standing up during the floor debate to publicly argue against it.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Carl Hulse (@hillhulse) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hillhulse/status/1395114462080913419?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 John Katko\uc2 , the Republican ranking member of the House homeland security committee who helped craft the bill to form a bipartisan commission to study the January 6 insurrection, urged his fellow Republicans to support the proposal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI strongly believe this is a fair and necessary legislation,\u8221\'20\'1D Katko said in a House floor speech. \u8220\'20\'1CI encourage all members, Republicans and Democrats alike, to put down their swords for once, just for once and support this bill.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Katko is one of the 10 House Republicans who supported impeaching \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for inciting the insurrection in January.\par \par \uc2 Another one of those 10 Republicans, \uc2 Fred Upton\uc2 , said in a speech that he will also support the bill.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJanuary 6 is going to haunt this institution for a long, long time,\u8221\'20\'1D Upton said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 The House is now beginning up to one hour of debate on the bipartisan bill to form a 9/11-style commission to study the Capitol insurrection.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe House is beginning up to one hour of debate on H.R. 3233 - National Commission to Investigate the January 6 Attack on the United States Capitol Complex Act (Sponsored by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BennieGThompson?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @BennieGThompson}}}\uc2  / Homeland Security Committee.)\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 House Press Gallery (@HouseDailyPress) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HouseDailyPress/status/1395108072922755073?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The lower chamber voted along party lines, 216 to 208, to begin debate on the bill.\par \par \uc2 The legislation itself is expected to attract some Republican support, despite House minority leader Kevin McCarthy \u8217\'20\'19s opposition to the proposal.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 The family of US Capitol Police Officer Howard \u8220\'20\'1CHowie\u8221\'20\'1D Liebengood has put out a statement in support of the bipartisan bill to form a commission to study the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 Liebengood died by suicide days after the insurrection, making him one of two \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2  officers who died in the immediate wake of the attack.\par \par \uc2 enltrU.S. Capitol Police Officer Howie Liebengood would still be with us if not for the January 6 attack.\par \par \uc2 Here is a new statement from his family, who I'm proud to represent, in support of the January 6 commission: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/oScbWm4Rzd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/oScbWm4Rzd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Rep. Jennifer Wexton\uc2  (@RepWexton) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepWexton/status/1395059911780880387?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe a thorough, non-partisan investigation into the root causes of and the response to the January 6th riot is essential for our nation to move forward,\u8221\'20\'1D Liebengood\u8217\'20\'19s family members said in their statement, which was released by their congresswoman, Democrat \uc2 Jennifer Wexton\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHowie\u8217\'20\'19s death was an immediate outgrowth of those events. Every officer who worked that day, as well as their families, should have a better understanding of what happened. Uncovering the facts will help our nation heal and may lessen the lingering emotional bitterness that has divided our country. We implore Congress to work as one and establish the proposed Commission.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The House will vote on the bill to form the commission this evening, and it is expected to pass, although it is unclear whether the legislation can make it through the Senate.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pelosi slams Republicans for opposing January 6 commission: 'They are afraid of the truth'\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  held a press conference to emphasize her support for the bipartisan bill to create a 9/11-style commission to study the Capitol insurrection.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic speaker noted that Republican congressman \uc2 John Katko\uc2  secured many of his party\u8217\'20\'19s requested changes to the legislation, yet House minority leader Kevin McCarthy is still not supporting it.\par \par \uc2 enltrSpeaker Pelosi on Republican opposition to bipartisan Jan. 6th commission: "It sounds like they are afraid of the truth and that's most unfortunate, but hopefully they'll get used to the idea that the American people want us to find the truth." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MHd3o5VNJF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/MHd3o5VNJF}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nEoOTNdfmu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/nEoOTNdfmu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 This Week (@ThisWeekABC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ThisWeekABC/status/1395092780897251328?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the interest of bipartisanship, we yielded on many points which we thought would be important,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t budge on the purpose, to examine what happened on January 6th.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pelosi said of the Republicans opposing the bill, \u8220\'20\'1CIt sounds like they are afraid of the truth, and that\u8217\'20\'19s most unfortunate, but hopefully they\u8217\'20\'19ll get used to the idea that the American people want us to find the truth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The bill is still expected to pass the Democratic-controlled House today, but it faces an uncertain fate in the evenly divided Senate.\par \par \uc2 Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  announced today that he will also oppose the legislation, describing it as \u8220\'20\'1Cslanted\u8221\'20\'1D, despite the concessions to Republicans in the final bill.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US mission to the \uc2 UN\uc2  pushed back against a French proposal for a Security Council resolution on the violence in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 When asked about the French proposal today, a US spokesperson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/china/us-says-no-french-push-un-mideast-action-2021-05-19/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Reuters}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve been clear and consistent that we are focused on intensive diplomatic efforts underway to bring an end to the violence and that we will not support actions that we believe undermine efforts to de-escalate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 France may circulate the text of a resolution as early as today, but a veto from the US (or any other member of the council) would prevent its approval.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke to Israeli Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  earlier today and expressed his expectation for a de-escalation in the attacks between Israeli forces and \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, Netanyahu has shown no sign of winding down the airstrikes in Gaza, saying Israel is \u8220\'20\'1Cdetermined to continue this operation until its aim is met\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/19/us-calls-on-israel-to-de-escalate-gaza-violence-in-push-for-ceasefire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US calls on Israel to \u8216\'20\'18de-escalate\u8217\'20\'19 Gaza violence in push for ceasefire}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Coral Murphy Marcos reports for \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 The St Louis lawyer who pointed a rifle at BLM protesters outside his home is running for the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  in Missouri.\par \par \uc2 Mark McCloskey will join the GOP race along with state Attorney General \uc2 Eric Schmitt\uc2  and former governor \uc2 Eric Greitens\uc2 . McCloskey made the announcement during an interview in Fox News\u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  Tonight\u8221\'20\'1D on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 McCloskey attracted national attention last June when he and his wife, Patricia McCloskey, stood on the lawn of their home and pointed a AR-15-style rifle and a semiautomatic handgun at peaceful protesters in their gated St. Louis community after the murder of George Floyd.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGod came knocking on my door disguised as an angry mob. It really did wake me up,\u8221\'20\'1D McCloskey said during the interview on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Mark and Patricia McCloskey, Missouri, standing in front their house in St Louis in June 28, 2020 Photograph: Laurie Skrivan/AP\par \par \uc2 The attorney made a similar comment in a \uc2 YouTube\uc2  video announcing his candidacy, in which he criticizes \u8220\'20\'1Ccancel culture, the poison of critical race theory\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe lie of systemic racism\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The couple also made an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/rnc-2020-schedule-speakers-how-to-watch-11598218846"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appearance at the Republican National Convention}}}\uc2  last year as the opening night\u8217\'20\'19s speakers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C Mark McCloskey \u8217\'20\'19s only qualifying characteristic is that he irresponsibly pointed a loaded assault weapon at unarmed peaceful protestors, mostly young people of color, ignoring the trigger discipline taught by nearly every firearm instructor in America,\u8221\'20\'1D said Christian Heyne of Brady: United Against Gun Violence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat he has capitalized on that notoriety is shameful and we hope that the people of Missouri recognize the need for common-sense candidates who will keep their communities safe and advance the interests of all of the state\u8217\'20\'19s residents.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The seat became sought after in March when Incumbent Republican Senator \uc2 Roy Blunt\uc2  announced that he will not seek another term next year. Three Democrats have announced Senate bids: former state Senator Scott Sifton, activist Timothy Shepard and Marine veteran Lucas Kunce.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will award his first Medal of Honor on Friday, as South Korean President \uc2 Moon Jae-in\uc2  visits the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn May 21, 2021, President \uc2 Joseph R. Biden, Jr\uc2 ., will award the Medal of Honor to Colonel Ralph Puckett, Jr., \uc2 United States Army\uc2 , Retired, for conspicuous gallantry during the Korean War. President \uc2 Moon Jae-in\uc2  of the Republic of Korea will join this ceremony,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House said in a new statement.\par \par \uc2 The White House statement describes how Puckett served as a commander in Korea in November 1950, when his unit was attacked while trying to take Hill 205.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLeaving the safety of his position and with full knowledge of the danger, First Lieutenant Puckett intentionally ran across an open area three times to draw enemy fire, thereby allowing the Rangers to locate and destroy the enemy positions and to seize Hill 205,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 New book details Obama\u8217\'20\'19s real thoughts on Trump\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/19/barack-obama-donald-trump-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to a new book}}}\uc2 , in conversations with advisers and donors during the Trump administration and the 2020 election, \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  called \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Cmadman\u8221\'20\'1D, a \u8220\'20\'1Cracist, sexist pig\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cthat fucking lunatic\u8221\'20\'1D and a \u8220\'20\'1Ccorrupt motherfucker\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 . Photograph: Brynn Anderson/AP\par \par \uc2 The remarks are reported in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/magazine/2021/05/19/edward-isaac-dovere-2020-campaign-book-excerpt-joe-biden-kamala-harris-489347"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Battle for the Soul: Inside the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 Campaigns to Defeat Donald Trump}}}\uc2  by Edward-Isaac Dovere, a staff writer at the Atlantic, which will be published next week. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  obtained a copy.\par \par \uc2 Extracts of Dovere\u8217\'20\'19s candid reporting have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/magazine/2021/05/19/edward-isaac-dovere-2020-campaign-book-excerpt-joe-biden-kamala-harris-489347"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published elsewhere}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 including a passage in which the now first lady, Jill Biden, is quoted as saying now Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  should \u8220\'20\'1Cgo fuck herself\u8221\'20\'1D after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G0WTx_ady48"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a memorable debate-stage attack}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The reported remarks by Obama about Trump seem likely to prompt an angry reaction from the 45th president. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s loathing for Obama is well-known and oft-expressed, beginning with his championing of the racist birther conspiracy which said Obama was not qualified to be president.\par \par \uc2 Obama\u8217\'20\'19s feelings are well-known, but have rarely been reported in such blunt detail.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s a madman,\u8221\'20\'1D Dovere reports Obama telling \u8220\'20\'1Cbig donors looking to squeeze a reaction out of him in exchange for the big checks they were writing to his foundation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 More often: \u8216\'20\'18I didn\u8217\'20\'19t think it would be this bad.\u8217\'20\'19 Sometimes: \u8216\'20\'18I didn\u8217\'20\'19t think we\u8217\'20\'19d have a racist, sexist pig.\u8217\'20\'19 Depending on the outrage of the day \u8230\'20\'26 a passing \u8216\'20\'18that fucking lunatic\u8217\'20\'19 with a shake of his head.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Obama\u8217\'20\'19s strongest remark, Dovere reports, was prompted by reports Trump was speaking to foreign leaders \u8211\'20\'13 including \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , amid the investigation of Russian election interference and links between Trump and Moscow \u8211\'20\'13 without aides on the call.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18That corrupt motherfucker,\u8217\'20\'19 he remarked.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/19/barack-obama-donald-trump-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Madman \u8230\'20\'26 racist, sexist pig\u8217\'20\'19: new book details Obama\u8217\'20\'19s real thoughts on Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Some Republican lawmakers are admitting that they do not support the creation of a commission to study the Capitol insurrection because they worry the panel\u8217\'20\'19s findings could hurt them in next year\u8217\'20\'19s midterms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want our midterm message to be on the kinds of things that the American people are dealing with: That\u8217\'20\'19s jobs and wages and the economy and national security, safe streets and strong borders -- not relitigating the 2020 elections,\u8221\'20\'1D Senate Republican whip \uc2 John Thune{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/05/19/politics/republican-reaction-january-6-probe/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of our members, and I think this is true of a lot of House Republicans, want to be moving forward and not looking backward. Anything that gets us rehashing the 2020 elections I think is a day lost on being able to draw a contrast between us the Democrats \u8217\'20\'19 very radical left-wing agenda.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The bipartisan bill to create a January 6 commission is expected to pass the House later today, but it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear whether the legislation can make it through the evenly divided Senate.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has responded to reports today that the attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office in New York has opened a criminal investigation into his business activities and those of other Trump family members.\par \par \uc2 The attorney general, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/06/letitia-james-new-york-attorney-general-donald-trump-andrew-cuomo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Letitia James}}}\uc2 , had been conducting a civil inquiry into the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  and, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/trump-investigation-new-york-attorney-general-letitia-james/2021/05/18/cd2f1288-b0cf-11eb-a980-a60af976ed44_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post}}}\uc2 , in April informed the former president\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers that the investigation had expanded.\par \par \uc2 Her office confirmed last night that it was joining a sweeping criminal investigation being conducted in parallel by Manhattan\u8217\'20\'19s district attorney, \uc2 Cyrus Vance\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump is accused of falsely manipulating the value of \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  properties in order to secure bank loans and lucrative tax breaks.\par \par \uc2 Trump said in a statement on Wednesday: \u8220\'20\'1CThere is nothing more corrupt than an investigation that is in desperate search of a crime.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/19/new-york-investigation-into-trump-organization-now-criminal-says-attorney-general"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York attorney general opens criminal investigation into Trump Organization}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Israel is 'determined to continue this operation,' Netanyahu says after Biden urges de-escalation\par \par \uc2 Israeli Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  appeared to dismiss \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s calls for a de-escalation of the violence in Gaza, as Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  continue to exchange attacks.\par \par \uc2 Netanyahu applauded the efforts of Israeli forces after a visit to the country\u8217\'20\'19s military headquarters earlier today.\par \par \uc2 The prime minister said Israel is \u8220\'20\'1Cdetermined to continue this operation until its aim is met.\u8221\'20\'1D He pledged that the military will work \u8220\'20\'1Cto return the calm and security to you, citizens of Israel\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Netanyahu also said he \u8220\'20\'1Cgreatly appreciates the support of the American president,\u8221\'20\'1D even though his latest statement appears to clash with Biden\u8217\'20\'19s requests.\par \par \uc2 The US president spoke to Netanyahu earlier today, and he \u8220\'20\'1Cconveyed to the Prime Minister that he expected a significant de-escalation today on the path to a ceasefire,\u8221\'20\'1D according to a White House readout of the call.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  told \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  he expects a \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant de-escalation today on the path to a ceasefire,\u8221\'20\'1D according to a White House readout of the latest call between the US president and the Israeli prime minister. The call comes as Israeli forces and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  continue to exchange attacks in Gaza, where more than 200 people, most of them Palestinian, have already died as a result of the violence.\par \par \uc2 * Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  announced he opposes the bipartisan bill to form a commission to study the Capitol insurrection. The Democratic-controlled House is expected to pass the bill later today, but McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s stance indicates the hurdles the legislation will face in the evenly divided Senate.\par \par \uc2 * Survivors of the 1921 Tulsa race massacre testified before a House committee, as lawmakers consider whether to compensate the massacre survivors and their descendants. One survivor, 107-year-old Viola Fletcher, told the committee, \u8220\'20\'1CI am here seeking justice. I am here asking my country to acknowledge what happened in Tulsa in 1921.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Texas governor signs extreme six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban into law\par \par \uc2 Mary Tuma reports for \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  from Austin, Texas:\par \par \uc2 Today, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  Republican governor, Greg Abbott, signed into law one of the most extreme six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in the US, despite strong opposition from the medical and legal communities, who warn the legislation could topple the state\u8217\'20\'19s court system and already fragile reproductive healthcare network.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis bill ensures that every unborn child who has a heartbeat will be saved from the ravages of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Abbott, flanked by several members of the Texas legislature this morning.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=87R&Bill=SB8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate Bill 8}}}\uc2  (SB 8), passed by both chambers of the Republican-dominated Texas legislature, bars \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at six weeks of pregnancy with no exception for rape or incest, amounting to a near-total ban as most women are not aware they are pregnant at this stage.\par \par \uc2 While a dozen states have passed similar so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cheartbeat\u8221\'20\'1D bills \u8211\'20\'13 bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once embryonic cardiac activity is detected \u8211\'20\'13 none have yet been enforced due to court challenges.\par \par \uc2 Unlike those measures, the Texas version absolves the state from enforcing the law. Instead it allows any private citizen the extraordinary authority to sue an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider \u8211\'20\'13 they do not need to be connected to the patient or even reside in the same state, opening up the floodgates to harassing and frivolous civil lawsuits that could shut down clinics statewide.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis law is so broadly written it could target not just \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics and staff but anyone that volunteers or donates to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund or activist organization like ours,\u8221\'20\'1D says Aimee Arrambide, executive director of reproductive rights advocacy group, Avow Texas.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/19/texas-abortion-ban-law-greg-abbott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas governor signs extreme six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban into law}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  closed his remarks at the Coast Guard commencement by telling the graduates that the country needs them.\par \par \uc2 The president said members of the youngest generation, such as the graduating cadets, make him optimistic about America\u8217\'20\'19s future.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re the most progressive, best educated, least prejudiced, most open generation in American history,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need you badly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  told the Coast Guard cadets that they will be graduating into a changing world.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re at a significant inflection point in world history,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said at the commencement ceremony.\par \par \uc2 Biden also delivered some criticism of Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  for his recent actions in the Arctic and Chinese President \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2  for his maneuvers in the South China Sea.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe United States must demonstrate our leadership and engagement,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden delivers keynote address at Coast Guard commencement\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now delivering the keynote address at the US Coast Guard Academy\u8217\'20\'19s 140th commencement exercises in Connecticut.\par \par \uc2 The president applauded the cadets\u8217\'20\'19 commitment and perseverance, noting they chose a \u8220\'20\'1Cmore difficult path\u8221\'20\'1D than many of their high school classmates.\par \par \uc2 enltr"This past year there can be no doubt the class of '21 is ready for whatever its mission may be," Pres. Biden says delivering the keynote address at the U.S. Coast Guard Academy. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BydPADz8Ea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/BydPADz8Ea}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GaBEv5IUlh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GaBEv5IUlh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 This Week (@ThisWeekABC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ThisWeekABC/status/1395045883763380230?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis past year, there can be no doubt the class of \u8216\'20\'1821 is ready for whatever its mission may be,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The president also asked the cadets to stand up and salute their parents to thank them for making this day possible.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 It is also worth noting that there were 10 congressional investigations into the 2012 attack on \uc2 US government\uc2  facilities in Benghazi, Libya, as an NBC News editor points out.\par \par \uc2 enltrIn case you were wondering as McConnell makes the case that the two existing congressional investigations into the Jan. 6 attacks are sufficient and nothing new could be learned by a bipartisan commission, the number of congressional investigations conducted about Benghazi: 10\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ginger Gibson (@GingerGibson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GingerGibson/status/1395036079372312578?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 But Republican leaders are now arguing that the two existing congressional investigations into the Capitol insurrection make a bipartisan commission unnecessary.\par \par \uc2 Republicans used the findings of the Benghazi investigations to denounce \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s leadership as secretary of state while she ran for president in 2016.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s worth comparing Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s comments today to what he said about the Capitol insurrection in January.\par \par \uc2 McConnell voted against convicting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for inciting the insurrection, but he made clear that he held the former president directly responsible for the violence of January 6.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe mob was fed lies,\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell said shortly after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second impeachment trial concluded.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey were provoked by the president and other powerful people, and they tried to use fear and violence to stop a specific proceeding of the first branch of the federal government which they did not like.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And yet, McConnell is opposing the bipartisan bill to form a commission to study the Capitol insurrection because he claims it is unnecessary considering other ongoing investigations into the attack.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 McConnell announces opposition to January 6 commission bill\par \par \uc2 Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  has announced that he will oppose the bipartisan bill to form a September 11-style commission to study the Capitol insurrection when it comes up for a Senate vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter careful consideration, I\u8217\'20\'19ve made the decision to oppose the House Democrats \u8217\'20\'19 slanted and unbalanced proposal for another commission to study the events of January 6,\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell said on the Senate floor moments ago.\par \par \uc2 Echoing comments from House minority leader Kevin McCarthy yesterday, McConnell argued that the existing investigations into the insurrection rendered the commission unnecessary.\par \par \uc2 enltrSenate Minority Leader Mitch McConnell: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve made the decision to oppose the House Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 slanted and unbalanced proposal for another commission to study the events of January the 6th.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DwoNRrxzPb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/DwoNRrxzPb}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1395036075131871232?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 It is worth noting that the bill the House will be voting on today is not the original Democratic proposal but rather a compromise measure crafted by Democrat \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  and \uc2 John Katko\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Katko, the Republican ranking member of the House homeland security committee, won some key concessions in the negotations over the bill. For example, the commission would be evenly divided between the two parties , whereas Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 original proposal gave them a slight advantage on the panel.\par \par \uc2 The House is expected to pass the commission bill later today. However, McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s stance indicates it will likely be difficult to get the bill through the evenly divided Senate, which would require 10 Republicans to support the proposal.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer denounced House Republicans voting against the bipartisan bill to form a commission to study the Capitol insurrection.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShame on the Republicans for choosing the \u8216\'20\'18big lie\u8217\'20\'19 over the truth -- not all Republicans, but the majority who seem to be doing it,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said on the Senate floor moments ago.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShame on them for defending the mob over our \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  officers and shame on the House Republican leadership for punishing Republicans who tell the truth, instead of those who poisoned faith in our democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenSchumer}}}\uc2  slams GOP over Jan 6 commission:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShame on the Republicans for choosing the Big Lie over the truth \u8230\'20\'26 Shame on them for defending the mob over our Capitol Police officers, and shame on the House Republican leadership for punishing Republicans who tell the truth \u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/eKs47oHKAh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/eKs47oHKAh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1395031505299202048?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 That final comment appeared to be a reference to both Republican congressman \uc2 John Katko\uc2 , who helped craft the commission bill, and congresswoman \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , who was recently ousted as House GOP conference chair because of her criticism of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Schumer reiterated his pledge that the Senate will hold a vote on the commission bill, despite Republican opposition.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe only way to stop these lies is to respond with the truth, with facts, with an honest objective investigation,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tulsa race massacre survivor testifies before House committee\par \par \uc2 A 107-year-old woman, the oldest living survivor of the Tulsa race massacre, has received a standing ovation for her testimony to a congressional committee.\par \par \uc2 Viola Fletcher told the House of Representatives\u8217\'20\'19 judiciary subcommittee that she was visiting Washington for the first time in her life. Wearing an aquamarine jacket, glasses and headphones, she read steadily from a prepared statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am here seeking justice,\u8221\'20\'1D Fletcher said. \u8220\'20\'1CI am here asking my country to acknowledge what happened in Tulsa in 1921.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The hearing takes place ahead of the centenary of the atrocity in which mobs of white residents attacked, ransacked and burned down the thriving African American community of Greenwood, known as \u8220\'20\'1CBlack Wall Street\u8221\'20\'1D, causing an estimated 300 deaths.\par \par \uc2 enltrWATCH: Complete statement from 107-year-old Viola Fletcher, the oldest living survivor of the Tulsa Race Massacre: "I'm here seeking justice and I'm asking my country to acknowledge what happened in Tulsa in 1921."\par \par \uc2 Full video here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zsDBRKWjCK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/zsDBRKWjCK}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hJFv4GY3mt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/hJFv4GY3mt}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1395029741506371587?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Fletcher recalled: \u8220\'20\'1CThe night of the massacre, I was woken up by my family. My parents and five siblings were there. I was told we had to leave. And that was it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will never forget the violence of the white mob when we left our house. I still see Black men being shot, and Black bodies lying in the street. I still smell smoke and see fire. I still see Black businesses being burned. I still hear airplanes flying overhead. I hear the screams. I live through the massacre every day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur country may forget this history. I cannot. I will not. The other survivors do not. And our descendants do not. When my family was forced to leave Tulsa, I lost my chance at an education. I never finished school past the fourth grade. I have never made much money.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy country, state, and city took a lot from me. Despite this, I spent time supporting the war effort in the shipyards of California. But for most of my life, I was a domestic worker serving white families. I never made much money. To this day, I can barely afford my everyday needs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fletcher and two other survivors are lead plaintiffs in a reparations lawsuit filed last year against city and state authorities. Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s hearing is considering the case for compensating the massacre survivors and their descendants.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 More than 200 people, the vast majority of them Palestinian, have been killed in the past week as Israeli forces and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  exchanged attacks in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEven if the airstrikes and the rockets stop, the Israeli-Palestinian crisis has entered a new stage,\u8221\'20\'1D the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Jerusalem correspondent, Oliver Holmes, says.\par \par \uc2 Oliver explains how we got to this point in a video explainer from \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s phone call with \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  came as the Israeli prime minister pushed back against demands for an immediate end to the violence in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t stand with a timer,\u8221\'20\'1D Netanyahu said at a briefing with foreign ambassadors this morning, per Walla News correspondent Barak Ravid.\par \par \uc2 He added, \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to achieve the goals of the operation. Previous operations lasted a long time, so it is not possible to set a time frame on the operation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Netanyahu says in a briefing to foreign ambassadors: \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t stand with a timer. We want to achieve the goals of the operation. Previous operations lasted a long time so it is not possible to set a time frame on the operation\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Barak Ravid (@BarakRavid) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BarakRavid/status/1394952836560166912?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Deputy White House press secretary Karine Jean-Pierre held a short press gaggle aboard Air Force One moments ago.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre reiterated the readout from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s call with Israeli Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  today, during which the US president expressed his expectation for an immediate de-escalation and pathway to ceasefire in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Asked if Netanyahu agreed with Biden\u8217\'20\'19s comments, Jean-Pierre did not answer directly.\par \par \uc2 Biden will soon deliver the keynote address at the US Coast Guard Academy\u8217\'20\'19s 140th Commencement Exercises, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Martin Chulov and Julian Borger and agencies report:\par \par \uc2 Egypt has urged a brokered end to the fighting between Israel and militants in Gaza, and France has called for a \uc2 UN\uc2  security council resolution on the violence, as international pressure for a ceasefire intensifies.\par \par \uc2 Signs are emerging that a ceasefire may be within sight, with the Egyptian effort gaining momentum among factions in Gaza, and the prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , reported by Israeli media to have told officials in the south of the country that the fighting could end \u8220\'20\'1Cwithin several days\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Jordan, too, has lobbied intensively for a cessation of violence and has joined a French push at the \uc2 UN\uc2  to present a draft resolution that safeguards urgent humanitarian relief. The US would have to use its veto power to block the resolution, something the Biden administration would be reluctant to do.\par \par \uc2 Israeli jets on Wednesday continued to pound what officials say is an extensive tunnel network under central Gaza used by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  to move fighters and weapons. The al-Rimal neighbourhood was also targeted and residents reported that several homes had been been destroyed.\par \par \uc2 Israel claimed it had twice tried to kill Hamas military commander, Mohammed Deif, but the elusive leader \u8211\'20\'13 who had previously escaped many other assassination attempts \u8211\'20\'13 had escaped.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/19/israel-gaza-conflict-frances-adds-to-ceasefire-pressure-on-us-as-violence-rages"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel-Gaza conflict: France adds to ceasefire pressure on US as violence rages}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden tells Netanyahu he expects immediate de-escalation and pathway to ceasefire in Gaza\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke to Israeli Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  today as Israeli forces and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  continued to exchange attacks in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe two leaders had a detailed discussion on the state of events in Gaza, Israel\u8217\'20\'19s progress in degrading the capabilities of \uc2 Hamas\uc2  and other terrorist elements, and ongoing diplomatic efforts by regional governments and the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House said in a readout of the call.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe President conveyed to the Prime Minister that he expected a significant de-escalation today on the path to a ceasefire.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s comments are noteworthy given that the US president merely indicated his support for a ceasefire in his conversation with Netanyahu on Monday.\par \par \uc2 After that Monday conversation, progressives criticized Biden for not demanding an immediate end to the violence, which has already killed more than 200 people, most of them Palestinian.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/18/joe-biden-gaza-israel-democrats-ceasefire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s meek stance on Gaza ceasefire does little to quell progressive ire}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Although most House Republicans are expected to vote against the January 6 commission bill, as many as 50 members of the GOP caucus may support the legislation, according to Punchbowl News.\par \par \uc2 enltrWe hear that anywhere between 20 to 50 Republicans could vote for this commission, with the total very fluid. Republicans are concerned about a \u8220\'20\'1Cjailbreak,\u8221\'20\'1D in which a flood of lawmakers back the legislation en masse.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1395007796815486980?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 It should also be noted that there are 31 sponsors of a separate Republican bill to form a January 6 commission, and that legislation looks very similar to the compromise proposal crafted by Democrat \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  and Republican J ohn Katko.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer has pledged to put the January 6 commission bill on the Senate floor for a vote, despite Republican opposition.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will put the January 6 Commission legislation on the floor of the Senate for a vote, period,\u8221\'20\'1D the Democratic leader said. \u8220\'20\'1C Republicans can let their constituents know, are they on the side of truth or do they want to cover up for the insurrectionists and for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrCHUCK SCHUMER: \u8220\'20\'1CI will put the Jan. 6 commission legislation on the floor of the Senate for a vote, period. Republicans can let their constituents know: Are they on the side of truth or do they want to cover up for the insurrectionists and for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ?" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NXusryVlOL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/NXusryVlOL}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 JM Rieger (@RiegerReport) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RiegerReport/status/1394750145686814729?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 18, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Schumer also argued that House minority leader Kevin McCarthy \u8217\'20\'19s opposition to the bill, even after Republican congressman \uc2 John Katko\uc2  helped craft the final version of the legislation, demonstrated the difficulties of working with Republicans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the Republican leaders are just going to throw their lead negotiators under the bus, why do they even participate in negotiations at all?\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer asked.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Martin Pengelly, Coral Murphy Marcos and agencies report:\par \par \uc2 House minority leader Kevin McCarthy has long said the 6 January commission should also investigate leftwing groups that protested against police violence after the murder of George Floyd.\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  flatly rejected that approach, seeking to focus the panel on 6 January and form it along the lines of the bipartisan and independent 9/11 commission, which investigated the terror attacks in New York, Washington and Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 The commission would be split evenly between Democratic and Republican appointees, none of them serving government officials, with agreement needed for subpoenas to be issued.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MZanona/status/1394636992776966145/photo/2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he supported that federal effort to hold attackers accountable but claimed the proposed commission could interfere with such work.\par \par \uc2 Pelosi subsequently told reporters that she was disappointed but not surprised by the \u8220\'20\'1Ccowardice\u8221\'20\'1D shown by some {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  who she said did \u8220\'20\'1Cnot to want to find the truth\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/18/kevin-mccarthy-rejects-bipartisan-commission-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kevin McCarthy rejects bipartisan plan for 9/11-style Capitol attack commission}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 House expected to pass bill to establish commission to study Capitol insurrection\par \par \uc2 Greetings from Washington, live blog readers.\par \par \uc2 Later today, the House is expected to pass a bill that would establish a September 11-style commission to study the Capitol insurrection.\par \par \uc2 The legislation will likely pass without much Republican support, given that House minority leader Kevin McCarthy announced yesterday he will vote against the bill.\par \par \uc2 A mob of supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  climb through a window they broke as they storm US Capitol on January 6. Photograph: Leah Millis/Reuters\par \par \uc2 McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s announcement came three days after Republican congressman \uc2 John Katko\uc2  and Democrat \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , the ranking member and chairman of the House homeland security commission, said they had reached a deal on the bill.\par \par \uc2 Even though Katko was able to secure many of the Republican requests for the commission, McCarthy still claimed the final bill was insufficient to garner his support.\par \par \uc2 The Republican leader\u8217\'20\'19s stance underscores how eager many members of the party are to move on from the January 6 attack, which was carried out by a group of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s supporters and resulted in five deaths.\par \par \uc2 That dynamic could make it difficult to get the bill through the evenly divided Senate, where it will need 60 votes to overcome a filibuster.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more details on the vote coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210519eh5j001bg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
