\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  view on US bishops versus the president: Biden is on the angels\u8217\'20\'19 side\b0\par\par\uc2 Editorial \par \uc2 608 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 May 2021\par 17:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s backing of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights is not a reason to deny him holy communion\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  wears his Catholicism on his sleeve. The American president carries the rosary beads of his late son, Beau, around his wrist, and each Sunday he attends mass in Washington, or in his home state of Delaware. After Mr Biden\u8217\'20\'19s election to the White House last year, \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  sent him a copy of his book on the Covid pandemic, Let Us Dream. In it, Francis calls for a new spirit of solidarity in societies which have learned the hard way that \u8220\'20\'1Cno one is saved alone\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Through his $2tn American Rescue Plan, Mr Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/apr/04/with-joe-bidens-own-audacious-new-deal-the-democratic-left-rediscovers-its-soul"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hopes}}}\uc2  to turn that theological claim into public policy, deploying the resources of the state in the name of a more equal, sustainable society. \u8220\'20\'1CI grew up with Catholic social doctrine, which taught me that faith without works is dead,\u8221\'20\'1D he has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncronline.org/news/people/how-joe-bidens-catholic-roots-have-shaped-his-public-life"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For millions of ordinary American Catholics, disillusioned and alienated by their church\u8217\'20\'19s shameful handling of sex abuse scandals, the Biden presidency is therefore an uplifting source of celebration and hope. But within the US Conference of Catholic Bishops (USCCB), it is instead treated as an insidious threat to ecclesial authority. As Archbishop Joseph Naumann of Kansas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/religion/2021/04/28/biden-catholic-president-bishops-abortion-communion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 put}}}\uc2  it recently: \u8220\'20\'1CBecause President Biden is Catholic, it presents a unique problem for us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The reason is Mr Biden\u8217\'20\'19s backing of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, which goes against Catholic teaching. On issues such as the rights of refugees, concern for the poor, the dignity of work and the climate emergency, the president and \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  march in virtual lockstep. But figures such as Archbishop Naumann and the president of the USCCB, Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Gomez, believe that the president\u8217\'20\'19s position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  confuses the faithful and brings his own Catholicism into disrepute. In such circumstances, they speculate, it may be appropriate to take the extreme step of denying him holy communion at mass.\par \par \uc2 The last similar discussion took place in 2004, when the pro-choice Catholic \uc2 John Kerry\uc2  was running for the White House. The issue was eventually parked and Mr Kerry didn\u8217\'20\'19t win. Now the bishops have announced a vote next month on the subject, with a view to issuing a clarificatory document. The arch-conservative cardinal Raymond Burke is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vanityfair.com/news/2020/10/how-qanon-and-trumpism-have-infected-the-catholic-church"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already}}}\uc2  on the record stating that \u8220\'20\'1Capostate\u8221\'20\'1D politicians backing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights should be denied communion.\par \par \uc2 As the conciliatory Mr Biden makes a credible fist of uniting a nation divided by decades of culture wars, it is tempting to despair. The USCCB has no power to order the withholding of communion, and the Vatican has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncronline.org/news/opinion/distinctly-catholic/vatican-throws-wet-blanket-us-bishops-who-want-deny-biden-communion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already}}}\uc2  made clear its disapproval of the proposed June vote. But this may cut little ice with prelates who have fiercely resisted the liberal priorities of Francis\u8217\'20\'19s papacy from its inception eight years ago.\par \par \uc2 The weaponising of the eucharist illustrates the extent to which much of the hierarchy of US Catholicism has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newyorker.com/news/daily-comment/can-joe-biden-save-american-catholicism-from-the-far-right"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 become}}}\uc2  the theological wing of extreme Republicanism. The end result, as one prominent theologian has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thetablet.co.uk/news/14143/us-bishops-in-dangerous-place-over-refusing-communion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2 , may be some kind of \u8220\'20\'1Csoft schism\u8221\'20\'1D as conservative bishops try to pull the church further to the right. Surveys {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/ddfe507d-0bc7-4b16-8ca1-97d0a0927d63"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indicate}}}\uc2  that a majority of US Catholics believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases.\par \par \uc2 The extraordinary violent denouement of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s polarising presidency meant that dialling down division became an urgent national priority. Mr Biden, in both tone and substance, has done a pretty good job on that front so far. If only the national leaders of his church could follow suit.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210519eh5j0028s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
