\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Alarm bells are ringing\u8217\'20\'19: activists brace for US  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  case that could rip up precedent\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 804 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 May 2021\par 12:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Justices to rule on Mississippi ban on terminations after 15 weeks in most consequential case for reproductive rights in decades\par \par \uc2 US reproductive rights groups are bracing for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/may/17/abortion-case-supreme-court-threatens-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most consequential \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  case}}}\uc2  in decades, after the supreme court agreed to hear a case that flies in the face of precedent.\par \par \uc2 The case could dramatically alter decades of rulings on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and eventually lead to dramatic restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 In the case, Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s last \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic is challenging the constitutionality of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/mar/19/mississippi-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a ban on abortions later than the 15th week}}}\uc2  of pregnancy.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/dec/13/us-air-force-pregnancy-susan-struck-abortion-motherhood-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Since 1973}}}\uc2 , the landmark supreme court case Roe v Wade has provided US women the constitutional right to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until a fetus can live outside the womb, generally around {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.acog.org/clinical/clinical-guidance/obstetric-care-consensus/articles/2017/10/periviable-birth"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 24 weeks}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The state is not asking the court to overrule Roe v Wade, or later cases that reaffirmed it. But many supporters of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are alarmed and many opponents of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are elated that the justices could undermine earlier \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rulings.\par \par \uc2 If the court upholds Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s law, it would be its first ratification of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban before 24 weeks. Such a ruling could lay the groundwork for allowing even more restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That includes state bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once a fetal heartbeat is detected, as early as six weeks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is incredibly concerning that the supreme court has taken a case that, based on its own precedents, it should have dismissed months ago,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Elizabeth Nash\uc2 , principal policy associate with the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a reproductive rights research organization.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMake no mistake: the purpose of any \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban \u8211\'20\'13 including this 15-week ban in Mississippi \u8211\'20\'13 is to snowball into an outright ban on all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any point in pregnancy and for any reason,\u8221\'20\'1D Nash said.\par \par \uc2 The case will become the first to be heard by a conservative bench remade by Donald Trump, which includes the devout Catholic {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/commentisfree/2020/oct/27/amy-coney-barretts-appointment-is-a-wake-up-call-for-female-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court justice Amy Coney Barrett}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAlarm bells are ringing loudly about the threat to reproductive rights,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Nancy Northup\uc2 , CEO of the Center for Reproductive Rights, a legal group representing Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s last \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic, Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe supreme court just agreed to review an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that unquestionably violates nearly 50 years of supreme court precedent and is a test case to overturn Roe v Wade,\u8221\'20\'1D Northup said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal in all 50 states, even as advocates say increased restrictions currently make it unavailable to many women. Restrictions on reproductive rights disproportionately affect low-income and minority women.\par \par \uc2 If Roe were overturned, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ng-interactive/2018/jun/30/abortion-supreme-court-law-anthony-kennedy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 20 states}}}\uc2  would ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  outright. Many states, including Mississippi, have enacted \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger\u8221\'20\'1D laws to immediately outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should the supreme court make such a decision.\par \par \uc2 If Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s law were to be upheld and Roe not entirely overturned, states may be able to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegal at 15 weeks. That would narrow the window in which women can seek abortions by more than two months. Roe set the legal standard of viability in 1973, and it has become a linchpin of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights law in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COnce viability is gone, all bets are off,\u8221\'20\'1D the law professor Mary Ziegler said on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maryrziegler/status/1394295275359977478"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Twitter}}}\uc2 . She said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/apr/25/the-anti-abortion-crusader-hopes-her-heartbeat-law-will-test-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  activists}}}\uc2  were \u8220\'20\'1Cbanking on\u8221\'20\'1D, much earlier limits, hoping the court will allow states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six or eight weeks. That is before many women know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 And there has never been a strong alternative to viability proposed by pro-choice forces. So if not viability, what? \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  foes are banking on a six/eight weeks. But once viability is gone, all bets are off. /fin\u8212\'20\'14 Mary Ziegler (@maryrziegler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maryrziegler/status/1394295275359977478?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Even before the court took up the case, 2021 has become the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/apr/27/us-tiny-towns-anti-abortion-ordinances"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most hostile year}}}\uc2  on record for reproductive rights in the US. The new makeup of the supreme court has prompted optimistic Republican lawmakers to pass more restrictions, hoping to send test cases to the court.\par \par \uc2 Since January, more than 500 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions have been introduced across 46 states. Sixty-one restrictions and eight bans have been enacted across 13 states. In 2011, 42 restrictions and six bans were enacted.\par \par \uc2 Even as some Republican state politicians disagree with colleagues over severe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions \u8211\'20\'13 some recently introduced bills would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/feb/12/anti-abortion-activists-womens-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charge women and doctors with murder}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 such rhetoric remains a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/09/us-voting-restrictions-conservative-groups-lobbying-against-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cornerstone of Republican organizing and fundraising}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 About {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2021/05/06/about-six-in-ten-americans-say-abortion-should-be-legal-in-all-or-most-cases/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six in 10 Americans}}}\uc2  believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases, according to the \uc2 Pew Research Center\uc2 , a remarkably steady level of support. However, the partisan divide over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights has grown. In recent years, Democrats have grown more likely to believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should remain legal and available.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210518eh5i00107\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
