\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Biden breaks silence on ceasefire eight days into Israel-Gaza conflict\b0\par\par\uc2 Miranda Bryant \par \uc2 1,279 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 May 2021\par 11:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  expresses support for ceasefire between Israel and Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s militant rulers \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . Plus, the \u8216\'20\'18patriotic millionaires\u8217\'20\'19 shaming Jeff BezosDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/18/biden-israel-gaza-ceasefire-netanyahu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has expressed support}}}\uc2  for a ceasefire between Israel and Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s militant rulers Hamas for the first time, but stopped short of calling for an immediate halt to the eight days of Israeli airstrikes and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  rocket barrages.\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s statement came after a phone conversation with \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , the Israeli prime minister. In the call, the White House said Biden \u8220\'20\'1Creiterated his firm support for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s right to defend itself\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cexpressed his support for a ceasefire\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the US blocked \u8211\'20\'13 for the third time in a week \u8211\'20\'13 the adoption of a joint \uc2 UN\uc2  security council statement calling for a halt to Israeli-Palestinian violence.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In the early hours\par \par \uc2 , Israel carried out fresh airstrikes on Gaza. Regional protests are expected on Tuesday following a call by Palestinian citizens of Israel for a general strike.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 According to the latest death tolls, 212 Palestinians have been killed, including 61 children, and 10 people have been killed in Israel, including two children.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What is the international reaction? Arab states have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/17/arab-states-split-for-first-time-on-refusal-to-condemn-israel-over-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 split}}}\uc2  for the first time on the issue. Meanwhile, the \uc2 EU\uc2  is being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/18/eu-sidelined-and-divided-as-war-rages-again-in-middle-east"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sidelined and divided}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Peter Beinart writes about the Jewish case for Palestinian refugee return in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/2021/may/18/a-jewish-case-for-palestinian-refugee-return"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the long read}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to hear landmark \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights groups fear access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US could be rolled back after the supreme court agreed to hear what could be the most consequential case on the divisive issue in nearly 50 years.\par \par \uc2 In the new case, Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s last \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic is challenging the constitutionality of outlawing abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s the significance of the case? Since Roe v Wade, the court\u8217\'20\'19s landmark 1973 ruling that legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide, women in the US have had the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until viability, usually at about 24 weeks. It will be the first heard big \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case heard by the court since the arrival of conservative Trump appointee Amy Coney Barrett.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 While the state is not asking to overrule Roe v Wade, the development has alarmed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/18/us-supreme-court-abortion-test-case-mississippi-precedent"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes}}}\uc2  Jessica Glenza. If the court upholds Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s law it could lead to more \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Over 20 states would ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  completely if Roe were overturned. Since January alone, more than 500 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions have been added across 46 states.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Around six in 10 Americans believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in either all or the majority of cases.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  is putting domestic terror and civil rights at the top of the justice agenda, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/18/merrick-garland-domestic-terrorism-civil-rights-justice-department"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes}}}\uc2  Peter Stone.\par \par \uc2 At least 1,000 people in LA under wildfire evacuation order\par \par \uc2 At least 1,000 Los Angeles residents are under evacuation orders and more than 1,300 acres have been burned after a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/17/la-fires-latest-evacuations-wildfire-orders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wildfire}}}\uc2  broke out in the Santa Monica Mountains.\par \par \uc2 Parts of LA are shrouded with plumes of smoke and ash from the Palisades fire, which broke out on Friday and exponentially grew on Saturday. Around 500 first responders are working to contain the fire.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What caused the fire? Investigators suspect an arsonist may have caused it and are holding a suspect in custody, LA mayor Eric Garcetti said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Due to global heating, the fire season in California and the west is \u8220\'20\'1Cstarting earlier and ending later each year,\u8221\'20\'1D warned \uc2 Cal Fire\uc2 , the state\u8217\'20\'19s wildfire agency.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Also in California,\par \par \uc2 Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/18/california-ghost-guns-deadly-toll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  on the deadly toll of \u8220\'20\'1Cghost guns\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 weapons ordered online and assembled at home.\par \par \uc2 In other news\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Just 20 firms produce a staggering 55% of the world\u8217\'20\'19s plastic waste, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/may/18/twenty-firms-produce-55-of-worlds-plastic-waste-report-reveals"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a report has found}}}\uc2 . The Plastic Waste Makers index revealed that \uc2 ExxonMobil\uc2  is the greatest single-use plastic waste polluter in the world, with 5.9m tonnes. It also found that Australia generates the most single-use plastic per capita, followed by the US, South Korea and the UK.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A \u8220\'20\'1CCovid casino\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/17/canada-covid-casino-police-stealing-watches-allegation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  case in Canada has collapsed}}}\uc2  after police officers were accused of stealing luxury watches and planting evidence. Police in Ontario previously said they had seized more than $10m in assets, firearms, liquor and cash following a months-long investigation and 29 people were arrested, including the owner of a mansion north of Toronto that allegedly operated an underground casino during the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/17/biden-20m-doses-covid-vaccines-overseas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden has pledged}}}\uc2  to send 20m doses of US-approved coronavirus vaccines overseas by the end of June. The president\u8217\'20\'19s announcement on Monday, combined with the 60m doses of \uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s vaccine that has already been promised, means a total of 80m doses will be sent abroad in the next six weeks. \u8220\'20\'1COur nation is going to be the arsenal of vaccines for the rest of the world,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nasa\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/18/electric-planes-nasa-carbon-emissions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leading}}}\uc2  a push for electric planes in the next frontier to cut emissions. In the next year, at a site in California, the agency will look for a breakthrough on how to remove carbon pollution from flying with a new generation of battery-powered planes. They hope to phase in electric flights within 15 years.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: \uc2 Amazon\uc2  paid only a 9.4% federal income tax rate in 2020 \u8211\'20\'13 under half what it should have done\par \par \uc2 According to calculations by the \uc2 Institute on Taxation and Economic Policy\uc2 , the global retail giant paid less than half the 21% statutory corporate tax. A group of millionaires {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/may/17/jeff-bezos-protest-patriotic-millionaires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protested}}}\uc2  outside the New York and Washington homes of its billionaire owner \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2  yesterday to mark Tax Day. The protest was led by Patriotic Millionaires, a group of rich individuals who support progressive policy changes, to mark Tax Day. The Biden administration has proposed raising the corporate tax rate to 28%, which would partly undo the cuts made by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in 2017. Previously the top rate was 35%.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: How green is Denver if you\u8217\'20\'19re Black?\par \par \uc2 How a 155-acre golf course has become a lightning rod in debates over gentrification, open spaces and racial equity in Denver, Colorado. Park Hill golf course is an oasis of green space in the middle of a neighbourhood where over 40% of residents identify as African American, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/18/denver-black-residents-green-space-golf-course"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes Caroline Tracey}}}\uc2 . It is supposed to be protected by state law, but after it was bought in 2019 it is feared it could be turned into a development. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not a golfer. I\u8217\'20\'19m interested in open space,\u8221\'20\'1D says Sandy Robnette, a Black resident. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd what I see here is environmental racism.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: As Shrek turns 20, the flatulent ogre has not aged well\par \par \uc2 When it was released in 2001, Shrek was a hit with audiences and critics. The animation, featuring a green flatulent ogre with the voice of Mike Myers as its protagonist and a donkey and princess voiced by Eddie Murphy and Cameron Diaz respectively, spurred an entire franchise, including several more films. But assessing the hit as it turns 20, Scott Tobias is not impressed, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2021/may/17/shrek-20-unfunny-overrated-low-blockbuster"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arguing}}}\uc2  that the film signified \u8220\'20\'1Cthe movement when blockbuster animation circled the drain. Shrek is a terrible movie. It\u8217\'20\'19s not funny. It looks awful.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.co