\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  expresses support for ceasefire on call with Netanyahu \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Julia Carrie Wong and Joan E Greve \par \uc2 8,379 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 May 2021\par 00:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 White House reported the US president urged Israel \u8216\'20\'18to make every effort to ensure the protection of innocent civilians\u8217\'20\'19Supreme court agrees to consider major rollback of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rightsLiz Cheney defiant over Trump as Republican civil war heats upJoe Biden feels political ground shift as Israel-Gaza conflict rages on\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Evening summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s all from me today. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a rundown of the day\u8217\'20\'19s biggest politics stories:\par \par \uc2 * The supreme court will take up a case challenging Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. The case will present an opportunity for the court\u8217\'20\'19s newly fortified conservative majority to reconsider Roe v Wade , the landmark 1973 decision that established the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 * The expanded child tax credit benefits included in the coronavirus relief package will start being distributed in July, the White House announced. The new benefits will send up to $300 a child to American families each month, and the payments are expected to help cut the country\u8217\'20\'19s child poverty rate nearly in half.\par \par \uc2 * At least {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/17/israel-gaza-conflict-200-palestinians-killed-in-a-week-say-officials"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 200 Palestinians, including 59 children, have been killed}}}\uc2  after a week of attacks between Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  in Gaza. Eight adults and two children in Israel have also been among the victims of the violence. A number of senior US officials, including the Senate majority leader. Chuck Schumer, have called for a ceasefire to the rocket attacks.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  expressed mild \u8220\'20\'1Csupport\u8221\'20\'1D for a ceasefire in a call with the Israeli prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , but stopped short of demanding an immediate end to the violence. The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , said today, \u8220\'20\'1COur approach is through quiet, intensive diplomacy, and that\u8217\'20\'19s where we feel we can be most effective.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The Biden administration will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/17/biden-20m-doses-covid-vaccines-overseas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 send 20m doses of US-approved coronavirus vaccines to foreign countries}}}\uc2  by the end of June. The shipments are in addition to the 60m doses of \uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s coronavirus vaccines that the US has already promised to foreign allies, meaning the administration will ship 80m doses abroad over the next six weeks. Announcing the news this afternoon, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said, \u8220\'20\'1COur nation is going to be the arsenal of vaccines for the rest of the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Coronavirus cases are declining in all 50 US states for the first time since the pandemic started. By tomorrow, about 60% of American adults will have received at least their first coronavirus vaccine dose. States are also continuing to relax coronavirus-related restrictions, with New York becoming the latest state to drop its mask mandate for fully vaccinated residents.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/17/joe-biden-tax-return-income-drop"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released their tax returns}}}\uc2  in a return to the tradition that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  scorned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.29am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.28am BST\par \par \uc2 States are continuing to adjust to the new CDC guidance on masks.\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, New York governor \uc2 Andrew Cuomo{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/may/17/joe-biden-covid-relief-bill-child-tax-credit-benefits-liz-cheney-latest-news-live?page=with:block-60a2aa3b8f08e659a47e81f3#block-60a2aa3b8f08e659a47e81f3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  that fully vaccinated New Yorkers can stop wearing masks indoors on Wednesday, 19 May.\par \par \uc2 Washington DC mayor Muriel Bowser lifted the district\u8217\'20\'19s mask mandate on Monday as well, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/local/coronavirus-dc-maryland-virginia/2021/05/17/11c446d0-b719-11eb-a6b1-81296da0339b_story.html?utm_source=feedly&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=wp_homepage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But California officials said Monday that that the state will keep its mask rules in place until 15 June in order to allow people and businesses to adjust, and to ensure that the case rate stays low, according to the AP.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis four week period will give Californians time to prepare for this change, while we continue the relentless focus on delivering vaccines particularly to underserved communities and those that were hard hit throughout this pandemic,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Dr Mark Ghaly\uc2 , the state\u8217\'20\'19s health director.\par \par \uc2 enltrCA has now administered over 35 MILLION vaccines.\par \par \uc2 We will implement the new CDC mask guidelines on 6/15, when we fully reopen our economy.\par \par \uc2 Protect yourself. Protect your loved ones. Get vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  (@GavinNewsom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GavinNewsom/status/1394373842601070594?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  had previously announced 15 June as the target date for fully reopening the state\u8217\'20\'19s economy.\par \par \uc2 Statewide, approximately {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://covid19.ca.gov/vaccination-progress-data/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 15.6m people}}}\uc2  (49% of the adult population) have been fully vaccinated, and another 4.7m are partially vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tennessee governor \uc2 Bill Lee\uc2  has signed an anti-transgender bathroom bill into law, in the latest attack on trans rights in a Republican-controlled state this year, the AP reports.\par \par \uc2 The bill would allow students, parents and employees to sue schools \u8220\'20\'1Cfor all psychological, emotional, and physical harm suffered\u8221\'20\'1D if the school allows a trans person to use a bathroom or locker room while someone else is using it.\par \par \uc2 Republican legislators across the country have unleashed an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/23/anti-trans-bills-us-transgender-youth-sports"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unprecedented attack on trans rights}}}\uc2  this year. Most of the bills have targeted trans youth, seeking to ban them from playing sports or from accessing the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/24/trans-children-healthcare-ban-gender-affirming"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gender-affirming care}}}\uc2  that is supported by all the relevant medical association in the US supports.\par \par \uc2 Most states have avoided repeating the 2015 push to ban transgender people from accessing the bathroom, however. After North Carolina enacted such a ban in 2016, the state faced a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/post-nation/wp/2017/03/27/north-carolinas-bathroom-bill-cost-the-state-at-least-3-7-billion-new-analysis-finds/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 boycott}}}\uc2  by sports leagues, corporations and artists that resulted in the loss of billions of dollars.\par \par \uc2 The ACLU of Tennessee said the bill was unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTransgender students should be treated with respect and dignity, just like everyone else,\u8221\'20\'1D said the group\u8217\'20\'19s executive director, Hedy Weinberg, in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CGovernor Lee\u8217\'20\'19s decision to sign this bill sends the opposite message \u8211\'20\'13 that students should be able to discriminate against a group of their classmates by avoiding sharing public spaces with them, and sue their schools if they are prevented from doing so.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The bathroom bill is just one of several anti-trans bills to pass the Tennessee legislature this year, the AP reported. Lee previously signed a bill to ban trans athletes from playing middle or high school girls sports, and a bill requiring schools to alert parents 30 days ahead of lessons about sexual orientation or gender identity.\par \par \uc2 Lee has not yet decided whether to sign bills to ban gender-affirming treatment for trans youth or requiring businesses to post a sign if they allow transgender people to use bathrooms or changing rooms.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.02am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s voting rights reporter Sam Levine on the latest developments in Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s election audit:\par \par \uc2 Arizona Republicans are overseeing a \u8220\'20\'1Cgrift disguised as an audit,\u8221\'20\'1D the chairman of the Maricopa county board of supervisors said on Monday, just before officials released a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.maricopa.gov/DocumentCenter/View/68972/20210517-Response-Letter-to-Senate-President-Fann---FINAL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blistering letter}}}\uc2  refuting accusations the county was hiding information from auditors.\par \par \uc2 The comments from Jack Sellers, a Republican and the chairman of the Maricopa County Board of Supervisors, marked the latest shot in a closely-watched fight in an unprecedented review of the 2.1m ballots cast in Maricopa county in 2020. Even though the county conducted multiple audits affirming the results of the 2020 race, the Arizona senate, controlled by Republicans are conducting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/14/arizona-election-audit-recount-ballots-maricopa-county"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 their own audit}}}\uc2  of the vote. The contractor the senate hired to oversee the audit is a company called Cyber Ninjas that has little experience in elections and whose CEO has voiced support for conspiracy theories that the 2020 election was stolen.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the Arizona senate accused county officials of deleting files on hardware and asking them to hand over passwords to routers. The auditors also alleged that there were discrepancies between the number of ballots the county said were on boxes and what was actually counted.\par \par \uc2 Maricopa county said in its letter Monday the claims were \u8220\'20\'1Care false, defamatory, and beneath the dignity of the Senate.\u8221\'20\'1D The county did not delete any data from the server it handed over to the auditors in April, the county said. Cyber Ninjas had only provided proof that its workers were unable to locate data, not that anything was deleted. There could be numerous explanations for this, the county wrote, suggesting that workers may have improperly executed their search or copied it in such a way that was unreadable.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRegardless, the failure of your so called \u8220\'20\'1Cauditors\u8221\'20\'1D to locate data files on the copy they made of the County\u8217\'20\'19s server speaks more to their ineptitude than it does to the integrity and actions of our dedicated public employees who effectively and accurately run the elections in the fourth largest county in the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D the county wrote.\par \par \uc2 County officials also said Cyber Ninjas were misreading the sheets that have the total number of ballots and in some cases. The number on the sheets Cyber Ninjas referenced reflect the total number of ballots that were submitted for tabulation, but there may have been ballots that were not readable by tabulators, which could explain the discrepancy.\par \par \uc2 enltrMaricopa county says Cyber Ninjas is just straight miscounting ballots {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/riK3xBi6l3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/riK3xBi6l3}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vM5Wa9XjnX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vM5Wa9XjnX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levine (@srl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/srl/status/1394400730132402178?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 In another instance, Cyber Ninjas claimed there were 218 ballots in a batch that should have had just 200. Maricopa county officials said they checked tabulation records and were confident there were 200 ballots in the box, suggesting auditors had just miscounted. An audit observer with the secretary of state\u8217\'20\'19s office {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/14/arizona-election-audit-recount-ballots-maricopa-county"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  told the Guardian}}}\uc2  earlier this month she was concerned there were not quality checks to ensure that data entry workers were correctly inputting data without typos.\par \par \uc2 The county also blasted auditors for requesting access both to voting machine equipment and county routers. Giving the auditors access to routers, the county said, would put sensitive law enforcement operations at risk. It also said the passwords to election equipment the auditors wanted were not needed to run elections and that only the equipment vendor, Dominion voting systems, had them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot give you a password that we do not possess any more than we can give you the formula for \uc2 Coca Cola\uc2 . We do not have it; we have no legal right to acquire it; and so, we cannot give it to you,\u8221\'20\'1D they wrote.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  released their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2021/05/17/the-president-and-vice-president-release-their-2020-tax-returns/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tax returns}}}\uc2  Monday, in what the White House called a continuation of \u8220\'20\'1Can almost uninterrupted tradition\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Biden and his wife, Jill Biden, reported a joint income of $606,336 and paid $157,414 in federal income tax, a 25.9% rate.\par \par \uc2 Harris and her husband, Doug Emhoff, reported a joint income of $1,695,225 and paid $621,893 in federal income tax, a 36.7% rate.\par \par \uc2 Both couples also paid state taxes.\par \par \uc2 According to Bloomberg News reporter Jennifer Epstein, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 income was \u8220\'20\'1Cdramatically\u8221\'20\'1D lower than prior years, as he stopped accepting speaking engagements in order to campaign for president.\par \par \uc2 enltrSCOOP: President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s income fell dramatically to $607,336 in 2020 as he dropped lucrative speaking engagements to campaign, but he still earned enough to pay the higher tax rates he\u8217\'20\'19s proposed for wealthy people. The Bidens paid $157,414 in federal income tax, 25.9%.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jennifer Epstein (@jeneps) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jeneps/status/1394397740906557440?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 What to make of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Csupport for a ceasefire\u8221\'20\'1D in a call with Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  ?\par \par \uc2 My colleague Julian Borger describes the readout of the call as a \u8220\'20\'1Cmildly worded statement, supporting but not demanding a ceasefire\u8221\'20\'1D. The statement also did not suggest that the ceasefire should begin immediately, Julian notes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden expresses support for ceasefire on call with Netanyahu\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cexpressed his support for a ceasefire\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cencouraged Israel to make every effort to ensure the protection of innocent civilians\u8221\'20\'1D in a phone conversation with Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  today, the White House said.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe White House readout of President Biden's call this afternoon with Prime Minister Netanyahu: "He encouraged Israel to make every effort to ensure the protection of innocent civilians." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/oC8ttM27Ea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/oC8ttM27Ea}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Daniel Strauss (@DanielStrauss4) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DanielStrauss4/status/1394403527406063616?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 According to the White House readout of the call, Biden \u8220\'20\'1Cdiscussed US engagement with Egypt and other partners\u8221\'20\'1D toward achieving a ceasefire. He also \u8220\'20\'1Cwelcomed efforts to address intercommunal violence\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cdiscussed progress in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military operations against \uc2 Hamas\uc2  and other terrorist groups in Gaza\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer joined a bipartisan call for a ceasefire in Gaza, following dozens of Democratic senators.\par \par \uc2 But the Biden administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/may/17/joe-biden-covid-relief-bill-child-tax-credit-benefits-liz-cheney-latest-news-live?page=with:block-60a2c60b8f0831dd83f7c6a4#block-60a2c60b8f0831dd83f7c6a4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seemed wary}}}\uc2  of such calls earlier Monday, with White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  responding to a question about the ceasefire by saying they were focused on \u8220\'20\'1Cquiet, intensive diplomacy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/17/israel-gaza-conflict-200-palestinians-killed-in-a-week-say-officials"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Two hundred Palestinians}}}\uc2 , including 59 children, have been killed over the past week as Israel launched airstrikes on Gaza. Ten people in Israel, including two children, have also been killed.\par \par \uc2 Read the latest report by my colleagues in Gaza and Jerusalem here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/17/israel-gaza-conflict-200-palestinians-killed-in-a-week-say-officials"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel-Gaza conflict: 200 Palestinians killed in a week, say officials}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 The number two official at the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  will retire this summer, in the latest departure for the public health agency.\par \par \uc2 Anne Schuchat\uc2 , the principal deputy director of the CDC, confirmed to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/health/2021/05/17/cdc-schuchat-announces-retirement/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post}}}\uc2  that she will step down from the agency after 33 years \u8220\'20\'1Cfor a retirement that I hope will allow more time for creative passions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Friday another longtime CDC official, Nancy Messonnier, also announced her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/health/2021/05/07/cdc-official-resigns/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resignation}}}\uc2 . In February 2020, Messonier famously warned, \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not a question of if this will happen, but when this will happen,\u8221\'20\'1D about the coronaviruses spread across the US, a statement that prompted a massive backlash from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Schuchat was also targeted by Trump. Officials told the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/health/2021/05/17/cdc-schuchat-announces-retirement/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Post}}}\uc2  that they were concerned that her departure may dampen the morale of the agency, which was placed under extraordinary pressure by the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2 , the New York governor, will earn $5.1m from his book about the coronavirus pandemic, the embattled politician revealed in financial disclosures Monday.\par \par \uc2 Cuomo was paid a $3.1m advance for the book, American Crisis: Leadership Lessons from the Covid-19 Pandemic, and will receive an additional $2m over the next two years, according to the AP.\par \par \uc2 The governor\u8217\'20\'19s spokesman said he had donated $500,000 to \uc2 the United Way\uc2  of New York State and would put the rest in a trust for his adult daughters.\par \par \uc2 The book has been something of an embarrassment for the governor, who oversaw one of the worst outbreaks in the world in the early days of the coronavirus pandemic, but received praise from the press for his media briefings.\par \par \uc2 It has sold just 50,000 copies, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/17/nyregion/cuomo-tax-returns-pandemic-book.html?partner=slack&smid=sl-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times}}}\uc2 . More than 52,000 New Yorkers have died of Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLast June, millions of New Yorkers were struggling to keep their families safe, and thousands of seniors were struggling to survive in the state\u8217\'20\'19s nursing homes, while the governor was having his staffers write a book that would make him millions off of the still-raging public health crisis,\u8221\'20\'1D the state director of the Working Families Party, Sochie Nnaemeka, told the AP.\par \par \uc2 News of Cuomo\u8217\'20\'19s coronavirus cash-in comes as the governor faces multiple investigations. The state attorney general is investigating allegations of sexual harassment from multiple women. The \uc2 FBI\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/article/andrew-cuomo-nursing-home-deaths.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigating}}}\uc2  whether Cuomo and his aides covered up the true number of deaths from Covid-19 among New York\u8217\'20\'19s nursing home residents.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hello everyone this is Julia Carrie Wong in Oakland, California picking up the politics blog for the rest of your Monday afternoon. Stay tuned for more news...\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Julia Carrie Wong, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * The supreme court will take up a case challenging Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. The case will present an opportunity for the court\u8217\'20\'19s newly fortified conservative majority to reconsider Roe v Wade, the landmark 1973 decision that established the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 * The expanded child tax credit benefits included in the coronavirus relief package will start being distributed in July, the White House announced. The new benefits will send up to $300 per child to American families each month, and the payments are expected to help cut the country\u8217\'20\'19s child poverty rate nearly in half.\par \par \uc2 * The Biden administration will send 20 million doses of US-approved coronavirus vaccines to foreign countries by the end of June. The shipments are in addition to the 60 million doses of \uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s coronavirus vaccines that the US has already promised to foreign allies, meaning the administration will ship 80 million doses abroad over the next six weeks. Announcing the news this afternoon, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said, \u8220\'20\'1COur nation is going to be the arsenal of vaccines for the rest of the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Coronavirus cases are declining in all 50 US states for the first time since the pandemic started. By tomorrow, about 60% of American adults will have received at least their first coronavirus vaccine dose. States are also continuing to relax coronavirus-related restrictions, with New York becoming the latest state to drop its mask mandate for fully vaccinated residents.\par \par \uc2 * At least 200 Palestinians, including 59 children, have been killed after a week of attacks between Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  in Gaza. Eight adults and two children in Israel have also been among the victims of the violence. A number of senior US officials, including Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer, have called for a ceasefire to the rocket attacks, but the White House has not yet echoed those demands. White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said today, \u8220\'20\'1COur approach is through quiet, intensive diplomacy, and that\u8217\'20\'19s where we feel we can be most effective.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Julia will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 200 Palestinians killed in a week, officials say as Gaza violence continues\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Hazem Balousha in Gaza and Oliver Holmes in Jerusalem report:\par \par \uc2 Two hundred Palestinians, including 59 children, have been killed during a week of attacks in Gaza, health officials in the territory have said, as \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  signalled Israel\u8217\'20\'19s bombardment would rage on despite mounting global pressure to stop the bloodshed.\par \par \uc2 Early on Monday, warplanes launched more heavy airstrikes on Gaza City, rocking apartment blocks and sending fireballs into the air. Israel said it had \u8220\'20\'1Cstruck 110 targets\u8221\'20\'1D overnight, including in a densely populated neighbourhood.\par \par \uc2 It was unclear how many people might have been killed. During the past week, Israeli attacks have destroyed a health clinic, hit the home of an aid worker, killed two doctors, destroyed high-rise residential towers, blown up a mattress factory and flattened the offices of international news organisations.\par \par \uc2 Israel says its strikes target militants. \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , the Islamist group that rules inside the strip, has stationed its fighters in and fired rockets from civilian areas. Ten people in Israel, including two children, have been killed by militants, who have launched over 3,000 rockets during the past week.\par \par \uc2 President Abdel Fatah al-Sisi of Egypt, which has long acted as a mediator between Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , said on Monday a ceasefire could be within reach. \u8220\'20\'1CHope still exists that a collective action could end the conflict,\u8221\'20\'1D he told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/17/israel-gaza-conflict-200-palestinians-killed-in-a-week-say-officials"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel-Gaza conflict: 200 Palestinians killed in a week, say officials}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer \u8217\'20\'19s comments in support of a Gaza ceasefire are even more notable in comparison to the much more muted response from the White House.\par \par \uc2 Asked why the Biden administration has not yet come out in favor of a ceasefire, White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said today, \u8220\'20\'1CThe prism we are making all of our decisions through is: How can we help bring an end to the violence and bring an end to de-escalate the situation on the ground?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd our calculation at this point is that having those conversations behind the scenes, weighing in with our important strategic partnership we have with Israel, also with other countries in the region, is the most constructive approach we can take.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Psaki added, \u8220\'20\'1COur approach is through quiet, intensive diplomacy, and that\u8217\'20\'19s where we feel we can be most effective.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrWH Press Sec. \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  on why the U.S. isn\u8217\'20\'19t yet calling for a ceasefire:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur approach is quiet, intensive diplomacy.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0JvKELddrM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/0JvKELddrM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1394332069241761794?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer has joined a bipartisan call for a ceasefire in Gaza, as airstrikes continue to cause devastation in the region.\par \par \uc2 Schumer told reporters on Capitol Hill that he agrees with a statement put out last night by Democratic senator \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2  and Republican senator \uc2 Todd Young\uc2  calling for a ceasefire.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want to see a ceasefire reached quickly and mourn the loss of life,\u8221\'20\'1D the Democratic leader said, per CNN.\par \par \uc2 enltrChuck Schumer, long-time defender of Israel, joined a bipartisan call for a ceasefire between Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "I agree with the statement put out by Sens. Murphy and Young last night in its entirety. I want to see a ceasefire reach quickly and mourn the loss of life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1394370199420383233?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 In their statement last night, Murphy and Young, the chairman and ranking member of the Senate foreign relations subcommittee on Near East, South Asia, Central Asia and counterterrorism, said Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  must deescalate their attacks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are encouraged by reports that the parties are exploring a ceasefire. We hope that this ceasefire can be reached quickly and that additional steps can be taken to preserve a two-state future,\u8221\'20\'1D the two senators said.\par \par \uc2 Dozens of Democratic senators, led by \uc2 Jon Ossoff\uc2  of Georgia, have also put out a statement calling for an immediate ceasefire.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.17pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/apr/20/supreme-court-joe-biden-black-female-justice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The US supreme court}}}\uc2  agreed on Monday to consider a major challenge to reproductive rights, saying it will take up Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s bid to enforce a ban on almost all abortions after the 15th week of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 It will be the first \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case to come before the court since the confirmation of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/19/amy-coney-barrett-william-barr-book-deals"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justice Amy Coney Barrett}}}\uc2 , a devout Catholic, gave conservatives a 6-3 majority. It could lead to the landmark Roe v Wade precedent being gutted after nearly half a century.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mississippi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi}}}\uc2  law, enacted in 2018, was blocked by lower courts as inconsistent with supreme court precedent that protects a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the foetus can survive outside her womb.\par \par \uc2 When the only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Mississippi, Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, sued to try to block the measure, a federal judge in 2018 ruled against the state. In 2019 the New Orleans-based fifth US circuit court of appeals reached the same conclusion, prompting the state to appeal to the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 The court will hear arguments in the case in its next term, which starts in October, and may not arrive at a decision until the spring or summer of 2022 \u8211\'20\'13 setting up a politically explosive showdown months before the midterm elections for Congress.\par \par \uc2 Former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s transformation of the judiciary included the appointment of three supreme court justices, most recently with Barrett replacing the late \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/28/justice-justice-thou-shalt-pursue-review-ruth-bader-ginsburg-rbg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a liberal champion of reproductive rights}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Steve Vladeck, a law professor at the University of Texas, told CNN: \u8220\'20\'1CThis will be, by far, the most important \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case the court will have heard since the Casey decision in 1992.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/may/17/abortion-case-supreme-court-threatens-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court agrees to consider major rollback of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 A pair of senators, Democrat Joe Manchin and Republican Lisa Murkowski, have sent a letter to congressional leaders calling for a bipartisan reauthorization of the Voting Rights Act.\par \par \uc2 In their letter, Manchin and Murkowski that the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision in the 2013 case Shelby v Holder \u8220\'20\'1C effectively gutted one of the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s most effective tools to preserve confidence in our nation\u8217\'20\'19s elections\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The two senators argue that the state laws passed since 2013 demonstrate the danger of not reauthorizing the VRA.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CProtecting Americans\u8217\'20\'19 access to democracy has not been a partisan issue for the past 56 years, and we must not allow it to become one now,\u8221\'20\'1D Manchin and Murkowski write.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe urge you to join us in calling for the bipartisan reauthorization of the Voting Rights Act through regular order. We can do this. We must do this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Manchin announced in an interview last week that he does not support the For the People Act, Democrats \u8217\'20\'19 broader election reform bill, but he did call for reauthorizing the VRA.\par \par \uc2 But as of now, it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear whether a VRA reauthorization has the 60 votes necessary to overcome a Senate filibuster.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Giuliani complains about treatment by prosecutors\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for former New York mayor, candidate for the Republican presidential nomination, lawyer to President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2020/oct/21/rudy-giuliani-faces-questions-after-compromising-scene-in-new-borat-film"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 victim of Borat}}}\uc2  Rudy Giuliani complained on Monday that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/29/trump-defends-giuliani-federal-agents-raid-home-office"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 federal prosecutors}}}\uc2  are treating him \u8220\'20\'1C as if he was the head of a drug cartel or a terrorist \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 . Photograph: Jonathan Ernst/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys made the claim in a letter to a Manhattan judge which was made public on Monday.\par \par \uc2 In the words of the Associated Press, recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/29/trump-defends-giuliani-federal-agents-raid-home-office"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raids on Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s residence and office}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cpertain to a federal investigation examining Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s interactions with Ukrainian figures and whether he violated a federal law that governs lobbying on behalf of foreign countries or entities without registering with the \uc2 US government\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s exertions in and in regard to Ukraine, seeking dirt on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , contributed to the first of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s two impeachments, both of which he survived when enough Republican senators stayed loyal.\par \par \uc2 The AP continues: \u8220\'20\'1CGiuliani\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers say the judge should wait to appoint someone to oversee a review of seized materials until deciding whether the government has acted constitutionally and legally in pursuit of the materials. They cited their \u8216\'20\'18serious concern over the broad and sweeping nature of the searches\u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\u8230\'20\'26 Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers wrote that the surprise raids were not necessary because Giuliani had made clear in 2019 that he would answer any questions without restrictions, except for privileged matters, as long as his lawyers knew what subjects would be discussed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey said prosecutors instead \u8216\'20\'18simply chose to treat a distinguished lawyer as if he was the head of a drug cartel or a terrorist, in order to create maximum prejudicial coverage of both Giuliani, and his most well known client - the former President of the United States\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for prosecutors declined comment to the AP, while an attorney for Giuliani, Robert Costello, said prosecutors have another week to respond.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 David Smith\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/29/rudy-giuliani-tucker-carlson-interview-fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tucker Carlson\u8217\'20\'19s conspiracy-obsessed Giuliani interview: not for the faint hearted | David Smith's sketch}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York drops mask mandate for the fully vaccinated\par \par \uc2 New Yorkers who have been fully vaccinated against Covid-19 can stop wearing masks even indoors from Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2 . Photograph: Justin Lane/EPA\par \par \uc2 Governor \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2  announced the change on Monday, from Radio City Music Hall in Manhattan, one of the venues which will reopen to vaccinated audiences.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s get back to life,\u8221\'20\'1D Cuomo said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you are vaccinated, you are safe. No masks. No social distancing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cuomo said the state would adopt CDC guidance issued last week \u8211\'20\'13 which has been contentious to say the least. (Reporting from a highly non-representative and extremely boujee co-op in Washington Heights, I can confirm that the weekend just gone featured rather heated arguments in the kids\u8217\'20\'19 playground about whether masks should be worn. The kids got on with playing while the adults argued. It was depressing.)\par \par \uc2 Unvaccinated and immunocompromised New Yorkers will still have to wear masks and everyone will need one in schools, nursing homes and on public transport.\par \par \uc2 As the AP reports, \u8220\'20\'1Cnew cases of the virus have been plummeting in New York in recent weeks and are down 78% since the end of March.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRadio City Music Hall will reopen in June at full capacity but only for vaccinated people with a red carpet event for the TriBeCa Film Festival. The city\u8217\'20\'19s two basketball teams, the \uc2 Knicks\uc2  and the Nets, will be allowed to expand attendance capacity for playoff games, with a majority of seats set aside for people who have gotten vaccines.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs for the subway\u8217\'20\'19s full reopening, the first morning of uninterrupted train service went well, Metropolitan Transportation Authority Chairman \uc2 Pat Foye\uc2  said. The system was shut down between 1am and 5am starting 30 April 2020, so trains and stations could be disinfected. The overnight closure was scaled back to 2am to 4am in February.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Also, here\u8217\'20\'19s a very New York touch to the good news about the subway, lest anyone get too delighted: Mayor \uc2 Bill de Blasio\uc2  said the city would add 250 police officers to the subway system to battle a spike in crime, including several slashings last week. Foye said the \uc2 MTA\uc2  would add 100 officers and 100 private security contractors.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 After concluding his prepared remarks on the coronavirus pandemic and vaccination efforts, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took one question from a reporter.\par \par \uc2 The reporter asked whether the president would support calling for a ceasefire in Gaza as violence between Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  escalates.\par \par \uc2 Biden noted he will be speaking to Israeli Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  in an hour, and he said he may have an update after their conversation.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 US to send 80 million vaccine doses overseas by end of next month, Biden says\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  confirmed that his administration will send 20 million doses of US-approved coronavirus vaccines overseas by the end of June.\par \par \uc2 In combination with the 60 million doses of \uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s coronavirus vaccine that the US has already promised to foreign allies, the Biden administration will send 80 million vaccine doses abroad over the next six weeks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur nation is going to be the arsenal of vaccines for the rest of the world,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The president noted that the US will be sending more vaccine doses to foreign countries than either China or Russia has, and he emphasized his administration will not be asking for \u8220\'20\'1Cfavors\u8221\'20\'1D from allies in exchange for the vaccines.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Coronavirus cases down in all US states while vaccinations rise, Biden says\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  celebrated the news that coronavirus cases are decreasing in all 50 US states for the first time since the pandemic started, marking a crucial moment in the country\u8217\'20\'19s fight against the virus.\par \par \uc2 The president also announced that tomorrow\u8217\'20\'19s data will show 60% of American adults have received at least one coronavirus vaccine dose.\par \par \uc2 Biden has set a goal of getting 70% of American adults at least partially vaccinated by July 4, and the president emphasized that unvaccinated Americans still face the risk of infection.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUltimately, those who are not vaccinated may end up paying the price,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not done fighting this virus.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now delivering remarks on the coronavirus pandemic and vaccination efforts at the White House.\par \par \uc2 The president started his speech by touting his administration\u8217\'20\'19s announcement that the enhanced child tax credit benefits, which were included in the coronavirus relief package, will start going out to American families in July.\par \par \uc2 The announcement comes on Tax Day, the deadline for Americans to file their federal tax returns.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs you file your taxes today, know that your tax cut is coming,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The president noted that families will start getting monthly payments on July 15th and the 15th of every month until the benefit runs out. Families will receive up to $300 per child each month.\par \par \uc2 Biden said the money sent a message to America\u8217\'20\'19s working families that \u8220\'20\'1Chelp is here\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg News was the first to report on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s plans to send 20 million doses of US-approved coronavirus vaccines to foreign countries.\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2021-05-17/biden-to-send-u-s-authorized-vaccines-abroad-for-first-time?sref=yYYRek8e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has these details}}}\uc2  as well:\par \par \uc2 Biden will also announce that he is putting Jeff Zients, who has served as the White House coronavirus response coordinator, in charge of his effort to beat back the pandemic globally, the official said. Zients will work with the National Security Council and other agencies to steer doses abroad....\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 , Moderna and \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccines are authorized for use in the U.S., but \uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s shot is not. It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t immediately clear which countries would receive U.S. shipments.\par \par \uc2 Mexico and Canada have already received doses of the U.S. AstraZeneca stockpile, and \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  has begun shipping doses of its U.S.-produced vaccine to countries including Mexico, Canada and Uruguay, apart from the Biden administration \u8217\'20\'19s plans to share doses.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 The White House press briefing has now ended. Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * The supreme court will take up a case challenging Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. The case will present an opportunity for the court\u8217\'20\'19s newly fortified conservative majority to reconsider Roe v Wade, the landmark 1973 decision that established the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 * The expanded child tax credit benefits included in the coronavirus relief package will start being distributed in July, the White House announced. The new benefits will send up to $300 per child to American families each month, and the payments are expected to help cut the country\u8217\'20\'19s child poverty rate nearly in half.\par \par \uc2 * The Biden administration will send 20 million doses of US-approved coronavirus vaccines to foreign countries by the end of June. The shipments are in addition to the 60 million doses of \uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s coronavirus vaccines that the US has already promised to foreign allies. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will formally announce the news when he delivers his remarks on the coronavirus pandemic, which are expected to start at any moment.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more details on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said the White House will \u8220\'20\'1Csoon\u8221\'20\'1D be releasing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s tax returns, although she did not specify whether it would be happening today.\par \par \uc2 enltrPsaki says White House will "soon" be releasing President Biden's tax returns, even if he is being audited\par \par \uc2 "We will continue to release the president's tax returns, as should be expected by every president of the United States." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/oI19khoeCW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/oI19khoeCW}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1394333303575138310?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Asked whether Biden will be releasing his tax returns even if he is audited, the White House press secretary replied, \u8220\'20\'1CWe will continue to release the president\u8217\'20\'19s tax returns, as should be expected by every president of the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The response seemed to be an implicit criticism of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who refused to publicly release his tax returns because he claimed a long-running audit prevented him from doing so. (Many tax experts said that an audit would not block him from publicly releasing his returns.)\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to send 20 million doses of US-approved coronavirus vaccines abroad\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will send 20 million doses of US-approved coronavirus vaccines to foreign countries by the end of June, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  just announced.\par \par \uc2 Those 20 million doses are in addition to the 60 million doses of \uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s coronavirus vaccine that Biden had already pledged to send abroad, the White House press secretary said.\par \par \uc2 The president is expected to formally announce the deal in his remarks on the pandemic this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Many US allies have called on the Biden administration to send more vaccine doses to other countries, noting that the pandemic will not truly come to an end until vaccines are widely available around the world.\par \par \uc2 Biden said last week that almost half of the world\u8217\'20\'19s leaders have contacted his administration asking for help in getting access to more vaccine doses.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI literally have, virtually 40% of the world leaders calling and asking, can we help them,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to try.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 US is engaged in 'quiet, intensive diplomacy' to bring end to Gaza violence, Psaki says\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , is now holding her daily briefing with reporters.\par \par \uc2 A reporter asked Psaki whether \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has reconsidered his comment from last week that Israel had not engaged in a \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant overreaction\u8221\'20\'1D as it continues to launch rocket attacks that have claimed hundreds of Palestinian lives.\par \par \uc2 Psaki replied that the president and his team are engaging in diplomatic negotiations to try to reduce the violence in Gaza, and she reiterated Biden\u8217\'20\'19s statement that Israel has a \u8220\'20\'1Cright to defend itself\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere needs to be a two-state solution over time,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is going to require both parties wanting to engage in that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked why the US is not joining other nations in calling for a ceasefire in Gaza, Psaki said the administration is engaging in \u8220\'20\'1Cquiet, intensive diplomacy\u8221\'20\'1D to bring an end to the violence.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/17/gaza-airstrikes-netanyahu-israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza rocked by fresh airstrikes after Netanyahu vows to keep attacks at \u8216\'20\'18full force\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 There were no cameras allowed inside the federal courtroom as Joel Greenberg entered his guilty plea, but a CNN reporter shared this sketch of Greenberg, an associate of Republican congressman \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , conferring with his lawyer.\par \par \uc2 enltrNo cameras in federal court but this is a sketch of Gaetz associate Joel Greenberg conferring with his defense attorney Fritz Scheller in hearing today where Greenberg admitted to soliciting a minor & paying her for sex. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OVEo7bxEGz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/OVEo7bxEGz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Paula Reid (@PaulaReidCNN) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PaulaReidCNN/status/1394314833823162368?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 A plane with a banner reading \u8220\'20\'1CTick tock \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D flew over the Orlando courthouse where the Republican congressman\u8217\'20\'19s associate, Joel Greenberg, just pleaded guilty to sex-trafficking.\par \par \uc2 A plane with a banner that reads \u8220\'20\'1C Tick tock \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D flies over the federal court in Orlando. Photograph: Joe Skipper/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  attracted even more controversy over the weekend, after the Republican congressman compared the sex-trafficking allegations against him to legislative earmarks.\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. Matt Gaetz (R) in OH, ahead of his associate\u8217\'20\'19s expected sex-trafficking guilty plea:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am being falsely accused of exchanging money for naughty favors, yet Congress has reinstituted a process that legalizes the corrupt act of exchanging money for favors through earmarks.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/byj6zaiHSy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/byj6zaiHSy}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1394279820700291073?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m being falsely accused of exchanging money for naughty favors,\u8221\'20\'1D Gaetz said at the Ohio Political Summit on Saturday. \u8220\'20\'1CYet, Congress has reinstituted a process that legalizes the corrupt act of exchanging money for favors, through earmarks, and everybody knows that that\u8217\'20\'19s the corruption.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At the risk of stating the obvious, there is absolutely no comparison between legislative earmarks and sex-trafficking.\par \par \uc2 Earmarks are a legal way for lawmakers to direct funds in bills toward their districts for specific projects, while sex-trafficking is a federal crime that can result in decades-long prison sentences.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Gaetz associate pleads guilty to sex-trafficking charge\par \par \uc2 Joel Greenberg, an associate of Republican congressman \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , has pleaded guilty to six federal criminal counts, including sex-trafficking of a 17-year-old girl.\par \par \uc2 Greenberg\u8217\'20\'19s guilty plea may cause more legal trouble for Gaetz, who was already facing sex-trafficking allegations as well. (The Florida congressman has denied those accusations.)\par \par \uc2 The AP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/politics-government-and-politics-baabc0bc60d898cacab299e7ff2c0ea4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Joel Greenberg, a longtime associate of Gaetz, appeared in federal court in Orlando. He pleaded guilty to six of the nearly three dozen charges he faced, including sex trafficking of a minor, and he admitted that he had paid at least one underage girl to have sex with him and other men.\par \par \uc2 Gaetz was not mentioned in the plea agreement or during the court hearing. But Greenberg\u8217\'20\'19s cooperation \u8212\'20\'14 as a key figure in the investigation and a close ally of Gaetz \u8212\'20\'14 may escalate the potential legal and political liability that the firebrand Florida congressman is facing.\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors are examining whether Gaetz and Greenberg paid underage girls or offered them gifts in exchange for sex, according to two people familiar with the matter. Investigators have also been looking at whether Gaetz and his associates tried to secure government jobs for some of the women, the people said. They are also scrutinizing Gaetz\u8217\'20\'19s connections to the medical marijuana sector, including whether his associates sought to influence legislation Gaetz sponsored.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Gaza rocked by fresh airstrikes after Netanyahu vows to keep attacks at \u8216\'20\'18full force\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Oliver Holmes, Bethan McKernan, Julian Borger and agencies report:\par \par \uc2 Israeli warplanes have launched what appeared to be the heaviest airstrikes yet on Gaza City, hours after the Israeli prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , signalled the bombardment would rage on.\par \par \uc2 The series of attacks early on Monday rocked the city from north to south for 10 minutes and was more intense, covered a broader area and lasted longer than the raids 24 hours earlier in which 42 Palestinians were killed \u8211\'20\'13 the deadliest single attack in the latest violence between Israel and the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  militant group that rules Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Local media reports said the main coastal road west of the city, security compounds and open spaces were among the targets hit early on Monday. The power distribution company said the airstrikes damaged a line feeding electricity from the only power plant to large parts of southern Gaza City. There were no immediate reports of injuries.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli army spokesperson\u8217\'20\'19s office said the strikes targeted \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cunderground military infrastructure\u8221\'20\'1D. As a result of the strike, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe underground facility collapsed, causing the civilian houses\u8217\'20\'19 foundations above them to collapse as well, leading to unintended casualties\u8221\'20\'1D, it said.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, air-raid sirens sounded for the seventh consecutive day across southern {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel}}}\uc2  as \uc2 Hamas\uc2  and other militant groups in Gaza launched more rocket attacks into the country \u8211\'20\'13 and reaching further \u8211\'20\'13 than in the entirety of the 2014 war.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/17/gaza-airstrikes-netanyahu-israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza rocked by fresh airstrikes after Netanyahu vows to keep attacks at \u8216\'20\'18full force\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 The selection of cases currently before the supreme court means that justices could theoretically create a constitutional right to carry a concealed firearm and overturn Roe v Wade by next June, just months before the 2022 midterms, as a writer for Slate notes.\par \par \uc2 enltrI had expected the conservative justices to put off blockbuster cases until after the midterm elections to deprive Democrats of ammunition for court reform. But nope: SCOTUS is poised to create a constitutional right to concealed carry AND overturn Roe by June 2022.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mark Joseph Stern (@mjs_DC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mjs_DC/status/1394288613471424517?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mary Ziegler\uc2 , a legal expert who specializes in the history of reproduction laws, said the Mississippi \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case is a threat to Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 But she added that the case could also give the supreme court the opportunity to reconsider how it determines the legality of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, which could have vast implications for the country.\par \par \uc2 enltrEveryone will interpret this (rightly) as a real threat to Roe. The alternative? That SCOTUS will jettison viability as the point at which bans are possible. And that could be almost as big of a deal. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4WXXFn6uvP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/4WXXFn6uvP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Mary Ziegler\uc2  (@maryrziegler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maryrziegler/status/1394285279318577154?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court will likely hear arguments in the Mississippi \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case this fall, setting up a decision for next year.\par \par \uc2 If the decision is announced in late June, which is when the court usually issues rulings in its most high-profile cases, the news would come about four months before the 2022 midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 The AP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/supreme-court-abortion-15-week-ban-5d066a9dc0030a4f8297711f341c9f5a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has more details}}}\uc2  on the Mississippi \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case and how it will be a test of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s newly fortified conservative majority:\par \par \uc2 The justices had put off action on the case for several months. Justice \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2 , an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights proponent, died just before the court\u8217\'20\'19s new term began in October. Her replacement, Justice Amy Coney Barrett, is the most open opponent of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to join the court in decades.\par \par \uc2 Barrett is one of three appointees of former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on the Supreme Court. The other two, Justices \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  and \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 , voted in dissent last year to allow Louisiana to enforce restrictions on doctors that could have closed two of the state\u8217\'20\'19s three \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics.\par \par \uc2 Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , joined by Ginsburg and the other three liberal justices, said the restrictions were virtually identical to a Texas law the court struck down in 2016.\par \par \uc2 But that majority no longer exists, even if Roberts, hardly an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporter in his more than 15 years on the court, sides with the more liberal justices.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court will likely hear arguments in the Mississippi \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case this fall, setting up a decision announcement sometime next year.\par \par \uc2 The 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban has so far been blocked by lower courts as inconsistent with previous supreme court decisions on the issue, including Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court to take up major \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case in opportunity to reconsider Roe\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has agreed to take up a case challenging a Mississippi law that bans most abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The case could give the majority-conservative court the chance to reconsider Roe v Wade, the landmark 1973 decision that established the right to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: The Supreme Court agrees to take up a major \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case that will give the court an opportunity to reconsider Roe v. Wade and Planned Parenthood v. Casey. The case involves the constitutionality of Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s ban on most abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1394284425224114176?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 There were initial concerns that the \uc2 IRS\uc2  would not be able to start sending the monthly child tax credit payments in July because of the demands of tax season and the rest of the coronavirus relief package.\par \par \uc2 However, IRS Commissioner \uc2 Charles Rettig\uc2  said at a Senate hearing last month that his agency was on track to meet the original timeline for distributing payments.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe fully expect to launch in July. We expect to launch with payments going out on a monthly basis,\u8221\'20\'1D Rettig told senators.\par \par \uc2 But the IRS commissioner acknowledged there may be some troubleshooting that needs to be done to improve the portal built to aid distribution of the funds.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is going to be as user-friendly as possible,\u8221\'20\'1D Rettig said of the portal.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 According to the treasury department, roughly 39 million American households will start receiving monthly payments from the enhanced child tax credit starting in July.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: The first monthly payment of the expanded and newly-advanceable Child Tax Credit (\uc2 CTC\uc2 ) from the American Rescue Plan will be made on July 15.\par \par \uc2 Roughly 39 million households\u8212\'20\'14covering 88% of children in the US\u8212\'20\'14are slated to begin receiving monthly payments automatically.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Treasury Department (@USTreasury) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/USTreasury/status/1394269088533393412?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The monthly payments are meant to help families with children budget with the tax credit in mind, rather than receiving the money as one lump sum.\par \par \uc2 The enhanced payments are phased out for married couples filing jointly who make more than $150,000 a year, heads of household who make more than $112,500 a year and any other single filers who make more than $75,000 a year.\par \par \uc2 The benefits are expected to cover about 88% of children in the US and will is expected to help reduce child poverty nearly in half across the country.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Child cash benefits from Covid relief bill to start in July\par \par \uc2 Greetings from Washington, live blog readers.\par \par \uc2 The White House has announced that the enhanced child tax credit benefits included in the $1.9 trillion coronavirus relief package will start being distributed in July.\par \par \uc2 With the benefits in effect, about 90% of Americans will receive monthly payments of up to $300 for each child in their families. The payments are expected to help significantly reduce child poverty.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  speaks prior to signing the American Rescue Plan on March 11. Photograph: Tom Brenner/Reuters\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe American Rescue Plan is delivering critical tax relief to middle class and hard-pressed working families with children,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said in a statement celebrating the news.\par \par \uc2 The president also called on Congress to pass his American Families Plan to \u8220\'20\'1Censure that working families will be able to count on this relief for years to come,\u8221\'20\'1D as the bill would make these benefits permanent.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor working families with children, this tax cut sends a clear message: help is here,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The president will likely tout the news when he delivers remarks on the pandemic later today, so stay tuned for updates on that.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210517eh5h001xk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
