\par\par \uc2 Global development\par \b \uc2 Biden urged to end US aid \u8216\'20\'18 \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Liz Ford \par \uc2 467 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 April 2021\par 13:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 More than 140 rights groups call for repeal of 1973 Helms amendment widely misinterpreted as total ban on funding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services overseas\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden is being urged to clarify a longstanding US law restricting overseas aid that has been misinterpreted by successive administrations as an outright ban on funding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for any reason.\par \par \uc2 As the US president marked his first 100 days in office on Friday, more than 140 human rights and global health organisations, including \uc2 Human Rights Watch\uc2 , \uc2 Amnesty International US\uc2  and the Global Justice Center, signed a letter asking him to confirm that US aid can be used for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in cases of rape, incest and when the woman\u8217\'20\'19s life is in danger.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://globaljusticecenter.net/files/UPR_Biden_Letter.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  calls on the president to back {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2020/jul/29/democrats-introduce-bill-to-repeal-anti-abortion-rule-for-us-overseas-aid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a bill}}}\uc2 , introduced in Congress last year, to permanently repeal the 1973 Helms amendment, which has been wrongly interpreted as a ban on US money being used for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in any circumstances.\par \par \uc2 The letter says: \u8220\'20\'1CAs written, the law restricts the use of US foreign assistance for \u8216\'20\'18\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a method of family planning\u8217\'20\'19. This does not include cases of rape, incest, or life-endangerment; however, lack of clarity around the law has prevented the use of funds in these cases, even in humanitarian emergency settings.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The group want clear guidance issued on Helms and another misinterpreted law, the Leahy amendment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe US is the largest funder of global health, including family planning, and is the only donor nation to single out \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in this way,\u8221\'20\'1D the letter says. \u8220\'20\'1CMany US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, including the Helms amendment, have consistently been in place for decades, causing generations\u8217\'20\'19 worth of harm \u8211\'20\'13 and they will continue to do so if action is not taken. This is a matter of utmost urgency as bodily autonomy and reproductive freedom are increasingly under siege.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During his first 10 days in office, Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2021/jan/28/joe-biden-global-gag-rule-health-groups"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rescinded the Mexico City Policy}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 known as the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/video/2017/jan/18/what-is-the-global-gag-rule-and-why-does-trump-support-it-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 global gag rule}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 which stopped overseas groups that received US aid using money from other sources to fund \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the US vice-president, co-signed a bill to repeal the policy permanently \u8211\'20\'13 currently, it can be reintroduced or rescinded by each president.\par \par \uc2 Akila Radhakrishnan, president of the Global Justice Center, said the belief that the Helms amendment banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under all circumstances had become \u8220\'20\'1Cnormalised\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Bethany Van Kampen, an adviser at the signatory reproductive health charity Ipas, said the law \u8220\'20\'1Chas to be fully repealed\u8221\'20\'1D but that in the meantime: \u8220\'20\'1CWhy would we not mitigate the harm of Helms? That would save lives immediately.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a pro-choice research organisation, has estimated that repealing the Helms amendment {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/infographic/2021/impact-repealing-helms-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could result}}}\uc2  in 19m fewer unsafe abortions and 17,000 maternal deaths a year.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210430eh4u001xo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
