\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden hails \u8216\'20\'18stunning progress\u8217\'20\'19 on Covid but warns Americans: \u8216\'20\'18Do not let up now\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh and Joanna Walters \par \uc2 10,153 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 April 2021\par 00:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President lauds vaccination effort to reduce cases and deathsBiden raises minimum wage for workers paid by federal contractorsTexas sheriff who criticized Trump is nominated to head IceCDC relaxes guidelines on mask-wearing for AmericansRepublicans still orbiting Trump dark star fail to derail Biden\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  a little earlier signed an executive order {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/apr/27/joe-biden-covid-coronavirus-us-politics-live-latest?page=with:block-608879898f08a84aa592039b#block-608879898f08a84aa592039b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raising}}}\uc2  the minimum wage paid by federal contractors to $15 an hour. \u8220\'20\'1C I believe no one should work full time and still live in poverty,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 * The president plans to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/apr/27/joe-biden-covid-coronavirus-us-politics-live-latest?page=with:block-60886a6b8f08505668d9d31d#block-60886a6b8f08505668d9d31d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nominate}}}\uc2 Ed Gonzalez\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a Texas sheriff who vocally opposed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s policy of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/jun/22/going-through-hell-at-the-border-parents-split-from-children-tell-of-anguish"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 separating migrant children}}}\uc2  from their families \u8211\'20\'13 to lead the \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  agency. In 2017, Gonzalez stopped allowing his personnel from participating in an Ice program that had local deputies helping identify undocumented immigrants for deportation.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2 , the governor of North Carolina, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/apr/27/joe-biden-covid-coronavirus-us-politics-live-latest?page=with:block-608870338f08a84aa5920345#block-608870338f08a84aa5920345"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called for}}}\uc2  a special prosecutor to be appointed to investigate the police {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/andrew-brown-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shooting of Andrew Brown}}}\uc2 . The shooting of Brown, 42, prompted days of protests and calls for accountability.\par \par \uc2 * Earlier this afternoon, Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/apr/27/joe-biden-covid-coronavirus-us-politics-live-latest?page=with:block-608851bd8f08080a7ae6dcb0#block-608851bd8f08080a7ae6dcb0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke}}}\uc2  outside the White House to hail progress towards ending the coronavirus pandemic, while warning that there was a long way to go. He said people in the US should not \u8220\'20\'1Clet up\u8221\'20\'1D and should definitely get vaccinated ASAP as a patriotic duty. The speech followed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/apr/27/joe-biden-covid-coronavirus-us-politics-live-latest?page=with:block-608839048f08080a7ae6db22#block-608839048f08080a7ae6db22"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new advice}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  that fully vaccinated people in US can go without mask s outdoors except in crowded settings.\par \par \uc2 * The governor of Arizona, \uc2 Doug Ducey\uc2 , signed a bill that criminalizes abortions based on genetic conditions and implements a raft of extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures. The bill confers civil rights to unborn children, requires fetal remains to be cremated or buried, and prevents public money from being used to support research involving abortions, among other things.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 US Interior Department\uc2  has reversed Trump-era policies governing Native American tribes\u8217\'20\'19 ability to establish and consolidate land trusts. The department restored jurisdiction to the regional \uc2 Bureau of Indian Affairs\uc2  directors to review and approve the transfer of private land into federal trust for tribes. The Trump administration had moved the oversight of the process to the department headquarters.\par \par \uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 Joanna Walters and Maanvi Singh\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.15am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Arizona governor signs extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill\par \par \uc2 The governor of Arizona, \uc2 Doug Ducey\uc2 , has signed a bill that criminalizes abortions based on genetic conditions and implements a raft of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures opposed by medical groups and women\u8217\'20\'19s health advocates.\par \par \uc2 The bill confers civil rights to unborn children, requires fetal remains to be cremated or buried, prohibits educational institutions from performing abortions unless the mother\u8217\'20\'19s life is in jeopardy, forbids the mailing or delivery of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -inducing drugs (which doctors use to manage miscarriages as well as to induce \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) and prevents public money from being used to support research involving abortions.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, the Republican governors of Oklahoma and Montana signed laws severely limiting abortions.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/apr/27/us-tiny-towns-anti-abortion-ordinances"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The tiny American towns passing anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rules}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.35am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans still orbiting Trump dark star fail to derail Biden\u8217\'20\'19s first 100 days\par \par \uc2 For Democrats it has been a hundred days of sweeping legislation, barrier-breaking appointments and daring to dream big. For Republicans, a hundred days {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/09/us/republicans-take-up-trumps-fight-leaving-policymaking-on-the-sidelines.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in the political wilderness.}}}\par \par \uc2 The party that just four years ago controlled the White House and both chambers of Congress now finds itself shut out of power and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/joe-biden/lost-shuffle-republicans-battle-around-biden-now-n1264812"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struggling to find its feet}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/09/us/republicans-take-up-trumps-fight-leaving-policymaking-on-the-sidelines.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 .}}}\uc2  As \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  forges ahead with ambitions to shift the political paradigm, Republicans still have a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  problem.\par \par \uc2 The former US president remains the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/21/opinion/trump-republicans.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unofficial leader of the party}}}\uc2  and exerts a massive gravitational pull on its senators, representatives, governors and state parties. Obsessed with \u8220\'20\'1Cculture wars\u8221\'20\'1D and voter fraud, the Trump distortion field has made it difficult for Republicans to move on.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is like a fire,\u8221\'20\'1D said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bgrdc.com/team-member-post/ed-rogers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ed Rogers,}}}\uc2  a political consultant and a veteran of the \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  and George H W Bush administrations. \u8220\'20\'1CToo close and you get burned. Too far away, you\u8217\'20\'19re out in the cold. So the party spends a lot of time talking about the fire, managing the fire, orbiting the fire. It takes a lot of energy out of the party.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election in 2008 was the last time Democrats swept the board of White House, House of Representatives and Senate. On that occasion conservatives exploited the financial crisis to stir resentment about government spending, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2010/oct/05/us-midterm-elections-2010-tea-party-movement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 giving rise to the Tea Party}}}\uc2  and winning back the House in the midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 But this time looks very different. Republicans were forced to watch from the sidelines as Biden oversaw the distribution of 200m coronavirus vaccination doses while bringing down unemployment. They failed to find a coherent line of attack on his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/10/joe-biden-covid-relief-bill-passed-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $1.9tn Covid relief package,}}}\uc2  which opinion polls showed was popular with the public, including Republican voters.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/27/joe-biden-100-days-republicans-orbit-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans still orbiting Trump dark star fail to derail Biden\u8217\'20\'19s first 100 days}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats are pushing Biden to admit more refugees into the US\par \par \uc2 Biden announced earlier this month that he would not increase refugee admissions from the record low cap of 15,000 that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  set before leaving office. After intense pushback from advocates and Democratic lawmakers, Biden said he\u8217\'20\'19d increase the cap by 15 May.\par \par \uc2 But it remains unclear what the new cap will be.\par \par \uc2 In a letter from Senator \uc2 Dick Durbin\uc2  of Illinois, 32 Democratic co-signatories asked Biden to admit up to 62,500 refugees by September, and then increase the cap to 125,000 for the next fiscal year, the Washington Post reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe United States must reject the previous administration\u8217\'20\'19s cruel legacy of anti-refugee policies and return to our long-standing bipartisan tradition of providing safety to the world\u8217\'20\'19s most vulnerable refugees,\u8221\'20\'1D the senators wrote, in a copy reviewed by The Washington Post\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/people/seung-min-kim/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Seung Min Kim}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more background on the issue:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/16/joe-biden-refugee-admissions-trump-us-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden walks back refugee admissions policy after outcry and will lift cap in May}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 WHO blames \u8216\'20\'18perfect storm\u8217\'20\'19 of factors for India Covid crisis\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday morning, a flight from the UK carrying vital medical supplies including ventilators landed in Delhi. Six oxygen containers were flown in from Dubai and in a phone conversation between the Indian prime minister, \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2 , and the US president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , on Monday, Biden pledged \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica\u8217\'20\'19s steadfast support\u8221\'20\'1D to India by providing oxygen-related supplies and vaccine raw materials.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust as India sent assistance to the United States as our hospitals were strained early in the pandemic, we are determined to help India in its time of need,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden wrote on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The crisis prompted the German army to provide a large oxygen production plant while France has said it will send supplies to India via air and sea, including eight oxygen concentrators, containers of liquid oxygen and 28 respirators.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 EU\uc2  said it would send medicine and oxygen to India in the coming days. \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 EU\uc2  is pooling resources to respond rapidly to India\u8217\'20\'19s request for assistance,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 , the president of the European commission, on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Pledges of support have also come from Denmark, Saudi Arabia, the UAE, Australia and Bhutan. The tiny kingdom which neighbours India, also said it would be sending \u8220\'20\'1Ca spare few hundred litres\u8221\'20\'1D of oxygen as soon as its newly built oxygen plant was up and running.\par \par \uc2 In March, India gifted Bhutan over half a million Oxford/\uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2  vaccines, which helped the country implement one of the world\u8217\'20\'19s fastest vaccinations rollouts, where it vaccinated 93% of the small population in just 16 days.\par \par \uc2 Many fear that the international aid being sent to India will not be enough to fill the acute gap in supplies of oxygen, which has been affecting hospitals in Delhi and Uttar Pradesh, despite the state\u8217\'20\'19s chief minister insisting there was \u8220\'20\'1Cno oxygen shortage\u8221\'20\'1D, and threatening private hospitals with criminal charges if they \u8220\'20\'1Cspread rumours\u8221\'20\'1D about oxygen scarcity.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/apr/27/international-aid-arrives-in-india-to-combat-deadly-covid-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 WHO blames \u8216\'20\'18perfect storm\u8217\'20\'19 of factors for India Covid crisis}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interior Department reverses Trump-era policies on tribal land\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Interior Department\uc2  has reversed Trump-era policies governing Native American tribes\u8217\'20\'19 ability to establish and consolidate land trusts.\par \par \uc2 The department restored jurisdiction to the regional \uc2 Bureau of Indian Affairs\uc2  directors to review and approve the transfer of private land into federal trust for tribes. The Trump administration had moved the oversight of the process to the department headquarters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CQe have an obligation to work with Tribes to protect their lands and ensure that each Tribe has a homeland where its citizens can live together and lead safe and fulfilling lives,\u8221\'20\'1D said Deb Haaland, the first Native American woman to lead the department. \u8220\'20\'1COur actions today will help us meet that obligation and will help empower Tribes to determine how their lands are used \u8211\'20\'13 from conservation to economic development projects.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The agency also reversed several Trump admin rules that hindered or complicated the process for putting land into trust.\par \par \uc2 The AP explains:\par \par \uc2 Whether land is in trust has broad implications for whether tribal police can exercise their authority, for tribal economic development projects to attract financing and for the creation of homelands and government offices for tribes that don\u8217\'20\'19t have dedicated land.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration put 75,000 acre (30,300 hectares) into trust over four years, versus more than 560,000 acres (226,600 hectares) in the eight years of the Obama administration, Interior officials said.\par \par \uc2 The trust land system was adopted in 1934, when Congress passed the Indian Reorganization Act in response to more than 90 million acres (36.4 million hectares) of tribal homelands that had been converted into private land under the 1887 Allotment Act.\par \par \uc2 Approximately 56 million acres (22.7 million hectares) are currently in trust. Combined that\u8217\'20\'19s an area bigger than Minnesota and makes up just over 2 percent of the U.S.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Jill Biden will visit former president Jimmy Carter and former first lady \uc2 Rosalynn Carter\uc2  this week.\par \par \uc2 A day after the president delivers his address to Congress, the Bidens will make a trip to Georgia, where the Carters reside. The Carters, who are both in their 90s, did not attend Biden\u8217\'20\'19s inauguration due to the pandemic. Now that they have both been vaccinated, they will be able to safely visit with the Bidens.\par \par \uc2 Biden will also likely hold some sort of drive-in event in Georgia to mark his 100th day in office, the White House has previously indicated.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 The blog will hand over from the US east coast to the west coast now, where our colleague Maanvi Singh is ready to take you through the next few hours of developing politics news. There\u8217\'20\'19s plenty of it, so please stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 Main items so far today:\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  a little earlier signed an executive order {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/apr/27/joe-biden-covid-coronavirus-us-politics-live-latest?page=with:block-608879898f08a84aa592039b#block-608879898f08a84aa592039b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raising}}}\uc2  the minimum wage paid by federal contractors to $15 an hour.\par \par \uc2 * The US president plans to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/apr/27/joe-biden-covid-coronavirus-us-politics-live-latest?page=with:block-60886a6b8f08505668d9d31d#block-60886a6b8f08505668d9d31d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nominate}}}\uc2 Ed Gonzalez \u8211\'20\'13 a Texas sheriff who vocally opposed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s policy of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/jun/22/going-through-hell-at-the-border-parents-split-from-children-tell-of-anguish"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 separating migrant children}}}\uc2  from their families \u8211\'20\'13 to become the head of the \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  agency.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2 , the governor of North Carolina, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/apr/27/joe-biden-covid-coronavirus-us-politics-live-latest?page=with:block-608870338f08a84aa5920345#block-608870338f08a84aa5920345"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called for}}}\uc2  a special prosecutor to be appointed to handle the investigation into the police {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/andrew-brown-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shooting of Andrew Brown}}}\uc2 , a 42-year-old Black man, in the state last week.\par \par \uc2 * Earlier this afternoon, Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/apr/27/joe-biden-covid-coronavirus-us-politics-live-latest?page=with:block-608851bd8f08080a7ae6dcb0#block-608851bd8f08080a7ae6dcb0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke}}}\uc2  outside the White House to hail progress towards ending the coronavirus pandemic, while warning that there was a long way to go. He said people in the US should not \u8220\'20\'1Clet up\u8221\'20\'1D and should definitely get vaccinated ASAP as a patriotic duty.\par \par \uc2 * This followed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/apr/27/joe-biden-covid-coronavirus-us-politics-live-latest?page=with:block-608839048f08080a7ae6db22#block-608839048f08080a7ae6db22"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new advice}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  that fully vaccinated people in US can go without masks outdoors except in crowded settings.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden raises minimum wage for workers paid by federal contractors\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  a little earlier signed an executive order raising the minimum wage paid by federal contractors to $15 an hour.\par \par \uc2 enltrI believe no one should work full time and still live in poverty. That\u8217\'20\'19s why today, I raised the minimum wage to $15 an hour for people working on federal contracts.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1387123131500924929?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 27, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The tweet and the sentiment didn\u8217\'20\'19t go down terribly well with everyone.\par \par \uc2 enltrSo in other words, you mean that everyone who makes minimum wage who is not a federal employee should work full time and still live in poverty.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 LADY BUNNY (@LADYBUNNY77) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LADYBUNNY77/status/1387147222689660936?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 27, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The $15 minimum is likely to take effect next year and increase the wages of hundreds of thousands of workers, according to a White House document.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 New York Times\uc2  has a lot more on this, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/27/business/economy/biden-minimum-wage-federal-contractors.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 , including this:\par \par \uc2 White House economists believe that the increase will not lead to significant job losses \u8212\'20\'14 a finding in line with recent research on the minimum wage \u8212\'20\'14 and that it is unlikely to cost taxpayers more money, two administration officials said in a call with reporters. They argued that the higher wage would lead to greater productivity and lower turnover.\par \par \uc2 And although the number of workers directly affected by the increase is small as a share of the economy, the administration contends that the executive order will indirectly raise wages beyond federal contractors by forcing other employers to bid up pay as they compete for workers.\par \par \uc2 Paul Light, an expert on the federal work force at \uc2 New York University\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brookings.edu/blog/fixgov/2020/10/07/the-true-size-of-government-is-nearing-a-record-high/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently estimated}}}\uc2  that about five million people are working on federal contracts, on which the government {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gao.gov/assets/720/710485.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spends}}}\uc2  hundreds of billions of dollars each year.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 When the former Minneapolis police officer Derek Chauvin was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/20/derek-chauvin-verdict-guilty-murder-george-floyd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found guilty}}}\uc2  a week ago today of murdering {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/george-floyd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 George Floyd}}}\uc2  last May, the judge in the case mentioned that sentencing was expected in eight weeks\u8217\'20\'19 time.\par \par \uc2 So the sentencing hearing had been expected on 18 June, but news just emerged from a brief court filing today that it will now be scheduled for 25 June.\par \par \uc2 Chauvin is white and Floyd was Black and his murder, seen around the world on a bystander\u8217\'20\'19s video as the officer kneeled on his neck for more than nine minutes, fanned the largest civil rights uprising in the US since the 1960s.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/17/daunte-wright-george-floyd-americas-recurring-tragedy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Daunte Wright and George Floyd: another chapter in America\u8217\'20\'19s recurring tragedy}}}\par \par \uc2 The only reason cited for the later sentencing date was a scheduling conflict, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The trial in the Hennepin county court house in downtown Minneapolis lasted three weeks before Chauvin was convicted on all three counts facing him.\par \par \uc2 Second degree murder carries a maximum sentence of 40 years. That was the most serious charge, which Chauvin had denied, along with the other two charges, of third degree murder and manslaughter.\par \par \uc2 The AP adds that the longest sentence Chauvin is expected to be given, according to experts, is 30 years, maybe less.\par \par \uc2 The jury only deliberated for about 10 hours, over two days, before unanimously reaching its verdict.\par \par \uc2 Do watch \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s excellent film about the trial and reverberations.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Governor calls for special prosecutor in Andrew Brown case\par \par \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2 , the governor of North Carolina, has called for a special prosecutor to be appointed to handle the investigation into the police {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/andrew-brown-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shooting of Andrew Brown}}}\uc2 , a 42-year-old Black man, in the state last week.\par \par \uc2 enltrGov. Cooper issued the following statement urging a special prosecutor following the Pasquotank County shooting: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6m5UqxyZ09"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6m5UqxyZ09}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Governor \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2  (@NC_Governor) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NC_Governor/status/1387129382213496834?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 27, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Cooper, a Democrat, put out a statement saying such an appointment would be \u8220\'20\'1Cin the interest of justice and confidence in the judicial system\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He said that: \u8220\'20\'1CThis would help assure the community and Mr Brown\u8217\'20\'19s family that a decision on pursuing criminal charges is conducted without bias.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Demonstrators called this morning for p0lice officers to be arrested, after an independent autopsy arranged by the family {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/27/andrew-brown-shooting-autopsy-attorneys"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 concluded}}}\uc2  that Brown was killed with a bullet that entered the back of his head.\par \par \uc2 Attorneys for Brown\u8217\'20\'19s family, who were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/26/andrew-brown-police-shooting-body-cam-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shown only a 20-second clip}}}\uc2  of police body camera footage yesterday, said in a press conference in Elizabeth City, North Carolina, that the man\u8217\'20\'19s hands were clearly placed on the steering wheel of his car, where police could see him, when they fired at him, and that he was driving away, presenting no threat.\par \par \uc2 The local North State Journal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nsjonline.com/article/2021/04/gov-cooper-urges-special-prosecutor-appointment-in-elizabeth-city-case/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 adds}}}\uc2  that:\par \par \uc2 Should the district attorney request a special prosecutor, the potential appointment could come from the North Carolina Attorney General\u8217\'20\'19s Special Prosecution Division, the Administrative Office of the Courts, or the Conference of District Attorneys.\par \par \uc2 Cooper\u8217\'20\'19s call follows the announcement of an \uc2 FBI\uc2  civil rights investigation into the shooting.\par \par \uc2 There will be a protest march tomorrow over the fatal shooting.\par \par \uc2 enltrHAPPENING NOW: Church members announced they will march from Mt. Zion A.M.E. Church tomorrow at 11:30 to the location where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/AndrewBrownJr?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #AndrewBrownJr}}}\uc2  was shot & killed here in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/ElizabethCity?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #ElizabethCity}}}\uc2 . They\u8217\'20\'19re calling on people of all denominations to join them {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpecNews1RDU?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SpecNews1RDU}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4x7aWhzdxJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4x7aWhzdxJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyleigh Panetta (@KyleighPanetta) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KyleighPanetta/status/1387116945426763790?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 27, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Texas sheriff who criticized Trump is nominated to head Ice\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  plans to nominate \uc2 Ed Gonzalez\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a Texas sheriff who vocally opposed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s policy of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/jun/22/going-through-hell-at-the-border-parents-split-from-children-tell-of-anguish"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 separating migrant children}}}\uc2  from their families \u8211\'20\'13 to a key post as the head of the \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  agency (Ice), the White House has announced.\par \par \uc2 enltrWhite House nominates Harris County Sheriff \uc2 Ed Gonzalez\uc2  to lead ICE {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/A5W3YP0SWI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/A5W3YP0SWI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Houston Chronicle (@HoustonChron) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HoustonChron/status/1387124973488283654?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 27, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Gonzalez is a Houston native and a veteran law enforcement officer and Democrat who has served since 2017 as sheriff of Harris county, the most populous county in Texas, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 In a July 2019 \uc2 Facebook\uc2  post, Gonzalez said he opposed sweeping immigration raids after Republican former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , a month earlier tweeted hyperbolically that ICE would begin deporting \u8220\'20\'1Cmillions of illegal aliens\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI do not support ICE raids that threaten to deport millions of undocumented immigrants, the vast majority of whom do not represent a threat to the US,\u8221\'20\'1D Gonzalez wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CThe focus should always be on clear & immediate safety threats.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The nomination would need to be approved by the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , divided 50-50 between Democrats and Republicans, with Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  able to break ties.\par \par \uc2 Biden campaigned on a pledge to reverse many of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s hardline immigration policies. After Biden took office on January 20, his administration placed a 100-day pause on many deportations and greatly limited who can be arrested and deported by ICE.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s deportation moratorium drew fierce pushback from Republicans and was blocked by a federal judge in Texas days after it went into effect.\par \par \uc2 Biden announced on April 12 that he would tap Chris Magnus, an Arizona police chief, to lead \uc2 U.S. Customs and Border Protection\uc2  (CBP). Magnus had criticized the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to force so-called \u8220\'20\'1Csanctuary\u8221\'20\'1D jurisdictions to cooperate with federal law enforcement.\par \par \uc2 Gonzalez similarly sought to limit ties between local police and federal immigration enforcement. In 2017, he ended Harris County\u8217\'20\'19s participation in a program that increased cooperation between county law enforcement and federal immigration authorities.\par \par \uc2 enltrWow. Thinking back to when \uc2 Ed Gonzalez\uc2  was the new sheriff in town, having run on a reform-minded platform, and quickly made the call to terminate Harris County's 287(g) partnership with ICE. Now the White House wants him to lead the agency, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nkhensley?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @nkhensley}}}\uc2  reports: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/B9R2YvCWvF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/B9R2YvCWvF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Meagan Flynn (@Meagan_Flynn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Meagan_Flynn/status/1387129310436372487?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 27, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s another view:\par \par \uc2 enltrRepublicans will hate his nomination. That should tell you everything you need to know. \uc2 Ed Gonzalez\uc2  withdrew from the 287(g) collaboration program with ICE while he was sheriff of Harris County.\par \par \uc2 Ed has fought ICE at every turn to protect Houstonians. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/RSn6kSFcOz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/RSn6kSFcOz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Stephanie Clay ???????????? (@_StephanieClay) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/_StephanieClay/status/1387129474848894978?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 27, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House is considering options for maximizing production and supply of Covid-19 vaccines for the world at the lowest cost, including backing a proposed waiver of intellectual property rights.\par \par \uc2 No decision has been made, press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said a little earlier.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are a lot of different ways to do that. Right now, that\u8217\'20\'19s one of the ways, but we have to assess what makes the most sense,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said, adding that US officials were also looking at whether it would be more effective to boost manufacturing in the United States.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been incredibly difficult to cope with assessing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2021/apr/25/oscars-2021-best-picture-nomadland-chloe-zhao"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Oscars ceremony}}}\uc2  without the help of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , so fortunately the former president has glided back into our lives for a moment to fill that void.\par \par \uc2 Here comes a statement from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s office. It speaks for itself.\par \par \uc2 Statement by \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2 , 45th president of the United States of America\par \par \uc2 What used to be called The Academy Awards, and now is called the \u8220\'20\'1COscars\u8221\'20\'1D\u8212\'20\'14a far less important and elegant name\u8212\'20\'14had the lowest Television Ratings in recorded history, even much lower than last year, which set another record low. If they keep with the current ridiculous formula, it will only get worse\u8212\'20\'14if that\u8217\'20\'19s possible. Go back 15 years, look at the formula they then used, change the name back to THE ACADEMY AWARDS, don\u8217\'20\'19t be so politically correct and boring, and do it right. ALSO, BRING BACK A GREAT HOST. These television people spend all their time thinking about how to promote the Democrat Party, which is destroying our Country, and cancel Conservatives and Republicans. That formula certainly hasn\u8217\'20\'19t worked very well for The Academy!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 So that clears that up.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Photograph: Mandel Ngan/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 Here is where the day stands so far in US political news. There will be a lot more coming up, so please stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  warned the nation \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/apr/27/joe-biden-covid-coronavirus-us-politics-live-latest?page=with:block-608851bd8f08080a7ae6dcb0#block-608851bd8f08080a7ae6dcb0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 do not let up now}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D in the battle against the coronavirus pandemic, as he said there was a long way to go but hailed \u8220\'20\'1Cstunning progress\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The US president said that getting vaccinated was everyone\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cpatriotic duty\u8221\'20\'1D and said those who have been fully vaccinated would be able to enjoy many activities outdoors safely without \u8220\'20\'1Cmasking up\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 FBI\uc2  has launched a federal civil rights i {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/apr/27/joe-biden-covid-coronavirus-us-politics-live-latest?page=with:block-608848678f08505668d9d19d#block-608848678f08505668d9d19d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nvestigation}}}\uc2  into the police killing of Andrew Brown in North Carolina last week.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 Centers for Disease Control\uc2  and Prevention{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/apr/27/joe-biden-covid-coronavirus-us-politics-live-latest?page=with:block-608839048f08080a7ae6db22#block-608839048f08080a7ae6db22"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  this morning that fully vaccinated people in US can go without masks outdoors except in crowded settings.\par \par \uc2 * Lawyers representing the family of Andrew Brow n, a Black man shot dead by police in North Carolina last week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/apr/27/joe-biden-covid-coronavirus-us-politics-live-latest?page=with:block-6088296b8f08080a7ae6d9fa#block-6088296b8f08080a7ae6d9fa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  after a private autopsy that he was killed with a police gunshot to the back of his head.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 'Do not let up now' - Biden\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said that getting vaccinated is a \u8220\'20\'1Cpatriotic duty\u8221\'20\'1D for everyone in the US and urged people to continue efforts to bring the pandemic under control.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDo not let up now, keep following the guidance and go get vaccinated NOW,\u8221\'20\'1D the US president said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s free, it\u8217\'20\'19s convenient,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding that 90% of people in the US live within five miles of a site where it is possible to get vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 He dangled the lure of \u8220\'20\'1Cgoing to the park for a picnic without having to mask up as long as you get vaccinated\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 More than half of US adults have had at least one shot against the coronavirus at this point. Biden said the US has made stunning progress but has a long way to go.\par \par \uc2 Biden said things had improved \u8220\'20\'1Cdramatically\u8221\'20\'1D in terms of case numbers and death rates compared with when he took office in January. Two thirds of the most vulnerable population group overall, seniors, are now fully vaccinated, he added.\par \par \uc2 The president remarked on what a gorgeous spring day it was, that he wished he could stay outside but needed to head inside to get back to work, donned his trademark aviator sunglasses and turned from the podium.\par \par \uc2 He lingered to answer a few press questions, however, and remarked briefly on how the US was sending help to India, where coronavirus is raging.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Photograph: Evan Vucci/AP\par \par \uc2 And this president occasionally tweets.\par \par \uc2 enltrBecause of the extraordinary progress we\u8217\'20\'19ve made in the fight against COVID-19, the CDC made a big announcement today: If you are fully vaccinated \u8212\'20\'14 and if you are outdoors and not in a large crowd \u8212\'20\'14 you no longer need to wear a mask.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1387104758335479813?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 27, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden hails 'stunning progress' in combating pandemic\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is speaking now about the US coronavirus efforts. The US president said the US was striving towards the target of being able to \u8220\'20\'1Cget life in America closer to normal\u8221\'20\'1D by the Fourth of July \u8220\'20\'1Cand celebrate our independence from the virus,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Standing in the sunshine in Washington, DC, Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CWhile we still have a long way to go and a lot of work to do in May and June...we have made stunning progress. Cases and deaths are down.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is late. As we wait for the president to present his latest remarks on the coronavirus pandemic, here is a wrap of the morning\u8217\'20\'19s news in the case of the police shooting of Andrew Brown in North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 The Reuters news agency reports:\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for the family of Andrew Brown Jr., a Black man killed by law enforcement in North Carolina, said an independent autopsy showed he died from a \u8216\'20\'18kill shot\u8217\'20\'19 to the back of his head, as the \uc2 FBI\uc2  on Tuesday opened a civil rights investigation of the shooting.\par \par \uc2 Brown, 42, was struck with four bullets to his right arm before the fatal shot penetrated the rear of his skull as he tried to drive away, the lawyers told a news conference in Elizabeth City, a riverfront community near the Virginia border where the shooting took place last Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 An official autopsy has yet to be released, though the death certificate had indicated Brown died of a gunshot to the head.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a \u8216\'20\'18kill\u8217\'20\'19 shot to the back of the head,\u8221\'20\'1D said attorney \uc2 Ben Crump\uc2 , citing the private autopsy conducted by Brent Hall, a former medical examiner in Boone, North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Shortly after the news conference, the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Charlotte Field Office announced that it has opened a federal civil rights investigation of the shooting, saying in a statement it would work with federal prosecutors in the Department of Justice to \u8220\'20\'1Cdetermine whether federal laws were violated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Brown\u8217\'20\'19s death led to six nights of protests in Elizabeth City and came one day after former Minneapolis police officer Derek Chauvin was convicted of murdering \uc2 George Floyd\uc2  in a trial that put a renewed spotlight on police violence against Black people.\par \par \uc2 The Brown family\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have said deputies belonging to the Pasquotank County Sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s Office continued firing their weapons after Brown drove his vehicle away from them, calling his death an \u8220\'20\'1Cexecution.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pasquotank County Sheriff Tommy Wooten and Chief Deputy Daniel Fogg have said the deputies were trying to serve warrants on Brown stemming from a felony drug charge, and that Brown had a history of resisting arrest.\par \par \uc2 They urged the public to reserve judgment until all evidence is reviewed by the State Bureau of Investigation, which is overseeing the probe of the shooting.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis tragic incident was quick and over in less than 30 seconds and body cameras are shaky and sometimes hard to decipher. They only tell part of the story,\u8221\'20\'1D Wooten said in a video posted on social media on Monday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 FBI\uc2  to investigate police killing of Andrew Brown\par \par \uc2 This news is just coming through on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/apr/27/joe-biden-covid-coronavirus-us-politics-live-latest?page=with:block-6088296b8f08080a7ae6d9fa#block-6088296b8f08080a7ae6d9fa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shooting}}}\uc2  of Brown last week in North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe FBI Charlotte Field Office has opened a federal civil rights investigation into the police involved shooting death of Andrew Brown Jr. Agents will work closely with the US Attorney\u8217\'20\'19s Office for the eastern district of North Carolina and the civil rights division at the Department of Justice to determine whether federal laws were violated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s from the bureau.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you more, probably after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s address on coronavirus, expected shortly.\par \par \uc2 enltrJUST IN: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FBICharlotte?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @FBICharlotte}}}\uc2  confirms with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpecNews1RDU?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SpecNews1RDU}}}\uc2  that it has opened a federal civil rights investigation into the \u8220\'20\'1Cpolice involved shooting death\u8221\'20\'1D of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/AndrewBrownJr?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #AndrewBrownJr}}}\uc2  in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/ElizabethCity?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #ElizabethCity}}}\uc2 . See the statement below ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/E8OUnY2pvU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/E8OUnY2pvU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyleigh Panetta (@KyleighPanetta) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KyleighPanetta/status/1387091961929256964?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 27, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vaccination rates growing 'in an extraordinary way' - CDC\par \par \uc2 CDC director \uc2 Rochelle Walensky\uc2  said that signs are encouraging in US efforts to bring the coronavirus pandemic under control.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s only four weeks since Walensky was so worried about the pace of vaccination and mitigation efforts being swamped by a fresh surge of infections that she said she was scared, threw away her prepared remarks and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/29/us-covid-cases-cdc-walensky-doom-scared-biden-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  of a \u8220\'20\'1Crecurring feeling I have of impending doom\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 While there are still huge problems, especially in states such as Michigan, which is experiencing a horrible wave of the virus, speaking nationally, Walensky described the curve of the incidences of serious illness and death was \u8220\'20\'1Cstabilizing, it\u8217\'20\'19s coming down\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She urged everyone in the US to \u8220\'20\'1Croll up your sleeves!\u8221\'20\'1D and said that \u8220\'20\'1Cvaccinations are growing in an extraordinary way\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 During questioning by the press, Walensky said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to encourage everyone to get vaccinated. She said the acceleration in the administration of vaccinations in the US meant that \u8220\'20\'1Ccases are staring to stabilize, plateau and come down..when vaccinations continue to soar we should be in good shape.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Around 54% of US adults have had at least one shot now, with almost 30% of US adults fully vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 Top infectious diseases official \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2  added that if anyone is hesitant about receiving the vaccine because they think the science was rushed, they should be reassured that although the coronavirus vaccine was developed in a record 11 months it came on the back of \u8220\'20\'1Cdecades of fundamental science. This was not rushed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The daily average of new confirmed cases in the US is now 34,600, a 21% decline from the previous seven-day average of 54,400 cases.\par \par \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2 , the nation\u8217\'20\'19s top infectious disease expert, left, Department of Health and Human Services Chief Science Officer for COVID Response David Kessler, center, and Centers for Disease Control and Prevention Director \uc2 Dr. Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , right, talk before the start of a House Select Subcommittee hearing on April 15, 2021 on Capitol Hill in Washington, DC. Photograph: \uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , the director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC), just said at a briefing from the White House coronavirus team that people who have been fully vaccinated against coronavirus \u8220\'20\'1Ccan begin to get back to normal\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Creturn to many activities safely\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COver the past year, we have spent a lot of time telling Americans what they cannot do,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CToday, I\u8217\'20\'19m going to tell you some of the things you can do, if you are fully vaccinated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Walensky said at the briefing that the coronavirus vaccines available in the US are safe and effective.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you are fully vaccinated things are much safer for you than for those not yet fully vaccinated. This guidance will help you, your family and your neighbors make decisions based on the latest science and safely get back to things you love to do.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are many situations where people who are fully vaccinated do not need to wear a mask, particularly if they are outdoors.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For those fully vaccinated: \u8220\'20\'1CIf you want to attend a small outdoor gathering with people who are vaccinated and unvaccinated, or dine at an outdoor restaurant with friends from multiple households, the science shows that if you are vaccinated you can do so safely, unmasked.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrCDC director \uc2 Rochelle Walensky\uc2  says fully vaccinated people do not have to wear masks at small outdoor gatherings or outdoor restaurants with people from multiple households. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OAMWGe9xa1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/OAMWGe9xa1}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/x8ge3MzixP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/x8ge3MzixP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1387082984801570821?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 27, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fully vaccinated people in US can go without masks outdoors except in crowded settings\par \par \uc2 US health officials say fully vaccinated Americans don\u8217\'20\'19t need to wear masks outdoors anymore unless they are in a big crowd of strangers, and those who are unvaccinated can go without a face covering outside in some cases, too, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  released the updated guidance Tuesday in yet another carefully calibrated step on the road back to normal from the coronavirus outbreak that has killed over 570,000 people in U.S.\par \par \uc2 For most of the past year, the CDC had been advising Americans to wear masks outdoors if they are within 6 feet of each other.\par \par \uc2 The change comes as more than half of U.S. adults have gotten at least one dose of coronavirus vaccine, and more than a third have been fully vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the return of freedom,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr. Mike Saag, an infectious disease expert at the \uc2 University of Alabama at Birmingham\uc2  who welcomed the change. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the return of us being able to do normal activities again. We\u8217\'20\'19re not there yet, but we\u8217\'20\'19re on the exit ramp. And that\u8217\'20\'19s a beautiful thing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 More people need to be vaccinated, and concerns persist about variants and other possible shifts in the epidemic. But Saag said the new guidance is a sensible reward following the development and distribution of effective vaccines and about 140 million Americans stepping forward to get their shots.\par \par \uc2 The CDC, which has been cautious in its guidance during the crisis, essentially endorsed what many Americans have already been doing over the past several weeks.\par \par \uc2 The CDC guidance says that fully vaccinated or not, people do not have to wear masks outdoors when they walk, bike or run alone or with members of their household. They also can go maskless in small outdoor gatherings with fully vaccinated people.\par \par \uc2 But from there, the CDC has differing guidance for people who are fully vaccinated and those who are not.\par \par \uc2 Unvaccinated people defined by the CDC as those who have yet to receive both doses of the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  or Moderna vaccine or the one-shot \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  formula should wear masks at outdoor gatherings that include other unvaccinated people. They also should keep using masks at outdoor restaurants.\par \par \uc2 Fully vaccinated people do not need to cover up in those situations, the CDC says.\par \par \uc2 However, everyone should keep wearing masks at crowded outdoor events such as concerts or sporting events, the CDC says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 The police department in Louisville, Kentucky, is to be the subject of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/26/louisville-kentucky-policing-justice-department-investigation-breonna-taylor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 federal investigation}}}\uc2  by the Department of Justice, attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  announced yesterday.\par \par \uc2 People attend a rally in March to mark one year since police officers shot and killed Breonna Taylor when they entered her home, in Louisville, Kentucky. Photograph: Amira Karaoud/Reuters\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/breonna-taylor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Breonna Taylor}}}\uc2  was shot dead by police there during a botched drug raid just over a year ago.\par \par \uc2 The local Courier Journal newspaper and website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courier-journal.com/story/news/politics/metro-government/2021/04/27/why-us-justice-department-investigating-louisville-police/7390977002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has this}}}\uc2  on the news about the Louisville Metro Police Department (LMPD):\par \par \uc2 Louisville Metro Police has become the latest department targeted by a \uc2 U.S. Department of Justice\uc2  investigation into potential bias in policing patterns and practices.\par \par \uc2 The news, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courier-journal.com/story/news/politics/metro-government/2021/04/26/justice-department-to-investigate-louisville-police-department/7385318002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  announced Monday by the U.S. Attorney General}}}\uc2 , follows the high-profile fatal police shooting last year of 26-year-old Breonna Taylor, whose name joined \uc2 George Floyd\uc2  as a national rallying cry for racial justice.\par \par \uc2 But the probe is expected to extend far beyond the March 13, 2020, shooting at Taylor\u8217\'20\'19s apartment, focusing as well on Louisville Metro Police\u8217\'20\'19s practices around traffic stops, search warrants and use of force.\par \par \uc2 The investigation could find police in Louisville have acted unconstitutionally and violated citizens\u8217\'20\'19 rights, but local officials have cast it as an opportunity to continue work around reforms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe all share a commitment and an urgency to this review, which is part and parcel of the work we\u8217\'20\'19ve been doing to reimagine public safety and build greater trust, respect, transparency and accountability with the people of Louisville and LMPD,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mayor \uc2 Greg Fischer\uc2 ....\par \par \uc2 The probe is set to examine if LMPD:\par \par \uc2 * Used unreasonable force, including during peaceful protests;\par \par \uc2 * Engaged in unconstitutional stops, searches and seizures;\par \par \uc2 * Discriminated against people based on race; and\par \par \uc2 * Failed to provide public services in compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act.\par \par \uc2 Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  speaks at the Department of Justice in Washington, Monday, April 26, 2021, as associate Attorney General Vanita Gupta (L) and Deputy Attorney General Lisa Monaco (R) listen. He announced a federal investigation of policing in Louisville, KY. Photograph: Mandel Ngan/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 An appeal hearing is due today in Texas in the case of the police officer who murdered Botham Jean in 2018. Jean was sitting at home eating ice cream.\par \par \uc2 The family of Botham Jean hug after unveiling the street sign for Botham Jean Boulevard which is named after their slain son and brother in Dallas, on Saturday, March 27, 2021. Botham Jean, who was murdered in his Cedars apartment by a Dallas police officer in September 2018, lived on this portion of the street formerly known as South Lamar Street. Photograph: Juan Figueroa/AP\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press takes up the report:\par \par \uc2 A Texas court is scheduled to hear arguments on overturning the conviction of a former Dallas police officer who was sentenced to prison for fatally shooting her neighbor in his home.\par \par \uc2 An attorney for Amber Guyger and prosecutors are set to clash before an appeals court over whether the evidence was sufficient to prove that her 2018 shooting of Botham Jean was murder.\par \par \uc2 The hearing before a panel of judges will examine a Dallas County jury\u8217\'20\'19s 2019 decision to sentence Guyger to 10 years in prison for murder.\par \par \uc2 It follows the recent conviction of a former Minneapolis police officer who was found guilty of murdering \uc2 George Floyd\uc2 , again focusing national attention on police killings and racial injustice.\par \par \uc2 More than two years before Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s death set off protests across the country, Guyger \u8217\'20\'19s killing of Jean drew national attention because of the strange circumstances and because it was one in a string of shootings of Black men by white police officers.\par \par \uc2 The basic facts of the case were not in dispute. Guyger, returning home from a long shift, mistook Jean\u8217\'20\'19s apartment for her own, which was on the floor directly below his. Finding the door ajar, she entered and shot him, later testifying that she through he was a burglar.\par \par \uc2 Jean, a 26-year-old accountant, had been eating a bowl of ice cream before Guyger shot him. She was later fired from the Dallas Police Department.\par \par \uc2 The appeal from Guyger, now 32, hangs on the contention that her mistaking Jean\u8217\'20\'19s apartment for her own was reasonable and, therefore, so too was the shooting. Her lawyers have asked the appeals court to acquit her of murder or to substitute in a conviction for criminally negligent homicide, which carries a lesser sentence.\par \par \uc2 In court filings, Dallas County prosecutors countered that Guyger\u8217\'20\'19s error doesn\u8217\'20\'19t negate \u8220\'20\'1Cher culpable mental state.\u8221\'20\'1D They wrote, \u8220\'20\'1Cmurder is a result-oriented offense.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jean\u8217\'20\'19s mother, Allison Jean, told the Dallas Morning News that the appeal has delayed her family\u8217\'20\'19s healing process.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know everyone has a right of appeal, and I believe she\u8217\'20\'19s utilizing that right,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut on the other hand, there is one person who cannot utilize any more rights because she took him away.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo having gotten 10 years, only 10, for killing someone who was in the prime of his life and doing no wrong in the comfort of his home, I believe that she ought to accept, take accountability for it and move on,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Gwen Carr, the mother of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/eric-garner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Eric Garner}}}\uc2 , who died when he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/jun/05/eric-garner-trial-nypd-daniel-pantaleo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 choked by police}}}\uc2  in New York in 2014 while he pleaded \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t breathe\u8221\'20\'1D, just spoke at the press conference in North Carolina called by attorneys and relatives of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/26/andrew-brown-police-shooting-body-cam-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Brown}}}\uc2 , who was shot dead there by police last week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey never intended to take him alive,\u8221\'20\'1D she said of the way police in Elizabeth City, NC, approached Brown, 42, last week before he was shot dead.\par \par \uc2 The details known publicly of what happened in the interaction are still very limited, mostly because the authorities have released very little.\par \par \uc2 There was uproar yesterday after county authorities said they would show Brown\u8217\'20\'19s family police body camera footage of the man\u8217\'20\'19s killing and then, after hours of delay, showed only a selected 20-second \u8220\'20\'1Csnippet\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Chantel Cherry-Lassiter, one of the group of attorneys for the family, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/26/andrew-brown-police-shooting-body-cam-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  at the time that when the short clip started, police guns - both assault rifles and pistols - appeared already to be firing. But that she could see Brown with both his hands on the steering wheel of his car and not \u8220\'20\'1Cat any time\u8221\'20\'1D threatening the officers.\par \par \uc2 Carr said moments ago that she believes the group of police had \u8220\'20\'1Ctheir own agenda\u8221\'20\'1D when they came to apprehend Brown with a drugs-related warrant last week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey is what they do in the Black and brown communities. They terrorize and they kill and it\u8217\'20\'19s swept under the rug,\u8221\'20\'1D Carr said.\par \par \uc2 Gwen Carr. Behind her on the right of the picture (in sunglasses) is Khalil Ferebee, Andrew Brown\u8217\'20\'19s son. Photograph: Jim Lo Scalzo/EPA\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Andrew Brown\u8217\'20\'19s son, Khalil Ferebee, just told those gathered for a press conference in North Carolina that he believed his statement yesterday that his father had been \u8220\'20\'1Cexecuted\u8221\'20\'1D by the police was confirmed by the evidence that brown died from a shot to the back of the head.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CViolence is not the key,\u8221\'20\'1D he told the crowd gathered in Elizabeth City.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut my pop,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, before trailing off. He talked about the independent autopsy that the family had requested as showing his father was shot three times in the arm before he was killed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAre three shots to the arm not enough? It\u8217\'20\'19s obvious that he was trying to get away, and they are going to shoot him in the back of the head? That\u8217\'20\'19s not right, something\u8217\'20\'19s got to change,\u8221\'20\'1D Ferebee said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/26/andrew-brown-police-shooting-body-cam-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Brown shooting: anger as family shown only \u8216\'20\'18snippet\u8217\'20\'19 of police footage}}}\par \par \uc2 The press conference is ongoing.\par \par \uc2 enltrFive penetrating bullet wounds including a \u8220\'20\'1Ckill shot\u8221\'20\'1D to the back of the head. That\u8217\'20\'19s the autopsy result being read by the attorneys for Andrew Brown\u8217\'20\'19s family now. They note four non-fatal bullet wounds to Brown\u8217\'20\'19s right arm, followed by a fatal shot to the head.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joy-Ann Pro-Democracy & Masks Reid ?? (@JoyAnnReid) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoyAnnReid/status/1387062197445029889?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 27, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Developments in police killing of Andrew Brown\par \par \uc2 Attorneys representing the family of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/andrew-brown-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Brown}}}\uc2  are holding press conference right now in Elizabeth City, North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Brown, 42, was killed by police there last week and details are coming out very slowly.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday the family and attorneys {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/26/andrew-brown-police-shooting-body-cam-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused the authorities}}}\uc2  of \u8220\'20\'1Chiding\u8221\'20\'1D video evidence of \u8220\'20\'1Can execution\u8221\'20\'1D on Monday after relatives were shown only a 20-second clip of the incident from a single officer\u8217\'20\'19s body camera.\par \par \uc2 Civil rights attorney \uc2 Ben Crump\uc2  is at the conference going on now and is announcing the results of an independent autopsy that was arranged.\par \par \uc2 He is confirming a report yesterday that came from the death certificate that Brown was killed with a bullet that entered the base of the back of Brown\u8217\'20\'19s head.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a kill shot to the back of the head,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Ben Crump\uc2 , one of the attorneys. \u8220\'20\'1CIt went into the base of the neck, bottom of the skull and got lost in his brain. That was the cause of death.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A group of attorneys is presenting findings and diagrams. They report that Brown was hit by five shots.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CArrest them right now,\u8221\'20\'1D people in the crowd are calling out, referring to the police.\par \par \uc2 Family attorney Harry Daniels reiterated that when Brown was shot dead in a hail of bullets after at least eight officers came to him with a drugs-related warrant last week, Brown put his hands on the wheel of his car, where they were visible.\par \par \uc2 Brown was driving away \u8220\'20\'1Ctrying to run because he was scared for his life\u8221\'20\'1D after being shot in the arm and then in the back of the head as he was heading away.\par \par \uc2 Protesters march in the evening after family members were shown a brief clip of body camera footage of a deputy sheriff shooting and killing Black suspect Andrew Brown Jr. last week, in Elizabeth City, North Carolina. Photograph: Jonathan Drake/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Police killings of Black Americans amount to crimes against humanity, international inquiry finds.\par \par \uc2 Minnesota prosecutor Jerry Blackwell successfully argued to the jury in the Derek Chauvin trial last week that the former police officer had murdered \uc2 George Floyd\uc2  on May 25 last year. Photograph: AP\par \par \uc2 Our colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edpilkington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ed Pilkington}}}\uc2  reports exclusively today that the systematic killing and maiming of defenseless African Americans by police amount to crimes against humanity that should be investigated and prosecuted under international law.\par \par \uc2 The news comes from an inquiry into US police brutality by leading human rights lawyers from around the globe.\par \par \uc2 A week after the former Minneapolis police officer Derek Chauvin was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/20/derek-chauvin-verdict-guilty-murder-george-floyd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 convicted of murder}}}\uc2  in \uc2 George Floyd\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s death, the unabated epidemic of police killings of Black men and women in the US has now attracted scorching international attention.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://inquirycommission.org/website/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/Commission-Report-15-April.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 devastating report}}}\uc2  running to 188 pages, human rights experts from 11 countries hold the US accountable for what they say is a long history of violations of international law that rise in some cases to the level of crimes against humanity.\par \par \uc2 They point to what they call \u8220\'20\'1Cpolice murders\u8221\'20\'1D as well as \u8220\'20\'1Csevere deprivation of physical liberty, torture, persecution and other inhuman acts\u8221\'20\'1D as systematic attacks on the Black community that meet the definition of such crimes.\par \par \uc2 They also call on the prosecutor of the international criminal court (ICC) in The Hague to open an immediate investigation with a view to prosecutions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis finding of crimes against humanity was not given lightly, we included it with a very clear mind,\u8221\'20\'1D Hina Jilani, one of the 12 commissioners who led the inquiry, told \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe examined all the facts and concluded that that there are situations in the US that beg the urgent scrutiny of the ICC.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 You can read Ed\u8217\'20\'19s full report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/26/us-police-killings-black-americans-crimes-against-humanity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate committee hears from tech policy chiefs on algorithm secrets\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a hearing underway at the Senate judiciary committee into the algorithms tech giants use to influence what pops up most frequently for you to look at or be directed towards on social media.\par \par \uc2 Policy chiefs from \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , \uc2 Twitter\uc2  and \uc2 YouTube\uc2  are testifying. You can watch the hearing live, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://video.gutools.co.uk/videos/13f3d93c-9f89-47ea-a771-778779d55f5d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Axios political news site has a lively and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/algorithms-congress-transparency-hearing-9893ea60-d4d0-43b9-a5f7-e267257c8968.html?utm_source=newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=newsletter_axiosam&stream=top"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reader-friendly take}}}\uc2  on all of this. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a chunk:\par \par \uc2 Tech platforms have built the heart of their businesses around secretive computer algorithms, and lawmakers and regulators now want to know just what\u8217\'20\'19s inside those black boxes.\par \par \uc2 Why it matters: Algorithms, formulas for computer-based decision making, are responsible for what we get shown on \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , \uc2 Twitter\uc2  and \uc2 YouTube\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 and, increasingly, for choices companies make about who gets a loan or parole or a spot at a college.\par \par \uc2 How it works: When posts \u8220\'20\'1Cgo viral,\u8221\'20\'1D algorithms are why. Often, they work by detecting small blips in user interest and amplifying them.\par \par \uc2 * Algorithms\u8217\'20\'19 complexity and obscurity have helped tech firms make the case that they are neutral platforms. They also allow companies to stand at one remove from responsibility for decisions about promoting and demoting content.\par \par \uc2 * But users and critics, increasingly aware of the power of these systems, now want to hold companies more responsible for the outcomes their code produces.\par \par \uc2 Driving the news : At a hearing on \u8220\'20\'1CAlgorithms and Amplification,\u8221\'20\'1D executives from \uc2 YouTube\uc2 , \uc2 Twitter\uc2  and \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , along with Harvard researcher Joan Donovan and ethicist Tristan Harris, will testify Tuesday before the \uc2 Senate Judiciary Committee\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s privacy, technology and law subcommittee.\par \par \uc2 * The subcommittee is led by Sen. Chris Coons (D-Del.) and ranking member \uc2 Sen. Ben Sasse\uc2  (R-Neb.).\par \par \uc2 The big picture: Government agencies around the world are starting to take up issues related to algorithms and machine learning.\par \par \uc2 Our thought bubble : The conversation in policy circles has long concentrated on the outer limits of content decisions \u8212\'20\'14 decisions about what gets removed and who gets banned. Those are what software people call \u8220\'20\'1Cedge cases.\u8221\'20\'1D What gets recommended, and why, is the center of the issue.\par \par \uc2 Between the lines : Platforms have long used their algorithms to boost business metrics, such at the amount of time spent on their site. Increasingly, though, they are also acknowledging and tapping the power of algorithms to limit the spread of misinformation or hate speech that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t merit an outright ban.\par \par \uc2 enltrHAPPENING NOW: A hearing on "Algorithms and Amplification," where social media executives + Harvard researcher {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BostonJoan?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @BostonJoan}}}\uc2  & ethicist {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tristanharris?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @tristanharris}}}\uc2  will testify before \uc2 Senate Judiciary Committee\uc2 's privacy, technology & law subcommittee. Livestream: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dxY9bGOTPC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/dxY9bGOTPC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Center for Democracy & Technology\uc2  (@CenDemTech) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CenDemTech/status/1387051520932212737?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 27, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is expected to propose beefing up the \uc2 Internal Revenue Service\uc2  to crack down on wealthy individuals and corporations that evade paying federal taxes.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will seek an extra $80 billion to fund U.S. tax collections that would help pay for his plan to bolster childcare, universal prekindergarten education and paid leave for workers, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reported on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic president\u8217\'20\'19s proposal to boost the \uc2 Internal Revenue Service\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s budget over 10 years would help the agency curb tax evasion through audits of high earners and large corporations and include new disclosure requirements, the Times said, citing two people familiar with the plan.\par \par \uc2 Representatives for the White House and the \uc2 U.S. Treasury Department\uc2 , which oversees the \uc2 IRS\uc2 , had no immediate comment.\par \par \uc2 IRS chief \uc2 Charles Rettig\uc2  told lawmakers earlier this month tax evasion costs the United States $1 trillion or more each year.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s American Families Plan, expected to be released before his address to Congress on Wednesday, is part of the Democratic president\u8217\'20\'19s sweeping economic agenda, but details are still emerging.\par \par \uc2 It would have to pass a closely divided Congress where Democrats hold a thin majority.\par \par \uc2 House of Representatives Ways and Means Committee Chairman Richard Neal on Tuesday set the stage for legislative action, introducing a bill expanding workers\u8217\'20\'19 paid leave, boosting state childcare efforts and expanding tax credits.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s potentially $1.5 trillion effort could reshape life for many people in the United States trying to balance work and family life, and the White House has said the wealthy and corporations can afford to pay for new programs.\par \par \uc2 It also increases taxes on the wealthiest Americans, sources said last week.\par \par \uc2 Republicans generally rejected higher taxes, and passed a sweeping tax cut in 2017 under Republican President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But Biden, who is also pushing for companies to help fund his separate $2.3 trillion infrastructure plan, has been adamant about targeting non-payers to re-invest in the nation.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  marks {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/26/biden-100-days-bold-action-broad-vision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 100 days}}}\uc2  in office later this week. The coronavirus and the health and economic fallout from the pandemic was priority one upon the Democrat being inaugurated at the US Capitol on January 20, 2021.\par \par \uc2 A medical worker administers the coronavirus vaccine to the public at a FEMA run mobile clinic at Biddeford High School in Bidderford, Maine on April 26. Photograph: Joseph Prezioso/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has this backgrounder on Biden and the virus.\par \par \uc2 Biden spent his first 100 days in office {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/joe-biden-donald-trump-jake-tapper-coronavirus-pandemic-fa365aa74f80e768bce3edc1649e4e8a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 encouraging Americans to mask up}}}\uc2  and stay home to slow the spread of the coronavirus. His task for the next 100 days will be to lay out the path back to normal.\par \par \uc2 When he entered office, Biden moved swiftly to overcome {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/merck-help-make-johnson-johnson-vaccine-9ca6f1f4c502b095531926a53abe7262"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vaccine supply issues}}}\uc2  and more than tripled the country\u8217\'20\'19s ability to administer them. But ending {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/hub/coronavirus-pandemic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the coronavirus pandemic}}}\uc2 , the central challenge of his presidency, will require more than putting shots into arms \u8212\'20\'14 a task now growing more difficult as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/nm-state-wire-health-coronavirus-government-and-politics-108f1fd0813f0d2ecec1589fd137625d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demand sags}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 but also a robust plan to help the nation emerge from a year of isolation, disruption and confusion.\par \par \uc2 If Biden launched the nation onto a war footing against a virus that infected nearly 200,000 Americans in January and killed about 3,000 of them per day, the next months will be tantamount to winning the peace. Already, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coronavirus.jhu.edu/map.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deaths are down}}}\uc2  to fewer than 700 per day and average daily cases are below 60,000. U.S. officials insist there is a long way to go before the country can be fully at ease, but the progress is marked.\par \par \uc2 Going forward, success will mean finishing the nation\u8217\'20\'19s herculean vaccination campaign \u8212\'20\'14 to date 43% of Americans have received at least one shot \u8212\'20\'14 overcoming lagging demand and communicating in clear terms what activities can be safely resumed by those who are vaccinated. Key milestones include Biden\u8217\'20\'19s July Fourth pledge that Americans can safely gather with friends and family, and the start of the new school year, when the president hopes to have all schools open safely.\par \par \uc2 The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  was expected to unveil new guidance on outdoor mask-wearing for unvaccinated people on Tuesday, ahead of a planned speech by Biden later in the day on the state of the pandemic response. Officials said a focus in the coming weeks will on easing guidance for vaccinated people, both in recognition of their lower risk and to provide an incentive to get shots.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re excited about the progress we\u8217\'20\'19ve made, and the opportunity ahead of us, and because of the vaccination program we built we\u8217\'20\'19re further along than almost anyone predicted,\u8221\'20\'1D said White House COVID-19 coordinator Jeff Zients in a Monday interview. \u8220\'20\'1CIt means we\u8217\'20\'19re closer to returning to normal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/joe-biden-inauguration-a01d1ffa7862661914cb92b22e359854"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Inauguration Day}}}\uc2 , the notion of COVID-19 vaccine supply eclipsing demand seemed fanciful, with only priority groups eligible for shots and an underground economy emerging for \u8220\'20\'1Cextra doses\u8221\'20\'1D for everyone else. Now, shots are so plentiful in many places that the Biden administration is encouraging states and pharmacy partners to set up walk-in sites for doses without appointments.\par \par \uc2 This \u8220\'20\'1Cnew phase,\u8221\'20\'1D as Biden\u8217\'20\'19s team calls it, has been the subject of intense preparation since even before the president\u8217\'20\'19s inauguration. Wary of wasting a moment, Zients and other officials drafted a mountain of emails to launch the federal bureaucracy into action to be sent in the first minutes after their government email accounts were activated. Even as more Americans get vaccinated, Zients said, the White House wasn\u8217\'20\'19t letting up its urgency just yet.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will address the nation this afternoon on latest developments in the coronavirus pandemic and is expected to announce new recommendations on mask-wearing for those who\u8217\'20\'19ve been fully vaccinated in the US.\par \par \uc2 The US president sometimes runs a bit (!) behind schedule but is due to speak from the White House at 1.15pm ET /6.15pm BST (5.15pm GMT). We\u8217\'20\'19re planning to run a live stream of that speech in this blog, so do stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 We don\u8217\'20\'19t know exactly what Biden will say and he\u8217\'20\'19s going to be channeling new recommendations from his federal agency the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC).\par \par \uc2 But the main message will revolve around whether fully-vaccinated people need to wear face masks outdoors, with growing speculation that he will say they don\u8217\'20\'19t. There could be more, linked to that and other activities.\par \par \uc2 The top US infectious diseases official, \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2 , told CNN on Sunday that the government \u8220\'20\'1Cwill be coming out with updating their guidelines of what people who are vaccinated can do and even some who are not vaccinated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Where is the US up to? The coronavirus pandemic has not been under control, on a national basis, at any point since Covid-19 was unleashed here about 15 months ago. The nation is in a race between how fast variants continue to spread and how fast vaccinations can be administered.\par \par \uc2 There is scope for hope. Around 140m people in the US have had at least one shot. It\u8217\'20\'19s understood that less than 10% of overall new cases are spread outdoors, with very little spread among those fully immunized.\par \par \uc2 At this point, confirmed cases in the US exceed 32m people and more than 570,000 have died of coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to give mask update in remarks on coronavirus crisis\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics live blog readers, it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be busy in Washington today and we\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you all the developments so let\u8217\'20\'19s get going.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will deliver remarks to the public this afternoon on the latest in the coronavirus crisis. The pandemic is not yet under control in the US but there is enough progress on vaccinations and efforts to stop the spread for an announcement stemming from new CDC data that\u8217\'20\'19s expected to include guidance that some mask-wearing can be relaxed for those who\u8217\'20\'19ve been immunized.\par \par \uc2 * The US president is under pressure from many parts of the globe to do more on manufacturing and shipping vaccine to other countries where Covid-19 is raging and getting worse. Nations such as India, Mexico and Brazil are suffering. Biden said yesterday that the US will send 60 million doses of \uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2  vaccine manufactured in the US elsewhere, but that\u8217\'20\'19s just a tiny start in what\u8217\'20\'19s needed.\par \par \uc2 * The White House coronavirus response team will give a briefing late morning on the latest with the disease around the country and progress on combating it.\par \par \uc2 * Biden is also expected to announce an executive order today raising the minimum wage paid by federal contractors to $15 an hour. The current minimum, established in the Obama administration, is $10.95. Hundreds of thousands of workers are expected to benefit.\par \par \uc2 * Also, the president is expected to request $80 billion from Congress to strengthen tax law enforcement, which the administration believes will raise more than $700 billion over a decade, by tougher auditing on wealthy individuals and corporations.\par \par \uc2 * Policy executives from \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , \uc2 Twitter\uc2  and \uc2 YouTube\uc2  will testify in \uc2 US Senate\uc2  committee hearing today on how their algorithms determine what pops up on our social media feeds.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210427eh4r001s0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
