\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 The tiny American towns passing anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rules\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 1,778 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 April 2021\par 15:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In the last year, 23 Texas towns have declared themselves \u8216\'20\'18sanctuary cities for the unborn\u8217\'20\'19, making the procedure punishable, and in April, a Nebraska village became the 24th\par \par \uc2 Over the last year of the pandemic, 23 tiny towns in Texas have approved local laws declaring themselves \u8220\'20\'1Csanctuary cities for the unborn\u8221\'20\'1D, passing ordinances to make the procedure punishable by a $2,000 fine.\par \par \uc2 In April, the tiny village of Hayes Center, Nebraska, became the 24th, and the first outside Texas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWould we ever see an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Hayes Center? Maybe not,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kim Primavera, a Hayes Center trustee. Four of the village\u8217\'20\'19s five trustees are women, and most are young. They represent about 280 people here. \u8220\'20\'1CBut it\u8217\'20\'19s always better to be proactive than reactive in life in general,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hayescentertimesrepublican.com/feature-stories/hayescentersanctuaryfortheunborn?fbclid=IwAR30hSYNyXyFaRXO-w3MjA5o_v4dfXt2arctFASJd4Xr0rD7miGQ3MKdPCM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Hayes Center Times-Republican}}}\uc2 , the local newspaper which Primavera partially owns, reported that not a single person in town spoke against the measure.\par \par \uc2 The towns and their leaders differ, but there is one constant: traveling preacher Mark Lee Dickson, a director of the tiny non-profit Right to Life of East Texas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  story, I\u8217\'20\'19m a 35-year-old virgin. But I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen the impacts of suicide and the throwing away of life in general,\u8221\'20\'1D Dickson said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s why I\u8217\'20\'19m so passionate about the subject of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Dickson has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/the-traveling-salesman-bringing-abortion-bans-to-a-texas-town-near-you_n_5e4479aec5b671eafe1e3880"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crisscrossed the south}}}\uc2  over the last year of the pandemic in a 2008 Ford F-150, hoping to spread the ordinances beyond Texas. In all cases, he is invited, and only shows up when there is significant support.\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ordinances that call the healthcare procedure \u8220\'20\'1Cmurder\u8221\'20\'1D and providers \u8220\'20\'1Ccriminal organizations\u8221\'20\'1D touch on \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat the majority of people here believe\u8221\'20\'1D, Dickson said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey took seriously the statement [Joe] Biden said about how he wants \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2021/01/22/statement-from-president-biden-and-vice-president-harris-on-the-48th-anniversary-of-roe-v-wade/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 every zip code}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Dickson\u8217\'20\'19s ordinances straddle a rift in the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement, between the litigation-focused mainstream and the grassroots extremists, and comes as the American right seeks to define itself post-Trump amid a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/interactive/2021/domestic-terrorism-data/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rising tide of domestic terrorism}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 They took seriously the statement [Joe] Biden said about how he wants \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in every zip code\par \par \uc2 Mark Lee Dickson\par \par \uc2 On one side are people like Primavera, a former {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/aug/03/anti-abortion-centers-paycheck-protection-program"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crisis pregnancy center}}}\uc2  director and mother of six who argues women are victims of doctors who perform abortions. In recent years this {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/video/2020/jan/28/what-do-liberals-supposedly-get-wrong-about-abortion-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mainstream vein}}}\uc2  of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement has sought to recast itself as the true home of American {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/video/index/571906/lila-rose/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 feminism}}}\uc2  and it views women as victims of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On the other side is a growing grassroots movement dominated by men who argue \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be prosecuted under homicide statues, and both women and doctors should be charged with murder. Dickson\u8217\'20\'19s ordinances have borrowed ideas and received plaudits from these groups.\par \par \uc2 These militant \u8220\'20\'1Cabolitionists\u8221\'20\'1D have seen increasing success pushing bills to criminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and share an affinity for anti-government ideology with rightwing militias, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://politicalresearch.org/2020/11/09/no-sanctuary#_edn56"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 researchers argue}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s absolutely no daylight between the substantive priorities of these groups,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mary Ziegler, a professor at Florida State University College of Law and the recent author of \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in America: A Legal History, Roe v Wade to the Present. \u8220\'20\'1CWhere the disagreement lies is pretty much about how to get \u8230\'20\'26 the criminalization of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  the most quickly and the most effectively.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Dickson\u8217\'20\'19s ordinance was first passed in Waskom, Texas, a town of 1,600 residents, where the town attorney describes meetings as mostly \u8220\'20\'1Ca formality\u8221\'20\'1D, and where the city secretary signs all emails \u8220\'20\'1Chave a blessed day\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Waskom lies directly west of Shreveport, Louisiana, where one of only three remaining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in Louisiana is located. As Louisiana lawmakers put increasing pressure on the clinic to shut down, Dickson said he wanted to forestall any clinics from coming to Texas, even though no such proposal had been made since 1991. Nevertheless, he called the aldermen of Waskom.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I reached out to them it was all about protecting Waskom,\u8221\'20\'1D Dickson said. \u8220\'20\'1CI didn\u8217\'20\'19t have any other city in mind.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The town\u8217\'20\'19s six aldermen found the ordinance appealing, and approved a measure to punish doctors and anyone who \u8220\'20\'1Caids and abets\u8221\'20\'1D an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a $2,000 fine. Women who chose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  were exempt from punishment.\par \par \uc2 Nationally, the ordinance was met with ridicule. The picture of six gray-haired east Texas men voting to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  went viral. Dickson and Waskom were at the center of a media maelstrom, and he coached the town through the moment.\par \par \uc2 When CNN, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and the Associated Press called about the ordinance, Dickson wrote potential quotes for Mayor Jesse Moore, emailed them to the city secretary and asked if Moore found any appealing. It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear if Moore ultimately used the quotes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CInnocent human life must always be protected and preserved,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote Dickson in one email to the city secretary. \u8220\'20\'1CThis would be a great quote as well. Let me know if he [the mayor] is good with these,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 Widespread attention propelled the ordinances forward as conservative media began to cover Dickson\u8217\'20\'19s successes. It also gained him the monied backing of the religious Thomas More Society law firm.\par \par \uc2 The firm represented Waskom and six other cities when they were sued by \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  (ACLU) for libel after calling \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers \u8220\'20\'1Ccriminal organizations\u8221\'20\'1D in their ordinances. Texas\u8217\'20\'19s former solicitor general, Jonathan F Mitchell, known for his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2018/07/18/business/economy/union-fees-lawyer.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 work against unions}}}\uc2 , also offered his services to towns sued by the \uc2 ACLU\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe do have a village attorney,\u8221\'20\'1D said Primaveria, \u8220\'20\'1Cbut in this case\u8221\'20\'1D Mitchell agreed to represent the towns, she said.\par \par \uc2 But even with the clout of lawyers behind the ordinances, some towns still found the legislation too divisive. The leaders of Carthage, Texas, where a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.roadsideamerica.com/story/44637"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 14ft statue of Jesus Christ}}}\uc2  stands on eastern outskirts of town, voted the ordinance down. It was simply bad policy, leaders argued.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am not going to be having an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That is left up to the individual themselves if they want to have it,\u8221\'20\'1D Ida Beck, Carthage commissioner, said in a meeting where the ordinance was voted down, according to local newspaper the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.panolawatchman.com/news/carthage-city-commission-denies-proposed-abortion-ordinance/article_b3a7c2bc-5764-11ea-933b-c71e30dd2255.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Panola Watchman}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re the ones who have to stand before God and face that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That Dickson is still busy passing such ordinances, traveling Texas, Nebraska and Missouri, is evidence of how the Trump administration empowered grassroots and often extreme campaigners, experts said.\par \par \uc2 The division within the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement resembles another period in American history: the early 1990s, when violence against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and clinics peaked. Then as now, hopes were high that a conservative supreme court could make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegal. The \u8220\'20\'1Cabolition\u8221\'20\'1D movement also shares some of the same leaders from that period.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of optimism,\u8221\'20\'1D in the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement right now, said Ziegler. \u8220\'20\'1CIf the supreme court doesn\u8217\'20\'19t do what people want, there will absolutely be more of a threat of violence.\u8221\'20\'1D Already, the US has seen {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/interactive/2021/domestic-terrorism-data/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increasing incidences of domestic terrorism}}}\uc2 , including against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, empowerment of domestic extremists during the Trump administration, and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s statement that \u8220\'20\'1Cthere has to be some form of punishment\u8221\'20\'1D, has emboldened a male-dominated, militant wing of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremism that last peaked in the early 1990s.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://politicalresearch.org/2020/11/09/no-sanctuary#_edn56"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Abolitionists}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, who compare themselves to 19th-century anti-slavery campaigners, have urged state and local governments to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  within city limits, criminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, block reproductive rights groups from operating within certain jurisdictions, to punish women who have abortions and to designate towns \u8220\'20\'1Csanctuary cities\u8221\'20\'1D for the unborn.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s murder going on, and the other branches of government need to stand up to the plate and stop it,\u8221\'20\'1D said Matthew Trewhella to the camera in a March YouTube video. Trewhella is one of the authors of a key text of the \u8220\'20\'1Cabolition\u8221\'20\'1D movement, the Doctrine of Lesser Magistrates.\par \par \uc2 Trewhella\u8217\'20\'19s group, Defy Tyrants, proclaims on their \uc2 Facebook\uc2  page: \u8220\'20\'1CThe supreme court does not make the law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Dickson has won plaudits from Defy Tyrants, though most in the \u8220\'20\'1Cabolition\u8221\'20\'1D movement want to go farther. Such groups have had success introducing bills in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/feb/12/anti-abortion-activists-womens-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2 , Oklahoma and Texas to charge women who have abortions with murder.\par \par \uc2 Trewhella was a prominent leader of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement in the 1990s, and was among those who have argued {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://indyweek.com/news/straight-shooters/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 violence against \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  providers}}}\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.splcenter.org/fighting-hate/intelligence-report/2015/signers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 justifiable homicide}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  abolition movement also has ties to pro-gun rights movements. In one image, a group of five \u8220\'20\'1CDefy Tyrants\u8221\'20\'1D supporters pose with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AbortionFront/status/1286738476810076160/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AR-15-style rifles}}}\uc2  and a sign that says: \u8220\'20\'1CThe state is not God.\u8221\'20\'1D In another instance, a Montana Republican party official and local pastor teamed up to create the first \u8220\'20\'1Csanctuary city\u8221\'20\'1D for both the \u8220\'20\'1Cunborn\u8221\'20\'1D and gun rights.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://politicalresearch.org/2020/11/09/no-sanctuary#_edn56"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Norman, Oklahoma}}}\uc2 , just outside Oklahoma City, has become a hotbed of \u8220\'20\'1Cabolitionist\u8221\'20\'1D organizing in recent years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just been more intense in Oklahoma City,\u8221\'20\'1D said Julie Burkhart, founder and CEO of Trust Women, which operates \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics there and in Kansas. Burkhart is a former assistant of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/may/30/he-gave-so-much-the-woman-fighting-the-abortion-wars-begun-by-george-tiller"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dr George Tiller}}}\uc2 , who was assassinated in 2009.\par \par \uc2 In one instance in early 2021, an armed man who regularly went to restaurants, parks and other public places to protest against gun control showed up outside the gates of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic. He was armed with an AR-15-style rifle, a pistol and knives.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know what\u8217\'20\'19s going on in his head,\u8221\'20\'1D said Burkhart. \u8220\'20\'1CWhether he\u8217\'20\'19s going to remain there peacefully or start firing at people, it was chilling, and the staff were terrified.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Dickson, who was at the 6 January insurrection at the Capitol, said he strictly opposes violence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not telling you anything I haven\u8217\'20\'19t told the \uc2 FBI\uc2  or anything else, but I was over by the Capitol building,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dickson. \u8220\'20\'1CAll the destructive acts that happened there \u8211\'20\'13 100% in disagreement with.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However, he also does not oppose the efforts of abolitionists. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t see them as enemies, I see them as on the same side \u8230\'20\'26 However, we have differing views on how things should be implemented.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The biggest challenge for Dickson is just around the corner. The voters of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texasstandard.org/stories/lubbock-moves-ahead-with-referendum-on-sanctuary-city-for-the-unborn/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lubbock, Texas}}}\uc2 , will decide whether their town of 253,000 should be described as a \u8220\'20\'1Csanctuary city\u8221\'20\'1D for the unborn on 1 May.\par \par \uc2 The vote would not undo the right to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Lubbock. Federal law supersedes local. But a success would sow confusion, heap pressure on a Planned Parenthood clinic, and further galvanize a movement bent on delegitimizing the courts.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210427eh4r000rv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
