\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden says US has enough vaccine for \u8216\'20\'18every single, solitary American\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 live\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now) and Joan E Greve (earlier) \par \uc2 9,705 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 April 2021\par 23:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President downplays concerns over pause of J&J Covid vaccineBiden pays respects to officer killed in attack outside US CapitolJohnson & Johnson Covid vaccine to be paused in US over blood clotsSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.20am BST\par \par \uc2 Endangered US rivers at grave risk from dams, mining and global heating\par \par \uc2 Dams, mining, factory farms and global heating are among the gravest threats facing America\u8217\'20\'19s endangered rivers, according to a new report.\par \par \uc2 The Snake River in the Pacific north-west is ranked the most endangered US river of 2021, where salmon runs are on the brink of extinction because of four federal dams obstructing the free flow of water, according to \uc2 American Rivers\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 annual report.\par \par \uc2 It poses an existential threat to north-western Native American tribes who depend on the fish for food, culture and their identities, as well disrupting the entire local ecosystem, from black bears and orcas.\par \par \uc2 But, the dire situation is salvable.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn the Snake River, we have an opportunity for the greatest river restoration effort the world has ever seen \u8230\'20\'26 saving iconic salmon and orcas, bolstering clean energy and strengthening the region\u8217\'20\'19s economy,\u8221\'20\'1D said Tom Kiernan, president of \uc2 American Rivers\uc2 , an advocacy group.\par \par \uc2 Advocates are urging \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to include a $33.5bn proposal by the Idaho congressman Mike Simpson, a Republican, to remove the four dams and recover salmon in his infrastructure package.\par \par \uc2 Every year \uc2 American Rivers\uc2  ranks the country\u8217\'20\'19s 10 most endangered rivers to highlight where imminent threats to human health, safety and survival could be resolved through decisive political, business and community measures.\par \par \uc2 This year\u8217\'20\'19s list highlights the unequal impact of unchecked big business, Native American treaty violations, and inadequate regulation on the nation\u8217\'20\'19s rivers and the communities who depend on them for water, food and cultural heritage.\par \par \uc2 In second place is the Lower Missouri River, where communities in Iowa, Kansas, Missouri and Nebraska face increasing floods that threaten homes and businesses, and environmental and public health. The risks are exacerbated by authorities\u8217\'20\'19 continued reliance on an antiquated flood control system, say advocates.\par \par \uc2 The Missouri is America\u8217\'20\'19s longest river, but the once meandering, ecologically diverse 2,300-mile waterway has long been artificially contained by hundreds of miles of levees, which are being increasingly breached.\par \par \uc2 Extreme weather events linked to the climate crisis, such as droughts, hurricanes and floods are a growing threat to rivers, communities and drinking and wastewater systems.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn Missouri we have coal ash, radioactive waste, abandoned lead mines and a variety of other toxic accidents waiting to happen. When an area floods, this chemical soup becomes part of our water system, potentially impairing your drinking water or your favorite fishing stream,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rachel Bartels, the director of Missouri Confluence Waterkeeper, a conservation group.\par \par \uc2 Aerial view of the Missouri River.Photograph: Brandon Knoblauch\par \par \uc2 Nationwide\uc2 , at least {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/specials/superfund-sites-climate-change/#:~:text=Superfund%20sites%20threatened%20by%20climate,and%20could%20damage%20human%20health."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 945 toxic superfund sites are vulnerable}}}\uc2  to extreme weather such as hurricanes, floods, rising sea levels and wildfires, which are becoming more frequent and intense as the planet heats up.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/apr/13/endangered-rivers-dams-mining-global-heating-climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Endangered US rivers at grave risk from dams, mining and global heating}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , Barack and Michelle Obama will appear in a TV special alongside former \uc2 NBA\uc2  stars, musicians, actors and Covid-19 adviser \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2  to promote the coronavirus vaccinations.\par \par \uc2 The special, which will air Sunday evening on NBC, is designed to encourage Americans to sign up for the jab. The NFL quarterback Russell Wilson and musician Ciara will host the event, which will feature celebrities including Sterling K Brown, Lana Condor, Billy Crystal, Faith Hill, Jennifer Hudson, Dale Jarrett, Ken Jeong, Joe Jonas, Eva Longoria, Jennifer Lopez, Demi Lovato, Joel McHale, Lin-Manuel Miranda, Kumail Nanjiani, Ellen Pompeo, Amanda Seyfried, Jane Seymour and Wanda Sykes.\par \par \uc2 The administration says it has made it a priority to increase vaccination rates in hard-hit communities of color, especially. The federal government has allocated $10m to improving vaccine access and promotion. Following today\u8217\'20\'19s announcement on the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine pause, public health leaders are especially anxious to reassure Americans that the government thoroughly vets vaccine safety, and encourage more people to sign up.\par \par \uc2 My colleague Jessica Glenza {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/apr/13/johnson-johnson-covid-vaccine-blood-clots"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The pause in administration of the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine may cause a hit to the American immunization campaign, which was set to administer hundreds of thousands of easy-to-administer doses provided by the company. The White House denied the pause would have a significant impact, and said vaccination appointments could be rescheduled.\par \par \uc2 Despite the strides made in immunizing all adult Americans, with 74 million people and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/18/us-vaccine-distribution-tracker-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 22% of the public}}}\uc2  fully immunized, Covid-19 cases are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coronavirus.jhu.edu/data/new-cases-50-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rising in several states}}}\uc2 , such as Minnesota, and remain high in others, such as Michigan.\par \par \uc2 With a weary public and the return of warm weather in much of the country, politicians have had little appetite to renew restrictions on social life and many instead say the vaccination campaign can curb cases.\par \par \uc2 The new concerns are also likely to inflame partisan tensions and the conspiracy theorists. Republicans, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/21/republican-men-covid-coronavirus-vaccine-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 especially men}}}\uc2 , remain the most hesitant to receive a coronavirus vaccine after national politicians and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  downplayed the seriousness of the virus.\par \par \uc2 Vaccine hesitancy could play an increasingly significant role in whether the US is able to curb the pandemic, or if the viral spread is allowed to continue and circulate regionally. Although the exact level of immunity needed to squash viral spread is not known, experts believe between {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2020/12/24/health/herd-immunity-covid-coronavirus.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 70-90%}}}\uc2  of the public will need to be vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.02am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Living near a US toxic waste site could shave a year off your life, study finds\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/paola-rosa-aquino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Paola Rosa-Aquino}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Superfund sites are scattered across America: they\u8217\'20\'19re places like landfills and manufacturing plants so contaminated with hazardous waste that the federal government has designated them a national priority to clean up. And according to a new, large-scale {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-021-22249-2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study}}}\uc2 , living near one can shave months \u8211\'20\'13 and in some cases, more than a year \u8211\'20\'13 off how long you live.\par \par \uc2 After Hurricane Harvey made landfall in south-east Texas in 2017, the \uc2 University of Houston\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Hanadi Rifai began research along the 50-mile-long Houston Ship Channel, the petrochemical industry\u8217\'20\'19s main artery. Rifai and her colleagues noticed how neighborhoods adjacent to hazardous waste sites, such as where the San Jacinto River meets the channel, seemed to have a lower life expectancy. \u8220\'20\'1CThat got us interested in a more comprehensive [national] study,\u8221\'20\'1D Rifai said.\par \par \uc2 In a first-of-its-kind study out Tuesday in Nature Communications, Rifai and a team of researchers found that living in a zip code in close proximity to a Superfund site may decrease average life expectancy by 0.2 years. It could be up to a year in socioeconomically challenged communities, says Rifai, who is a professor of civil and environmental engineering and the study\u8217\'20\'19s lead author.\par \par \uc2 In places with an even higher concentration of waste sites, like Texas\u8217\'20\'19s Harris County, where Rifai lives, \u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19re not talking 0.2 [years] \u8211\'20\'13 we\u8217\'20\'19re talking a few years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The study used data available for more than 65,000 of the 72,268 census tracts \u8211\'20\'13 defined geographical areas where census data is collected \u8211\'20\'13 within the contiguous US.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/13/superfund-site-hazardous-waste-americas-dirty-divide"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Living near a US toxic waste site could shave a year off your life, study finds}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden taps Latinx statistician Robert Santos to lead Census Bureau\par \par \uc2 The White House announced today that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  would nominate Robert Santos to lead the Census Bureau.\par \par \uc2 The Trump appointee in the position, Steven Dillingham, quit in January amid whistleblower reports that he tried to rush out a report on non-citizens, including undocumented immigrants, based on incomplete data.\par \par \uc2 If approved, Santos would be the first person of color to serve as a permanent director of the agency. The historic announcement comes after a tumultuous year for the Census Bureau, which under Trump was mired in controversy and legal battles over whether undocumented immigrants could be excluded from the census. Trump wanted to exclude undocumented people, and add in a citizenship question. But the US constitution holds that the \u8220\'20\'1Cwhole number of persons in each state\u8221\'20\'1D must be counted. Amid the former administration\u8217\'20\'19s immigration crackdowns, civil rights groups and lawmakers also worried that immigrants would be less likely to respond to the census, which is used to allocate funding and determine representation in Congress.\par \par \uc2 Santos, the vice-president and chief methodologist at the Urban Institute, specializes in survey design. He is the 116th president of the American Statistical Association.\par \par \uc2 enltrThis is a big deal!\par \par \uc2 Robert Santos would be the first Latino director of the US Census Bureau. He is a leading statistician and knows how important an accurate census count is for Latino, Black, and marginalized communities. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zVDs8VXvHd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/zVDs8VXvHd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Congressman Chuy Garc\u237\'00\'EDa (@RepChuyGarcia) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepChuyGarcia/status/1382088939490705416?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Around three months after it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/05/jacob-blake-officers-not-charged-kenosha-wisconsin-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was announced}}}\uc2  that the officer who shot {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jacob-blake"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jacob Blake}}}\uc2  in the back last summer would not face criminal charges, the police in Kenosha, Wisconsin, announced that the officer is back on the job.\par \par \uc2 Without mentioning Blake\u8217\'20\'19s name or details of the shooting last year, beyond referring to a \u8220\'20\'1Cuse of force incident\u8221\'20\'1D, the Kenosha police department put out a statement via \uc2 Twitter\uc2  this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Blake said in January of this year that he feared becoming the \u8220\'20\'1Cnext \uc2 George Floyd\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D if he had allowed himself to fall down last August when he was shot multiple times in the back and side next to his car after a confrontation with police. The shooting has left him paralyzed from the waist down.\par \par \uc2 The police statement today on behalf of the chief, Daniel Miskinis, said that the incident \u8220\'20\'1Cwas investigated by an outside agency, has been reviewed by an independent expert as well a the Kenosha county district attorney.\u8221\'20\'1D Officer Rusten Sheskey returned to work with the Kenosha PD on March 31\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COfficer Sheskey was found to have been acting within policy and will not be subjected to discipline,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement said, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CAlthough this incident has been reviewed at multiple levels, I know that some will not be pleased with the outcome; however, given the facts, the only lawful and appropriate decision was made.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrMedia Release {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wdq5QaNNyk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wdq5QaNNyk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kenosha Police Dept. (@KenoshaPolice) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KenoshaPolice/status/1382066056643117057?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 After meeting with Biden and Harris, members of the \uc2 Congressional Black Caucus\uc2  spoke with members of the press.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe started out by certainly saying this has been a tough week for us,\u8221\'20\'1D said CBC chair \uc2 Joyce Beatty\uc2 , a representative of Ohio. Legislators spoke with Biden and Harris on a range of issues, from healthcare disparities to food deserts to reparations.\par \par \uc2 Beatty also said that she encouraged the president to appoint a Black woman to the supreme court if a vacancy were to arise.\par \par \uc2 enltrCBC Chair Beatty on meeting with President Biden: \u8220\'20\'1CWe started out by certainly saying this has been a tough week for us\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1mCQUrLE54"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/1mCQUrLE54}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jordan Fabian (@Jordanfabian) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Jordanfabian/status/1382070743572299777?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Maanvi Singh, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 FDA\uc2  announced a pause in administering the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  coronavirus vaccine due to six reports of blood clots, among the more than 6 million people who have received the J&J vaccine. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and senior administration officials have emphasized the US will still be able to meet its vaccination goals because of the large supply of \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and Moderna vaccines. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is enough vaccine that is basically 100% unquestionable for every single solitary American,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 * Biden will announce plans tomorrow to withdraw all US troops from Afghanistan by September 11 of this year, which will mark the 20th anniversary of the September 11 attacks. The timeline means Biden will miss the May 1 deadline established by the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 * Biden and congressional leaders attended a ceremony to honor William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans, the US Capitol Police officer who was killed in a car attack at the Capitol earlier this month. The president told Evan\u8217\'20\'19s family, \u8220\'20\'1CThis is heroism. Your son, your husband, your brother, your dad was a hero.\u8221\'20\'1D Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  also paid her respects to Evans at the Capitol moments ago.\par \par \uc2 * The police officer who fatally shot Daunte Wright on Sunday and her police chief have resigned. Brooklyn Center Chief Tim Gannon and Officer Kim Potter submitted their resignations two days after Potter shot Wright, a 20-year-old Black man, during a traffic stop.\par \par \uc2 * Derek Chauvin\u8217\'20\'19s defense team opened its case today. The former police officer\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers attempted to highlight \uc2 George Floyd\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s previous encounters with law enforcement and his drug use, even though health experts have already testified Floyd died of a low level of oxygen caused by Chauvin keeping his knee on the Black man\u8217\'20\'19s neck for more than nine minutes.\par \par \uc2 Maanvi will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  paid her respects to US Capitol Police Officer William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans in the Rotunda moments ago.\par \par \uc2 enltrVice President Harris pays respects to the late US Capitol Police Officer Billy Evans lying in honor in the Rotunda. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6oVozLd48J"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6oVozLd48J}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Craig Caplan (@CraigCaplan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CraigCaplan/status/1382070496926314500?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and congressional leaders spoke at a ceremony this morning to honor Evans, who died in the car attack at the Capitol earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 The president told Evan\u8217\'20\'19s family, \u8220\'20\'1CThis is heroism. Your son, your husband, your brother, your dad was a hero.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 The CEO of Pfizer, \uc2 Albert Bourla\uc2 , said the company will deliver 10% more coronavirus vaccine doses to the US than previously agreed.\par \par \uc2 That means \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  will deliver a total of 220 million doses by the end of May, which is enough to vaccinate 110 million people, or roughly a third of the American population.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/pfizer?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Pfizer}}}\uc2  has ramped up production of our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/COVID19?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #COVID19}}}\uc2  vaccine & can deliver 10% more doses to the US by the end of May than previously agreed (total of 220M) & supply the full 300M agreed on for the end of July two weeks early. In the fight against COVID-19, we\u8217\'20\'19re in this together.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 AlbertBourla (@AlbertBourla) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AlbertBourla/status/1382064225229619202?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Moderna has also promised to deliver 200 million doses by the end of May, meaning the country will definitely have enough shots to vaccinate about 210 million people by the end of next month.\par \par \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s announcement comes as the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  has announced a \u8220\'20\'1Cpause\u8221\'20\'1D in administration of the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine due to six reports of blood clots among the more than 6 million people who have received the company\u8217\'20\'19s vaccine.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.12pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/apr/13/johnson-johnson-covid-vaccine-blood-clots"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The call in the US for a pause}}}\uc2  in the use of the single-shot Johnson & Johnson Covid vaccine is another blow to hopes of vaccinating the whole world as fast as possible.\par \par \uc2 Health agencies recommended that US states pause use of the jab while investigations take place into six cases of women who have experienced rare blood clotting events combined with low platelets in the days following vaccination.\par \par \uc2 J&J announced it would also \u8220\'20\'1Cproactively delay the rollout of our vaccine in Europe\u8221\'20\'1D, where the \uc2 European Medicines Agency\uc2  was already reviewing the US reports.\par \par \uc2 The six cases in the US \u8211\'20\'13 from 6.8m doses of J&J vaccine administered \u8211\'20\'13 seem to be similar to those that have caused alarm across Europe, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/apr/13/astrazeneca-blood-clotting-what-is-this-rare-syndrome-and-how-is-it-caused"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 linked to the Oxford/AstraZeneca vaccine}}}\uc2 . Some countries have suspended the Oxford/\uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2  vaccine while others have imposed age limits. In France, it will not be given to anyone under 55, while in Germany it is offered to the over-60s. The UK is allowing the under-30s to choose an alternative.\par \par \uc2 Between them the \uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2  and J&J vaccines were the best chance for many developing countries. The Oxford/\uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2  vaccine is being produced at no profit and is easy to transport and store at room temperature. That was deliberate \u8211\'20\'13 the university and the company have pledged to make it highly accessible. The J&J vaccine is the other great hope, because it is given as one dose, not two, cutting the cost and making it easier for countries with shaky health systems to mass-vaccinate.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/apr/13/us-decision-to-pause-jj-jabs-is-another-blow-to-global-covid-fight"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US decision to pause J&J jabs is another blow to global Covid fight}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Some Biden administration officials are reportedly preparing for the \u8220\'20\'1Cpause\u8221\'20\'1D in administration of the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  coronavirus vaccine to last for weeks, particularly for certain age groups.\par \par \uc2 Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/04/13/j-j-vaccine-supply-disruption-481180"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Two senior administration officials told POLITICO that the Biden administration is preparing for a potentially lengthy disruption in use of the J&J vaccine, particularly for certain groups \u8212\'20\'14 such as women ages 18-48, who make up all of the known clotting cases. The CDC is waiting for its independent vaccine advisory panel to make a determination on Wednesday about whether and how to restrict eligibility for the J&J shot, said the officials, who spoke on the condition of anonymity to offer a more thorough discussion of the issue.\par \par \uc2 The administration\u8217\'20\'19s preparations for a potentially lengthy stoppage highlight the level of concern among senior government scientists \u8212\'20\'14 especially after reports of similar rare but serious reports of blood clots among recipients of \uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Covid-19 shot, which uses the same technology as the J&J vaccine. The situation also presents a major political challenge for the Biden administration as it tries to balance the best scientific advice with concerns that the pause could dent public confidence in vaccines or lead to further infections or deaths.\par \par \uc2 Asked earlier today about how long the J&J pause might last, \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2 , the president\u8217\'20\'19s chief medical adviser, said, \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s going to be more like days to weeks, rather than weeks to months.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Independent health experts have said the \u8220\'20\'1Cpause\u8221\'20\'1D in administration of the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  coronavirus vaccine shows federal monitoring systems for potential adverse side effects of the vaccine are working.\par \par \uc2 Scott Gottlieb\uc2 , a former FDA commissioner, said on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SquawkCNBC/status/1381946616773500931"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNBC\u8217\'20\'19s Squawk Box}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CFor most consumers, I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be concerned about this. Really this is an alert to doctors. That\u8217\'20\'19s how \uc2 FDA\uc2  framed it. It\u8217\'20\'19s advice to doctors to be monitoring more closely.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The pause in administration of the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine may also cause a hit to the American immunization campaign, which was set to administer hundreds of thousands of easy-to-administer doses provided by the company. The White House denied the pause would have a significant impact, and said vaccination appointments could be rescheduled.\par \par \uc2 The J&J pause comes at a perilous time in the pandemic. Despite the strides made in immunizing all adult Americans, with 74 million people and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/18/us-vaccine-distribution-tracker-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 22% of the public}}}\uc2  fully immunized, Covid-19 cases are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coronavirus.jhu.edu/data/new-cases-50-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rising in several states}}}\uc2 , such as Minnesota, and remain high in others, such as Michigan.\par \par \uc2 With a weary public and the return of warm weather in much of the country, politicians have had little appetite to renew restrictions on social life and many instead say the vaccination campaign can curb cases.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 There is enough vaccine for 'every single solitary American,' Biden says\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  downplayed concerns about the newly announced pause in administration of the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  coronavirus vaccine over concerns about six reports of blood clots among the more than 6 million people who have received the vaccine.\par \par \uc2 The president emphasized the country will still be able to meet its vaccination goals because of the large supply of \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and Moderna vaccines, which have not raised any concerns regarding side effects.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden on \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine: "There is enough vaccine that is basically 100 unquestionable for every single solitary American." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KKrNo3njTz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/KKrNo3njTz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1382046108730425349?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy message to the American people on the vaccine is, I told y\u8217\'20\'19all I made sure we have 600 million doses\u8221\'20\'1D of \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and Moderna, Biden said moments ago at the start of his meeting with \uc2 Congressional Black Caucus\uc2  members.\par \par \uc2 The president added, \u8220\'20\'1CSo, there is enough vaccine that is basically 100% unquestionable for every single solitary American.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jeff Zients, the White House pandemic response coordinator, delivered a similar message earlier today, saying the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  pause \u8220\'20\'1Cwill not have a significant impact\u8221\'20\'1D on the US vaccine distribution strategy.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/apr/13/johnson-johnson-covid-vaccine-blood-clots"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Johnson & Johnson Covid vaccine to be paused in US over blood clots}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  addressed the police killing of Daunte Wright, a 20-year-old Black man, earlier today.\par \par \uc2 enltrVP Harris speaks on killing of Daunte Wright before roundtable on Black maternal health:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBefore we get started, I do want to address the killing of Daunte Wright: He should be alive today... Law enforcement must be held to the highest standards of accountability.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/j92DZzKncz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/j92DZzKncz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NBC News (@NBCNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NBCNews/status/1382045026750988289?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Speaking before a roundtable on Black maternal health, Harris said, \u8220\'20\'1CI do want to address the killing of Daunte Wright: He should be alive today. And to his family and loved ones, you must know that the president and I grieve with you as the nation grieves his loss, and we stand with you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The vice-president emphasized that police officers \u8220\'20\'1Cmust be held to the highest standards of accountability\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Harris added, \u8220\'20\'1CAt the same time, we know that folks will keep dying if we don\u8217\'20\'19t fully address racial injustice and inequities in our country, from implicit bias to broken systems.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Brooklyn Center police officer who shot Wright, Kim Potter, and the city\u8217\'20\'19s police chief, Tim Gannon, have both resigned in the wake of the young man\u8217\'20\'19s death.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/13/daunte-wright-officer-kim-potter-police-chief-resign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Minnesota officer who killed Daunte Wright resigns along with police chief}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Chauvin trial: defence opens its case with former police officer\par \par \uc2 The defence in the Derek Chauvin murder trial {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/apr/13/derek-chauvin-trial-george-floyd-defense-live-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opened its case on Tuesday}}}\uc2  by attempting to show \uc2 George Floyd\uc2  had a history of failing to cooperate with the police while under the influence of drugs.\par \par \uc2 Scott Creighton, a former {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/minneapolis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Minneapolis}}}\uc2  police officer, testified that he stopped a vehicle in May 2019 in which Floyd was a passenger and found him incoherent and unable to obey orders.\par \par \uc2 But the picture that emerged from the testimony and body-camera video may be of limited help to the defence. Floyd comes across as frightened and not threatening, pleading with the police not to shoot him while Creighton and other officers give contradictory orders and rapidly escalate the situation.\par \par \uc2 Full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/13/derek-chauvin-trial-defence-george-floyd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Derek Chauvin trial: defence opens its case with ex-police officer}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.26pm BST\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills will be available remotely during pandemic\par \par \uc2 In a move likely to inflame conservatives and the religious right, federal officials said on Tuesday women will be able to acquire \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills without visiting a doctor\u8217\'20\'19s office or clinic during the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports:\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) announced the policy change in a letter to the \uc2 American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists (ACOG)\uc2 , one of several medical groups that has sued over a restriction put in place under the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 Dr Janet Woodcock\uc2 , acting head of the \uc2 FDA\uc2 , said studies \u8220\'20\'1Cdo not appear to show increases in serious safety concerns\u8221\'20\'1D when women take the pill without visiting a health facility and discussing potential risks including internal bleeding.\par \par \uc2 The change clears the way for women to get a prescription for the pill, mifepristone, via telemedicine and to receive it through the mail. About 40% of all abortions in the US are now done through medication rather than surgery. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents are pushing legislation in several Republican-led states that would head off easier access.\par \par \uc2 Last year, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  waived in-person requirements for virtually all medications. But the \uc2 FDA\uc2  still required patients to pick up the single tablet of mifepristone at a hospital, clinic or medical office and sign a form that includes information about potential risks.\par \par \uc2 The ACOG sued to overturn the rule, setting off a series of conflicting court decisions. In January, the supreme court sided with the Trump administration to reinstate the rule.\par \par \uc2 Several groups are pushing to make medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  permanently available via online and mail-order. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  policy will apply during the Covid-19 emergency.\par \par \uc2 In November, Kelly Blanchard, president of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ibisreproductivehealth.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ibis Reproductive Health}}}\uc2 , a non-profit research and advocacy center, told \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CYears of experience and rigorous research in the US and around the globe show mifepristone is safe and effective.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/nov/01/at-home-abortion-pills-increasingly-in-demand-amid-pandemic-under-new-threats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  some further reading, from which that quote was pulled:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/nov/01/at-home-abortion-pills-increasingly-in-demand-amid-pandemic-under-new-threats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Use of 'at-home \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills' rises amid pandemic \u8211\'20\'13 and faces new threats}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Police chief and officer resign over fatal shooting of Daunte Wright\par \par \uc2 The police chief of Brooklyn Center, Minnesota and the officer who shot dead 20-year-old Daunte Wright on Sunday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/13/daunte-wright-officer-kim-potter-police-chief-resign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have both resigned}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Wright, who was unarmed when the police stopped his car, was black. Chief Tim Gannon and officer Kim Potter are both white. Gannon said on Monday Potter shot Wright by accident, thinking she was firing her Taser stun gun.\par \par \uc2 The suburb of Minneapolis has seen two nights of protests and confrontations between police and demonstrators.\par \par \uc2 Detailed coverage is continuing on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/apr/13/derek-chauvin-trial-george-floyd-defense-live-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 our other blog of the day}}}\uc2 , which is also covering the trial of Derek Chauvin in Minneapolis for the death last year of \uc2 George Floyd\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a killing which sparked worldwide protests against police brutality and for racial injustice:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/apr/13/derek-chauvin-trial-george-floyd-defense-live-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Minnesota police shooting: chief and officer resign over death of Daunte Wright \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 The White House press briefing has now concluded. Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and congressional leaders attended a ceremony to honor William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans, the US Capitol Police officer who was killed in a car attack at the Capitol earlier this month. The president told Evan\u8217\'20\'19s family, \u8220\'20\'1CThis is heroism. Your son, your husband, your brother, your dad was a hero.\u8221\'20\'1D Evans will lie in honor in the Capitol Rotunda for the rest of the day.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 FDA\uc2  announced a pause in administering the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  coronavirus vaccine due to six reports of blood clots in vaccine recipients, out of more than 6 million vaccine shots already delivered. White House officials said the US will still be able to hit its vaccine distribution goals, despite the pause, because of the large supply of \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and Moderna vaccine doses available.\par \par \uc2 * Biden will announce tomorrow plans to withdraw all US troops from Afghanistan by September 11 of this year, which will mark the 20th anniversary of the September 11 attacks. A senior administration official confirmed the timeline to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/13/biden-withdraw-troops-afghanistan-september-11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Julian Borger}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 A senior administration official echoed comments from White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  on the US military\u8217\'20\'19s path forward in Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve long known that military force would not solve Afghanistan\u8217\'20\'19s internal political challenges, would not end Afghanistan\u8217\'20\'19s internal conflict, and so we are ending our military operations while we focus our efforts on supporting diplomatically the ongoing peace process,\u8221\'20\'1D the official said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut what we will not do is use our troops as bargaining chips in that process,\u8221\'20\'1D the official added.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is expected to announce tomorrow that he is setting a deadline of September 11 to withdraw all US troops from Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Asked about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s speech tomorrow on the path forward in Afghanistan, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  declined to provide specific details on the plan that the president will propose.\par \par \uc2 But the White House press secretary did say this: \u8220\'20\'1CThe president has been consistent in his view that there is not a military solution to Afghanistan, that we have been there for far too long.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  pause demonstrates dedication to patient safety, Zients and Fauci say\par \par \uc2 White House Covid-19 task force coordinator Jeff Zeints said a \u8220\'20\'1Cpause\u8221\'20\'1D in \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine administration would not affect national vaccine distribution, despite that some officials expected to rely on the one-shot vaccine in rural and isolated communities.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have enough to continue the current pace of about 3 million shots per day, 200 million shots by [ \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s] 100th day in office,\u8221\'20\'1D Zeints said in the White House briefing room.\par \par \uc2 He later added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have enough supply of Moderna and \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 to head toward the Fourth of July we\u8217\'20\'19ve talked about as a country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Six cases of blood clots and low platelet counts in women between 18 and 48 caused the CDC and \uc2 FDA\uc2  to recommend states pause administration of the vaccine while potential links between the vaccine and very rare syndrome are investigated. More than 6 million \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine doses have been administered in the US.\par \par \uc2 Officials have said there are similarities between the syndrome being investigated and those associated with the \uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2  vaccine in Europe and Australia. The \uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2  vaccine is not available in the US. Both vaccines from \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  and \uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2  share a vaccine technology called an \u8220\'20\'1Cviral vector\u8221\'20\'1D. If a link was established, the syndrome would still be exceedingly rare, affecting less than one in one million people vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 Health authorities said it was also important to pause the administration and announce it to the public because of the treatment needed for patients who may be suffering from such clots. Standard treatment for blood clots uses heparin, a blood thinner. In this syndrome, officials said heparin could be \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous\u8221\'20\'1D and make the syndrome worse.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen individuals, particularly younger women, come into a physician with a thrombotic phenomenon, we want to alert physicians to take a history of a recent vaccination,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2 , Biden\u8217\'20\'19s chief medical advisor. \u8220\'20\'1CThat would be important.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The White House had \u8220\'20\'1Cno involvement\u8221\'20\'1D in the announcement about a \u8220\'20\'1Cpause\u8221\'20\'1D in administration of the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine in the US. Zeints said the administration is \u8220\'20\'1Cruled by science,\u8221\'20\'1D and would wait for health officials\u8217\'20\'19 investigation.\par \par \uc2 As to whether the very rare potential side effect could increase vaccine hesitancy, particularly in rural areas where the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine was expected to be deployed, Zeints and Fauci said the pause represents how seriously the \uc2 FDA\uc2  takes patient safety.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHesitancy amongst a group of people is a challenge,\u8221\'20\'1D said Zeints. \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 FDA\uc2  acting the way they did today shows they are indeed the gold standard, and I think that should reassure the American public they are very diligent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Flu-like side effects in the days immediately following vaccine administration are common established side effects, and would typically resolve within a few days. In all six cases, the blood clotting events occurred between six and 13 days after any of the patients received a vaccine.\par \par \uc2 Symptoms of the clotting syndrome include severe headache, shortness of breath, abdominal and leg pain. People experiencing such symptoms roughly one to three weeks after receiving the vaccine should seek medical attention. People who received the vaccine more than one month ago are at \u8220\'20\'1Cvery low\u8221\'20\'1D risk for complications.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to deliver speech on Afghanistan tomorrow\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will deliver a speech tomorrow on the US military\u8217\'20\'19s strategy in Afghanistan, the White House press secretary just announced.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president will deliver remarks tomorrow at the White House on the way forward in Afghanistan,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Speaking from the White House briefing room podium, Psaki told reporters, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to be limited on what I\u8217\'20\'19m going to share from here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The announcement comes as a senior administration official has confirmed to \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Julian Borger that Biden intends to set a September 11 deadline for all US troops to be withdrawn from Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/13/biden-withdraw-troops-afghanistan-september-11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden to withdraw US troops from Afghanistan by September 11}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jeff Zients, the White House pandemic response coordinator, said his team did not know about the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  coronavirus vaccine pause until this morning, when the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  released its announcement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe didn\u8217\'20\'19t know about anything in terms of the announcement until last night, and we didn\u8217\'20\'19t even know the content of the announcement until this morning, when everyone else read it,\u8221\'20\'1D Zients said in the White House briefing room.\par \par \uc2 enltrWH COVID response coordinator Jeff Zients on FDA/CDC\u8217\'20\'19s J&J vaccine pause recommendation:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe didn\u8217\'20\'19t know about anything in terms of the announcement until last night and we didn\u8217\'20\'19t even know the content of the announcement until this morning when everyone else read it.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Nhe3Nj1Bw6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Nhe3Nj1Bw6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1382018195188514819?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 US still has 'plenty of supply' of vaccines despite \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  pause, Zients says\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , is now holding her daily briefing with reporters.\par \par \uc2 Psaki was joined by Jeff Zients, the White House pandemic response coordinator, and \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2 , the president\u8217\'20\'19s chief medical adviser, to discuss the news that the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  is calling for a pause in administration of the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  coronavirus vaccine.\par \par \uc2 The pause comes after six cases of blood clots were reported in women who received the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine, out of more than 6 million doses administered.\par \par \uc2 Zients emphasized the US still has enough vaccine doses to continue administering 3 million shots a day, even with \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  on pause, because the country has \u8220\'20\'1Cplenty of supply\u8221\'20\'1D of the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and Moderna vaccines.\par \par \uc2 State and local officials are already working to reschedule vaccination appointments, so patients who expected to get the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine can soon receive the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  or Moderna vaccine.\par \par \uc2 Fauci stressed that these side effects appear to be \u8220\'20\'1Cvery rare,\u8221\'20\'1D adding that health experts have seen \u8220\'20\'1Cno red flag signals\u8221\'20\'1D from the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and Moderna vaccines.\par \par \uc2 The infectious disease expert said the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  pause will allow the \uc2 FDA\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Cfurther investigate these cases\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are totally aware that this is a very rare event. We want to get this worked out as quickly as we can,\u8221\'20\'1D Fauci said. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think it was pulling the trigger too quickly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/apr/13/johnson-johnson-covid-vaccine-blood-clots"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Johnson & Johnson Covid vaccine to be paused in US over blood clots}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senior official confirms September 11 deadline for withdrawal of US troops from Afghanistan\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will withdraw all the remaining US troops from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/afghanistan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Afghanistan}}}\uc2  by September 11, the 20th anniversary of the al-Qaida terrorist attacks on New York and Washington, a senior administration official has confirmed.\par \par \uc2 The president is expected to make a formal announcement on Wednesday. There are currently about 2,500 US troops in the country, serving alongside 7,000 other foreign troops as part of a Nato coalition. Most, if not all, Nato allies are likely to withdraw in coordination with the US.\par \par \uc2 The drawdown of US troops will begin by 1 May, the withdrawal deadline the Trump administration agreed with the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  last year, and will be completed by the 9/11 anniversary.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe went to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/afghanistan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Afghanistan}}}\uc2  to deliver justice to those who attacked us on September 11th and to disrupt terrorists seeking to use {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/afghanistan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Afghanistan}}}\uc2  as a safe haven to attack,\u8221\'20\'1D a senior administration official said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/13/biden-withdraw-troops-afghanistan-september-11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden to withdraw US troops from Afghanistan by September 11}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden proposes potential summit meeting in call with Putin\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke to Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  today, and the US president proposed a meeting in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden reaffirmed his goal of building a stable and predictable relationship with Russia consistent with U.S. interests, and proposed a summit meeting in a third country in the coming months to discuss the full range of issues facing the United States and Russia,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House said in a readout of the call.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear whether Putin agreed to the proposal on the call, during which Biden also \u8220\'20\'1Cemphasized the United States\u8217\'20\'19 unwavering commitment to Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s sovereignty and territorial integrity,\u8221\'20\'1D according to the White House.\par \par \uc2 The phone call comes as Russia has built up its military presence in the Crimea region of Ukraine and along Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s border, which prompted a rebuke from Nato\u8217\'20\'19s secretary general earlier today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe President voiced our concerns over the sudden Russian military build-up in occupied Crimea and on Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s borders, and called on Russia to de-escalate tensions.\u8221\'20\'1D the White House said.\par \par \uc2 Biden also addressed the Kremlin\u8217\'20\'19s attempts to interfere in recent US presidential elections, pledging that America will \u8220\'20\'1Cact firmly in defense of its national interests in response to Russia\u8217\'20\'19s actions, such as cyber intrusions and election interference\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/13/ukraine-russia-joe-biden-vladimir-putin-phone-call"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden urges Russia to de-escalate Ukraine tensions in call with Putin}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 The decision to withdraw all US troops from Afghanistan represents a reversal for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who previously said he supported keeping a small American footprint in the country.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to CBS News last year, Biden said he believed the US should maintain \u8220\'20\'1Ca very small presence\u8221\'20\'1D in Afghanistan, meaning several thousand troops, to ensure Al-Qaida and the Islamic State don\u8217\'20\'19t regain a foothold there.\par \par \uc2 The president has previously emphasized that he did not support the Obama administration \u8217\'20\'19s decision to approve a US troop surge to Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: US official confirms that Biden has decided to withdraw US forces from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Afghanistan?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Afghanistan}}}\uc2  by September 11, 2021 \u8211\'20\'13 the 20th anniversary of 9/11, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSDavidMartin?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CBSDavidMartin}}}\uc2  reports.\par \par \uc2 In Feb. last year, Biden told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/margbrennan?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @margbrennan}}}\uc2  he believed there should be a "small" US footprint that remains: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7REtqrQBUZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/7REtqrQBUZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Face The Nation (@FaceTheNation) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FaceTheNation/status/1382001542467817478?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to withdraw all US troops from Afghanistan by September 11 - reports\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is reportedly expected to announce he will withdraw all US troops from Afghanistan by September 11 of this year, which will mark the 20th anniversary of the September 11 attacks.\par \par \uc2 The Washington Post {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/biden-us-troop-withdrawal-afghanistan/2021/04/13/918c3cae-9beb-11eb-8a83-3bc1fa69c2e8_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The decision, which Biden is expected to announce on Wednesday, will keep thousands of U.S. forces in the country beyond the May 1 exit deadline that the Trump administration negotiated last year with the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 , according to one person familiar with the matter, who like others spoke on condition of anonymity to describe plans that are not yet public.\par \par \uc2 While the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  has vowed to renew attacks on U.S. and \uc2 NATO\uc2  personnel if foreign troops are not out by the deadline, it is not clear if the militants will follow through with those threats given Biden\u8217\'20\'19s plan for a phased withdrawal between now and September.\par \par \uc2 Officially, there are 2,500 U.S. troops in Afghanistan, although the number fluctuates and is currently about 1,000 more than that. There are also up to an additional 7,000 foreign forces in the coalition there, the majority of them \uc2 NATO\uc2  troops.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has repeatedly dodged questions about when specifically all US troops will be withdrawn from Afghanistan, although senior officials have acknowledged they will not make the May 1 deadline.\par \par \uc2 Asked about the US troop presence in Afghanistan at his press conference last month, Biden said, \u8220\'20\'1CWe will leave. The question is when we leave.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When a reporter followed up by asking if he anticipated US troops being there next year, the president replied, \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t picture that being the case.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 US Capitol Police Officer William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans will lie in honor in the Capitol Rotunda for the rest of the day.\par \par \uc2 Members of Congress are expected to pay their respects to Evans throughout the day, and Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is also scheduled to visit the Capitol later this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more details on her visit when it happens.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Capitol was a scene of heartbreak and grief this morning, as lawmakers and police officers gathered to honor the life of US Capitol Police Officer William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans, who was killed in a car attack earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 Evan\u8217\'20\'19s 7-year-old daughter, Abigail, could be seen wiping the tears off her mother Shannon\u8217\'20\'19s face as her father was lying in honor in the Capitol Rotunda.\par \par \uc2 enltrHeartbreaking. The young daughter of slain US Capitol police officer Billy Evans, wiping the tears of her mother and widow. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/TxkTzVIRw2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/TxkTzVIRw2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyung Lah (@KyungLahCNN) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KyungLahCNN/status/1381997726615838720?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden tells Officer Evans' family: 'Your dad was a hero'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  praised Officer William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans, reflecting on the sacrifice he made by giving his life as he defended the Capitol on April 2.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is heroism. Your son, your husband, your brother, your dad was a hero,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 After concluding his remarks, Biden appeared to give Evans\u8217\'20\'19 9-year-old son, Logan, his presidential challenge coin.\par \par \uc2 enltrAfter wrapping up his remarks, President Biden appears to give Officer Evans' 9-year old son, Logan, his challenge coin: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/kyWOiRg4Xf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/kyWOiRg4Xf}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Frank Thorp V (@frankthorp) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/frankthorp/status/1381996748357447681?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  reflected on his own losses as he offered his condolences to the family of Officer William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans.\par \par \uc2 The president noted he has buried two of his own children, as well as his first wife. His son, Beau, died of brain cancer in 2015. His first wife, Neilia, and his daughter, Naomi, died in a car crash in 1972.\par \par \uc2 Biden told Evans\u8217\'20\'19 family -- his wife, Shannon, and his two children, Logan and Abigail -- that he knows the pain they are going through, and he said things will get easier, even if that seems impossible now.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI promise you it\u8217\'20\'19s going to come. It just takes a while,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 He encouraged Shannon to cherish every moment with Logan and Abigail as they mourn together.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs long as you have them, you\u8217\'20\'19ve got Billy,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s still in your heart.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Moments ago, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  picked up a Capitol model toy that was dropped by Abigail Evans, the daughter of the late Officer William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden picks up a Capitol dome toy and hands it back to Abigail, Officer Evans' daughter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/oKjyeYOijb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/oKjyeYOijb}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kathryn Watson (@kathrynw5) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kathrynw5/status/1381993383170805761?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden pays his respects to Officer Evans: 'I didn\u8217\'20\'19t know Billy, but I knew Billy'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  delivered remarks at the congressional ceremony to pay his respects to William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans, the US Capitol Police officer killed in a car attack earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 The president extended his sympathy to all of the USCP force, noting this is the second time in two months that a USCP officer has been invited to lie in honor in the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Officer Brian Sicknick, who died of his injuries from the January 6 insurrection, also received the honor in February.\par \par \uc2 Biden said the memories shared by Evans\u8217\'20\'19 loved ones made him think of some of the people he grew up with in Pennsylvania and Delaware.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI didn\u8217\'20\'19t know Billy, but I knew Billy. I grew up with Billys,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe was the one who always kept his word. If he said he\u8217\'20\'19d be there, he\u8217\'20\'19d be there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  celebrated Officer William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans as \u8220\'20\'1Ca martyr for our democracy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic speaker noted Evans, who was Catholic, was killed on Good Friday, which commemorates the crucifixion of Jesus Christ.\par \par \uc2 Quoting the Bible, Pelosi said Evans \u8220\'20\'1Claid down his life for his friends\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe represented the best of public service,\u8221\'20\'1D the speaker said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer reflected on how Officer William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans was always ready to offer a smile to visitors of the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Quoting William Shakespeare, Schumer described Evans as \u8220\'20\'1Ca fellow of infinite jest\u8221\'20\'1D who capitalized on \u8220\'20\'1Cevery opportunity for a joke\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltr"To Billy's beloved children...I want you to know that we are forever indebted to your dad. We will remember his sacrifice and your sacrifice forever," Sen. Majority Leader Schumer says, as fallen Capitol Police officer William "Billy" Evans lies in honor. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LoNB8DVJRc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/LoNB8DVJRc}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NCi4Q4Bkm2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/NCi4Q4Bkm2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News (@ABC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABC/status/1381992980697997322?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Schumer said Evans based his life on the question, \u8220\'20\'1CHow can I help?\u8221\'20\'1D That was the question that brought Evans into danger on April 2, the Senate leader said.\par \par \uc2 Schumer told Evans\u8217\'20\'19 two children, Logan and Abigail, that the Capitol is \u8220\'20\'1Cforever indebted to your dad\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will remember his sacrifice and your sacrifice forever,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Congress holds ceremony to honor killed USCP Officer William Evans\par \par \uc2 The congressional ceremony to honor William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans, the US Capitol Police officer killed in the car attack at the Capitol earlier this month, has now started.\par \par \uc2 House chaplain Margaret Grun Kibben began the ceremony in the Rotunda by offering an opening prayer.\par \par \uc2 Kibben said the Capitol is \u8220\'20\'1Cstained with our tears, its luster dulled by our grief\u8221\'20\'1D. The House chaplain said the killing of Evans had \u8220\'20\'1Cscarred our souls\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers and \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2  officers are now seated in the Rotunda, in anticipation of the ceremony to honor Officer William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans, which will begin shortly.\par \par \uc2 enltrIn the Capitol Rotunda, lawmakers ready to honor Capitol Police officer Billy Evans, who was killed at a security checkpoint on Good Friday. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DSl9K5YYXt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/DSl9K5YYXt}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jamie Dupree (@jamiedupree) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jamiedupree/status/1381986962941341702?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 The children of William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans, Logan and Abigail, are at the Capitol with their mother, Shannon, to attend the congressional ceremony being held in their father\u8217\'20\'19s honor.\par \par \uc2 As his father\u8217\'20\'19s casket was carried up the Capitol steps, Logan could be seen clutching a teddy bear.\par \par \uc2 undltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/40oYXOyvVT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/40oYXOyvVT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1381984780137463811?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and congressional leaders will attend this morning\u8217\'20\'19s ceremony to honor William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans, the USCP officer who was killed in the car attack at the Capitol earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 Later today, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will also pay her respects to Evans, who will lie in honor in the Capitol Rotunda throughout the day.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Casket of killed USCP officer arrives at the Capitol\par \par \uc2 The hearse carrying the casket of Officer William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans, who was killed in a car attack at the Capitol earlier this month, has arrived at the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 undltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MpWTIc97KS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/MpWTIc97KS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1381980314537492481?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Evans will lie in honor in the Capitol Rotunda today, and congressional leaders will hold a ceremony to mourn his death, which will be attended by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Fellow USCP officers lined up outside the Capitol to salute Evans\u8217\'20\'19 casket.\par \par \uc2 The ceremony to honor Evans will get underway soon. The blog will have updates on it, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 The senior health officials said they are not seeing similar side effects from the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  or Moderna coronavirus vaccines.\par \par \uc2 Dr Anne Schuchat\uc2 , the principal CDC director, also noted the risk of these rare side effects is \u8220\'20\'1Cvery low\u8221\'20\'1D if someone received the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine more than a month ago.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  pause to last 'a matter of days,' senior FDA official says\par \par \uc2 Dr Peter Marks, the director of the FDA Center for Biologics Evaluation and Research, noted these rare side effects seem to be arising between six and thirteen days after administration of the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine.\par \par \uc2 Asked how long the pause might last, Dr Janet Woodcook, acting FDA commissioner, said that would depend on the information that health experts gather in the coming days.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe expect it to be a matter of days for this pause,\u8221\'20\'1D Woodcook said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 FDA\uc2  and CDC officials stress \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine side effects are 'extremely rare'\par \par \uc2 Senior officials from the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  and the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  are now holding a press briefing on the latest news about the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  coronavirus vaccine.\par \par \uc2 Dr Janet Woodcook, acting FDA commissioner, pledged the agencies would \u8220\'20\'1Cwork together to fully understand\u8221\'20\'1D the six reports of blood clots in women who received the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRight now, I would like to stress these events seem to be extremely rare,\u8221\'20\'1D Woodcook said.\par \par \uc2 Of the more than 6 million \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  shots administered, only six reports of this stroke-like illness have been recorded. Of those six cases, one was fatal, and one patient is in critical condition.\par \par \uc2 Dr Peter Marks, the director of the FDA Center for Biologics Evaluation and Research, added, \u8220\'20\'1CThat said, Covid-19 vaccine safety is a top priority for federal government.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The officials emphasized this pause in vaccine administration is meant to review the data on the reports and give information to healthcare providers on how to diagnose and treat these rare cases.\par \par \uc2 Dr Anne Schuchat\uc2 , the principal CDC director, promised that health experts will be \u8220\'20\'1Cfollowing the science and ensuring transparence\u8221\'20\'1D as they investigate the reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur intention is to update you in the days ahead,\u8221\'20\'1D Schuchat said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/apr/13/johnson-johnson-covid-vaccine-blood-clots"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Johnson & Johnson Covid vaccine to be paused in US over blood clots}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  pause 'will not have a significant impact' on US vaccine plan, White House says\par \par \uc2 The pause in administration of the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  coronavirus vaccine will not significantly affect the country\u8217\'20\'19s vaccine distribution strategy, the White House said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis announcement will not have a significant impact on our vaccination plan: \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine makes up less than 5 percent of the recorded shots in arms in the United States to date,\u8221\'20\'1D Jeff Zients, the White House pandemic response coordinator, said in a new statement.\par \par \uc2 Zients added, \u8220\'20\'1CBased on actions taken by the President earlier this year, the United States has secured enough \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and Moderna doses for 300 million Americans. Over the last few weeks, we have made available more than 25 million doses of \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and Moderna each week, and in fact this week we will make available 28 million doses of these vaccines. This is more than enough supply to continue the current pace of vaccinations of 3 million shots per day, and meet the President\u8217\'20\'19s goal of 200 million shots by his 100 th day in office\u8212\'20\'14and continue on to reach every adult who wants to be vaccinated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Zients noted the Biden administration is working with state and local officials to get people quickly rescheduled to receive the Moderna or \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  vaccine if they originally planned to get the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine.\par \par \uc2 Officials from the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  and the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  will soon hold a briefing on the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  news, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Johnson & Johnson Covid vaccine to be paused in US over rare blood clots\par \par \uc2 US health agencies have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/US_FDA/status/1381925612743499778?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recommended}}}\uc2  states pause administration of the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  coronavirus vaccine, after reports of rare and severe blood clots emerged in six women. More than 6.8m doses have been administered nationally.\par \par \uc2 The concerns {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/apr/13/astrazeneca-blood-clotting-what-is-this-rare-syndrome-and-how-is-it-caused"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mirror those}}}\uc2  of drugs agencies in Europe and Australia over the \uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2  vaccine. That vaccine is not authorized in the US, and there have been no significant safety concerns raised about the two other vaccines that makeup the majority of US supply, from \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 -BioNTech and Moderna.\par \par \uc2 enltrToday FDA and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CDCgov?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CDCgov}}}\uc2  issued a statement regarding the Johnson & Johnson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/COVID19?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #COVID19}}}\uc2  vaccine. We are recommending a pause in the use of this vaccine out of an abundance of caution.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 U.S. FDA\uc2  (@US_FDA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/US_FDA/status/1381925612743499778?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople who have received the J&J vaccine who develop severe headache, abdominal pain, leg pain, or shortness of breath within three weeks after vaccination should contact their health care provider,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) and the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC) said in a joint statement.\par \par \uc2 All six women were between the ages of 18 and 48. One woman died, and a woman in Nebraska is hospitalized in critical care, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/13/us/politics/johnson-johnson-vaccine-blood-clots-fda-cdc.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s vaccine is also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fiercepharma.com/pharma/johnson-johnson-s-covid-19-vaccine-spotlight-at-ema-after-4-serious-cases-unusual-blood"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 under scrutiny}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 European Medicines Agency\uc2 , which is investigating four cases of clotting.\par \par \uc2 Because US states control their own health response, the health agencies framed their statement as a recommendation, even as federal sites will immediately pause administration of the vaccine.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/apr/13/johnson-johnson-covid-vaccine-blood-clots"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Johnson & Johnson Covid vaccine to be paused in US over blood clots}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Capitol employees are making final arrangements to prepare for today\u8217\'20\'19s ceremony to honor Officer William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans, which will be attended by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and congressional leaders.\par \par \uc2 Two seats have been reserved for Evans\u8217\'20\'19 young children, Logan and Abigail. On their seats, someone placed two models of the Capitol, per an NBC News reporter:\par \par \uc2 enltrFinal preparations are underway for Officer Billy Evans lying in Honor at the Capitol today.\par \par \uc2 The seats for Officer Evans\u8217\'20\'19 young children, who will sit in the front row, have model Capitols on them. ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DvB99bhTit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/DvB99bhTit}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Leigh Ann Caldwell (@LACaldwellDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LACaldwellDC/status/1381963262644879361?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 House minority leader Kevin McCarthy reflected on the \u8220\'20\'1Ccourage and sacrifice\u8221\'20\'1D of Officer William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans, who will lie in honor in the Capitol Rotunda today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith heavy hearts and in recognition of his courage and sacrifice, a grateful nation bids farewell to Officer Billy Evans, a true hero,\u8221\'20\'1D McCarthy said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CHis loss is enormous\u8212\'20\'14our prayers are with his two children, his families, and his colleagues in Capitol Police.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrWith heavy hearts and in recognition of his courage and sacrifice, a grateful nation bids farewell to Officer Billy Evans, a true hero. His loss is enormous\u8212\'20\'14our prayers are with his two children, his families, and his colleagues in Capitol Police.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kevin McCarthy (@GOPLeader) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GOPLeader/status/1381963102472826881?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Posters of Officer William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans have been put up around the Capitol as lawmakers prepare to honor the US Capitol Police officer, who was killed on 2 April.\par \par \uc2 From an NBC News congressional reporter:\par \par \uc2 enltrToday we remember Officer Billy Evans. RIP ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PHrEAvurD0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/PHrEAvurD0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Haley Talbot (@haleytalbotnbc) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/haleytalbotnbc/status/1381955896172027906?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer acknowledged yesterday that today will be a difficult day for everyone who works in the upper chamber, as they honor Officer William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor everyone who works in the Senate, his loss is particularly painful,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said on the Senate floor yesterday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe was a familiar face who greeted lawmakers, reporters, staffers and employees at the North entrance as we entered the Senate side of the building. Whether you knew him or not, his wide smile was often the first thing you\u8217\'20\'19d see in the morning.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Shortly after his death, Evans\u8217\'20\'19 family released a statement describing him as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe best father, son, brother, and friend anyone could ever hope for\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to pay his respects to killed USCP officer at Capitol\par \par \uc2 Greetings from Washington, live blog readers.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will visit the Capitol today to pay his respects to William \u8220\'20\'1CBilly\u8221\'20\'1D Evans, the US Capitol Police officer who was killed in a car attack earlier this month, as he lies in honor in the Rotunda.\par \par \uc2 Evans died after an attacker attempted to ram his car through a security barrier at the Capitol and then exited the vehicle wielding a knife. The attacker, identified as Noah Green, was shot and killed by another USCP officer after exiting the car.\par \par \uc2 Mourning bunting is displayed outside of US \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  headquarters on 13 April. Photograph: Stefani Reynolds/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 After the attack, House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  called Evans \u8220\'20\'1Ca martyr for our democracy\u8221\'20\'1D. Days later, she and Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer announced Evans would lie in honor in the Capitol Rotunda.\par \par \uc2 Evans is the second USCP officer to lie in honor at the Capitol this year. Officer Brian Sicknick, who died of his injuries from the January 6 insurrection, also received the honor in February.\par \par \uc2 The two events underscore what a tragic and traumatic year this has been for the USCP force, as well as everyone who works at the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210413eh4d001xp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
