\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  groups shift focus to voting restrictions\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza and Sam Levine \par \uc2 1,317 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 April 2021\par 10:45 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Increased attention on elections has come from unexpected corners offering significant grassroots power and money to efforts to make it harder to vote\par \par \uc2 In the months since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lost his re-election bid, conservative groups traditionally focused on lobbying against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and LGBTQ+ rights have moved to support new restrictions on voting, offering significant grassroots power and money to efforts to make it harder to vote.\par \par \uc2 The increased attention on elections has come from unexpected corners, such as the \uc2 Susan B Anthony\uc2  List, which traditionally has a singular focus on restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 The group announced it intends to spend millions in a joint \u8220\'20\'1Celection transparency initiative\u8221\'20\'1D with the American Principles Project, which until recently concentrated on restricting trans participation in sports. The effort aims to scupper national voting rights legislation proposed by Democrats in Washington DC and mobilize lawmakers and volunteers in states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am not ready to say that everything that President Trump threw out there after the election was accurate, but it did motivate people who frankly have been hard to motivate in years past,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ken Cuccinelli, a former top official at the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  for the Trump administration who has been tapped to lead the effort. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s my own experience, on this issue,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Members of the organization \u8220\'20\'1Cdemanded\u8221\'20\'1D it engage on election issues \u8220\'20\'1Cas a pre-condition to be able to make the pro-life case\u8221\'20\'1D of further restricting abortions rights, Cuccinelli said in an interview.\par \par \uc2 The pivot to voting rights comes after the same groups put up tens of millions of dollars to support Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 campaign, which was defined by near daily claims that there was widespread voter fraud. The \uc2 Susan B Anthony\uc2  List spent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sba-list.org/newsroom/press-releases/sba-list-details-largest-campaign-effort-in-org-history-to-re-elect-trump-pro-life-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $52m}}}\uc2  backing the former president, making it the most expensive electoral effort in the organization\u8217\'20\'19s history.\par \par \uc2 Now their full-throated support has left the groups in a bind. Some small-dollar donors, believing there was widespread fraud, are uncertain why they should donate to electoral efforts if the process is rigged.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe hear from another batch of members that say, \u8216\'20\'18I don\u8217\'20\'19t know whether I should bother with this any more. It\u8217\'20\'19s a rigged system,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D said Cuccinelli. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is their perspective, whether it\u8217\'20\'19s correct or not \u8211\'20\'13 \u8216\'20\'18If this isn\u8217\'20\'19t fixed, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know that I really want to stay engaged.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There is no evidence of fraud or other wrongdoing in the 2020 election, and courts repeatedly rejected such claims from Trump and allies. Nevertheless, experts said support for restricting voting rights and the rights of LGBTQ+ people is strongly correlated with the belief the election was fraudulent.\par \par \uc2 The big lie of a stolen election that [Trump] was pushing \u8230\'20\'26 has taken hold in religious communities\par \par \uc2 Andrew Whitehead\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe big lie of a stolen election that [Trump] was pushing, and his supporters were pushing leading to the insurrection \u8230\'20\'26 has taken hold in religious communities,\u8221\'20\'1D said Andrew Whitehead, associate professor of sociology at Indiana University, and recent author of Taking Back America for God: Christian Nationalism in the United States.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a real distrust in the election, in electoral fraud, and questioning whether Biden is a legitimate president.\u8221\'20\'1D He added: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t see how that genie gets put back in the bottle.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups are in turn beginning to see trimming the electorate as essential to achieve their goals. Marjorie Dannenfelser, president of \uc2 Susan B Anthony\uc2  List, said in a statement that the group\u8217\'20\'19s ability to elect pro-life candidates depended on a \u8220\'20\'1Ctransparent, fair elections process\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe integrity of our electoral system was severely compromised in 2020 when pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 utilizing the Covid-19 pandemic as an excuse \u8211\'20\'13 weakened state laws that ensure free and fair elections,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Conservative support for anti-voting laws comes with significant financial backing. The political arm of \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 , the influential conservative group that has long backed voting restrictions, recently announced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://heritageaction.com/press/heritage-action-launches-election-integrity-campaign-commits-over-10-million"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it would spend $10m}}}\uc2  on an effort to push voting restrictions.\par \par \uc2 FreedomWorks, the group that helped spread the Tea Party movement, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/joe-biden-donald-trump-georgia-elections-campaigns-8ea24e5b4c240aceec71fbfa703d0394"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has its own $10m initiative}}}\uc2  led by Cleta Mitchell, an attorney who was on a phone call between Trump and the Georgia secretary of state, \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , in which Trump urged Raffensperger to overturn Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s election results.\par \par \uc2 Also joining the effort is the \uc2 Family Research Council\uc2 , which championed the issue during a town hall recently, according to the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThere is action taking place to go back and correct what was uncovered in this last election,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Tony Perkins\uc2 , the group\u8217\'20\'19s leader, said. The group is designated as a hate group by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.splcenter.org/fighting-hate/extremist-files/group/family-research-council"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Southern Poverty Law Center}}}\uc2 , which describes it as specializing in \u8220\'20\'1Cdefaming LGBTQ people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 All of these groups have also set to work pressuring individual US senators seen as swing votes not to support the Democratic push for expanded voting rights. They held a rally in West Virginia targeting the centrist Democratic US senator Joe Manchin, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newyorker.com/news/news-desk/inside-the-koch-backed-effort-to-block-the-largest-election-reform-bill-in-half-a-century"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New Yorker}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Many of the most fervent backers of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans are also championing anti-voting rights legislation in places such as Arizona, Georgia and Texas \u8211\'20\'13 three states that have emerged at the front of sweeping efforts across the US to make it harder to vote.\par \par \uc2 In Arizona, the Republican legislator Walter Blackman this session introduced an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/feb/12/anti-abortion-activists-womens-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2  bill that would have charged women and doctors with first-degree murder. The crime carries the death penalty in Arizona. Blackman, who sought to overturn the results of the 2020 presidential election, has also either sponsored or co-sponsored four bills the Brennan Center for Justice says would restrict voting in Arizona. Blackman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Blackman1Walter/status/1329826225414500352"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  in November he wanted to prevent Arizona from becoming another \u8220\'20\'1Cthird-world country when it comes to elections\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In Texas in 2019, the Republican state house representative \uc2 Briscoe Cain\uc2  authored a Texas version of the so-called \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://briscoecain.com/rep-cain-files-texas-heartbeat-bill/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heartbeat bill}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, another six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Cain also authored a sweeping bill with new voting restrictions that prohibits officials from mailing absentee ballot applications to voters who qualify, and gives poll watchers more power, something that could create more opportunities for voter intimidation. \uc2 The American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  of Texas said the measure \u8220\'20\'1Cwould make voting potentially dangerous with a new series of extreme criminal penalties\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Grassroots agitators once seen as too extreme for serious consideration, but who gained traction during the Trump administration, have also hewn to peddling election conspiracy theories to justify limits on voting rights.\par \par \uc2 The Ohio-based {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/apr/25/the-anti-abortion-crusader-hopes-her-heartbeat-law-will-test-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  extremist}}}\uc2  who wrote the first six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, Janet Porter, has been pushing fraud conspiracy theories since before Trump lost his re-election bid.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are the machines that are directly connected to \uc2 George Soros\uc2 . This is a very, very big problem,\u8221\'20\'1D Porter said on an evangelical TV show in late November 2020. The show now carries a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Y3V0DzXZJ2Y"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 YouTube disclaimer}}}\uc2  about election misinformation.\par \par \uc2 Doubling down on the big lie, however, does not come without risks. Anti-voting rights legislation threatens to undo the gains Trump made with Black and Latino voters, who will be disproportionately hurt by anti-voting rights legislation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Republican party and the Christian right has invested a tremendous amount into minority recruitment,\u8221\'20\'1D said Fred Clarkson, an expert on the religious right and a researcher at Political Research Associates. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is an underappreciated part of the strategy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt seems to run counter in some respects to the voter suppression bills that would clearly disproportionately affect poorer people and people of color,\u8221\'20\'1D said Clarkson.\par \par \uc2 Whitehead, the sociologist, said he believed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s anti-voting campaign would be a defining feature of the future of lobbying on the religious right: \u8220\'20\'1CIt had a huge effect and, I think it will be an effect that continues decades from now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210409eh49001e2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
