\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US reaches 100m Covid vaccine milestone six weeks early as Fauci urges vigilance \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton (now), Lauren Gambino and Martin Belam (earlier) \par \uc2 9,056 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 March 2021\par 01:06 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Biden team says US administered 100m vaccine shots in just 58 daysFauci says US must remain on alert as Covid cases remain highBiden and Harris meet Asian American leaders in AtlantaFBI releases Capitol footage as it seeks to identify 10 suspects\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a summary of the day from Lauren Gambino and me:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are in Atlanta meeting with Asian American leaders. Follow our coverage of their meeting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/mar/19/atlanta-shootings-biden-harris-visit-asian-americans-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * \u8220\'20\'1CScience is back\u8221\'20\'1D Biden declared during a visit to the CDC in Atlanta on Friday.\par \par \uc2 * Four men linked to the far-right Proud Boys have been charged with plotting to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/09/us-capitol-insurrection-white-supremacist-terror"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attack the US Capitol}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The Republican congressman \uc2 Tom Reed\uc2  has been accused of sexual misconduct by a former lobbyist. Reed, who is considering a run for governor of New York, has denied her account.\par \par \uc2 * DHS secretary Alejandro Mayorkas is traveling Friday to El Paso, Texas, with a bipartisan group of senators amid spiraling political fallout from an increase in migrants arriving at the US-Mexico border.\par \par \uc2 * Mar-a-Lago Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Palm Beach, Florida, country club has partially closed following a Covid-19 outbreak among the staff.\par \par \uc2 * Alyssa McGrath became the first current employee to accuse New York Governor \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2  of sexual harassment.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Dick\u8217\'20\'19s Sporting Goods\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DICKS/status/1373003157467463685"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offering}}}\uc2  to outfit the \uc2 NCAA\uc2  women\u8217\'20\'19s basketball team\u8217\'20\'19s weight room with truckloads of equipment. The \uc2 NCAA\uc2  came under fire after female athletes shared photos and videos of comparing their weight room, meals, and amenities to that of male athletes who are living in the March Madness bubble.\par \par \uc2 enltrHere are the differences in amenities/provisions between the Women\u8217\'20\'19s & Men\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 NCAA\uc2  Tournament I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen so far\par \par \uc2 - Weight room/equipment\par \par \uc2 - Food\par \par \uc2 - Swag Bags\par \par \uc2 Photos from: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Cpav15?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Cpav15}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sedonaprince_?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @sedonaprince_}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/danhenry3?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @danhenry3}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/alikershner?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @alikershner}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2YfCeXaJNn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/2YfCeXaJNn}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 AJ McCord (@AJ_McCord) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AJ_McCord/status/1372759106121912320?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NCAA\uc2  admitted that they \u8220\'20\'1Cfell short\u8221\'20\'1D and dropped the ball, in a statement posted to their \uc2 Twitter\uc2  page.\par \par \uc2 enltrNCAA leaders address weight room, other amenities in San Antonio: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XJrm0njBx4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/XJrm0njBx4}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uvqcQdDALi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/uvqcQdDALi}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 NCAA\uc2  (@NCAA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NCAA/status/1373033133784846348?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The church that the man charged with killing eight people in a recent mass shooting in Georgia attended has disavowed him, the Associated Press {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/atlanta-georgia-coronavirus-pandemic-84ea109933ce05dba5c61022f9b1d41f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 . In a statement, Crabapple First Baptist Church in Milton, Georgia says that Robert Aaron Long attended the church since childhood, and his actions completely contradict the Christian values he espoused.\par \par \uc2 No blame can be placed upon the victims,\u8221\'20\'1D Crabapple First Baptist told the AP. \u8220\'20\'1CHe alone is responsible for his evil actions and desires.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  gave speeches at \uc2 Emory University\uc2  in Atlanta, following the devastating mass shooting that left eight people, including six Asian women, dead. The pair also met with several Asian leaders in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president \u8211\'20\'13 who is half-Asian \u8211\'20\'13 definitively called the series of shootings a hate crime, while the Biden avoided the phrase, citing the ongoing investigation.\par \par \uc2 enltrPres. Biden on fatal Atlanta shootings: "Whatever the motivation, we know this: Too many Asian Americans have been walking up and down the streets and worrying, waking up each morning the past year feeling their safety and the safety of their loved ones are at stake." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KISzPvhQ3j"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/KISzPvhQ3j}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 This Week (@ThisWeekABC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ThisWeekABC/status/1373032762295394306?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is doing just fine after taking three small falls while climbing up the stairs to Air Force one earlier today. Conservatives, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DonaldJTrumpJr/status/1372977391031754757?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump Jr}}}\uc2 , have seized on the video Biden\u8217\'20\'19s loss of balance and argued that Democrats should scrutinize Biden\u8217\'20\'19s wellness with the same intensity they did \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , whose mental and physical fitness was frequently questioned.\par \par \uc2 Officials insisted there was no damage done. Karine Jean-Pierre, the deputy White House press secretary, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/press-briefings/2021/03/19/press-gaggle-by-principal-deputy-press-secretary-karine-jean-pierre-aboard-air-force-one-en-route-atlanta-georgia/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told reporters on Air Force One: }}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s very windy. I almost fell coming up the steps myself. He is doing 100% fine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Mar-a-Lago, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s club and hotel, has been partially shut down following a Covid-19 outbreak, the Associated Press {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/mar-a-lago-partially-closed-covid-19-outbreak-32a7a9694c1f738eef6af6d3fc6e5aa1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 . Since he lost his bid for a second term Trump has been living at the Palm Beach, Florida, resort where he takes regular meetings with his remaining Republican allies.\par \par \uc2 Just five days ago Sarah Huckabee, former White House press secretary and current Republican candidate for Arkansas governor, had a campaign event at Mar-a-Lago. Trump made an appearance.\par \par \uc2 enltrGreat weekend on the campaign trail featuring a surprise appearance at one of my events by President Trump! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mn81i9AbsU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/mn81i9AbsU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2  (@SarahHuckabee) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SarahHuckabee/status/1371274557659746308?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 15, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Right now \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are speaking at \uc2 Emory University\uc2  on the wave of hate and violence facing Asian Americans. My colleague Adam Gabbatt is following the speech here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/mar/19/atlanta-shootings-biden-harris-visit-asian-americans-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 'Outraged' Biden urges Congress to pass hate crimes bill in wake of Atlanta attacks \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today, a staffer in \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s office became the first current employee to come forward with sexual harassment claims against the governor. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Victoria Biekiempis has an overview of the latest bombshell that was published by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/19/nyregion/alyssa-mcgrath-cuomo-harassment.html?action=click&module=Alert&pgtype=Homepage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Alyssa McGrath, 33 told the newspaper that Cuomo made suggestive statements to her and another staffer. McGrath said that this co-worker is the woman who accused Cuomo of groping.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe has a way of making you feel very comfortable around him, almost like you\u8217\'20\'19re his friend,\u8221\'20\'1D McGrath reportedly said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut then you walk away from the encounter or conversation, in your head going, \u8216\'20\'18I can\u8217\'20\'19t believe I just had that interaction with the governor of New York.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While McGrath does not work directly for Cuomo, she claimed that she and her co-worker were frequently selected from the group of executive chamber assistants to work at the governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion on weekends.\par \par \uc2 The governor has denied wrongdoing, and said that his relationships with staffers he considered to be friends might have been misinterpreted.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Alejandro Mayorkas, the secretary of homeland security, and a bipartisan cohort of Senate members just finished a trip to the El Paso border to visit facilities that have seen a surge in accompanied minors.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week Trisha Garcia {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/16/el-paso-migrant-children-shelters-capacity-biden-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  on the mad dash to make room for migrant children who are coming into the city for \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Latest data revealed that more than 4,200 unaccompanied migrant children were now in US custody, but only 500 beds were available, the Associated Press said, further {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/immigration-coronavirus-pandemic-border-patrols-texas-9b959d739d59f03dd5873927171f2e29#:~:text=HOUSTON%20(AP)%20%E2%80%94%20Hundreds%20of,oversight%20of%20immigrant%20detention%20centers."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reporting}}}\uc2  that hundreds were packed into tents, some sleeping on the floor and waiting five days for a shower.\par \par \uc2 Senator Chris Murphy of Connecticut accompanied Mayorkas and shared his reflections in a series of tweets:\par \par \uc2 enltrJust left the border processing facility. 100s of kids packed into big open rooms. In a corner, I fought back tears as a 13 yr old girl sobbbed uncontrollably explaining thru a translator how terrified she was, having been separated from her grandmother and without her parents.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chris Murphy (@ChrisMurphyCT) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChrisMurphyCT/status/1373010068375887872?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Hello, this is Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton from the west coast bureau. I\u8217\'20\'19m going to be taking over the live blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Late afternoon summary\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are in Atlanta meeting with Asian American leaders. Follow our coverage of their meeting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/mar/19/atlanta-shootings-biden-harris-visit-asian-americans-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * \u8220\'20\'1CScience is back\u8221\'20\'1D Biden declared during a visit to the CDC in Atlanta on Friday.\par \par \uc2 * Four men linked to the far right the Proud Boys have been charged with plotting to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/09/us-capitol-insurrection-white-supremacist-terror"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attack the US Capitol}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Republican congressman \uc2 Tom Reed\uc2  has been accused of sexual misconduct by a former lobbyist. Reed, who is considering a run for governor of New York, has denied her account.\par \par \uc2 * DHS secretary Alejandro Mayorkas is traveling Friday to El Paso with a bipartisan group of senators amid spiraling political fallout from a spike of migrants arriving at the US-Mexico border.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, the House overwhelmingly passed a bipartisan resolution condemning the military coup in Myanmar on 1 February and calling for the release of those detained.\par \par \uc2 But fourteen Republicans voted against the measure. The list includes several arch-conservatives who objected to the electoral certification of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s presidential victory following the insurrection at the US Capitol by supporters loyal to Trump.\par \par \uc2 enltr14 House Republicans voted against a resolution condemning the military coup in Myanmar, per {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kristin__wilson?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @kristin__wilson}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Lauren Boebert\par \par \uc2 Andy Biggs\par \par \uc2 Matt Gaetz\par \par \uc2 Tom Massie\par \par \uc2 Ken Buck\par \par \uc2 Mary Miller\par \par \uc2 Chip Roy\par \par \uc2 Jodey Hice\par \par \uc2 Alex Mooney\par \par \uc2 Scott Perry\par \par \uc2 Andy Harris\par \par \uc2 Ted Budd\par \par \uc2 Barry Moore\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1372961377304899586?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for Pennsylvania congressman Scott Perry, who voted against certifying his state\u8217\'20\'19s electors, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/sites/andrewsolender/2021/03/19/14-house-republicans-vote-against-condemning-myanmar-military-coup/?sh=5a3eab9644bc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  Forbes that the measure was an \u8220\'20\'1Covert attempt to trap Republicans into condemning the claims of evidence of election fraud in Burma\u8221\'20\'1D while \u8220\'20\'1Cperpetuating similar claims (in the Democrat\u8217\'20\'19s views) of evidence in US elections.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Arizona congressman Andy Biggs, who objected to the certification of his state\u8217\'20\'19s electoral votes, denounced the violence in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepAndyBiggsAZ/status/1372973668041637888?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video}}}\uc2  posted to \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , but said he believed that the resolution was a way for the US to \u8220\'20\'1Cput our foot in the door in Burma.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Myanmar is also known as Burma.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 We have a separate live blog following the latest developments on the spa shootings that left eight dead, including six women of Asian descent. Tune in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/mar/19/atlanta-shootings-biden-harris-visit-asian-americans-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  for our full coverage of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s visit with Asian American leaders in Atlanta.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/mar/19/atlanta-shootings-biden-harris-visit-asian-americans-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 'Outraged' Biden urges Congress to pass hate crimes bill in wake of Atlanta attacks \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Twitter\uc2  said is temporarily suspended the account of congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  in error.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C We use a combination of technology and human review to enforce the Twitter Rules across the service,\u8221\'20\'1D a spokeswoman for the social media giant said. \u8220\'20\'1CIn this case, our automated systems took enforcement action on the account referenced in error. This action has been reversed, and access to the account has been reinstated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Responding on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  after her account was restored, Greene cast doubt on the explanation and demanded the company\u8217\'20\'19s CEO, \uc2 Jack Dorsey\uc2 , disclose the name of the employee who removed her account in error.\par \par \uc2 She wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CI was just told @Twitter suspended me for 12 hrs in \u8220\'20\'1Cerror,\u8221\'20\'1D on the same day Dems introduced a resolution to expel me from Congress. What a coincidence\par \par \uc2 Twitter\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s little error wasn\u8217\'20\'19t resolved until after 12 hrs. @jack which employee made the \u8216\'20\'18error?\u8217\'20\'19 Reply to my email, Jack.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Greene, a conspiracy-peddling conservative acolyte of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , had her account locked once before in January for what \uc2 Twitter\uc2  said was \u8220\'20\'1Cmultiple violations of our civic integrity policy,\u8221\'20\'1D including false claims of voter fraud in the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Greene\u8217\'20\'19s last tweets before her account was temporarily suspended on Thursday night angrily denounced the Democratic effort to expel her from Congress.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 President Biden and Vice President Harris visit the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  in Atlanta Photograph: Carlos Barr\u237\'00\'EDa/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Biden and Harris visited the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  headquarters in Atlanta, where staff discussed their concerns about coronavirus variants as well as the challenges confronting the racial and ethnic disparities exposed by the virus during a briefing on the agency\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to combat the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CScience is back, all kidding aside, \u8221\'20\'1D Biden declared as he praised the leadership of the agency, saying the nation owed them a \u8220\'20\'1Cgigantic debt of gratitude and we will for a long, long, long time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can build all the walls we want, we can have the most powerful armies in the world, but we cannot stop, we cannot stop, these viruses, other than be aware of where they are, move quickly on them when we find them,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The visit comes as Biden surpassed his goal to administer 100m vaccines within the first 100 days of his presidency, six weeks ahead of schedule. Before departing for Atlanta, Biden suggested he may set a new goal: 200m vaccinations before the end of his first 100 days.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A former lobbyist has accused Republican congressman \uc2 Tom Reed\uc2  of sexual misconduct, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/tom-reed-lobbyist-nicolette-davis/2021/03/19/10717562-84f3-11eb-8a67-f314e5fcf88d_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a new report }}}\uc2  in the Washington Post today. Reed is considering a run against New York governor \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2 , who is facing mounting calls to resign after multiple women accused him of sexual harassment.\par \par \uc2 The Post reports:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNicolette Davis said she was 25, on her first networking trip as a junior lobbyist for an insurance company, when she felt the 45-year-old congressman\u8217\'20\'19s hand on her back. She and other lobbyists had gathered at an Irish pub in Minneapolis after a day of ice fishing, Davis told The Washington Post, and Rep. Tom Reed (R-N.Y) was seated to her left. \u8216\'20\'18A drunk congressman is rubbing my back,\u8217\'20\'19 she texted a friend and co-worker at \uc2 Aflac\uc2  that evening in 2017, adding later, \u8216\'20\'18HELP HELP.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CReed, his hand outside her blouse, briefly fumbled with her bra before unhooking it by pinching the clasp, Davis told The Post. He moved his hand to her thigh, inching upward, she said. Frozen in fear, she said, she asked the person sitting to her right for help. He obliged by pulling the congressman away from the table and out of the restaurant, Davis said. Reed declined to be interviewed for this story.\par \par \uc2 In response to a detailed list of questions, he said in a statement provided by his office: \u8216\'20\'18This account of my actions is not accurate.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Four men linked to the far right the Proud Boys have been charged with plotting to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/09/us-capitol-insurrection-white-supremacist-terror"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attack the US Capitol}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The US Capitol as seen on Monday, January 25. Photograph: Leigh Vogel/UPI/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports that:\par \par \uc2 The four men, described as leaders of the Proud Boys have been charged in the US Capitol riots, as an indictment ordered unsealed today presents fresh evidence of how federal officials believe group members planned and carried out a coordinated attack to stop Congress from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/06/congress-certify-election-biden-republicans-object"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 certifying Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s electoral victory}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 So far, at least 19 leaders, members or associates of the neo-fascist Proud Boys have been charged in federal court with offenses related to the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 The latest indictment suggests the Proud Boys deployed a much larger contingent in Washington, DC, with over 60 users \u8220\'20\'1Cparticipating in\u8221\'20\'1D an encrypted messaging channel for group members that was created a day before the riots.\par \par \uc2 The Proud Boys abandoned an earlier channel and created the new \u8220\'20\'1CBoots on the Ground\u8221\'20\'1D channel after police arrested the group\u8217\'20\'19s top leader, Enrique Tarrio, in Washington.\par \par \uc2 Ethan Nordean and Joseph Biggs, two of the four defendants charged in the latest indictment, were arrested several weeks ago on separate but related charges. The new indictment also charges Zachary Rehl and Charles Donohoe.\par \par \uc2 Members of the Proud Boys met at the Washington Monument around 10am. on January 6 and marched to the Capitol before then-president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  finished addressing thousands of supporters near the White House.\par \par \uc2 They breached barricades and entered the Capitol, as windows and doors were smashed by rioters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was not simply a march. This was an incredible attack on our institutions of government,\u8221\'20\'1D Assistant US attorney Jason McCullough said during a recent hearing for Nordean\u8217\'20\'19s case.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Afternoon summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a lively morning in US political news so far, and we\u8217\'20\'19ll have more for you in the coming hours. For details on the aftermath of the shootings in Atlanta and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s visit there, please follow our special {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/mar/19/atlanta-shootings-biden-harris-visit-asian-americans-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 live blog}}}\uc2 . And for general politics, stay tuned right here.\par \par \uc2 The main events so far today:\par \par \uc2 * The Biden administration{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/mar/19/joe-biden-kamala-harris-atlanta-spa-shootings-china-georgia-covid-coronavirus-vaccine-live-updates?page=with:block-6054d3378f0825dddef5d68e#block-6054d3378f0825dddef5d68e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gave the 100 millionth coronavirus shot}}}\uc2  to a person in the US, beating the president\u8217\'20\'19s stated goal of 100 million shots by the 100th day of his presidency by six weeks.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  on Friday relaxed physical distancing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/mar/19/joe-biden-kamala-harris-atlanta-spa-shootings-china-georgia-covid-coronavirus-vaccine-live-updates?page=with:block-6054b5ef8f0824e5cc4fa35f#block-6054b5ef8f0824e5cc4fa35f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 requirements}}}\uc2  for children in school, from 6 feet to 3 feet.The change will allow more schools to open. Masks will still be required.\par \par \uc2 * US secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/mar/19/joe-biden-kamala-harris-atlanta-spa-shootings-china-georgia-covid-coronavirus-vaccine-live-updates?page=with:block-60548f928f0824e5cc4fa03c#block-60548f928f0824e5cc4fa03c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 head to Europe}}}\uc2  next week for talks with the (post-Brexit) \uc2 European Union\uc2  bloc and the \uc2 NATO\uc2  military alliance.\par \par \uc2 * The US and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/china"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 China}}}\uc2  publicly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/mar/19/joe-biden-kamala-harris-atlanta-spa-shootings-china-georgia-covid-coronavirus-vaccine-live-updates?page=with:block-60548f928f0824e5cc4fa03c#block-60548f928f0824e5cc4fa03c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clashed}}}\uc2  during their first face-to-face high-level talks since \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took office, with one senior Chinese official urging the US to address \u8220\'20\'1Cdeep-seated\u8221\'20\'1D issues such as racism. But Biden later praised Blinken for taking a tough stance with China.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden "100% fine" after stumbling while boarding Air Force One\par \par \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre, the White House deputy press secretary, told reporters aboard Air Force One, that the president plans to \u8220\'20\'1C offer his support for Asian Americans and Pacific Islanders in Georgia and across the country and talk about his fierce commitment to combating xenophobia, intolerance and hate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During his visit in Atlanta, Biden will meet with Asian American leaders \u8220\'20\'1Cto hear about the impact on their community of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s heartbreaking senseless acts of violence as well as their perspectives on increased anti-Asian incidents.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden will also make a stop at the CDC \u8220\'20\'1Cwhere they will receive an update from health and medical experts who are helping lead the fight against the pandemic,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. He will joined in the state by Senators \uc2 Rev Raphael Warnock\uc2  and \uc2 John Ossoff\uc2 , Atlanta mayor \uc2 Keisha Lance Bottoms\uc2  and \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Biden\u8217\'20\'19s tumble up the stairs of Air Force One, Jean-Pierre blamed the wind.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was very windy \u8211\'20\'13 I almost fell coming up the steps myself. He is doing 100%,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s doing fine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2  warned that the US must stay vigilant because the rate of infections \u8211\'20\'13 though it\u8217\'20\'19s plateaued \u8211\'20\'13 remains too high to relax public health guidelines.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s really quite risky to declare victory before you have the level of infection in the community to a much much lower level than 53,000 cases per day,\u8221\'20\'1D Fauci said. \u8220\'20\'1C So it is unfortunate but not surprising to me that you are seeing increases in number of cases per day in areas \u8211\'20\'13 cities states or regions \u8211\'20\'13 even though vaccines are being distributed at a pretty good clip.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a time for optimism, but it is not a time for relaxation,\u8221\'20\'1D Zients added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 During the coronavirus briefing, \uc2 Dr Rochelle Walensky\uc2  outlined new CDC guidelines changing the physical distancing guidelines for children in schools from 6ft to 3ft, as long as universal mask-wearing is in effect.\par \par \uc2 The agency said middle school and high school students should remain 6ft apart in communities where positivity rates are above 10% or in settings where co-horting \u8211\'20\'13 when groups of students are kept together with the same staff throughout the day \u8211\'20\'13 is unavailable.\par \par \uc2 She cited three new studies from the agency\u8217\'20\'19s Morbidity and Mortality Weekly Report, which found that children in kindergarten through grade 12 could safely reopen with proper mitigation strategies.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden administration reaches 100 millionth coronavirus vaccinations goal six weeks early\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration announced that it reached its goal of administering 100 million vaccines in the first 100 days of his presidency, six weeks ahead of schedule.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe reached our 100 million shots goal in just 58 days, weeks ahead of schedule,\u8221\'20\'1D White House Covid-19 response coordinator Jeff Zients said during a coronavirus briefing on Friday. He reiterated Biden\u8217\'20\'19s pledge to make enough vaccines available for every adult in America by the end of May.\par \par \uc2 The current seven-day average in the US is 2.5 million Covid-19 shots per day, Zients said.\par \par \uc2 He also touted the White House decision to \u8220\'20\'1Cloan\u8221\'20\'1D a combined 4 million doses of the AstraZeneca COVID-19 vaccine to Mexico and Canada. The vaccine has not yet been approved for use in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis loan will not reduce the available supply of vaccines,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CNo American will be without a vaccine because of this action.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In a statement released before he departed for Georgia, the president called on Congress to \u8220\'20\'1Cswiftly pass\u8221\'20\'1D legislation that would speed up law enforcement\u8217\'20\'19s response to hate crimes amid a rise in violence and abuse against Asian Americans since the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s visit to Georgia will be covered by our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/mar/19/atlanta-shootings-biden-harris-visit-asian-americans-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sister blog}}}\uc2 , which is following the latest on the spa shootings that left eight people dead, including six women of Asian descent.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said \u8220\'20\'1Conly five\u8221\'20\'1D employees lost their jobs as a result of a policy regarding past marijuana use, following a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/biden-white-house-sandbags-staffers-sidelines-dozens-for-pot-use"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Daily Beast report }}}\uc2  that young staffers were pushed to resign or reassigned to remote work after disclosing their past use of the drug.\par \par \uc2 The outlet reported on Thursday that the employment status of several White House staffers were affected, including some who were asked to resign, after voluntarily disclosing their past use of marijuana. The policy even affected staffers whose cannabis use was in one of the 14 states \u8211\'20\'13 or Washington DC \u8211\'20\'13 where the drug is legal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe announced a few weeks ago that the White House had worked with the security service to update the policies to ensure that past marijuana use wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t automatically disqualify staff from serving in the White House,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said in a statement posted on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CAs a result, more people will serve who would not have in the past with the same level of recent drug use.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrAs a result, more people will serve who would not have in the past with the same level of recent drug use. The bottom line is this: of the hundreds of people hired, only five people who had started working at the White House are no longer employed as a result of this policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  (@PressSec) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec/status/1372921409509462018?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Citing three anonymous sources, the Beast said the affected staffers were taken aback because the White House had previously indicated that recreational use of cannabis would not be immediately disqualify them from personnel jobs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s exclusively targeting younger staff and staff who came from states where it was legal,\u8221\'20\'1D one person said.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/biden-white-house-sandbags-staffers-sidelines-dozens-for-pot-use"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cproud\u8221\'20\'1D of his secretary of state, \uc2 Anthony Blinken\uc2 , after the first high level talks between the Biden administration and Chinese officials got off to a fiery start.\par \par \uc2 What was supposed to be a short photo opp with senior Chinese officials turned into a lengthy sparring match, with both sides leveling attacks at one another in a rare public display of the tensions between the two world superpowers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m very proud of the Secretary of State,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden told reporters before departing for Georgia. During the campaign, Trump repeatedly attacked Biden for being \u8220\'20\'1Csoft\u8221\'20\'1D on China.\par \par \uc2 In response to Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 s challenge that the leaders hold a live-streamed conversation, Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m sure we\u8217\'20\'19ll talk at some point\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Would there be any new sanctions on Russia? \u8220\'20\'1CThat will come in time\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On his goal to ramp up the pace of vaccinations, Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CHopefully we\u8217\'20\'19ll keep the pace of about 2.5 million a day, which we may be able to get to \u8212\'20\'14 we may be able to double.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Reporters observed Biden stumble and fall as he walked up the steps of Air Force One as he boarded. He quickly regained his footing and walked onto the plane.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Speaking during her weekly press briefing, House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  said Gomez\u8217\'20\'19s resolution to expel congresswoman Greene from Congress is his own endeavor and does not reflect the position of leadership.\par \par \uc2 She added that members are \u8220\'20\'1Cvery unhappy\u8221\'20\'1D about Greene\u8217\'20\'19s behavior.\par \par \uc2 Asked about the sharp rise of unaccompanied minors at the US-Mexico border, Pelosi said: \u8220\'20\'1CI think the administration is pulling this thing under control.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She said Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 focus on the border was a \u8220\'20\'1Cdiversionary tactic\u8221\'20\'1D that showed the party was \u8220\'20\'1Cbankrupt of ideas\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Pressed about when the Capitol would begin to return to normal, easing some of the public health restrictions which result in lengthy votes, Pelosi said that depended on members being vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe more people who get vaccinated, the shorter the time we have to be separated on the floor,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. But asked about Republican members who have refused to be vaccinated, Pelosi said there was little she could do.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou cant tell anyone to do anything,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CLeast of all around here\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 CDC relaxes physical distancing requirements in schools from 6ft to 3ft\par \par \uc2 The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  on Friday relaxed physical distancing requirements for children in school, from 6 feet to 3 feet.\par \par \uc2 The change will allow more students to be inside classrooms. Masks will still be required.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will officially nominate \uc2 Bill Nelson\uc2 , the former Florida senator, to serve as NASA administrator.\par \par \uc2 enltrJoe Biden will nominate \uc2 Bill Nelson\uc2  to serve as NASA administrator, the White House confirms.\par \par \uc2 The former Florida senator very narrowly lost his reelection race to \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  in 2018. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/n5nZEnGiUO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/n5nZEnGiUO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joan Greve (@joanegreve) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joanegreve/status/1372911258832400389?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Nelson, a longtime friend of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s who lost his re-election race in 2018, has been a staunch advocate for the space agency. As a congressman, he flew on a space shuttle mission in 1986.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 On Friday, Democratic Congressman Jimmy Gomez formally introduced a resolution to expel Republican congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , citing her \u8220\'20\'1Crepeated endorsements of sedition, domestic terrorism, and political violence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrI believe some of my {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HouseGOP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @HouseGOP}}}\uc2  colleagues \u8212\'20\'14 and one in particular \u8212\'20\'14 wish harm upon this legislative body.\par \par \uc2 I won\u8217\'20\'19t watch {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMTG?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepMTG}}}\uc2  threaten our democracy and do nothing.\par \par \uc2 Today, I formally introduced a resolution to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/ExpelGreene?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #ExpelGreene}}}\uc2  ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FBrFJtAbvU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/FBrFJtAbvU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. Jimmy Gomez (@RepJimmyGomez) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepJimmyGomez/status/1372906840841916430?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The resolution has no backing from Republicans and is falls well short of the two-thirds support it would need to remove her from Congress.\par \par \uc2 enltr"I take no joy in introducing this resolution, but any member who cites political violence and threatens our lives must be expelled,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rep Jimmy Gomez in introducing resolution to expel \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , per {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AnnieGrayerCNN?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @AnnieGrayerCNN}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI'm not saying this for shock value."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1372915990657384453?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The move comes after Greene said she had been temporarily suspended from \uc2 Twitter\uc2  for violating the platform\u8217\'20\'19s rules. \uc2 Twitter\uc2  has not confirmed the action.\par \par \uc2 enltrOn Telegram \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  says she has been temporarily stopped from tweeting by \uc2 Twitter\uc2  for violating the platform's rules. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wdrqPMHIeP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wdrqPMHIeP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Donie O'Sullivan (@donie) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/donie/status/1372906684591583238?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Twitter\uc2  previously locked out Greene, a staunch ally of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , from the platform in January after she repeated false claims about election fraud.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, House Democrats stripped Greene of two of her committee assignments over her long record of expressing bigoted and anti-Semitic sentiments online, as well as her belief in the conspiracy theory QAnon. Moments before the vote on her Congressional exile, she denounced QAnon and apologized for some of her offensive remarks, which included endorsing a call to execute Democrats and accosting a student survivor of the Stoneman Douglas High School shooting.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden said the US is on track to reach his goal of administering 100 million coronavirus vaccinations on Friday, weeks ahead of his initial target date.\par \par \uc2 This comes as \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2 , the nation\u8217\'20\'19s top infectious disease expert, told a Senate panel on Thursday that he was concerned about a possible fourth surge in cases as infections rise in some states and Europe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m concerned that if we pull back in our enthusiasm for the fact that vaccines are rolling out, and things look good, if we pull back prematurely, we may trigger another surge. And that would really set us back in all the things that we\u8217\'20\'19re trying to do,\u8221\'20\'1D he told lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats on Thursday passed two major immigration bills that would create a path to citizenship for Dreamers \u8211\'20\'13 immigrants brought to the US as children \u8211\'20\'13 and undocumented farmworkers.\par \par \uc2 Both bills received Republican support. Nine House Republicans voted for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://email.punchbowl.news/t/t-l-mtydjdd-gdudikhdi-u/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dream Act}}}\uc2  and 30 Republicans voted for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://email.punchbowl.news/t/t-l-mtydjdd-gdudikhdi-k/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Farm Workforce Modernization Act}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Despite broad public support, particularly for Dreamers, the legislation is unlikely to win 60 votes in the Senate. Recently, senator Dick Durbin, the No 2 Democrat in the caucus and a veteran of the institution, said Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 decades-long obstruction of the Dream Act prompted him to come out in favor of filibuster reform.\par \par \uc2 The prospects seem even unlikelier for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ambitious immigration overhaul, which he proposed earlier this year. The legislation would create a pathway to citizenship for 11 million undocumented immigrants, ease visa restrictions and deliver billions of dollars in aid to Central American countries in an attempt to alleviate the poverty and violence driving migration.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/18/us-house-immigration-bill-dreamers-citizenship"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US House passes bill that would give Dreamers a path to citizenship}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton reports for us this morning as part of our Rights and freedom series that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2021/mar/19/defund-the-police-gun-violence-surge-oakland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a surge in gun violence is a stress test for Oakland\u8217\'20\'19s defund the police campaign}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 While some crime survivors {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jun/23/defund-police-violence-survivors-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 support}}}\uc2  shifting resources from police and into prevention and healing services, others who have lost loved ones to shootings and live in high-crime areas worry that depleting police budgets without proven alternatives to fill any gaps will make Black and brown communities less safe.\par \par \uc2 And the further localities dive into the logistics of transforming public safety and lessening reliance on police, the more questions abound. Who are people to call after a shooting? How do we get the most-affected communities to trust new alternatives? How can we go beyond typical {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jun/16/its-not-about-bad-apples-how-us-police-reforms-have-failed-to-stop-brutality-and-violence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reforms}}}\uc2  into real, radical transformation?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a scary moment. The anxiety is in not knowing what the outcome of all of this is gonna be,\u8221\'20\'1D said Keisha Henderson, a resident of East Oakland, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Henderson, 28, said she has had to deal with bullets flying past her windows and the frustration of slow and sometimes nonexistent police responses to gunfire and other problems. Oakland is experiencing a 314% {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cityofoakland2.app.box.com/s/xqloqg6rpaljxz6h0cajle6skmoea5ct/file/787366323230"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increase}}}\uc2  in homicides compared with the same time last year, and a 113% increase in firearms assaults.\par \par \uc2 Henderson protested alongside thousands of others last summer [about police violence] but said she didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to see total abolition of police \u8211\'20\'13 at least until there are \u8220\'20\'1Cstress-tested\u8221\'20\'1D alternatives in place. She is one of 17 members on Oakland\u8217\'20\'19s Reimagining Public Safety Taskforce, an official board established last year which is currently parsing through dozens of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1LNzjfiWXYYVRZJs1vvoswztGCm6YvvmnE8c0R-crP0A/edit#gid=1625795919"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recommendations}}}\uc2  to decide which ones they will present to the city council for adoption in the upcoming budget. Oakland\u8217\'20\'19s goal is to cut police spending by 50%, or $150m a year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can do all these pilot programs but there has to be a balance between holding police accountable to Black residents, while also making sure we are protected some way,\u8221\'20\'1D Henderson said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to reallocate and rebuild our communities but we do not need to completely abolish the police so that everything goes haywire.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more of Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton\u8217\'20\'19s report here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2021/mar/19/defund-the-police-gun-violence-surge-oakland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Surge in gun violence is stress test for Oakland\u8217\'20\'19s defund the police campaign}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2021/mar/19/defund-the-police-gun-violence-surge-oakland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Surge in gun violence is stress test for Oakland's defund the police campaign}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Andrea Salcedo reports for the Washington Post this morning that a study has found that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2021/03/19/trump-tweets-chinese-virus-racist/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 racist anti-Asian hashtags spiked after Trump first tweeted \u8220\'20\'1CChinese virus\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 On March 16, 2020, Trump first tweeted the phrase \u8220\'20\'1CChinese virus.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That single tweet, researchers later found, fueled exactly the kind of backlash the \uc2 World Health Organisation\uc2  had feared: It was followed by an avalanche of tweets using the hashtag #chinesevirus, among other anti-Asian phrases.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe week before Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tweet the dominant term [on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 ] was #covid-19,\u8221\'20\'1D Yulin Hswen, an epidemiology professor at the University of California San Francisco and a co-author of the study told the Washington Post. \u8220\'20\'1CThe week after his tweet, it was #chinesevirus.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Hswen is among a group of researchers who analyzed hundreds of thousands of #covid-19 and #chinesevirus hashtags drafted the week before and after Trump first referred to the coronavirus as the \u8220\'20\'1CChinese virus\u8221\'20\'1D on the social media platform.\par \par \uc2 Not only did more people use the #chinesevirus hashtag days after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tweet, but those who did were more likely to include other anti-Asian hashtags in their tweets, according to the peer-reviewed study published by the American Journal of Public Health.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2021/03/19/trump-tweets-chinese-virus-racist/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wasington Post \u8211\'20\'13 Racist anti-Asian hashtags spiked after Trump first tweeted \u8216\'20\'18Chinese virus,\u8217\'20\'19 study finds}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Asian American lawmaker Grace Meng called out the violence and discrimination against her community at a hearing on Capitol Hill on Thursday. \u8220\'20\'1COur community is bleeding. We are in pain. And for the last year, we\u8217\'20\'19ve been screaming out for help,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. She told a panel the rising tide of anti-Asian bigotry was fuelled in part by rhetoric from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies, who have referred to Covid-19 as the \u8220\'20\'1CChina virus\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ckung flu\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Just two more jurors were needed for the trial of a former Minneapolis police officer charged in George Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s death, as the judge prepared to rule today on two major motions including whether to allow evidence from Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s earlier 2019 arrest.\par \par \uc2 The 12 jurors seated through Thursday are evenly split by race, with six white jurors, four Black and two multiracial, according to the court. The last two jurors chosen will be alternates.\par \par \uc2 Steve Karnowski and Amy Forliti report for the Associated Press that opening statements will be 29 March if the jury is complete. That process was on track to finish nearly a week early.\par \par \uc2 Hennepin County Judge Peter Cahill was to rule Friday on Chauvin attorney Eric Nelson\u8217\'20\'19s motion to halt or move the trial due to concerns that a settlement reached by the city with Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s family had tainted the jury pool.\par \par \uc2 But Cahill denied similar motions last year, and though some potential jurors were dismissed because they said news of the settlement would influence them, others were seated after saying either they hadn\u8217\'20\'19t heard of it or could set it aside.\par \par \uc2 A likely bigger issue was Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s 2019 arrest, just a year before his fatal encounter with Chauvin. Cahill also previously denied the defense\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to allow the year-old arrest at trial. But he heard fresh arguments this week.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutor Matthew Frank said the defense was simply looking for a backdoor way to portray Floyd as a bad person, and the only relevant issue in Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s death is how he was treated by police.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Representative \uc2 Pramila Jayapal\uc2  has posted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepJayapal/status/1372881690423611393"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a thread}}}\uc2  about her response to the Atlanta shootings this morning, and part of her focus is the law enforcement response. The chair of the Congressional Progressive Caucus says:\par \par \uc2 Police spokesperson was pictured promoting an anti-Asian t-shirt. He also sympathetically said shooter was \u8220\'20\'1Chaving a bad day.\u8221\'20\'1D He was removed as spokesperson, but what does this say about law enforcement environment? Police also said shootings appeared to be a matter of \u8220\'20\'1Csex addiction\u8221\'20\'1D not racially motivated \u8211\'20\'13 as if the two can\u8217\'20\'19t exist in tandem. That is absurd & belies the intersection between race, class & gender. It also ignores the fetishization of Asian women. Discrimination against Asian Americans [is] constantly minimized, even as it is deeply rooted in US immigration laws. The constant exclusion of Asian Americans \u8211\'20\'13 from polling data to representation to disaggregated data on health, income, etc. \u8211\'20\'13 is a form of invisibility that is deeply painful to all of us.\par \par \uc2 You can read it here:\par \par \uc2 enltrThread on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Georgia?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Georgia}}}\uc2  shootings:\par \par \uc2 1. Police spokesperson was pictured promoting an anti-Asian t-shirt. He also sympathetically said shooter was "having a bad day." He was removed as spokesperson, but what does this say about law enforcement environment? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/F7XbnyuSNW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/F7XbnyuSNW}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Rep. Pramila Jayapal\uc2  (@RepJayapal) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepJayapal/status/1372881690423611393?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Blinken to visit Europe next week for talks with Nato and the \uc2 EU\par \par \uc2 A quick one from Reuters here, that fresh from his talks with top officials from China \u8211\'20\'13 there\u8217\'20\'19s a further meeting in Anchorage, Alaska today \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  will be headed to Europe on his next diplomatic mission.\par \par \uc2 He will visit Brussels next week to meet with Nato foreign ministers and \uc2 European Union\uc2  officials, the \uc2 US Department of State\uc2  said, as the Biden administration seeks to repair transatlantic ties.\par \par \uc2 At the Nato meeting, Blinken will join other foreign ministers to discuss proposed changes to the transatlantic organization as well as concerns over China and Russia, climate change, cyber and energy security and other issues, the department said.\par \par \uc2 Blinken will also meet with European Commission President \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2  to discuss the Covid-19 pandemic and economic recovery, and efforts to strengthen democracy, it said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe meetings in Brussels reaffirm the United States\u8221\'20\'1D commitment to our Allies and European partners on our shared agenda,\u8221\'20\'1D the department said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The trip follows four years of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s harsh rhetoric toward the military alliance. Trump repeatedly accused the European members of Nato of not spending enough on their own defense.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 Joan Biskupic, CNN\u8217\'20\'19s legal analyst has an interesting piece this morning arguing that the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s conservatives want to topple \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights \u8211\'20\'13 but can\u8217\'20\'19t seem to agree on how. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://us.cnn.com/2021/03/19/politics/abortion-supreme-court-conservatives-thomas-roberts/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 She writes}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The aims of individual justices, based on their recent writings, range from reversing Roe v. Wade to forbidding clinics from challenging restrictions on behalf of women to relaxing the standard that states must meet to limit women\u8217\'20\'19s access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 New internal tensions in the age-old controversy have emerged, as the six Republican-appointed justices on the right wing diverge on curtailing precedent and more sharply clash with the court\u8217\'20\'19s three remaining Democratic-appointed liberals. The justices could move a step closer to their next chapter as they meet privately on Friday to consider whether to take up Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s ban on abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Then again, the newly reconfigured court may want to wait to take any dramatic action on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Multiple related laws are headed its way as states continue to adopt new prohibitions, including the near-total Arkansas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban passed earlier this month with no exceptions for cases of rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 While the number of abortions nationwide has declined over the decades, culturally and religiously fraught state restrictions, and subsequent litigation, have not diminished. If the justices were to take up a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and consider reversing decades-old precedent, it would intensify national divisions. Even if the justices ultimately deny the Mississippi petition, the case could give individual justices a chance to issue statements relative to the denial, laying out their arguments for future rollbacks of reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://us.cnn.com/2021/03/19/politics/abortion-supreme-court-conservatives-thomas-roberts/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN \u8211\'20\'13 Supreme Court conservatives want to topple \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights, but can\u8217\'20\'19t seem to agree on how}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 Nina Lakhani reports for us today from Texas, asking {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/18/us-mexico-immigration-border-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is there a crisis at the border?}}}\par \par \uc2 After four years of racist, chaotic, anti-immigration policies by the Trump administration \u8211\'20\'13 as well as growing desperation fuelled by the pandemic and extreme climate events \u8211\'20\'13 the number of people seeking to enter the US is rising.\par \par \uc2 But advocates in the Rio Grande Valley, where undocumented migrants have long been relied upon for cheap farm labour, reject incendiary claims that the numbers are overwhelming.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMigration goes up and down, that\u8217\'20\'19s the reality of the border. Biden has different values and has given people hope, but there\u8217\'20\'19s no border crisis, to say so is political manipulation,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ramona Casas, director of the migrant advocacy group Arise. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to address the root causes and transform the broken immigration system, not more militarization.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The current uptick started before Biden\u8217\'20\'19s election, according to Customs and Border Protection (CBP) figures.\par \par \uc2 Jenn Budd, a former senior border patrol agent turned whistleblower, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe only crisis at the border is the children, which the administration is trying to deal with, anything else is simply not true and an attempt to play politics, make Biden look bad and ensure the money keeps flowing to the border security industry.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In 2000, a total of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbp.gov/sites/default/files/assets/documents/2020-Jan/U.S.%20Border%20Patrol%20Fiscal%20Year%20Staffing%20Statistics%20%28FY%201992%20-%20FY%202019%29_0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  9,212 border patrol agents}}}\uc2  detained an average of almost {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbp.gov/sites/default/files/assets/documents/2020-Jan/U.S.%20Border%20Patrol%20Monthly%20Apprehensions%20%28FY%202000%20-%20FY%202019%29_1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 137,000 undocumented migrants}}}\uc2  per month on the southern border. In the 2021 fiscal year until February, the average was just over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbp.gov/newsroom/stats/cbp-enforcement-statistics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 76,000 per month,}}}\uc2  but the number of agents is more than double compared to 2000.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the Texas governor Greg Abbott deployed state troopers and the national guard to the border after claiming, without evidence, that illegal immigrants were spreading the coronavirus. Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s unsubstantiated Covid claims came shortly after he announced plans to end the state mask mandate and ordered businesses to reopen at 100% capacity.\par \par \uc2 But illegal or undocumented migrants are not being released into the US. The two groups being allowed in are some existing asylum seekers, thanks to the repeal of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Remain in Mexico policy, and some new arrivals presenting at legal ports of entry, including unaccompanied children and young families, who have been permitted to remain in the country pending asylum court hearings. In Texas, everyone else continues to be turned back, say advocates.\par \par \uc2 Read more of Nina Lakhani\u8217\'20\'19s report here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/18/us-mexico-immigration-border-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Is there a crisis at the border?: a look at both sides of the immigration argument}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/18/us-mexico-immigration-border-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Is there a crisis at the border?: a look at both sides of the immigration argument}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Atlanta shootings, where a white gunman killed eight people, most of them Asian American women, has thrown a national spotlight onto the community, and the way it is treated by the political establishment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re becoming increasingly more visible and active in the political ecosystem,\u8221\'20\'1D said Georgia state Sen. Michelle Au, a Democrat who represents part of the growing, diversifying suburbs north of the city. Yet, Au said, \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I\u8217\'20\'19ve heard personally, and what I have felt, is that people sometimes don\u8217\'20\'19t tend to listen to us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Au said today\u8217\'20\'19s White House visit, especially amid tragedy, is welcomed by a community whose influence and struggles are often overshadowed in national conversations about diversity. She notes President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and other Republicans merely brushed off charges of racism when they dubbed coronavirus the \u8220\'20\'1CChina virus\u8221\'20\'1D because of its origins.\par \par \uc2 Activists say they saw a rise of racist attacks. Nearly 3,800 incidents have been reported to Stop AAPI Hate, a California-based reporting center for Asian Americans and Pacific Islanders, and its partner advocacy groups, since March 2020.\par \par \uc2 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the first person of South Asian descent to hold national office, will be part of the visit to Atlanta today.\par \par \uc2 Associated Press report that the presidential trip was planned before the shooting, as part of a victory lap aimed at selling the benefits of pandemic relief legislation. But Biden and Harris will instead spend their visit consoling a community whose growing voting power helped secure their victory in Georgia and beyond.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 Incidentally there\u8217\'20\'19s been a slight hint of a row-back from the confrontational meeting on the Chinese side this morning. Reuters have a quick snap that at \uc2 China\u8217\'20\'19s foreign ministry\uc2  spokesman \uc2 Zhao Lijian\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s regular press briefing this morning, he said there was a lot of confrontation at the Sino-US talks in Alaska, and that was not what Beijing was aspiring to.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.56am GMT\par \par \uc2 US and China publicly rebuke each other in first major talks of Biden era\par \par \uc2 The big overnight development has been the open public rebukes between the US and China at a high level meeting in Anchorage, Alaska. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/mar/19/us-china-talks-alaska-biden-blinken-sullivan-wang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justin McCurry reports for us}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The United States and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/china"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 China}}}\uc2  have publicly clashed during their first face-to-face high-level talks since \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took office, with one senior Chinese official urging the US to address \u8220\'20\'1Cdeep-seated\u8221\'20\'1D issues such as racism, and accusing his American counterparts of \u8220\'20\'1Ccondescension\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Any hopes that the meeting, in Anchorage, would reset bilateral ties after years of tensions over trade, human rights and cybersecurity during \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidency evaporated when the US secretary of state, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/antony-blinken"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Antony Blinken}}}\uc2 , and the national security adviser, Jake Sullivan, opened their meeting with China\u8217\'20\'19s top diplomat Yang Jiechi and the state councillor Wang Yi.\par \par \uc2 After Blinken referred to rising global concern over Beijing\u8217\'20\'19s human rights record, Yang said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe hope that United States will do better on human rights. The fact is that there are many problems within the United States regarding human rights, which is admitted by the US itself,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in a 15-minute speech that appeared to irritate Blinken.\par \par \uc2 He added that US human rights issues were \u8220\'20\'1Cdeep-seated \u8230\'20\'26 they did not just emerge over the past four years, such as Black Lives Matter\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In his opening remarks Blinken had said world leaders had voiced \u8220\'20\'1Cdeep satisfaction\u8221\'20\'1D that the US was re-engaging with the international community after four years of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica first\u8221\'20\'1D doctrine. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m also hearing deep concern about some of the actions your government is taking.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Blinken, who added he had heard similar sentiments during his visits this week to Japan and South Korea, said the Biden administration and its allies were united in pushing back against China\u8217\'20\'19s increasing authoritarianism and assertiveness at home and abroad.\par \par \uc2 In response, Yang angrily demanded that the US stop pushing its own version of democracy at a time when it was dealing with discontent among its own population.\par \par \uc2 Read more of Justin McCurry\u8217\'20\'19s report here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/mar/19/us-china-talks-alaska-biden-blinken-sullivan-wang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US and China publicly rebuke each other in first major talks of Biden era}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/mar/19/us-china-talks-alaska-biden-blinken-sullivan-wang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US and China publicly rebuke each other in first major talks of Biden era}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 Cleve Wootson Jr and Amy Wang write for the Washington Post this morning about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s trip to Georgia, and his administration\u8217\'20\'19s wider attempts to engage with the Asian American community, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/biden-shootings-in-atlanta/2021/03/18/1e88c500-8800-11eb-8a8b-5cf82c3dffe4_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 President Biden has refocused his trip to Georgia on Friday so he can meet with Asian American leaders about violence against their community. He has ordered flags flown at half-staff after the shooting that killed six Atlanta-area women of Asian descent. His administration is backing a bill that allows the Justice Department to review coronavirus-related hate crimes.\par \par \uc2 And White House officials have spent two days working the phones, reaching out to leaders and advocates in the Asian American and Pacific Islander community and reaffirming their commitment to fighting anti-Asian hatred.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I\u8217\'20\'19m conveying to them is, we want you to be a part of the solution,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Cedric L. Richmond\uc2 , a White House senior adviser, said in an interview. \u8220\'20\'1CYou all have been in the community running these programs. We want your expertise, we want your input into how we get past this. But it\u8217\'20\'19s also been an intensive two days of making sure that we\u8217\'20\'19re listening.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But the flurry of activity comes as the massacre at three spas that left eight people dead is raising new questions about whether Biden has enough people of Asian descent on his staff to fully understand the needs and struggles of the more than 21 million Americans with Asian ancestry.\par \par \uc2 Several AAPI leaders said Thursday that they appreciate the White House effort \u8212\'20\'14 including forceful statements from Biden and Vice President Harris denouncing the shootings \u8212\'20\'14 but that the incident underscores the importance of having Asian representation in the most senior levels of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s administration.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/biden-shootings-in-atlanta/2021/03/18/1e88c500-8800-11eb-8a8b-5cf82c3dffe4_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post \u8211\'20\'13 Biden reaches out to Asian Americans after killings \u8212\'20\'14 but many remain frustrated by lack of representation}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden and Harris trip to Atlanta to focus on meeting Asian American community leaders\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  head to Atlanta in Georgia today in what was a planned trip, but which has now taken on additional significance after this week\u8217\'20\'19s Atlanta spa shootings, in which six of the victims were women of Asian descent. The itinerary of the trip has changed significantly as a result. as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/white-house/biden-harris-meet-asian-american-leaders-georgia-offer-support-n1261396"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reported overnight}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said that Biden and Harris will meet with representatives of the Asian American and Pacific Islander community, state lawmakers and community advocates to \u8220\'20\'1Chear about the impact of the incident on the community and to get their perspective on the rise of Anti-Asian hate incidents.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden and Harris\u8217\'20\'19 visit to Atlanta, which will be their first joint trip since taking office, had initially been scheduled as part of the administration\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CHelp is Here\u8221\'20\'1D tour promoting the $1.9 trillion Covid-19 relief package.\par \par \uc2 The shooting Tuesday night caused the White House to shift the focus of the visit, announcing Thursday afternoon that the American Rescue Plan event would be postponed to a later date.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said that Biden would offer his support to the Asian American community on Friday and highlight his commitment to \u8220\'20\'1Ccombating xenophobia, intolerance and hate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 Good morning and welcome to Friday\u8217\'20\'19s live coverage of US politics. The national focus on hate crimes against the Asian American community continues in the aftermath of the shooting in Atlanta, while strained US relations with China were on open display yesterday. Here\u8217\'20\'19s where we are and what can we expect to see today.\par \par \uc2 * President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will meet with Asian American community leaders at \uc2 Emory University\uc2  in Atlanta in the wake of this week\u8217\'20\'19s shootings in which six Asian American women were killed. That is at 3.35pm (1935GMT), and Biden will speak an hour later.\par \par \uc2 * The visit to Georgia was already scheduled as part of their tour promoting their American Rescue Plan while in the state, and Biden and Harris will still visit the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  while there today.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said the US is on track to reach 100m administered vaccine doses by tomorrow, his 58th day in office. The president had initially set the goal of reaching 100m doses by his 100th day in office.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2  raised concerns about a potential surge of Covid-19 in the US even as the vaccine rollout continues. Fauci noted that in past surges, the vaccine had plateaued before inching up in numbers and surging. During Senate testimony, Fauci also got into a spar with Republican senator \uc2 Rand Paul\uc2 , who called wearing a mask \u8220\'20\'1Ctheater\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * Two Biden appointees were confirmed by the Senate.Xavier Becerra was confirmed as health and human services secretary, the first Latino to serve in that role, while William Burns was confirmed as the new director of the CIA.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  responded to comments Biden made agreeing that Putin was \u8220\'20\'1Ca killer\u8221\'20\'1D. Putin said that people tend to view others as they see themselves and wished Biden good health.\par \par \uc2 * The House passed a bill to give undocumented immigrants, including Dreamers, a path to citizenship. The vote sets up a legal pathway to citizenship for about 2.5m people.\par \par \uc2 * There\u8217\'20\'19s no White House press briefing today, although there will be a \u8220\'20\'1Cgaggle\u8221\'20\'1D between the media and Karine Jean-Pierre on Air Force One. The Covid response team briefing is at 12.30.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210319eh3j001jr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
