\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Getting an  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  on Guam requires a $1,000, eight-hour flight. A lawsuit could change that\b0\par\par\uc2 Michelle Broder Van Dyke in Honolulu \par \uc2 1,298 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 February 2021\par 14:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 ACLU\uc2  is suing the US territory over restrictive laws that block people from accessing telemedicine medication abortions\par \par \uc2 Getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Guam, a remote US territory in the Pacific Ocean, has never been simple. Before 2016 there were only two \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors on the entire island, and anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protesters would often stand outside their clinics with signs.\par \par \uc2 But since 2018, it has been impossible. That year Guam lost its last \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider when Dr William Freeman retired and moved away, and the doctor who took over refused to conduct them. This means that the closest US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic is now in Hawai?i, an eight-hour and $1,000 flight away. The number of abortions on Guam dropped from more than 200 a year in 2017 to zero.\par \par \uc2 Now, \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  is suing Guam officials, including the attorney general, over restrictive laws that block people from accessing telemedicine medication abortions, which would allow the doctors involved in the lawsuit to prescribe and send \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication directly to patients.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit, filed in January, is backed by two Hawai?i-based doctors who are licensed to practice in Guam, Shandhini Raidoo and Bliss Kaneshiro. The \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  requires \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication be dispensed in clinics or hospitals, but the pair are part of a project called TelAbortion, which has an agreement with the \uc2 FDA\uc2  that allows them to provide virtual \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  consultations and medication by mail. Similar programs exist in 12 other states and Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 In the lawsuit, Kaneshiro said that before 2018 she only saw patients from Guam in rare cases with a fetal anomaly that required a specialist, but since then she and her colleagues have seen up to 10 patients every year coming to them for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDenial of a wanted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has both short-term and long-term negative effects on a person\u8217\'20\'19s health and wellbeing, along with that of their family,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote Kaneshiro in the motion for preliminary injunction. \u8220\'20\'1CA person who has been denied access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no choice but to continue their pregnancy to term, which leads to substantially increased risks.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 We are fighting for women to be able to exercise a constitutional right\par \par \uc2 Vanessa Williams, Guam lawyer\par \par \uc2 Kaneshiro said the risks include a greater likelihood of living in poverty and staying in an abusive relationship as well as attempting to end one\u8217\'20\'19s own pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Telemedicine medication abortions allow patients to meet with a doctor via videochat, and then receive and take the two medications needed to induce a miscarriage \u8211\'20\'13 mifepristonem and misoprostol \u8211\'20\'13 in the privacy of their own homes. When possible, a majority of women choose medication abortions over procedural abortions; they are substantially cheaper, costing about $240 for the medication and appointments, compared with anywhere from $400 to $7,000 for a procedural \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kaneshiro said Guam residents have requested services from the TelAbortion project, but two Guam laws have stopped doctors from providing them. The first, a law from 1978, requires abortions be \u8220\'20\'1Cperformed\u8221\'20\'1D in a \u8220\'20\'1Cclinic or hospital\u8221\'20\'1D. Criminal penalties for violating this law include a third-degree felony and the loss of medical license.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe purpose of the law was actually not to restrict access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but rather to decriminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Alexa Kolbi-Molinas, an ACLU attorney working on the case. \u8220\'20\'1CSo, because this law was enacted long before medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was available, it is not clear how to apply it in this context.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The second law was passed in 2012 and requires a doctor and patient have an in-person meeting \u8220\'20\'1Cin a private room\u8221\'20\'1D where mandated information is shared at least 24 hours before an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which bars telemedicine as an option.\par \par \uc2 Colonization, Catholicism and CHamoru values\par \par \uc2 While not illegal in Guam, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a complicated history in the territory due to restrictive laws and the lingering influence of Catholicism, a holdover from its colonial history.\par \par \uc2 Guam made national headlines in the 1990s after its legislature passed a restrictive law prohibiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  except when the mother\u8217\'20\'19s life was endangered. At the time, there was a local \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights movement led by attorney Anita Arriola, the now-governor Lou Leon Guerrero, and nursing director Rita Lujan Bevacqua. The latter testified that a man had called her clinic and said his wife was pregnant, but they already had six kids and felt they couldn\u8217\'20\'19t have more. He was too scared to leave his name or come in for help.\par \par \uc2 The US ninth circuit court of appeals eventually struck down the law, saying that it violated Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Guam, which has a population of about 165,000 people, was originally inhabited by the CHamoru people. It was colonized by Spain in the 17th century and Catholicism was brought to the island, which was ceded to the US in 1899.\par \par \uc2 Dr Michael Lujan Bevacqua is a teacher of CHamoru language, history and culture, and the son of Rita Lujan Bevacqua, the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activist. He says that the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in line with ancient CHamoru values.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen the Spanish came to colonize the island in the 17th century, the priests were shocked and appalled at how much power CHamoru women had in society at that time,\u8221\'20\'1D Bevacqua says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you think about what ancient CHamoru values would have been on this issue, it would have been that women should be empowered to make those choices.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 You asked what it is like being the only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider on Guam: scary\par \par \uc2 Dr William Freeman\par \par \uc2 While the Catholic church\u8217\'20\'19s influence on Guam has waned following sex abuse scandals, over 70% of the island residents still identify as Catholic, and anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment is apparent. Freeman said many landlords on Guam would not rent him office space and that he had received death threats because of his work.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou asked what it is like being the only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider on Guam: scary,\u8221\'20\'1D said Freeman.\par \par \uc2 Guam\u8217\'20\'19s first female governor, Lou Leon Guerrero, supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, but many other lawmakers do not. The government of Guam has strict reporting requirements for abortions, including disclosing where they took place and detailing demographic information about the patient. That makes it easy for anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protesters to target clinics, especially on a relatively small island.\par \par \uc2 Jayne Flores, the director of Guam\u8217\'20\'19s bureau of women\u8217\'20\'19s affairs, said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is only a small part of a larger conversation about education, poverty and women\u8217\'20\'19s health that needs to be had in the US territory. Guam has a higher poverty rate than anywhere else in the 50 states. Although less than 40% of Guam residents are CHamoru, they accounted for almost 60% of all abortions before 2018. The majority of women seeking abortions are mothers with children, according to the lawsuit, but there have also been troubling cases, including a 2019 report of an 11-year-old girl who had been raped, and was forced to carry her pregnancy to term.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have high rates of teen pregnancy, we have high rates of sexual assault, and we have high rates of domestic violence,\u8221\'20\'1D said Flores.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit seeks a court order to render the two laws in question unenforceable when it comes to telemedicine medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services. The case is now moving through the courts.\par \par \uc2 Vanessa Williams, a lawyer on Guam working with the \uc2 ACLU\uc2 , said she had received \u8220\'20\'1Cgratitude\u8221\'20\'1D from people on the island for challenging \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions. \u8220\'20\'1CNot just because we are fighting for women to be able to exercise a constitutional right, but also because lack of access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  exacerbates the endemic issues of poverty and violence Guam faces.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210222eh2m001gx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
