\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Texas storm: Biden to declare major disaster to secure federal aid \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Vivian Ho (now) and Daniel Strauss (earlier) \par \uc2 6,592 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 February 2021\par 01:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President says declaration could be signed todayBiden assures US allies he will reverse Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policiesAnti-Cruz outrage shows little sign of abatingAbout 6m vaccines delayed due to frigid weather across USSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.03am GMT\par \par \uc2 Evening summary\par \par \uc2 * New Mexico overturned a dormant, 52-year-old ban on some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medical procedures.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  told reporters that he would stand by Neera Tanden and not pull her nomination, despite Joe Manchin indicating he would vote against it.\par \par \uc2 * All registered voters in California will receive mail-in ballots for any and all elections in 2021, according to law signed by \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  - and that includes a recall of Newsom, if it reaches the ballot.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 Over here in California, governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  just signed into law a bill requiring that every registered voter in the state be mailed a ballot in an election in 2021. Politico\u8217\'20\'19s Jeremy White pointed out that would include any recall effort for the man who signed the bill into law.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: Every active California voter will be mailed a ballot for elections held or called in 2021 -- including a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GavinNewsom?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GavinNewsom}}}\uc2  recall if it happens\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jeremy B. White, cat attorney JD (@JeremyBWhite) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JeremyBWhite/status/1362918809275924481?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 20, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 In a state as large as California \u8211\'20\'13 and a population as varied \u8211\'20\'13 calls to recall Newsom are nothing new. Rural swaths of the inland empire and the north have long felt overlooked by Sacramento, and are by far more conservative than their coastal counterparts.\par \par \uc2 But as my colleague Maanvi Singh {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/07/california-coronavirus-gavin-newsom-pandemic-response"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported earlier this month}}}\uc2 , this long-lived discontent gained new legs in the pandemic, getting support from far-right groups, mainstream Republicans and some Silicon Valley bigwigs.\par \par \uc2 While his fast action was applauded early in the pandemic, Newsom\u8217\'20\'19s approval rating plummeted with the second state lockdown, as parents and teachers called for schools to reopen.\par \par \uc2 Then, of course, there was the French Laundry incident, where he attended an indoor birthday party at the opulent wine country restaurant after repeatedly telling Californians to avoid small indoor gatherings.\par \par \uc2 As Maanvi reports, most political observers do not think a recall effort will be successful in a state that is 46.1% registered Democrats and 24.2% registered Republicans, even if those who oppose Newsom manage to get it onto a ballot. Read more about it here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/07/california-coronavirus-gavin-newsom-pandemic-response"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California\u8217\'20\'19s governor, once praised, faces backlash over pandemic response}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a fun little tidbit in the Ted Cruz saga. The Texas Democratic Party acted swiftly yesterday when news broke about the senator\u8217\'20\'19s ill-timed trip to Canc\u250\'00\'FAn and snagged the URL, FlyinTedCruz.com \u8211\'20\'13 a play on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1C Lyin\u8217\'20\'19 Ted \u8221\'20\'1D nickname for Cruz when they ran against each other in the 2016 Republican presidential primaries.\par \par \uc2 enltrAs Ted Cruz, returns to Texas from Cancun, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/texasdemocrats?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @texasdemocrats}}}\uc2  are up with a new webpage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XYjrYbWzuZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/XYjrYbWzuZ}}}\uc2 , which redirects to a donation page for Feeding Texas. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rFEbMeEJxl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/rFEbMeEJxl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Priscilla Thompson (@PriscillaWT) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PriscillaWT/status/1362498831259234305?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 18, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The link goes to a page for Feeding Texas, to raise money to support Texans during the winter storm emergency.\par \par \uc2 enltrWell he did fly to Cancun and back in 24 hours so makes sense {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XJEBOe2pUM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/XJEBOe2pUM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kathryn Watson (@kathrynw5) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kathrynw5/status/1362911045908451329?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New Mexico overturns ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedures\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in New Mexico, a Democrat-led legislature has overturned a dormant 1969 ban on most \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedures.\par \par \uc2 enltrHistory made. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/SB10?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #SB10}}}\uc2 , affirming that decisions about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should remain with NM women, has passed both chambers of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/nmleg?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #nmleg}}}\uc2 . Thank you to every New Mexican who has fought for this progress. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/nmpol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #nmpol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OigA95YhMB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/OigA95YhMB}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NM House Democrats (@NMHouseDems) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NMHouseDems/status/1362902258543919104?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The 1969 law made it so a medical termination of a pregnancy was only allowed with the permission of a specialized hospital board in instances of incest, rape reported to law enforcement, grave medical risks to the woman or grave medical defects in the fetus.\par \par \uc2 Because of the Roe v Wade ruling by the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  in 1973, the law had ultimately been dormant in the historically blue and heavily Roman Catholic state.\par \par \uc2 With talk of overturning Roe v Wade growing among Republicans, the 1969 law would have reverted back into place if that have ever happened. This repeal ensures that will not.\par \par \uc2 enltrThis November, you elected leaders to build a better future for all New Mexicans. Thank you to the voters, activists, and champions who fought for a New Mexico where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care is accessible for all. You made this win possible! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/nmleg?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #nmleg}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/SB10?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #SB10}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/repealtheban?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #repealtheban}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ltIrJ0ZFJv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ltIrJ0ZFJv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Planned Parenthood Votes New Mexico (@PPVotesNewMex) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PPVotesNewMex/status/1362902385899626499?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senator Joe Manchin of West Virginia has already indicated that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/feb/19/texas-storm-latest-news-today-power-outages-ted-cruz-cancun-trip-backlash?page=with:block-6030294a8f08bdbed283bfc6#block-6030294a8f08bdbed283bfc6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he would oppose}}}\uc2  Neera Tanden \u8217\'20\'19s to be director of the Office of Management and Budget, in part because of combative statements she has made on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: Manchin is opposing Neera Tanden's nomination for OMB: "I believe her overtly partisan statements will have a toxic and detrimental impact on the important working relationship between members of Congress and the next director of the Office of Management and Budget."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Marianne LeVine (@marianne_levine) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/marianne_levine/status/1362870975646285833?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Despite this, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  says he will not pull her nomination.\par \par \uc2 enltrOMB: Biden tells reporters he will not pull {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/neeratanden?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @neeratanden}}}\uc2  nomination, will find the votes for her\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Erik Wasson (@elwasson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/elwasson/status/1362897282992115713?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWH press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 : "Neera Tanden is an accomplished policy expert who would be an excellent Budget Director and we look forward to the committee votes next week and to continuing to work toward her confirmation through engagement with both parties."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Felicia Sonmez (@feliciasonmez) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/feliciasonmez/status/1362894814103154688?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Hey all, Vivian Ho on the west coast, taking over the blog for Daniel Strauss.\par \par \uc2 It appears now that billionaire biotech investor \uc2 Dr Patrick Soon-Shiong\uc2  may not be selling the \uc2 Los Angeles Times\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrLos Angeles Times spokeswoman just told me: "\uc2 Dr. Soon-Shiong\uc2  and his family continue to invest in and plan for the future of the \uc2 Los Angeles Times\uc2 , and do not plan to sell."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Katie Robertson (@katie_robertson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/katie_robertson/status/1362861120118263813?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Evening summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it for me. I\u8217\'20\'19m passing the blogging baton to Vivian Ho.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what happened today:\par \par \uc2 * Senator Joe Manchin of West Virginia said he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/feb/19/texas-storm-latest-news-today-power-outages-ted-cruz-cancun-trip-backlash?page=with:block-6030294a8f08bdbed283bfc6#block-6030294a8f08bdbed283bfc6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would oppose}}}\uc2  Neera Tanden \u8217\'20\'19s nomination to be director of the Office of Management and Budget.\par \par \uc2 * A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/feb/19/texas-storm-latest-news-today-power-outages-ted-cruz-cancun-trip-backlash?page=with:block-603027558f08ad21ea600857#block-603027558f08ad21ea600857"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  in The Wall Street Journal said The \uc2 Los Angeles Times\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 owner is thinking of selling the publication.\par \par \uc2 * Congresswoman Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/feb/19/texas-storm-latest-news-today-power-outages-ted-cruz-cancun-trip-backlash?page=with:block-6030241b8f08ad21ea60082f#block-6030241b8f08ad21ea60082f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joined}}}\uc2  calls for an investigation of governor \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s handling of nursing homes in New York during the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/feb/19/texas-storm-latest-news-today-power-outages-ted-cruz-cancun-trip-backlash?page=with:block-60300dd88f08bdbed283be9f#block-60300dd88f08bdbed283be9f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 planning}}}\uc2  on making a disaster declaration for Texas.\par \par \uc2 * In his appearance at the G7 Biden also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/feb/19/texas-storm-latest-news-today-power-outages-ted-cruz-cancun-trip-backlash?page=with:block-603008858f08bdbed283be5b#block-603008858f08bdbed283be5b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 assured}}}\uc2  global allies that he will reverse \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s legacy.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senator Joe Manchin of West Virginia will oppose Neera Tanden \u8217\'20\'19s nomination to be director of the Office of Management and Budget.\par \par \uc2 enltr??Full MANCHIN statement on opposition to Neera TANDEN as OMB director ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ugzh3fxbaP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ugzh3fxbaP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Daniel Strauss (@DanielStrauss4) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DanielStrauss4/status/1362872136084381701?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 A few things to keep in mind here. In a 50-50 split Senate like this one any senator\u8217\'20\'19s opposition to a nomination is very influential.\par \par \uc2 Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s statement is also notable for why he\u8217\'20\'19s opposing Tanden. Tanden, the president of the Center for American Progress, has been an avid and combative \uc2 Twitter\uc2  user, oftentimes using the platform to excoriate members of both parties. That has become a liability for her nomination. In confirmation hearings she has said she regretted those past tweets.\par \par \uc2 Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s statement is also devoid of any mention of more substantive criticism Tanden has received, such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/14/us/politics/think-tank-with-ties-to-obama-discloses-corporate-sponsors.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some of the donations}}}\uc2  the liberal think tank received under Tanden\u8217\'20\'19s tenure or her feuding supporters of Senator Bernie Sanders of Vermont.\par \par \uc2 Once, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/15/us/politics/tanden-sanders-.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The New York Times}}}\uc2  citing a person in the room, Tanden punched Faz Shakir, then the top editor of the think tank\u8217\'20\'19s marquee blog. Shakir would eventually go on to serve as Sanders\u8217\'20\'19 presidential campaign manager. Tanden, an outspoken \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  supporter, was a regular critic of Sanders\u8217\'20\'19 candidacy.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\u8217\'20\'19s Lukas I. Alpert {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/los-angeles-times-owner-exploring-sale-of-company-11613765566"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  that billionaire \uc2 Patrick Soon-Shiong\uc2  is considering possibly selling the \uc2 Los Angeles Times\uc2 . Here are the key paragraphs:\par \par \uc2 When \uc2 Mr. Soon-Shiong\uc2  acquired {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/tronc-pushes-into-digital-future-after-los-angeles-times-sale-1518017136?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  the Times, the San Diego Union-Tribune}}}\uc2  and a handful of weeklies from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/market-data/quotes/TPCO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tribune Publishing}}}\uc2  Co. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/market-data/quotes/TPCO?mod=chiclets"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TPCO -0.06% }}}\uc2 , then called \uc2 Tronc Inc\uc2 ., in 2018, it was met with great fanfare from staff and media watchers after years of turmoil and downsizing at the publications. At the time, he said that the sale represented the beginning of a new era and that he intended to do what it took to make the business viable for the next 100 years.\par \par \uc2 He has since grown dissatisfied with the news organization\u8217\'20\'19s slow expansion of its digital audience and its substantial losses, the people said. He also has increasingly come to believe that the \uc2 Los Angeles Times\uc2  and San Diego Union-Tribune\u8212\'20\'14together known as the California Times company\u8212\'20\'14would be better served if they were part of a larger media group, they said.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Soon-Shiong\uc2  has been heavily focused on efforts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/l-a-times-owner-to-buy-closed-los-angeles-hospital-11586561836?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by his immunotherapy company}}}\uc2  to develop a Covid-19 vaccine and has had little time to devote to the Times, people familiar with the matter said. \u8220\'20\'1CCovid really brought him back to the lab,\u8221\'20\'1D said one of the people.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Soon-Shiong\uc2  didn\u8217\'20\'19t immediately respond to a message seeking comment and a spokeswoman for the Times had no immediate comment.\par \par \uc2 Not long after the Journal story went live Soon-Shiong denied the article\u8217\'20\'19s accuracy.\par \par \uc2 enltrWSJ article inaccurate. We are committed to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/latimes?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @LATimes}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dr. Pat Soon-Shiong (@DrPatSoonShiong)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DrPatSoonShiong/status/1362862504796282881?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 AOC wants \u8216\'20\'18full investigation\u8217\'20\'19 into Cuomo on nursing homes\par \par \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez has joined {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TweetBenMax/status/1362850483271061521"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 growing calls}}}\uc2  for an investigation into New York governor \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s handling of nursing homes during the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI \u8230\'20\'26 stand with our local officials calling for a full investigation of the Cuomo administration\u8217\'20\'19s handling of nursing homes during Covid-19,\u8221\'20\'1D the high-profile progressive congresswoman, who represents a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  City district, said in a statement on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Last week, it was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/new-york-cuomo-investigation-fbi-nursing-home-deaths-8aab170e-56d5-40d3-b013-1ba716f21c90.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revealed}}}\uc2  that a Cuomo aide told New York legislators the true picture of nursing home deaths wasn\u8217\'20\'19t given last year, for fear it would be used against the governor during an investigation launched by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s justice department.\par \par \uc2 Cuomo, who has already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/oct/17/american-crisis-review-andrew-cuomo-new-york-covid-trump-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published a book}}}\uc2  about his handling of the crisis, has dismissed claims of wrongdoing. On Friday, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/politics/cuomo-defiant-nursing-home-scandal-take-on-lies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  information was not produced fast enough, which created \u8220\'20\'1Ca void. And conspiracy theories and politics and rumors fill that void and you can\u8217\'20\'19t allow inaccurate information to go unanswered.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But in January, New York state attorney general Leticia James {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/new-york-undercounted-nursing-home-deaths-4758b7b9-d9ed-4aa0-9596-5445efcc6bcb.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  nursing home deaths from Covid-19 were undercounted by as much as 50%. Now, federal prosecutors in New York City and the \uc2 FBI\uc2  are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/18/andrew-cuomo-fbi-federal-prosecutors-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  to be investigating and state officials are seeking to strip Cuomo of emergency powers.\par \par \uc2 The governor is under increasing pressure and Ocasio-Cortez\u8217\'20\'19s intervention adds drama to a combustible mix.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/19/aoc-andrew-cuomo-nursing-homes-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AOC calls for 'full investigation' into Cuomo's handling of nursing homes}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 True to form, the Biden administration is declining to weigh in on Ted Cruz\u8217\'20\'19s Cancun trip.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PressSec}}}\uc2  aboard Air Force One: \u8220\'20\'1CI can assure you that with millions of people in Texas still suffering, we\u8217\'20\'19re not spending any time, energy or breath analyzing Sen. Cruz\u8217\'20\'19s whereabouts or his group chat."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ken Thomas (@KThomasDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KThomasDC/status/1362839835589935109?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 This is very much in line with how the Biden administration is trying to approach daily news cycles. They say they are focused on their major policy initiatives and rarely (at least compared to the last administration) weigh in.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 My colleague Oliver Milman reported out the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s decision to rejoin the Paris climate accord:\par \par \uc2 The US has marked its return to the Paris agreement by urging countries to do more to confront the climate crisis, with America\u8217\'20\'19s climate envoy, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/john-kerry"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 John Kerry}}}\uc2 , warning that international talks this year are the \u8220\'20\'1Clast, best hope\u8221\'20\'1D of avoiding catastrophic global heating.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the US officially returned to the Paris climate accord, 107 days after it left at the behest of former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/jan/20/paris-climate-accord-joe-biden-returns-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 moved to reverse this on his first day in office}}}\uc2  and Kerry conceded that the US is returning \u8220\'20\'1Cwith a lot of humility, for the agony of the last four years\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a significant day, a day that never had to happen,\u8221\'20\'1D Kerry said to \uc2 Al Gore\uc2 , the former US vice-president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ted.com/talks/john_kerry_and_al_gore_the_us_is_back_in_the_paris_agreement_what_s_next"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a conversation filmed}}}\uc2  on the eve of the re-entry. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s so sad that our previous president without any scientific basis or any legitimate economic rationale decided to pull America out. It hurt us and it hurt the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/19/us-paris-climate-agreement-john-kerry"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US rejoins Paris climate accord with warning: this year\u8217\'20\'19s talks are \u8216\'20\'18last, best hope\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the disaster declaration \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  plans to sign from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-to-sign-federal-disaster-aid-for-texas-snow-storm-11613756190?mod=hp_lead_pos6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Wall Street Journal}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Ken Thomas:\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency\uc2  made generators and fuel available to support critical infrastructure sites, after Mr. Biden approved an emergency declaration for all 254 counties in the state. As of Friday morning, FEMA had also distributed 729,000 liters of water, more than 10,000 wool blankets and 50,000 cotton blankets, and 225,000 meals in Fort Worth, Texas.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden spoke Thursday night with \uc2 Texas Gov. Greg Abbott\uc2  and said his administration was ready to provide additional federal disaster support, which would help pay for physical damage from the storm that left hundreds of thousands of people without power and caused water disruptions for millions of Texans. Mr. Abbott requested the major disaster assistance Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The president told reporters Friday that he planned to speak to the \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency\uc2  later in the day \u8220\'20\'1Cto ask them to accelerate the response to the request for a major disaster declaration so we can get everything done they need.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The declaration, once approved, would allow communities in Texas to seek federal assistance to pay for damages to infrastructure as well as state residents to help them pay for property damage.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden said he was directing several federal agencies, including U.S. Housing and Urban Development and the Defense Department, \u8220\'20\'1Cto identify other resources we can provide to assist the growing needs of the folks in Texas.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The White House on Friday released a list of Texas elected officials that it had been coordinating with \u8220\'20\'1Cto understand the dire situation on the ground\u8221\'20\'1D and ensure they were in touch with FEMA and other federal resources.\par \par \uc2 The list included several mayors, including those of Houston, San Antonio and Austin, along with leaders of the state\u8217\'20\'19s largest counties.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden ready to declare major disaster in Texas after deadly winter storm\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said Friday he was ready to declare a major disaster in Texas after a deadly winter storm cut power and disrupted water supplies for millions across the state.\par \par \uc2 Biden said the declaration, which follows a request from Texas governor Greg Abbott, could be signed as soon as this afternoon, and would open up broader federal aid for immediate and long-term recovery efforts.\par \par \uc2 Biden also said he would travel to the state as long as he was not a burden to local authorities.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs I said when I ran, I\u8217\'20\'19m going to be a president for all Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden, who won November\u8217\'20\'19s election without winning Texas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf I can do it without creating a burden for folks, I plan on going,\u8221\'20\'1D he said of the visit, which could take place next week.\par \par \uc2 Biden is expected to have a call with the acting administrator at the federal emergency management agency (FEMA) later on Friday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden assures US allies he will reverse Trump's legacy\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  made his virtual debut as president on the world stage on Friday, pledging \u8220\'20\'1Cunshakeable\u8221\'20\'1D US support for the transatlantic alliance in what he portrayed as an epoch-defining struggle to safeguard democracy.\par \par \uc2 In videoconference remarks first to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/g7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 G7}}}\uc2  and then the Munich Security Conference, Biden sought to assure America\u8217\'20\'19s allies of his determination to bury the legacy left by his predecessor.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was not mentioned but almost every sentence of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech to the Munich conference was framed by how the new US president would reverse the policies and approach of the past four years.\par \par \uc2 In the wake of the January insurrection in Washington in which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters had attempted to overturn the result of the US election by force}}}\uc2 , Biden said neither he nor Europe\u8217\'20\'19s leaders could take democracy for granted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn so many places, including Europe and the United States, democratic progress is under assault,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CHistorians are going to examine and write about this moment as an inflection point and I believe with every ounce of my being that democracy will and must prevail.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat, in my view, is our galvanizing mission,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said, in a livestreamed speech to Munich, where he shared the virtual stage with \uc2 Angela Merkel\uc2  and \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CDemocracy doesn\u8217\'20\'19t happen by accident. We have to defend it, fight for it, strengthen it, renew it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 My colleague Sam Levine has written a piece on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://beta.documentcloud.org/documents/20488034-hb-531-lc-28-0215"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sweeping new legislation}}}\uc2  unveiled by Georgia Republicans that would make it dramatically harder to vote in the state.\par \par \uc2 The move follows November\u8217\'20\'19s elections which had record turnout and surging participation among Black voters.\par \par \uc2 He reports:\par \par \uc2 The measure is one of the most brazen efforts to make it harder to vote in America in recent years. The bill would block officials from offering early voting on Sundays, a day traditionally used by Black churches to mobilize voters as part of a \u8220\'20\'1Csouls to the polls\u8221\'20\'1D effort. It would place new limits on the use of mail-in ballot dropboxes, restrict who can handle an absentee ballot, and require voters to provide their driver\u8217\'20\'19s license number or a copy of other identification with their application for a mail-in ballot. It would also require voters to provide the same driver\u8217\'20\'19s license information on the mail-in ballot itself or the last four digits of their social security number if they do not have an acceptable ID.\par \par \uc2 Read Sam\u8217\'20\'19s full report here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/19/georgia-republicans-legislation-bill-voting-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia Republicans in sweeping new effort to make it harder to vote}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 * The winter storms in Texas are also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/feb/19/texas-storm-latest-news-today-power-outages-ted-cruz-cancun-trip-backlash?page=with:block-602ff9f68f08c3cb92a5c943#block-602ff9f68f08c3cb92a5c943"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 affecting}}}\uc2  vaccine distribution.\par \par \uc2 * Congressional Republicans are being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/feb/19/texas-storm-latest-news-today-power-outages-ted-cruz-cancun-trip-backlash?page=with:block-602ff5b78f08bdbed283bcc7#block-602ff5b78f08bdbed283bcc7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 directed to oppose}}}\uc2  Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 Covid relief package.\par \par \uc2 * President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/feb/19/texas-storm-latest-news-today-power-outages-ted-cruz-cancun-trip-backlash?page=with:block-602fe9ba8f08bdbed283bbd2#block-602fe9ba8f08bdbed283bbd2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promising}}}\uc2  to use federal resources to help Texas. He also responded to a question on whether he would visit the state by saying \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D but adding he didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to be a burden.\par \par \uc2 * Biden also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/feb/19/texas-storm-latest-news-today-power-outages-ted-cruz-cancun-trip-backlash?page=with:block-602fe69a8f08ad21ea600423#block-602fe69a8f08ad21ea600423"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reaffirmed}}}\uc2  the United States\u8217\'20\'19 commitment to Nato.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 How the winter storms robbed Texas of a week of vaccine distribution\par \par \uc2 Shipment delays and vaccination site closures triggered by the catastrophic winter storm have essentially robbed Texas of an entire week in the race to protect Americans against Covid-19, even as widespread power outages, water shortages and lack of food cause yet another humanitarian crisis in the state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEverything was put on ice \u8212\'20\'14 literally \u8212\'20\'14 this week,\u8221\'20\'1D said Chris Van Deusen, director of media relations at the Texas Department of State Health Services.\par \par \uc2 Shipping hubs also affected by the winter weather generally didn\u8217\'20\'19t risk transporting most of the precious vaccine doses for jabs in Texas amid the storm. Exceptions included 125,000 Moderna vaccines that arrived at hub providers last Friday and a handful of \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  doses that were supposed to make it by Wednesday, though some sites hadn\u8217\'20\'19t received them on time, Van Deusen said.\par \par \uc2 But \u8220\'20\'1Ceven if it takes a day or two to get them delivered as conditions improve, it\u8217\'20\'19s not gonna put the vaccine in jeopardy,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 If vaccine providers have doses that are going to spoil and can\u8217\'20\'19t be stored safely, they\u8217\'20\'19re up for grabs to anyone who\u8217\'20\'19s willing to take them, regardless of whether that person meets Texas\u8217\'20\'19 current eligibility criteria prioritizing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dshs.texas.gov/coronavirus/immunize/vaccine.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 healthcare workers}}}\uc2 , long-term care residents, the elderly and people with pre-existing conditions.\par \par \uc2 But other than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.houstonchronicle.com/news/houston-texas/houston/article/Harris-County-hustles-to-distribute-8-400-15952293.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a storage facility}}}\uc2  in Houston\u8217\'20\'19s Harris county, where power went out, a backup generator failed, and thousands of doses were quickly redistributed to a university, the county jail, and local hospitals, Van Deusen hasn\u8217\'20\'19t heard of too many desperate scrambles to reallocate shots before they expire.\par \par \uc2 Both vaccines \u8212\'20\'14 and especially Moderna\u8217\'20\'19s \u8212\'20\'14 have enough of a shelf life to weather the storm if they\u8217\'20\'19re able to be stored correctly.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe haven\u8217\'20\'19t fortunately gotten a whole lot of reports, at least to this point, of vaccine being spoiled,\u8221\'20\'1D Van Deusen said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut, you know, people may just now be getting back into places, or over the next few days.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Icy, slick roads have caused treacherous driving conditions across Texas, making it incredibly dangerous for people to grab much-needed groceries or get to hotels and warming centers, much less attend their clinical appointments. Likewise, as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.houstonchronicle.com/news/houston-texas/health/article/Houston-s-weather-closed-COVID-vaccine-sites-15955329.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 natural disaster}}}\uc2  and subsequent failure of basic infrastructure have wreaked havoc on the state, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.austintexas.gov/news/aph-provides-update-covid-19-testing-and-vaccination-sites"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vaccination sites}}}\uc2  have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcdfw.com/news/local/fair-park-covid-19-vaccination-hub-reopens-sunday-after-closing-due-to-weather-outages/2556831/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shuttered for days}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Around 10.6% of Texans have received at least one dose of a Covid-19 vaccine and 4.3% have received both doses, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2020/us/covid-19-vaccine-doses.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times}}}\uc2 , lagging behind the nation at large.\par \par \uc2 Since the start of the pandemic, more than 2.2 million confirmed Covid-19 infections and roughly 340,000 probable cases have ravaged the state, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://txdshs.maps.arcgis.com/apps/opsdashboard/index.html#/ed483ecd702b4298ab01e8b9cafc8b83"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killing almost 41,000 }}}\uc2  residents so far.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Over on Capitol Hill, Republican members of Congress are being advised by their leadership to oppose Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 Covid rescue package.\par \par \uc2 enltrHouse GOP Leadership recommending a NO vote on Biden COVID relief package, which comes to floor next week.\par \par \uc2 Scalise team mockingly calling the legislation the "Pelosi\u8217\'20\'19s Payoff to Progressives Act" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PtT2RtJAuY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/PtT2RtJAuY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Scott Wong (@scottwongDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/scottwongDC/status/1362797636286361604?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve touched on this in my {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/18/joe-biden-republicans-bipartisan-covid-bill-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent reporting}}}\uc2 . Despite \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s interest in lowering the temperature in the national political discourse and offering a sincere olive branch to Republicans on policymaking it\u8217\'20\'19s looking increasingly like both Republicans and Democrats are going to dig in on their respective sides. Democrats will use their (slim) majorities to push through a Covid relief bill and Republicans will oppose it very likely along party lines.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s the way things are in Washington these days.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile there\u8217\'20\'19s a bunch of news coming out of a Covid-19 response team briefing. New vaccination sites are being set up. \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2  has also cautioned about the availability of data for vaccines for children until early next year.\par \par \uc2 A mix of top notch healthcare reporters and political reporters are covering this.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEWS: Fauci says unlikely to have vaccine data on *elementary children" until early 2022.\par \par \uc2 Safety/efficacy data likely for 12+ in the fall.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Heidi Przybyla (@HeidiNBC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HeidiNBC/status/1362811385336446978?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrHow weather is delaying COVID vaccines, per {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/aslavitt46?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @aslavitt46}}}\par \par \uc2 1. Weather hampering workforces at UPS, \uc2 FedEx\uc2 , McKesson\par \par \uc2 2. Road closures slow shipping\par \par \uc2 3. Power outages closing some vaccine sites\par \par \uc2 "We will be able to catch up," he says, but it will take effort up and down the line.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jonathan Cohn (@CitizenCohn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CitizenCohn/status/1362808420190085123?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: White House announces five new Covid-19 vaccination sites:\par \par \uc2 -Four new community vaccination centers in Florida in Orlando, Miami, Jacksonville and Tampa with total capacity for 12,000 shots a day\par \par \uc2 -One in Philadelphia, PA with capacity to deliver 6,000 doses per day\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sabrina Siddiqui (@SabrinaSiddiqui)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SabrinaSiddiqui/status/1362808452972765185?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden promises to use federal resources to help Texas\par \par \uc2 Notably, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is also promising to use the force of the federal government to help Texas.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: Pres. Biden says he will make a "major disaster declaration" for Texas to unlock more FEMA resources, after speaking with Gov. Abbott last night.\par \par \uc2 Says he will sign the declaration this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kayla Tausche (@kaylatausche) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaylatausche/status/1362803527807102976?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr"The answer is yes," Biden says if he has plans to go to Texas. But adds he doesn't want to be a burden.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kathryn Watson (@kathrynw5) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kathrynw5/status/1362803829935206400?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 And again, this speech is making clear that this is indeed a different president with a different foreign policy worldview. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in his speech has reaffirmed the United States\u8217\'20\'19 commitment to Nato and warned about Russia.\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden on Russia: "Putin seeks to weaken the European project and our \uc2 NATO\uc2  alliance. He wants to undermine the transatlantic unity and our resolve."\par \par \uc2 "It's so much easier for the Kremlin to bully & intimidate individual states."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jeremy Diamond (@JDiamond1)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JDiamond1/status/1362801336069345280?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The tonal shift in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s address here and that of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  when he was president is very apparent.\par \par \uc2 enltrPOTUS reiterates full commitment to \uc2 NATO\uc2  and Article 5, and says "we are at an inflection point" between those who argue that autocracy is best way forward, "and those that understand that democracy is essential" to meeting challenges. "I believe...that democracy will prevail."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Natasha Bertrand (@NatashaBertrand) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NatashaBertrand/status/1362800418691121152?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MunSecConf?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @MunSecConf}}}\uc2  : "America is back.\par \par \uc2 "The transatlantic alliance is back.\par \par \uc2 "Let me erase any lingering doubt: the United States will work closely with our European partners."\par \par \uc2 Affirms commitment to \uc2 NATO\uc2 's Article Five: "An attack on one is an attack on all."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Eli Stokols (@EliStokols) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EliStokols/status/1362799761368248321?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The US has officially rejoined the Paris climate agreement today, 107 days after it exited the global effort to stave off disastrous global heating at the behest of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  moved to reverse the withdrawal on his first day in the White House.\par \par \uc2 In an online event to mark the re-entry, \uc2 John Kerry\uc2 , Biden\u8217\'20\'19s climate envoy, said he was \u8220\'20\'1Csuper excited\u8221\'20\'1D and admitted that \u8220\'20\'1Cfor the last four years there were a lot of times when a lot of us thought the failure of this enterprise may rest on one word \u8211\'20\'13 Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The world is still committed to action on the climate crisis, Kerry said, although far more needs to be done to avert catastrophic flooding, heatwaves and other disasters. \u8220\'20\'1CParis is not enough,\u8221\'20\'1D said the former US secretary of state.\par \par \uc2 Crucial UN climate talks will be held in Scotland later this year and the Biden administration is starting to cajole other countries, including the fossil fuel-friendly leaderships of Brazil and Australia, to accelerate emissions cuts. Last night Kerry told \uc2 Al Gore\uc2 , the former US vice president, that the talks present the \u8220\'20\'1Clast, best hope\u8221\'20\'1D to avoid climate breakdown.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Switching gears, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is delivering his address to the Munich Security Conference. You can watch below:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @JoeBiden}}}\uc2  first attended the Munich Security Conference in 1980 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Xg5wapmy1o"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Xg5wapmy1o}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 davidshepardson (@davidshepardson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/davidshepardson/status/1362799065138941952?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Underscoring how unprepared the state was for a storm like this, the Dallas Morning News reports that the CEO of the Electric Reliability Council of Texas warned that the state\u8217\'20\'19s power grid was \u8220\'20\'1Cseconds or minutes\u8221\'20\'1D away from collapsing.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dallasnews.com/news/weather/2021/02/18/oncor-ends-controlled-outages-thousands-of-north-texans-still-without-power-due-to-equipment-damage/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dispatch}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Texas\u8217\'20\'19 electrical system was \u8220\'20\'1Cseconds or minutes\u8221\'20\'1D from collapsing and plunging the state into the dark for months, the power grid\u8217\'20\'19s operators said Thursday while defending their decision to initiate controlled outages.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur frequency went to a level that, if operators had not acted very rapidly \u8230\'20\'26 it could have very quickly changed,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Bill Magness\uc2 , CEO of the Electric Reliability Council of Texas, the agency that oversees the grid.\par \par \uc2 Starting about 11 p.m. Sunday, generation units started knocking off \u8220\'20\'1Cin rapid succession,\u8221\'20\'1D Magness said. Several big units could have gone offline by the minute if officials had waited.\par \par \uc2 He said controlled outages were the only real choice because a true blackout would leave the entire state without power for an indefinite amount of time \u8212\'20\'14 possibly months.\par \par \uc2 But Gov. Greg Abbott had harsh words for ERCOT during a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dallasnews.com/news/politics/2021/02/18/watch-live-texas-gov-greg-abbott-gives-update-on-state-response-to-winter-storm/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 news conference Thursday afternoon}}}\uc2 . In calling for reforms, he said that what happened in Texas \u8220\'20\'1Ccan never be replicated again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Communities throughout Texas are having to provide their own response to the snow storms and resource crises throughout Texas. Andrew Lapin in The \uc2 Jewish Telegraphic Agency\uc2  lays out how Jewish communities are responding throughout the state:\par \par \uc2 Jewish communities, like others across the state, are taking steps to address their own needs. In Dallas, one of the region\u8217\'20\'19s two Jewish senior living centers lost both its main power and backup generator, forcing the staff to quickly relocate residents to the area\u8217\'20\'19s other senior center \u8212\'20\'14 fortunately it had spare room, having just recently opened.\par \par \uc2 Two Orthodox Jewish-run emergency response units, Hatzalah of Dallas and the newly formed Texas Chaverim, both founded by a local resident, Baruch Shawel, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tjpnews.com/dallas-jewish-community-warming-up-by-helping-one-another/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sent out patrols}}}\uc2  to assist residents with dead car batteries, medical emergencies and other issues.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s been pretty wild out here,\u8221\'20\'1D Hannah Lebovits, a professor at the University of Texas-Arlington who lives in an Orthodox community in north Dallas, said of the rolling blackouts, which accompany other problems like loss of heat and water pressure. \u8220\'20\'1CThankfully in the Jewish community, very often we quickly create our own mutual aid systems.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Still, Lebovits said, \u8220\'20\'1CIt shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be Chaverim doing that. It should be the city of Dallas knocking on my door and checking on me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Houston, too, Jewish leaders are leaning on coordination groundwork laid long before the unusual cold snap set in. Traumatized by the patchwork Jewish response to Hurricane Harvey\u8217\'20\'19s devastating floods, the Jewish Federation of Greater Houston had convened the Jewish Response and Action Network in early 2020, even before the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter Harvey, each shul made its own response. They made their own food. It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t coordinated,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jackie Fisherman, the network\u8217\'20\'19s director and the Houston federation\u8217\'20\'19s director of government affairs. \u8220\'20\'1CWe thought there must be a better way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 More {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.jta.org/2021/02/18/united-states/in-a-texas-battered-by-cold-jewish-communities-join-a-desperately-needed-response"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 My colleague Nina Lakhani lays out how Texas is facing dwindling food supplies amid the ongoing storms and power problems:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/food-banks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Food banks}}}\uc2  in Texas have gone into disaster mode as they ramp up operations to tackle a surge in hunger after unprecedented freezing conditions disrupted almost every part of the food supply chain in the state.\par \par \uc2 Grocery stores are empty, school meal programs suspended, and deliveries disrupted by untreated, treacherous roads that have left millions of Texans trapped in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/18/texas-millions-struggle-drinking-water-winter-storm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 precarious living conditions}}}\uc2  with dwindling food supplies.\par \par \uc2 Even those who did stockpile before the Arctic conditions swept in have lost refrigerated groceries due to lengthy power cuts and cannot cook what food they do have without electricity or gas.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/18/texas-food-banks-crisis-storm-freezing-supplies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 'This is a disaster': Texas faces dwindling food supplies amid Arctic conditions}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19ve ever wondered what it was like to serve \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at the Trump hotel, Jessica Sidman at Washingtonian magazine has answers. Sidman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonian.com/2021/02/19/trump-hotel-employees-tell-all-what-it-was-really-like-serving-right-wing-elite/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 got her hands}}}\uc2  on a \u8220\'20\'1CStandard Operating Procedure\u8221\'20\'1D document for serving the now-former president:\par \par \uc2 As soon as Trump was seated, the server had to \u8220\'20\'1Cdiscreetly present\u8221\'20\'1D a mini bottle of Purell hand sanitizer. (This applied long before Covid, mind you.) Next, cue dialogue: \u8220\'20\'1CGood (time of day) Mr. President. Would you like your Diet Coke with or without ice?\u8221\'20\'1D the server was instructed to recite. A polished tray with chilled bottles and highball glasses was already prepared for either response. Directions for pouring the soda were detailed in a process no fewer than seven steps long\u8212\'20\'14and illustrated with four photo exhibits. The beverage had to be opened in front of the germophobe commander in chief, \u8220\'20\'1Cnever beforehand.\u8221\'20\'1D The server was to hold a longneck-bottle opener by the lower third of the handle in one hand and the Diet Coke, also by the lower third, in the other. Once poured, the drink had to be placed at the President\u8217\'20\'19s right-hand side. \u8220\'20\'1CRepeat until POTUS departs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Trump children were easier, Sidman writes:\par \par \uc2 By contrast, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s children were fairly low-key and polite. (The most salacious detail any former staff offered about Ivanka is that one time she showed up in yoga pants and indulged in a single margarita.) \u8220\'20\'1CThey just came in, did their thing, and left,\u8221\'20\'1D says former assistant general manager Alyssa O\u8217\'20\'19Clock. \u8220\'20\'1CIvanka would sit with her back to the rest of the dining room. She didn\u8217\'20\'19t really want to be seen there, necessarily.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s hard not to at least pay a little attention o the fallout of senator Ted Cruz of Texas\u8217\'20\'19s poorly timed escape to Cancun. Plenty of backlash is pouring out online. As The Washington Post\u8217\'20\'19s Ashley Parker {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/ted-cruz-cancun-storm/2021/02/19/ce1dc25e-7252-11eb-93be-c10813e358a2_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted}}}\uc2 , Cruz has gained new nicknames:\par \par \uc2 But his brief tropical sojourn yielded at least two unflattering nicknames on social media \u8212\'20\'14 Cancun Cruz and Flyin\u8217\'20\'19 Ted \u8212\'20\'14 and prompted a \uc2 Twitter\uc2 -fueled news cycle that seemed to unite a broken nation.\par \par \uc2 [...]\par \par \uc2 Cancun-gate checked nearly every possible box of a scandal. The sad-sack black roller suitcase and oversize canvas tote, awaiting its beach debut! The fleece half-zip as part of the classic frumpy Dad ensemble! The 6 a.m. scramble to book a return flight! The politician seeming to blame his preteen daughters! The adorable family dog, possibly left home alone! The police escort! The leaked text messages, with a \u8220\'20\'1CReal Housewives of Houston\u8221\'20\'1D mood!\par \par \uc2 Cruz hasn\u8217\'20\'19t tweeted in about 11 hours and the last tweet he published was him promising to fight to restore power back to Texas.\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19m making sure we do everything we can to get the power turned on in Texas and to make sure this never happens again. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/aSrrZuFjNl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/aSrrZuFjNl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ted Cruz (@tedcruz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tedcruz/status/1362596251544477696?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 19, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Texas Tribune has a must-read story this morning on how Black and Hispanic communities are suffering through the storm. Here\u8217\'20\'19s are the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2021/02/19/Texas-winter-storm-suffering-inequities/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 key lines}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Low-income Texans of color bore some of the heaviest weight of the power outages as the inequities drawn into the state\u8217\'20\'19s urban centers were exacerbated in crisis. And already more impacted by unemployment and devastation of the pandemic, their troubles won\u8217\'20\'19t end after the storm clears and the heat is running again in their homes.\par \par \uc2 As temperatures dropped into single digits in Austin, electricity was kept on in neighborhoods sharing circuits with critical facilities like hospitals \u8212\'20\'14 facilities less commonly found in poor communities or those whose residents are predominantly Black and Hispanic.\par \par \uc2 [...]\par \par \uc2 Local leaders, particularly those representing mostly Black and Hispanic communities, pointed out that neighborhoods with mostly Black and Hispanic residents tend to have older homes with bad insulation, leaking roofs and older pipes that make them less likely to withstand extreme weather. In the case of Almendarez, this has led to power bills of up to $500 during the summer.\par \par \uc2 With the state\u8217\'20\'19s food supply chain also buckling under the storm\u8217\'20\'19s strain, those local leaders are worried about the fallout for areas that lack grocery stores and pharmacies. Plummer said during the storm, the few store shelves in those neighborhoods emptied fast and older people had trouble finding medication.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ted Cruz facces backlash over Canc\u250\'00\'FAn trip as millions face power shortages\par \par \uc2 Hello from Washington and happy Friday.\par \par \uc2 Daniel Strauss here. All eyes in the US are on Texas, which is still suffering power and resource shortages. Across the state, millions of Texans are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2021/02/19/texas-winter-storm-power-outage-ercot/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 without heat}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-cities-under-boil-water-orders-11613671450?mod=hp_lead_pos5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 safe drinking water}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dallasnews.com/news/weather/2021/02/19/thousands-of-outages-remain-in-north-texas-substantial-amount-of-power-to-be-restored-by-friday-e/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 and power}}}\uc2  as winter storms ravage the state.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Senator Ted Cruz of Texas is still facing backlash over traveling to Canc\u250\'00\'FAn with his family to escape the weather.\par \par \uc2 Last night, news outlets began to report out a text chain that Heidi Cruz, the senator\u8217\'20\'19s wife, was on showing how she was looking to spearhead the trip to Canc\u250\'00\'FAn with her family.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the write-up from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/02/18/us/politics/ted-cruz-storm-cancun.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The New York Times}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Text messages sent from Ms. Cruz to friends and Houston neighbors on Wednesday revealed a hastily planned trip. Their house was \u8220\'20\'1CFREEZING,\u8221\'20\'1D as Ms. Cruz put it \u8212\'20\'14 and she proposed a getaway until Sunday. Ms. Cruz invited others to join them at the \uc2 Ritz-Carlton\uc2  in Canc\u250\'00\'FAn, where they had stayed \u8220\'20\'1Cmany times,\u8221\'20\'1D noting the room price this week ($309 per night) and its good security. The text messages were provided to The \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and confirmed by a second person on the thread, who declined to be identified because of the private nature of the texts.\par \par \uc2 For what it\u8217\'20\'19s worth, governor Greg Abbott of Texas digressed when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.statesman.com/videos/news/2021/02/19/texas-governor-abbott-senator-ted-cruz-cancun-trip-weather-power-outage-crisis/4499683001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked}}}\uc2  about the senator\u8217\'20\'19s trip.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI haven\u8217\'20\'19t been following people\u8217\'20\'19s vacation plans,\u8221\'20\'1D Abbott said at a press conference. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve been working literally all night since we talked to you guys yesterday. And today \u8211\'20\'13 I don\u8217\'20\'19t know about people\u8217\'20\'19s travel plans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Abbott also has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.houstonchronicle.com/politics/texas/article/Gov-Greg-Abbott-urges-lawmakers-to-mandate-Texas-15961639.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  on lawmakers in the state to order power plants to be better prepared for weather emergencies.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 2021-02-19T14:27:55Z 2021-02-20T01:23:50Z {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/86372474d992a6216b8c4c86e110fb68dda8bcd3/0_0_3000_1801/500.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/86372474d992a6216b8c4c86e110fb68dda8bcd3/0_0_3000_1801/500.jpg}}}\uc2  Mark Majkrzak gives out bottles of water to people in need on Friday in Austin, Texas.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210219eh2j0028o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
