\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump impeachment: defense wraps up, claiming free speech is at stake \u8211\'20\'13as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now), Adam Gabbatt and Martin Belam (earlier) \par \uc2 11,625 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 February 2021\par 01:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lawyers say \u8216\'20\'18President Trump did not incite the horrific violence\u8217\'20\'19Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team relies heavily on videos of Democrats saying \u8216\'20\'18fight\u8217\'20\'19\u8216\'20\'18Accomplice\u8217\'20\'19 senators who amplified Trump lies now get a say in his fateSenate hears how Trump stoked Capitol assault over yearsDemocrats rest case with warning that Trump remains a threat\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap, from me and Adam Gabbatt:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legal team laid out their defense argument in the impeachment trial. The former president\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers said he was protected by the right to free speech.\par \par \uc2 * Lawyers for Trump played a video showing out-of-context clips of Democratic lawmakers \u8211\'20\'13 and for some reason, Madonna \u8211\'20\'13 using the word \u8220\'20\'1Cfight\u8221\'20\'1D repeatedly. They then accused Democrats of hypocrisy for criticizing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech to supporters on 6 January, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/12/trump-impeachment-video-democrats-fight-ridicule"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faced ridicule}}}\uc2  for an argument that amounted to peak whataboutism.\par \par \uc2 * Before adjourning for the night, the Senate unanimously approved awarding officer Eugene Goodman with a gold medal for his bravery during the 6 January attack. \u8220\'20\'1COfficer Goodman is in the chamber tonight. Officer Goodman, thank you,\u8221\'20\'1D said Chuck Schumer, before senators stood to applaud the officer.\par \par \uc2 The impeachment trial resumes tomorrow \u8211\'20\'13 come back for live Guardian coverage.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 Report: Trump berated House Republican leader while Capitol was under seige\par \par \uc2 Based on interviews with multiple Republicans briefed on the matter, CNN is reporting new details about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s call to House Republican leader Kevin McCarthy to castigate him during the 6 January attack on the Capitol.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/02/12/politics/trump-mccarthy-shouting-match-details/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 From CNN}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 In an expletive-laced phone call with House Republican leader Kevin McCarthy while the Capitol was under attack, then-President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said the rioters cared more about the election results than McCarthy did.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWell, Kevin, I guess these people are more upset about the election than you are,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, according to lawmakers who were briefed on the call afterward by McCarthy. McCarthy insisted that the rioters were Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters and begged Trump to call them off. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comment set off what Republican lawmakers familiar with the call described as a shouting match between the two men. A furious McCarthy told the President the rioters were breaking into his office through the windows, and asked Trump, \u8220\'20\'1CWho the f--k do you think you are talking to?\u8221\'20\'1D according to a Republican lawmaker familiar with the call.\par \par \uc2 The newly revealed details of the call, described to CNN by multiple Republicans briefed on it, provide critical insight into the President\u8217\'20\'19s state of mind as rioters were overrunning the Capitol. The existence of the call and some of its details have been previously reported and discussed publicly by McCarthy. The Republican members of Congress said the exchange showed Trump had no intention of calling off the rioters even as lawmakers were pleading with him to intervene. Several said it amounted to a dereliction of his presidential duty.\par \par \uc2 Read more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/02/12/politics/trump-mccarthy-shouting-match-details/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 Analysis: Fight, fight, fight: Trump lawyers subject senators to repetitive strain\par \par \uc2 Fight, fight, fight, fight, fight, fight, fight, fight, fight, fight. The first rule of Fight Club is just keep bashing your audience with the same word ad nauseam.\par \par \uc2 A video in which \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and other Democratic politicians uttered the word \u8220\'20\'1Cfight\u8221\'20\'1D 238 times, according to a count by the MSNBC TV network, was the most bizarre turn yet at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s impeachment trial.\par \par \uc2 The montage was played by Trump lawyer David Schoen on Friday in an attempt to demonstrate that such language is common in today\u8217\'20\'19s political discourse, and protected by the first amendment to the constitution, so Trump\u8217\'20\'19s call for his supporters to \u8220\'20\'1Cfight like hell\u8221\'20\'1D should not be blamed for the insurrection at the US Capitol.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou didn\u8217\'20\'19t do anything wrong,\u8221\'20\'1D Schoen told senators, many of whom had seen themselves on TV screens inside the chamber. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a word people use, but please stop the hypocrisy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He was not wrong that it\u8217\'20\'19s a word people use. \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , who was seen in the video, made Fight Song the theme of her ill-starred 2016 campaign against Trump. The world champion \u8220\'20\'1Cfighter\u8221\'20\'1D is surely Senator Elizabeth Warren, who sprinkles the word in interviews liberally and wrote a book called This Fight is Our Fight.\par \par \uc2 But what Schoen was also doing was displaying whataboutism in its purest form \u8211\'20\'13 a wonder to behold, like a flawless diamond or pristine snow.\par \par \uc2 Whataboutism is a dodge often seen in rightwing media. If allegations are made against Trump\u8217\'20\'19s connections in Russia, respond: what about Clinton\u8217\'20\'19s emails? If Trump\u8217\'20\'19s family are accused of exploiting their position, respond: what about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s son Hunter? If white supremacists are running riot, respond: what about antifa? It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t matter if the equivalence is false because it\u8217\'20\'19s all about attacking the opponent in order to muddy the waters.\par \par \uc2 The Trump legal team\u8217\'20\'19s relentless \u8220\'20\'1Cfight\u8221\'20\'1D video was a case in point. Some of the Democrats were quoted out of context due to selective editing. We heard Biden, for example, say \u8220\'20\'1Cnever, never, never give up this fight\u8221\'20\'1D but did not hear the full quotation: \u8220\'20\'1CI looked into the eyes of people who survived school shootings, and I made each of them a promise: I will never, never, never give up this fight.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 (Speaking of hypocrisy, Schoen accused the impeachment managers of \u8220\'20\'1Cmanipulating video\u8221\'20\'1D during his presentation.)\par \par \uc2 In addition, these Democrats were urging supporters to fight for a political cause. Trump was urging supporters to fight against democracy: his cause was based on the mendacious claim of a stolen election. And as the impeachment managers laid out on Thursday, he had spent years deploying incendiary rhetoric and demonising opponents.\par \par \uc2 Still, the Trump defence cleared the very low bar set by their opening Laurel-and-Hardy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/09/trump-impeachment-trial-lawyers-bruce-castor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gambit on Tuesday}}}\uc2 . On Friday they provided talking points for rightwing media, straws for Republican consciences to clutch at and a boost for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s spirits after some very grim days.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/12/trump-impeachment-lawyers-fight-video-whataboutism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fight, fight, fight: Trump lawyers subject senators to repetitive strain | David Smith's sketch}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senate honors Eugene Goodman, adjourns trial for the day\par \par \uc2 The Senate unanimously approved awarding officer Eugene Goodman with a gold medal for his bravery during the 6 January attack.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COfficer Goodman is in the chamber tonight. Officer Goodman, thank you,\u8221\'20\'1D said Chuck Schumer, before senators stood to applaud the officer.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on Goodman:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/20/eugene-goodman-capitol-police-officer-inauguration-hero"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Officer hailed as a hero in Capitol assault escorts Kamala Harris to inauguration}}}\par \par \uc2 The trial has adjourned until tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.51am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Bruce Castor has made yet another head-scratching argument:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no January exception to impeachment,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding that private citizens are subject to criminal prosecution.\par \par \uc2 This runs counter to the defense\u8217\'20\'19s argument that the trial is not constitutional. Castor also did not clarify whether Trump should face criminal charges.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Things got heated there for a minute.\par \par \uc2 Louisiana Senator \uc2 Bill Cassidy\uc2 , who has hinted at some mild hesitation in siding with most of his GOP colleagues to acquit Trump, asked about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tweets castigating Mike Pence, even after reports that Alabama senator Tommy Tuberville told Trump that Mike Pence had been pursued by rioters and evacuated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnfortunately we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to know the answer to the facts of this proceeding, because the House did nothing to investigate what went on,\u8221\'20\'1D said Van der Veen, without directly responding to the substance of the question.\par \par \uc2 Raskin did not appreciate that line of argument. \u8220\'20\'1CRather than yelling at us and screaming about, \u8216\'20\'18We didn\u8217\'20\'19t have time to get all of the facts about what your client did,\u8217\'20\'19 bring your client up here and have him testify under oath,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CRather than yelling at us and screaming about how we didn\u8217\'20\'19t have time to get all of the facts about what your client did, bring your client up here and have him testify under oath\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9AosuctWQp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/9AosuctWQp}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Acyn Torabi (@Acyn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Acyn/status/1360359190607261696?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Hi there, it\u8217\'20\'19s Maanvi Singh \u8211\'20\'13 taking over the blog.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s defense would not answer a question from Bernie Sanders on whether they believe Trump won the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy judgment. Who asked that? My judgment is irrelevant in this proceeding,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump attorney Van der Veen said.\par \par \uc2 enltrVan der Veen on Sanders question: "In my judgment, who asked that? My judgment is irrelevant." Leahy presiding then tells him Senators can't respond to the question. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Iw6QqVVqSK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Iw6QqVVqSK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Craig Caplan (@CraigCaplan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CraigCaplan/status/1360350646159966213?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Warren, Democratic senator from Massachusetts, asks a question. She notes that the defense pointed out that Democrats have objected to electoral college results before, and asks if they have ever done so hours after an insurrection at the Capitol?\par \par \uc2 enltrElizabeth Warren uses a question to body Hawley, Cruz, and other Republican who voted to throw out electoral votes after the insurrection {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MkjHGrKmK0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/MkjHGrKmK0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1360347848982855680?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 No one really answers it but Warren is getting a lot of fire emoji tweets on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator \uc2 Ed Markey\uc2  asks when Trump learned of the breach at the Capitol, and what he did about it. (It\u8217\'20\'19s the same question Collins and Murkowski asked earlier.)\par \par \uc2 Stacey Plaskett\uc2 , a House delegate from the Virgin Islands and an impeachment manager, says we do not know. \u8220\'20\'1CThe reason this question keeps coming up is because the answer is nothing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2 , Republican senator and Trump foe, asks if Trump knew whether Mike Pence had been removed from the Senate when the president criticized him in a 2.24pm tweet.\par \par \uc2 Defense lawyer Van der Veen says \u8220\'20\'1Cthe answer is no, at no point was the president informed that the vice president was in any danger\u8221\'20\'1D. Van der Veen then criticizes the House impeachment managers for rushing the trial.\par \par \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t see the connection.\par \par \uc2 enltrvan der Veen responds: "At no point was the president informed the vice president was in any danger."\par \par \uc2 Says the q is irrelevant: "This is an article of impeachment for incitement."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Eli Stokols (@EliStokols) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EliStokols/status/1360341121923227651?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWhich is untrue of course. And then van der Veen went on to argue that even if Trump did recklessly endanger the life of VP Pence, it's nobody's business. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cdC4kN81cy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/cdC4kN81cy}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Frum (@davidfrum) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/davidfrum/status/1360341076339474432?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican senator Tim Scott has a question: \u8220\'20\'1CIsn\u8217\'20\'19t this simply a political show trial that is designed to discredit President Trump [...] and shame the 74m Americans who voted for him?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bruce Castor, for the defense: \u8220\'20\'1CThats precisely what the 45th president believes this is about.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Castor says the purpose of the trial \u8211\'20\'13 which is actually related to an insurrection that left five people dead \u8211\'20\'13 is to \u8220\'20\'1Cembarrass\u8221\'20\'1D Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A question for the defense team, from GOP senators Susan Collins and Lisa Murkowski:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CExactly when did President Trump learn of the breach of the Capitol \u8221\'20\'1D and what actions did he take to bring the riot to an end?\par \par \uc2 Van der Veen, for the defense, doesn\u8217\'20\'19t give a proper answer.\par \par \uc2 enltrWoah. Trump lawyer can\u8217\'20\'19t answer it. At all. He just rants about the lack of due process. Seems to me this would be the first thing I would ask if I were Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer while getting ready. Devastating silence.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Neal Katyal\uc2  (@neal_katyal) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/neal_katyal/status/1360335901558263816?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Collins and Murkowski are believed to be swing voters on whether to convict Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  has a question for the defense. The question is on behalf of Graham, Senator Ted Cruz, and others \u8211\'20\'13 all ardent Trump defenders.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDoes a politician raising bail for rioters encourage more rioting?\u8221\'20\'1D the defense is asked.\par \par \uc2 One of the defense lawyers \u8211\'20\'13 I think it\u8217\'20\'19s Castor says: \u8220\'20\'1CYes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This is part of the Republican strategy to compare the Capitol rioters to Black Lives Matter protesters.\par \par \uc2 enltrOf course {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LindseyGrahamSC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @LindseyGrahamSC}}}\uc2  uses his question to throw a bomb at Black Lives Matter who are who he means when he says "rioters." (Narrator: BLM protesters were not "rioters," and insurrectionist \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  would fit in perfectly in the Confederacy.)\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joy WE VOTED!! WEAR A MASK!! Reid ??) (@JoyAnnReid) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoyAnnReid/status/1360334142978850819?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIsn\u8217\'20\'19t it the case that the attack [on January 6] would not have happened if not for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ?\u8221\'20\'1D was the first, strangely worded question. It\u8217\'20\'19s posed by Democratic senators to the House impeachment managers (essentially, the prosecution.)\par \par \uc2 Rep Joaquin Castro\uc2 , one of the impeachment managers, answered. Castro said \u8211\'20\'13 essentially \u8211\'20\'13 yes.\par \par \uc2 He said Trump, as far back as mid-December, directed his supporters to travel to the Capitol on January 6. Once there, Trump told his supporters to \u8220\'20\'1Cfight like hell\u8221\'20\'1D, and told them \u8220\'20\'1Cthey could play by different rules\u8221\'20\'1D, Castro said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The impeachment trial has restarted shortly. In the next phase, Senators will have four hours to ask the defense and the prosecution questions.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not clear how late they\u8217\'20\'19ll run tonight. There\u8217\'20\'19s a dinner break scheduled for 5pm, but the questioning could resume after. The Senate will reconvene at 10am ET Saturday, and a final vote could take place later that day, at 3pm.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team has wrapped up its defense\par \par \uc2 That was a bit of an anti-climax. Castor finished by pivoting back to the free speech argument Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers made earlier \u8211\'20\'13 that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech to his supporters on January 6 was protected under the first amendment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis trial is about far more than President Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D Castor said. He said the trial is instead about canceling speech that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe majority does not agree with\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAre we going to allow canceling and silencing to be sanctioned in this body?\u8221\'20\'1D Castor asked.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s defense argument seems to hinge both on a) Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech on January 6 did not incite the riot (although the defense team did not address Trump\u8217\'20\'19s previous statements) and b) in any case, what Trump said is protected by free speech laws.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Castor suggested that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech on January 6 did not incite the riot\par \par \uc2 The lawyer hasn\u8217\'20\'19t addressed the broader issue of whether Trump\u8217\'20\'19s months-long tirade against the election result had anything to do with it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe January 6 speech did not cause the riots,\u8221\'20\'1D Castor said.\par \par \uc2 Castor then moved onto the January phone call between Trump and Georgia secretary of state \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 . During that call {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/trump-raffensperger-call-georgia-vote/2021/01/03/d45acb92-4dc4-11eb-bda4-615aaefd0555_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump pressured Raffensperger}}}\uc2 , a Republican, to \u8220\'20\'1Cfind\u8221\'20\'1D votes so that Trump could be announced the winner in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Georgia prosecutors have opened a criminal inquiry into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s call.\par \par \uc2 Castor read from a transcript of the call and said Trump was expressing legitimate concern over the election result.\par \par \uc2 For some context, here is some of what Trump said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/trump-raffensperger-call-transcript-georgia-vote/2021/01/03/2768e0cc-4ddd-11eb-83e3-322644d82356_story.html?itid=lk_interstitial_manual_10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in that Georgia phone call}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo look. All I want to do is this. I just want to find 11,780 votes, which is one more than we have. Because we won the state.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Bruce Castor continues. He says the House impeachment managers \u8220\'20\'1Cmanipulated\u8221\'20\'1D Trump\u8217\'20\'19s words when they presented their case.\par \par \uc2 Castor then speaks Latin for a little bit and suggests House impeachment managers are \u8220\'20\'1Ctrying to fool you\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump was immediate in his calls for calm,\u8221\'20\'1D Castor says. (Trump wasn\u8217\'20\'19t.)\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump\u8217\'20\'19s words couldn\u8217\'20\'19t have incited the events at the capitol,\u8221\'20\'1D Castor said, because people were already gathering at the Capitol before Trump gave his speech at the Ellipse, which a 15 minute walk away.\par \par \uc2 enltrCastor -- the lawyer who's rambling, unfocused opening statement on Tuesday enraged Trump -- begins by going over ground argued earlier, and showing the same clips.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Trip Gabriel (@tripgabriel) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tripgabriel/status/1360315618684268545?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewDesiderio/status/1360315113731989504"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://twitter.com/AndrewDesiderio/status/1360315113731989504}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrDOJ has specifically referred to the events of Jan. 6 as an insurrection. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/msWzru3fXd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/msWzru3fXd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Desiderio (@AndrewDesiderio) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewDesiderio/status/1360315113731989504?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump's lawyers are arguing that he is not guilty because 1. The trial is unconstitutional 2. The trial is politically motivated 3. Trump's use of word "fight" and other language was ordinary political talk 4. Trump loves law and order. Our full coverage: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/RMwlZdYR56"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/RMwlZdYR56}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Eliza Collins (@elizacollins1) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/elizacollins1/status/1360315395677315073?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Castor began his defense by showing a video, most of which is cribbed from the video Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team played earlier.\par \par \uc2 It contrasts Democrats defending Black Lives Matter protesters, spliced in with selected clips of violence at some of the BLM demonstrations, with Trump talking about \u8220\'20\'1Claw and order\u8221\'20\'1D. Law and order is frequently used as a racist dog whistle.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJanuary 6 was a terrible day for our country,\u8221\'20\'1D Castor conceded, but he continued: \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump did not incite or cause the horrific violence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This tactic from the defense \u8211\'20\'13 that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters storming the Capitol was bad, but it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t Trump\u8217\'20\'19s fault \u8211\'20\'13 is something we expected.\par \par \uc2 Castor added: \u8220\'20\'1CPolitical hatred has no place in the American justice system, and certainly no place in the \uc2 congress of the United States\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legal team has resumed their defense. Bruce Castor, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/02/09/us/politics/trump-bruce-castor-david-schoen.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly left Trump furious}}}\uc2  after a lackluster performance earlier this week, will handle the next section.\par \par \uc2 During the break, Democratic senators lined up to pan the defense.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was told that if he didn\u8217\'20\'19t stop lying about the election people would be killed,\u8221\'20\'1D Senator Tim Kaine told reporters, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2021/02/12/trump-impeachment-trial-live-updates/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Washington Post}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CHe wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t stop, and the Capitol was attacked and seven people are dead who would be alive today.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Senator Richard J. Blumenthal said the Trump defense team is \u8220\'20\'1Ctrying to draw a false, dangerous and distorted equivalence\u8221\'20\'1D, the Post reported.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I think it is plainly a distraction from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s inviting the mob to Washington, knowing it was armed; changing the route and the timing so as to incite them to march on the Capitol; and then reveling, without remorse, without doing anything to protect his own vice president and all of us,\u8221\'20\'1D Blumenthal said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think that the case is even more powerful after this very distorted and false argument.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Afternoon summary\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legal team has set out their defense in the former president\u8217\'20\'19s second impeachment trial.\par \par \uc2 * The defense has centered largely on two themes: that Trump is protected by the right to free speech, and that Democrats are guilty of hypocrisy.\par \par \uc2 * Lawyers for Trump played a video showing various Democrats using the word \u8220\'20\'1Cfight\u8221\'20\'1D, as they accused Democrats of hypocrisy for criticizing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech to supporters on 6 January.\par \par \uc2 * The video, or a version of it, was played at least four times by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team. But the film lacked key context \u8211\'20\'13 at no point were Democrats speaking to an angry, pugnacious crowd, and at no point did those Democrats urge their supporters to march on the US Capitol.\par \par \uc2 * In a separate argument, lawyers seemed to suggest that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech, whether it was dangerous or not, was protected by the first amendment.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not for me to say Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have run out of ideas, but we\u8217\'20\'19ve now seen the fight video, or a version of it, at least four times.\par \par \uc2 The video cuts crucial context from Democrat\u8217\'20\'19s remarks. Trump discussed fighting on January 6 after he had whipped up a crowd with false claims of election fraud, then he urged them to march on the US Capitol, where he implied more fraud was about to occur.\par \par \uc2 None of the Democrats ever did that.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Van der Veen is quoting former Associate Justice \uc2 James Wilson\uc2 , who died in 1798, then loops in some of the other \u8216\'20\'18founding fathers\u8217\'20\'19. He is still on the subject of freedom of speech.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the house managers had their way they would ignore all of the constitution,\u8221\'20\'1D Van der Veen said. He then added something about the impeachment being \u8220\'20\'1Canti-American\u8221\'20\'1D, and moved on to quoting case law from the 1960s.\par \par \uc2 enltrThis argument is dumb. Conduct can be generally "constitutional" while also being disruptive to the *constitutional order.*\par \par \uc2 Trump incited the violent disruption of the *constitutional process* by which our elections conclude.\par \par \uc2 It doesn't matter if the speech itself is protected.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Greg Sargent (@ThePlumLineGS)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ThePlumLineGS/status/1360295762199007233?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a little more on Van der Veen, who is usually a personal-injury lawyer:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump lawyer Michael T. van der Veen, speaking right now, once sued Trump, citing "an environment subject to repeated claims by President \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  that voting by mail is ripe with fraud, despite having no evidence in support of these claims" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2m9Nmb4TCn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/2m9Nmb4TCn}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Tapper (@jaketapper) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jaketapper/status/1360274675637624832?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Warren, the Democratic senator from Massachusetts, is among those using the word \u8220\'20\'1Cfight\u8221\'20\'1D in this video that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team keeps rolling out. Here\u8217\'20\'19s some context:\par \par \uc2 enltrGiven how much Warren footage we just watched, it feels worthwhile to point out: I covered Warren's campaign for over a year. Every day was about "why she's in this fight." For policy. It's laughable to think anyone ever thought she was urging people towards physical violence.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ali Vitali (@alivitali) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/alivitali/status/1360285277877637125?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 More video! Trump\u8217\'20\'19s defense team plays clips of Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 and, weirdly, Madonna \u8211\'20\'13 using pugnacious language. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s always curious claim that he\u8217\'20\'19d like to take Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cbehind the gym\u8221\'20\'1D is included.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not what about-ism,\u8221\'20\'1D Van der Veen said. \u8220\'20\'1CI show you this video because all robust speech must be protected.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That video was almost identical to the two videos Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have already shown.\par \par \uc2 Van der Veen then showed the text of the first amendment on a big screen. The free speech part of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s defense continues.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 This happened at Mar-a-Lago, the private club where Trump is living, apparently indefinitely:\par \par \uc2 enltrMinutes before his lawyers begin their defense, a banner flew over Trump's Mar-a-Lago reading: "CONVICT TRUMP AND LOCK HIM UP" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LMMjsw9B3s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LMMjsw9B3s}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Allie Malloy (@AlliemalCNN) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AlliemalCNN/status/1360273220239298566?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Michael Van der Veen, the Trump lawyer who kicked things off for the defense, has returned to the podium.\par \par \uc2 Van der Veen brought up the \u8220\'20\'1Cfree speech\u8221\'20\'1D defense that we heard Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team would use.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMr Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech deserves full protection under the first amendment,\u8221\'20\'1D Van der Veen said.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, a Republican senator has apparently just {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/politics/live-news/trump-impeachment-trial-02-12-2021/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN}}}\uc2  there is \u8220\'20\'1Creal concern\u8221\'20\'1D about the quality of the Trump team\u8217\'20\'19s defense today:\par \par \uc2 The senator, who has been among those paying far closer attention to the proceedings in the chamber than many colleagues, said there is no question the House impeachment managers\u8217\'20\'19 presentation will almost certainly be stronger that the defense presentation. But the senator said Republicans hope the defense is presented \u8220\'20\'1Cin a professional and serious way \u8211\'20\'13 unlike the rambling show\u8221\'20\'1D from the first day of the trial.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 More video from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team, as the defense ticks past the one hour mark.\par \par \uc2 This video shows clips from Black Lives Matter protests over the summer. It\u8217\'20\'19s another attempt to compare protests against racism to a bunch of Trump supporters smashing their way into the US Capitol and threatening to kill politicians.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s some takes on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltrA reminder that Schoen was on Fox News this week where he said that only Trump had a base that would actually be riled up by language about fighting! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Jk3fl16wUe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Jk3fl16wUe}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Philip Bump (@pbump)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/pbump/status/1360285733316157451?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrSchoen has made serious accusations of fraud and deceit against the House Impeachment Managers.\par \par \uc2 He better have receipts, because what he has shown thus far is not even close.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Katie S. Phang (@KatiePhang)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KatiePhang/status/1360282819654807554?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrJust after Schoen accused Managers of "manipulating" evidence because they took excerpts of videos, he shows a lengthy video of numerous, extremely spliced video clips without any context for the comments.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Daniel Goldman (@danielsgoldman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/danielsgoldman/status/1360286325728022528?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team has played another video. The video, like one earlier, shows a number of Democrats using the word \u8220\'20\'1Cfight\u8221\'20\'1D during political interviews and at rallies.\par \par \uc2 A key difference is that none of the Democrats used the word fight as they amped up their supporters then urged them to march to the US Capitol, where the result of a presidential election was about to be formalized. In some cases the Democrats were talking about fighting for policy changes or fighting for healthcare coverage. (Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team clipped out those bits, just leaving the word \u8216\'20\'18fight\u8217\'20\'19.)\par \par \uc2 The Trump legal case so far seems to be: a) Democrats rushed the impeachment hearing, which seems irrelevant, b) the impeachment is unconstitutional, which is wrong, and c) some Democrats have used the word sometimes used the word \u8220\'20\'1Cfight\u8221\'20\'1D, but \u8211\'20\'13 as far as I can tell \u8211\'20\'13 none of them ever used the word in the same volatile circumstances Trump faced on January 6.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Schoen, being done no favors by the top-down camera angle in the Senate chamber, continued to talk about the second impeachment of Trump being rushed. He claims impeachment managers \u8220\'20\'1Cmanufactured evidence\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He claimed that two tweets, gathered by House impeachment managers as evidence that rioters were incited by Trump, were not posted on January 6. This is kind of irrelevant, because those tweets \u8211\'20\'13 as Schoen pointed out \u8211\'20\'13 were not part of the impeachment managers\u8217\'20\'19 case.\par \par \uc2 Schoen then plays longer versions of Trump videos that impeachment managers played. Schoen claimed that impeachment managers cut the videos to remove context.\par \par \uc2 One video showed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s infamous \u8220\'20\'1Cvery fine people on both sides\u8221\'20\'1D remarks about a white supremacist rally in Charlottesville. I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure the longer video helps Trump\u8217\'20\'19s case.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s defense attorney David Schoen. Photograph: \uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 David Schoen said he wants to discuss the \u8220\'20\'1Chatred\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cvitriol\u8221\'20\'1D that Democrats have for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . He then proceeded to discuss neither.\par \par \uc2 Schoen, who previously represented the one-time convict, and some-time Trump associate \uc2 Roger Stone\uc2 , instead suggested the impeachment was rushed.\par \par \uc2 The impeachment seeks to bar Trump from holding public office again, Schoen said, and also seeks to disenfranchise \u8220\'20\'1C75m voters\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Schoen then complained that the previously unseen footage Democrats released yesterday \u8211\'20\'13 which showed members of Congress, and the vice-president, fleeing for their lives \u8211\'20\'13 should have been given to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team first.\par \par \uc2 Schoen continued with the theme that the impeachment was rushed. He played a clip showing impeachment managers quoting news reports as examples that evidence that Democrats cannot be trusted.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The impeachment case is \u8220\'20\'1Cpreposterously wrong on the facts\u8221\'20\'1D, Van der Veen said. He added, for the second time, that the impeachment trial is \u8220\'20\'1Cplainly unconstitutional\u8221\'20\'1D. (Again, the Senate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/02/09/us/politics/trump-impeachment-trial-senate.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including six Republicans}}}\uc2 , found this week that the trial is constitutional.)\par \par \uc2 This trial is \u8220\'20\'1Cconstitutional cancel culture\u8221\'20\'1D, Van der Veen said, a phrase that possibly sounded better in his head. Van der Veen then tags in his colleague, David Schoen.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Van der Veen, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer, posted a video mash up of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  calling for law and order at certain times over the past four years, contrasted with some Democrats using words like \u8220\'20\'1Cfight\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Van der Veen continued by claiming: \u8220\'20\'1COne of the first people arrested was the leader of Antifa.\u8221\'20\'1D Van der Veen was referring to the anti-facist movement that does not have a leader.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer continues by drawing a false equivalence between Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters seeking to attack politicians as they besieged the US Capitol, and Black Lives Matter protesters who have held demonstrations demanding equal rights and an end to racism.\par \par \uc2 Van der Veen blamed a \u8220\'20\'1Csmall group\u8221\'20\'1D for the riot, not Trump, and claimed most protesters on January 6 were peaceful.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Michael Van der Veen, a lawyer for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , kicked off Trump\u8217\'20\'19s defense by railing against the impeachment trial.\par \par \uc2 The trial, according to Van der Veen, is an \u8220\'20\'1Cunjust and blatantly unconstitutional act of political vengeance\u8221\'20\'1D. This argument overlooks the fact that the Senate, including a number of Republicans, voted at the start of the week that the trial is constitutional.\par \par \uc2 Anyway \u8211\'20\'13 the impeachment of Trump, who is accused of inciting an insurrection also \u8220\'20\'1Cfurther divides our nation\u8221\'20\'1D, Van der Veen said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo thinking person could seriously believe\u8221\'20\'1D Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech to his supporters on the morning of the Capitol riot \u8220\'20\'1Cwas in any way an incitement to violence or insurrection,\u8221\'20\'1D Van der Veen said. Democrats have argued the opposite.\par \par \uc2 Van der Veen said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe president\u8217\'20\'19s remarks explicitly encouraged those in attendance to exercise their rights peacefully and patriotically\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s defense team expected to push for swift conclusion of trial\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22The impeachment trial of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  continued on Friday, as lawyers for the president began to present their defense.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22That defense is not expected to last very long. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers are expected to use about four hours of their possible sixteen \u8211\'20\'13 apparently the defense team believe they have enough Republican votes to avoid a conviction.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22Lawyers for Trump will reportedly concede that Capitol riot was traumatic and unacceptable, but claim that Trump was not responsible for the actions of his supporters.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22House impeachment managers rested their case against Trump on Thursday. Democrats argued that the US Capitol riot was a direct result of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric, not just on January 6, but throughout his presidency.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22Joe Biden has been reluctant to weigh in on the impeachment, but said on Friday: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m just anxious to see what my Republican friends do, if they stand up.\u8221\'20\'1D Biden told reporters he did not plan to call any Republican senators.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence has \u8220\'20\'1Cno plans to condemn Trump or to speak out during the Senate impeachment trial\u8221\'20\'1D, the Washington Post {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2021/02/12/trump-impeachment-trial-live-updates/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reported}}}\uc2 , despite the near miss the former-vice president experienced on January 6.\par \par \uc2 Video shown by impeachment managers this week showed Pence fleeing as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters broke into the Capitol, but the close call was apparently not enough to spur Pence into action.\par \par \uc2 According to the Post:\par \par \uc2 [Pence] is still operating from a playbook of obsequiousness that has become second nature \u8212\'20\'14 never airing grievances publicly, and delivering his often rose-colored counsel to Trump only in private, one-on-one settings.\par \par \uc2 Pence has received praise from some for not attempting to break the law on January 6 \u8211\'20\'13 when he did not block the results of the presidential election. That praise seemingly overlooks Pence\u8217\'20\'19s four years of not doing anything in the face of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s most egregious policies.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As we gear up for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers to present their defense, here\u8217\'20\'19s a handy clip of congressman Jamie Raskin, the lead {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/11/trump-impeachment-managers-diverse-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 impeachment manager}}}\uc2 , making the case that Trump incited his supporters on January 6.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday Raskin wrapped up the House\u8217\'20\'19s case against the president, asking senators:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you think this is not impeachable, what is? What would be?\par \par \uc2 Raskin added: \u8220\'20\'1CIf you don\u8217\'20\'19t find this a high crime and misdemeanor today, you have set a new, terrible standard for presidential misconduct in the United States of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. Raskin: Trump HAS incited violence before. Roll the tape {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tpavGBooXG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/tpavGBooXG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NowThis (@nowthisnews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nowthisnews/status/1360240493062459395?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team will kick off their defense at 12pm ET, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/feb/12/donald-trump-impeachment-senate-trial-defense-lwayer-republican-senators-coronavirus-covid-live-updates?page=with:block-60265d868f08b555964bc750#block-60265d868f08b555964bc750"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are expected}}}\uc2  to wrap up their arguments today.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Some people online are getting very excited about events at the White House, where Jill Biden has installed some heart-shaped signs ahead of Valentine\u8217\'20\'19s Day.\par \par \uc2 enltrOvernight, the First Lady\u8217\'20\'19s surprise Valentine messages to the country were installed on the north lawn of the White House for the weekend! Happy Valentines, America...from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FLOTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @FLOTUS}}}\uc2  ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HPHjFbDfhD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/HPHjFbDfhD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Michael LaRosa (@MichaelLaRosa46)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MichaelLaRosa46/status/1360230245488619524?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Some of the signs bear traditional Valentine\u8217\'20\'19s messages like \u8220\'20\'1Clove\u8221\'20\'1D, but others have messages saying \u8220\'20\'1Cstrength\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Chealing\u8221\'20\'1D, possibly so single people don\u8217\'20\'19t feel left out.\par \par \uc2 If you like that kind of thing, here\u8217\'20\'19s a video of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , wearing jeans and a leather jacket, and Jill Biden, in smarter attire, walking among the signs this morning. Their dogs are there too:\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden: " {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/ValentinesDay?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #ValentinesDay}}}\uc2  is a big. Jill's favorite day. For real."\par \par \uc2 Q: "What inspired you to do this?" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FLOTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @FLOTUS}}}\uc2  : "I just wanted some joy. With the pandemic, just everybody's feeling a little down. So, it's just a little joy. A little hope. That's all." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JW0S1cclNO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JW0S1cclNO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1360215437427027969?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have injected \u8220\'20\'1Csearing criticism of Democrats\u8221\'20\'1D into their arguments, Associated Press reports \u8211\'20\'13 doing so at the behest of their client.\par \par \uc2 According to AP Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team is hoping \u8220\'20\'1Cto convince not only GOP senators but also viewers of the trial around the country that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second impeachment is fueled by \u8216\'20\'18hatred\u8217\'20\'19 of the former president\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 To that end the lawyers are expected to call out Democrats they say similarly incited violence in cities around the country.\par \par \uc2 We heard {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/feb/12/donald-trump-impeachment-senate-trial-defense-lwayer-republican-senators-coronavirus-covid-live-updates?page=with:block-602675b68f0886db2aba772e#block-602675b68f0886db2aba772e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier}}}\uc2  that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal defense will center on the argument that the former president had nothing to do with the riot itself, but lawyers for Trump also seemed determine to damage Democrats as much as possible as they lay out their arguments.\par \par \uc2 David Schoen, a member of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team, said he believed Democrats were effectively making the public relive the tragedy in a way that \u8220\'20\'1Ctears at the American people\u8221\'20\'1D and impedes efforts at unity, AP reported.\par \par \uc2 This is Adam Gabbatt taking over from Martin Belam.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Interior Department\uc2  will start consultations with Native American tribal leaders next month on Covid-19, economic security, racial justice and climate change, report Reuters. It is part of efforts py President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to get more tribal input in federal policy deliberations.\par \par \uc2 Biden issued an executive order on 26 January aimed at strengthening relations between the federal government and Native American tribes.\par \par \uc2 The Interior Department, which oversees the country\u8217\'20\'19s tribal and federal lands, will be led by New Mexico Representative \uc2 Deb Haaland\uc2 , who would become the first Native American to head a cabinet-level agency if she is confirmed by Congress.\par \par \uc2 Some tribes felt sidelined after major decisions by former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration, such as approving the Dakota Access Pipeline and drastically {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2020/feb/06/trump-utah-national-parks-energy-development-drilling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reducing the size of the Bears Ears National Monument in Utah}}}\uc2  that had been created with input of an inter-tribal council.\par \par \uc2 A 2019 \uc2 Government Accountability Office\uc2  report found serious lapses in outreach to tribes, especially on infrastructure projects.\par \par \uc2 Native American tribes have also been hard hit by the coronavirus pandemic due to health disparities and higher rates of poverty. Under Trump tribes received $8 billion in coronavirus aid, but only after major delays caused by a legal dispute.\par \par \uc2 The consultations will take place by video in the week of March 8.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMeaningful consultations ensure we center Tribal voices as we address the health, economic, racial justice and climate crises \u8211\'20\'13 all of which disproportionately impact American Indian and Alaska Natives,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ann Marie Bledsoe Downes, the department\u8217\'20\'19s designated Tribal Governance Officer and Deputy Solicitor for Indian Affairs.\par \par \uc2 Haaland is awaiting her confirmation hearing, which has not yet been scheduled.\par \par \uc2 A few western state Republican senators have said they are likely to oppose her because of her support for policies like the Green New Deal championed by the progressive Left, but she is still expected to have enough support to be confirmed.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In states across the US legislation from Republican lawmakers seeking to undermine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights is on the move. For anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists, the goal has long been to challenge the supreme court decision that gave pregnant people the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  48 years ago: the landmark Roe versus Wade.\par \par \uc2 Each spring, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2016/01/last-five-years-account-more-one-quarter-all-abortion-restrictions-enacted-roe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 especially in the last decade}}}\uc2 , Republicans have introduced restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws tailored to challenge that supreme court precedent by creating test cases. In 1973, Roe versus Wade provided women with a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to the point the fetus can survive outside the womb, generally understood to be 24 weeks.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  restrictions investigate the outer limits of that right, by creating laws that provoke reproductive rights advocates to sue, and for courts to consider their legitimacy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe more ambitious a restriction the court upholds, that will greenlight even more restrictions in the states,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mary Ziegler, a Florida State University law professor whose recent book, \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in America: A Legal History, tracked the history of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most important \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cases.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we\u8217\'20\'19ve been seeing is not what anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lawmakers want, but it\u8217\'20\'19s been tailored to what they think the supreme court wants,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ziegler.\par \par \uc2 This effort is not meant to reflect the will of the majority of Americans, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2019/06/07/730183531/poll-majority-want-to-keep-abortion-legal-but-they-also-want-restrictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 77% of whom}}}\uc2  believe the supreme court should uphold Roe v Wade. The effort is meant to please a motivated, religious voter base, who have helped power Republican victories since the Reagan era. Trump played for the same \u8220\'20\'1Csocial conservatives\u8221\'20\'1D when vowing to appoint supreme court justices who would overturn Roe. But since Trump rose to power, exactly how to do that has become a vexing question for the Republican party.\par \par \uc2 Bills that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/may/22/iowa-anti-abortion-heartbeat-bill-passed-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , demand doctors perform the impossible and \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/nov/29/ohio-extreme-abortion-bill-reimplant-ectopic-pregnancy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reimplant\u8221\'20\'1D ectopic pregnancies}}}\uc2 , punish women and doctors under murder statutes and whose authors believe the fundamental legal principle of precedent should not apply to their cases have all shown up in state legislatures in the last couple years.\par \par \uc2 Bans in recent sessions have been \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely aggressive\u8221\'20\'1D, said Hillary Schneller, a senior staff attorney for the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights\uc2 , and who is now fighting a Mississippi law that could ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 15 weeks. The state has appealed to the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Recent bans have been, \u8220\'20\'1Csaying the quiet part out loud \u8211\'20\'13 that they\u8217\'20\'19re not just restriction \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they want to end access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  entirely\u8221\'20\'1D, said Schneller.\par \par \uc2 Read more of Jessica Glenza\u8217\'20\'19s report here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/feb/12/anti-abortion-activists-womens-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans employ new \u8216\'20\'18extremely aggressive\u8217\'20\'19 tactics to ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/feb/12/anti-abortion-activists-womens-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans employ new \u8216\'20\'18extremely aggressive\u8217\'20\'19 tactics to ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US fast food workers hold Black History Month strike to demand $15 an hour\par \par \uc2 Fast-food workers in 15 cities will hold a Black History Month strike on Tuesday to demand that the \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2 , \uc2 Burger King\uc2  and \uc2 Wendy\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  restaurant chains pay them $15 an hour.\par \par \uc2 The action comes as Congress prepares to debate a federal rise in the minimum wage to $15 from its current rate of $7.25, the first federal raise since 2009.\par \par \uc2 Workers in cities including Atlanta, Charleston, Chicago, Detroit, Houston and St Louis will be joined by home care and nursing home workers in support of a $15 minimum wage and the right to join a union.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  pledged to increase the minimum wage during his election campaign but has recently suggested the increase may not make it into the $1.9tn coronavirus relief package he is trying to push through Congress. Biden has said the increase is central to his pledge to narrow racial economic inequality.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis Black History Month, we have a chance to make our own history by winning a living wage of at least $15 an hour and lifting millions of families out of poverty,\u8221\'20\'1D said Taiwanna Milligan, a \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  worker from Charleston, South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Milligan added: \u8220\'20\'1CFor decades, \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  has made billions in profit off the backs of workers like me, paying us starvation wages. I\u8217\'20\'19m striking today because I need at least $15 an hour to survive and because I know the only way to make change is to stand up, speak out and demand it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more of Dominic Rushe\u8217\'20\'19s report here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/12/fast-food-workers-15-cities-black-history-month-strike-15-an-hour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US fast food workers hold Black History Month strike to demand $15 an hour}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/12/fast-food-workers-15-cities-black-history-month-strike-15-an-hour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US fast food workers hold Black History Month strikes to demand $15 an hour}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden has more important things on his mind than Valentine\u8217\'20\'19s Day, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/white-house/biden-prepares-move-next-phase-his-agenda-infrastructure-push-n1257567"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this report}}}\uc2  from Mike Memoli and Carol E. Lee at NBC News sets out:\par \par \uc2 Even before he has secured his first major legislative priority, President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is crafting the pitch for his second: an even larger spending plan that the White House is billing as the infrastructure package long sought by both parties.\par \par \uc2 Biden has already begun wooing Republicans over his infrastructure push, which is likely to be the focus of a historically late first address to Congress, probably sometime in March. But even as he courts Republican support, White House officials have already begun discussing the possibility of moving ahead without it, just as Democrats appear poised to do with pandemic relief.\par \par \uc2 Biden outlined a more than $2 trillion infrastructure plan during the presidential campaign, saying at the time that it would be the \u8220\'20\'1Clargest mobilization of public investment since World War II.\u8221\'20\'1D The plan and a similar framework that passed the Democratic-led House in the last Congress are the basis of what Biden will propose.\par \par \uc2 Beyond just repairs or new construction of roads and bridges, the plan included expanding broadband access, as well as an ambitious climate agenda.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/white-house/biden-prepares-move-next-phase-his-agenda-infrastructure-push-n1257567"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News \u8211\'20\'13 Biden prepares to move to next phase of his agenda with infrastructure push}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As well as Lunar New Year celebrations, this weekend also sees Valentine\u8217\'20\'19s Day, and Dr. Jill Biden has decorated one of the White House lawns for that, with hearts bearing messages like \u8216\'20\'18compassion\u8217\'20\'19, \u8216\'20\'18unity\u8217\'20\'19, \u8216\'20\'18healing\u8217\'20\'19 and \u8216\'20\'18love\u8217\'20\'19. The Bidens \u8211\'20\'13 and their dogs \u8211\'20\'13 have just been out to have a look at them.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden and First Lady Jill Biden walked out on the North Lawn of the White House this morning with their dogs, Champ and Major, to look at the Valentine's Day messages that Jill Biden had installed overnight. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/kFLc9wUply"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/kFLc9wUply}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kate Sullivan (@KateSullivanDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KateSullivanDC/status/1360216551501271042?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrValentine... Biden... dog {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/F2fUajmwqS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/F2fUajmwqS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Howard Mortman\uc2  (@HowardMortman)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HowardMortman/status/1360212926775390208?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump advisor: legal team expected to use just four hours today in Senate for defense\par \par \uc2 Two more little snippets of detail about the defense legal team\u8217\'20\'19s plans today, courtesy of Trump advisor Jason Miller appearing on Newsmax. Their presentation will last about four hours out of their possible sixteen, and Bruce Castor, a man whose performance was widely questioned on Tuesday, will get a do-over.\par \par \uc2 enltrJason Miller makes clear on Newsmax that Bruce Castor WILL have a speaking role today. He says his arguments are \u8220\'20\'1Ccrisper\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ctighter\u8221\'20\'1D and adds that the defense team reviewed their plan with Trump last night. They will go about four hours.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaitlan Collins (@kaitlancollins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins/status/1360207974204080135?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Though in-person gatherings might be limited across the world, millions are still celebrating Lunar New Year today and ushering in the year of the ox.\par \par \uc2 Based on a traditional calendar observed by China, South Korea, Vietnam and others, this year\u8217\'20\'19s new year and spring festival comes with its own specific significance. \u8220\'20\'1CThe ox, in Chinese culture, is a hardworking zodiac sign. It usually signifies movements so, hopefully, the world will be less static than last year and get moving again in the second half of the year,\u8221\'20\'1D said Thierry Chow, a Hong Kong-based feng shui master, in a CNN interview.\par \par \uc2 enltrHappy Lunar New Year!! The Year of the Ox ?????? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/khZ0Af6gk2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/khZ0Af6gk2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Andrew Yang\uc2 ???????? (@AndrewYang)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewYang/status/1360049766290370569?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, some are encouraging the celebration as a means of diplomacy. Australia\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister Scott Morrison encouraged federal politicians to celebrate the Lunar New Year to help foster good relationships with Chinese people in the country, despite ongoing political tension with Beijing, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.smh.com.au/politics/federal/important-opportunity-pm-urges-mps-to-celebrate-lunar-new-year-with-chinese-australians-20210202-p56yu3.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according}}}\uc2  to the Sydney Morning Herald.\par \par \uc2 Others are highlighting the recent racism and attacks against Asian American people in their posts about the festival.\par \par \uc2 enltrHappy Lunar New Year, Chinese New Year, T?t, and Seollal!?? Please remember that the United States has a history of violence and racism towards Asian Americans and we need to acknowledge that we are celebrating a holiday of people we systematically oppress. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/gu0ibyftL0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/gu0ibyftL0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Velo Librarian (@velolibrarian)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/velolibrarian/status/1360065182001627138?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Here in New York, organizations in the city {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gothamist.com/arts-entertainment/lunar-new-year-2021-the-year-of-the-ox-festivities-in-person-and-online"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are holding}}}\uc2  both in person and virtual events in a year like no other.\par \par \uc2 Lunar New Year decorations are displayed in Chinatown on the eve of the Lunar New Year in New York. Photograph: Spencer Platt/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump's laywers expected to concede violence was traumatic and unacceptable, but argue Trump had nothing to do with it\par \par \uc2 The Senate will reconvene today for the impeachment trial at noon EST (1700 GMT). Bearing in mind that he will almost certainly be acquitted by enough Republican senators to make it immaterial anyway, the Associated Press have this rundown on what to expect from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s defense team later today.\par \par \uc2 They report that after a prosecution case rooted in emotive, violent images from the Capitol siege, his lawyers will make a fundamental concession and agree that the violence that day was every bit as traumatic, unacceptable and illegal as Democrats say.\par \par \uc2 But, they will say, Trump had nothing to do with it.\par \par \uc2 The move is meant to blunt the visceral impact of the House Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 case and quickly pivot to what they see as the core \u8212\'20\'14 and more winnable in the public eye \u8212\'20\'14 issue of the trial: whether Trump can be held responsible for inciting the deadly 6 January riot.\par \par \uc2 The argument is likely to appeal to Republican senators who themselves want to be seen as condemning the violence without convicting the president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey haven\u8217\'20\'19t in any way tied it to Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D David Schoen, one of the president\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers, told reporters near the end of two full days of Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 arguments aimed at doing just that.\par \par \uc2 He had already previewed the essence of his argument on Tuesday, telling the Senate jurors: \u8220\'20\'1CThey don\u8217\'20\'19t need to show you movies to show you that the riot happened here. We will stipulate that it happened, and you know all about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats used the rioters\u8217\'20\'19 own videos and words from 6 January to pin responsibility on Trump. \u8220\'20\'1CWe were invited here,\u8221\'20\'1D said one. \u8220\'20\'1CTrump sent us,\u8221\'20\'1D said another. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19ll be happy. We\u8217\'20\'19re fighting for Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The prosecutors\u8217\'20\'19 goal was to cast Trump not as a bystander but rather as the \u8220\'20\'1Cinciter in chief\u8221\'20\'1D who spent months spreading falsehoods and revving up supporters to challenge the election.\par \par \uc2 But Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have made clear their position \u8211\'20\'13 that the only people responsible for the riot are the ones who actually stormed the building and who are now being prosecuted by the Justice Department.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Georgia officials investigate groups that mobilized Black voters in state crucial to election outcome\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  state election board referred two cases to prosecutors on Wednesday connected to organizations that helped mobilize a record number of voters in the state during the 2020 election, a move critics say is an intimidation effort.\par \par \uc2 One case involves the New Georgia Project (NGP), the group founded by \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  in 2014, that helps mobilize voters of color. In 2019, investigators allege, the group violated state law by not handing in 1,268 voter registration applications within the 10 days required under {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sos.ga.gov/admin/files/183-1-6-02_Code.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state rules}}}\uc2 . The named respondent in the matter is Senator \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 , who the group says was serving as the chairman of its board at the time, but was incorrectly listed on documents as the group\u8217\'20\'19s CEO, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/election-board-investigates-warnock-and-new-georgia-project/V4YRQNRIRVENTI4GVH2OY5SNQY/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Atlanta Journal-Constitution}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe February 10th State Election Board meeting was the first time NGP heard about the allegations regarding NGP\u8217\'20\'19s important voter registration work from 2019,\u8221\'20\'1D Nse Ufot, who has served as the group\u8217\'20\'19s CEO since 2014, said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have not received any information on this matter from the Secretary or any other Georgia official so we will have no further comment on the investigation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The episode marks the latest example of Republicans targeting the group. In 2014, Brian Kemp, then the state\u8217\'20\'19s top election official, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://slate.com/news-and-politics/2014/09/stacey-abrams-new-georgia-project-shocks-georgias-gop-republicans-fighting-minority-voter-drive-with-voter-suppression.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced an investigation}}}\uc2  into allegations of forged registration materials but found {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/news/state--regional-govt--politics/georgia-fraud-investigation-closed-state-hands-voter-cases-attorney-general/cww2jBoqgjkySI2twq9zOK/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no widespread wrongdoing}}}\uc2 . Late last year, the secretary of state, \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , a Republican, accused the group of soliciting people from outside of Georgia to register in the state \u8211\'20\'13 which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/dec/14/georgia-senate-runoffs-black-voters-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the group denied.}}}\par \par \uc2 Those investigations force the organization to allocate resources towards lawyers it says could otherwise be invested in voter registration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery dollar that we have to spend to defend ourselves against the nuisance and partisan investigations is a dollar that we aren\u8217\'20\'19t able to put into the field to register new voters and have high quality conversations about the power of their vote and the importance of this moment,\u8221\'20\'1D Ufot {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/dec/14/georgia-senate-runoffs-black-voters-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  told the Guardian}}}\uc2  last year.\par \par \uc2 Read more of Sam Levine\u8217\'20\'19s report here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/12/georgia-voting-rights-stacey-abrams"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Intimidation tactic\u8217\'20\'19: Georgia officials investigate groups that mobilized Black voters}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/12/georgia-voting-rights-stacey-abrams"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Intimidation tactic\u8217\'20\'19: Georgia officials investigate groups that mobilized Black voters}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Asylum-seekers waiting in Mexico to be allowed into US while cases proceed in reverse of Trump policy\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has announced its plans for tens of thousands of asylum-seekers waiting in Mexico for their next immigration court hearings to be allowed into the United States while their cases proceed.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press report that the first of an estimated 25,000 asylum-seekers in Mexico with active cases will be allowed in the United States on 19 February, authorities said. They plan to start slowly with two border crossings each processing up to 300 people a day and a third crossing taking fewer.\par \par \uc2 The move is a major step toward dismantling one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policies to deter asylum-seekers from coming to the US. About 70,000 asylum-seekers were enrolled in \u8220\'20\'1CRemain in Mexico,\u8221\'20\'1D officially called \u8220\'20\'1CMigrant Protection Protocols,\u8221\'20\'1D since it was introduced in January 2019.\par \par \uc2 On Biden\u8217\'20\'19s first day in office, the \uc2 Homeland Security Department\uc2  suspended the policy for new arrivals. Since then, some asylum-seekers picked up at the border have been released in the US. with notices to appear in court.\par \par \uc2 Biden is quickly making good on a campaign promise to end the policy, which exposed people to violence in Mexican border cities and made it extremely difficult for them to find lawyers and communicate with courts about their cases.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs President Biden has made clear, the \uc2 US government\uc2  is committed to rebuilding a safe, orderly, and humane immigration system,\u8221\'20\'1D said Homeland Security Secretary Alejandro Mayorkas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dhs.gov/news/2021/02/11/dhs-announces-process-address-individuals-mexico-active-mpp-cases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a statement}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThis latest action is another step in our commitment to reform immigration policies that do not align with our nation\u8217\'20\'19s values.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Homeland Security said the move \u8220\'20\'1Cshould not be interpreted as an opening for people to migrate irregularly to the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D Administration officials have said repeatedly that the vast majority of people who cross the border illegally are quickly expelled under a public health order in place since the pandemic struck in March\par \par \uc2 Hearings for people enrolled in \u8220\'20\'1CRemain in Mexico\u8221\'20\'1D have been suspended since June due to the pandemic. Getting word out on when to report to the border for release in the United States may prove a daunting job.\par \par \uc2 Homeland Security said it would soon announce a \u8220\'20\'1Cvirtual registration process\u8221\'20\'1D available online and by phone for people to learn where and when they should report. It urged asylum-seekers not to report to the border unless instructed.\par \par \uc2 Asylum-seekers will be tested for Covid-19 before entering the US.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.41am GMT\par \par \uc2 Alexander Bolton has some choice quotes from a Republican senator i {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/538565-even-with-acquittal-gop-sees-trial-ending-trumps-shot-at-future-office"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 n his piece for the Hill today}}}\uc2 . According to Bolton one senator, after watching day two of the House managers\u8217\'20\'19 presentation, said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt just makes you realize what an asshole \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There will be some who suggest for this to be a revelation now raises questions about what the senator was watching for the last four years. Bolton\u8217\'20\'19s piece outlines that while Trump will doubtless be acquitted, for some Republican senators, it does mean the possibility of any Trump comeback is dead in the water.\par \par \uc2 From the viewpoint of some Republican senators, the compelling case presented by House prosecutors carries a silver lining: It means they likely won\u8217\'20\'19t have to worry about Trump running for president again in three years, while at the same time eroding his influence in party politics more generally.\par \par \uc2 Several Republican senators became irate watching videos of the violence and chaos inside the Capitol on 6 January, including footage of police officers being called \u8220\'20\'1Cpigs\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ctraitors\u8221\'20\'1D and one officer screaming as he was crushed by rioters battering a police line.\par \par \uc2 Other Republican senators, even those who have indicated they will vote to acquit, say it would be a good thing if the impeachment trial helps distance the party from Trump, who has thoroughly dominated GOP politics over the past five years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t imagine the emotional reaction, the visceral reaction to what we saw today doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have people thinking, \u8216\'20\'18This is awful,\u8217\'20\'19 whatever their view is on whether the president ought to be impeached or convicted,\u8221\'20\'1D said another GOP senator. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat would stand out to my colleagues is there was no rescue, there was nothing that came to put an end to it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/538565-even-with-acquittal-gop-sees-trial-ending-trumps-shot-at-future-office"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Hill \u8211\'20\'13 Even with acquittal, GOP sees trial ending Trump\u8217\'20\'19s shot at future office}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 On the Covid front, this morning Politico note that the Biden administration have been taking a gentle approach towards states relaxing restrictions, even as experts warn that there are still dangers ahead. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/02/12/biden-white-house-govenors-coronavirus-468787"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 They write}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s team has used its thrice-weekly Covid-19 press briefings to emphasize the need to uphold basic public health measures, including limiting travel and gatherings, in the face of the variant threat. But officials leading the administration\u8217\'20\'19s pandemic response have shied away from criticizing specific states. And behind the scenes, the White House\u8217\'20\'19s weekly calls with governors have largely focused on vaccine distribution, according to two sources on the calls.\par \par \uc2 Biden campaigned on promises he\u8217\'20\'19d take strong action to bring the pandemic under control \u8212\'20\'14 and touted his skills as a negotiator. Now, public health experts say that the administration\u8217\'20\'19s reticence to pressure states that are easing restrictions could jeopardize the fragile progress in reducing the rate of cases and deaths. If cases of variants begin surging, that could overwhelm hospitals and even undermine ongoing vaccination efforts by giving the virus more chances to mutate.\par \par \uc2 Roughly a year into the pandemic, at least 35 states mandate the use of masks. Others \u8212\'20\'14 including Iowa, Montana and North Dakota \u8212\'20\'14 have let their requirements lapse or rolled them back. The number of cases per day are higher now in many places than during strict lockdowns last spring and early fall. But with pandemic fatigue setting in and economies battered from months of restrictions, politicians in red and blue states alike are under pressure to loosen restrictions.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/02/12/biden-white-house-govenors-coronavirus-468787"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico \u8211\'20\'13 White House tiptoes around governors relaxing coronavirus rules}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 Covid deaths in US now over 475,000 \u8211\'20\'13 but hospitalizations drop below 75,000\par \par \uc2 The number of people killed during the coronavirus pandemic in the US has now topped 475,000. There were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ng-interactive/2020/sep/21/coronavirus-covid-19-map-us-cases-deaths-state-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 105,353 new cases yesterday}}}\uc2 , and 3,877 deaths.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://covidtracking.com/data/national/hospitalization"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hospitalizations in the US}}}\uc2  have dropped to 74,225. It\u8217\'20\'19s the first time the level has been below 75,000 since 16 November.\par \par \uc2 At least 35.4 million people have received a dose of the vaccine. 11.8 million of them have been fully vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 default\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.14am GMT\par \par \uc2 The government\u8217\'20\'19s nationalized health insurance program for seniors, Medicare, has kept money at the back of Ellen\u8217\'20\'19s mind while she struggles with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jan/05/im-still-at-half-capacity-long-covid-sufferers-reflect-on-brutal-year"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 long Covid}}}\uc2 . She pays $150 for the coverage each month and has spent less than $100 since she contracted Covid in April on prescription drugs.\par \par \uc2 But Ellen, who asked not to use her last name for privacy, has had Covid symptoms for 10 months \u8211\'20\'13 including 128 days of nonstop headaches.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI still have fatigue, right now I am laying down in bed, a shower will wipe me out,\u8221\'20\'1D she said from her home in Littleton, Colorado. \u8220\'20\'1CI still have brain fog, after we have this talk, I will be exhausted.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ellen is just one of the people {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/12/us-financial-cost-covid-coronavirus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amanda Holpuch has spoken to for us}}}\uc2 , investigating the financial cost of having Covid in the US.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/12/us-financial-cost-covid-coronavirus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I don\u8217\'20\'19t make enough\u8217\'20\'19: the financial cost of having Covid in the US}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/12/us-financial-cost-covid-coronavirus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 'I don't make enough': the financial cost of having Covid in the US}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump advisor: lawyers will wrap up his defense in less than a day\par \par \uc2 One of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s senior advisers yesterday said that his legal are expected to wrap up their defense in less than a day.\par \par \uc2 Mary Clare Jalonick reports for the Associated Press that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers plan to argue their client\u8217\'20\'19s innocence on multiple fronts. Their main arguments include that the trial is unconstitutional, that the insurrectionists who broke into the Capitol did so on their own accord and that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric to supporters was common political speech protected under the First Amendment.\par \par \uc2 Hoping that brevity will appeal to their restless Senate audience, and in the belief that there is very little chance of Republican Senators finding Trump guilty anyway, the lawyers are expected to keep their arguments short. Like the House prosecutors, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have up to 16 hours over two days to plead their case. Once the defense\u8217\'20\'19s presentation is finished, senators will have time to submit written questions to both sides.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have injected searing criticism of Democrats into their arguments, hoping to convince not only senators but also viewers of the trial around the country that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second impeachment is fuelled by what they say is \u8220\'20\'1Chatred\u8221\'20\'1D of the former president. They are expected to continue with that strategy on Friday, calling out Democrats they say similarly incited violence in cities around the country.\par \par \uc2 One of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers, David Schoen, told reporters in the Capitol on Thursday that Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 recounting of the riots on Wednesday \u8212\'20\'14 almost 90 minutes of brutal footage that saw the rioters injuring law enforcement and calling for the death of the vice president and the speaker of the House \u8212\'20\'14 was \u8220\'20\'1Coffensive.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 Rather than the Senate impeachment trial yesterday, president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was preoccupied with the plan to vaccinate the nation against a Covid pandemic which has now cost over 475,000 lives.\par \par \uc2 enltrWhen I took office three weeks ago, America didn\u8217\'20\'19t have a plan or enough supplies to vaccinate most of the country. But my team got right to work, and as of today, we\u8217\'20\'19ve increased weekly vaccine shipments by nearly 30% and purchased enough vaccines to vaccinate all Americans.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1360058795947393026?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 12, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Talking at the \uc2 National Institutes of Health\uc2  on Thursday, he spoke of the efforts his team had gone through to ensure high vaccination numbers and criticised Trump\u8217\'20\'19s strategy for distributing vaccines. \u8216\'20\'18My predecessor, to be very blunt about it, did not do his job,\u8217\'20\'19 Biden said. \u8216\'20\'18He didn\u8217\'20\'19t order enough vaccines. He didn\u8217\'20\'19t mobilise enough people to administer the shots\u8217\'20\'19. He confirmed the country had ordered an additional 200m vaccine doses to be delivered by the end of July.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the analysis of those closing arguments yesterday from the House impeachment managers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/trump-impeachment-trial-day-3-democrats-press-their-case-against-n1257436"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from NBC News overnight}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe didn\u8217\'20\'19t react to the violence with shock or horror or dismay, as we did. He didn\u8217\'20\'19t immediately rush to \uc2 Twitter\uc2  and demand in the clearest possible terms that the mob disperse, that they stop it, that they retreat,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Rep Joe Neguse\uc2  said. \u8220\'20\'1CInstead, he issues messages in the afternoon that sided with them, the insurrectionists, who had left police officers battered and bloodied.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The managers made the case that the mob believed they were acting at the direction of president, citing many of the rioters\u8217\'20\'19 own statements. They also cited the words of Republicans who publicly pleaded with Trump to call off his supporters as the siege was underway to bolster their argument that Trump was in control.\par \par \uc2 The House managers previewed likely arguments from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys. The First Amendment would not protect Trump\u8217\'20\'19s exhortations for the crowd to \u8220\'20\'1Cfight\u8221\'20\'1D the acceptance of the presidential electoral votes before his supporters marched on the Capitol, the Democrats argued, comparing him not to the proverbial private citizen who falsely shouts \u8220\'20\'1Cfire\u8221\'20\'1D in a crowded theater but to a fire chief who incites a mob to set the theater ablaze and then lets it burn.\par \par \uc2 Will it make any difference?\par \par \uc2 Sen Lindsey Graham\uc2  had a one-word response when asked by NBC News whether anything he had heard had changed his mind: \u8220\'20\'1CNope.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/trump-impeachment-trial-day-3-democrats-press-their-case-against-n1257436"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News \u8211\'20\'13 House managers rest case, argue Trump could stoke more violence if not convicted}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 North Carolina man charged with phoning threats to Biden at the White House\par \par \uc2 Reuters report that a man in North Carolina has been charged with threatening president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A federal criminal complaint against David Kyle Reeves, 27, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/usao-wdnc/pr/individual-charged-threatening-president-united-states-appears-federal-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unsealed in federal court}}}\uc2  on Thursday, US attorney for the Western District of North Carolina Andrew Murray said.\par \par \uc2 The charge of making a threat against a US president carries a maximum penalty of five years in prison, and a $250,000 fine.\par \par \uc2 Reeves, who was arrested last week, contacted the White House switchboard via telephone multiple times and made threats against Biden and others, according to allegations in the affidavit filed in support of the criminal complaint.\par \par \uc2 Following a court hearing on Thursday, US magistrate judge David Keesler ordered that Reeves remain in custody, the department of justice said.\par \par \uc2 The development comes as the Seante has spent two days watching dramatic video footage of Trump supporters rampaging though the US Capitol, seeking out lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 Senators who amplified Trump's lies now get a say in his fate\par \par \uc2 A desk in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  was notably empty for chunks of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s second impeachment trial on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 , a Republican from Missouri, was instead lounging in the upstairs public gallery with a pile of documents. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/politics/live-news/trump-impeachment-trial-02-10-2021/h_d8cebbeda92c93211783aca310dc5a34"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 He explained to CNN:}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m sitting up there A, because it\u8217\'20\'19s a little less claustrophobic than on the floor, but B, I\u8217\'20\'19ve also got a straight shot,\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a reference to his seating location that also conjured an unfortunate image.\par \par \uc2 But some critics would suggest that Hawley\u8217\'20\'19s rightful place is in the dock, along with his colleague Ted Cruz of Texas and others who unabashedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/12/josh-hawley-fanned-flames-diehard-trump-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s assault on democracy.}}}\par \par \uc2 This week\u8217\'20\'19s trial necessarily has a narrow focus on the ex-president but that means little scrutiny of Hawley, who was photographed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vogue.com/article/josh-hawley-missouri-senator-capitol-protests-resign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saluting Trump supporters}}}\uc2  with a raised fist hours before the insurrection at the US Capitol on 6 January.\par \par \uc2 The Kansas City Star newspaper in his home state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kansascity.com/opinion/editorials/article248317375.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote in an editorial:}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CNo one other than President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  himself is more responsible for Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s coup attempt at the US Capitol than one \uc2 Joshua David Hawley\uc2 , the 41-year-old junior senator from Missouri, who put out a fundraising appeal while the siege was under way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Undeterred by the deadly violence, Hawley and Cruz were prominent among eight senators and 139 representatives who objected to certifying \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s electoral college win. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/10/capitol-attack-republican-senators-josh-hawley-ted-cruz-face-resign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Both faced calls to resign.}}}\uc2  Yet now they get a say in whether Trump should be held accountable for his actions.\par \par \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , a former secretary of state and first lady, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HillaryClinton/status/1359524284469817349?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted on Thursday:}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CIf Senate Republicans fail to convict \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , it won\u8217\'20\'19t be because the facts were with him or his lawyers mounted a competent defense. It will be because the jury includes his co-conspirators.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more of David Smith\u8217\'20\'19s report here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/11/republican-senators-accomplices-trump-impeachment-josh-hawley-ted-cruz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Accomplice\u8217\'20\'19 senators who amplified Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lies now get a say in his fate}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/11/republican-senators-accomplices-trump-impeachment-josh-hawley-ted-cruz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 'Accomplice' senators who amplified Trump's lies now get a say in his fate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 House impeachment managers yesterday warned that more political violence could occur if Trump is not held accountable. Representative \uc2 Diana DeGette\uc2  argued the vote to impeach would make sure an attack like the 6 January Capitol riot would never happen again.\par \par \uc2 The managers rested their case on the third day of the trial after presenting arguments for convicting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . They have stressed that by taking no action, the Senate will set a precedent that it is ok for an outgoing president to try and overthrow their election defeat with mob violence.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Welcome to our live coverage of US politics and the ongoing impeachment trial of former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . The Senate will reconvene at noon EST today \u8211\'20\'13 1700 GMT \u8211\'20\'13 when his lawyers will begin to present their defense.\par \par \uc2 * That defense may not last very long. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers are pretty certain they have enough Republican jurors on their side to secure an early acquittal, and may not use all of their 16 allotted hours.\par \par \uc2 * Yesterday Democrats rested their case that the commander-in-chief committed \u8216\'20\'18incitement of insurrection\u8217\'20\'19 with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/11/trump-impeachment-trial-democrats-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a warning that Trump remains a threat}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has kept clear of commenting on the trial as it goes on, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/11/joe-biden-trump-impeachment-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said yesterday}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cmy guess is some minds may be changed\u8221\'20\'1D based on the presentation by the House impeachment managers.\par \par \uc2 * There were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ng-interactive/2020/sep/21/coronavirus-covid-19-map-us-cases-deaths-state-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 105,353 new coronavirus cases in the US yesterday}}}\uc2 , and 3,877 further deaths.\par \par \uc2 * Emergency crews in Richmond, California, are rushing to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/feb/11/richmond-california-chevron-oil-spill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clean up an estimated 600 gallons of oil that spilled from a Chevron refinery}}}\uc2  into the San Francisco Bay.\par \par \uc2 * Senior US lawmakers have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/feb/12/us-lawmakers-urge-uk-to-help-end-complicity-in-saudi-arabias-war-in-yemen"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called on the UK}}}\uc2  to live up to its \u8220\'20\'1Cmoral responsibility\u8221\'20\'1D and help end both countries \u8220\'20\'1Ccomplicity\u8221\'20\'1D in Saudi Arabia \u8217\'20\'19s war in Yemen.\par \par \uc2 * Today Biden and vice president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will meet with a bipartisan group of governors and mayors at 11.15am to discuss \u8220\'20\'1Cthe vital need to pass the American Rescue Plan\u8221\'20\'1D. Biden and Harris will also lunch together, and receive an Ovel office economic briefing from treasury secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/11/trump-impeachment-trial-democrats-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Impeachment trial: Democrats rest case with warning that Trump remains a threat}}}\par \par \uc2 2021-02-12T10:00:48Z 2021-02-13T02:02:54Z {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/821bc3c096225c04881b8176f42375a5c7691745/0_116_3500_2101/500.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/821bc3c096225c04881b8176f42375a5c7691745/0_116_3500_2101/500.jpg}}}\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s defense attorney David Schoen. Lunar New Year decorations are displayed in Chinatown on the eve of the Lunar New Year in New York.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210212eh2c001bg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
