\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Republicans employ new \u8216\'20\'18extremely aggressive\u8217\'20\'19 tactics to ban  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 1,450 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 February 2021\par 14:59 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bills that ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and punish women and doctors under murder statutes have shown up in state legislatures recently\par \par \uc2 At a church-style rally in Arizona, the state Republican lawmaker Walter Blackman described his \u8220\'20\'1Cperfect\u8221\'20\'1D legislative proposal: to prosecute women who have abortions for homicide alongside the doctors who provide them.\par \par \uc2 Such a bill would be patently unconstitutional in the US \u8211\'20\'13 but for anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists like Blackman that\u8217\'20\'19s the point.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not going to amend this bill,\u8221\'20\'1D Blackman said in January. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a perfect bill. I just want to tell you that now.\u8221\'20\'1D Nine of Blackman\u8217\'20\'19s colleagues {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/legislature-homicide-arizona-legislation-phoenix-5496422d5db9892af2cb4b1ea12215fb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed on to the bill}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bill was just one of nine more Arizona bills designed to ban, restrict or undermine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights \u8211\'20\'13 ranging from funding religious crisis pregnancy clinics which oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at six weeks, before most women know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s nothing less than appalling,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Julia Kwatra, an obstetrician and gynecologist who has practiced in Scottsdale for 20 years. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is just representing a full frontal assault on women\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare in Arizona this legislative session.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But this slew of legislation is just one state\u8217\'20\'19s effort to redefine reproductive rights in a year of Republican party schism. In other states across the US \u8211\'20\'13 from Florida to North Dakota \u8211\'20\'13 legislation from Republican lawmakers seeking to undermine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights is on the move. For anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists, the goal has long been to challenge the supreme court decision that gave pregnant people the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  48 years ago: the landmark Roe versus Wade.\par \par \uc2 Each spring, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2016/01/last-five-years-account-more-one-quarter-all-abortion-restrictions-enacted-roe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 especially in the last decade}}}\uc2 , Republicans have introduced restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws tailored to challenge that supreme court precedent by creating test cases. In 1973, Roe versus Wade provided women with a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to the point the fetus can survive outside the womb, generally understood to be 24 weeks.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions investigate the outer limits of that right, by creating laws that provoke reproductive rights advocates to sue, and for courts to consider their legitimacy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe more ambitious a restriction the court upholds, that will greenlight even more restrictions in the states,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mary Ziegler, a Florida State University law professor whose recent book, \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in America: A Legal History, tracked the history of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most important \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cases.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we\u8217\'20\'19ve been seeing is not what anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lawmakers want, but it\u8217\'20\'19s been tailored to what they think the supreme court wants,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ziegler.\par \par \uc2 This effort is not meant to reflect the will of the majority of Americans, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2019/06/07/730183531/poll-majority-want-to-keep-abortion-legal-but-they-also-want-restrictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 77% of whom}}}\uc2  believe the supreme court should uphold Roe v Wade. The effort is meant to please a motivated, religious voter base, who have helped power Republican victories since the Reagan era. Trump played for the same \u8220\'20\'1Csocial conservatives\u8221\'20\'1D when vowing to appoint supreme court justices who would overturn Roe.\par \par \uc2 But since Trump rose to power, exactly how to do that has become a vexing question for the Republican party. Grassroots extremists came to power alongside \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , making {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/01/11/us/how-white-evangelical-christians-fused-with-trump-extremism.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 common cause with some evangelical Christians}}}\uc2 , and demanding immediate gratification in bills like Blackman\u8217\'20\'19s.\par \par \uc2 Bills that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/may/22/iowa-anti-abortion-heartbeat-bill-passed-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , demand doctors perform the impossible and \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/nov/29/ohio-extreme-abortion-bill-reimplant-ectopic-pregnancy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reimplant\u8221\'20\'1D ectopic pregnancies}}}\uc2 , punish women and doctors under murder statutes and whose authors believe the fundamental legal principle of precedent should not apply to their cases have all shown up in state legislatures in the last couple years.\par \par \uc2 Bans in recent sessions have been \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely aggressive\u8221\'20\'1D, said Hillary Schneller, a senior staff attorney for the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights\uc2 , and who is now fighting a Mississippi law that could ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 15 weeks. The state has appealed to the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Recent bans have been, \u8220\'20\'1Csaying the quiet part out loud \u8211\'20\'13 that they\u8217\'20\'19re not just restriction \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they want to end access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  entirely\u8221\'20\'1D, said Schneller.\par \par \uc2 Until recently, most slates of new bills avoided this type of exposure. Establishment anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups, like the \uc2 National Right to Life Committee\uc2 , preferred calculated legal strategies designed to elicit maximum supreme court interest and minimum voter outrage.\par \par \uc2 This year, since Trump lost re-election and the Republican party has split into warring factions, the spectrum of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation has come to reflect that intra-party feud \u8211\'20\'13 a war between extremists and established anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists. In states like Mississippi, lawmakers have passed both kinds of legislation.\par \par \uc2 More extreme members of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement are \u8220\'20\'1Cmaking bids to control strategy for their movement\u8221\'20\'1D, said Ziegler. Extremists have shown, \u8220\'20\'1CThey have legislators in a way we would assume only people like the \uc2 National Right to Life Committee\uc2  would have,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 In Arizona, the architect of most of the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions over the last decade {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.12news.com/article/news/politics/executions-for-abortion-arizona-bill-would-treat-procedure-as-murder-but-backlash-is-growing/75-69b0899d-d68e-4c70-9372-a0ddf8083170"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opposes Blackman\u8217\'20\'19s bill}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Cathi Herrod\uc2 , president of the Center for Arizona Policy, told a local television station, \u8220\'20\'1CIn the pro-life community, we love both the woman and her unborn child. Both are victims.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 These bans don\u8217\'20\'19t come out of nowhere. They are the result of a sustained campaign from anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politicians\par \par \uc2 Hillary Schneller\par \par \uc2 Arizona is in the process of turning from red to purple \u8211\'20\'13 recently sending two Democratic senators to Washington DC and helping flip the presidential election for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Kwatra said she views the huge number of new restrictions as a \u8220\'20\'1Clast gasp\u8221\'20\'1D from the state Republican party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s literally all men on deck\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cassault from every direction\u8221\'20\'1D, said Kwatra, adding that as more than 14,000 Arizonans have died of Covid-19, \u8220\'20\'1Cour legislature is focused on taking voting rights away and healthcare rights away from women\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 One bill being championed in both Arizona and South Carolina is a \u8220\'20\'1Cfetal heartbeat bill\u8221\'20\'1D that would ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before most women know they are pregnant, without exemptions for rape or incest. As of 2019, nine other states had done the same.\par \par \uc2 Actually a misnomer, \u8220\'20\'1Cfetal heartbeat bills\u8221\'20\'1D use the detection of \u8220\'20\'1Ccardiac activity\u8221\'20\'1D in an embryo (the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/ncbddd/fasd/documents/fasdbrochure_final.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stage of development before a fetus}}}\uc2  ) as early as six weeks. At that stage, embryos have a pulse, but not a fully developed heart to power a circulatory system. This kind of restriction would outlaw the vast majority of abortions.\par \par \uc2 The author of that bill is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/apr/25/the-anti-abortion-crusader-hopes-her-heartbeat-law-will-test-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Janet Porter}}}\uc2 , an evangelical Christian based in Ohio. Alongside her anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocacy, she is fiercely anti-gay, and promotes the baseless idea that the election was stolen from Trump.\par \par \uc2 In one interview in late January, she said Biden\u8217\'20\'19s inauguration had the mood of a funeral. \u8220\'20\'1CMaybe that\u8217\'20\'19s what it feels like to steal an election, and you know you\u8217\'20\'19re not there rightfully so,\u8221\'20\'1D Porter said.\par \par \uc2 Her interviewer concurred: \u8220\'20\'1CI do believe God wanted \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to be re-elected, I think it was God\u8217\'20\'19s will, yet sometimes in this fallen world the devil wins.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, establishment groups {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rewirenewsgroup.com/legislative-tracker/law-topic/dilation-and-evacuation-bans/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 like NRLC}}}\uc2  have pushed to ban specific procedures, such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/induced-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dilation and evacuation}}}\uc2 , and to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to earlier and earlier in pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 such as in 15 weeks in Mississippi.\par \par \uc2 By banning specific procedures, which are not well understood by lawmakers or the public, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates may see fewer objections to their efforts while still significantly eroding rights. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wfpl.org/daniel-cameron-asks-u-s-supreme-court-to-uphold-abortion-law/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kentucky version}}}\uc2  of the dilation and evacuation ban could come before the supreme court this session (just {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.acog.org/clinical/clinical-guidance/practice-bulletin/articles/2013/06/second-trimester-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 4% of abortions}}}\uc2  overall).\par \par \uc2 Problematically, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates view extreme bills \u8211\'20\'13 such as Blackman\u8217\'20\'19s \u8211\'20\'13 as providing political cover for potentially more damaging establishment bills.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese bans don\u8217\'20\'19t come out of nowhere. They are the result of a very sustained campaign from anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politicians,\u8221\'20\'1D said Schneller.\par \par \uc2 In 2021, with a new Democratic presidential administration, not all efforts are focused exclusively on defending reproductive rights. The Biden administration rolled back several funding restrictions for reproductive health counseling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2021/jan/28/joe-biden-global-gag-rule-health-groups"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 domestically and abroad}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists\uc2  has sued the \uc2 US Food and Drug Administration\uc2  to end in-person dispensing requirements for medication abortions during the pandemic, which the professional association has said are not medically justified.\par \par \uc2 In Oregon, a bill would require the state to examine whether specific {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thelundreport.org/content/bills-would-target-mergers-among-hospital-systems-clinic-networks-others"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 healthcare mergers reduce access to reproductive rights}}}\uc2 . In Arizona, advocates are fighting to allow birth control to be dispensed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azcentral.com/story/news/politics/arizona/2020/02/12/arizona-may-let-women-get-birth-control-without-prescription/4733094002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 without a prescription}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know how to decrease the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, while at the same time improving women\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kwatra. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to take care of women in all their complicated ways \u8230\'20\'26 which is really not hard to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This article was amended on 12 February 2021 to clarify a quote on the number of people in Arizona who have died from Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210212eh2c001bd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
