\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden signs healthcare order to undo Trump 'damage' as US detects two South Africa Covid variant cases \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now), Amanda Holpuch and Martin Belam (earlier) \par \uc2 13,955 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 January 2021\par 01:50 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Biden signs executive order on health marketplacesCases of variant detected in South CarolinaUS economy shrank by 3.5% in 2020House members ask for more security amid fears they\u8217\'20\'19re targetsSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a review of today\u8217\'20\'19s news, from me and Amanda Holpuch:\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/28/obamacare-aca-markets-reopening-biden-coverage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden signed an executive order}}}\uc2  reopening federal health insurance marketplaces, to help those who have lost employer-provided healthcare due to the economic crisis. He also signed another directing federal agencies to reconsider rules and other policies which limit access to healthcare and consider actions to improve access.\par \par \uc2 * Addressing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, Biden signed an order ending the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2019/mar/26/trump-global-gag-rule-us-aid-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 global gag rule}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D that bans foreign non-government groups that receive US funding from providing abortions or information about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a memorandum instructing the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  to reconsider a Trump-era rule that stopped clinics that received federal family planning funding from providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referrals.\par \par \uc2 * South Carolina officials said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/28/coronavirus-south-african-variant-identified-in-us-for-first-time"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two cases of the coronavirus variant}}}\uc2  first identified in South Africa had been detected in the state \u8211\'20\'13 the first time the variant has been found in the US. The news came as \uc2 Novavax\uc2  found preliminary evidence that its vaccine candidate was less effective against that variant than others. \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and Moderna also said their vaccines were slightly less effective against the variant.\par \par \uc2 * The Senate voted to advance \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nomination as secretary of homeland security, Alejandro Mayorkas. A final vote on his nomination is scheduled for Monday night.\par \par \uc2 * Survivors of the 2018 mass shooting in Parkland, Florida, asked congressional Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/28/marjorie-taylor-greene-parkland-david-hogg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to publicly censure Marjorie Taylor Greene}}}\uc2  for suggesting the school shooting was a \u8220\'20\'1Cfalse flag\u8221\'20\'1D and for harassing a teenage survivor on Capitol Hill in 2019. House Republicans this week announced that Greene, a newly elected Georgia congresswoman, had been appointed to the House education and labor committee.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 Hours of scrolling, endless refreshing: US tech woes make scheduling vaccine a nightmare\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the New York-based photographer Hee Jin Kang woke up at 3am and went online to register her elderly parents for the coronavirus vaccine.\par \par \uc2 She created accounts on five different websites, including portals for state-run vaccination programs as well as hospitals, pharmacies and primary care locations. After hours of clicking through and refreshing various landing pages, she secured time slots for both parents.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just crazy,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no centralized system. I just couldn\u8217\'20\'19t stop thinking, if you are not tech literate this would just be impossible \u8211\'20\'13 they make you jump through so many hoops.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 People across the United States have likened signing up for a vaccine shot in recent weeks to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=vaccine%20ticketmaster&src=typed_query"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refreshing a page}}}\uc2  for highly coveted concert tickets. In Michigan, a website for vaccine sign-ups {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.detroitnews.com/story/news/nation/coronavirus/2021/01/11/beaumont-triples-server-capacity-vaccine-demand-crashes-system/6619290002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crashed}}}\uc2  almost immediately after the state expanded vaccine access to people 65 and older. The site, which processes 900 appointments on a typical day, saw more than 25,000 people trying to register. In Texas one website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kens5.com/article/news/health/coronavirus/city-says-covid-19-registration-website-didnt-crash-after-9000-vaccine-appointments-filled-in-6-minutes/273-5477c5ae-86b5-4189-9936-18ca82a3ca77"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saw 9,000 appointments}}}\uc2  fill in less than six minutes. Users in Minnesota {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kttc.com/2021/01/19/some-minnesota-elementary-students-head-back-in-school-3/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  similar issues. Some health departments in Florida are using the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vice.com/en/article/pkdqgz/florida-is-using-eventrite-for-covid-19-vaccine-slots-and-its-not-going-well"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ticketing site Eventbrite}}}\uc2 , leading to concerns about ticket scalpers buying up slots and reselling them.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration promised in November that 20m Covid-19 vaccines could be distributed by 2021. As of this week just 18.5 million people have received at least one dose of the vaccine, according to the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 , and about 3.2 million people have been fully vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 New vaccine doses can only be produced so quickly, but supply is just part of the problem. For Americans whose vaccines are not being arranged through their workplace, scheduling can be a major setback.\par \par \uc2 Most states have no centralized system to register for appointments and those that do exist are rife with glitches. Both these hurdles have made it difficult for those who aren\u8217\'20\'19t tech savvy and people who don\u8217\'20\'19t have time to refresh an online sign-up all day to get a potentially life-saving vaccine slot.\par \par \uc2 In fact, online sign-ups raise a number of ethics concerns, public health experts say. Most states in the US are in the second stage of vaccines, meaning people aged 65 and older are allowed to be vaccinated. That poses issues for elderly patients and others with little tech literacy, said Susan Lee, a primary care internist in New York. \u8220\'20\'1CThe only elderly patients who have been able to get appointments \u8211\'20\'13 my parents included \u8211\'20\'13 are those who have someone able to advocate for them,\u8221\'20\'1D Lee said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is heartbreaking.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jan/28/coronavirus-vaccine-appointments-older-americans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hours of scrolling, endless refreshing: US tech woes make scheduling vaccine a nightmare}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s an update on the former president, from the AP:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been living at his Mar-a-Lago club since leaving office more than a week ago \u8212\'20\'14 a possible violation of a 1993 agreement he made with the Town of Palm Beach that limits stays to seven consecutive days.\par \par \uc2 Town Manager Kirk Blouin said in an email Thursday that Palm Beach is examining its options and the matter might be discussed at the town council\u8217\'20\'19s February meeting.\par \par \uc2 The South Florida town last month received a letter from an attorney representing a Mar-a-Lago neighbor demanding it enforce the agreement\u8217\'20\'19s residency clause \u8212\'20\'14 something it rarely if ever did when Trump was president or before. The unnamed neighbor believes Trump\u8217\'20\'19s residency would decrease property values, according to Reginald Stambaugh\u8217\'20\'19s letter. Stambaugh did not return a call or email Thursday asking whether he has received a response.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 Sarah Sanders\uc2 , the former White House press secretary in the Trump administration, has raised $1m since announcing she was running to be Arkansas governor this week.\par \par \uc2 Sanders has joined two other Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 the lieutenant governor, Tim Griffin, and the attorney general, Leslie Rutledge \u8211\'20\'13 in the 2022 race for governor. No Democrat has yet announced their candidacy.\par \par \uc2 More from the AP:\par \par \uc2 Sanders announced on Monday she was running for Arkansas governor with a nearly eight-minute video that embraced former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , even as the Senate prepares for an impeachment trial on charges he incited the deadly Jan. 6 riot at the U.S. Capitol.\par \par \uc2 The fundraising haul shows how much more expensive the 2022 GOP race for Arkansas governor will become with Sanders in it. Griffin has raised $1.8m since March for the race while Rutledge has raised $1m since July.\par \par \uc2 Arkansas is a solidly red state, with Republicans holding all of its statewide and federal offices. Sanders, the daughter of former governor \uc2 Mike Huckabee\uc2 , left the White House in 2019 to return to her home state. Trump, who publicly encouraged her to run for Arkansas governor, endorsed her candidacy on Monday night.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.18am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.03am GMT\par \par \uc2 Bounchan Keola, a California firefighter who was taken into US immigration custody last year, has been released.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEWS: Bounchan Keola, the incarcerated firefighter who California sent to ICE for deportation, is free after 22 years.\par \par \uc2 He was released from ICE custody yesterday and is now reuniting with his family for the first time in decades: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6f2uImw8gR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6f2uImw8gR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levin (@SamTLevin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SamTLevin/status/1354905662342356994?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Keola, 39, was working as an incarcerated firefighter in October when he suffered a near-death injury on the frontlines of a major blaze. He had just two weeks left in his prison term when he was crushed by a tree while battling a northern California fire. Days later, California prison officials notified federal immigration agents that his release would be coming up, and the state made arrangements to directly transfer him to \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  (Ice), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/nov/12/after-an-incarcerated-firefighter-was-nearly-killed-on-the-frontlines-california-delivered-him-to-ice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Guardian reported in November}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 His case sparked national outrage, with critics calling for California to end its practice of handing over state prisoners to Ice. Keola, who was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/audio/2020/nov/30/he-risked-his-life-fighting-the-californian-wildfires-now-he-faces-deportation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatened with deportation to Laos}}}\uc2 , a country his family fled when he was four, was released from Ice custody on Wednesday, walking free for the first time in 22 years.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/aaaj_alc/status/1354898291280982025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement upon his release}}}\uc2 , Keola called on California\u8217\'20\'19s governor to end the policy of coordinating transfers to Ice and urged him to pardon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/sep/22/california-inmate-firefighter-ice-deportation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kao Saelee, another refugee from Laos}}}\uc2  who was taken into immigration detention after he served as an imprisoned firefighter.\par \par \uc2 More from our original coverage here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/nov/12/after-an-incarcerated-firefighter-was-nearly-killed-on-the-frontlines-california-delivered-him-to-ice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 After an incarcerated firefighter was nearly killed on the frontlines, California delivered him to Ice}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republicans considering more than 100 bills to restrict voting rights\par \par \uc2 After an election filled with misinformation and lies about fraud, Republicans have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/dec/19/republicans-strategize-future-elections-harder-to-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  doubled down}}}\uc2  with a surge of bills to further restrict voting access in recent months, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brennancenter.org/our-work/research-reports/voting-laws-roundup-2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new analysis}}}\uc2  by the Brennan Center for Justice.\par \par \uc2 There are currently 106 pending bills across 28 states that would restrict access to voting, according to the data. That\u8217\'20\'19s a sharp increase from nearly a year ago, when there were 35 restrictive bills pending across 15 states.\par \par \uc2 Among the Brennan Center\u8217\'20\'19s findings:\par \par \uc2 * More than a third of the bills would place new restrictions on voting by mail\par \par \uc2 * Pennsylvania has 14 pending proposals for new voter restrictions, the most in the country. It\u8217\'20\'19s followed by New Hampshire (11), Missouri (9), and Mississippi, New Jersey and Texas (8)\par \par \uc2 * There are seven bills across four states that would limit opportunities for election day registration\par \par \uc2 * There are also 406 bills that would expand voting access pending across 35 states, including in New York (56), Texas (53), New Jersey (37), Mississippi (39) and Missouri (21)\par \par \uc2 The restrictions come on the heels of an election in which there was record turnout and Democrat and Republican election officials alike said there was no evidence of widespread wrongdoing or fraud. There were recounts, audits and lawsuits across many states to back up those assurances. Federal and state officials {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cisa.gov/news/2020/11/12/joint-statement-elections-infrastructure-government-coordinating-council-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  the election \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most secure in American history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/28/republicans-considering-100-bills-restrict-voting-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans considering more than 100 bills to restrict voting rights}}}\par \par \uc2 And do sign up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2017/feb/22/us-politics-minute-sign-up-email-newsletter-app-notification"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  here }}}\uc2  to receive the weekly email newsletter from \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Fight to Vote newsletter.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Los Angeles is vaccinating healthcare workers, first responders and residents older than 65. But as the region battles one of the worst coronavirus outbreaks in the US, people are chasing vaccine doses ahead of their allotted tier, queueing for hours, and visiting sites after the official time ends.\par \par \uc2 Information about where to show up for extra doses and when is typically passed word of mouth.\par \par \uc2 Officially, there is no waiting or end-of-the day policy, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://publichealth.lacounty.gov/acd/docs/LACPhase1AFullGuidance.pdf?utm_content=&utm_medium=email&utm_name=&utm_source=govdelivery&utm_term="}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 county officials}}}\uc2  say. But given the dire health emergency, they also don\u8217\'20\'19t want doses to go to waste. The gap between these two creates a space for \u8220\'20\'1Cvaccine vultures\u8221\'20\'1D to swoop down.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s hard to put a number on how many people are scoring vaccine doses ahead of schedule, but it could be a few dozen each day at each of the six mega sites scattered around the 500 square miles of Los Angeles county.\par \par \uc2 That there are vaccines left over at all is due to several factors. About 10% of people with appointments do not show up for their shot, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2021-01-23/standby-lines-backdoor-vaccine-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to press reports}}}\uc2 . Vials containing the Moderna vaccine have to be used within six hours after opening before they have to be thrown out. And while vials are supposed to contain five doses, injectors can often coax six doses out of them.\par \par \uc2 In a mid-January statement, Los Angeles county said its department of public health \u8220\'20\'1Cdoes not condone wasting of any precious vaccine doses and has not and is not directing providers to throw away unused doses\u8221\'20\'1D. The statement added that the county was moving to set up vaccine clinics on quick turnaround whenever it learned of potential vaccine expirations. (The county public health department did not respond to requests for comment for this story.)\par \par \uc2 Dr Monya De, an LA-area physician who volunteered at the Inglewood Forum, which is one of six mega sites for vaccine dispersal in LA county, said some family members accompanying seniors to get their shot asked if there were any available for them as well. \u8220\'20\'1COur instructions are to vaccinate only the person who was registered,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a volume issue: we have a large volume of people in LA who need to get vaccinated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But De said she did wonder about resource allocation and if the current approach is the best way to get the most needles in the most arms. \u8220\'20\'1CI could see potentially the instruction being changed to: yes, if you have an extra vaccine you can inject people who are coming along in the same family.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At the end of her recent shift, De and the other injectors circled the Forum to get an accurate count of how much vaccine was left. They then got the go-ahead from the site administration to summon people who could quickly drive over for the extra doses. \u8220\'20\'1CWe heard at least one person saying, \u8216\'20\'18I think we\u8217\'20\'19re going to throw some of this away,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D she recalled. \u8220\'20\'1CThat was really concerning.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/28/los-angeles-residents-stalk-covid-vaccine-sites-in-hopes-of-leftover-doses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Los Angeles residents stalk Covid vaccine sites in hopes of leftover doses}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Novavax\uc2  says its Covid-19 vaccine is 89% effective\par \par \uc2 Novavax Inc\uc2  said its vaccine is 89% effective in early findings from an ongoing study of 15,000 people in the UK. But the vaccine appears to be less effective against the P1 variant first detected in South Africa. In a small South Africa trial with 4,400 people, it was only about 49% effective.\par \par \uc2 Novavax\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s vaccine was among six supported by the US\u8217\'20\'19 Operation Warp Speed.\par \par \uc2 The research is still at an early state. Of 15,000 participants in Britain, only 62 have had Covid-19. Six of those people had received the vaccine. The South Africa trial is too small to draw useful estimates of precisely how much protection the vaccine provides, the company said \u8211\'20\'13 but the early findings there have prompted \uc2 Novavax\uc2  to begin studying a new vaccine that\u8217\'20\'19s more tailored toward the P1 Variant.\par \par \uc2 Earlier Thursday, the US reported its first cases of the P1 variant, in South Carolina. Moderna and \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  also said their vaccines are slightly less effective against the variant.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 11.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 10.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 American Medical Association\uc2  has praised the Biden administration for beginning the process of reconsidering a Trump administration that overhauled the Title X federal family planning program.\par \par \uc2 Biden signed a memo directing the Department of Health and Human services to review the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s rule, saying there were legal obstacles to fully rescinding the previous administration\u8217\'20\'19s rule. The Title X overhaul by the Trump administration redirected tens of millions in funds from Planned Parenthood and other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers to anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and religious groups.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 American Medical Association\uc2  (AMA) strongly applauds the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s decision to consider reversing the Trump administration rule that imposed drastic changes on the Title X program,\u8221\'20\'1D said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.mediaoutreach.meltwater.com/ls/click?upn=21QTKcOpbrkkXVz39mGzM5-2BzBqxoGFjtLyFoDixq4LjRIPI52YN-2BLspjhHPhKSLC-2B-2BkWSNGkKnvypwIwrqEz2FTg96Fu1wGzdZBPzqWUQ4s-3Det-8_cI2SpRnkHOVQduPKId9oPFmHXO4Nq1W4yANcF8sRqKV84gDyjm93RMA690vL1ox9Ff3V-2BcuEquY1FHGunoEkrYwGCZhtOHRro14HvbLQmdqNeojqYs63-2FgU-2FK3DnNh-2BzydGYklzT6xKReLkQY9vp8giCNE-2BJ-2FfzILiVYFhTfpimNgZMmNJUy5VDIKLOhTI8Tw2qOQ04gh3f25-2BG-2FlZ59eN0A-2BBl4TPy0Mbe5eHEIY0rHHzcvq5CUfZEQkZOq1bQwadgsnaf-2B9RY7C4CliGpNYhmsyy59-2Bxo8vN-2F4oqgjjZCRz0EMRi-2F-2BEJ5679xW-2B4IEnnfYlToaxhtF-2BjfEGBewZPcIojh2htcf7ZE6RWpF85UpHUfUUAt63cZIZNfaH5QxfE3i9TOTxpFssBEAKd-2FRdxdKioJzmej-2BSSyHJbGGa40-3D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Susan R. Bailey,}}}\uc2  the AMA president. \u8220\'20\'1CTitle X has an essential role in ensuring that all Americans \u8211\'20\'13 regardless of their location or economic situation \u8211\'20\'13 have access to quality, evidence-based reproductive health care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She said in a statement that rescinding the Trump-era rule \u8220\'20\'1Cwould also mean the government will no longer inappropriately interfere in the patient-physician relationship, and physicians will no longer be forced to violate the ethical standards of the medical profession.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Per the rule, clinics that receive Title X funding are not to provide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referrals. The rule also lifted a requirement that clinics counsel on all reproductive options, including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 allowing anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  organizations to become eligible for Title X funds.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more background on the impact of the rule:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/aug/22/planned-parenthood-trump-abortion-gag-rule-harms-patients"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  \u8216\'20\'18gag rule\u8217\'20\'19 leaves poor patients \u8216\'20\'18with nowhere to go\u8217\'20\'19 in US}}}\par \par \uc2 10.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Senate banking committee is planning a hearing after trading platforms including Robinhood cut off or restricted small investors from buying more shares of \uc2 GameStop\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople on Wall Street only care about the rules when they\u8217\'20\'19re the ones getting hurt. American workers have known for years the Wall Street system is broken \u8211\'20\'13 they\u8217\'20\'19ve been paying the price,\u8221\'20\'1D said the committee chair, \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2 , in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s time for the SEC and Congress to make the economy work for everyone, not just Wall Street.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Following Robinhood\u8217\'20\'19s decision to curb its users, the progressive representative Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez, a member of the House financial services committee, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is unacceptable. We now need to know more about Robinhood\u8217\'20\'19s decision to block retail investors from purchasing stock while hedge funds are freely able to trade the stock as they see fit... I\u8217\'20\'19d support a hearing if necessary.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more background:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/jan/28/gamestop-shares-robinhood-app-ban-blackberry-amc-nokia-reddit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 GameStop shares plunge after ban by Robinhood app}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated at 10.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 10.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/28/obamacare-aca-markets-reopening-biden-coverage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden signed two health-related executive orders}}}\uc2  in the Oval Office. He said the best way to describe the actions was \u8220\'20\'1Cto undo the damage Trump has done\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * The White House press secretary, Jen Psaki, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jan/28/joe-biden-donald-trump-impeachment-kamala-harris-covid-coronavirus-live-updates?page=with:block-60131be28f08653792879888#block-60131be28f08653792879888"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmed}}}\uc2  the White House wants every American, including undocumented immigrants, to have access to the Covid-19 vaccine. She also confirmed that the immigration executive orders originally slated to be announced tomorrow, would be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jan/28/joe-biden-donald-trump-impeachment-kamala-harris-covid-coronavirus-live-updates?page=with:block-6012df698f08afe716c7243a#block-6012df698f08afe716c7243a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced next week instead}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The Senate voted today to advance \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nomination as secretary of Homeland Security, Alejandro Mayorkas. A final vote on his nomination is scheduled for Monday night.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 10.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 9.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In addition to rescinding the \u8216\'20\'18global gag rule\u8217\'20\'19 on Thursday, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  ordered funding restored to the \uc2 UN\uc2  population fund, \uc2 UNFPA\uc2 , which Trump stopped.\par \par \uc2 UNFPA\uc2  said the US decision to restore funding will have an \u8220\'20\'1Cenormous\u8221\'20\'1D impact on the agency\u8217\'20\'19s work, particularly coming as the world continues to grapple with the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe renewal of the strong partnership between \uc2 UNFPA\uc2  and the \uc2 US government\uc2  is a ray of hope for millions of people around the world who desperately need help,\u8221\'20\'1D said the agency\u8217\'20\'19s executive director, \uc2 Dr Natalia Kanem\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEnding funding to \uc2 UNFPA\uc2  has become a political football, far removed from the tragic reality it leads to on the ground. Women\u8217\'20\'19s bodies are not political bargaining chips, and their right to plan their pregnancies, give birth safely and live free from violence should be something we can all agree on.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She said Covid-19 had hit particularly hard the vulnerable communities in which the \uc2 UNFPA\uc2  works. \u8220\'20\'1CUS support will be instrumental in helping us build back better and fairer.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2021/jan/28/joe-biden-global-gag-rule-health-groups"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden axes 'global gag rule' but health groups call on him to go further}}}\par \par \uc2 9.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 It was a big day for the country\u8217\'20\'19s first second gentleman, or as he is also known, the SGOTUS (yes).\par \par \uc2 Today, Kamala Harris\u8217\'20\'19s husband, Douglas Emhoff, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SecondGentleman/status/1354812409043509256"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  that the title \u8220\'20\'1Csecond gentleman\u8221\'20\'1D has been officially recognized by Merriam Webster\u8217\'20\'19s dictionary and wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CI might be the first, but I won\u8217\'20\'19t be the last.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In another step for the future\u8217\'20\'19s second gentleman, the White House on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bgittleson/status/1354791926483058689"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Thursday released Emhoff\u8217\'20\'19s schedule}}}\uc2 . The White House does this almost every day for the president and vice president, and often the first lady, but today marked the first public schedule for second gentleman in US history.\par \par \uc2 One of his first orders of business on Thursday was teaching an entertainment law class at \uc2 Georgetown University\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the afternoon, he participated in his first solo event as second gentleman and visited a Washington DC nonprofit which supports healthy food distribution to people in need. Reporters asked Emhoff if food insecurity would be his issue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s got to be an issue for everybody,\u8221\'20\'1D Emhoff said. \u8220\'20\'1CSo, I want to do what I can to amplify it. I think it\u8217\'20\'19s something everyone needs to be concerned about.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 9.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A West Virginia man armed with two handguns and 20 rounds of ammunition was arrested near the US Capitol on Wednesday, DC police said.\par \par \uc2 Police approached Dennis Westover, 71, when he was parked in the middle of an intersection near the Capitol and found and recovered the weapons. Westover was charged with having a handgun and unregistered ammunition\par \par \uc2 On Friday, 37-year-old Macias Santiago, of Texas, was arrested outside the White House last week for having a weapon and ammunition.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, the homeland security department {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/27/us-terrorism-bulletin-homeland-security-joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued a national terrorism bulletin}}}\uc2  warning of the lingering potential for violence from people motivated by anti-government sentiment after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 8.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary, Jen Psaki, said the Covid-19 vaccine should be made available to everyone, including undocumented immigrants.\par \par \uc2 Immigrant advocates have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/jan/14/herd-immunity-vaccinate-immigrants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raised concerns}}}\uc2  over whether language about every \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican\u8221\'20\'1D having access to vaccines included undocumented people, but Psaki confirmed the US intends to vaccinate every resident.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are focused on making sure we get the vaccine out broadly,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 She said it was important for everyone to have access to the vaccine for \u8220\'20\'1Cmoral\u8221\'20\'1D reasons, as well as public health reasons.\par \par \uc2 8.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democratic representative Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez said Republican senator Ted Cruz \u8220\'20\'1Calmost had me murdered 3 weeks ago,\u8221\'20\'1D after the senator unexpectedly agreed with her position on financial regulation on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Cruz had responded to an Ocasio-Cortez tweet about regulations and said \u8220\'20\'1Cfully agree,\u8221\'20\'1D but the representative was quick to point out that there were some lingering issues between several Republicans, like Cruz, who contested the presidential election results and Democrats.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am happy to work with Republicans on this issue where there\u8217\'20\'19s common ground, but you almost had me murdered 3 weeks ago so you can sit this one out,\u8221\'20\'1D Ocasio-Cortez tweeted. \u8220\'20\'1CHappy to work w/ almost any other GOP that aren\u8217\'20\'19t trying to get me killed. In the meantime if you want to help, you can resign.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Seven Democratic senators filed a formal complaint last week urging the Senate ethics committee to investigate Cruz, and senator Josh Hawley, because of their efforts to overturn the election results.\par \par \uc2 Ocasio-Cortez is one of several prominent figures to blame Cruz for his role in inciting the insurrection at the US Capitol earlier this month. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/01/23/politics/garret-miller-capitol-riot-threaten-alexandria-ocasio-cortez/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 At least one }}}\uc2  of the people charged in the attack had posted death threats against Ocasio-Cortez online.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile you conveniently talk about \u8216\'20\'18moving on,\u8217\'20\'19 a second Capitol police officer lost their life yesterday in the still-raging aftermath of the attacks you had a role in,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis isn\u8217\'20\'19t a joke. We need accountability, and that includes a new senator from Texas.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 You haven\u8217\'20\'19t even apologized for the serious physical + mental harm you contributed to from Capitol Police & custodial workers to your own fellow members of Congress.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, you can get off my timeline & stop clout-chasing. Thanks.\par \par \uc2 Happy to work with other GOP on this.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez (@AOC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC/status/1354852019023052801?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 8.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Senate voted today to advance \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nomination as secretary of Homeland Security, Alejandro Mayorkas.\par \par \uc2 A final vote on his nomination is scheduled for Monday night. He is expected to be confirmed.\par \par \uc2 Republicans objected to efforts to quickly confirm Mayorkas, but Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer was ultimately able to use Senate procedure to end the Republican filibuster on the nomination.\par \par \uc2 Mayorkas would be the first immigrant and first Latino to hold the post.\par \par \uc2 Former DHS secretaries Janet Napolitano and Michael Chertoff told reporters they were concerned Republicans were holding up the confirmation over political differences.\par \par \uc2 Chertoff, who was appointed by George W Bush, said: \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s not let Ali Mayorkas\u8217\'20\'19 nomination become a hostage to the fact that some people don\u8217\'20\'19t like a policy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 8.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary, Jen Psaki, is holding a briefing with reporters and said the health care executives order signed today build on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to put \u8220\'20\'1Cequity at center of response to Covid-19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She also highlighted the health department\u8217\'20\'19s move on Wednesday to allow recently retired doctors and nurses to administer vaccines. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is an effort to put more vaccinators in the field,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 Psaki was also asked about the White House\u8217\'20\'19s position on a decision by Pakistan \u8217\'20\'19s supreme court. The court on Thursday ordered the release of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/28/daniel-pearl-pakistan-supreme-court-orders-release-of-acquitted-man"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ahmed Omar Saeed Sheikh}}}\uc2 , the British-born Islamist militant who had been sentenced to death for the murder of the Wall Street Journal reporter Daniel Pearl in 2002.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said the US was \u8220\'20\'1Coutraged by the Pakistani supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision\u8221\'20\'1D and said it is \u8220\'20\'1Cis an affront to terrorism victims everywhere, including in Pakistan.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Psaki confirmed that the immigration executive orders originally slated to be announced tomorrow, would be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jan/28/joe-biden-donald-trump-impeachment-kamala-harris-covid-coronavirus-live-updates?page=with:block-6012df698f08afe716c7243a#block-6012df698f08afe716c7243a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced next week instead}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 7.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Humanitarian aid and women\u8217\'20\'19s rights groups have celebrated the roll-back of the \u8216\'20\'18global gag rule,\u8217\'20\'19 but said it is only the first step in expanding access to women\u8217\'20\'19s health care across the world.\par \par \uc2 The head of \uc2 M\u233\'00\'E9decins Sans Fronti\u232\'00\'E8res\uc2  task force on safe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, Dr Manisha Kumar, said \uc2 MSF\uc2  was relieved to see the end of the global gag rule, but much more was needed to mitigate its effects. \uc2 MSF\uc2  does not accept \uc2 US government\uc2  funding so it was not directly affected by the policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHowever, we see the harmful impacts these types of policies have on limiting women\u8217\'20\'19s access to essential health care. In 2019, \uc2 MSF\uc2  treated more than 25,800 women and girls with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related complications, many of which resulted from unsafe attempts to end a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve seen women who have used pens, broken glass, or sticks to try to induce an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We\u8217\'20\'19ve seen women who drank chlorine or poisons. We have treated women who received medicines from private pharmacies but weren\u8217\'20\'19t given the correct pills, or the right information or appropriate support they needed. These are examples of what women will turn to when they don\u8217\'20\'19t have access to safe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National Women\u8217\'20\'19s Law Center\uc2  president and CEO, Fatima Goss Graves, said reversing the policy was an important first step.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut let\u8217\'20\'19s be clear: we are facing a reproductive health care crisis, compounded by the COVID-19 crisis and underlying systemic racism,\u8221\'20\'1D Graves said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe new administration must do more to urgently address the dire gaps in pregnancy related care, including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and birth control. We\u8217\'20\'19re ready to work with this administration to accomplish more sweeping change.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 7.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Now that the \u8216\'20\'18global gag rule\u8217\'20\'19 has been rescinded, it\u8217\'20\'19s worth returning to this December piece by \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Liz Ford on the expected end of the policy:\par \par \uc2 Nelly Munyasia breathed a huge sigh of relief when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won the US election in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am excited and I am hopeful that things are going to be better. We are going to access funding and we are going to save the lives of women and girls,\u8221\'20\'1D she says, before explaining how tough the past four years has been.\par \par \uc2 Munyasia is executive director of Reproductive Health Network Kenya (RHNK), which promotes health services, including offering information about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . All of its funding came from the US, via Planned Parenthood Global (PPG), which had refused to sign the global gag order. RHNK lost as much as $1m a year. Munyasia had to stop outreach programmes to marginalised communities and halt the training of more than 500 health workers. Thousands of women couldn\u8217\'20\'19t get contraceptives, HIV tests or cancer screening. Teenage pregnancies increased, and women resorted to unsafe abortions. Foetuses were found on riverbanks, Munyasia says.\par \par \uc2 The organisation went from seeing 300,000 women and girls a year to just 150,000 over two years \u8211\'20\'13 thanks only to money secured through the SheDecides movement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe lost 100% of our funding. It was devastating. We were in the process of renewing our contracts \u8230\'20\'26 when we were told by PPG that they were not able to give us funding.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2020/dec/24/were-going-to-save-lives-aid-groups-look-to-end-of-trumps-global-gag-rule"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 'We're going to save lives': aid groups look to end of Trump's 'global gag rule'}}}\par \par \uc2 6.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden signs executive orders to expand healthcare access and end 'global gag rule'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  just signed two health-related executive orders in the Oval Office. He said the best way to describe the actions was \u8220\'20\'1Cto undo the damage Trump has done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said there is nothing new in the orders. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is going back to what the situation was prior to the [former] president\u8217\'20\'19s executive orders,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The two actions:\par \par \uc2 * End the Mexico City policy, also known as the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2019/mar/26/trump-global-gag-rule-us-aid-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 global gag rule}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. This policy bans foreign non-government groups that receive US funding from providing abortions or from providing information about abortions.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/28/obamacare-aca-markets-reopening-biden-coverage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Open the health insurance market}}}\uc2  on the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare.gov from 15 February to 15 May. The Trump administration resisted calls to open the market outside of the usual six-week window for enrollment in the fall, which would have helped people seeking health insurance after losing work during the recession.\par \par \uc2 * Direct federal agencies to reconsider rules and other policies which limit access to health care and consider actions to improve access.\par \par \uc2 Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe got a lot to do and the first thing I have to do is get this Covid package passed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated at 7.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 6.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Afternoon summary\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/28/obamacare-aca-markets-reopening-biden-coverage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 At 1.30pm ET, Biden is set to sign executive actions}}}\uc2  to improve access to healthcare and end the so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cglobal gag rule\u8221\'20\'1D, which bars US funding for international non-profit organizations that provide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  counseling.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/jan/28/us-economy-shrank-2020-worst-year-since-second-world-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The US economy saw its worst year for growth}}}\uc2  since second world war. The US economy shrank by 3.5% in 2020 as the coronavirus pandemic brought the country to a shuddering halt.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jan/28/joe-biden-donald-trump-impeachment-kamala-harris-covid-coronavirus-live-updates?page=with:block-6012ee968f08653792879635#block-6012ee968f08653792879635"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Carolina state health officials}}}\uc2  said on Thursday that two cases of the coronavirus variant identified in South Africa had been detected in the state \u8211\'20\'13 the first time the variant has been found in the US.\par \par \uc2 * Ohio representative Marcia Fudge and Princeton University economist Cecilia Rouse testified in confirmation hearings before a Senate committee this morning. Biden nominated Fudge to be secretary of housing and urban development and Rouse to lead the \uc2 White House council of economic advisers\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/28/marjorie-taylor-greene-parkland-david-hogg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Survivors of the 2018 mass shooting in Parkland, Florida}}}\uc2 , asked congressional Republicans to publicly censure \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  for suggesting the school shooting was a \u8220\'20\'1Cfalse flag\u8221\'20\'1D and for harassing a teenage survivor on Capitol Hill in 2019\par \par \uc2 Updated at 6.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 6.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A key player in Fox News\u8217\'20\'19 decision to call Arizona for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on election night who came under fire from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  before losing his job has defended his role in the drama.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was proud of our being first to project that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  would win Arizona,\u8221\'20\'1D former Fox News politics editor Chris Stirewalt wrote {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/opinion/story/2021-01-28/fox-news-chris-stirewalt-firing-arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for the Los Angeles Times}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cand very happy to defend that call in the face of a public backlash egged on by former President Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBeing right and beating the competition is no act of heroism; it\u8217\'20\'19s just meeting the job description of the work I love.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CThe rebellion on the populist right against the results of the 2020 election was partly a cynical, knowing effort by political operators and their hype men in the media to steal an election or at least get rich trying. But it was also the tragic consequence of the informational malnourishment so badly afflicting the nation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I defended the call for Biden in the Arizona election, I became a target of murderous rage from consumers who were furious at not having their views confirmed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Stirewalt {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2021/jan/19/two-fox-news-executives-involved-in-election-night-arizona-call-are-out"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 left Fox News last week}}}\uc2 . The company said it had \u8220\'20\'1Crealigned its business and reporting structure to meet the demands of this new era\u8221\'20\'1D. In the LA Times, Stirewalt referred to \u8220\'20\'1Cmy firing last week\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2020/11/04/us/politics/trump-fox-news-arizona.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it has been widely reported}}}\uc2 , reacted furiously to the call on election night, which Fox News made first, surprising even its own anchors, and did not retract despite White House pressure. The Associated Press {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2020/11/19/936739072/ap-explains-calling-arizona-for-biden-early-before-it-got-very-close"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 followed}}}\uc2  hours later but other outlets did not {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.marketwatch.com/story/other-news-organizations-finally-call-arizona-for-biden-11605243924"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 call Arizona for Biden}}}\uc2  for days. By then, Pennsylvania had given the Democrat victory in the electoral college.\par \par \uc2 Arizona became one state subject to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn announced results \u8211\'20\'13 efforts repeatedly thrown out of court but in support of which a pro-Trump mob attacked the US Capitol in Washington on 6 January.\par \par \uc2 Graffiti including \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/01/06/business/media/media-murder-capitol-building.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Murder the Media}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D was found inside the Capitol, where some rioters reportedly searched for lawmakers to kidnap or kill. Five people died, one a police officer struck with a fire extinguisher.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe lie that Trump won the 2020 election wasn\u8217\'20\'19t nearly as much aimed at the opposing party as it was at the news outlets that stated the obvious, incontrovertible fact,\u8221\'20\'1D Stirewalt wrote.\par \par \uc2 He said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cconfident that the current depredations of the digital revolution will pass, just as those of the telegraph, radio and broadcast television did\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But he added: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat tugs at my mind after seeing a mob of enthusiastic ignoramuses sack the Capitol, though, is whether that sophistication will come quickly enough when outlets have the means to cater to every unhealthy craving of their consumers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 5.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 South Carolina detects first known US case of Covid-19 variant from South Africa\par \par \uc2 South Carolina state health officials said Thursday that two cases of the coronavirus variant identified in South Africa had been detected in the state- the first time the variant has been found in the US.\par \par \uc2 South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s department of health and environmental control said the two cases don\u8217\'20\'19t appear to be connected and the two people affected did not have a history of recent travel. One was detected by the state\u8217\'20\'19s public health lab and the other by the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC).\par \par \uc2 The department\u8217\'20\'19s interim public health director, Dr Brannon Traxler, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://scdhec.gov/index.php/news-releases/south-carolina-public-health-officials-detect-nations-first-known-cases-covid-19"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a statement}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThe arrival of the Sars-CoV-2 variant in our state is an important reminder to all South Carolinians that the fight against this deadly virus is far from over. While more Covid-19 vaccines are on the way, supplies are still limited. Every one of us must recommit to the fight by recognizing that we are all on the front lines now. We are all in this together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know that viruses mutate to live and live to mutate,\u8221\'20\'1D Dr Traxler said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s why it\u8217\'20\'19s critical that we all continue to do our part by taking small actions that make a big difference. These include wearing our masks, staying at least six feet apart from others, avoiding large crowds, washing our hands, getting tested often, and when we can, getting vaccinated. These are the best tools for preventing the spread of the virus, no matter the strain.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 4.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Survivors of the 2018 mass shooting in Parkland, Florida, asked congressional Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/28/marjorie-taylor-greene-parkland-david-hogg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to publicly censure Marjorie Taylor Greene}}}\uc2  for suggesting the school shooting was a \u8220\'20\'1Cfalse flag\u8221\'20\'1D and for harassing a teenage survivor on Capitol Hill in 2019.\par \par \uc2 House Republicans this week announced that Greene, a newly elected Georgia congresswoman, had been appointed to the House Education and Labor Committee.\par \par \uc2 Speaker of the House, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , said on Thursday: \u8220\'20\'1CAssigning her to the education committee when she has mocked the killing of little children at Sandy Hook, when she mocked the killing of teenagers at Marjory Stoneman Douglas - what could they be thinking?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The committee chair, Democrat Bobby Scott, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AdamHSays/status/1354818191680135171"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a strongly-worded statement that House Republicans}}}\uc2  must explain why they appointed Greene to the committee, after her documented history of promoting conspiracy theories.\par \par \uc2 House EdLabor committee chair {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BobbyScott?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @BobbyScott}}}\uc2  on \uc2 Rep. Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s appointment to the committee:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHouse Republicans have appointed someone to this Committee who claimed that the killing of 20 children and six educators at Sandy Hook... was a hoax\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VoPgJ3tSLF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VoPgJ3tSLF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 adam harris (@AdamHSays) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AdamHSays/status/1354818191680135171?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated at 6.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 4.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New York attorney general Letitia James said governor Andrew Cuomo\u8217\'20\'19s administration may have underreported nursing home deaths related to Covid-19 by as much as 50% in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ag.ny.gov/press-release/2021/attorney-general-james-releases-report-nursing-homes-response-covid-19"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a report on Thursday.}}}\uc2  According to the AP:\par \par \uc2 James has, for months, been examining discrepancies between the number of deaths being reported by the state\u8217\'20\'19s department of health, and the number of deaths reported by the homes themselves.\par \par \uc2 Her investigators looked at a sample of 62 of the state\u8217\'20\'19s roughly 600 nursing homes. They reported 1,914 deaths of residents from Covid-19, while the state department of health logged only 1,229 deaths at those same facilities.\par \par \uc2 If that same pattern exists statewide, James\u8217\'20\'19 report said, it would mean the state is underreporting deaths by nearly 56%.\par \par \uc2 Part of the gap is explained by a decision by New York\u8217\'20\'19s health agency to exclude from its count the number of nursing home patients who die after being transferred to hospitals. Hospital and nursing home officials say the state has ready access to that figure.\par \par \uc2 Health Commissioner \uc2 Howard Zucker\uc2  has said at times that the state is working on compiling that data. His department has not responded to repeated requests by the Associated Press for that figure in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 4.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 4.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has each day this week announced executive orders falling under themes including racial equity (Tuesday) and healthcare (today). Tomorrow is expected to be a day of new immigration action , but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/immigration/biden-likely-delay-executive-orders-immigration-including-task-force-reunite-n1255896"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News is reporting}}}\uc2  that might be delayed, citing two anonymous sources.\par \par \uc2 One of the expected announcements for Friday was the formation of a presidential task force {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/04/trump-administration-family-separation-immigrants-joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to reunite migrant families}}}\uc2  separated by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration at the US-Mexico border.\par \par \uc2 Biden is also expected to expand refugee admissions to the US after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/jun/26/trump-refugees-us-resettlement-program"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump lowered refugee admissions}}}\uc2  to the lowest levels since 1980; to unwind Trump programs which severely limited asylum processing, including the program known as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2021/jan/20/asylum-seekers-stranded-mexico-joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Remain in Mexico;}}}\uc2  and to review the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/feb/14/will-they-take-my-kids-away-the-immigrants-refusing-food-aid-amid-trump-crackdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 public charge}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D rule which made it difficult for poor immigrants to secure benefits and stay in the country.\par \par \uc2 3.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 After some technical difficulties, representative Marcia Fudge has been sworn-in to testify in her confirmation hearing as nominee for secretary of the department of housing and urban development (Hud).\par \par \uc2 Fudge began by introducing her family, who are in the room with her as she testifies from in her home state of Ohio. The group includes her 87-year-old mother, Marian L Garth Saffold, a retired union organizer for the \uc2 American Federation of State, County and Municipal Employees\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt bears mentioning, particularly in this moment of crisis, that Hud \u8212\'20\'14 perhaps more than any other department \u8212\'20\'14 exists to serve the most vulnerable people in America,\u8221\'20\'1D Fudge said in her opening remarks. \u8220\'20\'1CThat mandate matters a great deal to me. It is consistent with my own values, and it is precisely what has always motivated me to service.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19d like to know more about Fudge, I really recommend this {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cleveland.com/open/2020/12/years-of-work-fighting-for-northeast-ohio-earn-marcia-fudge-a-seat-at-bidens-cabinet-table.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cleveland Plain Dealer profile from December.}}}\par \par \uc2 The Senate committee on banking, housing and urban affairs is also considering the nomination of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/dec/04/joe-biden-economy-treasury-janet-yellen-neera-tanden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cecilia Rouse}}}\uc2  to be chair of the White House Council of Economic Advisers. The Princeton University economist would be the first Black woman to lead the council. She is an expert on the impact of education on the labor force and long-term unemployment and has also championed paid sick leave.\par \par \uc2 3.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Attorney {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/07/merrick-garland-joe-biden-attorney-general"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Merrick Garland}}}\uc2  has submitted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://assets.documentcloud.org/documents/20465948/sjquestionnairembg20210126-final-public.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the paperwork }}}\uc2  necessary for his nomination to be attorney general. A confirmation hearing has not yet been scheduled for Garland, whose {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2016/mar/16/obama-nominates-merrick-garland-supreme-court-dc-appeals-court-judge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2016 supreme court nomination}}}\uc2  was blocked by Senate Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Garland\u8217\'20\'19s 107-page questionnaire is essentially an extremely long CV, which also includes details about recent speeches and remarks he has made.\par \par \uc2 Amid the expected law schools speeches and ceremonial appearances, Garland has also listed his participation in a performance of Midsummer Night\u8217\'20\'19s Dream, via Zoom, as spotted by Washington Post reporter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/seungminkim/status/1354808215448416266"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Seung Min Kim.}}}\par \par \uc2 Thanks to some investigative work by \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joanegreve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joan Greve}}}\uc2 , we now know Garland\u8217\'20\'19s appearance was at an annual mock trial hosted by Shakespeare Theatre in Washington DC which examines a fictional event.\par \par \uc2 The mock trial considered the effects in a Midsummer Night\u8217\'20\'19s Dream after a play within the play was canceled because one of the lead actors is turned into a donkey. Garland was one of the judges to rule on the case.\par \par \uc2 Artistic director Simon Godwin told local news station WTOP that several supreme court justices have participated in previous mock trial events.\par \par \uc2 3.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New Jersey representative Andy Kim, a Democrat, was pictured in a viral photo on his hands and knees cleaning up the ruins left after the US Capitol insurrection. The congressmen spent an hour and a half filling trash bags with debris in the Capitol rotunda and other rooms in the building.\par \par \uc2 On \uc2 Twitter\uc2  today, he shared a photo of his first trip to the building as a child and wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CMany of you asked me why I cleaned the Capitol on Jan 6. I want to show you this photo. This is my mom, an immigrant from Korea, bringing me to DC for the first time. She took me to the Capitol and taught me to love and care for this nation that gave us everything.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Many of you asked me why I cleaned the Capitol on Jan 6. I want to show you this photo. This is my mom, an immigrant from Korea, bringing me to DC for the first time. She took me to the Capitol and taught me to love and care for this nation that gave us everything. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PecgTb5HWB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/PecgTb5HWB}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andy Kim (@AndyKimNJ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndyKimNJ/status/1354798085575233537?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 After the insurrection, Kim {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/asian-america/behind-viral-photo-rep-andy-kim-cleaning-midnight-after-riots-n1253519"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told NBC News}}}\uc2  the rotunda is his favorite room in the building: \u8220\'20\'1CI was just overwhelmed with emotion. It\u8217\'20\'19s a room that I love so much \u8212\'20\'14 it\u8217\'20\'19s the heart of the Capitol, literally the heart of this country. It pained me so much to see it in this kind of condition.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 2.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 At 10am ET today, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s nominee for secretary of housing and urban development (Hud), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/dec/08/marcia-fudge-ohio-joe-biden-housing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Marcia Fudge}}}\uc2 , will appear before a Senate committee for her confirmation hearing.\par \par \uc2 Fudge is a Democratic representative for Ohio and the former chairwoman of the Congressional Black Caucus. If confirmed, she is expected to seek to improve fair housing protections, expand access to affordable housing and to address the urgent need for households at risk of eviction, according to her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.banking.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/Fudge%20Testimony%201-28-21.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prepared remarks.}}}\par \par \uc2 Fudge will be appear at the hearing via video chat from her home in Warrensville Heights, Ohio.\par \par \uc2 Advocacy group, the \uc2 National Low Income Housing Coalition\uc2 , said Fudge:\par \par \uc2 Must work to repair the significant harm done by the current administration \u8211\'20\'13 by reinstating and furthering fair housing regulations, reinforcing protections for LGBTQ+ people experiencing homelessness, protecting immigrant families in public housing, reinvigorating and reinforcing the purpose of HUD with a depleted and demoralized workforce, and advocating for the level of investments in HUD programs that match the scale of the need.\par \par \uc2 2.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Survivors of the 2018 mass shooting in Parkland, Florida, are asking congressional {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  to publicly censure \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  for suggesting the school shooting was a \u8220\'20\'1Cfalse flag\u8221\'20\'1D and for harassing a teenage survivor on Capitol Hill in 2019, reports {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/28/marjorie-taylor-greene-parkland-david-hogg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Lois Beckett}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Greene, the newly elected Georgia congresswoman who is known for her support of the pro-Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/qanon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 QAnon}}}\uc2  conspiracy theory, was filmed in March 2019 as she followed 18-year-old David Hogg, one of the students who survived the shooting at Marjorie Stoneman Douglas high school, outside Capitol Hill.\par \par \uc2 In the video, Greene also echoes false yet frequently spread conspiracy claims that mass shooting survivors and family members of victims are \u8220\'20\'1Ccrisis actors\u8221\'20\'1D and the attacks that killed their loved ones were staged as a plot to pass gun control laws.\par \par \uc2 Fred Guttenberg, whose 14-year-old daughter, Jaime, was among the 17 students and staff killed in the shooting, told \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CShe hasn\u8217\'20\'19t disowned any of it. She hasn\u8217\'20\'19t said, \u8216\'20\'18I was wrong.\u8217\'20\'19 She hasn\u8217\'20\'19t said, \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19m sorry to the families I\u8217\'20\'19ve hurt.\u8217\'20\'19 She hasn\u8217\'20\'19t said, \u8216\'20\'18I accept the truth around Parkland, Sandy Hook, and 9/11.\u8217\'20\'19 She has let the lie live. That makes her incapable of serving as a representative in Congress.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/28/marjorie-taylor-greene-parkland-david-hogg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Parkland survivors call for Marjorie Taylor Greene's censure after harassment}}}\par \par \uc2 1.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US economy sees worst year for growth since Second World War\par \par \uc2 Those fourth quarter economic figures that came out earlier work out to the US having the worst year for growth since the end of the Second World War. It\u8217\'20\'19s a dismal coda to the Trump presidency, during which he frequently boasted of building the greatest economy in history. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2021/01/28/gdp-2020-economy-recession/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rachel Siegel and Andrew Van Dam write for the Washington Post}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The economy shrank by 3.5 percent last year as the novel coronavirus upended American business and households, making 2020 the worst year for economic growth since 1946. It is the first time the economy has contracted for the year since 2009, when Gross Domestic Product shrank by 2.5 percent during the depths of the Great Recession.\par \par \uc2 This is the last GDP report from former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s tenure. Until the pandemic, Trump was on track for an economic record that put him near the middle of the pack among recent presidents. But the covid-19 crisis has ensured that he is likely to have overseen the slowest economic growth of any president in the period since the Second World War.\par \par \uc2 1.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 It may have been on the receiving end of a lot of jokes, but Robert Burns reports for the Associated Press that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Space Force is likely to survive through the Biden era.\par \par \uc2 The reason Space Force is unlikely to go away is largely this: elimination would require an act of Congress, where a bipartisan consensus holds that America\u8217\'20\'19s increasing reliance on space is a worrying vulnerability that is best addressed by a branch of the military focused exclusively on this problem. The service celebrated its one year anniversary in December.\par \par \uc2 The new service also is linked to an increasing US wariness of China, which is developing capabilities to threaten US satellites in space and which has become, in the minds of some, the singular national security challenge. Russia, too, stands accused by Washington of seeking to challenge American dominance in space.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re building capabilities to use space against us. We have to be able to respond to that,\u8221\'20\'1D Gen. John Hyten, vice chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, told the National Security Space Association, an advocacy group, last week, referring to Russia and China.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has not publicly commented on his intentions with Space Force. His defense secretary, Lloyd Austin, has been noncommittal, while also stressing the strategic importance of space.\par \par \uc2 Although some see it as a Trump vanity project, in the military it\u8217\'20\'19s seen more soberly as an affirmation of the need to more effectively organize for the defense of US interests in space.\par \par \uc2 While far smaller than any other branch of the military, Space Force is acquiring the standard trappings of a service, including an official flag, logo, seal and doctrine. It has launched commercials to attract recruits. The force is planning to expand its ranks from 2,400 active-duty members to 6,400 by the end of this year.\par \par \uc2 Still, there have been mis-steps along the way. Social media and Marvel Comics fans were incredibly amused when, after lengthy debate, it was decided last month that Space Force members would be called \u8220\'20\'1Cguardians\u8221\'20\'1D, echoing the Guardians of the Galaxy franchise.\par \par \uc2 1.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Number of Americans filing first-time unemployment claims falls slightly to 847,000\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/useconomy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US economy}}}\uc2  grew at an annual rate of 4% in the fourth quarter, following 33.4% growth in the previous quarter, when the economy bounced back after sharp declines earlier in the year caused by the coronavirus pandemic, according to the advance estimate from the \uc2 US Commerce Department\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s essentially the last verdict on the Trump era, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/gdp-fourth-quarter-b63627cc-59c4-47fd-a389-33501283be41.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes Courtenay Brown at Axios}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It shows a sharp slowdown in growth compared to the previous quarter, as the pandemic got worse and government aid petered out.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile other data just out shows that the number of Americans filing for first-time unemployment claims fell slightly to 847,000 last week. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/business/economy/weekly-initial-jobless-claims-fall-slightly-847-000-vs-estimates-n1255953"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lucy Bayly at NBC News notes}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Economists had predicted a total of 875,000 claims for the week ended 23 January.\par \par \uc2 Ten months into the pandemic, the weekly figure \u8212\'20\'14 which is a proxy for layoffs \u8212\'20\'14 continues to hover just below 1 million. That\u8217\'20\'19s five times higher than its pre-pandemic average, though far lower than the March peak of 7 million.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThanks to Covid-19, there are still 10 million jobs missing from the economy, and there are still 14.5 million people claiming unemployment benefits. People need help,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dan North, chief economist at Euler Hermes North America. \u8220\'20\'1CMaintaining stimulus spending, in particular, income support, has been the right thing to do all along and it still is.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There will be more follow-up to these figures on our business live blog today:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2021/jan/28/gamestop-share-surge-sparks-concerns-stock-markets-slide-again-business-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 GameStop surges further 40% amid frenzy; global stock markets slide \u8211\'20\'13 business live}}}\par \par \uc2 1.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Nina Lakhani has also written for us today on the theme of demands on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s environmental policies:\par \par \uc2 Border communities and environmentalists are urging \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to take immediate steps to remediate the environmental and cultural destruction caused by construction of the border wall during the previous administration.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  sequestered $15bn \u8211\'20\'13 most of it from military funds \u8211\'20\'13 to partially fulfill an anti-immigration campaign promise to build a \u8220\'20\'1Cbig beautiful wall\u8221\'20\'1D along the southern border with Mexico.\par \par \uc2 As a result, hundreds of miles of the borderlands \u8211\'20\'13 including sacred Native American sites and protected public lands \u8211\'20\'13 have been bulldozed, blasted and parched over the past four years, with little environmental assessment or oversight thanks to waivers suspending dozens of federal laws in order to expedite construction.\par \par \uc2 Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/presidential-actions/2021/01/20/proclamation-termination-of-emergency-with-respect-to-southern-border-of-united-states-and-redirection-of-funds-diverted-to-border-wall-construction/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordered construction to pause}}}\uc2  on his first day in office, but community leaders and experts consulted by \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  warned that urgent action is needed to stop the damage to fragile biodiverse landscapes and scarce water sources getting worse. They are urging Biden to:\par \par \uc2 * Cancel the outstanding contracts, most of which the \uc2 army corps of engineers\uc2  awarded to a handful of firms with little transparency. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2020/10/27/border-wall-texas-cost-rising-trump/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Top officials at these firms are regular donors to the Republican party.}}}\uc2  The \uc2 Government Accountability Office\uc2  will soon publish its audit of the army corps\u8217\'20\'19 role in the wall including the contracts and status of construction.\par \par \uc2 * Deploy a team of experts including hydrologists, ecologists, zoologists and botanists, community and tribal advocates to assess the damage, and formulate a plan to restore critical habitat, waterways, wildlife migration corridors and tribal cultural sites.\par \par \uc2 * Tearing down the wall where safe to do so, and allocate federal funds for the clean-up to ensure hundreds of tonnes of metal, concrete and barbed wire are safely disposed of.\par \par \uc2 * Rescind the waivers which suspended {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://u.osu.edu/madsen.34/maps/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 84 federal laws }}}\uc2  that mandate protections relating to clean air and water, endangered species, public lands, contracts and the rights of Native Americans.\par \par \uc2 * Withdraw scores of lawsuits against private landowners on the border that seek to strip them of their land through eminent domain.\par \par \uc2 Read more of Nina Lakhani\u8217\'20\'19s report here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/jan/28/border-wall-reverse-environmental-cultural-destruction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden faces call to heal environmental and cultural scars of Trump border wall}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/jan/28/border-wall-reverse-environmental-cultural-destruction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden faces call to heal environmental and cultural scars of Trump border wall}}}\par \par \uc2 1.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Back to more serious matters, and on the environment, Nick Estes, a citizen of the Lower Brule Sioux Tribe, writes for us today to say that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/jan/28/joe-biden-keystone-pipeline-climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden doesn\u8217\'20\'19t get a climate pass yet just for cancelling the Keystone XL pipeline}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 There is every reason to celebrate the end of a decade-long fight against Keystone XL. Tribal nations and Indigenous movements hope it will be a watershed moment for bolder actions, demanding the same fates for contentious pipeline projects such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthout.org/articles/as-biden-axes-kxl-pipeline-water-protectors-urge-him-to-reject-dapl-and-line-3/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Line 3}}}\uc2  and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://indiancountrytoday.com/news/tribes-to-joe-biden-stop-dakota-access-pipeline-wFl-6qRUm06uku7ktsJ-GA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dakota Access pipeline}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Biden has also vowed to review more than 100 environmental rules and regulations that were weakened or reversed by Trump and to restore Obama-era protections to two Indigenous sacred sites, Bears Ears and Grand Staircase-Escalante, which are also national monuments in Utah. And he issued a \u8220\'20\'1Ctemporary moratorium\u8221\'20\'1D on all oil and gas leases in the Arctic national wildlife refuge, sacred territory to many Alaskan Natives.\par \par \uc2 None of these victories would have been possible without sustained Indigenous resistance and tireless advocacy.\par \par \uc2 But there is also good reason to be wary of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/biden-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration}}}\uc2  and its parallels with the Obama administration. The overwhelming majority of people appointed to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s climate team come from Obama\u8217\'20\'19s old team. And their current climate actions are focused almost entirely on restoring Obama-era policies.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s policy catchphrases of \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica is back\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cbuild back better\u8221\'20\'1D and his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2019-06-19/biden-tells-elite-donors-he-doesn-t-want-to-demonize-the-rich"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 assurance}}}\uc2  to rich donors that \u8220\'20\'1Cnothing would fundamentally change\u8221\'20\'1D should also be cause for concern. A return to imagined halcyon days of an Obama presidency or to \u8220\'20\'1Cnormalcy\u8221\'20\'1D\u8211\'20\'13 which for Indigenous peoples in the United States is everyday colonialism \u8211\'20\'13 isn\u8217\'20\'19t justice, nor is it the radical departure from the status quo we need to bolster Indigenous rights and combat the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/jan/28/joe-biden-keystone-pipeline-climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nick Estes \u8211\'20\'13 Biden killed the Keystone Pipeline. Good, but he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t get a climate pass just yet}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/jan/28/joe-biden-keystone-pipeline-climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden killed the Keystone Pipeline. Good, but he doesn't get a climate pass just yet | Nick Estes}}}\par \par \uc2 1.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 It takes all sorts to make the world go around, and I note that for our books desk New York writer and journalist J Oliver Conroy has taken on the unenviable task of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2021/jan/28/erotica-fan-fiction-for-the-trump-era-chuck-tingle-jessica-stranger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reading the weirdest Trump-era erotica so you don\u8217\'20\'19t have to}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In recent years, \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s e-books market has nurtured a flourishing cottage industry of self-published romance and erotic literature \u8211\'20\'13 and the Trump years have inspired many to put pen to paper. The most successful authors (most write under pseudonyms) are known for their prolific publication, thesaurus-aided descriptions of the human anatomy, and responsiveness to current events. The surreality of the past four years was particularly generative of their creative juices. With the Trump era now drawn to a chaotic close, we decided to review four of the most memorable entries in this niche literary genre.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m strangely drawn to the title \u8220\'20\'1CMy Antifa Lover\u8221\'20\'1D, although slightly disappointed that Conroy opted to review Chuck Tingle\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CPounded In The Butt By The Handsome Physical Manifestation Of Tromp\u8217\'20\'19s [sic] Twitter Ban That Should\u8217\'20\'19ve Come Years Sooner But Fine Now That It\u8217\'20\'19s Here High Five\u8221\'20\'1D rather than the frankly superior \u8220\'20\'1CDomald Tromp [sic] Pounded In The Butt By The Handsome Russian T-Rex Who Also Peed On His Butt And Then Blackmailed Him With The Videos Of His Butt Getting Peed On\u8221\'20\'1D. No, I have no idea how the internet got us here either, really.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2021/jan/28/erotica-fan-fiction-for-the-trump-era-chuck-tingle-jessica-stranger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18My Antifa Lover\u8217\'20\'19: I read the weirdest Trump-era erotica so you don\u8217\'20\'19t have to}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2021/jan/28/erotica-fan-fiction-for-the-trump-era-chuck-tingle-jessica-stranger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18My Antifa Lover\u8217\'20\'19: I read the weirdest Trump-era erotica so you don't have to}}}\par \par \uc2 12.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration already has a very different approach to promoting Covid information to what went on before under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Dr Anthony Fauci described himself as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe skunk at the picnic\u8221\'20\'1D under that administration, but the new president has promised a new era of openess, with regular briefings from officials.\par \par \uc2 Fauci will be up before an audience again today \u8211\'20\'13 he will be joining a virtual event hosted by the \uc2 American Federation of Teachers\uc2  (AFT).\par \par \uc2 AFT president \uc2 Randi Weingarten\uc2  and National Education Association president Becky Pringle will also take part in the online \u8220\'20\'1Ctown hall\u8221\'20\'1D style event, which will discuss the Covid-19 pandemic and its specific impact on educators, students and schools.\par \par \uc2 Fauci will answer questions from educators around the country and engage in an in-depth conversation with Weingarten and Pringle about reopening schools safely, testing, and vaccines roll-out. It takes place at 6 pm EST, you can {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://actionnetwork.org/forms/fauci"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 submit questions in advance}}}\uc2 , and watch it either {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/AFTunion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on Facebook}}}\uc2  or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/c/aftvideos"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on YouTube}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 12.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The regulatory changes Biden is asking federal health officials to undertake today aren\u8217\'20\'19t likely to happen overnight, because hastily written rules are more easily overturned in court, as the Trump administration repeatedly found out. Time and again, federal judges ruled that Trump officials had ran roughshod over legal requirements for regulators, such as demonstrating they\u8217\'20\'19ve considered all sides of an issue.\par \par \uc2 The idea of reopening Obamacare\u8217\'20\'19s health insurance markets for a period of time has broad support though, including from consumer groups, professional medical associations, insurers and business organizations.\par \par \uc2 Ricardo Alonso-Zaldivar writes for the Associated Press that although the number of uninsured Americans has grown because of job losses in the coronavirus economy, the Trump administration did little to address the issue.\par \par \uc2 The Obama-era Affordable Care Act law covers more than 23 million people through a mix of subsidized private insurance sold in all states, and expanded Medicaid adopted by 38 states, with Southern states being the major exception. Coverage is available to people who don\u8217\'20\'19t have job-based health insurance, with the Medicaid expansion geared to those with low incomes.\par \par \uc2 Of some 28 million uninsured Americans before the pandemic, the nonpartisan \uc2 Kaiser Family Foundation\uc2  has estimated that more than 16 million were eligible for some form of subsidized coverage through the health law.\par \par \uc2 Experts agree that number of uninsured people has risen because of layoffs in the coronavirus economy, perhaps by 5 million to 10 million, but authoritative estimates await government studies due later this year.\par \par \uc2 12.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The role that race should play in deciding who gets priority for the Covid-19 vaccine in the next phase of the rollout is being put to the test in Oregon as tensions around equity and access to the shots emerge nationwide, reports Gillian Flaccus for the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 An advisory committee that provides recommendations to Oregon\u8217\'20\'19s governor and public health authorities will vote later today on whether to prioritize people of color, target those with chronic medical conditions or focus on some combination of groups at higher risk from the coronavirus. Others, such as essential workers, refugees, inmates and people under 65 living in group settings, are also being considered.\par \par \uc2 The 27-member committee in Oregon, a Democratic-led state that\u8217\'20\'19s overwhelmingly white, was formed with the goal of keeping fairness at the heart of its vaccine rollout. Its members were selected to include racial minorities and ethnic groups, from Somalian refugees to Pacific Islanders to tribes. The committee\u8217\'20\'19s recommendations are not binding but provide critical input for Gov. Kate Brown and guide health authorities crafting the rollout.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s about revealing the structural racism that remains hidden. It influences the disparities we experienced before the pandemic and exacerbated the disparities we experienced during the pandemic,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kelly Gonzales, a member of the Cherokee Nation of Oklahoma and a health disparity expert on the committee.\par \par \uc2 The virus has disproportionately affected people of color. Last week, the Biden administration reemphasized the importance of including \u8220\'20\'1Csocial vulnerability\u8221\'20\'1D in state vaccination plans with race, ethnicity and the rural-urban divide at the forefront and asked states to identify \u8220\'20\'1Cpharmacy deserts\u8221\'20\'1D where getting shots into arms will be difficult.\par \par \uc2 Overall, 18 states included ways to measure equity in their original vaccine distribution plans last fall and more have likely done so since the shots started arriving, said Harald Schmidt, a medical ethicist at the \uc2 University of Pennsylvania\uc2  who has studied vaccine fairness extensively.\par \par \uc2 Some, such as Tennessee, proposed reserving 5% of its allocation for \u8220\'20\'1Chigh-disadvantage areas,\u8221\'20\'1D while states like Ohio plan to use social vulnerability factors to decide where to distribute vaccine, he said.\par \par \uc2 Attempts to address inequities in vaccine access have already prompted backlashes in some places. Dallas authorities recently reversed a decision to prioritize the most vulnerable ZIP codes primarily communities of color after Texas threatened to reduce the city\u8217\'20\'19s vaccine supply. That kind of pushback is likely to become more pronounced as states move deeper into the rollout and wrestle with difficult questions about need and short supply.\par \par \uc2 To avoid legal challenges, almost all states looking at race and ethnicity in their vaccine plans are turning to a tool called a \u8220\'20\'1Csocial vulnerability index\u8221\'20\'1D or a \u8220\'20\'1Cdisadvantage index.\u8221\'20\'1D Such an index includes more than a dozen data points everything from income to education level to health outcomes to car ownership to target disadvantaged populations without specifically citing race or ethnicity.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe point is not, \u8216\'20\'18We want to make sure that the Obama family gets the vaccine before the Clinton family.\u8217\'20\'19 We don\u8217\'20\'19t care. They can both safely wait,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe do care that the person who works in a meatpacking plant in a crowded living situation does get it first. It\u8217\'20\'19s not about race, it\u8217\'20\'19s about race and disadvantage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 12.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Los Angeles is vaccinating health care workers, first responders and residents older than 65. But as the region battles one of the worst coronavirus outbreaks in the US, people are chasing vaccine doses ahead of their allotted tier, queuing in lines for hours, visiting sites after the official time ends. Information about where to show up for extra doses and when is typically passed word of mouth.\par \par \uc2 Officially, there is no waiting or end-of-the day policy, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://publichealth.lacounty.gov/acd/docs/LACPhase1AFullGuidance.pdf?utm_content=&utm_medium=email&utm_name=&utm_source=govdelivery&utm_term="}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 county officials}}}\uc2  say. But given the dire health emergency, they also don\u8217\'20\'19t want doses to go to waste. The gap between these two creates a space for \u8220\'20\'1Cvaccine vultures\u8221\'20\'1D to swoop down.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s hard to put a number on how many people are scoring vaccine doses ahead of schedule, but it could be a few dozen each day at each of the six mega sites scattered around the 500 square miles of Los Angeles county.\par \par \uc2 That there are vaccines left over at all is due to several factors. About 10% of people with appointments do not show up for their shot, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2021-01-23/standby-lines-backdoor-vaccine-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to press reports}}}\uc2 . Vials containing the Moderna vaccine have to be used within six hours after opening before they have to be thrown out. And while vials are supposed to contain five doses, injectors can often coax six doses out of them.\par \par \uc2 In a mid-January statement, Los Angeles county said its department of public health \u8220\'20\'1Cdoes not condone wasting of any precious vaccine doses and has not and is not directing providers to throw away unused doses\u8221\'20\'1D. The statement added that the county was moving to set up vaccine clinics on quick turnaround whenever it learned of potential vaccine expirations. (The county public health department did not respond to requests for comment for this story.)\par \par \uc2 Dr Monya De, an LA-area physician who volunteered at the Inglewood Forum, which is one of six mega sites for vaccine dispersal in LA county, said some family members accompanying seniors to get their shot asked if there were any available for them as well. \u8220\'20\'1COur instructions are to vaccinate only the person who was registered,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a volume issue: we have a large volume of people in LA who need to get vaccinated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But De said she did wonder about resource allocation and if the current approach is the best way to get the most needles in the most arms. \u8220\'20\'1CI could see potentially the instruction being changed to: yes, if you have an extra vaccine you can inject people who are coming along in the same family.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more of Katharine Gammon\u8217\'20\'19s report here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/28/los-angeles-residents-stalk-covid-vaccine-sites-in-hopes-of-leftover-doses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Los Angeles residents stalk Covid vaccine sites in hopes of leftover doses}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/28/los-angeles-residents-stalk-covid-vaccine-sites-in-hopes-of-leftover-doses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Los Angeles residents stalk Covid vaccine sites in hopes of leftover doses}}}\par \par \uc2 11.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trevor Hunnicutt at Reuters provides this breakdown of the actions on healthcare we are expecting from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  later today:\par \par \uc2 * Biden will restore access to Healthcare.gov with an executive order on Thursday afternoon. The order will allow people to sign up for insurance through the government exchange from 15 February to 15 May. The program is normally accessible for just six weeks a year.\par \par \uc2 * Biden also plans to direct federal agencies to \u8220\'20\'1Cre-examine\u8221\'20\'1D Trump-era policies like work requirements that made it more difficult for people to qualify for Medicaid, the government-run health insurance program for low earners.\par \par \uc2 * He will rescind the \u8220\'20\'1CMexico City Policy\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 also known as the \u8220\'20\'1CGlobal gag rule\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 that bans US funding for international non-profit organizations that provide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  counseling.\par \par \uc2 Biden has vowed to shore up the Healthcare.gov and other programs created under former President Barack Obama\u8217\'20\'19s sweeping 2010 Affordable Care Act. He has argued that the changes are more urgent because of the coronavirus pandemic, which has killed more than 400,000 Americans.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have long opposed the healthcare restructuring law, criticizing the cost and quality of care as well as extensive government involvement in healthcare markets.\par \par \uc2 11.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 The nomination of Alejandro Mayorkas as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s preferred secretary of Homeland Security looks like it is the first cabinet position to get mired in Republican delaying tactics in the Senate, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2021/01/27/politics/senate-republicans-mayorkas-nomination-dhs/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Manu Raju and Veronica Stracqualursi report for CNN}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 In confirming Republican plans to filibuster, Sen. John Cornyn of Texas told reporters yesterday on Capitol Hill that \u8220\'20\'1Cthere\u8217\'20\'19s a number of problems\u8221\'20\'1D with Mayorkas\u8217\'20\'19 nomination.Republicans argue that Mayorkas hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been properly vetted on immigration issues and are calling for an additional hearing into his nomination.\par \par \uc2 The Senate has scheduled a procedural vote to break the filibuster at 1:45pm ET today. After the Senate breaks the filibuster \u8211\'20\'13 which requires 51 votes \u8211\'20\'13 the final confirmation vote will be Monday evening.\par \par \uc2 Sen. Josh Hawley of Missouri attempted to block Mayorkas\u8217\'20\'19 quick consideration after last week\u8217\'20\'19s hearing, arguing in a statement that Mayorkas had inadequately explained how he will secure the US southern border.\par \par \uc2 In a letter Tuesday, Cornyn led seven other Republican senators on the \uc2 Senate Judiciary Committee\uc2  in demanding a hearing for Mayorkas before their panel. They argued that Mayorkas spoke about \u8220\'20\'1Cimmigration priorities at length\u8221\'20\'1D during his 19 January hearing proving that immigration issues will be a \u8220\'20\'1Ctop focus\u8221\'20\'1D of his, and that the \uc2 Senate Judiciary Committee\uc2  has jurisdiction over immigration matters.\par \par \uc2 Democratic Sen. Dick Durbin, who is set to chair the Judiciary Committee, told CNN, \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t see why that\u8217\'20\'19s necessary\u8221\'20\'1D and called the request for a hearing \u8220\'20\'1Ctotally political.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2021/01/27/politics/senate-republicans-mayorkas-nomination-dhs/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN \u8211\'20\'13 GOP threatens filibuster for Mayorkas nomination to be DHS secretary}}}\par \par \uc2 11.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 John Hudson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/blinken-state-department-media/2021/01/27/1c195286-60db-11eb-ac8f-4ae05557196e_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had this overnight}}}\uc2  at the Washington Post, on newly-confirmed secretary of state Antony Blinken :\par \par \uc2 Blinken\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to overhaul the combative relationship between State Department officials and the media is among the decisions he is facing about what to keep or discard from the Trump era.\par \par \uc2 In an early change, Blinken said he would resume the department\u8217\'20\'19s daily news briefing starting next week \u8212\'20\'14 a practice that ended during the Trump administration as spokespeople feared contradicting the president\u8217\'20\'19s rapidly shifting positions.\par \par \uc2 He also pledged to allow journalists access to him during trips abroad once the coronavirus pandemic subsides, something that secretaries of state Mike Pompeo and Rex Tillerson sharply curtailed during their tenures.\par \par \uc2 While the Biden administration has begun overturning several Trump-era actions, on foreign policy, Blinken has pledged not to throw out all of the previous policies, such as moving the US Embassy to Jerusalem.\par \par \uc2 On Yemen, Blinken said he would move quickly to review the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s decision to label the country\u8217\'20\'19s Houthi rebels a terrorist organization, acknowledging concerns from aid groups that the designation would worsen what the United Nations considers the world\u8217\'20\'19s worst humanitarian crisis.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/blinken-state-department-media/2021/01/27/1c195286-60db-11eb-ac8f-4ae05557196e_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post \u8211\'20\'13 Blinken turns away from Trump-era approaches, starting with media relations}}}\par \par \uc2 11.18am GMT\par \par \uc2 Also on the foreign policy front, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said in a presidential debate last October that he would only agree to meet North Korean leader Kim Jong Un if he agreed to \u8220\'20\'1Cdraw down\u8221\'20\'1D North Korea\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear capacity.\par \par \uc2 South Korea\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister Chung Sye-kyun has today said North Korea and the United States should seek an initial denuclearisation deal that includes a halt to the North\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear activity and a cut in its programme in exchange for some sanctions relief.\par \par \uc2 In his first interview with a foreign media outlet since taking office a year ago, the prime minister told Reuters that \u8220\'20\'1Ccreative\u8221\'20\'1D thinking and mutual incentives were needed to get negotiations going again and prevent another breakdown.\par \par \uc2 Kim Jong Un and former US president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  promised to build new relations and work towards the denuclearisation of the Korean peninsula at their first summit in 2018, but a second summit and ensuing working-level talks fell apart.\par \par \uc2 North Korea had offered to dismantle its main nuclear complex in exchange for the lifting of major \uc2 UN\uc2  sanctions but the United States said North Korea should also hand over its nuclear weapons and bomb fuel.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can begin with a freeze in all nuclear activities and reduction of some of their programme,\u8221\'20\'1D Chung said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt would be best if we could get rid of all of it, once and for all, but it\u8217\'20\'19s not easy and we need an alternative.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden has not yet announced any new policy for North Korea.\par \par \uc2 Chung said limited sanctions relief could help revive and sustain the momentum of any talks as that was the most attractive incentive for North Korea. \u8220\'20\'1CSouth Korea and the United States know what North Korea wants,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Chung\u8217\'20\'19s remarks came days after South Korea\u8217\'20\'19s President Moon Jae-in called for new US president to build on progress made by Kim and Trump.\par \par \uc2 11.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 US takes aim at China territorial claims as Biden vows to back Japan\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  has vowed to strengthen the US\u8217\'20\'19s alliance with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/japan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Japan}}}\uc2  to counter growing Chinese military activity in the volatile Asia-Pacific region, including a commitment to defend the Senkakus, a group of islands in the East China sea administered by Tokyo but claimed by Beijing.\par \par \uc2 The US president and Prime Minister {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/yoshihide-suga"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Yoshihide Suga}}}\uc2  agreed during a phone call that their countries\u8217\'20\'19 security alliance was \u8220\'20\'1Cthe cornerstone of peace and prosperity in a free and open Indo-Pacific\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s vow to strengthen security arrangements in the region contrasted with the approach taken by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who publicly mulled withdrawing troops from Japan and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/south-korea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Korea}}}\uc2 , both key US allies.\par \par \uc2 Trump also complained that Tokyo and Seoul were not paying enough towards their own security and called on them to buy more US-made defence equipment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe managed to have substantial exchanges,\u8221\'20\'1D Suga said after his 30-minute call with Biden. \u8220\'20\'1CWe agreed to strengthen our alliance firmly by having more phone calls like this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden reaffirmed the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US}}}\uc2  commitment to provide \u8220\'20\'1Cextended deterrence\u8221\'20\'1D to Japan, a reference to the US nuclear umbrella, the White House said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 They also agreed on the need for the complete denuclearisation of the Korean peninsula, as speculation mounts over how Biden intends to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jan/12/north-korea-set-for-collision-course-with-us-as-kim-jong-un-solidifies-one-man-rule"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 engage with the North Korean leader, Kim Jong-un}}}\uc2 , over his nuclear and ballistic missile programmes.\par \par \uc2 Read more of Justin McCurry\u8217\'20\'19s report from Tokyo: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/28/us-takes-aim-at-china-territorial-claims-as-biden-vows-to-back-japan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US takes aim at China territorial claims as Biden vows to back Japan}}}\par \par \uc2 11.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 If today is all about healthcare from the Biden administration, yesterday was all about the climate crisis. As well as the executive orders signed by the president, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s climate envoy \uc2 John Kerry\uc2  also spoke.\par \par \uc2 He said that US workers have been fed a false narrative on climate change over the last few years. Kerry highlighted job growth in renewable energy as evidence of a misled belief that had spread that resolving climate change would come at a cost to workers. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the clip\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 10.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 Associated Press have this brief vaccine story today, that Oregon health workers who got stuck in a snowstorm on their way back from a Covid-19 vaccination event went car to car injecting stranded drivers before several of the doses expired.\par \par \uc2 Josephine County Public Health said on \uc2 Facebook\uc2  that the \u8220\'20\'1Cimpromptu vaccine clinic\u8221\'20\'1D took place after about 20 employees were stopped in traffic on a highway after a vaccination clinic.\par \par \uc2 Six of the vaccines were getting close to expiring so the workers decided to offer them to other stranded drivers.\par \par \uc2 The shots were meant for other people, but \u8220\'20\'1Cthe snow meant those doses wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t make it to them before they expired,\u8221\'20\'1D the health department said.\par \par \uc2 Not wanting to waste them, staff walked from vehicle to vehicle, offering people a chance to receive the vaccine. A county ambulance was on hand for safety.\par \par \uc2 All the doses were administered, including one to a Josephine County Sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s Office employee who had arrived too late for the vaccination clinic but ended up stopped with the others, officials said.\par \par \uc2 Josephine County Public Health Director \uc2 Mike Weber\uc2  said it was one of the \u8220\'20\'1Ccoolest operations he\u8217\'20\'19d been a part of.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 10.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 Rachana Pradhan and Fred Schulte of Kaiser Health News report for us this morning on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/jan/28/us-covid-data-race-occupation-healthcare-workers-vaccines"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 concerns over gaps in the data collection around the vaccination program}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 As they rush to vaccinate millions of Americans, health officials are struggling to collect critically important information, such as race, ethnicity and occupation, of every person they jab.\par \par \uc2 The data being collected is so scattered that there\u8217\'20\'19s little insight into which healthcare workers, or first responders, have been among the people getting the initial vaccines, as intended \u8211\'20\'13 or how many doses instead have gone to people who should be much further down the list.\par \par \uc2 The gaps \u8211\'20\'13 which experts say reflect decades of underfunding of public health programs \u8211\'20\'13 could mean that well-connected people and health personnel who have no contact with patients are getting vaccines before front-line workers, who are at much higher risk for illness. Federal and state officials prioritized health workers plus residents and staffs of nursing homes for the first wave of shots.\par \par \uc2 Although officials leading president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Covid response have pledged to tackle racial equities as they seek to control the pandemic, lapses in reporting race or ethnicity could hinder efforts to identify and track whether minorities hit especially hard by the pandemic are getting shots at a high-enough rate to achieve hoped-for levels of herd immunity. So far, limited data in multiple states shows Black residents are getting vaccinated at lower rates than whites.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery state knows where they\u8217\'20\'19ve sent vaccine, and every provider has to report inventory. But as far as who is being vaccinated, that one is a little more tricky,\u8221\'20\'1D said Claire Hannan, executive director of the Association of Immunization Managers.\par \par \uc2 Data that eventually makes its way to the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  and other federal systems is \u8220\'20\'1Conly going to be as good as whatever you can get out of the vaccine registries\u8221\'20\'1D that vary by state, said \uc2 Dr Marcus Plescia\uc2 , chief medical officer for the Association of State and Territorial {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Health}}}\uc2  Officials. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re all different and, going into this, they were all at different stages of how robust they were.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/jan/28/us-covid-data-race-occupation-healthcare-workers-vaccines"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Data gaps make it hard to know if priority health workers got vaccines first}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/jan/28/us-covid-data-race-occupation-healthcare-workers-vaccines"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Data gaps make it hard to know if priority health workers got vaccines first}}}\par \par \uc2 10.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 Yesterday there were 152,478 new coronavirus cases recorded in the US, and 3,943 further deaths. The total death toll, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gisanddata.maps.arcgis.com/apps/opsdashboard/index.html#/bda7594740fd40299423467b48e9ecf6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Johns Hopkins University figures}}}\uc2 , has risen to 428,865. Experts have projected it will reach 500,000 by the end of February. Yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s death toll puts it among the ten worst days since the pandemic began, and January\u8217\'20\'19s death toll is already the worst on record.\par \par \uc2 There continued to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://covidtracking.com/data/national/hospitalization"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brighter news on hospitalizations}}}\uc2 , with the number of people in hospital in the US falling to 107,444. It is the fifteenth consecutive day the number has fallen, and the lowest level seen since 11 December.\par \par \uc2 CDC figures state that 24.6m doses of vaccine have been administered out of the 47.2m distributed. Madeline Holcombe and Theresa Waldrop {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2021/01/27/us/us-coronavirus-wednesday/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report for CNN}}}\uc2  that this discrepancy is due to shots being held back to give people a second dose.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s important that when you\u8217\'20\'19re looking at states\u8217\'20\'19 inventories that you recognize that some of that inventory is being held for the very important second shot,\u8221\'20\'1D White House Covid-19 Response Coordinator Jeff Zients said yesterday.\par \par \uc2 Some of the distributed doses may have also just arrived at their destination or may still be on the way, and there\u8217\'20\'19s also a lag in reporting the number of shots given, CDC Director \uc2 Dr. Rochelle Walensky\uc2  said in a CNN town hall Wednesday night.\par \par \uc2 Still, a bottleneck remains, she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you do all that math, you still end up with some millions of doses that are sitting on the shelves and have not yet been administered,\u8221\'20\'1D Walensky said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd in fact, that\u8217\'20\'19s one of the ways that we have to get resources to the states to make sure that they can quickly administer the vaccines that are on the shelves.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 default\par \par \uc2 10.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden to re-open HealthCare.gov sign-up and expand access to Medicaid\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a reminder of what we are expecting from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  today when he addresses the issue of healthcare access at 1:30pm EST (6:30pm GMT). {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/health/biden-to-reopen-aca-insurance-marketplaces-as-pandemic-has-cost-millions-of-american-their-coverage/2021/01/25/ccfc2402-5e74-11eb-9061-07abcc1f9229_story.html?utm_campaign=KHN%3A%20Daily%20Health%20Policy%20Report&utm_medium=email&_hsmi=108166802&_hsenc=p2ANqtz-92bdcbbWw8kEAzKtGppQi_cEvZuPVXbn6FN7aRL9t5TQiEgaTqmAoUqRIUv8nE6dWsikY21AwHnYWURc9H_7xrVt6vDw&utm_content=108166802&utm_source=hs_email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 As the Washington Post reported}}}\uc2 , he will reopen federal marketplaces selling Affordable Care Act health plans and lower recent barriers to joining Medicaid:\par \par \uc2 Under one order, HealthCare.gov, the online insurance marketplace for Americans who cannot get affordable coverage through their jobs, will swiftly reopen for at least a few months. Ordinarily, signing up for such coverage is tightly restricted outside a six-week period late each year.\par \par \uc2 Another part of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s scheduled actions is intended to reverse Trump-era changes to Medicaid that critics say damaged Americans\u8217\'20\'19 access to the safety-net insurance. It is unclear whether Biden\u8217\'20\'19s order will undo a Trump-era rule allowing states to impose work requirements, or simply direct federal health officials to review rules to make sure they expand coverage to the program that insures about 70 million low-income people in the United States. Biden has been saying for many months that helping people get insurance is a crucial federal responsibility.\par \par \uc2 The most ambitious parts of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign health-care platform would require Congress to provide consent and money. Those include creating a government insurance option alongside the ACA health plans sold by private insurers, and helping poor residents afford ACA coverage if they live in about a dozen states that have not expanded their Medicaid programs under the decade-old health law.\par \par \uc2 10.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 Much criticism of \u8220\'20\'1CGreen New Deal\u8221\'20\'1D and environmental policies in the US from Republicans has focussed on the cost to the economy and specifically to jobs. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has been attempting to sell his program for dealing with the climate crisis as specifically good for the creation of well-paid union jobs.\par \par \uc2 When I think of climate change I think of jobs. We're going to tackle the climate crisis and create good-paying, union jobs at the same time. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2VXwVmp7QZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/2VXwVmp7QZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1354617694495141898?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 28, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a reminder of what the president said yesterday about the climate crisis. In a sharp 180-degree turn from the Trump administration, Biden signed a series of executive orders to address the \u8216\'20\'18existential threat\u8217\'20\'19 of the climate crisis. He insisted his climate plan would create millions of new \u8216\'20\'18clean\u8217\'20\'19 jobs to replace those lost in the coal and oil industries.\par \par \uc2 10.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 Welcome to our US politics live blog for Thursday. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a quick catch-up on where we are, and what we can expect to see today.\par \par \uc2 * During the first Covid-19 briefing with Biden administration experts, officials said the US coronavirus death toll would hit 500,000 by February. Yesterday there were 152,478 new cases and 3,943 further deaths in the US. Hospitalizations in the US fell slightly to 107,444.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will sign executive orders on expanding access to healthcare at 1:30pm EST (6:30pm GMT). Jen Psaki will hold a press briefing an hour later.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/27/joe-biden-climate-change-executive-orders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The president signed a flurry of executive orders to address the climate crisis yesterday}}}\uc2 , by focusing on creating good-paying jobs in renewable energy. \u8220\'20\'1CWe must do this, we can do this, we will do this,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 * Democratic senator Tim Kaine told reporters he is considering a resolution to formally censure \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . It is an acknowledgment that the impeachment trial is unlikely to result in a conviction.\par \par \uc2 * The White House is said to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/jan/27/gamestop-stocks-us-hedge-fund-pulls-out-after-heavy-losses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18monitoring\u8217\'20\'19 the GameStop share surge}}}\uc2  as hedge fund Melvin Capital Management pulls out.\par \par \uc2 * In the latest Republican in-fighting, Florida Rep. Matt Gaetz is expected in Wyoming to denounce colleague \uc2 Rep. Liz Cheney\uc2  who voted for impeachment.\par \par \uc2 * Three nominees for cabinet secretary posts faced Senate committee hearings yesterday. There appears to be Republican resistance to the appointment of Alejandro Mayorkas as secretary of Homeland Security.\par \par \uc2 * Housing and Urban Development secretary nominee Marcia Fudge will appear before the Senate Banking and Urban Affairs Committee today at 10am.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 10.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 2021-01-28T10:01:35Z2021-01-29T01:50:17Z{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/8e9f5bda3b086d91615e0df2e43ba934429e895d/0_195_3500_2102/500.jpgJoe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/8e9f5bda3b086d91615e0df2e43ba934429e895d/0_195_3500_2102/500.jpgJoe}}}\uc2  Biden signs executive orders on access to affordable healthcare in Washington\par \par \uc2 US second gentleman Doug Emhoff speaks with volunteers of Dreaming out Loud, a nonprofit organization focused on food security and economic opportunityAlejandro Mayorkas, nominee to be secretary of homeland security, testifies during his confirmation hearingJoe Biden signs executive orders on health care in the White House in Washington DC on 28 January 2021In this 11 Dec 2020 photo, Ohio representative Marcia Fudge speaks during an event at The Queen theater in Wilmington, DelawareRepresentative Kim cleans up debris and personal belongings strewn across the floor of the Rotunda in the early morning hours of Thursday, 7 Jan 2021, after protesters stormed the Capitol.Chief of Space Operations at US Space Force Gen. John Raymond speaks at a ceremony to commemorate the first birthday of the. Space Force at the White House in December 2020.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210128eh1s001bg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
