\par\par \uc2 Global development\par \b \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  axes 'global gag rule' but health groups call on him to go further\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Safi , Liz Ford and Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 1,070 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 January 2021\par 21:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President\u8217\'20\'19s move to end \u8216\'20\'18\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\u8217\'20\'19 on overseas funding hailed \u8211\'20\'13 now aid groups want apology for harmful Trump policies\par \par \uc2 Health groups around the world are celebrating the end of a harmful policy banning US funding for overseas aid organisations that facilitate or promote \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was scrapped by the US president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , in a presidential memorandum on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights advocates are urging the new administration to now go further and permanently repeal the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/video/2017/jan/18/what-is-the-global-gag-rule-and-why-does-trump-support-it-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mexico City policy}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 known as the \u8220\'20\'1Cglobal gag rule\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 to prevent it being reinstated by a future Republican president. The policy has been blamed for contributing to thousands of maternal deaths in the developing world over the past four years.\par \par \uc2 The gag rule prevents overseas organisations that receive American aid from using their own money to provide information about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or carry out abortions. First adopted by the Reagan administration in 1984, it has been repealed by every Democratic administration and reinstated by every Republican one in the years since.\par \par \uc2 In a short appearance in the Oval Office on Thursday afternoon, Biden said he ended the policy as part of an effort to \u8220\'20\'1Cprotect women\u8217\'20\'19s health at home and abroad\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  went further than previous Republican presidents. The policy usually applies to family planning organisations. But the Trump administration expanded the policy to include all global health programmes, including programmes that address HIV, nutrition, malaria and cholera.\par \par \uc2 Widening the rule increased the pool of aid funds it affected from roughly $600m to about $12bn (\u163\'00\'A38.7bn), according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a health policy research group.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can breathe,\u8221\'20\'1D said Serra Sippel, the president of the Center for Health and Gender Equity, of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s plans to repeal the policy. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s just so much hope and optimism in Washington DC right now. We have a lot of work to do, but it\u8217\'20\'19s so much better.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The consequences of Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s memorandum will ripple out from Washington into more than 70 countries including some of the poorest places in the world, where essential women\u8217\'20\'19s health operations were abruptly halted or scaled down after Trump reinstated the rule in January 2017.\par \par \uc2 In Zimbabwe, a women\u8217\'20\'19s health team run by Abebe Shibru, from the organisation MSI Reproductive Choices, cut its operations by 60%. \u8220\'20\'1CWe reduced our outreach from 700,000 women to about 300,000,\u8221\'20\'1D Shibru, who now heads the organisation\u8217\'20\'19s Ethiopian operations, told \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWomen missed out on information, they had no access to family planning, and in return they were exposed to unintended pregnancy and unsafe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which contributed to higher maternal mortality.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Zimbabwe\u8217\'20\'19s teenage pregnancy rate increased by 2% over the past four years, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://data.unicef.org/resources/data_explorer/unicef_f/?ag=UNICEF&df=GLOBAL_DATAFLOW&ver=1.0&dq=ZWE.MNCH_BIRTH18..&startPeriod=1990&endPeriod=2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Unicef data}}}\uc2 , a trend Shibru said was exacerbated by cuts as a result of the gag rule.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe were not providing services to rural women, so they had no choice but to get pregnant against their wish,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Pledging conferences {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2017/mar/02/countries-to-join-forces-to-raise-funds--safe-abortions-trump-order-conference-global-gag-rule"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attracted hundreds of millions of dollars}}}\uc2  in donations from governments and private groups to try to bridge the gap in American funding, but could not meet the total shortfall.\par \par \uc2 An {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2019/jun/05/trump-global-gag-rule-anti-abortion-harms-women-africa-asia-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 assessment of the rule\u8217\'20\'19s impact}}}\uc2  released last year, surveying health organisations in Nigeria, Kenya, South Africa and Nepal, found a sector in \u8220\'20\'1Ccrisis\u8221\'20\'1D with confusion over what was banned and permitted using US aid, a growing stigma around reproductive health services and widespread closures and scaling downs of programmes.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s ban also spawned a new wave of activism, including a new grassroots movement, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2018/dec/26/how-trump-gag-rule-inspired-worldwide-movement-shedecides"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SheDecides}}}\uc2 , which is pressuring policymakers around the world to commit to upholding reproductive and sexual health rights.\par \par \uc2 Zara Ahmed, the associate director of federal issues at the Guttmacher Institute, said repealing the gag rule \u8220\'20\'1Cis just the first step in undoing [the US\u8217\'20\'19s] current status as the greatest global hindrance to reproductive health\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are glad that the Biden-Harris administration is addressing the global gag rule \u8230\'20\'26\u8230\'20\'26 But let\u8217\'20\'19s be clear, repealing the global gag rule is the bare minimum this administration can do to address the harm caused by the previous administration\u8217\'20\'19s coercive and spiteful approach to foreign policy,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Biden-Harris administration can, and must, take a comprehensive approach to unravelling the dangerous, punitive and coercive policies the outgoing administration has woven into our foreign policy, and it must take action to address longstanding harmful policies like the Helms amendment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.populationconnectionaction.org/the-helms-amendment/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Helms amendment}}}\uc2  has been widely misinterpreted as a total ban on US funding used for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  overseas, when in fact it can be used to support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in cases of rape, incest or a woman\u8217\'20\'19s life being in danger. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2020/jul/29/democrats-introduce-bill-to-repeal-anti-abortion-rule-for-us-overseas-aid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bill to permanently repeal}}}\uc2  it was introduced last year.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the Global Health, Empowerment and Rights Act (Global HER Act) to permanently repeal the global gag rule will be introduced for the third time in Congress. The bill, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/116th-congress/senate-bill/368/cosponsors?r=477&s=3&searchResultViewType=expanded"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cosponsored}}}\uc2  by the new vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , has received cross-party support, and hopes are high it will pass.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not automatic and it\u8217\'20\'19s not going to be easy but we\u8217\'20\'19re starting in a very strong place to get the act passed,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sippel. \u8220\'20\'1CIf not the bill itself, but the language of the bill incorporated into another bill. Getting rid of the GGR, that\u8217\'20\'19s what we\u8217\'20\'19re striving for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sippel also called on the Biden administration to disavow the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/oct/22/us-trump-administration-signs-anti-abortion-declaration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Geneva consensus declaration}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy Trump promoted last year \u8211\'20\'13 to \u8220\'20\'1Csignal to the world that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and LGBTQ rights and sexual and reproductive rights are important, and to state that loudly to the world\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She added that some activists wanted the Biden administration to issue a formal apology for US policies on sexual and reproductive health and rights over the past four years.\par \par \uc2 Biden also ordered funding restored to the \uc2 UN\uc2  population fund, \uc2 UNFPA\uc2 , which Trump stopped.\par \par \uc2 The agency\u8217\'20\'19s executive director, \uc2 Natalia Kanem\uc2 , hailed the \u8220\'20\'1Cenormous\u8221\'20\'1D impact of the decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEnding funding to \uc2 UNFPA\uc2  has become a political football, far removed from the tragic reality it leads to on the ground. Women\u8217\'20\'19s bodies are not political bargaining chips, and their right to plan their pregnancies, give birth safely and live free from violence should be something we can all agree on,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210128eh1s00335\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
