\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  becomes the first US president to be impeached for a second time \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now), Joan E Greve and Martin Belam (earlier) \par \uc2 17,165 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 January 2021\par 03:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Full report: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  impeached a second timeImpeachment puts Trump in first place among lords of misruleAOC thought she \u8216\'20\'18was going to die\u8217\'20\'19 during Capitol attackKamala Harris: how will the next vice-president wield her power? Join \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  for a live conversation on 18 January\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56am GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 From me and Joan E Greve:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  became the first US president to be impeached twice. The House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/13/trump-impeached-again-president-history-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted to impeach Trump}}}\uc2  on incitement of insurrection, after the president incited a violent mob to storm the Capitol last week, resulting in five deaths.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/13/republicans-donald-trump-impeached-house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ten House Republicans}}}\uc2  voted in favor of impeachment. Their votes made this the most bipartisan presidential impeachment in US history. The final vote on the article of impeachment was 232-197.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  delivered an impassioned speech calling on members to support impeachment. \u8220\'20\'1CHe must go,\u8221\'20\'1D the Democratic speaker said of the president. \u8220\'20\'1CHe is a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/13/impeachment-quotes-remarks-democrats-on-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clear and present danger}}}\uc2  to the nation we all love.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Kevin McCarthy said Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cbears responsibility\u8221\'20\'1D for the Capitol attack but did not deserve to be impeached. \u8220\'20\'1CThe president bears responsibility for Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s attack on Congress by mob rioters,\u8221\'20\'1D the Republican minority leader said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe should have immediately denounced the mob when he saw what was unfolding.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  has said the impeachment trial will happen after Biden has taken office on 20 January. McConnell will remain the majority leader in the Senate until at least 22 January, when the results of the two Georgia elections are certified and Democrats Raphael Warnock and \uc2 Jon Ossoff\uc2  take offices.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said the senate must balance the impeachment trial with coronavirus response. \u8220\'20\'1CI hope that the Senate leadership will find a way to deal with their constitutional responsibilities on impeachment while also working on the other urgent business of this nation,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 * Pelosi introduced a rule change to fine members who evade the detectors. This after several Republican members of Congress protested the metal detectors installed after the deadly attack on the US Capitol. The House will vote on the fines when Congress returns to session on 21 January.\par \par \uc2 * Banned from social media, Trump has released a video statement condemning violence. He made no mention of his impeachment and did not take responsibility for inciting or encouraging the attack on the US Capitol last week.\par \par \uc2 Read more about today\u8217\'20\'19s historic events:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/13/trump-impeached-again-president-history-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump impeached a second time over mob attack on US Capitol}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/13/trump-second-impeachment-house-of-representatives-sketch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Second impeachment puts Trump in first place among lords of misrule}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/13/donald-trump-second-impeachment-key-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump's second impeachment: five key takeaways}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's second impeachment: five key takeaways\par \par \uc2 1. There are signs of a deep split within the Republican party\par \par \uc2 Some of the most high-profile members of Republican leadership aren\u8217\'20\'19t denouncing the Democratic effort. Quite the contrary. Congresswoman \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  of Wyoming, the chairwoman of the House Republican Conference, announced on Tuesday that she would join Democrats and a handful of House Republicans in voting to impeach Trump.\par \par \uc2 2. The most bipartisan impeachment in American history\par \par \uc2 Unlike the last time Democrats impeached Trump, there\u8217\'20\'19s a higher level of bipartisan support for the move. Congressman Kevin McCarthy, the House minority leader and top-ranking Republican in that chamber, said during a speech on Wednesday that Trump was partially to blame for the mob assault on the Capitol last week.\par \par \uc2 3. The vast majority of Republicans refused to concede any fault\par \par \uc2 Throughout the debate on Wednesday two patterns emerged among the arguments Republicans made: deflect and denounce. Republicans repeatedly denounced the mob attack last week.\par \par \uc2 4. The Senate is a mystery\par \par \uc2 How things will shake out in the Senate is a mystery. McConnell wrote in a letter to colleagues that he has not \u8220\'20\'1Cmade a final decision on how I will vote and I intend to listen to legal arguments when they are presented to the Senate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 5. Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 security concerns seem well-founded\par \par \uc2 Reporters and lawmakers noted the increased security presence around the Capitol. Congressman \uc2 Seth Moulton\uc2  of Massachusetts noted in his floor speech that there were more US soldiers patrolling the Capitol than were stationed in Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/13/donald-trump-second-impeachment-key-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump's second impeachment: five key takeaways}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 Riots, effigies and a guillotine: Capitol attack could be a glimpse of violence to come\par \par \uc2 A guillotine outside the state capitol in Arizona. A Democratic governor burned in effigy in Oregon. Lawmakers evacuated as pro-Trump crowds gathered at state capitols in Georgia and New Mexico. Cheers in Idaho as a crowd was told fellow citizens were \u8220\'20\'1Ctaking the Capitol\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ctaking out\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mike-pence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike Pence}}}\uc2 , the vice-president.\par \par \uc2 As a mob of thousands invaded the US Capitol on 6 January, Trump supporters threatened lawmakers and fellow citizens in cities across the country. Compared with the violent mob in Washington, the pro-Trump crowds elsewhere in the country were much smaller, attracting dozens to hundreds of people. But they used the same extreme rhetoric, labeling both Democratic politicians and Republicans perceived as disloyal to Trump as \u8220\'20\'1Ctraitors\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 As the \uc2 FBI\uc2  warns of plans for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/11/trump-impeachment-house-democrats-charge-president-with-incitement-of-insurrection"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new armed protests}}}\uc2  in Washington and all 50 state capitols in the days leading up to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s inauguration, and fresh calls for extreme violence circulate on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jan/11/trump-supporters-rightwing-violent-protest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 social media forums}}}\uc2 , the intensity of the nationwide pro-Trump demonstrations and attacks last week offer evidence of what might be coming next.\par \par \uc2 Some of the pro-Trump demonstrations on Wednesday did not turn violent. The dozens of Trump supporters who entered the Kansas state capitol remained peaceful, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/joe-biden-donald-trump-georgia-coronavirus-pandemic-evacuations-e81e82d4c6d3db6bc45a68ae0124c85e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 multiple}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ksnt.com/capitol-bureau/protesters-disperse-from-inside-kansas-statehouse/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 news reports}}}\uc2 . In Carson City, Nevada, hundreds of Trump supporters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rgj.com/story/news/politics/2021/01/06/nevada-trump-supporters-protest-drink-beer-rock-carson-city/6571166002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drank beer and listened to rock music}}}\uc2  while denouncing the election results, the Reno Gazette Journal reported.\par \par \uc2 But in Los Angeles, white Trump supporters assaulted and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2021-01-08/black-woman-describes-terrifying-attack-by-trump-mob-in-l-a-im-thinking-im-dead"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ripped the wig off }}}\uc2  the head of a young black woman who happened to pass their 6 January protest, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2021-01-08/black-woman-describes-terrifying-attack-by-trump-mob-in-l-a-im-thinking-im-dead"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Los Angeles Times reported}}}\uc2 . A white woman was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2021-01-08/black-woman-describes-terrifying-attack-by-trump-mob-in-l-a-im-thinking-im-dead"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 captured on video }}}\uc2  holding the wig and shouting, \u8220\'20\'1CFuck BLM!\u8221\'20\'1D and, \u8220\'20\'1CI did the first scalping of the new civil war.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dispatch.com/story/news/local/2021/01/06/tempers-were-short-fists-flew-street-during-trump-rally/6565956002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MrOlmos/status/1346944954971557890"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oregon}}}\uc2 , fights broke out between counter-protesters and members of the Proud Boys, the neo-fascist group Trump directed in September to \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/sep/29/trump-proud-boys-debate-president-refuses-condemn-white-supremacists"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stand back and stand by}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. Proud Boys also reportedly demonstrated in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tstevensmedia/status/1346947854309343236"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Utah}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abc7news.com/president-donald-trump-sacramento-rally-news-twitter/9425081/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HamptonStall/status/1348673366023090184"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HamptonStall/status/1348673361484926979"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Carolina}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And in Washington state, Trump supporters, some armed, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.q13fox.com/news/pro-trump-supporters-broke-through-gate-at-gov-inslees-olympia-home"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushed through the gate}}}\uc2  of the governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.seattletimes.com/seattle-news/politics/trump-supporters-open-gate-at-governors-mansion-in-olympia-occupy-front-lawn/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stormed on to the lawn}}}\uc2  of Democrat Jay Inslee\u8217\'20\'19s house. In Georgia, where lawmakers were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JerodMacEvoy/status/1346859162186125313"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 evacuated}}}\uc2  from the state capitol, members of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HamptonStall/status/1346881822999896064"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 III% Security Force militia}}}\uc2 , a group known for its anti-Muslim activism, had gathered outside.\par \par \uc2 Militia members, neo-Nazis, and other rightwing extremists have discussed multiple potential dates for armed protests in the coming days, researchers who monitor extremist groups say, with proposals ranging from rallies or attacks on state capitols to a \u8220\'20\'1Cmillion militia march\u8221\'20\'1D in Washington.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/fbi-warns-armed-protests-next-week-ec75b26289166b4afd30c15b0dd2ded5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  intelligence bulletin}}}\uc2  has warned of potential armed protests from 16 January \u8220\'20\'1Cat least\u8221\'20\'1D through inauguration day on 20 January, but researchers say that energy had not yet coalesced around a single event. Public social media forums where Trump supporters have gathered to discuss plans are full of dramatic, contradictory rumors, but experts say that more concrete plans are likely being made in private and in smaller forums that are more difficult to infiltrate.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/13/capitol-attack-violence-far-right-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Riots, effigies and a guillotine: Capitol attack could be a glimpse of violence to come}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.57am GMT\par \par \uc2 Andrew Yang announces he's running for New York mayor\par \par \uc2 The former Democratic presidential candidate was expected to make this announcement.\par \par \uc2 enltrI moved to New York City 25 years ago. I came of age, fell in love, and became a father here. Seeing our City in so much pain breaks my heart.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s fight for a future New York City that we can be proud of \u8211\'20\'13 together. Join us at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/TGnxwuBiHB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/TGnxwuBiHB}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/n9zxPybgbh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/n9zxPybgbh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Yang???????? (@AndrewYang) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewYang/status/1349522020615278593?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 14, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 Analysis: Second impeachment puts Trump in first place among lords of misrule\par \par \uc2 It was always going to end this way. A presidency centered on fear, rage and division is climaxing in a Grand Guignol of three acts at the US Capitol in Washington: last Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s insurrection, this Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s impeachment, next Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s inauguration.\par \par \uc2 As Barack Obama noted after act one, \u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19d be kidding ourselves if we treated it as a total surprise\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 What remains uncertain is whether this is the moment that the fever breaks and the nation gets back on track or merely a harbinger of further polarisation, violence and decline.\par \par \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  and nine other {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  who joined Democrats in a 232-197 bipartisan vote to impeach Trump did not provide a comprehensive answer to that question. Yes, it was 10 more than the first impeachment just over a year ago and, yes, there are cracks in the dam. But it has not yet burst.\par \par \uc2 And certainly on this Wednesday, with its besieged capital being prised from the grasp of a would-be autocrat, America resembled the sort of fragile state that it used to think it was in the business of rescuing and rebuilding.\par \par \uc2 Barriers, checkpoints and a ring of steel had been erected on Capitol Hill. Members of the national guard, with masks, guns and military garb, could be seen sleeping on hard floors in the hallways of the Capitol. The last time troops were quartered here was during the American civil war; there were more of them than in Afghanistan or Iraq today.\par \par \uc2 Inside the chamber, where members wore masks under strict new coronavirus rules, the historic day began with a prayer from R Adm Margaret Grun Kibben, the House chaplain. She noted that last week \u8220\'20\'1Cwe found ourselves seizing the scales of justice from the jaws of mobocracy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But it did not take long for partisanship to bare its teeth. Although this process has been much speedier than Impeachment One, which sanctioned Trump for pressuring Ukraine for political favours, there were again angry speeches from both sides.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/13/trump-second-impeachment-house-of-representatives-sketch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Second impeachment puts Trump in first place among lords of misrule}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.18am GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden: Senate must juggle impeachment and coronavirus response\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, the members of the House of representatives exercised the power granted to them under our constitution and voted to impeach and hold the president accountable,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CThis nation also remains in the grip of a deadly virus and a reeling economy. I hope that the Senate leadership will find a way to deal with their constitutional responsibilities on impeachment while also working on the other urgent business of this nation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earlier today Senator \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  said that the impeachment trial will not take place until after Biden is inaugurated.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.03am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 House will vote on fines for members who evade metal detectors\par \par \uc2 After several Republican members of Congress protested the metal detectors installed after the deadly attack on the US Capitol, House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  introduced a rule change to fine members who evade the detectors.\par \par \uc2 The House will vote on the fines when Congress returns to session on 21 January.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn behalf of the House, I express my deepest gratitude to the US \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  for the valor that they showed during the deadly insurrection on the Capitol, as they protected the lives of the staff and the Congress,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said. \u8220\'20\'1CSadly, just days later, many House Republicans have disrespected our heroes by verbally abusing them and refusing to adhere to basic precautions keeping members of our congressional community, including the \uc2 Capitol police\uc2 , safe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Members, including QAnon conspiracy theory supporter Lauren Boebert, refused to comply with new safety protocols yesterday, clashing with officers. The newly-elected congresswoman of Colorado has drawn criticism for tweeting Pelosi\u8217\'20\'19s location during the violent riot last week.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.36am GMT\par \par \uc2 Snapchat will permanently ban \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , per multiple reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLast week we announced an indefinite suspension of President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Snapchat account, and have been assessing what long term action is in the best interest of our Snapchat community,\u8221\'20\'1D a spokesperson told Axios. \u8220\'20\'1CIn the interest of public safety, and based on his attempts to spread misinformation, hate speech, and incite violence, which are clear violations of our guidelines, we have made the decision to permanently terminate his account.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Twitter\u8217\'20\'19s CEO, meanwhile, has weighed in for the first time on the company\u8217\'20\'19s decision to de-platform Trump following the US Capitol attack last week:\par \par \uc2 enltrI do not celebrate or feel pride in our having to ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realDonaldTrump}}}\uc2  from \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , or how we got here. After a clear warning we\u8217\'20\'19d take this action, we made a decision with the best information we had based on threats to physical safety both on and off \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . Was this correct?\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 jack (@jack) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jack/status/1349510769268850690?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 14, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Read more analysis of social media companies\u8217\'20\'19 bans and restrictions on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s accounts, from \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Kari Paul :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/07/donald-trump-facebook-social-media-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 'Four years of propaganda': Trump social media bans come too late, experts say}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.35am GMT\par \par \uc2 The former Michigan governor charged with crimes related to Flint water crisis\par \par \uc2 Former governor Rick Snyder has been charged with willful neglect of duty, for his role in the Flint water crisis.\par \par \uc2 In 2014, the city of Flint, Michigan had its water supply switched to the Flint river to save costs. Some 9,000 children, who are especially vulnerable to lead poisoning, were exposed to lead-contaminated drinking water.\par \par \uc2 The AP reports:\par \par \uc2 The charges, shown in an online court record, are misdemeanors punishable by up to a year in jail and a $1,000 fine.\par \par \uc2 The indictment filed by the attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office is groundbreaking: No governor or former governor in Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s 184-year history had been charged with crimes related to their time in that office, according to the state archivist.\par \par \uc2 Besides Snyder, a Republican who served until 2019, charges are expected against other people, including former officials who served as state health director, Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s chief medical executive, Snyder\u8217\'20\'19s communications chief and a senior adviser.\par \par \uc2 Flint was in chronic financial trouble in 2014 when a Snyder-appointed manager who was running the majority Black city carried out a money-saving decision to use the Flint River for water while a regional pipeline from Lake Huron was under construction. The corrosive water, however, wasn\u8217\'20\'19t treated properly and released lead from old plumbing into homes in one of the worst manmade environmental disasters in U.S. history.\par \par \uc2 Despite desperate pleas from residents holding jugs of discolored, skunky water, the Snyder administration took no significant action until a doctor reported elevated lead levels in children about 18 months later.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Revealed: walkie-talkie app Zello hosted far-right groups who stormed Capitol\par \par \uc2 Micah Loewinger and Hampton Stall report:\par \par \uc2 Audio and chat logs reveal that at least two insurrectionists who broke into the Capitol on 6 January used Zello, a social media walkie-talkie app that critics say has largely ignored a growing far-right user base.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are in the main dome right now,\u8221\'20\'1D said a female militia member, speaking on Zello, her voice competing with the cacophony of a clash with \uc2 Capitol police\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe are rocking it. They\u8217\'20\'19re throwing grenades, they\u8217\'20\'19re frickin\u8217\'20\'19 shooting people with paintballs, but we\u8217\'20\'19re in here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGod bless and godspeed. Keep going,\u8221\'20\'1D said a male voice from a quiet environment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJess, do your shit,\u8221\'20\'1D said another. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is what we fucking lived up for. Everything we fucking trained for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The frenzied exchange took place at 2.44pm in a public Zello channel called \u8220\'20\'1CSTOP THE STEAL J6\u8221\'20\'1D, where Trump supporters at home and in Washington DC discussed the riot as it unfolded. Dynamic group conversations like this exemplify why Zello, a smartphone and PC app, has become popular among militias, which have long fetishized military-like communication on analog radio.\par \par \uc2 After years of public pressure, \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , and Discord have begun to crack down on inciting speech from far-right groups, but Zello has avoided proactive content moderation thus far.\par \par \uc2 Most coverage on Zello, which claims to have 150 million users on its free and premium platforms, has focused on its use by the Cajun Navy groups that send boats to save flood victims and grassroots organizing in Venezuela. However, the app is also home to hundreds of far-right channels, which appear to violate its policy prohibiting groups that espouse \u8220\'20\'1Cviolent ideologies\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Responding to a list of over 800 far-right channels, Zello said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cprepared to take action on those\u8221\'20\'1D. The company also said it was working on a more elaborate response. In addition to locking some public features that would help researchers uncover more extremist content, Zello had begun purging some far-right groups as of Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/13/zello-app-us-capitol-attack-far-right"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Revealed: walkie-talkie app Zello hosted far-right groups who stormed Capitol}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The violent attack on the US Capitol last week followed a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  speech in which he told his supporters to \u8220\'20\'1Cfight\u8221\'20\'1D for him. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you don\u8217\'20\'19t fight like hell, you\u8217\'20\'19re not going to have a country anymore,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told his supporters. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ll never take back our country with weakness. You have to show strength.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And yet yesterday, in Alamo, Texas, Trump again insisted: \u8220\'20\'1CIf you read my speech \u8230\'20\'26 people thought that what I said was totally appropriate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But with an impeachment trial coming up, the president seems to have slightly shifted his rhetoric.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump, as others in his party have done, also tried to chastise both sides for the violence, despite the fact that it was his supporters who led the attack last week.\par \par \uc2 This year, he said, \u8220\'20\'1Cwe have seen political violence spiral out of control. We have seen too many riots, too many mobs too many acts of intimidation and destruction. It must. Whether you are on the right, or on the left, a Democrat or Republican. There is never a justification for violence. No excuses. no exceptions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  makes a video statement, doesn't mention impeachment\par \par \uc2 Banned from social media, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has released a video statement condemning violence but making no mention of his impeachment and without taking any responsibility for inciting the attack on the Capitol last week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThose who engaged in the attacks last week will be brought to justice,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 undltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FIJbvCYGJ6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/FIJbvCYGJ6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The White House (@WhiteHouse) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WhiteHouse/status/1349492130578919425?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSadly and with a heart broken,\u8221\'20\'1D House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  said, as she signed the impeachment article that will be sent to the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Pelosi arrives for an engrossment ceremony after the \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2  voted to impeach the US president at the US Capitol. Photograph: Brendan Smialowski/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a clear and present danger to our country,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, and that she was sad about \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat this means for our country\u8221\'20\'1D as she signed the article accusing Trump of incitement of insurrection.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Democrats are huddling on how they\u8217\'20\'19d prosecute.\par \par \uc2 CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Manu Raju:\par \par \uc2 enltrPelosi is meeting with impeachment managers. Lead manager Jamie Raskin told me it was uncertain how many witnesses they would seek and how long trial would be.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re still just getting organized, but if it comes to it, we'll get you answers as soon as we've got some answers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1349489223859105792?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A lot could happen between now and the impeachment trial...\par \par \uc2 But it remains unclear whether enough Republican senators will vote to convict the president. Pat Toomey, a Republican senator of Pennsylvania, who condemned Trump\u8217\'20\'19s role in inciting violence and called on him to resign, has nevertheless hedged on whether he\u8217\'20\'19d vote to convict.\par \par \uc2 Whether the Senate can convict a president after leaving office is \u8220\'20\'1Cdebatable\u8221\'20\'1D Toomey said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CShould the Senate conduct a trial, I will again fulfill my responsibility to consider arguments from both the House managers and President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second impeachment has led to some strong responses from political commentators, including former US labor secretary and Guardian US columnist Robert Reich:\par \par \uc2 enltrIn case you weren't clear about the state of today's GOP: Only 10 House Republicans voted to impeach a president who incited an attempted overthrow of the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Robert Reich (@RBReich) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RBReich/status/1349472892136824833?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrEspecially white Americans don\u8217\'20\'19t like to hear it, but we got to the \u8220\'20\'1Ccoup\u8221\'20\'1D stage of fascism because we didn\u8217\'20\'19t impeach at the concentration camps, cages, family separations, beatings, gassing, disappearances. Fascism\u8217\'20\'19s a pattern of escalation and nobody tried to really break it\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ?? (@umairh) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/umairh/status/1349461663553114121?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe bottom line is that after everything, ten House Republicans voted to impeach Trump, two Cabinet officers quit, \uc2 Twitter\uc2  banned Trump, Lindsey Graham got off the train and back on again, and Trump is staying in office.\par \par \uc2 For a week.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Susan Glasser (@sbg1) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sbg1/status/1349475751616258049?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWe all know that the Republicans are going to try to impeach Biden at some point, right? To do another one of their "sorry, these are the new rules. See how you like it," things.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Parker Molloy (@ParkerMolloy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ParkerMolloy/status/1349471499367886851?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Senate\u8217\'20\'19s leading Democrat, Chuck Schumer responds to the Trump impeachment: \u8220\'20\'1CA Senate trial can begin immediately, with agreement from the current Senate Majority Leader to reconvene the Senate for an emergency session, or it will begin after January 19th. But make no mistake, there will be an impeachment trial in the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDespite the efforts of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and violent insurrectionists, America is not a dictatorship,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said.\u8221\'20\'1D We have been and will forever remain a Democracy that respects and reveres the rule of law, including the bedrock principle that the voters choose our leaders \u8211\'20\'13 that just power can only derive from the consent of the governed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 McConnell says Trump impeachment trial will take place after Biden inauguration\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  has said there\u8217\'20\'19s no chance of an impeachment trial for Trump until after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is inaugurated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGiven the rules, procedures, and Senate precedents that govern presidential impeachment trials, there is simply no chance that a fair or serious trial could conclude before President-elect Biden is sworn in next week,\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn light of this reality, I believe it will best serve our nation if Congress and the executive branch spend the next seven days completely focused on facilitating a safe inauguration and an orderly transfer of power to the incoming Biden administration,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The Republican leader did not indicate his position on whether he\u8217\'20\'19d vote to convict or acquit Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Second Trump impeachment summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Maanvi Singh, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where this historic day stands:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  became the first US president to be impeached twice. The House voted to impeach Trump on incitement of insurrection, after the president incited a violent mob to storm the Capitol last week, resulting in five deaths.\par \par \uc2 * Ten House Republicans voted in favor of impeachment. Their votes made this the most bipartisan presidential impeachment in US history. The final vote on the article of impeachment was 232-197.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  delivered an impassioned speech calling on members to support impeachment. \u8220\'20\'1CHe must go,\u8221\'20\'1D the Democratic speaker said of the president. \u8220\'20\'1CHe is a clear and present danger to the nation we all love.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Kevin McCarthy said Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cbears responsibility\u8221\'20\'1D for the Capitol attack but did not deserve to be impeached. \u8220\'20\'1CThe president bears responsibility for Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s attack on Congress by mob rioters,\u8221\'20\'1D the Republican minority leader said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe should have immediately denounced the mob when he saw what was unfolding.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  has said there will be no impeachment trial earlier than 19 January, when the Senate is currently set to return from recess. Chuck Schumer, the Senate Democratic leader, had said the chamber should return early to take up impeachment, but McConnell has signaled no interest in doing so.\par \par \uc2 Maanvi will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 Photographers take pictures of the article of impeachment against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  during an engrossment ceremony after the \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2  voted to impeach him at the US Capitol. Photograph: Brendan Smialowski/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Why did \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just get impeached on the charge of incitement of insurrection?\par \par \uc2 In the chaotic aftermath of the Capitol riot, Trump and his now dwindling number of Republicans allies tried to claim he did nothing wrong.\par \par \uc2 But as \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Ed Pilkington has laid out, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s incitement can be traced all the way back to 19 December, when he first mentioned a \u8220\'20\'1Cbig protest in DC\u8221\'20\'1D, and said \u8220\'20\'1CBe there, will be wild!\u8221\'20\'1D. This reached a climax on 6 January, when Trump urged a crowd outside the White House to march on the Capitol. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/07/trump-incitement-inflammatory-rhetoric-capitol-riot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full timeline here}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/07/trump-incitement-inflammatory-rhetoric-capitol-riot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Incitement: a timeline of Trump's inflammatory rhetoric before the Capitol riot}}}\par \par \uc2 And here is Trump before the Capitol riot whipping up the crowd:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The most surprising Republican \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D vote on impeachment came from Tom Rice of South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Before the vote, Rice did not offer any indication that he was planning to support impeachment, and he was not considered one of the likely \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D votes.\par \par \uc2 Rice has not yet put out a statement explaining his vote, but this tweet from last week, sent during the violent riot at the Capitol, captures his frustration with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrTo all my friends back home, I am fine. Capitol Police evacuated us from the Capitol Building. DC is in chaos.\par \par \uc2 This will accomplish nothing.\par \par \uc2 Where is the President!? He must ask people to disperse and restore calm now.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Congressman Tom Rice (@RepTomRice) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepTomRice/status/1346918665422131202?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 6, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here are the ten House Republicans who voted to impeach \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on the charge of incitement of insurrection:\par \par \uc2 * John Katko of New York.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  of Wyoming.\par \par \uc2 * Adam Kinzinger of Illinois.\par \par \uc2 * Fred Upton of Michigan.\par \par \uc2 * Jaime Herrera Beutler of Washington state.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Dan Newhouse\uc2  of Washington state.\par \par \uc2 * Peter Meijer of Michigan.\par \par \uc2 * Tom Rice of South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 * Anthony Gonzalez of Ohio.\par \par \uc2 * David Valadao of California.\par \par \uc2 The Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 votes made this the most bipartisan presidential impeachment in history. In comparison, five Democrats voted to impeach \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  in 1998.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump becomes the first US president to be impeached twice\par \par \uc2 The House has voted to impeach \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on the charge of incitement of insurrection, after the president incited a violent mob to storm the Capitol last week, resulting in five deaths.\par \par \uc2 The final vote was 232-197, with 10 House Republicans supporting the measure.\par \par \uc2 Trump has become the first president in US history to ever be impeached by the House twice.\par \par \uc2 The matter will now go before the Senate, which will decide whether Trump should be convicted and removed from office.\par \par \uc2 The trial will likely conclude after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  takes office anyway, but a conviction would prevent Trump from running for president again.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A tenth House Republican, David Valadao of California, has voted \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D on the article of impeachment against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The vote currently stands at 229-195 in favor of impeachment.\par \par \uc2 Nine members have not yet voted.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Article of impeachment reaches majority level of support\par \par \uc2 The article of impeachment has now reached a majority level of support, with at least 229 House members voting \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D on impeaching \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for a second time.\par \par \uc2 The vote currently stands at 229-194.\par \par \uc2 But the vote is still ongoing, and members can change their votes until it is gaveled out. Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Mike Gallagher of Wisconsin, \uc2 Ann Wagner\uc2  of Missouri and \uc2 Brian Fitzpatrick\uc2  of Pennsylvania have all voted \u8220\'20\'1Cno\u8221\'20\'1D on impeachment.\par \par \uc2 The three members were some of the last remaining Republicans who were considered possible \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D votes, but they have apparently decided against impeaching the president for a second time.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s looking like the total number of Republicans supporting impeachment will likely be nine, but we won\u8217\'20\'19t know for sure until the vote is complete.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Seven House Republicans have already voted \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D on impeaching \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and at least two more are expected to do so.\par \par \uc2 Assuming no one charges their vote, this will be the most bipartisan presidential impeachment in US history, as a CBC News reporter noted.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: This is now the most *bipartisan* presidential impeachment in American history.\par \par \uc2 Six Republicans have already voted to impeach Trump - the most ever from one party again a president of that same party.\par \par \uc2 Previous record: five Democrats vs \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  in 1998.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alexander Panetta (@Alex_Panetta) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Alex_Panetta/status/1349463004581081090?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In his statement explaining his vote in support of impeachment, Anthony Gonzalez also accused \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  of having \u8220\'20\'1Cabandoned his post\u8221\'20\'1D amid the violence at the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Gonzalez argued that the president\u8217\'20\'19s failure to act further endangered those present at the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 The Republican congressman described the president\u8217\'20\'19s actions as \u8220\'20\'1Cfundamental threats\u8221\'20\'1D to American democracy.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Two more House Republicans, Tom Rice of South Carolina and Anthony Gonzalez of Ohio, have voted \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D on impeaching the president.\par \par \uc2 Assuming they do not change their votes, they will be the eighth and ninth Republicans to support impeachment.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Gonzalez said he was supporting impeachment because \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Chelped organize and incite a mob that attacked the \uc2 United States Congress\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrSee my full statement on impeachment below. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/pBBYRI2RUP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/pBBYRI2RUP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. Anthony Gonzalez (@RepAGonzalez) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepAGonzalez/status/1349461350456717312?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House votes on article of impeachment against Trump\par \par \uc2 The House has now concluded its two hours of debate on the article of impeachment against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The chamber has moved on to a roll-call vote on the article, incitement of insurrection.\par \par \uc2 The measure is expected to pass with the support of all Democrats and at least seven Republicans.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Seventh House Republican says he will support impeachment\par \par \uc2 Peter Meijer, a Republican congressman from Michigan, has become the seventh Republican House member to say he will support the impeachment of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe President betrayed his oath of office by seeking to undermine our constitutional process, and he bears responsibility for inciting the insurrection last week,\u8221\'20\'1D Meijer said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWith a heavy heart, I will vote to impeach President \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Trump betrayed his oath of office by seeking to undermine our constitutional process, and he bears responsibility for inciting the insurrection we suffered last week. With a heavy heart, I will vote to impeach President \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SREfFp0nd2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SREfFp0nd2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. Peter Meijer (@RepMeijer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMeijer/status/1349457669229322241?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Meijer, a freshman congressman, previously said he was considering supporting impeachment, but this is the first time he has clearly said he will do so.\par \par \uc2 Seven Republicans have now said they will vote to impeach Trump, which means the president will be impeached in a bipartisan vote. When Trump was impeached the first time, only Democrats supported the measure.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The debate on the article of impeachment against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is now wrapping up, and the House will soon move on to the final vote on impeachment.\par \par \uc2 Steve Scalise, the House minority whip, was the final Republican speaker, and he applauded the Capitol Police officers who work to protect lawmakers every day. Two Capitol Police officers have died since last week, when a violent, pro-Trump mob stormed the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 House members in the chamber stood to applaud the fallen Capitol Police officers, marking a rare moment of bipartisanship during today\u8217\'20\'19s contentious debate.\par \par \uc2 The House majority leader, \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2 , is the final Democratic speaker, and he has repeatedly cited the words of Republican \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , who has said she will support impeachment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWill we stay silent, will we not stand up and say this is not acceptable?\u8221\'20\'1D Hoyer said. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has constructed a glass house of lies, fear-mongering and sedition.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 McConnell indicates he is open to convicting Trump\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Daniel Strauss reports:\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the top-ranking Republican in the Senate, indicated to colleagues that he is undecided on how he would vote on impeachment.\par \par \uc2 In a letter to his Senate colleagues sent out Wednesday afternoon, as members of the House moved forward with impeaching \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the Kentucky Republican wrote, \u8220\'20\'1Cwhile the press has been full of speculation, I have not made a final decision on how I will vote and I intend to listen to the legal arguments when they are presented to the Senate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The line in his note to Senate colleagues follows The \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reporting Tuesday night that McConnell is pleased with Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 move to impeach the president again and has been sharing that sentiment with associates.\par \par \uc2 McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s openness to impeaching the president, a fellow Republican, is the most significant sign so far that congressional Republican leaders are less resistant to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s impeachment than the last time the president was impeached.\par \par \uc2 In the House, congresswoman \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  of Wyoming, the House Republican Conference chair, said she would vote to impeach Trump. Five other House Republicans have also come out in support of impeachment.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear how Senate Republicans will vote. It\u8217\'20\'19s also unclear if McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s openness will offer cover for other Republicans who privately would like to see the president impeached. Two-thirds of senators would have to support conviction in order for him to be removed from office.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Congressman \uc2 Seth Moulton\uc2 , a Massachusetts Democrat and a Marine Corps veteran, noted that there are currently more troops in Washington than in Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. Moulton: "There are more troops right now in Washington DC than in Afghanistan. And they are here to defend us against the commander in chief, the POTUS and his mob." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/bpf9mdWhYi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/bpf9mdWhYi}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1349453713111441411?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd they are here to defend us against the commander in chief, the president of the United States and his mob,\u8221\'20\'1D Moulton said.\par \par \uc2 Moulton encouraged his colleagues to look at the National Guard members protecting the Capitol and search for \u8220\'20\'1Can ounce of their courage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Young Kim\uc2 , a freshman Republican congresswoman who flipped a California district that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lost by 10 points, will vote against impeachment.\par \par \uc2 enltrHowever, I believe impeaching the president now will fail to hold him accountable or allow us to move forward once President-elect Biden is sworn in. This process will only create more fissures in our country as we emerge from some of our darkest days. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NK1EdO5xoN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/NK1EdO5xoN}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IJIlb6oGva"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IJIlb6oGva}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Young Kim\uc2  (@RepYoungKim) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepYoungKim/status/1349442547211505665?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe violence we saw last week was disgusting. Our law enforcement was attacked, lives were lost and more were put in danger. These rioters must be held accountable. Words have consequences and I believe the president should also be held accountable,\u8221\'20\'1D Kim said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHowever, I believe impeaching the president at this time will fail to hold him accountable or allow us to move forward once President-elect Biden is sworn in. This process will only create more fissures in our country as we emerge from some of our darkest days.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 So far, only six House Republicans have signaled they intend to support the article of impeachment.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 It is now past 3 pm in Washington, but the House has not yet moved on to the final vote on the article of impeachment.\par \par \uc2 The House majority leader, \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2 , said yesterday that the final vote would occur at roughly 3 pm, but there are about 20 minutes of debate left.\par \par \uc2 Once the debate has concluded, the chamber will move on to voting on the article, which is expected to be approved.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Chip Roy, a Republican of Texas who has criticized his colleagues\u8217\'20\'19 efforts to cast baseless doubt upon the legitimacy of the presidential election, said he believed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had committed \u8220\'20\'1Cimpeachable\u8221\'20\'1D offenses.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president of the United States deserves universal condemnation for what was clearly, in my opinion, impeachable conduct, pressuring the vice president to violate his oath to the constitution.\u8221\'20\'1D Roy said in his speech.\par \par \uc2 And yet Roy will not be supporting the article of impeachment. The congressman argued the article had been drafted in a manner that targeted political speech itself.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what the article says, in part: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald John Trump\uc2  engaged in high Crimes and Misdemeanors by inciting violence against the \uc2 Government of the United States\uc2 ...\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald John Trump\uc2 , by such conduct, has demonstrated that he will remain a threat to national security, democracy, and the Constitution if allowed to remain in office[.]\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , the freshman Georgia congresswoman who supports the QAnon conspiracy theory, delivered her speech while wearing a mask that said \u8220\'20\'1Ccensored\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Greene did not seem to pick up on the irony that she was claiming to be \u8220\'20\'1Ccensored\u8221\'20\'1D while delivering a speech on the floor of the House of Representatives, which was broadcast on national television.\par \par \uc2 enltrYes, \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  is wearing a mask that says \u8220\'20\'1CCENSORED\u8221\'20\'1D as she speaks into a microphone on the floor of the \uc2 U.S. House of Representatives\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/i7401gseIU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/i7401gseIU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jessie Opoien (@jessieopie) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jessieopie/status/1349438418451886081?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  will speak today at the lectern that was taken by one of the rioters during the violence at the Capitol last week.\par \par \uc2 A House staffer was seen wheeling the lectern through Statuary Hall as the floor debate on the article of impeachment continued.\par \par \uc2 A staff member moves \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lectern on Wednesday. Photograph: Leah Millis/Reuters\par \par \uc2 During the riot last week, a man was photographed carrying the speaker\u8217\'20\'19s lectern through the Rotunda with a smile and a wave to the camera.\par \par \uc2 The man, identified as Adam Christian Johnson of Florida, was arrested on federal charges two days later.\par \par \uc2 A pro-Trump protester carries the lectern of \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  through the Rotunda. Photograph: Win McNamee/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New York Democratic representative \uc2 Adriano Espaillat\uc2  just spoke in utter fury about a mob \u8220\'20\'1Csummoned and dispatched\u8221\'20\'1D by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/09/us-capitol-insurrection-white-supremacist-terror"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attack the US Capitol}}}\uc2  on January 6, including one rioter who waved a Confederate flag inside the complex.\par \par \uc2 He said he believed that those exhorted by the president to march on the Capitol as both chambers of Congress were in session to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/06/congress-certify-election-biden-republicans-object"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 certify the election result}}}\uc2  in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2020/nov/24/us-election-results-2020-joe-biden-defeats-donald-trump-to-win-presidency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden \u8217\'20\'19s favor}}}\uc2  were intent on trying to kidnap lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 Espaillat said he believes thugs aimed \u8220\'20\'1Cto assassinate Pence and Pelosi\u8221\'20\'1D, referring to the Republican vice president Mike Pence and the Democratic Speaker of the House, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump had urged his supporters at a rally before the riot to march on the Capitol and \u8220\'20\'1Cfight\u8221\'20\'1D to overturn the election result, after his requests to Pence somehow to engineer such a thing (which is not in the vice president\u8217\'20\'19s power) had failed.\par \par \uc2 Adriano Espaillat\uc2  on Fifth Avenue in New York in an action of civil disobedience near Trump Tower on September 19, 2017 in New York, calling attention to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s anti-immigration policies, including the rollback of special provisions for young undocumented immigrants known as \u8220\'20\'1CDreamers\u8221\'20\'1D. Photograph: Kevin Hagen/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Moments ago, Cori Bush, the newly elected progressive congresswoman from St Louis, delivered an impassioned speech calling for the impeachment of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. Cori Bush: "The 117th Congress must understand that we have a mandate to legislate in defense of Black lives. The first step in that process is to root out white supremacy, starting with impeaching the white supremacist-in-chief." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/AOSBKrUbre"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/AOSBKrUbre}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XU0N3HHtRW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/XU0N3HHtRW}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1349432715888762881?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we fail to remove a white supremacist president who incited a white supremacist insurrection, it\u8217\'20\'19s communities like Missouri\u8217\'20\'19s 1st district that suffer the most,\u8221\'20\'1D Bush said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe 117th Congress must understand that we have a mandate to legislate in defense of Black lives. The first step in that process is to root out white supremacy, starting with impeaching the white supremacist-in-chief.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As she finished her speech, Bush\u8217\'20\'19s denunciation of white supremacy was booed by some of her Republican colleagues.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The statement from the president, which calls for \u8220\'20\'1Cno violence,\u8221\'20\'1D comes a week after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  incited a violent mob to storm the Capitol, resulting in five deaths.\par \par \uc2 The president has consistently denied responsibility for inciting the riot, despite telling a group of his supporters to march to the Capitol moments before the building was breached.\par \par \uc2 Trump claimed yesterday that his words were \u8220\'20\'1Ctotally appropriate,\u8221\'20\'1D even though they have been intensely criticized by members of both parties.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Statement from the president\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has put out a statement from the White House.\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ufdgSCInVC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ufdgSCInVC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jim Acosta (@Acosta) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Acosta/status/1349429943869038594?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The statement includes: \u8220\'20\'1CIn light of reports of more demonstrations, I urge that there must be NO violence, NO lawbreaking and NO violence of any kind.\u8221\'20\'1D He calls for folks to calm down.\par \par \uc2 Pro-Trump mob attacks the US Capitol on January 6. Photograph: Shannon Stapleton/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Afternoon summary\par \par \uc2 The House of Representatives is on track to impeach \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  this afternoon, so do stay tuned. It\u8217\'20\'19s been a busy morning. Here are the main points so far:\par \par \uc2 * Six {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jan/13/donald-trump-impeachment-nancy-pelosi-joe-biden-mike-pence-congress-covid-coronavirus-live-updates?page=with:block-5fff3fca8f0853a2a9aab1e5#block-5fff3fca8f0853a2a9aab1e5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican members}}}\uc2  of the House of Representatives have now indicated they will support the impeachment of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . That will boost the overwhelming Democratic push for the action, with the official impeachment moment not long away.\par \par \uc2 * Senate Republican leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s office has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jan/13/donald-trump-impeachment-nancy-pelosi-joe-biden-mike-pence-congress-covid-coronavirus-live-updates?page=with:block-5fff36248f08f301ebd54f3b#block-5fff36248f08f301ebd54f3b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said there will be no}}}\uc2 impeachment trial before 19 January, when the chamber is currently set to return from recess.\par \par \uc2 * House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  quotedAbraham Lincoln, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jan/13/donald-trump-impeachment-nancy-pelosi-joe-biden-mike-pence-congress-covid-coronavirus-live-updates?page=with:block-5fff2e0e8f0853a2a9aab0cf#block-5fff2e0e8f0853a2a9aab0cf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot escape history. We... will be remembered in spite of ourselves.\u8221\'20\'1D She said Trump must be removed from office. \u8220\'20\'1CHe must go...he is a clear and present danger to the nation we all love.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2 , the House majority leader, rejected Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 arguments that a swift impeachment would only further divide the country. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are consequences to actions, and the actions of president of the United States demand urgent, clear action by the \uc2 Congress of the United States\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/jan/13/donald-trump-impeachment-nancy-pelosi-joe-biden-mike-pence-congress-covid-coronavirus-live-updates?page=with:block-5fff09fc8f08f301ebd54c49#block-5fff09fc8f08f301ebd54c49"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hoyer said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Sixth House Republican says he will support the impeachment of Trump\par \par \uc2 Washington state Republican \uc2 Dan Newhouse\uc2  just rose on the floor of the House and said he would support the historic impeachment today of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. \uc2 Dan Newhouse\uc2  (R-Washington) votes to impeach President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4pzr0RnmEM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4pzr0RnmEM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Drew Mikkelsen (@drewmikkelsenk5) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/drewmikkelsenk5/status/1349428972686229504?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 In a strongly worded statement last night, \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , a representative from Wyoming, the No. 3 Republican in the House, and the daughter of the former vice-president Dick Cheney, said that Trump had \u8220\'20\'1Csummoned this mob, assembled the mob, and lit the flame of this attack\u8221\'20\'1D during the Capitol riot on January 6.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEverything that followed was his doing,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CNone of this would have happened without the president. I will vote to impeach the president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After setting the ball rolling by House GOP members, Cheney {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/12/donald-trump-texas-impeachment-effort"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was joined}}}\uc2  last night by the Washington representative Jaime Herrera Beutler, the New York representative John Katko, the Illinois representative Adam Kinzinger, and representative Fred Upton, of Michigan, the Republicans who all said they would vote for impeachment.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/12/trump-impeachment-liz-cheney-republicans-capitol"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Liz Cheney, No 3 House Republican, will vote to impeach Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 Newhouse said there was \u8220\'20\'1Cno excuse\u8221\'20\'1D for the president\u8217\'20\'19s actions, when he encouraged hyper-loyal supporters to march on the US Capitol a week ago, egged on to attempt to overturn the results of the election by force.\par \par \uc2 enltrRepublican Rep. Dan Newhouse announces he is voting to impeach Trump even though he thinks the articles are "flawed." He says there is "no excuse" for Trump's actions; he says Trump "misinformed and inflamed a violent mob."\par \par \uc2 Newhouse says he and others should've spoken up sooner.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Daniel Dale (@ddale8) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ddale8/status/1349427147178434568?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House minority leader Kevin McCarthy is decrying the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/09/us-capitol-insurrection-white-supremacist-terror"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 events of January 6}}}\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe worst day I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever seen in Congress\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy said:\u8220\'20\'1CThe president bears responsibility for Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s attack on Congress by mob rioters. He should have immediately denounced the mob when he saw what was unfolding.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrAfter arguing he shouldn't be impeached, Kevin McCarthy says, "The president bears responsibility for Wednesday's attack on Congress by mob rioters. He should have immediately denounced the mob when he saw what was unfolding."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaitlan Collins (@kaitlancollins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins/status/1349424497150091264?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 But the California Republican is not in favor of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-impeachment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 impeaching}}}\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . He\u8217\'20\'19s arguing for a creating a fact-finding commission and an official censure of the president to suffice.\par \par \uc2 House Minority Leader Kevin McCarthy (R-CA), left, and Representative Jim Jordan (R-OH), right, talk during a joint session of Congress to certify the 2020 Electoral College results after supporters of President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  stormed the Capitol earlier in the day on Capitol Hill in Washington, DC, 06 January 2021. Photograph: Erin Schaff/EPA\par \par \uc2 He repeated something that he reportedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/12/donald-trump-texas-impeachment-effort"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Trump}}}\uc2  directly - that, unlike what he points out \u8220\'20\'1Csome say\u8221\'20\'1D, the violent mob that invaded the US Capitol last week was not driven by far left anti-fascist activists collectively known as \u8220\'20\'1Cantifa\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no evidence of that,\u8221\'20\'1D McCarthy said.\par \par \uc2 He talked of pledging a smooth transition to the presidency of Joe Bide n a week from today. Smattering of applause for McCarthy.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/12/donald-trump-texas-impeachment-effort"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Growing cohort of Republicans turn against Trump as he denies inciting Capitol attack}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House Democrats have consistently denounced \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for inciting the Capitol riot during the debate on the article of impeachment.\par \par \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , who served as an impeachment manager during the president\u8217\'20\'19s first Senate trial, referred to Trump as \u8220\'20\'1Ca living, breathing impeachable offense\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltr"\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a living, breathing impeachable offense" -- \uc2 Rep. Hakeem Jeffries{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/8P8I7Dgebi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/8P8I7Dgebi}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1349418011967582210?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Moments later, Jamie Raskin, the Democrat who will serve as the lead impeachment manager this time around, also criticized Republicans who have tried to blame Democrats for the violence seen last week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a bit much to be hearing that these people would not be trying to destroy our government and kill us if we just weren\u8217\'20\'19t so mean to them,\u8221\'20\'1D Raskin said.\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. Raskin: "It is a bit much to be hearing that these people would not be trying to destroy our government and kill us if we just weren't so mean to them." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/TEydYa2PSn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/TEydYa2PSn}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1349421331964715008?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 At least 20,000 National Guard troops may be deployed to help safeguard the nation\u8217\'20\'19s capital ahead of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s inauguration next week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think you can expect to see somewhere upwards beyond 20,000 members of the National Guard that will be here in the footprint of the District of Columbia,\u8221\'20\'1D acting DC police chief Robert Contee said at a news conference on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Members of the National Guard rest in the Capitol Visitors Center on Wednesday. Photograph: Brendan Smialowski/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 The announcement comes one week after a mob of Trump loyalists breached and vandalized the US capitol, where Biden will be inaugurated next Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Despite threats of potential violence on Inauguration Day, Biden has said he is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot afraid\u8221\'20\'1D to take the oath of office outside on the Capitol steps.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Cedric Richmond, the Democratic congressman who is leaving the House to join Joe Biden \u8217\'20\'19s administration, delivered a fiery speech in support of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s impeachment.\par \par \uc2 enltrDuring debate on Impeachment of President Trump, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepRichmond?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @reprichmond}}}\uc2  concludes his final House floor speech: "Simply put, we told you so. Richmond out." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/bwMxwCqmoR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/bwMxwCqmoR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1349418471298375687?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The Louisiana Democrat noted that, during the president\u8217\'20\'19s first impeachment, his party warned Trump would carry out more attacks on American democracy if he were not removed from office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSimply put, we told you so,\u8221\'20\'1D Richmond said. Nodding at his imminent departure from the House, he then added, \u8220\'20\'1CRichmond out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 No Senate impeachment trial before 19 January, McConnell's office says\par \par \uc2 Senate Republican leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s office has said there will be no impeachment trial before 19 January, when the chamber is currently set to return from recess.\par \par \uc2 McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s press secretary confirmed the Washington Post\u8217\'20\'19s report on the timing on the trial.\par \par \uc2 enltrCan confirm \u8212\'20\'14> {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/l2U1WlyQSF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/l2U1WlyQSF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Doug Andres (@DougAndres) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DougAndres/status/1349414139928702980?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Senate Democratic leader Chuck Schumer had called for the chamber to return early to take up the impeachment of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , but McConnell is apparently declining to do so.\par \par \uc2 The decision means that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s impeachment trial will overlap with the first days of Joe Biden \u8217\'20\'19s presidency.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Adam Schiff, who served as the lead impeachment manager during \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s first impeachment trial, said the Capitol riot represented \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most dangerous moment for our democracy in a century.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr"This is one of those moments."\par \par \uc2 Rep. Adam Schiff says America has endured a Civil War, world wars and more, and will endure "a Trumpist and white nationalist insurrection," because "patriotic Americans step forward to say 'enough.'" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vdtbbFfqdP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/vdtbbFfqdP}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/bmtjEcpzSa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/bmtjEcpzSa}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News (@ABC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABC/status/1349415677791244292?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, we invoke the remedy the founders provided for just such a lawless president: impeachment,\u8221\'20\'1D Schiff said.\par \par \uc2 The California Democrat added, \u8220\'20\'1CMore important, today we begin the long road to restoration.... To preserve this sacred place, this citadel of democracy, for ourselves and for posterity, let us say enough. Enough.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Jim Jordan, one of the president\u8217\'20\'19s congressional attack dogs, argued against the impeachment of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for inciting a violent mob to attack the Capitol by condemning \u8220\'20\'1Ccancel culture\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltr"They want to cancel the president" -- Jim Jordan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ttM0wzF8Bi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ttM0wzF8Bi}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1349410932691263490?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe should be focused on bringing the nation together. Instead, Democrats are going to impeach the president for a second time one week, one week before he leaves office. Why?\u8221\'20\'1D Jordan said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey want to cancel the president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jordan added, \u8220\'20\'1CIt won\u8217\'20\'19t just be the president of the United States. The cancel culture will come for us all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In reality, Democrats have said they want to impeach the president for a second time because Trump incited a violent mob to attack the Capitol, resulting in five deaths.\par \par \uc2 Moments ago, Pelosi argued Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cmust go\u8221\'20\'1D because he represents \u8220\'20\'1Ca clear and present danger to the nation we all love\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  described January 6, when a violent mob stormed the Capitol, as a \u8220\'20\'1Cday of fire.\u8221\'20\'1D George W Bush used {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://georgewbush-whitehouse.archives.gov/infocus/bushrecord/documents/Selected_Speeches_George_W_Bush.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the same phrase}}}\uc2  to describe the September 11 attacks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know that the president of the United States incited this insurrection, armed rebellion, against our common country,\u8221\'20\'1D the Democratic speaker said.\par \par \uc2 Pelosi argued it was a vital necessity to impeach the president, but she said of the need to impeach, \u8220\'20\'1CIt breaks my heart. It should break your heart. It should break all of our hearts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The speaker said she stood before the chamber today as \u8220\'20\'1Can officer of the constitution.\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CSearch your souls,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said, \u8220\'20\'1Cis the president\u8217\'20\'19s war on democracy in keeping with the constitution?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Pelosi: Trump 'is a clear and present danger to the nation we all love'\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  kicked off the two hours of debate on the article of impeachment against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Democratic speaker began her remarks by quoting Abraham Lincoln, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot escape history. We... will be remembered in spite of ourselves.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pelosi argued Trump must be removed from office because he represents a clear threat to national security.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe must go,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe is a clear and present danger to the nation we all love.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The article of impeachment, incitement of insurrection, is now being read on the House floor before the debate begins.\par \par \uc2 The article reads, in part, \u8220\'20\'1CIn his conduct while President of the United States \u8212\'20\'14 and in violation of his constitutional oath faithfully to execute the office of President of the United States and, to the best of his ability, preserve, provide, protect, and defend the Constitution of the United States and in violation of his constitutional duty to take care that the laws be faithfully executed \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Donald John Trump\uc2  engaged in high Crimes and Misdemeanors by inciting violence against the \uc2 Government of the United States\uc2 ...\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald John Trump\uc2 , by such conduct, has demonstrated that he will remain a threat to national security, democracy, and the Constitution if allowed to remain in office, and has acted in a manner grossly incompatible with self-governance and the rule of law. \uc2 Donald John Trump\uc2  thus warrants impeachment and trial, removal from office, and disqualification to hold and enjoy any office of honor, trust, or profit under the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House adopts rule to begin debate on article of impeachment\par \par \uc2 The House has voted 221-203 to begin debate on the article of impeachment, incitement of insurrection, against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrThe House voted 221-203 to adopt H.Res. 41. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KQHegRyHhp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/KQHegRyHhp}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 House Press Gallery (@HouseDailyPress) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HouseDailyPress/status/1349406708649648130?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The House will now debate the article for two hours, with a final vote on impeachment expected later this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  went outside to thank the National Guard troops who are protecting the Capitol today, as members vote on the article of impeachment against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Democratic speaker also presented the troops with her challenge coin as a token of appreciation, per NBC News.\par \par \uc2 enltrPelosi just went outside and thanked the troops protecting the Capitol, and game them all her challenge coin: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VbOhyFxcVj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VbOhyFxcVj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Frank Thorp V (@frankthorp) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/frankthorp/status/1349396857760444418?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Graham opposes impeachment despite distancing himself from Trump\par \par \uc2 Lindsey Graham has released a statement expressing opposition to the second impeachment of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , claiming the resolution \u8220\'20\'1Cwill do great damage to the institutions of government and could invite further violence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrSupporting the impeachment of President Trump under these circumstances will do great damage to the institutions of government and could invite further violence at a time the President is calling for calm.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lindsey Graham (@LindseyGrahamSC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LindseyGrahamSC/status/1349397976914010117?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf there was a time for America\u8217\'20\'19s political leaders to bend a knee and ask for God\u8217\'20\'19s counsel and guidance, it is now,\u8221\'20\'1D the Republican senator said in the statement. \u8220\'20\'1CThe most important thing for leaders to do in times of crisis is to make things better, not worse.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Graham interestingly leveled criticism at fellow Republicans who are supporting the impeachment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs to Senate leadership, I fear they are making the problem worse, not better,\u8221\'20\'1D Graham said. \u8220\'20\'1CTo my Republican colleagues who legitimize this process, you are doing great damage not only to the country, the future of the presidency, but also to the party.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Graham\u8217\'20\'19s statement comes after reports indicated that Senate Republican leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  has told colleagues he believes Trump committed impeachable offenses.\par \par \uc2 It also comes one week after Graham seemed to distance himself from the president in response to Trump inciting a violent mob to storm the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll I can say is count me out,\u8221\'20\'1D Graham said last week. \u8220\'20\'1CEnough is enough.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Republican proposal to amend the rule for debate on the article of impeachment has failed, by a vote of 221-205.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe House voted 221-205 to order the previous question on H.Res. 41. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KQHegRyHhp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/KQHegRyHhp}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 House Press Gallery (@HouseDailyPress) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HouseDailyPress/status/1349393751857385478?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The House is now voting on the rule itself. If it passes, as is expected, that will kick off two hours of debate on the article of impeachment.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Andy Biggs, a Republican congressman of Arizona, is circulating a petition calling on \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  to resign from her post as House Republican conference chair, according to Axios.\par \par \uc2 enltrThis petition is being sent around by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepAndyBiggsAZ?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepAndyBiggsAZ}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s team {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/S3eoLlEYXE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/S3eoLlEYXE}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alayna Treene (@alaynatreene) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/alaynatreene/status/1349393445987737600?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The petition comes one day after Cheney, the third-ranking House Republican, announced she would support the article of impeachment against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe President could have immediately and forcefully intervened to stop the violence. He did not,\u8221\'20\'1D Cheney said in a statement explaining her vote. There has never been a greater betrayal by a President of the United States of his office and his oath to the Constitution.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will vote to impeach the President.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senate impeachment trial as soon as this week?\par \par \uc2 Republican leadership in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  is mulling the possibility of beginning an impeachment trial of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as early as Friday if (as appears highly likely) the Democratic Party-dominated House of Representatives approves one article of impeachment, according to a report this morning.\par \par \uc2 A senior Senate Republican aide, who asked not to be identified, has told the above to the Reuters news agency, and stressed that no decisions had yet been made on whether to take that step.\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of \uc2 US National Guard\uc2  troops rest in the US Capitol Visitors Center, on Capitol Hill in Washington DC today. Photograph: Michael Reynolds/EPA\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Jim Jordan, one of the president\u8217\'20\'19s fiercest congressional allies, said \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  should be removed as House Republican conference chair for supporting impeachment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe ought to have a second vote,\u8221\'20\'1D Jordan said, per the Washington Post. \u8220\'20\'1CThe conference ought to vote on that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrNEWS: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Jim_Jordan?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Jim_Jordan}}}\uc2  says {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Liz_Cheney?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Liz_Cheney}}}\uc2  should be removed as conference chair.\par \par \uc2 "We ought to have a second vote."\par \par \uc2 "The conference ought to vote on that."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mike DeBonis (@mikedebonis) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mikedebonis/status/1349383159587229698?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The proposal to oust Cheney for her impeachment vote seems to be at odds with Republicans \u8217\'20\'19 calls for unity and healing after a violent, pro-Trump mob stormed the Capitol last week.\par \par \uc2 Apparently the unity does not apply to House members.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The vote on the rule to set up debate on the article of impeachment is underway, and a number of Republicans are voting by proxy.\par \par \uc2 The decision is noteworthy because Republican members have criticized House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  for allowing voting by proxy amid the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 But today, a week after a violent mob stormed the US Capitol, many Republican members are taking the proxy option.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As the vote continues, House members are once again sidestepping the metal detectors that have been set up outside the chamber.\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. Bob Gibbs walks right around the metal detector and enters the House floor.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re back to this.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Matt Fuller (@MEPFuller) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MEPFuller/status/1349382998072971265?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 A HuffPost reporter saw three Republican members -- Bob Gibbs, Chip Roy and Garret Graves -- ignore the metal detectors.\par \par \uc2 Another Republican member, Russ Fulcher, pushed past a cop guarding the metal detectors to gain access to the floor.\par \par \uc2 The metal detectors were set up yesterday to provide more security on the floor, in response to the violent riot at the Capitol last week, but some Republicans have objected to their use or ignored them entirely.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The House is now voting on the rule to open debate on the article of impeachment, incitement of insurrection, against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Dozens of Republicans have already voted against the rule, but it is expected to pass with all Democrats \u8217\'20\'19 support.\par \par \uc2 This is a procedural vote that will allow the House to move on to debate the article of impeachment itself. The final vote on the article will come this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A New York Times reporter captured a picture of a group of black National Guard troops posing for a photo with the statue of civil rights leader Rosa Parks in the Capitol\u8217\'20\'19s Statuary Hall.\par \par \uc2 enltrTaking a photo with the statue of Rosa Parks in Statuary Hall. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wUcGRnPFLS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wUcGRnPFLS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Emily Cochrane (@ESCochrane) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ESCochrane/status/1349371666481217544?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The picture resonated with many, given that it was taken just a week after violent rioters (many of whom espoused white supremacist views) stormed the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 These black service members are now protecting the very lawmakers who were forced to shelter in place because of that mob.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Nancy Mace, a Republican of South Carolina, delivered her first floor speech as a congresswoman moments ago, addressing the article of impeachment against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not the reason why I wanted to give my first speech in our chambers,\u8221\'20\'1D Mace said.\par \par \uc2 enltrRepublican Rep. Nancy Mace, making her first speech on the House floor, argues against Trump's impeachment because it's "rushed" and "there is violence on both sides of the aisle" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Ym534qDLbx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Ym534qDLbx}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1349372271371153410?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Mace expressed dismay about the violence at the Capitol last week, saying she was very grateful that she sent her children home before Wednesday because she was worried about the rhetoric she was seeing.\par \par \uc2 Mace, who has been very critical of Trump and his allies who have echoed his baseless claims of widespread fraud in the presidential election, then went on to argue this impeachment is \u8220\'20\'1Crushed,\u8221\'20\'1D so she will not be supporting it.\par \par \uc2 She added that \u8220\'20\'1Cthere is violence on both sides of the aisle.\u8221\'20\'1D But the violence last week, which resulted in five deaths, was incited by the president and was carried out by a group of his supporters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hold him accountable for the events that transpired,\u8221\'20\'1D Mace said of Trump. And yet... she is not supporting impeachment.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Capitol rioter who was photographed wearing a sweatshirt that said \u8220\'20\'1CCamp Auschwitz\u8221\'20\'1D has been arrested, according to multiple reports.\par \par \uc2 The rioter was identified as Robert Keith Packer of Virginia.\par \par \uc2 CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/01/10/politics/man-camp-auschwitz-sweatshirt-capitol-riot-identified/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 An image of Packer inside the Capitol, whose sweatshirt bore the name of the Nazi concentration camp where about 1.1 million people were killed during World War II, has evoked shock and disbelief on social media. The bottom of his shirt stated, \u8216\'20\'18Work brings freedom,\u8217\'20\'19 which is the rough translation of the phrase \u8216\'20\'18Arbeit macht frei\u8217\'20\'19 that was on the concentration camp\u8217\'20\'19s gates....\par \par \uc2 One Virginia resident, who spoke to CNN on the condition of anonymity due to the sensitivity of the matter, described Packer as a long-time extremist who has had run-ins with the law.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18He\u8217\'20\'19s been always extreme and very vocal about his beliefs,\u8217\'20\'19 the resident said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House majority leader: Trump's behavior demands 'urgent, clear action by the Congress'\par \par \uc2 Steny Hoyer, the House majority leader, rejected Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 arguments that a swift impeachment would only further divide the country, after the president incited a violent mob to storm the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are consequences to actions, and the actions of president of the United States demand urgent, clear action by the \uc2 Congress of the United States\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Hoyer said.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LeaderHoyer?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @LeaderHoyer}}}\uc2  : "There are consequences to actions and the actions of president of the United States demand urgent clear action by the \uc2 Congress of the United States\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 He then reads impeachment statement from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepLizCheney?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepLizCheney}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/L1fIhCaQbh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/L1fIhCaQbh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1349369121453047808?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Hoyer quoted the five Republican members of Congress who have already said they will support impeachment, including \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , the House Republican conference chair.\par \par \uc2 The majority leader predicted that more Republicans would join them in supporting impeachment when the vote happens this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The appearance of National Guard troops at the Capitol this morning is a visceral reminder of the violence that took place last week.\par \par \uc2 One picture, captured by a New York Times photographer, shows troops resting in a hallway that \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  frequently passes through on her way to her office.\par \par \uc2 enltrInside the Capitol this morning where Speaker Pelosi usually walks to her office. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BQIEf5b2s4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/BQIEf5b2s4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Erin Schaff (@erinschaff) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/erinschaff/status/1349361672151040002?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The plaque next to the troops honors the service members who were quartered in the Capitol during the Civil War.\par \par \uc2 A CNN reporter shared a tweet comparing photos of troops at the Capitol today to sketches of troops at the Capitol during the Civil War.\par \par \uc2 enltrTroops quartered in the Capitol, the Civil War vs now. (Photos via {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DaniellaMicaela?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @DaniellaMicaela}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ReedReports?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ReedReports}}}\uc2  ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DCnR3E9fh2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/DCnR3E9fh2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rebecca Buck (@RebeccaBuck) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RebeccaBuck/status/1349359743350009859?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Tom Cole, the top Republican on the House rules committee, made a process argument against the second impeachment of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not the type of robust process we\u8217\'20\'19ve followed for every modern impeachment,\u8221\'20\'1D Cole said on the House floor.\par \par \uc2 The Republican congressman called for \u8220\'20\'1Chealing\u8221\'20\'1D after a violent mob stormed the Capitol, arguing another impeachment would only further divide the nation.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s worth noting that last week, Cole supported an objection to counting Arizona and Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s electoral votes for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  after the violence at the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Steny Hoyer, the House majority leader, told NBC News that the chamber would immediately send the impeachment article to the Senate if it passes the House.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LeaderHoyer?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @LeaderHoyer}}}\uc2  told me Democrats would send impeachment articles to the Senate immediately.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Leigh Ann Caldwell (@LACaldwellDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LACaldwellDC/status/1349362013730963459?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 There had been discussions among Democrats about holding back the article until their party took control of the Senate, but it seems House leadership decided against that.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The House is now debating the rule to set up the debate on the impeachment article later today, which will precede the vote on the article.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe House is back in session and will debate for up to one hour H.Res. 41 - Rule providing for consideration of H.Res. 24 \u8211\'20\'13 Impeaching \uc2 Donald John Trump\uc2 , President of the United States, for high crimes and misdemeanors.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 House Press Gallery (@HouseDailyPress) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HouseDailyPress/status/1349359865244880897?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Speaking on the House floor, Jim McGovern, the Democratic chairman of the rules committee, noted that today\u8217\'20\'19s vote is taking place at \u8220\'20\'1Can actual crime scene\u8221\'20\'1D after a violent mob stormed the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 McGovern recounted how \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  incited the crowd to attack the Capitol, by encouraging a group of his supporters at a rally to march down Pennsylvania Avenue as Congress certified \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s victory in the presidential election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI saw evil,\u8221\'20\'1D McGovern said of the rioters.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Grun Kibben, the House chaplain, reflected on the gravity of the day and the grief of the past week in her opening prayer this morning.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe stand before you to give account for our role in today\u8217\'20\'19s momentous decisions and our deepest desire to carry out responsibilities to govern, protect and preserve this nation while yet unsettled by the events of this past week,\u8221\'20\'1D Kibben said.\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s likely impeachment comes exactly one week after he incited a violent, pro-Trump mob to storm the Capitol, resulting in five deaths.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 After gaveling in the session, the House immediately went into a brief recess before starting the debate on the article of impeachment.\par \par \uc2 The final vote on the article, incitement of insurrection, is expected around 3 pm ET.\par \par \uc2 The article is expected to pass with the support of all Democrats and at least five Republicans, meaning this impeachment (unlike \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s first impeachment) will be bipartisan.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House gavels in session to consider article of impeachment\par \par \uc2 The House has now gaveled in its session to debate and vote on the article of impeachment, incitement of insurrection, against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Over on Capitol Hill, National Guard troops have been deployed to protect lawmakers and staffers amid the impeachment vote, in response to the violence last week that has left five people dead.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe scene at the Capitol Visitor Center - absolutely filled with National Guard. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/A9JNT7nwlh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/A9JNT7nwlh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Grace Segers (@Grace_Segers) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Grace_Segers/status/1349348020748505093?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 This is Joan Greve in Washington, taking over for Martin Belam.\par \par \uc2 The House will soon gavel in its session to consider the article of impeachment against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , which charges the president with incitement of insurrection in connection to the violent riot at the Capitol last week.\par \par \uc2 If the article is approved, as is expected, Trump will become the first president in US history to ever be impeached twice.\par \par \uc2 The matter will then move on to the Senate, where two-thirds of senators would have to vote to convict Trump to remove him from office.\par \par \uc2 It currently seems unlikely that the Senate would vote to convict, but reports indicate the Republican leader, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , has told colleagues he believes Trump has committed impeachable offenses.\par \par \uc2 It will be quite an interesting day on Capitol Hill, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As the coronavirus pandemic continues to sweep across the country state and local governments across the US are bracing for severe economic impacts in 2021 that could force layoffs of government employees and swinging cuts to services.\par \par \uc2 The last few months have offered a more detailed picture of what the pandemic\u8217\'20\'19s economic recession will look like for state and local governments. While some have been spared the doomsday scenarios predicted at the outset of the pandemic, others have been \u8220\'20\'1Csavaged\u8221\'20\'1D. On the line are millions of jobs and drastic cuts to already struggling services in the midst of a national health and economic crisis that is only getting worse.\par \par \uc2 State and local governments set the budgets for local police and fire departments, public schools, health departments, road constructions and repair, public transportation and many other essential public services. How each state, city or town gets revenue varies widely, though it ultimately is some combination of income, sales and property taxes. No matter what the combination, when the economy is hurting \u8211\'20\'13 people are unemployed and are buying less and businesses are closing \u8211\'20\'13 state and local governments can take a huge hit.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are a lot of state and local governments who are seeing very, very strong impacts, and they\u8217\'20\'19re going to have to make very sizable tax increases or spending cuts, especially at the local level,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dan White, director of government consulting and fiscal policy research with Moody\u8217\'20\'19s Analytics, which has estimated that budget deficits will total about $80bn to $100bn even with federal aid from Congress\u8217\'20\'19 stimulus packages.\par \par \uc2 The outlook for some state governments is not as bad as economists had feared at the beginning of the pandemic. States including California and Virginia have been spared from huge losses, partly because tax revenue in those states have not declined as much as initially expected as people went back to work and wealthier workers continued to work from home.\par \par \uc2 But other states are looking at huge deficits, some worth billions of dollars, particularly as the industries that they rely on for revenue, like tourism or energy, have declined because of the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Read more of Lauren Aratani\u8217\'20\'19s report here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jan/13/us-state-local-governments-covid-pandemic-economic-impacts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US state and local governments brace for layoffs and cuts due to pandemic}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jan/13/us-state-local-governments-covid-pandemic-economic-impacts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US state and local governments brace for layoffs and cuts due to pandemic}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A month after federal regulators ordered it to disclose how its practices affect children and teenagers, TikTok is tightening its privacy practices for the under-18 crowd.\par \par \uc2 Starting today, the default privacy setting for accounts with users aged 13 to 15 will be private. That means only someone the user approves as a follower can view their videos, which was not the case previously. But teens can still change this setting to public if they want.\par \par \uc2 Older teenagers won\u8217\'20\'19t see this default setting change. For users aged 16 or 17, the default setting to let people download the videos they created will now be \u8220\'20\'1Coff,\u8221\'20\'1D rather than \u8220\'20\'1Con.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Reuters report that TikTok is also blocking users\u8217\'20\'19 ability to download videos created by those 15 or younger. This age group will also see direct messaging restricted and won\u8217\'20\'19t be able to host live streams. A tool called \u8220\'20\'1Cfamily pairing,\u8221\'20\'1D meanwhile, lets parents link their TikTok account to their teen\u8217\'20\'19s to enable content and privacy settings.\par \par \uc2 Last month, the \uc2 Federal Trade Commission\uc2  asked TikTok\u8217\'20\'19s parent company, along with \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , Amazon and five other social media companies to provide detailed information on how they collect and use consumers\u8217\'20\'19 personal data and how their practices affect children and teens.\par \par \uc2 TikTok users are asked to put in their birthday when they sign up for the service, but, as with other social media platforms, there is no real verification to ensure it is accurate.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration was involved in a protracted attempt last year to ban TikTok in the US altogether. The irony that in the end it was the president himself who was banned from most social media services following last week\u8217\'20\'19s assault on the US Capitol has not been lost on many users.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Some truly unprecedented scenes in the US Capitol in the run-up to the inauguration of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as president.\par \par \uc2 enltrJust walked into the Capitol to find literally hundreds of troops napping and lining up in the Congressional Visitor Center\u8212\'20\'14 as streets around here are largely blocked.\par \par \uc2 Many are cuddling their firearms, fatigues over their heads to block light, and riot gear in neat piles. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vCHAOGMdfA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vCHAOGMdfA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nathaniel Reed (@ReedReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ReedReports/status/1349326874573463555?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Mike Allen and Jim VandeHei at Axios have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/republicans-trump-impeachment-conviction-a811503e-129d-4f52-bb0c-10f155710d22.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this}}}\uc2  to say on the strategy of the Republican leadership over the attempt to impeach \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for a second time:\par \par \uc2 Top Republicans want to bury president Trump, for good. But they are divided whether to do it with one quick kill via impeachment, or let him slowly fade away.\par \par \uc2 Sources tell Axios Senate majority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  would be more likely than not to vote to convict Trump \u8212\'20\'14 a green light for other Republican senators to follow.\par \par \uc2 House Republican Leader Kevin McCarthy would love a Trumpless world, but doesn\u8217\'20\'19t want to knife him with fingerprints. This school of thought wants to let Trump do himself in, without a big party fight over his sins and sentence.\par \par \uc2 The fade-away caucus sees a danger that the impeachment-conviction route is, as a prominent conservative put it, \u8220\'20\'1Cmaking him Jesus.... Truly stupid.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But an effort by McCarthy to push a lighter punishment for Trump censure has crumbled.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/republicans-trump-impeachment-conviction-a811503e-129d-4f52-bb0c-10f155710d22.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios \u8211\'20\'13 Top Republicans want Trump done \u8212\'20\'14 forevermore}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Jacob Blake\u8217\'20\'19s uncle, Justin Blake, has written for us today about how there are two justice systems in America :\par \par \uc2 Last week, I was again reminded that we live under two justice systems. One lets armed white insurrectionists violently attack our nation\u8217\'20\'19s seat of government. Another gasses, beats, and shoots rubber bullets at people defending Black lives. And even though I live nowhere near Washington DC, this is personal for me.\par \par \uc2 The day before the attempted insurrection at the US Capitol, Rusten Sheskey got off scot-free. He is the Kenosha cop who shot my nephew, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jacob-blake"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jacob Blake}}}\uc2 , seven times in the back. The Kenosha district attorney, Michael Gravely, declined to charge Sheskey, and he faces no consequences. Jacob is now permanently paralyzed from the waist down.\par \par \uc2 Sheskey is just like the thousands of Trump-supporting, white nationalists who laid siege to the US Capitol in broad daylight. They broke windows, stole federal property, and ransacked offices. They endangered lawmakers, their staff, and other employees in the complex. They may have exposed countless people to Covid-19. They had flex cuffs and placed pipe bombs. They were out for blood.\par \par \uc2 This justice system calls these people \u8220\'20\'1Cprotesters\u8221\'20\'1D, and they are protected by the first amendment. Sheskey operates under this justice system, and it is unacceptable. He claimed self-defense after he shot Jacob in the back, in front of his kids, also in broad daylight. No plausible explanation exists for this escalated response.\par \par \uc2 The fact that the Capitol insurrection and Jacob\u8217\'20\'19s shooting both happened in broad daylight shows how barefaced state-sanctioned violence has become.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/jan/13/there-are-two-justice-systems-in-america-ask-my-nephew-jacob-blake"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justin Blake \u8211\'20\'13 There are two justice systems in America. Ask my nephew, Jacob Blake}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/jan/13/there-are-two-justice-systems-in-america-ask-my-nephew-jacob-blake"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 There are two justice systems in America. Ask my nephew, Jacob Blake | Justin Blake}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Megan Rapinoe has spoken on the recent attack on the US Capitol, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is America. We showed our true colours\u8221\'20\'1D. The 35-year old soccer forward opened a media teleconference yesterday with a six-minute exposition on the fractious state of the country in the wake of last week\u8217\'20\'19s siege. She added: \u8220\'20\'1CUnleashing a white supremacist mob is nothing new to America\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 Sahil Kapur at NBC News says that the decisions Republican lawmakers make in the coming days over the impeachment of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Ccould define the party and shape American democracy for generations to come\u8221\'20\'1D. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/trump-impeachment-may-define-republican-party-n1254034?cid=sm_npd_nn_tw_np"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 He writes}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The Senate requires a two-thirds majority to convict a president, which will mean at least 17 Republicans would need to join Democrats if the vote is taken after 20 January. That\u8217\'20\'19s a tall order.\par \par \uc2 The judgment of history looms. And for some who want to make a break from Trump and chart a new path for the Republican Party, time is running short.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt sure seems like the last best chance to stand up to the guy while it still matters,\u8221\'20\'1D said Liam Donovan, a lobbyist and former Republican campaign operative. \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans can speak up now or they can follow the path of least resistance, but at some point there will be a reckoning, and it will come at a political cost.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Kapur\u8217\'20\'19s analysis, it may come down to the actions of one man:\par \par \uc2 The outcome may center on Senate majority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , a Trump ally who broke with him on 6 January when making an impassioned plea to affirm \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory. But McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s intentions aren\u8217\'20\'19t clear. His office had no comment Tuesday on impeachment.\par \par \uc2 Others say his position could determine the outcome. \u8220\'20\'1CI think if McConnell supports conviction in the Senate then the votes will be there to convict the president,\u8221\'20\'1D said a senior Republican aide, who requested anonymity to speak candidly.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/trump-impeachment-may-define-republican-party-n1254034?cid=sm_npd_nn_tw_np"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News \u8211\'20\'13 Trump impeachment may define the Republican Party}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 President-elect \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has announced ambassador \uc2 Samantha Power\uc2  as his nominee for Administrator of the United States \uc2 Agency for International Development (USAID) \uc2 and has also said he will elevate the position to become a member of the National Security Council. Power served in the Obama administration as the US permanent representative to the United Nations.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://buildbackbetter.gov/press-releases/president-elect-biden-announces-ambassador-samantha-power-as-his-nominee-for-usaid-administrator/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 , Biden said:\par \par \uc2 Samantha Power\uc2  is a world-renowned voice of conscience and moral clarity \u8212\'20\'14 challenging and rallying the international community to stand up for the dignity and humanity of all people. I know firsthand the unparalleled knowledge and tireless commitment to principled American engagement she brings to the table, and her expertise and perspective will be essential as our country reasserts its role as a leader on the world stage. As USAID Administrator, Power will be a powerful force for lifting up the vulnerable, ushering in a new era of human progress and development, and advancing American interests globally.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19ve got a few minutes to spare, then I can recommend investing a bit of time on this. The Hill this morning have undertaken publishing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/house/533932-i-saw-my-life-flash-before-my-eyes-an-oral-history-of-the-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a 4,500 word \u8220\'20\'1Coral history\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  of last week\u8217\'20\'19s assault on the US Capitol. It takes in words from lawmakers on both sides of the aisle and reporters who were there on the day, and some of the quotes bring home the extreme sense of danger that they felt on the day. Here are the words of Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Rep. Jason Crow\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 If there was a plan, that plan had deteriorated, and things were going to get bad quickly. Which they did. I made the decision to call my wife, tell her that I loved her, to pass that along to the kids, and I was preparing to either make a stand or fight our way out, and I would let her know as soon as I could.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/house/533932-i-saw-my-life-flash-before-my-eyes-an-oral-history-of-the-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Hill \u8211\'20\'13 \u8216\'20\'18I saw my life flash before my eyes\u8217\'20\'19: An oral history of the Capitol attack}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 The New York based {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hrw.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Human Rights Watch}}}\uc2  are releasing their annual report today, and head of the group \uc2 Kenneth Roth\uc2  has told Reuters that president-elect \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will need to restore the credibility of the US on human rights at home and abroad.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump has been a complete disaster for human rights, he flouted human rights at home with the fomenting of the 6 January attack on the Capitol being just the latest example of the natural culmination of four years of abuse of democratic principles,\u8221\'20\'1D Roth said.\par \par \uc2 Roth accused Trump of having \u8220\'20\'1Ccozied up to every friendly autocrat under the sun\u8221\'20\'1D while reserving criticism on human rights issues for his \u8220\'20\'1Cperceived adversaries\u8221\'20\'1D - Venezuela, Cuba, Iran, and \u8220\'20\'1Csometimes China\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut that kind of utterly inconsistent approach had no credibility. There was no force to his criticism when people knew that it was serving another political agenda, not a principled agenda,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Biden should articulate human rights as a \u8220\'20\'1Cguiding principle of US foreign policy and then to stick with it, even when that\u8217\'20\'19s difficult\u8221\'20\'1D, Roth said.\par \par \uc2 He urged him to call off arms sales to countries such as Egypt, Saudi Arabia and Israel and also called for Biden to re-engage with the \uc2 United Nations\u8217\'20\'19 Human Rights Council\uc2 , a Geneva forum which Trump quit in June 2018.\par \par \uc2 In his introductory essay to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hrw.org/world-report/2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the World Report 2021}}}\uc2 , he argues that \u8220\'20\'1CThe past four years show that Washington is an important but not indispensable leader on human rights. Many other governments treated Trump\u8217\'20\'19s retreat as cause for resolve rather than despair and stepped up to protect human rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 So far there are five Republicans in Congress who have come out in support in public of impeaching president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Here is who they are and what they have said:\par \par \uc2 Rep. John Katko\uc2  (New York) : \u8220\'20\'1CBy deliberately promoting baseless theories suggesting the election was somehow stolen, the president created a combustible environment of misinformation, disenfranchisement, and division. When this manifested in violent acts on 6 January, he refused to promptly and forcefully call it off, putting countless lives in danger.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rep. Liz Cheney\uc2  (Wyoming) : \u8220\'20\'1CThe president summoned this mob, assembled the mob, and lit the flame of this attack. Everything that followed was his doing. None of this would have happened without the president. The president could have immediately and forcefully intervened to stop the violence. He did not.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rep. Fred Upton (Michigan) : \u8220\'20\'1CI would have preferred a bipartisan, formal censure rather than a drawn-out impeachment process. But it is time to say: Enough is Enough.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rep. Herrera Beutler\uc2  (Washington) : \u8220\'20\'1CI understand the argument that the best course is not to further inflame the country or alienate Republican voters. But I am a Republican voter. I believe in our Constitution.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rep. Adam Kinzinger (Illinois) : \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no doubt in my mind that the president of the United States broke his oath of office and incited this insurrection. He used his position in the Executive to attack the Legislative. So in assessing the articles of impeachment brought before the House, I must consider: if these actions \u8211\'20\'13 the Article II branch inciting a deadly insurrection against the Article I branch \u8211\'20\'13 are not worthy of impeachment, then what is an impeachable offense?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 A broad coalition of organizations is urging \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  to mandate a national moratorium on water and other utility shutoffs on day one in the White House, in order to curtail the spread of Covid-19 and ease the financial burden on struggling Americans.\par \par \uc2 More than 600 environmental, rights and religious groups will on Wednesday present the incoming Democratic administration with a draft executive order that would impose an immediate nationwide ban on disconnecting essential utilities like water, gas and electricity until at least 12 months after the coronavirus pandemic ends.\par \par \uc2 The groundswell of pressure comes amid mounting reports of water and energy shutoffs across the country despite Covid cases, hospitalizations and deaths spiralling. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nicholasinstitute.duke.edu/articles/policy-pandemic-housing-security-policies-reduce-us-covid-19-infection-rates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study from Duke University}}}\uc2  last year found that banning water and utility shutoffs helps reduce the Covid infection rates.\par \par \uc2 Cutting off access to running water is particularly dangerous as regular handwashing is crucial to minimize the spread of the highly contagious virus.\par \par \uc2 Yet moratoriums on water shutoffs have so {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/aug/14/water-shutoffs-moratoriums-end-coronavirus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 far been patchy and often short lived}}}\uc2 . Only 20 states banned disconnections last year despite warnings from public health experts, and 11 of these moratoriums have expired. Currently, 56% of Americans \u8211\'20\'13 183m people \u8211\'20\'13 are at risk of losing their water supply if they cannot keep up with bill payments.\par \par \uc2 There is no national watchdog tracking water debt and shutoffs, but at least 226 utilities that issued moratoriums last year have also since let the bans expire, according to analysis by Food and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/water"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Water}}}\uc2  Watch (FWW).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis patchwork of protections has more than half of the country falling through the cracks and vulnerable to water shutoffs during the height of the pandemic. Zip code should not determine access to water. This is a basic matter of public health and humanity,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mary Grant, the Public Water For All campaign director from FWW, which is spearheading the campaign for a federal moratorium.\par \par \uc2 Read more of Nina Lakhani\u8217\'20\'19s report here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/13/water-shutoffs-coronavirus-moratorium-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vast coalition calls on Biden to impose national moratorium on water shutoffs}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/13/water-shutoffs-coronavirus-moratorium-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vast coalition calls on Biden to impose national moratorium on water shutoffs}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  reinstates restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill previously lifted due to Covid\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2  has reinstated a requirement that women visit a hospital or clinic to obtain a drug used for medication-induced abortions, lifting an order by a lower court allowing the drug to be posted or delivered during the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 The justices granted a request by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  to lift a federal judge\u8217\'20\'19s July order that had suspended the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) rule requiring in-person visits.\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s three liberal justices said they would have denied the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s request while litigation over the dispute continued in lower courts.\par \par \uc2 A district judge in Maryland, Theodore Chuang, had ruled that owing to the health risks that Covid-19 poses, the in-person requirements \u8220\'20\'1Cplace a substantial obstacle in the path of women seeking a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D and likely violate their constitutional rights.\par \par \uc2 He said the government had also taken actions to, in effect, waive several in-person requirements for dispensing other drugs, including opioids.\par \par \uc2 The dispute centres on the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s requirement that the drug mifepristone, one of two pills used to perform a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , be dispensed in-person by a certified prescriber. Medication abortions are approved through the first 10 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Groups representing tens of thousands of physicians, including the \uc2 American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists\uc2 , sued the \uc2 FDA\uc2  in May, saying that requiring in-person visits to pick up a pill needlessly exposes patients, doctors, and workers to a greater risk of contracting Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jan/13/us-supreme-court-reinstates-restrictions-abortion-pill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court reinstates restrictions on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jan/13/us-supreme-court-reinstates-restrictions-abortion-pill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court reinstates restrictions on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 Prominent lawyers who helped fuel \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s baseless charges of election fraud to try and thwart \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s win, are now facing potentially serious legal and financial problems of their own tied to their aggressive echoing of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s false election claims, say former Department of Justice lawyers and legal experts.\par \par \uc2 They include a federal investigation into the Capitol attack by a pro-Trump mob, possible disbarment and a defamation lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s personal attorney Rudy Giuliani, who led Trump\u8217\'20\'19s conspiratorial drive to overturn the election and gave an incendiary talk to the Trump rally right before the march on the Capitol began, could be ensnared in a federal probe of the attack and is facing a disbarment complaint in New York.\par \par \uc2 Pro-Trump lawyers Sidney Powell and Cleta Mitchell have, respectively, been hit with a defamation lawsuit for making false claims, and losing her law firm post after coming under scrutiny for her work promoting Trump\u8217\'20\'19s false claims.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI never saw allegations of misconduct that I think are as seriously unethical as the conduct of lawyers who have been propounding the false claims of President Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mary McCord, who led the DoJ\u8217\'20\'19s national security division at the end of the Obama administration until May 2017, and also served for six years on the DC Circuit\u8217\'20\'19s Grievance Committee.\par \par \uc2 Giuliani, a former New York mayor and ex federal prosecutor who led Trump\u8217\'20\'19s ad hoc legal team, seems to be the most endangered of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers.\par \par \uc2 Without offering evidence, Giuliani told Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Save America rally in DC before the Capitol attack that \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m willing to stake my reputation, the president is willing to stake his reputation, on the fact that we\u8217\'20\'19re going to find criminality there.\u8221\'20\'1D And he pointedly said, \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s have trial by combat.\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The day after the mob attack which led to five deaths, Michael Sherwin, the acting US attorney for Washington DC, publicly launched an investigation into the riot, and signaled he would be looking at numerous participants including instigators which could implicate Trump and Giuliani for their roles in inciting the attack.\par \par \uc2 McCord said Giuliani seems to have crossed the legal red lines in advising Trump after Giuliani left a detailed voice message at the wrong office for Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s newly elected senator Tommy Tuberville on 6 January about how to \u8220\'20\'1Cslow down\u8221\'20\'1D the electoral college vote.\par \par \uc2 Read more of Peter Stone\u8217\'20\'19s report here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/jan/13/donald-trump-lawyers-fallout-election-fraud-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lawyers face fallout from fueling Trump\u8217\'20\'19s false claims of election fraud}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 Michael Kranish writes for the Washington Post overnight about \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , the highest ranking Republican yet to come out in favor of impeaching president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/cheney-trump-house-impeach/2021/01/12/648c677a-54d2-11eb-a08b-f1381ef3d207_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 He reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The decision marked an extraordinary denouement for Cheney and her potentially precarious perch in the party\u8217\'20\'19s leadership. She had feuded for months with Trump and lately had been at odds with the majority of her caucus, even as speculation mounts about whether she might one day seek the speakership. The move was applauded by those in the party who have urged a clean break with Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a remarkable statement that sets a new bar for leadership in the House,\u8221\'20\'1D said Brendan Buck, a former aide to House Speaker \uc2 John A. Boehner\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CShe is turning the page on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . I think she is doing the right thing in her mind, and when you do the right thing for the right reasons you have to hope the politics work out for you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also traced her actions back to a phone call from her father on 6 January:\par \par \uc2 Cheney was in the House chamber, urging that Republicans reject efforts pushed by Trump and many others in her party to challenge the electoral college results that determined Trump had lost his reelection bid. She did not know she was being attacked by Trump, who was delivering the speech that would incite a mob to storm the Capitol, until her father reached her by phone in the House cloakroom.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe got to get rid of the weak congresspeople, the ones that aren\u8217\'20\'19t any good, the Liz Cheneys of the world,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in the speech, singling her out as he urged the mob to march to the Capitol. After being informed of the president\u8217\'20\'19s tirade by her father, Cheney walked out on the House floor, still hoping to stop the effort backed by Trump to overturn the electoral college votes. Then she heard a mob banging on the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s doors and a shot fired, and realized that an attempted insurrection was underway.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/cheney-trump-house-impeach/2021/01/12/648c677a-54d2-11eb-a08b-f1381ef3d207_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post \u8211\'20\'13 Before riot, Trump said \u8216\'20\'18we got to get rid\u8217\'20\'19 of Rep. Liz Cheney. Now she supports impeaching him.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 US sees new record of 4,327 Covid deaths in a single day\par \par \uc2 According to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gisanddata.maps.arcgis.com/apps/opsdashboard/index.html#/bda7594740fd40299423467b48e9ecf6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 figures from the Johns Hopkins university}}}\uc2 , yesterday the US recorded 215,805 new coronavirus cases, and 4,327 further deaths. This takes the total death toll in the pandemic in the US to 380,485, and marks the highest single daily death figure recorded by the university since the pandemic began. The previous highest figure of 4,194 was recorded on 7 January.\par \par \uc2 The Covid Tracking Project reports that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://covidtracking.com/data/national/hospitalization"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 131,326 people are currently hospitalized}}}\uc2  in the US with Covid-19. It is the 42nd day in a row that the figure has exceeded 100,000.\par \par \uc2 Christina Maxouris at CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2021/01/13/health/us-coronavirus-wednesday/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  that over the past week, the US has averaged more than 3,300 deaths every day, a jump of more than 200% since November. She writes:\par \par \uc2 Arizona reported a record-high 5,082 hospitalized Covid-19 patients Tuesday and on the same day broke a second record: more than 1,180 patients with the virus in ICU beds. In Louisiana, Gov. John Bel Edwards extended an order which keeps Covid-19 mitigation measures in place for nearly another month, saying the state was seeing a \u8220\'20\'1Chuge spike\u8221\'20\'1D in cases and hospitalizations.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC) stated that more than 27.6 million vaccine doses have so far been distributed in the US, and Health and Human Services Secretary Alex Azar announced changes in the distribution plan to try and speed up the roll-out.\par \par \uc2 Azar said \u8220\'20\'1CWe are telling states they should open vaccinations to all people 65 and over, and all people under age 65 with a comorbidity with some form of medical documentation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Dr. Anthony Fauci, one of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s leading immunologists, said that \u8220\'20\'1CWhen people are ready to get vaccinated, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to move right on to the next level, so that there are not vaccine doses that are sitting in a freezer or refrigerator where they could be getting into people\u8217\'20\'19s arm.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 default\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 US carries out first federal execution of a woman in nearly seven decades\par \par \uc2 Overnight, Kansas woman Lisa Montgomery was executed, the first time in nearly seven decades that the \uc2 US government\uc2  has put to death a female inmate.\par \par \uc2 Montgomery, 52, was pronounced dead at 1.31am after receiving a lethal injection at the federal prison complex in Terre Haute, Indiana. She was the 11th prisoner to receive a lethal injection there since July when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , an ardent supporter of capital punishment, resumed federal executions after a 17-year hiatus.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe craven bloodlust of a failed administration was on full display tonight,\u8221\'20\'1D Montgomery\u8217\'20\'19s attorney, Kelley Henry said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CEveryone who participated in the execution of Lisa Montgomery should feel shame.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe government stopped at nothing in its zeal to kill this damaged and delusional woman,\u8221\'20\'1D Henry said. \u8220\'20\'1CLisa Montgomery\u8217\'20\'19s execution was far from justice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It came after hours of legal wrangling before the supreme court cleared the way for the execution to move forward. Montgomery was the first of the final three federal inmates scheduled to die before next week\u8217\'20\'19s inauguration of president-elect \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who is expected to discontinue federal executions.\par \par \uc2 An appeals court granted Montgomery a stay of execution on Tuesday, shortly after another appeals court lifted an Indiana judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling that found she was likely mentally ill and couldn\u8217\'20\'19t comprehend she would be put to death. But both appeals were lifted, allowing the execution of the only female on federal death row to go forward.\par \par \uc2 Montgomery killed 23-year-old Bobbie Jo Stinnett in the north-west Missouri town of Skidmore in 2004. She used a rope to strangle Stinnett, who was eight months pregnant, and then cut the baby girl from the womb with a kitchen knife. Montgomery took the child with her and attempted to pass the girl off as her own.\par \par \uc2 Ed Pilkington wrote for us last week about the background story to Lisa Montgomery\u8217\'20\'19s life: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jan/05/lisa-montgomery-death-row-execution-history"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A lifetime of torture\u8217\'20\'19: the story of the woman Trump is rushing to execute}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jan/05/lisa-montgomery-death-row-execution-history"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A lifetime of torture\u8217\'20\'19: the story of the woman Trump is rushing to execute}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi accused Donald Trump of associating himself with sedition and treason in a strong statement yesterday calling for the removal of the president through impeachment after a failed call for enactment of the 25th amendment.\par \par \uc2 The final vote on Tuesday night was 223 to 205, with only one Republican backing the non-binding resolution that asked Mike Pence, the vice-president, to declare Trump \u8216\'20\'18incapable\u8217\'20\'19 under the 25th amendment.\par \par \uc2 The vote was largely symbolic, since Pence had already said he would not do so, arguing he did not believe \u8220\'20\'1Csuch a course of action is in the best interest of our nation or consistent with our constitution\u8221\'20\'1D and warned that efforts to remove Trump from office risked \u8220\'20\'1Cfurther divide and inflame the passions of the moment\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Welcome to our live coverage of US politics for Wednesday, when the House of Representatives is expected to vote to impeach president Donald Trump for a historic second time.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/12/house-vote-resolution-pence-invoke-25th-amendment-remove-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The House voted to formally call on the vice-president, Mike Pence, to invoke the 25th amendment}}}\uc2  and strip Donald Trump of his presidential authority. Only one Republican backed the measure and Pence has rejected the call.\par \par \uc2 * It will now move forward with impeachment. A single article charges Trump with \u8220\'20\'1Cincitement of insurrection,\u8221\'20\'1D and directly quotes the president\u8217\'20\'19s speech to supporters at the rally near the White House on 6 January.\par \par \uc2 * Four Republican representatives, including third-ranking GOP member {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/12/trump-impeachment-liz-cheney-republicans-capitol"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Liz Cheney}}}\uc2 , have said they\u8217\'20\'19ll vote to impeach Trump. \u8220\'20\'1C The president of the United States summoned this mob, assembled the mob, and lit the flame of this attack,\u8221\'20\'1D Cheney said.\par \par \uc2 * Senate majority leader Mitch McConnell has told colleagues that he believes Trump committed impeachable offenses, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/01/12/us/mitch-mcconnell-trump-impeachment.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the New York Times}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Representatives for the FBI and the justice department said more than 160 case files have been opened in connection to last week\u8217\'20\'19s violence at the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 * The US military\u8217\'20\'19s Joint Chiefs of Staff put out {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/12/us-capitol-attack-joint-chiefs-of-staff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a rare message to service members}}}\uc2  saying the pro-Trump mob attack on the US Capitol last week was an assault on America\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional process and against the law.\par \par \uc2 * There were 215,805 new cases of coronavirus recorded in the US yesterday, and 4,327 further deaths. It is the highest daily death count recorded by the Johns Hopkins university since the pandemic began.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jan/13/us-carries-out-first-federal-execution-of-a-woman-in-nearly-seven-decades"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The US carried out the first federal execution of a woman in nearly seven decades}}}\uc2 . Lisa Montgomery was pronounced dead early in the morning after supreme court cleared the path for her death.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/12/house-vote-resolution-pence-invoke-25th-amendment-remove-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stage set for impeachment after Pence dismisses House call to invoke 25th amendment}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210113eh1d001jp\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 atleast5(abortion)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Date\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\int